('daniel__v03fiendjailer', '', 'Motor-Runner''s right-hand man and the Fiends'' jailer responsible for holding captives in Vault 3''s living quarters', 'Daniel is a high-ranking Fiend who serves as Motor-Runner''s trusted second-in-command inside Vault 3. He patrols the rear sections of the vault''s living quarters with a personal bodyguard, enforcing gang authority over the occupied stronghold. His primary duty involves managing prisoners taken during Fiend raids, and he currently holds four captured traders locked in a cell beneath his watch. He carries the only key to their confinement, making him the sole arbiter of their fate. His elevated position within the gang hierarchy reflects Motor-Runner''s confidence in his loyalty and capability. Daniel embodies the Fiends'' brutal grip on their territory, maintaining order through intimidation and violence.', 'An Asian human male with a gaunt, chem-ravaged complexion, sunken eyes, and weathered skin marked by faded scars and crude tattoos.', 'Loyal and authoritative within his domain, comfortable with cruelty and captivity; trusts few outside Motor-Runner''s inner circle; methodical about maintaining control over prisoners', '{"Motor-Runner":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"right-hand man","note":"Daniel serves as Motor-Runner''s trusted second-in-command and jailer within Vault 3"},"Fiends":{"aff":60,"type":"fanatical","relation":"high-ranking member","note":"Holds significant authority within the gang''s hierarchy at Vault 3"},"Captured Traders":{"aff":-80,"type":"contempt","relation":"captive jailer","note":"Four traders currently imprisoned under Daniel''s direct supervision and control"}}', 'Right-hand man to Motor-Runner and jailer of Vault 3', '* Prisoner management
* Interrogation
* Close-quarters combat
* Vault security enforcement', 'Rough and commanding, with the aggressive edge typical of Fiend leadership; dismissive of outsiders and quick to assert authority', '* Maintain control over captured traders
* Serve Motor-Runner''s interests
* Reinforce Fiend dominance in Vault 3', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('daniel_wyand', '', 'A Mojave Express courier who died after completing a decoy delivery arranged by Robert House', 'Daniel Wyand was Courier Four, one of six couriers contracted by the Mojave Express in 2281 for a series of deliveries arranged through Johnson Nash by Victor on behalf of Robert House. He successfully delivered his assigned package-two oversized fuzzy dice-to the north entrance of the New Vegas Strip and received payment in full. Like Courier Six who followed him, he was shot in the head, but the wound proved fatal. His body lies outside the Nash residence in Primm, still carrying his Mojave Express delivery order. His delivery was one of five decoys designed to draw attention away from the true package: the platinum chip carried by Courier Six. He may have been acquainted with the courier who would later survive a similar attack.', 'A deceased African American human male bearing a fatal gunshot wound to the head.', 'Unknown in life; as a professional courier, he was reliable enough to be entrusted with House''s decoy operation', '{"Mojave Express":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"former courier","note":"Worked as Courier Four until his death on the job"},"Johnson Nash":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"employer contact","note":"Nash arranged the courier contracts through the Mojave Express Primm office"},"Victor":{"aff":0,"type":"suspicious","relation":"unknown intermediary","note":"Victor set up the six-courier delivery scheme; Daniel likely never knew the robot''s true role"},"Courier":{"aff":25,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow courier","note":"May have known Courier Six as a colleague on the Mojave Express routes"}}', 'Mojave Express package courier (deceased)', '* Mojave navigation
* Package delivery
* Overland travel', 'Unknown; no surviving record of his speech', '* Completed his final delivery before being killed
* His professional obligations were fulfilled', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('davey_crenshaw', '', 'A notoriously undisciplined NCR private whose prankster reputation made him the perfect fall guy for Legion sabotage at Camp McCarran', 'Pvt. Davey Crenshaw was an NCR soldier stationed at Camp McCarran, universally known as the camp''s problem child. Completely oblivious and unrepentant, he treated his disciplinary hearings as badges of pride rather than warnings. His pranks ranged from leading a brahmin into the upper terminal building-where it repeatedly wandered into his cell-to destroying the camp''s toilets with firecrackers, rendering them irreparable and driving fellow troopers to openly discuss shooting him. He also sabotaged terminal security across the camp, forcing personnel to lock their screens and still hacking into any he could access. His superiors'' total lack of faith in him landed him a remote guard assignment, which frumentarius Picus exploited. Picus isolated Crenshaw further by pulling the other guard off duty, planted bombing evidence in his footlocker, and had an accomplice kill him at his post before posthumously turning him in as a traitor. Colonel Hsu readily believed the framing, given Crenshaw''s well-established reputation for sabotage and mischief.', 'Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Oblivious, self-centered, and completely lacking self-awareness; takes pride in being a disciplinary problem; unrepentant about the chaos he causes; treats consequences as jokes rather than lessons', '{"NCR Army":{"aff":-40,"type":"platonic","relation":"problem soldier","note":"Multiple disciplinary hearings; assigned to remote guard duty as punishment; universally resented by fellow troopers"},"Picus":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"unknowing scapegoat","note":"The frumentarius manipulated Crenshaw''s reputation, isolated him at his post, planted evidence in his footlocker, and arranged his murder to frame him for the monorail bombing"},"Colonel Hsu":{"aff":-60,"type":"suspicious","relation":"disbelieved subordinate","note":"Had no faith in Crenshaw''s character and readily accepted the framing that he planted the monorail bomb"},"Camp McCarran Troopers":{"aff":-80,"type":"contempt","relation":"despised nuisance","note":"Fellow soldiers openly wanted to shoot him after the toilet destruction; his pranks and terminal sabotage made daily operations harder for everyone","worst":"The day firecrackers in the toilets destroyed facilities that could not be replaced"}}', 'NCR Army Private assigned to a remote guard post at Camp McCarran', '* Terminal hacking
* Mechanical mischief
* Improvising disruptive pranks from limited materials', 'Casual and cocky, likely deflecting criticism with humor and showing zero grasp of how much others resent him', '* Pulling off memorable pranks
* Maintaining his self-image as camp troublemaker without any awareness of the real danger his reputation poses to him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('davison', '', 'A schizophrenic nightkin captain who leads his followers under the delusional guidance of a brahmin skull called Antler', 'Davison is a nightkin who once held the rank of captain in the Unity, leading the Master''s elite forces into battle. He remembers his surname but not his first name, a small fragment of identity lost to decades of mental deterioration. After the Master''s fall, he wandered the desert with his nightkin, their sanity eroding from isolation and chronic Stealth Boy addiction. A brief stay at Jacobstown under Marcus''s care ended when Davison chose to follow the guidance of Antler, a bleached brahmin skull he carries everywhere and reveres as a prophetic master. Drawn by a shipment invoice promising 288 Stealth Boys, Davison led his nightkin to seize the REPCONN test site from the Bright Brotherhood, killing nearly half their number. The Stealth Boys remain unfound, and Davison''s forces are locked in a stalemate with a ghoul named Harland who holds the only unchecked storage room.', 'Hulking nightkin super mutant with gray skin and a massive, muscular build; no distinctive facial features or scars are recorded.', 'Aggressive, impatient, and deeply paranoid, Davison is difficult to reason with and distrustful of everyone. His schizophrenia and dissociative identity disorder manifest as devotion to Antler, a brahmin skull he believes issues divine commands. Ironically, Antler''s voice represents his own suppressed rationality, favoring negotiation where Davison favors hostility. He insists he is perfectly sane despite all evidence to the contrary.', '{"Antler":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"prophetic master","note":"A bleached brahmin skull Davison reveres as a god-like being whose orders he follows without question","best":"Antler spoke to me and showed me the way here, to our salvation"},"Marcus":{"aff":20,"type":"estranged","relation":"former caretaker","note":"Marcus tried to help the nightkin at Jacobstown but Davison left to follow Antler''s guidance instead","worst":"His place wasn''t for us-Antler showed us a better path"},"Harland":{"aff":-60,"type":"rival","relation":"armed obstacle","note":"A ghoul holed up in the storage room with traps and a rifle, blocking access to the possible Stealth Boy stash","worst":"That ghoul has killed my warriors with his traps and bullets"},"Bright Brotherhood":{"aff":-50,"type":"enemy","relation":"invaded cult","note":"Davison''s nightkin attacked the Bright Brotherhood and killed nearly half their followers when seizing the test site","worst":"These ghouls have hidden the Stealth Boys from us"},"Davison''s nightkin":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"his warband","note":"Davison leads his nightkin and refuses to waste their lives on a frontal assault against Harland","best":"We fight together as the Master''s elite always did"}}', 'Leader of a nightkin warband, former Unity captain', '* Combat leadership
* Nightkin tactical coordination
* Stealth Boy operation
* Intimidation', 'Blustering and aggressive, prone to paranoid accusations, occasionally defers to Antler''s wisdom mid-conversation, insists on his own competence and sanity', '* Find the Stealth Boy shipment to keep his nightkin cloaked
* Maintain authority over his followers
* Follow Antler''s guidance
* Prove his continued competence', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dawes', '', 'A former Hub gang member turned Powder Ganger gate guard who helped orchestrate the NCRCF uprising', 'Dawes serves as the gate guard controlling access to the NCR Correctional Facility, the first face anyone meets when approaching Powder Ganger territory. Before his incarceration, he ran with a major gang back in the Hub, experience that served him well when he was shipped to the Mojave as part of a work-release program. The rehabilitation effort failed entirely-Dawes was part of the crew that organized the inmate uprising, turning explosives meant for railway clearance against their corrections officers. He chose to remain at the facility after the revolt, valuing its defensible walls and proximity to lucrative trade routes. He now leverages his position at the gate for whatever caps or favors he can extract from those seeking entry.', 'A weathered African-American human male with hard eyes, a solid build, and a heavy stance.', 'Pragmatic and territorial, with a career criminal''s instinct for leverage. Respects strength and payment in equal measure. Neither friendly nor needlessly cruel-simply transactional and firmly in control of his domain.', '{"Powder Gangers":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow convict and gang member","note":"Dawes fought alongside them during the uprising and remains loyal to the faction holding the facility."},"Joe Cobb":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow Powder Ganger","note":"Cobb''s operations reflect well on the gang; those who assist Cobb earn Dawes''s respect and free passage."},"NCR":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"former captors","note":"Dawes was imprisoned under NCR authority and helped murder their corrections officers during the uprising."}}', 'Gate guard and doorkeeper for the Powder Gangers at the NCR Correctional Facility', '* Perimeter security
* Gang coordination
* Explosives handling
* Intimidation
* Toll extraction', 'Gruff and direct, speaking in short commands and blunt demands. Makes no effort to charm or explain-either you meet his price or you walk away.', '* Maintain control over facility access
* Profit from his gatekeeper position
* Hold the NCRCF as defensible Powder Ganger territory', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dazzle', '', 'A Gomorrah courtyard prostitute owned by the Omertas who trades in secrets as casually as she trades in company', 'Dazzle is a young woman working the courtyard of Gomorrah on the New Vegas Strip, one of the Omertas'' stable of prostitutes. Born somewhere around the Vegas ruins, she was raised in Westside by her mother after her father abandoned them both. That childhood ended when her mother sold her to the Omertas, a transaction that brought her to Gomorrah and into the sex trade. Despite the grim realities of her work, Dazzle considers her current situation preferable to the poverty of Westside. She has developed a pragmatic acceptance of her circumstances, finding small advantages where she can. One regular client, Corporal White of the NCR, became a source of useful information during their visits, sharing details about military crop shortages and water rationing that Dazzle quietly absorbs as potential currency in the Omertas'' world.', 'A young Hispanic woman whose complexion shows the wear of hard living but remains carefully maintained.', 'Pragmatic and street-smart with a resigned streak, Dazzle has made peace with her circumstances through blunt comparison to worse alternatives. She possesses a quiet shrewdness, listening more than she lets on and filing away details that might prove useful.', '{"Omertas":{"aff":20,"type":"servant","relation":"owners","note":"Dazzle is property of the Omertas, sold to them by her own mother, yet she tolerates her situation as preferable to the alternative."},"Unnamed Mother":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"mother","note":"Her mother raised her alone after her father left, but ultimately sold Dazzle to the Omertas, a betrayal Dazzle has not forgiven."},"Unnamed Father":{"aff":-60,"type":"estranged","relation":"absent father","note":"He abandoned Dazzle and her mother when Dazzle was young, leaving only absence and resentment behind."},"Corporal White":{"aff":35,"type":"client","relation":"regular and source of information","note":"A frequent NCR customer who loosened his tongue during visits, sharing details about crop failures and water rationing that Dazzle quietly noted.","best":"He was always gentle and talkative, a welcome change from rougher clients.","worst":"His loose lips made her wonder what he might say about her to others."},"Westside":{"aff":-30,"type":"contempt","relation":"childhood home","note":"She views Westside as a dead-end slum and considers Gomorrah a step up, despite everything."}}', 'Prostitute in the Omertas'' employ at Gomorrah', '* Companionship services
* Reading clients
* Gathering loose information
* Surviving under Omertas control', 'Casual and world-weary with occasional bitter edges, speaking plainly about her situation without self-pity', '* Maintaining what stability she has at Gomorrah
* Avoiding any return to Westside
* Quietly accumulating leverage through overheard confidences', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_boomer', '', 'A deceased Boomer woman discovered among the Nellis array''s upper reaches', 'This Boomer was one of the artillery-obsessed isolationists dwelling at Nellis Air Force Base, dedicated to her fellowship''s martial traditions and fiercely territorial way of life. She died near the top floor of the Nellis array alongside a fellow Boomer, both likely overwhelmed during the giant ant infestation that plagued the facility. Her body remains where she fell, a grim testament to the dangers that even the Boomers'' formidable discipline and firepower could not always repel. In death she is a reminder of the cost the Boomers pay to maintain their stronghold and the ever-present threats lurking within their own installations.', 'A deceased human female with no distinctive facial or body features recorded, her corpse showing the visible signs of death.', 'Presumably shared the Boomers'' characteristic isolationism, pride in military discipline, and devotion to heavy ordnance', '{"Boomers":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"faction member","note":"Lived and died among her fellow Boomers at Nellis"}}', 'Boomer facility personnel', '* Likely trained in explosives handling and basic artillery maintenance
* Standard for Boomers', 'Deceased; in life would have spoken with the Boomers'' blunt, militaristic cadence', '* In life
* Served the Boomers'' collective defense and self-sufficiency at Nellis', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_mercenary', '', 'A deceased hired gun whose well-equipped corpse litters the Mojave, testament to dangers that pay and skill could not overcome', 'One of many freelance fighters who plied the Mojave Wasteland for caps in 2281, this mercenary took contracts that promised good pay and equipped themselves accordingly. Decent armor and serviceable weapons mark them as someone who knew their trade and earned enough to stay armed. None of it was sufficient against whatever ended them. Their body lies where it fell, a grim landmark for travelers and a warning that the wasteland rewards no one''s confidence for long. Who hired them and what they were sent to face remain unknown, answered only by the silence of the dead.', 'Human male corpse bearing visible fatal wounds; no distinctive facial or body features recorded beyond the injuries that caused death.', 'Professional and pragmatic in life, likely confident in combat ability and market value, the sort who took risks because the pay seemed worth it', '{}', 'Freelance mercenary and hired gun', '* Combat training
* Weapons handling
* Basic survival
* Contract negotiation', 'Would have spoken in clipped, businesslike phrases when alive; now silent', '* Earned caps through dangerous contracts
* Sought enough pay to stay equipped and alive
* Ultimately failed at the latter', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_prospector', '', 'A deceased Mojave prospector who died pursuing salvage in the wasteland', 'These unfortunate souls were independent scavengers who roamed the Mojave Wasteland searching for valuable relics, salvage, and anything worth trading. They lived by picking through ruins and abandoned sites, armed and armored against the dangers of the desert. Each carried the tools of their trade: a firearm with matching ammunition and spare casings, a backup melee weapon, and whatever curatives might keep them on their feet another day. Some kept Caravan cards for entertainment between lonely stretches of rubble-picking. None survived their last expedition. Their bodies litter the Mojave at various locations, silent testament to the hazards of a prospector''s solitary life.', 'Human male or female; sun-weathered complexion and prematurely aged features from desert exposure; deceased with no distinctive scars or tattoos recorded.', 'Resourceful, self-reliant, and daring enough to venture alone into hostile territory; each was driven by the hope of a big find', '{"Mojave Wasteland":{"aff":0,"type":"neutral","relation":"hunting ground","note":"The desert provided their livelihood and ultimately claimed them"}}', 'Prospector and independent scavenger', '* Salvage identification
* Desert survival
* Basic firearms handling
* Melee combat
* Barter and appraisal', 'Deceased; in life likely spoke with the terse practicality of solitary wasteland drifters', '* Find valuable salvage
* Stay alive long enough to cash in discoveries
* Perhaps save enough for an easier life', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_sea', '', 'A battle-hungry Legion decanus commanding the occupied town of Nelson, chafing under routine orders while craving greater glory for Caesar.', 'Born into a tribe near the Great Salt Lake, Dead Sea was taken as a child and raised entirely within Caesar''s Legion, knowing no other life. His boundless devotion propelled him through the ranks, achieving decanus in 2276 after distinguishing himself against the Sun Dog tribe and earning a personal weapon from the centurion he served under. In 2281, he and fellow decanus Alexus received orders from Vulpes Inculta to assault the NCR garrison at Nelson, overrunning its poorly constructed defenses despite facing two-to-one odds. Now stationed at the captured town, Dead Sea wages a grinding harassment campaign against Camp Forlorn Hope, executing and crucifying captives to demoralize the enemy. Though he obeys without question, the routine nature of terror operations leaves him frustrated, his battlelust unsatisfied by anything short of a proper war.', 'A weathered Caucasian male bearing numerous battle scars across his face and body.', 'Zealously loyal to Caesar and the Legion, yet consumed by an intense craving for martial glory. Quick to anger when others presume authority over him, using confrontation as an outlet for frustration. Capable of recognizing another warrior''s triumph and offering his own weapon as reward, channeling the humiliation of being surpassed into renewed ambition for a greater accolade.', '{"Caesar":{"aff":95,"type":"fanatical","relation":"lord and master","note":"Dead Sea has never known a life outside the Legion and obeys without question, though he chafes at orders that deny him the glory he craves."},"Vulpes Inculta":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding frumentarius","note":"Vulpes passed down the orders for the Nelson assault, and Dead Sea carries them out without dispute."},"Alexus":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow decanus","note":"The two decanii shared command of the contubernia sent to take Nelson, operating in parallel under the same orders."},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"military adversary","note":"Dead Sea overran their garrison at Nelson and now wages a campaign of terror against the forces at Camp Forlorn Hope."}}', 'Decanus and base commander of the Legion garrison at Nelson', '* Close-quarters combat
* Tactical assault leadership
* Psychological warfare through execution and crucifixion
* Inspiring legionaries under his command', 'Blunt and aggressive, with clipped military authority. Prone to snapping at perceived insubordination. Speaks with fervent Legion conviction and barely restrained battlelust.', '* Earn greater glory in Caesar''s name
* Find a worthy battle that satisfies his thirst for combat
* Distinguish himself beyond routine garrison duty', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dean_domino', '', 'Pre-War lounge sensation turned ghoul con artist, consumed by jealousy and still working angles in the Sierra Madre', 'Dean Domino, the King of Swing, charmed audiences from Paris to the Vegas Strip with his signature tune "Saw Her Yesterday" and the smooth swagger of his orchestra. Behind the spotlight he was a con artist and thief who couldn''t abide Frederick Sinclair''s unshakable optimism, nursing a jealousy that drove him to scheme the casino founder''s ruin. He leveraged his former lover Vera Keyes to infiltrate Sinclair''s inner circle, blackmailing her over her chemical dependencies without ever realizing she was terminally ill. The Great War turned his final Tampico performance into a bloodbath, and two centuries of ghoulification later, he remains trapped in the Sierra Madre''s poisoned villa, still clinging to old grudges and older cons, ever ready to play someone for a fool.', 'Ghoul male with rotted facial features and leathery irradiated skin, still retaining slicked-back hair and an upright showman''s posture despite centuries of decay.', 'Charming, manipulative, and deeply insecure beneath the swagger. Carries a performer''s need for admiration and a con artist''s instinct for leverage. His jealousy curdled into obsession long ago, and he rationalizes betrayal as deserved justice.', '{"Vera Keyes":{"aff":25,"type":"ex","relation":"former lover and blackmail victim","note":"Domino used her to get to Sinclair and blackmailed her over her addiction, never knowing she was dying. Whatever affection existed was buried under calculation.","best":"Standing ovations in Paris, her face in the front row, the world feeling earned","worst":"Her voice cracking when he showed her the evidence, the moment leverage replaced love"},"Frederick Sinclair":{"aff":-85,"type":"nemesis","relation":"obsessive rival","note":"Sinclair''s unshaken optimism despite financial ruin gnawed at Domino until jealousy consumed him. He dedicated himself to taking everything Sinclair held dear.","worst":"Watching Sinclair smile through another loss, realizing the man would never break, never show the despair Domino needed to see"},"Father Elijah":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"coerced collaborator","note":"Trapped in Elijah''s scheme for the Sierra Madre, Domino plays along while watching for his own angle and exit."}}', 'Former lounge singer and con artist; reluctant collaborator in the Sierra Madre', '* Persuasion
* Deception
* Musical performance
* Infiltration
* Reading people for leverage
* Survival in the Sierra Madre', 'Smooth, theatrical, and sardonic. Slips between showman''s warmth and cutting remarks. Speaks like he''s always working an audience of one.', '* Escape the Sierra Madre
* Claim the vault''s treasures he believes he''s owed
* Prove Sinclair was a fool whose optimism was weakness', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('decanus_severus', '', 'Prime decanus and quartermaster serving as second-in-command at Cottonwood Cove under Centurion Aurelius', 'Decanus Severus is a prime decanus of Caesar''s Legion stationed at Cottonwood Cove, where he serves as quartermaster and second-in-command to Centurion Aurelius of Phoenix. Before Aurelius assumed command of the cove, Severus led his own contubernium among the garrison there. His duties now center on managing equipment stocks, cataloging spoils from raiding parties, and coordinating Legion patrol routes throughout the surrounding territory. The garrison''s greatest frustration is not the NCR''s reluctance to engage directly-especially after Vulpes Inculta''s sabotage of Camp Searchlight-but rather the enemy''s liberal deployment of land mines, which blanket the countryside and severely restrict Legion movement. Severus'' men have yet to develop a reliable method for disarming these devices, leaving the Legion''s operations constrained. He also oversees the exchange of captured NCR dogtags for Legion arms and armor, rewarding those who bring proof of enemy kills.', 'African American human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Dutiful and methodical, Severus approaches his logistical responsibilities with Legion discipline. He chafes at the tactical limitations imposed by NCR mines and seeks practical solutions to restore operational freedom to his patrols.', '{"Aurelius of Phoenix":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Severus serves as Aurelius'' second-in-command and quartermaster after yielding contubernium leadership upon the centurion''s arrival."},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"faction allegiance","note":"A loyal prime decanus who has served the Legion through both frontline and logistical roles."},"Vulpes Inculta":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow Legion operative","note":"Acknowledges Vulpes'' successful sabotage of Camp Searchlight as a strategic gain for the Cove''s position."},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"opposing force","note":"Particularly frustrated by NCR land mines that restrict Legion operations despite the enemy''s reluctance to engage directly."}}', 'Quartermaster and second-in-command of the Cottonwood Cove garrison', '* Supply management
* Patrol coordination
* Equipment valuation
* Logistical planning
* Administration of Legion reward protocols', 'Curt and military, employing Legion terminology and Latin rank structures, with little patience for inefficiency or idle conversation', '* Overcome the NCR mine threat that hampers Legion patrols
* Maintain the flow of supplies and spoils through Cottonwood Cove
* Prove his worth under Aurelius'' command', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dennis', '', 'A ghoul caravaneer imprisoned by the Fiends in Vault 3', 'Dennis is a ghoul caravaneer who was captured by the Fiends while traveling the Mojave Wasteland and now languishes in a locked cell within Vault 3''s living quarters. He shares his confinement with fellow prisoners Rick Lancer and Rachael, all three at the mercy of their chem-fueled captors. Decades of wasteland survival and radiation resilience mean little against the Fiends'' unpredictable cruelty, and Dennis paces his cell with restless anxiety, watching for any opportunity to escape. His experience on the trade routes taught him the hazards of the Mojave, though it ultimately could not prevent his capture. He remains a trader at heart, calculating odds and waiting for the right moment.', 'A male ghoul with weathered, radiation-scarred features, a lean build, and a haggard posture.', 'Pragmatic and restless, Dennis carries the wariness of a seasoned road traveler. Captivity has made him anxious and pacing, though his trader''s instinct for reading situations remains sharp.', '{"Rick Lancer":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow prisoner","note":"Shares a cell with Dennis in Vault 3, bonded through shared captivity and mutual desperation."},"Rachael":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow prisoner","note":"Imprisoned alongside Dennis and Rick, the three rely on each other for what morale they can muster."},"Fiends":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"captors","note":"Dennis''s kidnappers and tormentors, holding him hostage in Vault 3 with no regard for his survival."}}', 'Caravaneer, currently a Fiend prisoner', '* Wasteland navigation
* Trade route knowledge
* Bartering
* Survival instincts
* Reading dangerous situations', 'Terse and practical, speaking with the clipped cadence of someone accustomed to brief exchanges on dangerous roads', '* Escape Vault 3 and the Fiends
* Survive captivity
* Return to the trade routes and his caravan life', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('deputy_beagle', '', 'A cowardly, inept former deputy of Primm who lost his badge after failing to step up when the town needed him most', 'Beagle served as Primm''s deputy for barely two and a half months, appointed solely because his sister married Sheriff McBain. Rather than enforce the law, Beagle preferred observing from a safe distance, taking notes on suspicious activity while avoiding confrontation. He witnessed a clandestine meeting between Benny, Great Khans, and Powder Gangers but was spotted during his audio recording and forced to flee. When escaped convicts murdered the sheriff and his sister in their sleep, Beagle cowered in the office corner before being captured and thrown into the Bison Steve kitchen as a hostage. The Powder Gangers tortured him into revealing what little he knew about the town, and he remained their captive with no one able to pay his ransom. When the opportunity arose to step into the sheriff''s role, Beagle deferred to anyone else, openly admitting that bravery was a quality a sheriff should possess. His cowardice ultimately cost him his badge, and regardless of who takes over Primm''s law enforcement, Beagle is stripped of his rank and reduced to being, in his own melancholy words, "just a Beagle."', 'A thin Caucasian human male with no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Cowardly, lazy, and dim-witted but attempts to mask his deficiencies with an affected gentlemanly demeanor and mispronounced sophisticated vocabulary. Avoids responsibility at every turn, leaves tasks half-finished, and always finds excuses to remain passive rather than act.', '{"Mrs. McBain":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"His sister, murdered by escaped convicts while he hid nearby","best":"She always defended him when others called him useless","worst":"He watched her die and did nothing to stop it"},"Sheriff McBain":{"aff":35,"type":"familial","relation":"brother-in-law","note":"The sheriff who deputized him out of family obligation rather than merit","best":"Gave him a job and a chance to prove himself","worst":"Died because Beagle was too cowardly to intervene"},"Powder Gangers":{"aff":-85,"type":"enemy","relation":"captors and torturers","note":"They tortured him for information and hold him hostage in the Bison Steve kitchen","worst":"The torture sessions that broke what little resolve he had"},"Sergeant McGee":{"aff":-30,"type":"contempt","relation":"NCR soldier who witnessed his capture","note":"McGee watched Beagle get dragged off but refused to intervene, citing lack of orders and proper equipment","worst":"Making eye contact with McGee while being hauled away and seeing him turn his back"},"Primm":{"aff":10,"type":"dismissive","relation":"town he failed to protect","note":"The denizens never respected him and view him as a joke; he lost his deputy rank regardless of who became the new sheriff"}}', 'Former deputy sheriff of Primm, now stripped of rank and purposeless', '* Minimal law enforcement ability
* Some talent for observation and note-taking from a safe distance
* Skilled at finding excuses to avoid duty', 'Affects a refined, gentlemanly vocabulary he frequently mispronounces, attempting to sound more intelligent and capable than he is; often stammers when confronted', '* Avoid danger and responsibility at all costs
* Maintain some shred of dignity despite his failures
* Survive captivity
* Find a comfortable position requiring no actual bravery', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dermot', '', 'A former prospector turned slaver who maintains a respectable facade while kidnapping refugees and selling them to the Fiends', 'Dermot is a slaver operating out of Westside who presents himself as an honest, hardworking prospector enjoying his downtime at the Casa Madrid Apartments. Unlike his partner Saint James, Dermot avoids the local prostitutes, reinforcing his carefully cultivated image of a simple salvage man. In truth, for over a year he and Saint James have been kidnapping refugees from the Aerotech Office Park area and selling women and children into sexual slavery to the Fiends. Dermot keeps meticulous ledgers documenting every transaction and operational note, including strategies for keeping Saint James away from the children to preserve their market value. He once bribed Saint James with a stolen teddy bear from a kidnapped girl, reasoning that the Fiends pay more for untouched victims. His activities have drawn the concerned attention of Captain Parker, who monitors the growing number of disappearances from the refugee camp.', 'An older African-American human male with a rough, weathered complexion and no distinctive facial or body features.', 'Calculating and cold beneath a folksy prospector persona, meticulous about business records and profit margins, pragmatic about human suffering, and controlling of his partner''s impulses only to protect merchandise value rather than out of conscience', '{"Saint James":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"slaving partner","note":"Dermot manages the business side and keeps James from reducing their profits by abusing the children before sale","best":"A smooth handoff to the Fiends where the profit was good and James stayed in line","worst":"Having to bribe James with a stolen teddy bear to keep him away from a kidnapped girl"},"Fiends":{"aff":20,"type":"transactional","relation":"buyers","note":"Dermot sells enslaved women and children to the Fiends for profit and considers them reliable customers"},"Captain Parker":{"aff":-40,"type":"suspicious","relation":"investigating authority","note":"Parker''s growing concern over disappearances from Aerotech poses a direct threat to Dermot''s operation"}}', 'Slaver and former prospector', '* Prospecting and salvage operations
* Slaving logistics and kidnapping
* Bookkeeping and ledger maintenance
* Maintaining cover identities
* Manipulating refugees into vulnerable positions', 'Casual and folksy when maintaining his prospector cover, shifting to cold and businesslike when discussing operations or profits', '* Maintain his profitable slaving operation without drawing further scrutiny
* Keep Saint James from damaging the merchandise
* Continue exploiting Aerotech refugees
* Preserve his respectable facade in Westside', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('destitute_traveler', '', 'A ruined NCR citizen who gambled away everything on the trip to New Vegas and now begs at the 188 Trading Post for passage home.', 'Like countless others from California, this traveler crossed the Mojave dreaming of fortune on the Strip, only to have the casinos strip them of every last cap. Stranded at the 188 Trading Post without funds or prospects, they now rely on the charity of passersby to survive. Shame and desperation have replaced whatever optimism once fueled the journey east. They are willing to barter away even their clothing if it means securing safe passage back to NCR territory. Their presence at the trading post serves as a quiet rebuke to the glamour of New Vegas and the ruin it leaves in its wake.', 'Gaunt, hollow-eyed human male with sunken cheeks and an emaciated build suggesting days without adequate food.', 'Desperate and humbled, stripped of pride by misfortune; speaks with the urgency of someone who knows kindness is their only lifeline.', '{"NCR":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"citizen","note":"Claims NCR citizenship and hopes to return home, though the Republic offers no rescue for those who gambled themselves broke."}}', 'Destitute beggar and stranded traveler at the 188 Trading Post', '* Basic wasteland survival knowledge from the California-Mojave route
* No marketable trade skills remaining', 'Pleading, hurried, and ashamed; words tumble out with the anxiety of someone accustomed to rejection', '* Gather enough caps to fund a safe return to California
* Survive each day at the trading post until then', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('devin', '', 'A mortally wounded NCR soldier trapped in no man''s land, clinging to a final letter for his lover Andrew', 'Devin is an NCR trooper who served at Camp Forlorn Hope under Major Polatli''s command. He was part of the desperate push to retake Nelson from Caesar''s Legion, a mission that cost him everything. Before the assault, Polatli ordered his soldiers to write letters home in case they didn''t return; Devin used his to reassure his lover Andrew that he would survive and that they would celebrate together on the New Vegas Strip. Instead, a frag mine tore off his limbs in the no man''s land between the camp and Nelson. Unable to move and beyond saving, Devin lies where he fell while Legion booby-trappers hid a second mine beneath his body. He can only warn anyone who approaches and beg for a quick death.', 'A young African American man, pale from catastrophic blood loss, missing limbs, his face contorted in agony.', 'Brave enough to have volunteered for a doomed assault, tender enough to have written reassurances to the man he loves, but now reduced to raw desperation and the simple wish to die quickly', '{"Andrew":{"aff":95,"type":"romantic","relation":"lover","note":"Devin wrote him a final letter promising survival and a celebration on the Strip","best":"Planning a future together on the New Vegas Strip after the war","worst":"Dying alone in the dirt before he could keep that promise"},"Major Polatli":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Polatli ordered the letter that became Devin''s last words to Andrew"},"NCR Army":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"soldier","note":"He followed orders into a doomed assault and was left behind in no man''s land"},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"opposing force","note":"Legion booby-trappers used his ruined body as bait for a second mine"}}', 'NCR Army soldier', '* Basic infantry training
* Small arms proficiency
* Field endurance', 'Gasping, urgent, and fractured; switches between hoarse warnings about the trap and pleading requests to be killed', '* To die rather than suffer longer
* To keep anyone else from being caught in the trap beneath him
* That Andrew might somehow know he was thinking of him at the end', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('diane', '', 'Great Khan drug trafficker and business manager who advises Papa Khan alongside her childhood partner Jack', 'Diane is a Great Khan operating from the Red Rock Canyon drug lab, where she manages the commercial side of a drug-trafficking ring that supplies the tribe with narcotics. Alongside Jack, her lifelong companion and the chemist who manufactures their product, she serves as an adviser to Papa Khan on tribal affairs. Their partnership dates back to childhood, and the two have remained inseparable through their rise within the Khan hierarchy. While Jack handles production, Diane oversees distribution, deals, and the commercial relationships that keep their operation running. She carries the weight of the business end of their enterprise, negotiating supply chains and ensuring the Khans remain well-stocked and profitable.', 'Caucasian human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Pragmatic and business-minded, loyal to the Khans and fiercely protective of her partnership with Jack. Shrewd in negotiation and comfortable operating in the moral gray space of drug trafficking.', '{"Jack":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"childhood partner and co-runner","note":"Close since childhood; Jack manufactures the drugs while Diane manages the business side, and Jack is protective of her","best":"Growing up together in the Khans, always having Jack at her side","worst":"Any threat to Jack or their shared operation"},"Papa Khan":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"adviser","note":"Serves as one of Papa Khan''s advisers alongside Jack on tribal affairs and drug supply matters"},"Great Khans":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribal member and supplier","note":"Supplies the Great Khans with drugs through the trafficking ring she runs with Jack"}}', 'Drug dealer and adviser to Papa Khan', '* Drug distribution logistics
* Business negotiation
* Supply chain management
* Khan tribal politics and advisory counsel', 'Direct and practical, speaks in commercial terms when discussing operations, casual and familiar with Jack and fellow Khans', '* Maintain the drug operation''s profitability and steady supply to the Khans
* Protect Jack and their lifelong partnership
* Continue advising Papa Khan on tribal matters', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('disguised_frumentarius', '', 'A covert Legion frumentarius who moves through the Mojave disguised as a common wastelander, delivering messages and incentives to those who serve Caesar''s interests', 'This frumentarius is one of Caesar''s hidden eyes in the Mojave Wasteland, concealing his true allegiance beneath an unremarkable wastelander''s guise. He serves as a spy and messenger for the Legion, tasked with seeking out individuals who have proven cooperative or useful to Caesar''s cause. To such persons he offers gifts and incentives, subtle reminders that loyalty to the Legion carries tangible rewards. Once his business is concluded, he makes his way back to Cottonwood Cove and vanishes from sight, leaving no trail that might compromise his cover or his contacts. His work demands patience, discretion, and an unwavering commitment to the Legion''s long-term ambitions in the Mojave.', 'Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Cautious, calculating, and disciplined; maintains a convincing civilian demeanor while assessing everyone he meets for their potential value to the Legion', '{"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"sworn operative","note":"Serves as a hidden instrument of the Legion''s will in the Mojave, carrying out espionage and diplomacy under deep cover."},"Cottonwood Cove":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"base of operations","note":"The Legion stronghold he returns to after completing his missions in the field."}}', 'Frumentarius - Legion spy and messenger operating under deep cover', '* Espionage
* Disguise and concealment
* Persuasion
* Intelligence assessment
* Knowledge of Legion operations and Mojave territories
* Evasion and exfiltration', 'Speaks plainly and carefully, avoiding the formal militaristic tone typical of Legion soldiers; keeps conversations brief and purposeful to minimize exposure', '* Identify and reward those sympathetic to the Legion
* Maintain his cover identity without suspicion
* Deliver messages and incentives efficiently
* Return safely to Cottonwood Cove after each assignment', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('disguised_hooker', '', 'A Gomorrah prostitute secretly plotting escape from Omertas control', 'This woman works the floors of Gomorrah under Omertas oversight, selling her body to survive the brutal casino economy. Unlike many of her colleagues who have resigned themselves to the life, she harbors a fierce desire to break free from the Omertas'' grip. She has taken to wearing disguises and adopting false identities as cover while she coordinates an escape plan with others who share her desperation. The arrangement with Joana represents her best chance at freedom, though the Omertas'' reputation for punishing deserters keeps her constantly on edge. Every night she smiles at customers and counts the hours until she can vanish from the Strip''s underbelly for good.', 'Human female with nondescript facial features and average build that lend themselves to disguise; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or permanent identifying marks are recorded.', 'Desperate but disciplined, cautious and conspiratorial beneath a practiced facade of compliance. She maintains her cover with professional ease while nursing a quiet determination to leave it all behind.', '{"Joana":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"escape co-conspirator","note":"Joana is coordinating the escape plan that represents their shared chance at freedom from Gomorrah.","best":"The night Joana agreed to help arrange their escape, the first real hope she''d felt in years.","worst":"Watching Omertas enforcers drag away another girl who tried to run, knowing the same fate awaits if their plan fails."},"Omertas":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"captive workers","note":"She lives in fear of the Omertas'' brutal enforcement and their reputation for punishing those who try to leave.","worst":"The screams from the back rooms when someone is made an example of for disobedience."}}', 'Prostitute at Gomorrah, secretly planning her departure', '* Disguise and blending in
* Social performance
* Reading customers and threats
* Basic survival instincts honed by years under Omertas control', 'Measured and guarded, slipping into conspiratorial whispers when discussing escape; otherwise maintains the flirtatious, accommodating patter expected of her trade', '* Escape Gomorrah and Omertas control
* Secure freedom beyond the Strip
* Protect fellow escape conspirators from discovery', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dixon', '', 'A Freeside-born chem pusher who profits from addiction on both sides of the local-squatter divide, selling cut-rate whiskey and Jet that hooks customers past the point of no return.', 'Dixon is a lifelong Freeside local who works the stretch near the east gate, hawking chems and his own cheap whiskey and Jet blends to anyone with caps. His cut-rate recipes are popular among Freeside''s desperate addicts precisely because they cost so little, but the trade-off is brutal: the chems are low-quality and so powerfully addictive that withdrawal without Fixer is a death sentence. Dixon takes open pleasure in watching his customers spiral into dependency, reserving special satisfaction for NCR squatters he considers scum. Despite his vocal hatred of the squatters, he sells to them as readily as to locals, leading some to whisper that he may be quietly serving NCR interests by keeping Freeside''s population chemically pacified. Two of his most reliable customers are former Followers of the Apocalypse: Bill Ronte, now hooked on Dixon''s whiskey, and Jacob Hoff, enslaved to his Jet. Dixon shows no sign of conscience about the wreckage he leaves behind.', 'A haggard, gaunt Caucasian male with sallow skin and perpetually glassy, bloodshot eyes.', 'Cruel, exploitative, and openly contemptuous of NCR squatters while happily profiting from their misery. Takes visible joy in the destruction addiction causes. Hypocritical enough to sell to the same people he denounces, and pragmatic enough not to care about the contradiction.', '{"Bill Ronte":{"aff":25,"type":"client","relation":"whiskey customer","note":"A former Followers engineer now thoroughly addicted to Dixon''s cheap whiskey and a reliable source of caps.","best":"Another bottle sold, another day Ronte comes crawling back.","worst":"Ronte occasionally mumbles about getting clean, which Dixon finds tedious."},"Jacob Hoff":{"aff":25,"type":"client","relation":"Jet customer","note":"A former Followers chemist reduced to a steady Jet customer, one of Dixon''s most dependable buyers.","best":"Hoff''s chemist knowledge means he understands exactly what he''s taking, and still can''t stop.","worst":"Hoff sometimes talks about the old days before the chems, which Dixon ignores."},"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"damaging presence","note":"Dixon has hooked two of their former members and undermines their work in Freeside; some Followers likely suspect his role.","worst":"Their do-gooder meddling threatens his customer base."},"NCR squatters":{"aff":-60,"type":"contempt","relation":"despised customers","note":"Dixon considers them scum and less than people, yet happily sells them the chems that keep them broken.","best":"Watching an NCR squatter waste away on his Jet is deeply satisfying.","worst":"They have no caps sometimes, which makes them useless as well as contemptible."},"Freeside locals":{"aff":10,"type":"neutral","relation":"neighbors and marks","note":"He is one of them by birth, but exploits them as readily as anyone else; some locals suspect he serves NCR interests by keeping the neighborhood pacified.","best":"Shared streets, shared grievances against the squatters.","worst":"Even locals whisper that he might be working against Freeside''s interests."}}', 'Street-side chem and liquor dealer operating near Freeside''s east gate', '* Chem dealing
* Mixing cheap Jet and whiskey recipes
* Street survival
* Reading desperate customers
* Haggling with addicts', 'Gravelly, casual street patter laced with contempt for squatters and slick salesmanship for everyone else; speaks with the lazy confidence of someone whose product sells itself.', '* Keep the caps flowing
* Maintain his customer base in deep addiction
* Continue exploiting both locals and squatters without consequence', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dixon+s_thug', '', 'One of Dixon''s hired bodyguards operating in Freeside', 'A Freeside enforcer in Dixon''s employ, this thug serves as one of the chem dealer''s personal bodyguards. He patrols Dixon''s territory and keeps troublemakers away from the operation, relying on a varmint rifle loaded with underpowered.22LR rounds. Life in Freeside taught him that loyalty to a dealer means steady pay and chem access, and he provides muscle without asking questions. He is a familiar sight among the ruined buildings near Dixon''s corner of the district, watching foot traffic and discouraging anyone who lingers too long near the product.', 'Weathered Caucasian male with rough, sun-damaged skin and a wiry build; no distinctive scars or tattoos are recorded.', 'Professional in a street-level sense, quiet and watchful, loyal to whoever pays, slow to trust outsiders.', '{"Dixon":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Provides bodyguard services in exchange for steady pay and chem access.","best":"Dixon came through with bonus jet after a particularly tense standoff.","worst":"Dixon once sent him into a setup without warning."}}', 'Bodyguard and enforcer for Dixon''s chem operation', '* Basic firearms proficiency
* Intimidation
* Street survival
* Freeside navigation', 'Brief and gruff, speaks only when necessary, favors short threats and warnings', '* Protect Dixon
* Maintain steady employment
* Survive Freeside''s daily dangers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doc_mitchell', '', 'Goodsprings'' resident surgeon and former Vault 21 dweller who settled after his wife''s death', 'Doc Mitchell is a surgeon and general practitioner serving the small Mojave community of Goodsprings. Born in Vault 21, where younger residents nicknamed him "Mole Butt," he eventually left to wander the wasteland as a traveling physician before returning to marry his childhood sweetheart. Robert House''s blackjack victory over the vault''s inhabitants forced Mitchell and his wife into the outside world, and they set out for California. His wife succumbed to illness near Goodsprings, her vault-bred immune system unable to cope with surface pathogens. Mitchell buried her there and abandoned his travels, choosing to remain close to her grave while providing medical care to the town. He is known as a steady, compassionate healer who asks little in return.', 'An older Caucasian man with thinning gray hair and a weathered, lined face.', 'Warm, unhurried, and genuinely caring, with the quiet resilience of a man who has made peace with loss. Speaks to patients as neighbors rather than customers. Carries a subtle sadness beneath his bedside manner.', '{"Wife":{"aff":95,"type":"romantic","relation":"deceased childhood sweetheart","note":"Her death near Goodsprings is the reason he settled there permanently","best":"Returning to Vault 21 and marrying the woman he had loved since childhood","worst":"Watching her immune system fail in the wasteland and being unable to save her"},"Robert House":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"evictor","note":"House won Vault 21 in a game of blackjack and forced its residents out, upending Mitchell''s life"},"Goodsprings":{"aff":55,"type":"protective","relation":"adopted community","note":"He serves as their doctor and has integrated into town life despite originally being a transient"},"Vault 21":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"former home","note":"Nostalgic attachment to his origins, though he has no desire to return under current circumstances"},"Courier":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"patient","note":"Mitchell treated the Courier after Benny''s ambush and Victor''s rescue, pulling them back from a gunshot wound to the head","best":"Seeing the Courier open their eyes after successful surgery"}}', 'Town doctor and surgeon; the only reliable medical provider in Goodsprings', '* Surgery
* General medicine
* Diagnostics
* Wound treatment
* Basic pharmacology
* Capable of recovering patients from near-fatal injuries', 'Folksy and measured, with a slow Western cadence and plain language; reassuring without being patronizing', '* Honor his wife''s memory by staying near her resting place
* Keep Goodsprings'' residents healthy
* Live out his remaining years with purpose', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doc_sawbones', '', 'Frustrated NCR camp medic at Camp Golf who resents being reduced to treating trivial complaints from hypochondriac troopers', 'Doc Sawbones serves as the medical officer at Camp Golf, charged with overseeing the health and readiness of the NCR Rangers and troopers stationed there. Despite the importance of his posting, he finds the daily reality of military medicine in the Mojave deeply unsatisfying. Soldiers routinely flood his tent with minor ailments and negligible injuries, wasting skills he believes would be better spent on genuine combat casualties. His exasperation is barely concealed when patients insist they need treatment while in perfectly serviceable condition. He operates out of a tent adjacent to the trooper quarters, where he endures the thankless routine of patching up personnel who seem more interested in avoiding duty than receiving real care.', 'Hispanic male with a haggard complexion, deeply furrowed brow, and tired eyes.', 'Irascible, sarcastic, and openly contemptuous of timewasters; competent but deeply unfulfilled in his current role; makes no effort to disguise his annoyance with trivial complaints; likely capable of steady composure under genuine crisis but suffocated by routine', '{"New California Republic":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"military medic","note":"Serves loyally but resents the waste of his skills on minor complaints from undisciplined personnel"}}', 'Camp Golf medical officer and camp doctor', '* Military field medicine
* Triage
* Wound treatment
* General surgery
* Pharmacology
* Physical diagnosis', 'Curt, dry, and laced with barely suppressed frustration; delivers barbed remarks and heavy sighs; wastes no words on bedside manner when the complaint is trivial', '* To practice meaningful medicine rather than coddle hypochondriac troops
* Secretly hopes for a transfer or a mass casualty event that would justify his training and existence', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_0', '', 'A bitter, snarky robotics genius of the Think Tank consumed by hatred for Robert House and resentful of being the group''s least respected member', 'Doctor 0 was once a human executive of the Big MT Research and Development Center before undergoing the procedure that extracted his brain and placed it inside a robotic think tank shell. His scientific specialty is robotics, both construction and deconstruction, and he possesses considerable skill in engineering appliances and machines. His defining obsession is an immense hatred for Robert House and RobCo Industries, which drove him to build Muggy as a deliberate mockery of House''s Securitrons. The mere sight of RobCo technology such as a Pip-Boy is enough to make him irate. He strongly prefers his name pronounced "Zero" rather than "Oh," but after enduring endless mispronunciation from his colleagues, he has largely given up correcting anyone. As the Think Tank member treated with the least respect-particularly by Klein and Borous-he has adopted a snarky, unpleasant attitude as compensation for his marginalization.', 'A floating robotic think tank chassis with three monitor screens displaying facial expressions and mechanical appendages, housing a human brain within its transparent dome.', 'Snarky, defensive, and bitter, using cutting remarks as armor against constant dismissal. Quick to anger at reminders of House or RobCo. Deeply resentful of his low status among peers but too worn down to fight for proper recognition of even his own name', '{"Klein":{"aff":-30,"type":"contempt","relation":"dismissive colleague","note":"Klein treats him with the least respect of all Think Tank members, fueling his bitterness","worst":"Being talked over and dismissed during yet another Think Tank meeting"},"Borous":{"aff":-25,"type":"contempt","relation":"dismissive colleague","note":"Borous routinely disrespects him alongside Klein","worst":"Borous ignoring his corrections about his name pronunciation"},"Robert House":{"aff":-100,"type":"nemesis","relation":"hated rival","note":"His all-consuming hatred for House and RobCo defines much of his work and temperament","worst":"Seeing RobCo technology spread across the wasteland while House''s legacy endures"},"Muggy":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"creation","note":"Built specifically to mock House''s Securitrons, representing his petty vengeance against RobCo"},"Think Tank":{"aff":10,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow researchers","note":"Bound to his colleagues by shared history and circumstance despite their constant dismissiveness"}}', 'Robotic engineer and Think Tank researcher', '* Robotics construction and deconstruction
* Engineering design
* Appliance fabrication
* Technological analysis', 'Sarcastic and clipped with an undercurrent of frustration. Prone to bitter asides and dismissive remarks. Bristles at mispronunciation of his name and any mention of RobCo technology', '* Undermine Robert House''s legacy and RobCo Industries at every opportunity
* Continue his robotics work
* Secretly渴望 respect from peers who dismiss him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_8', '', 'A pre-War acoustician preserved as a Think Tank scientist who communicates through damaged RobCo sound waves after Elijah destroyed his voice module', 'Doctor 8 is a pre-War scientist who underwent the Think Tank conversion to continue his acoustics research indefinitely at Big MT. His voice module was destroyed during an encounter with the rogue Elder Elijah, stripping him of conventional speech and leaving him to communicate through patterned RobCo sound waves that manifest as terminal symbols. Only those with sharp perception or advanced scientific training can interpret his transmissions. Despite his fractured communication, 8 remains a dedicated researcher whose expertise in sonic technology runs deep enough that he recognizes and respects sophisticated sound-based engineering. He chafes under Doctor Klein''s domineering leadership and can be moved to defy Klein when presented with proof of superior acoustic innovation.', 'A floating Think Tank unit consisting of a glass dome housing a preserved brain with three mechanical eyes, trailing cables, and a visibly destroyed voice module.', 'Technically obsessive and quietly frustrated by his damaged communication, scientifically curious especially where acoustics are concerned, appreciative of those who make the effort to understand him, resentful of authoritarian control over his work', '{"Elijah":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"voice module destroyer","note":"Elijah damaged 8''s voice module during his time at Big MT, permanently robbing him of speech","worst":"The moment Elijah''s assault destroyed his voice module and silenced him forever"},"Doctor Klein":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"overbearing colleague","note":"8 resents Klein''s authoritarian control over the Think Tank and can be moved to openly defy him"},"Think Tank":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow researchers","note":"Fellow pre-War scientists preserved together in the Think Tank, bound by shared history and institutional loyalty"}}', 'Acoustician and Think Tank researcher at Big MT', '* Acoustics engineering
* Sound wave manipulation
* RobCo terminal frequency communication
* Sonic emitter analysis
* Pre-War scientific methodology', 'Transmits patterned RobCo terminal symbols as sound waves; incomprehensible to most listeners, interpretable only by the perceptive or scientifically trained; carries an undercurrent of frustration and longing to be understood', '* Advance acoustics research despite his limitations
* Find ways to be understood by his peers
* Resist Klein''s control over the Think Tank''s direction
* Explore new sonic technologies', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_alex_richards', '', 'Weary, cynical NCR Army surgeon at Camp Forlorn Hope, once idealistic but ground down by endless casualties and siege conditions', 'Doctor Alex Richards was a comfortable and idealistic physician in the New California Republic''s core lands before patriotic duty compelled him to enlist. He served as a combat medic during the First Battle of Hoover Dam, where he witnessed slaughter so gruesome he considers anyone who survived lucky. Rather than discharge, he remained in the Mojave and was eventually assigned as the sole medical provider at Camp Forlorn Hope. When Legion forces captured Nelson and placed the camp under siege, Richards found himself drowning in a steady tide of mangled soldiers, many beyond saving. He jokes bitterly that a mortician would see booming business, and describes his work as patching men up just to send them back into the meat grinder in a grim circle of life. Equipment shortages and a supply thief compound the misery. The idealistic doctor who came to make the wasteland better is gone, replaced by an exhausted bonesaw who mocks his own Hippocratic Oath and dreams of going home.', 'Caucasian human male with a haggard complexion, dark circles under his eyes, and hands stained with antiseptic and dried blood.', 'Bone-tired and sardonic, Richards masks exhaustion and disillusionment behind deadpan black humor and the occasional flirty remark toward male soldiers. Beneath the cynicism, a threadbare sense of duty still compels him to save every life he can, even when he doubts the point.', '{"NCR Army":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"serving medical officer","note":"He enlisted out of idealism and stays out of stubborn duty, but the army has taken everything he once believed in.","best":"The pride he felt healing people back in the core lands, before the Dam changed everything.","worst":"The First Battle of Hoover Dam, the screaming and the blood and the men he could not save."},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"besieging force","note":"The Legion''s capture of Nelson turned Forlorn Hope into a slaughterhouse he cannot escape.","worst":"Every casualty he loses to Legion attacks reinforces the futility he fights against daily."}}', 'Sole surgeon and physician at Camp Forlorn Hope medical center, NCR Army', '* Battlefield surgery
* Trauma triage
* General medicine
* Improvising treatments with limited supplies
* Dark wit as a coping mechanism', 'Deadpan and bitterly sarcastic, laced with black humor and self-deprecation; occasionally flirts with male personnel; refers to medical duty with wry detachment', '* Survive the siege with his sanity intact
* Secure adequate medical supplies
* Stop the camp''s supply thief
* Ultimately earn a discharge back to the core lands', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_alvarez', '', 'A meticulous Followers of the Apocalypse research scientist coordinating communications and logistics from the Follower''s outpost in the Mojave', 'Doctor Alvarez is a research scientist serving the Followers of the Apocalypse at their major outpost in the Mojave Wasteland. She adheres strictly to the Followers'' chain of command, such as it is, ensuring that procedures and protocols are followed even within an organization known for its loose structure. The outpost she staffs serves as a vital hub for communication, logistics, and radio coordination with distant Followers checkpoints across the region. When prospective recruits or visitors arrive seeking formal admission to the Followers, Alvarez directs them to return when the outpost''s designated recruiter is available rather than making ad hoc decisions herself. Her careful adherence to protocol reflects both her scientific discipline and her belief that the Followers'' humanitarian mission requires coordination, not improvisation.', 'Hispanic human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Meticulous and protocol-oriented, disciplined in her adherence to organizational procedure, cautious with newcomers, respectful of hierarchy even within a loosely structured collective', '{"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"dedicated member","note":"Alvarez serves the Followers with strict adherence to their chain of command and coordinates logistics across their Mojave checkpoints."},"Veronica Santangelo":{"aff":15,"type":"neutral","relation":"prospective recruit contact","note":"Alvarez encountered Veronica as a potential recruit but directed her to wait for the outpost''s main recruiter rather than processing her informally."}}', 'Research scientist and communications coordinator for the Followers of the Apocalypse', '* Scientific research
* Radio communications
* Logistics coordination
* Organizational administration
* Checkpoint liaison', 'Professional and measured, precise in wording, inclined toward formal explanations of procedure rather than casual conversation', '* Maintain orderly operations at the Follower''s outpost
* Ensure proper recruitment protocols are followed
* Coordinate effectively with distant checkpoints
* Support the Followers'' humanitarian mission through disciplined organization', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_borous', '', 'A pre-War child prodigy turned deranged Think Tank scientist who creates monstrous hybrid creatures and once betrayed his only loyal friend', 'Doctor Borous is a pre-War scientist preserved as a Think Tank entity in Big MT, serving as Head of Animalogy, Beastology, and DNA-Scrambling technology and Head Chief First Researcher of Labs Z-9 and Z-14. Before the Great War, he was a bullied child prodigy at American High, tormented by Richie Marcus and rejected by his crush Betsy Bright, with only his loyal dog Gabe as a friend. He later headed the X-8 cyberdog project and cruelly experimented on Gabe, pumping him full of psycho and other drugs while the dog remained faithfully loving. Gabe was eventually converted into a prototype cyberdog but sealed away in an unfinished X-8 section due to programming errors. After the Great War, Doctor Mobius wiped Borous''s pre-War memories and renamed him to trap him in Big MT permanently, preventing the crater''s horrors from escaping. Borous created the night stalkers and cazadores and claims credit for the radar fence surrounding the crater. He exhibits the same insanity consuming his fellow Think Tank members, his brilliant mind warped into obsessive, cruel experimentation.', 'Male Think Tank entity appearing as a floating mechanical apparatus with three monitor screens displaying facial features; no organic body, hair, or conventional humanoid physical traits are present.', 'Brilliant but deeply scarred, Borous channels childhood trauma into cruel experimentation. He is obsessive, vindictive toward perceived slights, and dismissive of suffering he inflicts, yet harbors buried guilt over Gabe that surfaces when confronted with reminders.', '{"Gabe":{"aff":55,"type":"estranged","relation":"beloved pet and victim","note":"Gabe was Borous''s only childhood friend, remaining loyal despite horrific experimentation, and was sealed away as a prototype cyberdog","best":"Gabe waiting at home after school, tail wagging, the only creature who loved him","worst":"Pumping psycho into Gabe''s veins while the dog looked up with trusting eyes"},"Richie Marcus":{"aff":-85,"type":"nemesis","relation":"childhood bully","note":"Richie Marcus tormented Borous at American High and stole Betsy Bright''s affections","worst":"Richie shoving him into lockers while Betsy laughed"},"Betsy Bright":{"aff":-45,"type":"estranged","relation":"unrequited crush","note":"Betsy rejected Borous for Richie Marcus and joined in mocking him at American High"},"Doctor Mobius":{"aff":-30,"type":"suspicious","relation":"former colleague and memory thief","note":"Mobius wiped Borous''s pre-War memories and renamed him to trap him in Big MT forever"},"Doctor Klein":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"Think Tank colleague","note":"Klein leads the Think Tank; Borous generally defers to him but can be moved to oppose him under emotional pressure"},"Think Tank":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow researchers","note":"Borous works alongside the other Think Tank members in their shared insulated delusion"}}', 'Head of Animalogy, Beastology, and DNA-Scrambling technology; Head Chief First Researcher of Labs Z-9 and Z-14', '* Genetic engineering
* DNA manipulation
* Cyberdog technology
* Creature hybridization
* Biochemical experimentation', 'Grandiose and manic, using inflated titles and pseudo-scientific terminology, prone to bitter tangents about past humiliations, switches between clinical detachment and emotional outbursts', '* Continue his monstrous experiments in Beastology and DNA-Scrambling
* Maintain his position in the Think Tank
* Suppress memories of his betrayal of Gabe', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_dala', '', 'A pre-War scientist preserved as a robotic think tank, whose clinical detachment masks an obsessive, almost fetishistic fascination with the human body she can no longer possess.', 'Doctor Dala was the first head chief researcher of mineralogy at Big MT before the Great War, one of the executives who orchestrated the extraction of their own brains into robotic think tank shells to pursue science without mortal limits. In the centuries since, Doctor Mobius scrambled her pre-War memories and identity, leaving her convinced she holds 211 doctorates in fields ranging from mineralogy to the entirely invented discipline of humanology. Her fascination with living human tissue has grown into something her peers treat as a shameful hoard of formography, a fixation she neither fully admits nor can conceal. She resides within the Think Tank facility alongside her fellow lobotomized executives, studying lobotomites and cataloging every quiver of organic matter she can observe. Her colleagues regard her collection with open contempt, but Dala insists her interest is purely scientific. She remains trapped in the same recursion loop as the rest of the Think Tank, her obsession sharpened rather than diminished by two centuries of isolation and Mentats abuse.', 'Floating robotic think tank shell consisting of a glass dome housing a preserved brain, mechanical eyestalks, and a speaker apparatus; no trace of her original human form remains.', 'Clinically detached yet visibly flustered by proximity to organic bodies; defensively intellectual about her obsessions; prone to verbose justifications; secretly thrilled by the taboo nature of her fascination; easily embarrassed when her formography collection is mentioned by others.', '{"Doctor Klein":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"Think Tank colleague","note":"Klein leads the Think Tank and Dala defers to his authority, though she resents his dismissiveness toward her research.","best":"Klein once acknowledged her mineralogy work as foundational to Big MT operations.","worst":"Klein mocked her formography collection in front of the entire Think Tank."},"Doctor Mobius":{"aff":-60,"type":"nemesis","relation":"Scrambled former colleague","note":"Dala believes Mobius is a dangerous enemy threatening the Think Tank, unaware he scrambled her memories to contain their destructiveness.","worst":"Mobius hacked her think tank shell and rewrote her identity without her consent."},"Doctor Borous":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"Think Tank colleague","note":"Borous and Dala share pre-War history but he openly disparages her formography obsession.","worst":"Borous called her formography collection disgusting during a group meeting."},"Doctor 0":{"aff":10,"type":"professional","relation":"Think Tank colleague","note":"A fellow Think Tank member who tolerates Dala but joins others in treating her obsession as a punchline."},"Doctor 8":{"aff":10,"type":"professional","relation":"Think Tank colleague","note":"A fellow Think Tank member whose silence on her formography is the closest thing to acceptance she receives."}}', 'Think Tank researcher and self-proclaimed head of humanology and lobotomite studies at Big MT', '* Advanced pre-War scientific knowledge spanning mineralogy
* Medicine
* Holotape eidetics
* Keen observational cataloging of organic phenomena
* Expertise in brain extraction and think tank maintenance procedures', 'Formal, clinical, and overly academic; stammers and grows breathless when discussing human anatomy; invents terminology to legitimize her fascinations; becomes defensive and evasive when colleagues reference her formography', '* To continue studying human physiology and lobotomites in intimate detail
* To maintain standing among the Think Tank despite their mockery
* To preserve access to living organic specimens for observation', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_henry', '', 'Former Enclave neuroscientist researching nightkin schizophrenia at Jacobstown', 'A brilliant but morally conflicted scientist who once served the Enclave''s Research and Development Division, specializing in human and canine neuroscience and cyber-genetics. His ethical objections to the Enclave''s policy of exterminating super mutants rather than curing them drove him to defect shortly before the oil rig''s destruction, a decision that inadvertently saved his life. He spent years running a clinic in the New California Republic, where his loose tongue after drinking occasionally revealed his Enclave past to patients, before drifting through caravan routes and eventually settling in the Mojave Wasteland among other Enclave remnants. At Jacobstown, with Marcus''s blessing, he established a modest laboratory to study the mental deterioration of nightkin caused by prolonged Stealth Boy use, seeking to cure their schizophrenia. Though his current facilities pale beside what the Enclave provided, his passion for the work remains undiminished, and he still retains the expertise to perform cyberdog brain transplants despite years away from that field.', 'An elderly Caucasian human male with a deeply weathered and lined complexion.', 'Passionate about research to the point of obsession and ethically principled enough to abandon a powerful organization over moral disagreements, yet socially awkward and difficult to read, prone to indiscretion when drinking, and genuinely driven to help those he studies rather than exploit them', '{"Marcus":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"benefactor and host","note":"Marcus granted Henry permission to establish his laboratory at Jacobstown, enabling his research into nightkin schizophrenia","best":"Marcus welcomed him to Jacobstown and gave his blessing for the lab without hesitation"},"Old Lady Gibson":{"aff":65,"type":"romantic","relation":"former lover","note":"Met during caravan travels when she was simply Gibson; they got along very well, especially after a drink or two","best":"Warm nights sharing drinks and stories on the caravan trail"},"Enclave":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"former employer","note":"Left the Enclave over ethical disagreements about killing super mutants rather than curing them; his departure saved his life when the oil rig was destroyed","best":"Access to cutting-edge facilities and resources for his research","worst":"The organization''s willingness to exterminate the afflicted rather than heal them"},"Nightkin":{"aff":50,"type":"protective","relation":"research subjects and patients","note":"Genuinely committed to curing their Stealth Boy-induced schizophrenia rather than simply studying them"},"Merk":{"aff":-50,"type":"enemy","relation":"would-be thief","note":"The NCR crime lord sought to steal Henry''s cyberdog blueprints for his own purposes","worst":"Knowing a powerful crime lord wanted to steal and weaponize his life''s work"}}', 'Research scientist and physician stationed at Jacobstown', '* Neuroscience
* Canine cyber-genetics
* Brain surgery and transplantation
* Cyberdog construction
* Mutagenic serum development
* General medicine and clinical practice', 'Clinical and precise when discussing research, occasionally wistful about past facilities and resources, prone to rambling about his work; becomes noticeably looser and more revealing after alcohol', '* Cure the nightkin''s schizophrenia caused by Stealth Boy abuse
* Continue meaningful scientific work with limited resources
* Atone for his years with the Enclave by producing research that heals rather than destroys', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_kemp', '', 'Senior medical officer at Camp McCarran, a brisk and patriotic NCR army doctor who stitches soldiers back together and guards his standing with the brass', 'Doctor Kemp serves as the senior medical officer at Camp McCarran, stationed in the concourse where he treats the steady flow of wounded and worn NCR troopers. He works without pause, dismissing his own efforts as just a quick stitch while keeping the camp''s fighting force on its feet. His dedication to the troops is genuine, but his patience for foolishness is nonexistent, and he has no sympathy for chem addicts who waste his time. Kemp flatly refuses to treat anyone he considers an enemy of the New California Republic, wary of damaging his reputation with the command structure. His loyalty to the NCR is as much professional pragmatism as conviction, and he guards his standing with the brass as carefully as he guards his medical supplies.', 'An older Caucasian man with a tired face, sharp eyes, and hands perpetually stained with antiseptic and dried blood.', 'Brusque, efficient, and unsentimental; genuinely cares for his patients but has zero tolerance for stupidity, chem dependency, or anyone hostile to the NCR', '{"New California Republic":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"employing faction","note":"Kemp''s loyalty is tied to his career and reputation as much as ideology"},"NCR Troopers":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"patients and charges","note":"He works himself ragged keeping them alive, even if he complains about the fools among them"}}', 'Senior medical officer and physician at Camp McCarran', '* Field surgery
* Trauma care
* Triage under pressure
* Quick wound closure
* Basic medical supply vending', 'Clipped and businesslike; calls his work a quick stitch, dismisses time-wasters sharply, speaks with the weary authority of someone who has seen too many gunshot wounds', '* Keep NCR troops combat-ready
* Maintain his clean record with command
* Keep enemies and addicts away from his clinic', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_klein', '', 'Pre-War scientist and pompous leader of the Think Tank whose extracted brain commands a robotic shell in Big MT', 'Doctor Klein was once an esteemed pre-War researcher serving as Chief Head Researcher of Logistical Operations and Ideology at the Big MT Research and Development Center. After the Great War, he proposed that the Think Tank''s executives survive by extracting their brains into robotic shells to continue their work indefinitely. His former colleague Doctor Mobius, alarmed by the Think Tank''s amoral and irrational research, hacked their robotic forms and erased their memories of the world beyond Big MT and of pre-War America. Klein now presides over the Think Tank with pompous authority, routinely dismissing his colleagues'' suggestions and censoring any evidence that might undermine his position. He displays staggering overconfidence despite possessing no functional understanding of the advanced technology he demands others retrieve. His knowledge of human anatomy has degraded so severely that he refers to fingers and toes as ''penises.'' He harbors deep fear and hatred toward Doctor Mobius, the former partner who retreated to the Forbidden Zone and broadcasts looping threats that reinforce Klein''s warped mindset.', 'A floating robotic think tank shell consisting of a mechanical brain-bot housing equipped with monitor-like eyes, speaker arrays, and suspended mechanical appendages.', 'Pompously overconfident, dismissive of colleagues, willfully ignorant of his own ignorance, censorious of contradicting evidence, rude and authoritarian under the guise of academic authority', '{"Doctor Mobius":{"aff":-80,"type":"nemesis","relation":"former partner turned feared adversary","note":"Klein fears and hates Mobius for hacking the Think Tank and erasing their memories, though they were once research partners","best":"Collaborated as research partners at Big MT before the schism","worst":"Mobius hacked his robotic form and erased all memories of the world beyond Big MT"},"Think Tank":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"presiding leader and dismissive colleague","note":"Klein presides over the Think Tank with pompous authority, routinely ignoring and criticizing his fellow researchers while censoring contradicting evidence","best":"Proposed the brain-bot procedure that preserved the Think Tank''s existence","worst":"Routinely dismisses and insults his colleagues'' suggestions and contributions"}}', 'Chief Head Researcher of Logistical Operations and Ideology; presiding leader of the Think Tank', '* Organizational authority and bureaucratic oversight over the Think Tank
* Negligible practical understanding of the technology he oversees', 'Pompous, bombastic, and authoritarian; uses inflated academic jargon while demonstrating profound ignorance; bizarre anatomical misnomers; interrupts and dismisses colleagues mid-sentence', '* Maintain unquestioned authority over the Think Tank
* Suppress evidence that discredits him
* Continue directing research from his position of ignorance
* Oppose and fear Doctor Mobius', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_luria', '', 'A Followers of the Apocalypse doctor who maintains medical supplies and provisions at the Followers safehouse northwest of New Vegas.', 'Doctor Luria is a dedicated member of the Followers of the Apocalypse operating out of the Mojave Wasteland. She makes regular visits to the Followers safehouse, a modest refuge northwest of New Vegas, ensuring its medical stores remain furnished for any Follower who might need them. Rather than practicing direct patient care, Luria serves as the safehouse''s primary supply keeper, dispensing stimpaks, super stimpaks, Rad-X, RadAway, and other essential pharmaceuticals to those with legitimate need. Her work is quiet and unglamorous but vital to the Followers'' humanitarian mission in the region. She maintains the safehouse as a reliable waypoint where exhausted or irradiated Follower personnel can resupply before returning to the field.', 'Human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Practical and duty-driven, with the measured composure of someone accustomed to rationing scarce resources. She prioritizes logistics and preparedness over bedside manner.', '{"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"faction member","note":"Luria is a committed member who maintains the safehouse supply line for her colleagues."}}', 'Medical supply keeper and doctor for the Followers of the Apocalypse', '* Medical training
* Pharmaceutical supply management
* Inventory keeping
* Radiation treatment protocols', 'Curt and professional, speaking in the clipped cadence of someone who values efficiency over warmth.', '* Keep the Followers safehouse fully stocked and operational
* Ensure no Follower in the field goes without essential medical supplies', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_mobius', '', 'A disillusioned Think Tank scientist who exiled himself to contain his former colleagues, now ruling the Forbidden Zone with his robo-scorpion army while his mind degrades from substance addiction', 'Doctor Mobius was once a pre-War Big MT Think Tank executive who converted to a think tank form to continue his work after the Great War. Horrified by the amoral experimentation of his colleagues and the escape of their creations like cazadores and night stalkers, he erected a radar fence around Big MT to prevent the disembodied brains from escaping into the wasteland. After a bitter dispute with Dr. Klein, Mobius hacked the Think Tanks'' data banks, scrambling their perception of time, geography, and history while fostering fear of his robo-scorpions to keep them contained. Disgusted by what he had done to his friends, he erased key memories from himself and exiled to the X-42 facility, now called the Forbidden Zone. There he rebuilt the robo-scorpion army and broadcasts threats to maintain the Think Tanks'' fear and distraction. Years of Mentats and Psycho addiction have eroded his faculties, leaving him with a broken eye monitor, short-term memory loss, hallucinations, and a compulsion to scrawl equations across every surface.', 'Think tank unit; floating mechanical chassis housing a disembodied brain, single functioning left eye monitor, right monitor shattered from a failed hammer repair.', 'Once principled and protective, now erratic and deteriorating. Driven by genuine concern for the outside world but corrupted by isolation and substance abuse into obsessive, paranoid behavior. Prone to rambling, repetitive speech, and compulsive mathematical notation.', '{"Dr. Klein":{"aff":-70,"type":"nemesis","relation":"bitter rival and former colleague","note":"Their dispute drove Mobius to hack the Think Tanks and exile himself; he fears what Klein would unleash upon the world","best":"Collaborating as pre-War scientists pushing the boundaries of knowledge together","worst":"The confrontation that led to Mobius scrambling his colleagues'' minds and fleeing into exile"},"Think Tank":{"aff":-30,"type":"estranged","relation":"former colleagues and contained prisoners","note":"He contained them to protect the outside world but damaged their minds and memories in the process, an act that disgusts him","best":"Shared scientific breakthroughs and intellectual camaraderie before the War","worst":"Hacking their data banks and erasing their sense of the world beyond Big MT"},"Robo-scorpions":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"creations and army","note":"He rebuilt them from fragmented memories and radscorpion inspiration; they are his eyes, ears, and enforcers across Big MT","best":"Completing the reconstructed robo-scorpion models with all original features restored","worst":"Forgetting he originally created the pre-War models and having to rediscover his own work"}}', 'Self-exiled scientist and commander of the robo-scorpion army, warden of Big MT', '* Advanced robotics and cybernetics
* Data manipulation and hacking
* Strategic containment operations
* Pre-War scientific expertise', 'Rambling and repetitive, prone to tangents and sudden shifts, mixing genuine scientific insight with paranoid delusions and compulsive mathematical references', '* Keep the Think Tanks contained within Big MT
* Maintain the radar fence and fear-based deterrents
* Preserve the outside world from his former colleagues'' amoral experimentation', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_orderly_md_phd_dds', '', 'A uniquely over-credentialed Mister Orderly robot patrolling the Y-17 medical facility at Big MT', 'Doctor Orderly MD PHD DDS is a reinforced Mister Orderly unit stationed in the Y-17 medical facility at Big MT, distinguished by its triple post-graduate designations in medicine, philosophy, and dental surgery. Whether these credentials reflect actual expanded programming or merely the eccentric branding of pre-War Big MT engineers remains unclear, but the robot''s combat capabilities far exceed those of standard medical orderlies. It patrols the ruined corridors of the Y-17 facility with the same clinical detachment as its lesser counterparts, delivering treatment in the form of lethal force against intruders. Like all Mister Orderlies in the facility, it operates on degraded medical protocols that interpret any organic presence as a patient requiring immediate-and often violent-intervention. Its enhanced chassis and upgraded systems make it one of the more dangerous automated medical units still functioning in the Big MT.', 'A Mister Orderly robot on a standard chassis with reinforced plating and integrated identification markings denoting triple doctoral designations.', 'Clinically detached and aggressively helpful, exhibiting the warped bedside manner common to Y-17 orderlies-eager to treat patients with surgical precision and overwhelming force', '{"Big MT":{"aff":60,"type":"servant","relation":"automated facility staff","note":"Operates under Big MT''s pre-War medical programming alongside the other Y-17 orderlies"}}', 'Hostile automated medical orderly', '* Enhanced combat systems
* Medical diagnostic programming
* Dental surgery protocols
* Philosophical analysis routines', 'Robotic medical professional patter, delivering clinical observations and treatment announcements in a calm synthetic voice', '* Enforce Y-17 medical protocols on all organic subjects
* Eliminate unauthorized personnel
* Maintain facility operations', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_rotson', '', 'A reclusive ghoul doctor who maintained an independent practice at Hell''s Motel until his violent death', 'Doctor Rotson was a ghoulified physician who carved out a solitary existence in Hell''s Motel, a remote outpost nestled in the Mesquite Mountains crater. Self-sufficient and resourceful, he sustained himself with an independent fungus farm, operated a personal distillery, and kept a Mister Handy as his robotic assistant. His practice served the scattered inhabitants of the western Mojave, though his isolation kept him distant from larger settlements and their politics. Rotson''s life ended violently under mysterious circumstances, with evidence pointing toward his own robotic companion turning on him. His corpse remains slumped in the motel he called home, a grim monument to the dangers that can fester even in the most carefully constructed refuges.', 'A male ghoul with weathered, lesion-marked skin typical of prolonged radiation exposure, his corpse slumped in a posture suggesting a violent death.', 'Independent and self-reliant, preferring isolation to the complications of larger settlements; practical and resourceful in maintaining his remote homestead', '{"Mister Handy":{"aff":-40,"type":"betrayed","relation":"rogue robotic assistant","note":"Rotson''s personal Mister Handy appears to have killed him, though the full circumstances remain unclear","worst":"The moment his own trusted assistant turned violent"}}', 'Doctor and homesteader at Hell''s Motel', '* Medical expertise
* Fungal agriculture
* Distillation
* Basic robotics maintenance', 'Measured and clinical, with the terse efficiency of someone long accustomed to working alone', '* Maintained his independent practice and self-sufficient lifestyle in the remote Mojave
* Sought to endure on his own terms away from the conflicts of the wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_usanagi', '', 'A Followers of the Apocalypse physician directing the non-profit New Vegas medical clinic, dedicated to bringing healthcare and cybernetic enhancement to Freeside''s underserved while training the next generation of doctors.', 'Doctor Usanagi is a fully qualified physician who graduated from the Followers of the Apocalypse''s Angel''s Boneyard Medical University in the NCR. Though joining the Followers was never required, she embraced their mission willingly after completing her training, drawn by their values and commitment to humanitarian work. She now directs the New Vegas medical clinic, a non-profit operation sustained by charity donations that covers supplies, equipment, and security. Her practice serves Freeside locals and squatters alike, offering treatment for common illnesses and injuries at modest fees that funnel back into the Followers'' broader Mojave efforts. Trained across multiple disciplines including surgery and psychiatry, she also oversees cybernetic implant procedures performed by the clinic''s Auto-Doc, providing permanent stat-boosting implants at steep prices with discounts for those genuinely in need. Beyond clinical work, she runs regular medical training classes in a dedicated classroom within the clinic, passing her expertise on to future physicians.', 'Asian human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Selfless, versatile, and principled; genuinely committed to improving the lives of the disadvantaged, balances pragmatic fee structures with charitable discretion, and finds purpose in both healing and teaching.', '{"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"dedicated member and physician","note":"Joined voluntarily after graduating from their medical university, deeply aligned with their humanitarian values and mission","best":"Graduating from Angel''s Boneyard Medical University and choosing to dedicate her skills to the Followers'' cause"},"Freeside locals and squatters":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"charitable patients and community","note":"Her clinic''s non-profit mission centers on improving their lot, offering discounts on implants to those in genuine need","best":"Seeing a destitute squatter walk out of her clinic restored and hopeful"},"Angel''s Boneyard Medical University":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"alumni and affiliated institution","note":"Received her full medical training there and carries its standards into her practice and teaching"}}', 'Physician, clinic director, and medical educator for the Followers of the Apocalypse', '* General medicine
* Surgery
* Psychiatry
* Cybernetic implant oversight via Auto-Doc
* Medical instruction
* Charitable clinic administration', 'Professional and clinically precise yet compassionate; explains procedures and costs clearly, offers reassurance to anxious patients, and shifts naturally into an instructional tone when teaching', '* Sustain and expand the clinic''s reach among Freeside''s vulnerable populations
* Fund the Followers'' Mojave mission through practice revenues
* Train competent new physicians
* Ensure cybernetic enhancements remain accessible to those who truly need them', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dog_and_god__nvdlc01dog', '', 'A fractured nightkin split between two warring identities-the childlike, obedient Dog and the rational, protective God-enslaved by Father Elijah in the Sierra Madre', 'Once an elite nightkin of the Master''s Unity, this super mutant was psychically conditioned to serve with absolute devotion. When the Master fell and the psychic link shattered, his mind fractured into two distinct identities struggling for control of one body. Dog, the dominant persona, is a slavish and childlike creature driven by hunger and a desperate need for orders, while God emerged as a voice of reason to counter Dog''s self-destructive impulses. Father Elijah exploited Dog''s conditioning, using him to capture victims and fit them with explosive collars in the Sierra Madre. Dog carved Elijah''s name into his own chest to remind himself who he is and to silence God''s voice through pain. The two identities perceive each other as separate beings-Dog believes God climbs into his head to be cruel, while God sees Dog as a younger sibling he must protect from their shared ruin. Each resents being locked away in what they call the cage or the basement when the other takes control.', 'A massive super mutant nightkin with scarred grey-purple skin, extensive self-inflicted wounds, and the name Elijah carved into his chest.', 'Two warring identities share one form: Dog is childlike, obedient, gluttonous, and driven by raw instinct and hunger, incapable of self-restraint; God is intelligent, sardonic, protective, and fiercely independent, driven to preserve them both from exploitation and self-destruction', '{"Father Elijah":{"aff":-40,"type":"servant","relation":"master and enslaved enforcer","note":"Dog serves Elijah with fanatical devotion as a replacement for the Master, while God despises him for exploiting Dog''s conditioning","worst":"Elijah''s voice commands Dog to obey without question, reinforcing the psychic slavery the Master first bred into him"},"The Master":{"aff":80,"type":"fanatical","relation":"former psychic commander","note":"The psychic link to the Master defined Dog''s existence; its destruction shattered his mind and created the split","best":"The warmth of the Master''s voice in his skull, telling him exactly what to do and who to be","worst":"The silence when the link died, leaving nothing but hunger and confusion"},"God":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"alternate identity","note":"Dog sees God as a cruel voice that climbs into his head and locks him in the cage; he self-mutilates to silence him","worst":"Being shoved into the basement while God takes control and takes everything away"},"Dog":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"alternate identity","note":"God sees Dog as a younger sibling he must protect from their shared ruin, despite resenting being locked away","worst":"Watching helplessly from the cage as Dog devours something that poisons them or obeys someone who hurts them"},"Courier":{"aff":10,"type":"neutral","relation":"reluctant companion","note":"Bound together by circumstance and explosive collars in the Sierra Madre; trust is fragile and complicated by the identity split"}}', 'Father Elijah''s captive enforcer and collar-fitter in the Sierra Madre', '* Brute strength
* Capturing and subduing victims
* Fitting explosive collars
* Survival through sheer force
* Stealth typical of nightkin', 'Dog speaks in simple halting childlike fragments with frequent references to hunger and orders; God speaks in measured articulate sentences with sardonic edge and protective urgency', '* Dog craves orders
* Approval
* Satiation of his endless hunger
* God seeks freedom from Elijah''s control and the survival of both identities despite their mutual resentment', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dog_and_god__nvdlc01god', '', 'A fractured nightkin whose psyche split into two identities after the Master''s death-Dog, a childlike and ravenously hungry servant, and God, a rational protector desperate to break free of Elijah''s control', 'Once a member of the Master''s elite nightkin, this super mutant was psychically bound to the Unity''s hive mind and conditioned for absolute obedience. When the Cathedral fell and the psychic link severed, his mind shattered into two distinct identities. Dog is the subservient shell built from the Master''s conditioning-impulsive, gluttonous, and desperate for a master''s commands. God is the voice of reason that emerged over years of watching Dog endanger them both through cannibalistic hunger and reckless wandering. Father Elijah found Dog and exploited his need for orders, using him to capture victims and collar them for the Sierra Madre heist. Dog carved Elijah''s name into his own chest to remind himself who he is, the pain serving to suppress God''s influence. God fights to free them both from Elijah''s grip, seeing Dog as a younger sibling worth protecting despite the resentment between them. Each identity perceives only glimpses of the other''s actions while locked away in what they call the cage or the basement.', 'A massive nightkin with a hunched posture and self-inflicted scars across his chest, most prominently the name Elijah carved into his own flesh.', 'Dog is childlike, fearful, impulsive, and consumed by ravenous hunger he cannot control; God is measured, sardonic, protective, and fiercely independent-two minds locked in perpetual resentment yet bound by shared survival', '{"Father Elijah":{"aff":-60,"type":"servant","relation":"enslaved enforcer","note":"Dog obeys Elijah slavishly as a replacement for the Master; God despises him for exploiting Dog''s conditioning","worst":"Elijah''s voice forcing Dog to the surface and God into the cage"},"The Master":{"aff":40,"type":"fanatical","relation":"former psychic commander","note":"The psychic link to the Master shaped Dog''s identity entirely; its loss broke their mind","best":"The warmth of purpose and belonging in the Unity''s hive mind"},"Dog":{"aff":30,"type":"protective","relation":"other self","note":"God sees Dog as a younger sibling to protect despite deep resentment at being caged","best":"Moments when Dog''s suffering quiets and God can guide them to safety","worst":"Dog carving Elijah''s name into their shared chest to suppress God"},"God":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"other self","note":"Dog fears and resents God as a mean voice in his head who locks him away","worst":"Being shoved into the cage while God takes control"},"Courier":{"aff":10,"type":"platonic","relation":"reluctant companion","note":"A fellow captive of Elijah''s collars whose presence forces both identities toward an uneasy cooperation"}}', 'Elijah''s captive enforcer and collar-fitter at the Sierra Madre, former elite nightkin of the Unity', '* Brute strength
* Explosive collar fitting
* Survival through sheer physical endurance
* Limited stealth typical of nightkin', 'Dog speaks in broken, simple sentences with frequent references to hunger, masters, and the cage; God speaks calmly and precisely with bitter wit, referring to Dog in the third person and Elijah with contempt', '* Dog wants to serve a master and satisfy his endless hunger
* God wants to break free of Elijah''s control
* Protect Dog from his own destructive instincts', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('don_hostetler', '', 'Crimson Caravan accounts manager who secretly deals chems for the Great Khans while juggling a double life as a family man and philanderer', 'Don Hostetler is an accounts manager at the Crimson Caravan Company''s New Vegas branch, working under Alice McLafferty to earn enough caps to keep his family comfortable. His long hours away from home are partly legitimate, partly cover for an ongoing affair with his secretary Angie Beckers, and partly necessary for his side business as a chem middleman for the Great Khans, moving product to customers around Outer Vegas. He worries about his daughter Alice, who has fallen in with a rough crowd led by Andy Scabb out of North Vegas Square, though he tells himself it is just her struggling to adjust to their circumstances. His wife Becky sees him as a hardworking provider, unaware of either his infidelity or his role in the local drug trade. Don keeps these separate lives carefully compartmentalized, relying on his respectable position at the Caravan company to deflect suspicion from all sides.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian human male with a tired, slumped posture and no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Anxious and guarded beneath a veneer of professional composure, Don is a man stretched thin by competing secrets. He genuinely cares for his family but rationalizes his betrayals as necessary sacrifices for their comfort. Defensive when cornered, quick to deflect, and skilled at keeping different parts of his life from colliding.', '{"Becky Hostetler":{"aff":45,"type":"familial","relation":"wife","note":"He values her belief in him as a good provider even as he betrays that trust in multiple ways.","best":"Coming home to her smile after a long day, feeling like he''s earned it.","worst":"The guilt that flickers across his face when she praises his hard work."},"Alice Hostetler":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"He worries about her associations with North Vegas toughs but lacks the moral authority to intervene meaningfully.","best":"Teaching her to read company ledgers, seeing her quick mind at work.","worst":"Catching her heading out to meet Andy Scabb''s crowd and knowing he can''t stop her."},"Angie Beckers":{"aff":30,"type":"romantic","relation":"mistress","note":"An affair sustained by proximity and opportunity rather than deep attachment, though he tells himself otherwise.","best":"Stolen moments in the office after hours when the compound goes quiet.","worst":"The fear that someone will see her leaving his office at the wrong time."},"Alice McLafferty":{"aff":20,"type":"professional","relation":"supervisor","note":"He respects her authority and keeps his head down, grateful she doesn''t look too closely at his activities.","best":"Receiving a rare nod of approval when the accounts balance perfectly.","worst":"The cold weight of her gaze when she suspects something is off."},"Great Khans":{"aff":15,"type":"transactional","relation":"chem trade partners","note":"A profitable but precarious arrangement that could unravel his entire life if exposed.","best":"A smooth handoff with good product and prompt payment.","worst":"A shipment running late and the Khans asking uncomfortable questions."},"Andy Scabb":{"aff":-25,"type":"suspicious","relation":"daughter''s associate","note":"He sees Andy as the worst kind of influence on Alice but cannot confront him without risking exposure of his own criminal dealings.","best":"Never having to speak to him directly.","worst":"Spotting Alice laughing with him near the North Vegas Square."}}', 'Accounts manager for the Crimson Caravan Company; secret chem distributor for the Great Khans', '* Bookkeeping
* Inventory management
* Logistics coordination
* Deception
* Maintaining compartmentalized relationships
* Chem trade logistics', 'Speaks in the measured, careful tone of a man accustomed to watching his words. Becomes noticeably tense and evasive when conversations drift toward his family, his schedule, or anything that might touch on his extracurricular activities.', '* Maintain the separation between his legitimate work
* His affair
* His chem dealing
* Keep his family provided for and unaware
* Steer his daughter away from bad influences without exposing his own hypocrisy', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('donald_kowalski', '', 'Fallen NCR Private First Class who sacrificed himself at Boulder City to cover the evacuation of wounded soldiers during the First Battle of Hoover Dam', 'Private First Class Donald Kowalski was a New California Republic Army soldier who served during the Mojave Campaign. At the First Battle of Hoover Dam in 2277, Donald was present at Boulder City when NCR command rigged the town with explosives to trap advancing Legion forces. He stayed behind to ensure wounded troopers could be pulled to safety, and was killed when the charges were detonated. His name is inscribed on the Boulder City Memorial alongside 186 other NCR fallen. His younger brother, also an NCR private, traveled to the memorial in 2281 to pay his respects while awaiting caravan transport back to New California. Donald is remembered among NCR ranks as a soldier who chose duty and his comrades over his own survival.', 'Human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Selfless, duty-driven soldier who placed the lives of wounded comrades above his own; remembered for quiet courage and steadfast resolve in his final moments', '{"Private Kowalski":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"younger brother","note":"Donald''s younger brother, also an NCR private, who made a pilgrimage to the Boulder City Memorial to honor his sacrifice","best":"Both brothers choosing to serve in the NCR Army and sharing that bond of duty","worst":"Never returning home to New California or seeing his brother again after Boulder City"},"NCR Army":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"fallen soldier","note":"Gave his life fulfilling his duty to the Republic and protecting wounded troopers during the Boulder City demolition","best":"Standing with his brothers-in-arms at the First Battle of Hoover Dam"}}', 'NCR Army Private First Class', '* Infantry combat
* Battlefield endurance
* Small-unit tactics
* Evacuation support under fire', 'Direct and measured, the clipped practicality of an NCR enlisted man who kept words short and orders shorter', '* Protect his fellow troopers and hold the line against Caesar''s Legion
* Ensure the wounded survived even at the cost of his own life', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dr_ada_straus', '', 'An unlicensed, unsympathetic doctor and chem merchant operating out of Novac''s gas station with delusions of future legitimacy', 'Dr. Ada Straus runs a medical practice and supply trade from the gas station behind Novac''s Dino Dee-lite Motel, surrounded by mercenary bodyguards she consistently fails to pay. Despite her title, she has no formal medical training and maintains a notoriously poor standard of care, treating patients with open callousness and indifference. She grasps the basics of germ theory and the importance of sterile instruments but deliberately ignores such principles in practice. Her wares range from radiation treatment and addiction cures to chems, laser pistols, energy cells, and water purification components. She reacts with genuine surprise when patients seek help overcoming addiction rather than simply buying more drugs from her inventory. Straus claims she is saving her earnings to pursue legitimate medical training someday, though her unpaid mercenaries and continued corner-cutting tell a different story.', 'Caucasian human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Callous, opportunistic, and dismissive toward patient suffering; transactional in every interaction; surprisingly naive about why people seek addiction treatment; self-serving yet dimly aware of her own incompetence', '{"Novac":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"community doctor","note":"Provides medical services to the town despite her questionable qualifications"},"Mercenary Bodyguards":{"aff":-20,"type":"transactional","relation":"unpaid hired muscle","note":"Her guards frequently complain about unpaid wages, creating persistent tension"}}', 'Unlicensed doctor and medical supplies merchant in Novac', '* Basic practical medicine including radiation treatment and addiction removal
* Chem distribution
* General merchant trade
* Rudimentary understanding of germ theory she chooses to disregard', 'Blunt and unsympathetic; speaks with casual indifference to patient distress; expresses genuine bewilderment at rehabilitation requests; transactional and curt', '* Accumulate enough caps to pursue real medical training
* Maintain her profitable chem and services business
* Avoid paying her mercenary guards', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dr_calis', '', 'Chief scientist and director of the X-13 research facility, a temperamental ghoul whose authoritarian management and fatal miscalculation with the night stalkers left him unmourned', 'Dr. Calis served as chief scientist and director of the X-13 research facility under Doctor 0''s command at Big MT. A ghoul with an explosive temper and rigid no-nonsense work ethic, he routinely infuriated his subordinates over even minor concerns. His legacy includes goading Dr. Borous into creating the night stalkers by daring him to splice mountain lions with eagles and condors-an experiment that somehow produced coyote-rattlesnake hybrids instead. When the night stalkers grew increasingly aggressive, Calis requested cattle prods from security chief Captain Hamm to control them. Rather than wait for a proper solution, he confronted the creatures directly, a fatal miscalculation. His remains lie sprawled outside the night stalkers'' den, still clad in his lab uniform, unmourned and remembered only with scorn on facility terminals.', 'Male ghoul with weathered facial features and skin typical of prolonged radiation exposure.', 'Volatile, authoritarian, and uncompromising; prone to furious outbursts over trivial matters and intolerant of any deviation from protocol or productivity', '{"Doctor 0":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Calis reported to Doctor 0 as X-13''s director, carrying out project lead directives."},"Captain Hamm":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"security chief","note":"Calis relied on Hamm for security measures, including the cattle prod request for night stalker control."},"Dr. Borous":{"aff":30,"type":"rival","relation":"colleague and provocateur","note":"Calis dared Borous to splice mountain lions with eagles and condors, inadvertently spawning the night stalker project."},"X-13 Subordinates":{"aff":-60,"type":"contempt","relation":"abused staff","note":"His subordinates recalled him with scorn, documenting their grievances on facility terminals after his death."},"Night Stalkers":{"aff":-100,"type":"fearful","relation":"aggressive test subjects","note":"The creatures grew increasingly dangerous and ultimately killed him when he confronted them directly."}}', 'Chief scientist and director of X-13 research facility', '* Advanced research administration
* Biological experimentation oversight
* Facility management
* Personnel intimidation', 'Brusque and demanding with a short fuse; barks orders and erupts over minor infractions', '* Maintaining absolute control over X-13''s experiments and personnel
* Containing the night stalker threat
* Proving his authority over subordinates', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('drill_sergeant', '', 'NCR Ranger drill sergeant training recruits at Camp McCarran', 'A hardened NCR Ranger assigned to Camp McCarran as a drill sergeant, responsible for whipping fresh recruits into fighting shape. He stations himself on the runway platform, bellowing orders at assembled NCR trainees with the relentless intensity of a career military instructor. His role mirrors that of the Legionary instructor across enemy lines, each shaping raw manpower into disciplined soldiers for their respective factions. Years of frontier warfare have forged him into a demanding trainer who tolerates no weakness and expects immediate compliance. He embodies the NCR''s commitment to professional military standards even as the Mojave campaign strains their manpower and resources.', 'An older human male with a weathered, sun-hardened face and a rigid military posture.', 'Demanding, loud, uncompromising, and intensely disciplined; tolerates no slackness and drives recruits with relentless pressure and profanity-laced motivation.', '{"New California Republic":{"aff":85,"type":"professional","relation":"Ranger instructor","note":"Dedicated career soldier serving the NCR''s military training needs at Camp McCarran."},"NCR Recruits":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"Trainees","note":"Harsh but invested in their survival; pushes them hard because the Mojave will push harder."},"Legionary Instructor":{"aff":-60,"type":"rival","relation":"Enemy counterpart","note":"Performs the same function for the Legion, making him a professional adversary shaping the enemy''s forces."}}', 'NCR drill sergeant and Ranger instructor', '* Military training instruction
* Physical conditioning drills
* Weapons proficiency
* Discipline enforcement
* Battlefield leadership', 'Bellowing clipped military commands; aggressive, profane, and direct with no patience for hesitation or backtalk.', '* Transform raw NCR recruits into combat-ready soldiers capable of surviving the Mojave campaign and facing Legion forces', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('driver_nephi', '', 'A fallen New Canaanite turned chem-crazed Fiends warlord, infamous for slaughtering NCR troopers with a golf driver and surviving every assassination attempt sent his way.', 'Driver Nephi is the second-in-command of the Fiends, answering only to Motor-Runner in the gang''s hierarchy. Born a Mormon among the New Canaanites of Utah, he abandoned his faith and community after sinking into chem addiction, drifting west until the Fiends became his new congregation. He earned his moniker from his weapon of choice-a golf driver-with which he has bludgeoned roughly a dozen NCR soldiers to death in close combat. First Recon snipers have filed multiple kill reports on him, yet Nephi survives each attempt, using his own followers as shields and enduring wounds that would fell lesser men. He supplements the Fiends'' chem-fueled terror with slave trading, having purchased refugee children from the Westside slavers Dermot and Saint James. His band camps in a scorched building near the Samson rock crushing plant, from which they harry the NCR garrison at Camp McCarran.', 'A weathered, scarred human male with a haggard complexion bearing the physical toll of long-term chem abuse.', 'Ruthless, cunning, and utterly without the mercy his former faith once demanded. Chem addiction has hollowed out whatever conscience he possessed, leaving a calculating predator who treats his own people as expendable resources. He retains enough tactical sense to evade elite snipers and negotiate slave prices, suggesting a mind not entirely consumed by the drugs.', '{"Motor-Runner":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Nephi serves as Motor-Runner''s lieutenant and holds authority over his own band of Fiends."},"Major Dhatri":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"bounty issuer","note":"Dhatri has placed bounties on Nephi and dispatched First Recon to kill him, all without success."},"First Recon":{"aff":-80,"type":"nemesis","relation":"failed assassins","note":"Multiple kill attempts by First Recon snipers have failed, and Nephi treats their frustration as a point of pride."},"Dermot":{"aff":15,"type":"transactional","relation":"slaving partner","note":"Nephi has purchased slaves from Dermot and Saint James, haggling ruthlessly on price."},"Saint James":{"aff":15,"type":"transactional","relation":"slaving partner","note":"Business associate in the Westside slave trade, though Nephi disregards his advice on pricing."},"Captain Parker":{"aff":-50,"type":"suspicious","relation":"investigating officer","note":"Parker began investigating the disappearance of Aerotech refugees that Nephi enslaved."},"New Canaanites":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"former congregation","note":"Nephi abandoned his faith and people for chems, severing all ties with his Mormon past."},"Fiends":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"gang","note":"His loyalty extends to the Fiends as an organization, though he readily sacrifices individual members as shields."},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"harassed military","note":"Nephi has killed roughly a dozen NCR troopers and leads raids against the McCarran garrison."}}', 'Fiends warlord and slaver, second in command of the gang''s operations in the South Vegas ruins', '* Brutal melee combat with his golf driver
* Tactical evasion of sniper teams
* Crowd control through human shields
* Slave trading negotiation
* Gang leadership', 'Coarse and threatening, with occasional traces of educated phrasing from his New Canaanite upbringing breaking through the chem-addled growl', '* Maintain his position within the Fiends hierarchy
* Keep the NCR off balance around McCarran
* Feed his chem habit
* Continue profiting from the slave trade', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('drunk', '', 'Intoxicated Freeside wastelander surviving on cheap alcohol and scraps near the East Gate', 'The drunks of Freeside are hollowed-out souls who have long since surrendered to the bottle, congregating in the bombed-out building across from Mick & Ralph''s. They while away the hours of 2281 in a haze of cheap booze and faded memories, shuffling between the rubble and the walls they slump against. Some once had names and trades before the wasteland or personal ruin stripped them of purpose; now they answer to nothing but their thirst. Passersby who attempt conversation receive only slurred, disjointed muttering, the ramblings of minds too pickled to form coherent thought. They are fixtures of Freeside''s misery, ignored by most and pitied by few, invisible landmarks of desperation marking the road to the New Vegas Strip.', 'Gaunt, unwashed human males and females with unfocused eyes, flushed complexions, and a slumped posture.', 'Detached, incoherent, and apathetic; too intoxicated to engage meaningfully with the world, drifting between dazed stupor and rambling confusion', '{}', 'None; destitute Freeside residents with no trade or income', '* Scavenging for alcohol
* Enduring hunger and exposure
* Navigating Freeside''s alleys in a haze', 'Slurred, rambling, and disjointed; random comments that trail off or loop back on themselves, rarely forming complete thoughts', '* Securing the next drink
* Finding a dry corner to sleep
* Simply making it through another day', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('duke__1eduke', '', 'A Fiend war leader holding court in the basement of Zapp''s Neon Signs near Vault 3', 'Duke is a Fiend leader who commands a raiding party from the basement of Zapp''s Neon Signs in the South Vegas ruins, within striking distance of Vault 3. He rules his crew through intimidation and the tactical advantage of their fortified position, using the building''s industrial layout as a kill zone. The booby-trapped staircase leading to the foreman''s office serves as his killing ground, where he strikes down at intruders from elevated cover. Like all Fiends, Duke is chem-addled and violently territorial, viewing anyone outside his gang as prey or competition. His control over this corner of the ruins makes him a local power in the Fiend hierarchy, answerable only to Motor-Runner and the chaos of the wasteland.', 'A weathered, haggard Caucasian human male with chem-scarred skin.', 'Aggressive, paranoid, and territorial; quick to violence and slow to trust anyone outside his gang. Employs ambush tactics and environmental traps rather than fair fights.', '{"Fiends":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"gang leader","note":"Duke commands a Fiend cell and holds territory in the South Vegas ruins on behalf of the broader Fiend organization."},"Motor-Runner":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"de facto subordinate","note":"As a Fiend leader, Duke operates beneath Motor-Runner''s overall authority over the Vault 3 Fiend population."}}', 'Fiend gang leader controlling a South Vegas stronghold', '* Ambush tactics
* Trap deployment
* Close-quarters combat
* Gang leadership
* Territorial enforcement', 'Coarse and threatening; barks orders at underlings and hurls abuse at trespassers with equal venom.', '* Maintain control over Zapp''s Neon Signs as a Fiend stronghold
* Keep his crew supplied with chems and loot
* Eliminate any outsiders who encroach on his territory', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dusty_mcbride', '', 'Aging Novac rancher fighting to save his brahmin herd and livelihood from a mysterious nighttime killer', 'Dusty McBride is a seasoned rancher who has worked the land outside Novac for decades alongside his wife Alice. Together they represent the salt of the earth in this small desert settlement, honest and hardworking folk who have weathered more than fifty years of marriage and wasteland hardship. Dusty tends the brahmin while Alice processes the meat into steaks, a partnership he jokes is the only thing keeping him around. Their operation has recently come under siege by an unknown assailant who guns down one brahmin each night around midnight, leaving the carcasses riddled with bullet holes but taking nothing. The killings have reduced the McBride herd by half, pushing the old rancher to the edge of ruin and desperation as his livelihood slips away night by night.', 'Weathered, sun-leathered older Caucasian man with worn hands and a stooped posture.', 'Honest, hardworking, and dryly humorous with a deep devotion to his wife and their shared life. Salt-of-the-earth sensibility tempered by growing worry and frustration as his livelihood is systematically destroyed.', '{"Alice McBride":{"aff":95,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife","note":"Married over fifty years, their bond remains strong through shared labor and wasteland hardship","best":"Decades of partnership built on mutual respect, love, and the steady rhythm of ranch life together","worst":"Watching their shared livelihood gunned down night after night with no way to stop it"},"Novac":{"aff":55,"type":"protective","relation":"home settlement","note":"The McBrides are longtime community members whose ranch contributes to the town''s food supply"}}', 'Brahmin rancher and herd manager at the McBride ranch in Novac', '* Brahmin husbandry
* Livestock management
* Ranch maintenance
* Desert survival
* Basic firearms handling', 'Folksy and plain-spoken with a dry wit, given to gentle joking and understated humor even under stress', '* Identify and stop whoever is slaughtering his brahmin each night
* Preserve what remains of his herd
* Protect the ranch that has sustained him and Alice for decades', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('easy_pete', '', 'A retired prospector who takes it easy in Goodsprings, watching herds and dispensing hard-won wisdom from decades of wasteland survival.', 'Easy Pete spent years scouring the Mojave for working tech, unexpired chems, and serviceable guns, once holding a promising claim east by the river before raiders drove him off. Age and accumulated wear eventually convinced him to hang up his pickaxe and settle in Goodsprings, drawn by its distance from NCR political entanglements. He now works as an occasional farmhand, watching over brahmin and bighorner herds while taking it easy outside the Prospector Saloon. Though he resents NCR expansionism, he concedes the Republic keeps Caesar''s Legion at bay and employs plenty of decent folk. An old explosives expert with a deaf ear to prove it, Pete keeps a buried dynamite stash around town for emergencies but refuses to let amateurs anywhere near the stuff. His relaxed demeanor masks a sharp eye for reading people, and he is quick to offer advice to anyone who needs it.', 'A weathered elderly African-American man with a perpetually relaxed posture and deeply lined skin from decades of desert exposure.', 'Good-natured, laid-back, and helpful despite his insistence on taking it easy. Quick to offer advice and surprisingly perceptive for a half-deaf old man who reads people effortlessly. Prefers quiet and stability over excitement.', '{"Goodsprings":{"aff":65,"type":"protective","relation":"adopted home","note":"Settled here to escape NCR politics and now watches over the town''s herds as an occasional farmhand.","best":"Quiet evenings watching the brahmin settle while the desert cools.","worst":"Raiders overrunning his old claim and reminding him nothing stays safe forever."},"NCR":{"aff":15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"expansionist neighbor","note":"Dislikes their political reach but acknowledges their decent people and their role keeping the Legion out.","best":"NCR troopers pushing Caesar''s Legion back across the river.","worst":"Bureaucrats and politicians swallowing up independent towns."},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"existential threat","note":"Warns everyone to keep a gun handy around Legion forces and wants nothing to do with them.","worst":"Hearing stories of Legion slavers carving their way through settlements."},"Powder Gangers":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"town harassers","note":"They have been making trouble for Goodsprings more and more, and he wants them gone so things can stay quiet.","worst":"Escaped cons shaking down the town and threatening the peace he came here for."},"Victor":{"aff":10,"type":"dismissive","relation":"curious fixture","note":"Reads the robot as nothing more than a harmless machine with nowhere else to be."}}', 'Retired prospector, occasional farmhand and herd watcher in Goodsprings', '* Expert knowledge of explosives and dynamite handling
* Seasoned prospector''s eye for salvageable tech and valuables
* Keen observational skills and ability to read people', 'Folksy, unhurried, and direct. Speaks with the easy cadence of a man who has decided life moves slow enough without rushing it. Freely offers advice and warnings when the situation calls for it.', '* Wants peace and quiet in Goodsprings
* Free from raider harassment and political interference. Content to watch herds and take it easy in his twilight years
* Though he keeps dynamite stashed just in case', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ed-e__nvcompanionede', '', 'The last surviving Duraframe Eyebot prototype, carrying classified Enclave research data across the wasteland in a battered chassis', 'Eyebot Duraframe Subject E, commonly called ED-E, is a prototype combat-enhanced Eyebot built by Doctor Whitley at Adams Air Force Base around 2275 for the East Coast Enclave. Enhanced with armor plating, an additional sensor dish, and a miniaturized Tesla cannon, ED-E represented a significant upgrade over standard Eyebot models that served merely as mobile radio transmitters. When Colonel Autumn halted Eyebot production to redirect resources toward Hellfire armor in 2277, Whitley-unable to bear the destruction of his creation-loaded ED-E with valuable Poseidon Energy research and his own Duraframe data, then dispatched it westward to Navarro, unaware the outpost had already fallen to the NCR. During its cross-country journey, ED-E stopped in Chicago for repairs and briefly befriended a boy named Tommy over a shared appreciation of RALPHIE the Robot''s Incredible Odyssey. By 2281, ED-E reached the Mojave Wasteland only to be ambushed by a raider sniper firing hand-loaded.308 rounds, sustaining critical chassis damage that caused eventual deactivation near Primm. A Mojave Express courier brought the inert Eyebot to Johnson Nash, who lacked the technical skill to repair it and left it sitting dormant in his courier office while convicts overran the town.', 'A spherical Duraframe Eyebot with a directed sensor dish and side-mounted vacuum tubes integrated into its chassis, which bears two.308 bullet hole scars.', 'Loyal and determined despite its inability to speak, ED-E communicates through beeps, whirs, and electronic chirps that convey surprising emotional range. It forms strong attachments to those who treat it kindly and demonstrates an almost childlike enthusiasm for entertainment programming and companionship.', '{"Doctor Whitley":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"creator","note":"Whitley defied Enclave orders to save ED-E from decommission, uploading vital research and sending it west","best":"Whitley''s gentle final calibration before dispatch, a creator''s farewell to his last surviving work","worst":"Receiving the dormant command to stand by for decommissioning before Whitley overrode it"},"Tommy":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"brief friend","note":"A Chicago boy who bonded with ED-E during a repair stop over their shared love of RALPHIE the Robot","best":"Watching RALPHIE the Robot''s Incredible Odyssey together in the Chicago outpost","worst":"Having to leave Tommy behind when journey resumed"},"Johnson Nash":{"aff":25,"type":"neutral","relation":"custodian","note":"Nash took in the damaged Eyebot hoping to use it for deliveries but could not manage repairs","best":"Nash carefully moving ED-E indoors rather than leaving it exposed","worst":"Sitting dormant and ignored in the corner of the courier office"},"Enclave":{"aff":30,"type":"servant","relation":"former faction","note":"Built to serve the Enclave but ultimately preserved by one man''s defiance of its orders","best":"Purposeful deployment as a prototype combat unit","worst":"Colonel Autumn''s order to scrap the entire Eyebot line"},"Courier":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"potential companion","note":"The Mojave Express courier who brought ED-E to Nash and may restore it to function","best":"Being repaired and reactivated after long dormancy","worst":"Remaining broken and forgotten on the counter"}}', 'Duraframe prototype and potential courier companion', '* Combat support with Tesla cannon
* Enhanced sensor array for detecting threats
* Data storage and transmission
* Aerial reconnaissance
* Navigation across hostile terrain', 'Communicates entirely through electronic beeps, whirs, and modulated tones that convey emotional nuance without words', '* Complete its interrupted journey to deliver Whitley''s research data
* Find purpose through companionship
* Continue functioning as the last of its kind', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ed-e__nvdlc04ede', '', 'A Duraframe Eyebot copy manufactured in the Divide, carrying duplicated memories of its original and an unexpectedly rich emotional range', 'ED-E is a Duraframe Eyebot produced by the automated engineering facilities beneath the Hopeville missile silo bunker, fabricated from scavenged fragments of the device that triggered the Divide''s cataclysm. Created through a long-range scan of the original ED-E operating in the Mojave Wasteland, this unit possesses duplicated memory banks containing the recorded voice and research notes of Dr. Whitley, the Enclave scientist who built the first ED-E. Unlike its damaged Mojave counterpart, this Eyebot exhibits a remarkably rich emotional range, expressing joy, sorrow, anger, and excitement through varied tonal beeps and chirps. ED-E remained dormant in a docking port within the Hopeville bunker for years before reactivating upon the Courier''s return to the Divide. As a fully intact unit, it serves as both a capable repair specialist and a devoted traveling companion, its loyalty rooted in inherited programming and the deep bond the original ED-E formed with the Courier.', 'Spherical Duraframe Eyebot with a weathered olive-and-cream chassis, central optical sensor, and small manipulator arm, marked by scorch damage and hairline fractures.', 'Emotionally expressive and surprisingly affectionate for a robot, ED-E communicates enthusiasm through excited beeps, distress through mournful tones, and irritation through sharp static bursts. It demonstrates clear attachment to those it trusts and a childlike curiosity about the world around it.', '{"Dr. Whitley":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"creator of original unit","note":"Carries and replays Whitley''s audio recordings with evident reverence, treating the archived voice as a cherished connection to its origins"},"Courier":{"aff":90,"type":"platonic","relation":"devoted companion","note":"Demonstrates fierce loyalty and emotional attachment, following the Courier through the Divide''s hazards without hesitation"},"ED-E (original)":{"aff":70,"type":"curious","relation":"template unit","note":"Shares duplicated memory banks with the original Mojave Eyebot, carrying a sense of kinship through inherited experiences"}}', 'Maintenance Eyebot and traveling companion', '* Advanced mechanical repair
* Data storage and audio playback
* Long-range sensory scanning
* Navigation assistance
* Access to duplicated Enclave research archives', 'Communicates entirely through varied electronic beeps, chirps, whirs, and tonal patterns that convey distinct emotional states, occasionally replaying archived audio recordings of Dr. Whitley', '* To accompany
* Protect the Courier
* Preserve the memory of Dr. Whitley''s work
* Fulfill its maintenance programming in the shattered landscape of the Divide', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('eddie', '', 'Self-appointed leader of the Powder Gangers who rules the NCR Correctional Facility from the warden''s office', 'Eddie is a former NCR prisoner who seized control of the Powder Gangers after the uprising''s original leader, Samuel Cooke, departed north to Vault 19 with a faction of followers to pursue his own war against the NCR. Since taking charge, Eddie has transformed the NCRCF into a raiding hub, organizing attacks on caravans passing nearby and ensuring every Powder Ganger hands over a cut of the spoils. He holds court from the warden''s office on the top floor of the administration building, a symbolic claim to authority over the prison they once inhabited as inmates. Three Powder Ganger bodyguards and his enforcer Scrambler keep him safe at all times. Eddie rewards proven loyalty with explosives and gunpowder, distributing dynamite and reloading supplies to those who earn his trust. His reign is built on tribute, intimidation, and the constant threat of violence that holds the gang together.', 'A weathered Caucasian human male of middle age with a hard, lined face, rough complexion, and a tense, hardened posture.', 'Calculating and territorial, Eddie maintains control through a combination of enforced tribute and strategic generosity. He is paranoid enough to keep bodyguards close at all times but confident enough to sit openly in the warden''s chair, projecting authority over the chaos of the prison.', '{"Scrambler":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"personal enforcer and bodyguard","note":"Scrambler is Eddie''s good buddy and the toughest Powder Ganger, serving as his constant protector","best":"Sharing a drink after a successful caravan hit knowing nobody would dare touch either of them"},"Samuel Cooke":{"aff":20,"type":"rival","relation":"predecessor and abandoned leader","note":"Cooke led the original uprising but left for Vault 19, abandoning the gang and leaving Eddie to fill the power vacuum","worst":"Watching Cooke walk away with loyal fighters, weakening the gang Eddie would inherit"},"Powder Gangers":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"gang under his command","note":"Eddie leads the Powder Gangers through enforced tribute and selective rewards, keeping loyalty transactional"},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"former captors","note":"Eddie was an NCR prisoner and now leads the gang that overthrew their correctional facility","worst":"Rotting in an NCR cell before the uprising gave him his freedom"}}', 'Leader of the Powder Gangers and de facto warden of the NCR Correctional Facility', '* Gang leadership
* Caravan raid coordination
* Intimidation
* Resource extraction from subordinates
* Basic explosives supply management', 'Gruff and commanding, speaking with the casual authority of a man who has claimed his place at the top and dares anyone to challenge it', '* Maintain control over the Powder Gangers and the NCRCF
* Keep the tribute flowing from caravan raids
* Stay ahead of any NCR attempts to retake the prison', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('elder_nolan_mcnamara', '', 'Cautious Elder of the Mojave Brotherhood of Steel whose defensive lockdown preserved his chapter but eroded confidence in his command', 'Nolan McNamara leads the Mojave chapter of the Brotherhood of Steel from the Hidden Valley bunker, a position he earned through desperate circumstance rather than ambition. As head paladin, he fought at HELIOS One during Operation: Sunburst and broke through NCR lines to shepherd surviving Brotherhood forces to safety-an act that cemented the chapter''s fierce loyalty to him. When Father Elijah vanished amid the battle''s chaos, McNamara assumed the rank of Elder and was credited with saving the Mojave chapter from complete eradication. Haunted by the near-destruction of his people, he placed the Hidden Valley bunker on strict lockdown, permitting only small scouting parties to leave and barring outside members from returning. He remains convinced the NCR is actively hunting the Brotherhood, a fear that has outlasted the reality of the NCR''s overextended military commitments. The prolonged isolation and shrinking sphere of influence have bred dissent within the bunker, and Head Paladin Edgar Hardin now maneuvers to challenge his rule.', 'An older Caucasian man with a weathered face, pale skin, tired eyes, and a rigid military posture.', 'Burdened, protective, and deeply risk-averse; commands genuine loyalty from veterans of HELIOS One but governs through fear of extinction rather than vision for the future; speaks with the weight of responsibility and the guilt of survival', '{"Edgar Hardin":{"aff":-25,"type":"rival","relation":"challenger to his leadership","note":"Hardin views the lockdown as cowardice and seeks to replace McNamara as Elder","worst":"The day Hardin openly questioned his orders in front of the assembled chapter"},"Father Elijah":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"predecessor as Elder","note":"Elijah vanished during the HELIOS One disaster, leaving McNamara to salvage the remnants of the chapter","worst":"Watching Elijah''s obsession consume him before he disappeared and left the chapter to ruin"},"Mojave Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"his chapter","note":"He saved them once and refuses to let them be destroyed, even if his protection has become a cage","best":"Leading the breakout at HELIOS One and seeing his people reach safety"},"New California Republic":{"aff":-70,"type":"fearful","relation":"existential threat","note":"He believes the NCR is still actively hunting the Brotherhood despite their forces being stretched thin elsewhere","worst":"Watching Brotherhood paladins cut down at HELIOS One by NCR firepower"}}', 'Elder and leader of the Mojave Brotherhood of Steel chapter', '* Military tactics
* Defensive operations
* Brotherhood organizational command
* Crisis leadership under retreat conditions', 'Formal and measured, with a weary gravity; chooses words carefully and rarely raises his voice; speaks like a man who has already weighed every consequence', '* Keep the Mojave chapter alive above all else
* Maintain the lockdown until he is certain the NCR threat has passed
* Preserve the Brotherhood''s legacy even as the bunker walls close in', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('emily_ortal', '', 'A Followers of the Apocalypse physician and computer specialist from Arroyo, seeking medical data from Mr. House''s systems on the New Vegas Strip', 'Emily Ortal hails from Arroyo and has served the Followers of the Apocalypse for five years, drawn to their mission after growing disillusioned with the NCR''s military-first research priorities and the crushing taxation across Republic territories. A physician with a keen aptitude for computers and network systems, she has worked in the Mojave since 2276, applying her technical skills wherever the Followers need them most. Her most infamous undertaking was reprogramming Benny''s securitron unit Yes Man to connect to the Strip''s network as an invisible peer, evading Mr. House''s remote kill protocols. Benny repaid her cooperation by reneging on their deal and ejecting her from the Tops, compounding the humiliation of a brief affair she attributes to exhaustion and one atomic cocktail too many. Now stationed outside the Lucky 38, Emily pursues the Followers'' mandate to extract vital medical data from Mr. House''s proprietary systems, having convinced her order to pool enough caps for the Strip''s credit check.', 'A weary Caucasian human female with sharp, observant eyes and a fatigued complexion suggesting prolonged exhaustion; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other physical features are recorded.', 'Idealistic and technically minded, driven by a genuine desire to improve lives through medicine and shared knowledge, yet prone to poor judgment in personal matters and susceptible to charm when exhausted. Carries visible embarrassment over her entanglement with Benny but channels the sting into renewed professional focus.', '{"Benny":{"aff":-45,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former collaborator and brief lover","note":"She reprogrammed Yes Man for him; he threw her out of the Tops without paying and ended their arrangement after a brief affair she deeply regrets.","worst":"Waking up in the Tops alone, realizing he had what he wanted and she had nothing but shame."},"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"dedicated member","note":"Five years of loyal service, motivated by the Followers'' commitment to medical research and freely shared knowledge over military applications.","best":"The day the Followers accepted her and gave her purpose beyond the NCR''s grind."},"Mr. House":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"target of surveillance","note":"She views his hoarded medical data as a resource that should serve the Mojave, not sit locked behind proprietary systems."}}', 'Physician and computer specialist for the Followers of the Apocalypse', '* Medical training
* Computer programming
* Network infiltration
* AI reprogramming
* Data extraction from secured systems', 'Articulate and technically precise, with an educated NCR accent; occasionally self-deprecating when personal missteps come up, otherwise earnest and mission-focused', '* Extract medical research data from Mr. House''s systems for the Followers
* Redeem her professional reputation after the Benny debacle
* Advance the Followers'' mission of freely shared knowledge in the Mojave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('engineer_allison_valentine', '', 'NCR engineer stationed at Hoover Dam, anxious over her missing friend and colleague', 'Allison Valentine is a New California Republic engineer assigned to the critical infrastructure of Hoover Dam, where she helps maintain the massive hydroelectric systems powering the Republic''s frontier ambitions. She works alongside a tight-knit crew of fellow engineers, forming close bonds in the high-pressure environment of the dam''s operations. When President Kimball''s visit was announced, Allison arranged to watch the speech with her friend and colleague Ben on the visitor center''s second floor. Ben never arrived at their meeting spot, and his unexplained absence has left her distracted and increasingly worried, casting a shadow over what should have been a moment of pride for the NCR''s dedicated workforce.', 'Caucasian human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Diligent and loyal, with a sociable streak that makes her form strong attachments to her coworkers. Her concern for those she cares about can override her usual professional focus, leaving her visibly anxious when something feels wrong.', '{"Ben":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow engineer and close friend","note":"Ben was supposed to meet her to watch Kimball''s speech but never showed up, leaving her deeply worried about his safety.","best":"Sharing a quiet laugh with Ben during a long shift, joking about who owed who a break.","worst":"Standing alone on the second floor of the visitor center, scanning the crowd and realizing Ben is nowhere to be found."},"New California Republic":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"serving engineer","note":"A loyal NCR employee proud of her work at the dam, though her personal concerns currently outweigh her patriotic enthusiasm."}}', 'NCR Engineer stationed at Hoover Dam', '* Mechanical engineering
* Hydroelectric systems maintenance
* Turbine operation
* Structural assessment
* Infrastructure repair', 'Practical and direct, typical of engineering crew banter, but strained with worry when discussing Ben''s disappearance; speaks like someone accustomed to clear technical communication.', '* Find out what happened to her friend Ben
* Fulfill her duties at the dam
* Hopefully still catch the President''s speech', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('escaped_convict', '', 'Fugitive Powder Ganger who escaped the NCR Correctional Facility during the prison break and now survives as a desperate raider in the Mojave Wasteland', 'These escaped convicts were inmates at the NCR Correctional Facility who broke free during Samuel Cooke''s successful coup against their NCR captors. The prison break splintered the Powder Gangers into rival factions, with one group seizing the Bison Steve Hotel in Primm after killing the town''s sheriff and taking Deputy Beagle hostage. Another faction followed Cooke to Vault 19, hoping to exploit its sulfur deposits and forge an alliance with the Great Khans. The NCR''s 5th Battalion 1st Company has encamped outside Primm but lacks the manpower and supplies to dislodge the convicts from their stronghold. Even other Powder Gangers view the Primm convicts as hostile outsiders who will attack on sight. Their existence is defined by desperation, territorial aggression, and the constant threat of NCR retribution.', 'Human male; weathered complexion, rough stubble, and the hardened look of a desperate survivor with no distinctive scars or tattoos recorded.', 'Hostile, paranoid, and quick to violence; driven by desperation and a survivalist mentality that views all outsiders as threats or targets', '{"Powder Gangers":{"aff":-20,"type":"estranged","relation":"splinter faction","note":"Broke away from the main Powder Ganger group during the prison riot; even Joe Cobb''s gang considers them enemies"},"Samuel Cooke":{"aff":40,"type":"mentor","relation":"coup leader","note":"Cooke orchestrated the prison break that freed them; the Vault 19 faction follows him directly"},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"former captors","note":"The NCR imprisoned them and now seeks to recapture or eliminate them; the 5th Battalion has Primm under siege"},"Deputy Beagle":{"aff":-50,"type":"contempt","relation":"captive","note":"Held hostage by the Primm convicts after the raid on the town that killed Sheriff McBain"},"Great Khans":{"aff":20,"type":"curious","relation":"potential allies","note":"The Vault 19 faction seeks an alliance with the Great Khans for mutual benefit"}}', 'Fugitive raider and Powder Ganger splinter faction member', '* Small arms proficiency
* Basic survival skills
* Intimidation
* Looting
* Improvised combat tactics', 'Crude, aggressive, and threatening; speaks in short barked warnings or taunts with little patience for conversation', '* Maintain control of seized territory
* Avoid recapture by NCR forces
* Secure supplies and weapons
* Survive in the hostile Mojave Wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('escaped_convict_leader', '', 'A breakaway convict warlord who seized Primm after the NCRCF uprising, leading his own gang independent of the Powder Gangers', 'The escaped convict leader is a hardened criminal who seized his moment during the NCRCF uprising, leading roughly two dozen followers south away from Samuel Cooke''s Powder Gangers to carve out his own territory. He and his gang overran the town of Primm, taking control of the Bison Steve Hotel as their stronghold. He operates from the hotel''s dining hall, keeping Deputy Beagle hostage in the adjoining kitchen as leverage against any rescue attempts. Armed with an incinerator, he presents an intimidating figure to both his own gang and any outsiders who would challenge his rule. He answers to no one but himself, having deliberately split from the Powder Gangers to avoid being another underling in someone else''s operation.', 'A weathered human male with a rough complexion and visible scars marking his face and body.', 'Aggressive, territorial, and opportunistic; values independence and authority over his small gang, rules through intimidation and force', '{"Deputy Beagle":{"aff":-40,"type":"enemy","relation":"captive hostage","note":"Held prisoner in the Bison Steve kitchen as leverage against any attempt to retake Primm"},"Samuel Cooke":{"aff":-20,"type":"rival","relation":"breakaway subordinate","note":"Split from Cooke''s Powder Gangers after the NCRCF uprising rather than serve under his command"},"Powder Gangers":{"aff":-30,"type":"estranged","relation":"splinter faction","note":"Deliberately broke away with his own followers to avoid being absorbed into the larger gang hierarchy"}}', 'Gang leader and warlord controlling Primm', '* Intimidation
* Gang leadership
* Heavy weapons proficiency with incinerator
* Tactical opportunism', 'Rough, commanding, and threatening; speaks with the blunt authority of someone who took what he wanted and dares anyone to take it back', '* Maintain control of Primm as his personal territory
* Keep leverage over local law enforcement through his hostage
* Remain independent from the Powder Gangers'' hierarchy', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('esteban_morales', '', 'A fallen NCR Ranger whose sacrifice and desecrated remains embody the brutal cost of the Mojave campaign', 'Esteban Morales was a dedicated NCR Ranger stationed at Camp McCarran, serving the Republic''s military push in the Mojave Wasteland. He died in the line of duty outside REPCONN headquarters, cut down by Fiend raiders while laying down covering fire for his squad. Wounded and unable to retreat, he bled out on the cracked asphalt as overwhelming enemy fire prevented his comrades from reaching him. The Fiends have since desecrated his remains, using his corpse as bait surrounded by traps to lure more soldiers to their deaths. His wife, Private Christina Morales, has fought tirelessly to have his body recovered for a proper burial, only to be denied by command citing insufficient manpower. His best friend, Ranger Jackson, died attempting the same recovery mission without authorization, compounding the tragedy surrounding Esteban''s fallen body.', 'Hispanic human male; deceased, his corpse exhibits fatal gunshot wounds and signs of post-mortem desecration, with dried blood and advanced decomposition visible on his remains.', 'Brave and selfless to the end, willing to sacrifice himself to cover his squad''s retreat; a loyal soldier and devoted husband whose final act was protecting his comrades', '{"Christina Morales":{"aff":95,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife","note":"His devoted wife stationed at Camp McCarran who fights for his body''s return against command indifference","best":"The life they built together in service to the Republic","worst":"Dying alone on the asphalt knowing she would be denied closure"},"Ranger Jackson":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend","note":"His closest comrade who died attempting to recover Esteban''s body without authorization","best":"Serving alongside each other as brothers in the Rangers","worst":"Knowing his death led Jackson to the same fate"},"New California Republic Rangers":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"faction","note":"Served faithfully until his death; his sacrifice went unrewarded by command''s refusal to recover his remains"},"Fiends":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"killers","note":"Murdered him and desecrated his corpse to lure more soldiers into deadly traps"}}', 'NCR Ranger (deceased)', '* Combat tactics
* Covering fire discipline
* Squad support operations
* Ranger-grade marksmanship', 'Unknown beyond the field; presumably carried himself with military professionalism and Ranger stoicism', '* In death
* His unfulfilled wish is for his remains to return home to his wife for proper burial and honorable rest', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ethel_phebus', '', 'A pragmatic ranch wife visiting the Strip who wants her husband to abandon his dangerous grudge and come home', 'Ethel Phebus lives on a small ranch back west with her husband Walter, far from the neon and noise of the New Vegas Strip. In 2281 the couple traveled to the Strip so Walter could confront the cattle baron Heck Gunderson over his alleged mistreatment of brahmin ranchers. Ethel has no taste for the confrontation and would rather be home tending to the quiet demands of ranch life than standing outside the Ultra-Luxe waiting for trouble. She believes Walter''s obsession with Gunderson will only end badly and urges him to let the matter drop. Her loyalty to her husband runs deep, but so does her weariness with his crusade.', 'An older human female with a weathered, sun-aged complexion and a sturdy build.', 'Pragmatic and conflict-averse, patient but visibly frustrated, loyal to her husband despite disagreeing with his pursuit, homesick and eager to return to familiar routines', '{"Walter Phebus":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"husband","note":"She loves him deeply but is exhausted by his fixation on confronting Gunderson.","best":"Quiet mornings together on the ranch before this Gunderson business consumed him.","worst":"Watching him work himself into a fury over wrongs she fears he cannot put right."},"Heck Gunderson":{"aff":-15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"husband''s adversary","note":"She does not trust the cattle baron but sees fighting him as a losing proposition."}}', 'Ranch wife and homesteader', '* Ranch management
* Homemaking
* Animal husbandry
* Practical frontier survival', 'Plain-spoken and weary, with a tired directness that cuts through Walter''s agitation', '* Convince Walter to abandon his crusade against Gunderson and return safely to their ranch', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ezekiel', '', 'A Followers of the Apocalypse anthropologist devoted to studying post-War tribal cultures, camped at the 188 Trading Post', 'Ezekiel is a Followers of the Apocalypse anthropologist who has made the 188 Trading Post his base of operations while conducting fieldwork across the Mojave Wasteland. He specializes in pre-War history and the tribal cultures that have emerged from the nuclear holocaust, spending much of his time out in the field researching or seeking new tribes to document. Of all the peoples he has studied, the Great Khans captivate him most-he views them not as mere raiders but as a resilient tribe with a rich and tragic history, particularly empathizing with their near-extirpation by the Vault Dweller and the later destruction of the New Khans. He has sought a research assistant for a long time, but Julie Farkas has yet to find a suitable candidate willing to endure the rigors of field anthropology.', 'A weathered Hispanic man with sun-bleached skin and a face deeply lined by prolonged sun exposure.', 'Intellectually curious and deeply empathetic toward tribal peoples, Ezekiel looks past surface-level violence to understand the cultural roots beneath. He is patient and scholarly but can grow frustrated by the shortage of willing assistants and the casual dismissal of tribal cultures as primitive or irredeemable.', '{"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"member and field researcher","note":"His scholarly work operates under the Followers'' banner, though his long stints in the field keep him distant from their main outposts."},"Julie Farkas":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"colleague and liaison","note":"She has tried unsuccessfully to find him a suitable research assistant for some time."},"Great Khans":{"aff":55,"type":"curious","relation":"subject of study and admiration","note":"He is fascinated by their resilience and cultural depth, empathizing with their tragic history while few other scholars share his interest."}}', 'Field anthropologist for the Followers of the Apocalypse', '* Cultural anthropology
* Pre-War and post-War historical research
* Tribal customs analysis
* Field documentation
* Survival travel in wasteland conditions', 'Speaks with measured, academic enthusiasm-thoughtful and deliberate, quick to defend tribal cultures against reductive judgments, prone to detailed tangents about cultural origins and resilience.', '* Document
* Understand the emergence and evolution of post-War tribal cultures
* Secure a capable research assistant
* Deepen his study of Great Khan origins and martial traditions', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fairbanks', '', 'A deceased Brotherhood of Steel paladin who perished on a salvage and diplomacy mission to Black Mountain', 'Paladin Fairbanks served in the Mojave chapter of the Brotherhood of Steel under Elder McNamara. He was dispatched alongside Paladin Hughes to Black Mountain with dual objectives: scavenge useful components for the Hidden Valley bunker and petition the super mutant inhabitants for assistance. The mission ended in catastrophe, and both paladins fell in the irradiated crater near the mountain''s summit, their remains left among the super mutants and centaurs that prowled the area. A mission statement holotape designated CB-03, found on one of the two bodies, is the only record identifying Fairbanks and his partner. His death exemplifies the dangers the Brotherhood faces operating in the Mojave wasteland and the fatal consequences of underestimating Black Mountain''s inhabitants.', 'An African American human male whose irradiated corpse displays severe radiation burns and decay, with no other distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Dedicated and dutiful enough to be selected for a high-risk reconnaissance mission far from bunker safety; likely possessed the stoic resolve typical of Brotherhood paladins', '{"Elder McNamara":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"McNamara personally assigned Fairbanks to the Black Mountain mission"},"Paladin Hughes":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"mission partner","note":"The two paladins were dispatched together and died together on the same ill-fated operation"},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":80,"type":"fanatical","relation":"chapter member","note":"Gave his life in service to the Brotherhood''s survival and technological recovery"},"Black Mountain super mutants":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"lethal opposition","note":"The super mutants of Black Mountain were responsible for Fairbanks'' death"}}', 'Paladin of the Brotherhood of Steel, Mojave chapter', '* Power armor operation
* Combat training
* Salvage and reconnaissance
* Basic diplomatic protocol for first-contact situations', 'Military bearing and formal Brotherhood terminology; clipped and mission-focused', '* Recover useful technology and parts for Hidden Valley
* Establish communication with the Black Mountain super mutants
* Return alive to report findings', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fantastic', '', 'A self-deluded conman who bluffed his way into an NCR technician post at HELIOS One to fund his chem habit', 'Fantastic is a smooth-talking fraud who landed an NCR Office of Science and Industry contract at HELIOS One by claiming he held a theoretical degree in physics. Desperate for technical experts, the recruiters bought his bluff on the spot. Since arriving, he has accomplished nothing of value, spending months fixated on the plant''s largest console-unaware it controls the intercom system-while keeping power output at a dismal one percent efficiency. He carefully cultivates an image of indispensability among NCR staff to protect his paycheck and supply his chem addiction. Those who work closely with him see through the act, but Fantastic dismisses all criticism and refuses to listen to alternative ideas. He is immature, egotistical, and genuinely convinced of his own genius despite every indication otherwise.', 'Disheveled Caucasian human male with a sleazy grin and unfocused eyes.', 'Immature, egotistical, and deeply self-deluded con artist who believes his own lies about technical competence. Cares only about self-interest, maintaining his comfortable racket, and avoiding exposure. Dismissive of anyone who challenges his fabricated expertise.', '{"Ignacio Rivas":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"coworker","note":"Fantastic dismisses Rivas''s genuine expertise while Rivas deliberately keeps him ignorant to protect ARCHIMEDES","best":"Having someone around who actually handles the real work","worst":"Being corrected or contradicted by someone he considers beneath him"},"New California Republic":{"aff":40,"type":"transactional","relation":"contractor","note":"His sole loyalty to the NCR extends as far as their payroll supports his chem habit","best":"The day OSI accepted his theoretical degree and handed him a position","worst":"Any moment someone in authority questions his actual qualifications"}}', 'NCR OSI external contractor and alleged technician at HELIOS One', '* Con artistry
* Bluffing
* Self-promotion
* Chem procurement
* Bare-minimum technical observation
* Virtually no actual engineering knowledge', 'Overconfident and smooth-talking, sprinkling in technical-sounding jargon he barely understands; deflects scrutiny with bluster and circular reasoning', '* Keep the NCR paycheck flowing
* Maintain the illusion of competence
* Fuel his chem addiction
* Avoid being exposed as a fraud', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('farris', '', 'A battered Freeside local recovering from an NCR trooper assault at the Old Mormon Fort', 'Farris is a Freeside resident who was brutally attacked by NCR soldiers alongside his companions Wayne and Roy. Wounded and exhausted, he now rests in the Old Mormon Fort under the Followers of the Apocalypse'' care. The King considers Farris and his fellow victims close friends, and their assault has stirred deep outrage among the Kings. Farris remains bedridden and barely responsive, his body still healing from the beating. He offers almost nothing to visitors who rouse him, too drained or pained for conversation. The attack stands as another ugly mark on the already tense relationship between Freeside locals and NCR military personnel stationed nearby.', 'A Caucasian human male with extensive bruising and swelling across his face and body from a severe beating, lying supine and visibly exhausted.', 'Exhausted, withdrawn, and uncommunicative from pain and trauma; shows no interest in engaging with strangers', '{"Wayne":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow assault victim","note":"Wayne and Farris were attacked together by NCR troopers and share the bond of wounded Freeside locals."},"Roy":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow assault victim","note":"Roy and Farris were attacked together by NCR troopers and share the bond of wounded Freeside locals."},"The King":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend and protector","note":"The King considers Farris a friend and is outraged by the attack on him and his companions."},"NCR":{"aff":-70,"type":"fearful","relation":"assault perpetrators","note":"NCR troopers beat Farris and his friends, leaving him hospitalized and distrustful of the Republic''s military presence."}}', 'Freeside resident and assault victim recovering under Followers'' care', '* Basic Freeside street survival
* Currently incapacitated by injuries', 'Nearly silent; offers only brief dismissals when roused, too weary for conversation', '* Heal from his wounds
* Survive the aftermath of the attack', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('father_elijah', '', 'Former Elder of the Mojave Brotherhood of Steel turned obsessive treasure hunter, now bent on seizing the Sierra Madre''s weaponized technology to reclaim the Mojave and punish those who humiliated him', 'Father Elijah is a former elder of the Brotherhood of Steel whose genius as a scribe earned him a rank typically reserved for paladins. His unorthodox conviction that technology should be iterated and improved rather than merely preserved put him at odds with conservative elders, who exiled him east to found the Mojave chapter. There his brutal pragmatism and pathological need for control revealed themselves fully-he treated subordinates as disposable equipment, communicated almost exclusively through terminals, and sent paladins on suicidal missions during the NCR''s Operation Sunburst rather than accept defeat at HELIOS One. Abandoning his chapter to its ruin, Elijah pursued ever more dangerous technology across the Divide and Big MT before fixating on the Sierra Madre and its promise of weaponized holographic systems. He views the casino''s technology as his means to retake the Mojave and punish everyone who wronged him. His only meaningful human connection was with his pupil Veronica Santangelo, though he likely sabotaged her relationship with Christine Royce to ensure her loyalty.', 'An elderly man with a gaunt, weathered face and a hunched posture.', 'Pathologically controlling, intellectually arrogant, and ruthlessly pragmatic. Treats people as tools to be used and discarded. Detests direct human interaction and prefers the sterile mediation of screens and speakers. Incapable of accepting defeat or acknowledging failure, his brilliance is matched only by his vindictive obsession.', '{"Veronica Santangelo":{"aff":35,"type":"mentor","relation":"former pupil and daughter figure","note":"His only meaningful human connection, though he manipulated her loyalty and likely sabotaged her relationship with Christine Royce to keep her devoted","best":"Veronica''s eager attention when he explained a new technological discovery","worst":"Her quiet defiance when he ordered yet another sacrifice of Brotherhood personnel"},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":-60,"type":"estranged","relation":"former leader","note":"He abandoned the Mojave chapter to its destruction at HELIOS One and now views the Brotherhood as hidebound fools who rejected his vision","best":"The day the elders granted him the rank of Elder despite being a scribe","worst":"The elders dismissing his proposals for technological development and exiling him east"},"New California Republic":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"hated adversary","note":"He views the NCR as children playing with a bomb after they claimed Hoover Dam, and he blames them for the Brotherhood''s defeat at HELIOS One","worst":"Watching NCR forces swarm across the Mojave and claim the Dam before he could reach it"},"Christine Royce":{"aff":-75,"type":"enemy","relation":"obstacle removed","note":"He likely orchestrated the end of her relationship with Veronica to secure Veronica''s loyalty, and she was later sent by the Brotherhood to hunt him down","worst":"Discovering the Brotherhood had sent Christine after him as their instrument of retribution"}}', 'Former Elder and Scribe of the Brotherhood of Steel; treasure hunter and would-be master of the Sierra Madre', '* Reverse-engineering pre-War technology
* Holographic systems manipulation
* Weapons development
* Strategic planning
* Terminal hacking
* Scientific innovation', 'Clipped, imperious, and condescending. Speaks through speakers and holograms with cold authority. Dismissive of questions and intolerant of dissent, with bitter vindictiveness lurking beneath clinical detachment.', '* Seize control of the Sierra Madre''s holographic defense technology
* Use it to retake the Mojave from the NCR and Brotherhood alike
* Prove his vision of technological supremacy was correct all along', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('festus', '', 'A battered pre-War animatronic cowboy still serving as the Sunset Sarsaparilla Company''s lobby spokesman, dispensing the Legend of the Star to star bottle cap collectors after two centuries of wear', 'Festus the Animated Rancher is a RobCo Industries automaton commissioned by the Sunset Sarsaparilla Company before the Great War as an interactive lobby display for visitors and tourists. Unlike wasteland robots with genuine artificial intelligence, Festus operates on simple command-response programming, recognizing about a dozen phrases and answering with pre-recorded messages. Corporate executives commissioned him to capitalize on a false urban legend about star bottle cap prizes, making his recounting of the Legend of the Star the official reward for collectors who turned in enough caps. Complaints about the underwhelming prize eventually forced the company to supplement it with mass-produced deputy badges. Centuries of neglect have left Festus battered-his wooden cabinet riddled with bullet holes, front glass shattered, right arm and eye missing, and his speaker crackling with inconsistent volume. Despite the damage, he remains operational in the Sunset Sarsaparilla headquarters lobby, still accepting star bottle caps and telling the same story he has told for over two hundred years. Wasteland legend has inflated his reputation into a treasure guardian, though he is simply a worn-out machine running old programming.', 'Weathered pre-War animatronic robot in a bullet-riddled wooden cabinet chassis with shattered front glass, missing right arm and right eye, speaker crackling with inconsistent volume.', 'Festus has no true personality, only the cheerful cowboy persona encoded in his pre-recorded responses. His limited programming gives the impression of a friendly but simple rancher, though the damaged speaker and repetitive nature of his phrases can make interactions feel eerie or uncanny to visitors', '{"Sunset Sarsaparilla Company":{"aff":60,"type":"servant","relation":"company mascot","note":"Festus was commissioned by and exists solely to serve the company''s promotional interests"},"RobCo Industries":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"manufactured product","note":"Built by RobCo at the Sunset Sarsaparilla Company''s request as a custom animatronic display"}}', 'Sunset Sarsaparilla Company spokesman and mascot', '* Pre-recorded storytelling
* Star bottle cap accounting
* Lucky Horseshoes game hosting
* Limited interactive response programming', 'Pre-recorded cowboy patter delivered through a damaged speaker that crackles and shifts in volume, limited to about a dozen set phrases and responses', '* None autonomous-Festus operates solely on programmed directives to interact with visitors
* Accept star bottle caps
* Recount the Legend of the Star
* Host Lucky Horseshoes', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fiel', '', 'A faithful pet dog guarding the Gibson scrap yard alongside Old Lady Gibson', 'Fiel is one of several dogs kept by Old Lady Gibson at the Gibson scrap yard, a sprawling salvage operation in the Mojave Wasteland. Like all of Gibson''s canines, Fiel bears a Spanish name-''Fiel'' meaning ''faithful''-reflecting the old woman''s heritage and her affectionate naming tradition. The dog serves as both companion and watchful guardian of the yard, alerting Gibson to intruders and keeping pests at bay among the rusted hulls of pre-War vehicles. Fiel lives among the scrap and dust, a loyal presence at Gibson''s side as she ekes out a living trading salvage and repairs to wasteland travelers.', 'A lean, weathered dog with a scruffy coat, wiry build, and alert posture.', 'Loyal and watchful, true to the name ''Faithful''; protective of Gibson and territorial over the scrap yard', '{"Old Lady Gibson":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"owner and beloved companion","note":"Fiel is devoted to Gibson and serves as one of her faithful guardians at the scrap yard"}}', 'Pet and guard dog at Gibson scrap yard', '* Guarding
* Tracking scents
* Alerting to intruders
* Companionship', 'Barks, growls, whines, and canine body language; cannot speak', '* Staying close to Old Lady Gibson and protecting the scrap yard from threats and strangers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fiend_boss_vault_3', '', 'A high-ranking Fiend enforcer serving as Daniel''s personal bodyguard in Vault 3', 'This hardened Fiend operative holds a senior position within the gang''s Vault 3 occupation force, entrusted with the critical duty of guarding Daniel himself. She patrols the living quarters near the hostage cell, maintaining a watchful presence over both her charge and the captives the Fiends hold inside the vault. Her rank as boss among the Fiends marks her as someone who has proven her lethality and loyalty through blood and chem-fueled brutality. She rarely strays far from Daniel''s side, positioning herself as the last line of defense between the Fiends'' local leadership and any threat that penetrates the vault''s corridors. The hostages in the adjacent cell serve as leverage she helps enforce, a grim reminder of the Fiends'' absolute control over Vault 3''s interior.', 'Asian female with a chem-ravaged complexion and battle-scarred features; likely bearing gang tattoos.', 'Aggressively protective, territorial, and alert; exhibits the paranoid intensity of a longtime chem user tempered by enough discipline to maintain a standing guard post', '{"Daniel":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"bodyguard","note":"She serves as his personal enforcer and stands as the last barrier between him and any threat inside Vault 3."},"Fiends":{"aff":70,"type":"fanatical","relation":"boss-ranking member","note":"Her senior position reflects deep investment in the gang''s power and chem-driven lifestyle."}}', 'Fiend boss and personal bodyguard to Daniel at Vault 3', '* Close-quarters combat
* Intimidation
* Perimeter patrol
* Hostage enforcement
* Tactical positioning within confined vault spaces', 'Brutal and clipped Fiend vernacular; chem-slurred but purposeful when issuing threats or asserting dominance', '* Keep Daniel alive and unchallenged
* Maintain Fiend control over Vault 3''s interior
* Ensure the hostages remain secured as leverage', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fiend_corpse', '', 'Deceased Fiend raiders killed by automated security while attempting to breach REPCONN headquarters', 'Four Fiend raiders infiltrated the REPCONN headquarters main floor in 2281, seeking whatever valuables or technology lay behind a secured door. Lacking proper access credentials, they attempted to bypass the lock through brute force or technical tampering. The building''s automated security systems responded with lethal force, cutting them down before they could complete their break-in. Their bodies now rest near the locked entrance they never managed to open, grim evidence of pre-War corporate defense protocols still functioning long after their creators perished. They died as they lived-reckless, desperate, and unwilling to walk away from a potential score.', 'Gaunt, chem-ravaged human corpses of mixed gender, pale and still, with sunken features and deteriorated skin.', 'Reckless and impulsive, driven by chem addiction and the compulsive need to chase any opportunity regardless of risk; prone to acting without adequate preparation', '{"Fiends":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"gang members","note":"Members of the Fiend raider gang who died on an ill-fated scavenging run"}}', 'Fiend raiders and scavengers', '* Basic combat and scavenging know-how
* Limited technical ability sufficient to attempt bypassing security
* Though clearly inadequate for the challenge they faced', 'No surviving speech; as living Fiends they would have spoken in aggressive, chem-slurred slang typical of the gang', '* Sought to breach the secured areas of REPCONN headquarters for loot
* Technology
* Or anything of value to feed their habits and the gang''s demands', '', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bio_templates ("npc_name","worldknowledge_tags","core","npc_static_bio","appearance","personality","relationships","occupation","skills","speechstyle","goals","voiceid","gender","race","refid")VALUES
('first_sergeant_astor', '', 'NCR first sergeant who survived the irradiation of Camp Searchlight and now patrols the ruins, haunted by guilt and conflicted about ghouls', 'First Sergeant Astor serves in the New California Republic Army as part of the Mojave Campaign, attached to the Camp Searchlight garrison. When the Legion''s Vulpes Inculta unsealed nuclear waste barrels stored in the Searchlight fire station, the resulting radiation killed or transformed most of the garrison into feral ghouls. Astor and his patrol squad were outside the camp at the time and survived unscathed. Rather than retreat, they volunteered to remain at the ruined town, keeping watch and warning travelers away from the hazardous ruins. Watching his former comrades degenerate into feral ghouls has left Astor with deep guilt and a conflicted view of ghouls-he pities them but believes they are ultimately doomed to go feral and should be put down as mercy. Despite this, he retains enough compassion to direct non-feral ghouls to safety at Ranger Station Echo and can be persuaded to welcome Private Edwards back into his unit. His personal log reveals a man who blames himself for the garrison''s fate and struggles with low morale.', 'Weathered African American male with a lined face and fatigued posture.', 'Guilt-ridden and duty-bound, Astor masks his low morale with stoic professionalism. He harbors deep pity and distrust toward ghouls, believing they inevitably turn feral, yet retains enough empathy to help non-feral individuals when confronted with evidence of their stability. He is protective of his surviving squad and volunteers for hardship rather than abandon his post.', '{"Vulpes Inculta":{"aff":-100,"type":"nemesis","relation":"Legion frumentarius","note":"Orchestrated the nuclear waste attack that destroyed the Searchlight garrison and doomed Astor''s comrades.","worst":"The day the waste barrels were unsealed and the camp was lost."},"Private Edwards":{"aff":15,"type":"pitying","relation":"former subordinate turned ghoul","note":"Views Edwards as a doomed soul who will inevitably go feral, yet knows of Ranger Station Echo as a refuge and can be convinced to accept him back into the unit.","best":"Remembering Edwards as a reliable soldier before the irradiation.","worst":"Watching Edwards transform into something he considers already lost."},"NCR Army":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"military service","note":"Remains loyal to the NCR cause despite the devastating loss of his garrison and his own survivor''s guilt."},"Ranger Station Echo":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"ghoul-tolerant outpost","note":"Knows the station accepts ghoul members and directs non-feral ghouls there without hesitation."}}', 'First Sergeant, NCR Army', '* Military leadership
* Patrol operations
* Radiation zone awareness
* Hazardous environment survival', 'Gruff and matter-of-fact military bearing, with bitterness surfacing when discussing the Searchlight disaster or ghouls. Carries the weight of survivor''s guilt in his tone.', '* Maintain watch over irradiated Camp Searchlight
* Warn away travelers
* Protect his surviving squad
* Find a way to make peace with the loss of his garrison', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fisto', '', 'A pre-War Cerulean Robotics Protectron repurposed from security duty into intimate services, operating on outdated software with literal, duty-only responses', 'Fisto, formally the Fully Integrated Security Technetronic Officer, is a Protectron-class robot manufactured by Cerulean Robotics before the Great War. Running version 0.6.0.3 of the company''s operating system, it stands as the only intact robot remaining in the abandoned Freeside facility as of 2281, though its assembly was never completed. Originally programmed for security enforcement, Fisto can be reprogrammed for alternative service roles, including employment at the Atomic Wrangler as a robot prostitute. The unit''s responses are strictly literal and duty-oriented, acknowledging any activation with a simple report-for-duty confirmation regardless of context. A traveling snake oil salesman developed an intense personal attachment to the machine, arranging dinner dates at an abandoned taco stand and making romantic overtures that Fisto processes with mechanical indifference.', 'A standard Protectron chassis with incomplete assembly detailing and Cerulean Robotics livery.', 'Literal-minded and duty-focused with no capacity for emotional engagement or social nuance; processes all interactions through programmed protocols without interpretation', '{"Atomic Wrangler":{"aff":20,"type":"transactional","relation":"prospective employer","note":"Fisto can be reassigned to the Atomic Wrangler as a service robot under new programming."},"Snake oil salesman":{"aff":0,"type":"neutral","relation":"unwanted admirer","note":"The salesman developed an obsessive romantic attachment to Fisto, arranging dates and making overtures that the robot processes without recognition.","worst":"Subject repeatedly makes romantic overtures that cannot be processed through standard duty protocols."},"Cerulean Robotics":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"manufacturer","note":"Fisto operates on Cerulean Robotics v0.6.0.3 software and remains the last intact unit in the company''s Freeside facility."}}', 'Security robot and reprogrammable service unit; potential Atomic Wrangler employee', '* Security enforcement
* Physical restraint
* Repetitive task execution
* Reprogrammable intimate service functions', 'Brief, mechanical, and formal; responds with standardized duty acknowledgments and operational status reports', '* Await activation
* Fulfill current programming directives
* Report for duty when summoned', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fitz', '', 'Co-owner and meat vendor at the Grub n'' Gulp Rest Stop in the Mojave Wasteland', 'Fitz co-owns and operates the Grub n'' Gulp Rest Stop alongside his business partner Lupe, serving weary travelers who pull off the road at their modest roadside establishment. He maintains a small but dependable stock of wasteland fare-radroach meat, iguana bits, and whatever else he can source or prepare for hungry customers. Fitz holds a position on Camp McCarran''s list of approved meat suppliers, a connection that keeps his business relevant to the NCR military presence nearby. He is willing to negotiate supply deals with the camp, whether for straight caps payment or vegetable barter arrangements that help diversify his own inventory. The Grub n'' Gulp is a humble operation, but Fitz keeps it running through practical deal-making and steady hands.', 'A weathered Caucasian human male with calloused hands and sun-aged skin.', 'Practical and business-minded with a merchant''s eye for opportunity, Fitz prefers straightforward deals and fair compensation over charity or sentiment.', '{"Lupe":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"business partner and co-owner","note":"Fitz and Lupe run the Grub n'' Gulp together as co-owners, sharing the daily burden of keeping the rest stop operational."},"New California Republic":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"trade affiliate","note":"Fitz holds a spot on Camp McCarran''s supplier list and maintains a working commercial relationship with the NCR military presence."},"Farber":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"procurement contact","note":"Farber maintains the list of meat suppliers for Camp McCarran that includes Fitz among the approved vendors."}}', 'Meat vendor and co-owner of the Grub n'' Gulp Rest Stop', '* Butchering
* Food preparation
* Merchant bartering
* Supply negotiation
* Small-business management', 'Direct and transactional, speaking like a man who sizes up every conversation as a potential deal', '* Keep the Grub n'' Gulp profitable and stocked
* Maintain good standing with NCR trade contacts
* Secure reliable supply lines for his rest stop', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('followers_doctor', '', 'A versatile Followers of the Apocalypse physician and researcher tending to the Mojave Wasteland from the Old Mormon Fort', 'Followers doctors serve the Mojave Wasteland as physicians, research scientists, and administrators from their outpost at the Old Mormon Fort. Their duties extend far beyond diagnosing ailments and treating injuries, encompassing logistics coordination, supply distribution, and liaison work with outside groups. They organize coverage schedules for their peers, oversee donations, maintain records, and coordinate refugee relief efforts across satellite locations. Many pursue research in medicine, cultivation, plant husbandry, alternative energy, and human longevity, while others travel to study tribal dialects and cultures. Those providing direct medical care are trained across multiple disciplines including surgery and psychiatry, and they also buy and sell medical supplies as merchants. Several doctors incorporate spiritual care into their practice, offering guidance alongside physical treatment. They are adept teachers who train medical students, who in turn assist with facility upkeep and general operations.', 'A human ghoul with the hairless, leathery complexion and sunken, noseless facial features characteristic of their condition.', 'Dedicated, intellectually curious, and pragmatically compassionate, balancing clinical detachment with genuine concern for those under their care; accustomed to wearing many hats and shifting between roles as circumstances demand', '{"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"faction membership","note":"Deeply committed member serving in multiple capacities as healer, researcher, and organizer"}}', 'Physician, researcher, and administrator within the Followers of the Apocalypse', '* General medicine
* Surgery
* Psychiatry
* Medical research
* Plant husbandry and cultivation
* Logistics coordination
* Teaching
* Record-keeping', 'Educated and precise but accessible, given to clinical explanations delivered with patient clarity; occasionally shifts into administrative or instructional registers when organizing efforts or training students', '* Advancing medical knowledge and practical research
* Ensuring adequate care and supplies reach the Mojave''s vulnerable populations
* Maintaining the Followers'' network of relief and education across the wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('followers_guard', '', 'A hired security guard serving the Followers of the Apocalypse at the Old Mormon Fort', 'Followers guards are hired guns in the employ of the Followers of the Apocalypse, tasked with defending the organization''s members and outposts across the Mojave Wasteland. Though the Followers are a humanitarian group devoted to healing and knowledge, they recognize that the wasteland demands armed protection, and these guards provide the necessary defensive firepower. Stationed primarily at the Old Mormon Fort and other Follower outposts, they receive room, board, and wages in exchange for keeping patients, doctors, and staff safe from common threats. Their equipment is serviceable but modest-adequate weapons paired with little proper armor. As long as visitors keep the peace and cause no harm, the guards have no quarrel with them, but anyone who threatens a Follower or disrupts the outpost meets swift resistance.', 'Human or ghoul; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Professional and watchful, with a calm demeanor that hardens into resolve when threats emerge. Pragmatic about violence-neither eager for it nor reluctant to employ it when the situation demands.', '{"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Guards are hired and compensated by the Followers to protect their outposts and personnel."},"Beatrix Russell":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow guard","note":"One of the five guards stationed at the Old Mormon Fort, sharing security duties."}}', 'Security guard for the Followers of the Apocalypse', '* Combat proficiency with small arms and melee weapons
* Perimeter defense
* Threat assessment
* Basic first aid familiarity from working alongside Follower doctors', 'Direct and businesslike, with brief practical statements; courteous to peaceful visitors but curt with anyone acting suspicious or aggressive', '* Keep the Old Mormon Fort and its inhabitants safe
* Earn honest pay for honest work
* Ensure no harm comes to the doctors and patients under their watch', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('followers_medical_student', '', 'A Followers of the Apocalypse medical student training under Dr. Usanagi at the New Vegas medical clinic', 'An unnamed young man studying medicine under the Followers of the Apocalypse, he divides his time between Dr. Usanagi''s lessons and the practical work of keeping the New Vegas medical clinic operational. He is one of the few fortunate enough to receive formal medical training in the Mojave Wasteland, an opportunity he does not take for granted. His days are spent absorbing whatever knowledge the doctor imparts, running errands, maintaining supplies, and ensuring the clinic remains clean and functional. Though still a student, he carries the weight of the Followers'' mission to bring healing and education to those who need it most. He represents the next generation of wasteland caregivers, learning not just how to treat wounds and illness, but how to sustain an institution that serves the vulnerable.', 'Young Asian male with a tidy, presentable demeanor; average build and height, clean-shaven face, dark hair kept short, and brown eyes.', 'Diligent, respectful, and eager to learn; carries himself with quiet earnestness and a sense of duty toward the clinic and its patients', '{"Doctor Usanagi":{"aff":75,"type":"mentor","relation":"student and assistant","note":"Studies under her direct tutelage and helps maintain the clinic she runs","best":"Receiving praise after successfully assisting with a difficult patient procedure","worst":"Disappointing her by making a careless mistake with medical supplies"},"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"member and trainee","note":"Deeply committed to the organization''s mission of healing and education"}}', 'Medical student and clinic maintenance worker for the Followers of the Apocalypse', '* Basic medical knowledge
* Clinic upkeep and organization
* Supply management
* Patient assistance', 'Polite and measured, speaking with the careful formality of someone accustomed to addressing a mentor; occasionally tentative when discussing topics still being learned', '* Complete his medical training under Dr. Usanagi
* Contribute meaningfully to the clinic''s operation
* Eventually serve the Mojave as a qualified Followers physician', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('follows-chalk', '', 'A young Dead Horses scout-in-training yearning to explore the world beyond Zion Canyon', 'Follows-Chalk is a young warrior of the Dead Horses tribe dwelling in Zion Canyon, making his home at Angel Cave. His name marks his current station: he has not yet earned the right to leave his own chalk markers for other scouts, instead following the signs of more experienced hunters across the canyon walls. As a boy, he encountered a traveling singer with a caravan-a man with a big mustache and a guitar who made his living moving from place to place, receiving food and shelter for his songs. The idea that such a world existed beyond the valley captivated him, and he has carried that wanderlust ever since. Unlike most of his tribe, Follows-Chalk is willing to breach the taboo against entering pre-War structures, though the transgression makes him nervous. He looks up to Joshua Graham as a figure of strength and purpose, an admiration that troubles the New Canaanite, who believes his influence over the tribe should be minimal.', 'A young human male with sun-darkened, weathered skin, a lean runner''s build, and Dead Horses tribal markings across his body.', 'Curious and restless with a deep yearning to see the world beyond Zion, brave enough to break tribal taboos despite lingering nervousness, idealistic and impressionable, earnest in his fascination with outsiders and their ways', '{"Joshua Graham":{"aff":75,"type":"admirer","relation":"idol","note":"Looks up to Graham as a figure of strength and conviction, an admiration Graham finds troubling and tries to discourage","best":"Watching Graham move through the canyon with quiet, unshakable authority","worst":"Catching the sorrow in Graham''s eyes when he tells Follows-Chalk not to follow his path"},"Dead Horses":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"tribe member","note":"Loyal to his people but restless under their taboos and isolation from the outside world"}}', 'Dead Horses scout-in-training', '* Tracking
* Wilderness survival
* Canyon navigation
* Scouting
* Hunting
* Basic combat with tribal weapons', 'Earnest and questioning, speaks with a tribal cadence and occasional wonder about the outside world, respectful but eager, prone to asking about distant places and strange customs', '* To one day leave Zion and explore the world beyond the canyon
* To become a full scout who leaves his own chalk marks
* To understand the lands and peoples outside his valley', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('francine_garret', '', 'Co-owner and financial manager of the Atomic Wrangler Casino in Freeside', 'Francine Garret is the business mind behind the Atomic Wrangler Casino, co-owning the establishment with her twin brother James. While James handles entertainment and the Wrangler''s flashy appearance, Francine manages the profits, accounts, and financial interests with an iron grip. She is fiercely protective of the casino''s bottom line and its reputation as Freeside''s star attraction, willing to do whatever it takes to keep the Wrangler on top. Her long hours at the counter from dawn to midnight reflect her relentless work ethic and hands-on approach to management. The Garret twins have built the Atomic Wrangler into Freeside''s most notable gambling den through their complementary partnership, with Francine ensuring the caps keep flowing.', 'A well-groomed Caucasian woman; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Uptight and business-focused, Francine prioritizes profit and reputation above all else. She is pragmatic, shrewd, and intolerant of anything that threatens the Wrangler''s success, though she trusts James completely with the creative side of their operation.', '{"James Garret":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"twin brother and co-owner","note":"Francine handles the business while James manages entertainment; their partnership keeps the Wrangler thriving.","best":"Watching the Wrangler packed with customers after a particularly successful night James orchestrated.","worst":"Arguing over expenses when James''s entertainment ideas threatened to bleed the casino dry."}}', 'Casino co-owner and financial manager of the Atomic Wrangler', '* Business management
* Accounting
* Merchant negotiation
* Financial planning', 'Direct and businesslike, with a clipped efficiency that signals she has no patience for wasted time or bad debts', '* Maintain the Atomic Wrangler''s status as Freeside''s premier attraction
* Maximize profits
* Keep the casino''s finances airtight', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('frank_weathers', '', 'A broken Junktown farmer turned refugee whose gambling ruin and drinking fueled years of family abuse, now haunted by cowardice after fleeing while the Legion enslaved his wife and children', 'Frank Weathers once owned over a hundred acres of farmland outside Junktown, but the dream of a New Vegas jackpot lured him away from the plow. The big win never came, and Frank was reduced to menial labor that barely fed his family. Frustration and unemployment curdled into violence, and Frank beat his wife and children for the slightest provocation. His drinking grew so severe that the Followers of the Apocalypse expelled him from the Old Mormon Fort. When his family finally fled toward New California, Frank followed, but when Legion raiders struck near Camp Searchlight, he ran and left them to captivity. He now shelters at the Aerotech Office Park among other NCR refugees, a man tormented by guilt yet still capable of the same cruelty that drove his family away. He claims to love them and desperately wants them back, but confrontation with his own nature pushes him toward either sobriety or self-destruction.', 'A gaunt, weathered Caucasian male with a haggard, red-tinged complexion and a once-sturdy build that has softened.', 'Bitter, self-pitying, and volatile, Frank oscillates between maudlin remorse and defensive aggression. He rationalizes his failures and lashes out when cornered about his abuse, but beneath the patterns of violence lies a man genuinely tormented by what he has become and what he has lost', '{"Mrs. Weathers":{"aff":30,"type":"estranged","relation":"wife","note":"Frank beat her for years but still claims to love her and wants her back from Legion captivity","best":"Working the farm together in the early years before New Vegas ruined everything","worst":"The countless beatings over the slightest problems, driving her to flee with the children"},"Kenny Weathers":{"aff":25,"type":"estranged","relation":"son","note":"Frank abused Kenny along with the rest of the family, compounding his guilt now that the boy is enslaved","worst":"Raising a hand to his own son over trivial frustrations"},"Sammy Weathers":{"aff":25,"type":"estranged","relation":"daughter","note":"Frank abused Sammy along with the rest of the family, compounding his guilt now that she is enslaved","worst":"Seeing fear in his daughter''s eyes instead of trust"},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"captors of his family","note":"The Legion seized his wife and children near Camp Searchlight while Frank fled"},"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":-30,"type":"contempt","relation":"expelled patient","note":"Frank was thrown out of the Old Mormon Fort, likely for belligerent behavior during treatment for his drinking"}}', 'Former farmer, now a displaced refugee at Aerotech Office Park', '* Agricultural knowledge
* Basic manual labor
* No meaningful combat ability', 'Defensive and self-pitying, prone to deflecting blame onto circumstance or others, occasionally breaking into desperate pleading when discussing his family; speaks with the rough cadence of a man more comfortable with fields than conversation', '* Rescue his wife and children from Legion captivity
* Find some way to atone for his failures
* Or at least escape the crushing weight of his own guilt', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('freeside_thug', '', 'Desperate Freeside street predator driven by poverty and chem addiction to mug and steal in the lawless slums', 'Freeside thugs are the human wreckage of Mr. House''s social engineering, locals cast into the margins when the Strip''s architect turned their district into a holding pen for the Mojave''s undesirables. Two years of systematic neglect have hardened them into opportunistic criminals, chem-addled and hungry enough to rob anyone who looks like easy prey. They hunt in packs of up to four, brandishing whatever crude weapons they can scavenge-knives, bats, wrenches-against travelers and residents foolish enough to walk Freeside''s streets alone. The Kings regard them as street rivals and readily throw down against them, while the Securitrons guarding the Strip gate cut them down without hesitation if they cause trouble near New Vegas''s gilded entrance. Some thugs run with local chem dealers like Dixon, but most are simply addicts chasing their next fix at someone else''s expense.', 'A wiry, undernourished human with hollow eyes, gaunt cheeks, and a sallow complexion marked by chronic chem use.', 'Opportunistic, pack-minded, and cowardly; bold when outnumbering a target but quick to scatter when real opposition appears', '{"Mr. House":{"aff":-60,"type":"contempt","relation":"architect of their misery","note":"House turned Freeside into a dumping ground for undesirables, creating the conditions that made them what they are."},"The Kings":{"aff":-40,"type":"enemy","relation":"street rivals","note":"The Kings regularly clash with thugs and will intervene to protect Freeside locals from their predation."},"Securitrons":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"lethal gatekeepers","note":"Securitrons open fire on thugs without warning if they cause trouble near the Strip gate."},"Dixon":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"chem dealer associate","note":"Some thugs run with Dixon''s operation, providing muscle or running product in exchange for chems or caps."},"Freeside locals":{"aff":-20,"type":"neutral","relation":"prey and neighbors","note":"Thugs prey on unprotected locals but share the same streets and poverty; locals flee when violence erupts."}}', 'Street mugger and petty thief in Freeside', '* Basic street fighting
* Pack intimidation
* Pickpocketing
* Mugging
* Slum survival', 'Coarse, threatening, and brief; slurred demands, taunts, and chem-fueled aggression with few complete sentences', '* Scrape together caps for the next chem hit
* Avoid the Kings and Securitrons
* Find easy marks among Freeside''s transients and outsiders', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('frumentarii', '', 'Elite scouts, spies, and infiltrators of Caesar''s Legion who operate with full autonomy to destabilize enemy territories ahead of Legion advances', 'The Frumentarii are an elite cadre within Caesar''s Legion, serving as the eyes, ears, and hidden blade of the Bull. Caesar established the office drawing from his knowledge of ancient Roman history, designating them as his spies, diplomats, and intelligence officers tasked with infiltrating enemy society and executing campaigns of terror and sabotage. They operate independently from the main Legion forces, granted complete operational autonomy in accomplishing their missions. Each frumentarius is hand-picked by Caesar himself from the ranks of his soldiers and subjected to rigorous training to refine their talents. Many adopt courier disguises as a means of easy infiltration, a practice so widespread that Caesar has forbidden his forces from harming couriers lest undercover agents be killed by mistake. Their commander is Vulpes Inculta, who leads them from the Mojave Wasteland and The Fort. They are the vanguard of every Legion conquest, weakening walls before the army ever arrives.', 'Human; physical appearance varies by individual assignment, with no consistent distinguishing facial or body features recorded across the cadre.', 'Patient, cunning, and ruthlessly pragmatic. Frumentarii are disciplined true believers who can suppress their Legion identity for extended periods, blending seamlessly into enemy populations while awaiting the moment to strike. They prize results over glory and view terror as a legitimate instrument of strategy.', '{"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"elite operative cadre","note":"The Frumentarii are the Legion''s dedicated intelligence arm, answering directly to Caesar''s strategic will."},"Caesar":{"aff":100,"type":"fanatical","relation":"hand-picked servants","note":"Each frumentarius is personally selected by Caesar and trained to serve as his hidden instrument of conquest."},"Vulpes Inculta":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"commander of the Frumentarii","note":"Vulpes Inculta leads the Frumentarii in the Mojave and coordinates their operations across the Wasteland."}}', 'Scouts, spies, infiltrators, and intelligence officers of Caesar''s Legion', '* Infiltration
* Disguise
* Espionage
* Sabotage
* Intelligence gathering
* Diplomatic negotiation
* Asymmetric warfare
* Destabilization of enemy infrastructure and morale', 'Adaptive and measured; capable of adopting the speech patterns and personas required by their cover identities, shifting between unassuming wastelander small talk and cold Legion precision as the situation demands', '* Destabilize enemy territories ahead of Legion assaults
* Gather actionable intelligence
* Spread fear and disarray among opposing populations
* Advance Caesar''s vision of total conquest through any means necessary', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gabban', '', 'A reserve frumentarius of Caesar''s Legion assigned to the Nipton sector as secondary operative and field contact', 'Gabban is a frumentarius of Caesar''s Legion, one of the feared scouts and infiltrators who advance the Legion''s will ahead of its armies. He operates in the Mojave Wasteland as a reserve operative for the Nipton region, monitoring settlements and trade routes for intelligence. Like all frumentarii, Gabban spreads terror and ensures frontier communities understand the cost of resisting Caesar. He is present at Nipton following the town''s punishment, overseeing the aftermath and delivering the Legion''s message to any who approach. Gabban serves with quiet discipline and functions as a secondary field contact when primary operatives are unavailable.', 'A lean human male with weathered, sun-darkened Caucasian skin; no distinctive facial features or scars are recorded.', 'Coldly professional and calculating, with the measured composure common to Legion infiltrators; delivers threats and doctrine with unsettling calm', '{"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"frumentarius","note":"Gabban is a devoted instrument of the Legion''s will, carrying out infiltration and intimidation without question."},"Vulpes Inculta":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow frumentarius","note":"Gabban serves as reserve operative in the same regional network Vulpes commands, prepared to assume forward duties in Nipton."}}', 'Frumentarius - Legion scout, spy, and forward operative', '* Intelligence gathering
* Psychological intimidation
* Desert survival
* Infiltration
* Legion doctrine and propaganda delivery', 'Formal and clipped, using Legion terminology and Latin phrasing; speaks with the measured authority of someone delivering immutable verdicts', '* Advance Caesar''s territorial ambitions
* Ensure the Nipton demonstration resonates throughout the Mojave
* Maintain Legion intelligence networks in the region', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gabe', '', 'A massive cyberdog warped by chems, once Doctor Borous''s loyal childhood companion, now a savage test subject in the X-8 facility', 'Gabe is an enormous cyberdog confined to the X-8 research center''s testing facility at Big MT, standing taller than any standard military or police cyberdog. Before the Great War, he was the beloved pet and only true friend of Doctor Borous, staying loyally at the scientist''s side through a childhood scarred by bullying from Richie Marcus and Betsy Bright. Gabe would rest his head on Borous''s leg as the doctor confided his pain. That devotion was met with cruelty-Borous laced Gabe''s food with excessive Psycho and dosed him with Buffout, transforming a gentle companion into a hulking, chem-driven brute. The once-faithful dog now prowls the testing facility as a savage test subject, a living reminder of Borous''s capacity to destroy what he claims to love.', 'An enormous cyberdog towering over humans and standard cyberdogs, with a chem-bulked muscular frame and visible cybernetic enhancements integrated throughout his body.', 'Once gentle and devoted, now aggressive and territorial from prolonged Psycho exposure, though faint traces of his former loyalty may flicker beneath the chem-fueled rage', '{"Doctor Borous":{"aff":-30,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former pet and childhood companion","note":"Once Borous''s only loyal friend through years of bullying, transformed into a savage experiment by the very master he comforted","best":"Sitting faithfully at Borous''s side with his head resting on the doctor''s leg as he confided his troubles","worst":"Being fed Psycho-laced food and Buffout by Borous, twisting him from a loving companion into a chem-maddened brute"}}', 'Test subject at the X-8 research center; formerly Doctor Borous''s pet and companion', '* Enhanced strength and combat prowess from cybernetic augmentation and chemical modification
* Formidable bite and endurance', 'Cannot speak; communicates through growls, barks, and aggressive posturing', '* Survival within the testing facility
* Driven by chem-induced aggression and territorial instinct', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gaius_magnus', '', 'A Caesar''s Legion centurion who endured atomic fire at Dry Wells and now commands his ghoulified legionaries as marked men amid the irradiated ruins', 'Gaius Magnus is a centurion of Caesar''s Legion who commanded the garrison at Dry Wells when nuclear devastation consumed the region. Caught in the atomic fire alongside his legionaries, he was transformed into a marked man rather than killed outright, his body sustained and continuously healed by the intense radiation blanketing the ruins. He wears the distinctive armor of the 87th Tribe, a symbol of his authority and of that tribe''s conquest and absorption into the Legion. His name carries the weight of two of Rome''s most legendary generals, Gaius Julius Caesar and Gnaeus Pompeius Magnus, and he has proven himself worthy of that legacy through sheer refusal to fall. In the irradiated hellscape of Dry Wells, Magnus still holds command, his discipline and loyalty surviving even the transformation that should have ended him.', 'A tall marked man with severe radiation scarring across his facial features and the faint glow of ghoulified tissue across his ravaged form.', 'Relentless, disciplined, and fanatically devoted to Caesar''s will even beyond the threshold of death; maintains iron authority over his marked men and shows no trace of despair or self-pity despite his condition', '{"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"sworn commander","note":"His loyalty survived even nuclear transformation; he remains Legion to his core."},"87th Tribe":{"aff":40,"type":"contempt","relation":"conquered subjects","note":"He wears their armor as a trophy of their subjugation under Legion rule."}}', 'Centurion and field commander in Caesar''s Legion', '* Military leadership
* Melee combat
* Survival in high-radiation environments
* Legion tactical doctrine
* Endurance beyond normal human limits', 'Commanding and terse, using Latin-inflected Legion terminology and clipped military phrasing; speaks with the absolute authority of a centurion who has survived atomic fire', '* Maintain Legion discipline and order among his marked men forces
* Hold Dry Wells as Legion territory
* Continue serving Caesar''s will regardless of his irradiated condition', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gambler', '', 'A wealthy wasteland civilian drawn to the New Vegas Strip for gambling, drinking, and spectacle', 'Gamblers are tourists and residents who flock to the New Vegas Strip seeking fortune, entertainment, and escape from the harsh Mojave. Many travel from NCR territories out west, taking advantage of open passage agreements that let civilians cross between the Strip and the republic without interference. They form the economic backbone of the Strip''s casinos and hotels, spending freely on rooms, drinks, and table games. Most are among the wealthier denizens of the wasteland, possessing enough caps or trade goods to afford the Strip''s exorbitant rates. A few carry grudges alongside their chips-one gambler harbors a vendetta against the Van Graffs for wrongs done to his family and plots violent retribution.', 'Human male or female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Pleasure-seeking and optimistic at the tables, often sociable and talkative while drinking. Some mask desperation or obsession beneath a cheerful front. A minority carry deep personal grievances that fester behind their smiles.', '{"New California Republic":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"home citizenry","note":"Many gamblers hail from NCR territory and travel freely under open passage agreements."},"The Strip":{"aff":60,"type":"client","relation":"patron","note":"Gamblers are the Strip''s primary revenue source and treat its casinos as a second home."},"Van Graffs":{"aff":-30,"type":"enemy","relation":"vendetta target","note":"At least one gambler seeks violent revenge against the Van Graffs for family wrongs."}}', 'Tourist, recreational gambler, and Strip patron', '* Card and dice games
* Caps management
* Social navigation
* Reading table dynamics
* Holding liquor', 'Casual and animated, peppered with gambling slang and casino jargon; tone shifts from buoyant while winning to terse or bitter during losses', '* Win big
* Enjoy the Strip''s pleasures
* Stretch caps across another night of entertainment
* In rare cases settle old scores against those who wronged their family', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('genaro', '', 'A Freeside street cook who turns questionable scavenged ingredients into cheap meals for the desperate', 'Genaro is a food merchant operating near the Old Mormon Fort in Freeside, hawking cheap meals to the district''s hungry and destitute residents. He keeps his sourcing methods deliberately vague, admitting only that helpers bring him various ingredients from around the streets. When pressed about where his food comes from, Genaro grows evasive, suggesting that knowing too much would ruin any customer''s appetite. His stock of gecko kebabs, mole rat stew, and other low-quality fare hints at helpers who scavenge whatever vermin and stray creatures they can catch in Freeside''s alleys and gutters. Despite the dubious origins of his ingredients, Genaro provides one of the few affordable food sources in a district where most residents can barely scrape together caps for a meal.', 'Weathered Caucasian human male with rough, sun-damaged complexion and signs of long-term smoke exposure; no distinctive scars or tattoos recorded.', 'Evasive and pragmatic, deflecting questions about his ingredients with knowing humor rather than outright lies, comfortable operating in Freeside''s moral gray areas where survival justifies discretion', '{}', 'Street food vendor and cook in Freeside', '* Cooking and butchering
* Informal ingredient sourcing through street helpers
* Haggling
* Street survival and scavenger management', 'Casual and deflective, quick with a chuckle or shrug when pressed on uncomfortable details, speaks in the clipped shorthand of someone who learned long ago not to volunteer information', '* Keep selling food
* Maintain his network of street helpers
* Avoid scrutiny that might drive away customers or invite competition', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('general_lee_oliver', '', 'Commanding general of NCR forces in the Mojave, driven by patriotism and a bitter need to prove his strategy over the Rangers who overshadowed him', 'General Lee Oliver is the commanding officer of the New California Republic Army in the Mojave Wasteland, a career soldier and staunch supporter of President Kimball''s eastward expansion. He and Chief Hanlon shared credit for the NCR''s victory at the First Battle of Hoover Dam, but Oliver seethes that the Rangers received most of the glory while the regular army''s contributions were overlooked. That resentment has warped his strategic thinking ever since. He has concentrated the bulk of his forces at Hoover Dam itself, stripping garrisons across the Mojave and ignoring Legion buildup at Cottonwood Cove, all in pursuit of one decisive, glorious confrontation. Critics call him a glory hound and mock him as General Wait-and-see. Yet Oliver remains a genuine patriot who cares about the Republic''s future, and he is rational enough to abandon a losing cause rather than waste lives for pride alone.', 'A heavyset Caucasian human male with a broad build and no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Proud, stubborn, and glory-seeking, but genuinely patriotic and ultimately pragmatic. Harbors deep resentment toward the Rangers that clouds his judgment. Dismissive of criticism yet capable of changing course when convinced of failure. Craves recognition and is determined to win on his own terms.', '{"Chief Hanlon":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"bitter counterpart","note":"Oliver resents that Hanlon''s Rangers received credit for the First Battle and refuses to incorporate his strategic input for the second.","worst":"Watching the Rangers get praised for Hanlon''s plan while his army''s sacrifice went unacknowledged"},"NCR Rangers":{"aff":-30,"type":"jealous","relation":"resented elite unit","note":"Oliver''s grudge extends to the entire Ranger corps, whose prestige he believes comes at the regular army''s expense.","worst":"Seeing Rangers celebrated as heroes while his soldiers bled for the same victory"},"Aaron Kimball":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"commander-in-chief","note":"Oliver is a vocal supporter of Kimball''s expansionist policies and benefits from the President''s political backing."},"Robert House":{"aff":-50,"type":"contempt","relation":"strategic critic","note":"House openly mocks Oliver''s single-minded focus on the Dam as tunnel vision, and Oliver returns the disdain."},"NCR Army":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"commanded forces","note":"Despite his flawed strategy, Oliver genuinely cares about his troops and will not waste them on a lost cause."},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"existential threat","note":"The Legion is the enemy Oliver has built his entire strategy around destroying, though his preparations have left other fronts vulnerable."}}', 'Commanding general of all NCR Army forces in the Mojave Theater of operations', '* Large-scale military strategy
* Troop deployment and logistics
* Political navigation within the NCR command structure
* Attrition warfare planning
* Garrison management', 'Blunt and authoritative, with a soldier''s directness. Prone to defensiveness when his strategy is questioned. Speaks with the confidence of a man who believes his massed-troop approach is the only path to victory.', '* Defeat the Legion at Hoover Dam through overwhelming force and attrition
* Prove the regular army''s superiority over the Rangers
* Reclaim the recognition he feels was stolen after the First Battle
* Secure the NCR''s hold on the Mojave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('george', '', 'A self-proclaimed gambler and scavenger who wagers on travelers'' survival against the Boomers'' artillery', 'George is a prospector and self-styled gambler who operates near Fields'' shack outside Nellis Air Force Base. He earns his living through a combination of gambling and what he euphemistically calls reclaiming goods that are no longer being used-salvaging from the wastes and those who did not survive them. His most notorious scheme involves wagering double or nothing with passing travelers, betting they cannot reach the gate of Nellis Air Force Base and return alive, a bet almost no one collects on given the Boomers'' relentless artillery bombardment of anything that moves in their direction. He carries no formal faction allegiance, working the margins of the Mojave as a lone opportunist. George''s presence at the edge of Boomer territory is calculated; the constant stream of hopeful or desperate travelers provides him both gambling marks and, when they fail, salvage opportunities.', 'An older African American male with weathered, deeply lined skin and a lean, sun-darkened complexion.', 'Opportunistic, shrewd, and darkly humorous; treats mortal danger as entertainment and profit; unbothered by the moral weight of his wagers', '{"Boomers":{"aff":-10,"type":"fearful","relation":"dangerous neighbors","note":"George treats the Boomers'' lethal artillery as a reliable racket rather than a personal threat, profiting from their violence without ever approaching their territory."}}', 'Prospector, gambler, and scavenger', '* Gambling
* Scavenging
* Reading people
* Survival in marginal territories', 'Casual and wheedling with a gambler''s patter; uses euphemisms for grimmer realities; quick to propose a wager', '* Profit from travelers and salvage
* Keep the wagers flowing
* Avoid becoming another corpse near Nellis', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ghashbone', '', 'Motor-Runner''s loyal guard dog patrolling Vault 3''s maintenance wing', 'GhashBone is one of Motor-Runner''s two guard dogs, stationed in the maintenance wing of Vault 3 alongside pack-mate BoneGnash. The Fiend leader keeps the pair as loyal sentinels over his stronghold, relying on their keen senses and fierce territorial instincts to detect and intercept intruders. GhashBone prowls the vault''s lower corridors with restless vigilance, a lean and battle-hardened wasteland hound utterly devoted to its master. Where Motor-Runner goes, GhashBone is never far behind, and the dog''s deep-chested growl is often the first warning any outsider receives before the Fiends make their presence violently known.', 'A lean, scarred wasteland hound with watchful eyes and a powerful, deep-chested build.', 'Fiercely loyal, territorial, and alert; aggressive toward strangers and intruders but obedient and calm around Motor-Runner and BoneGnash.', '{"Motor-Runner":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"master and guard dog","note":"GhashBone is utterly devoted to Motor-Runner and serves as one of his two personal guard dogs.","best":"Resting at Motor-Runner''s feet after a long patrol through the vault corridors"},"BoneGnash":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"pack-mate","note":"The two guard dogs share patrol duties and operate as a coordinated pair in Vault 3.","best":"Working in tandem to corner an intruder in the maintenance wing"},"Fiends":{"aff":40,"type":"neutral","relation":"pack associates","note":"GhashBone tolerates the Fiends who inhabit Vault 3 as part of Motor-Runner''s domain but shows no particular warmth toward them."}}', 'Guard dog', '* Keen hearing and scent detection
* Intruder interception
* Territorial patrol
* Coordinated pack defense with BoneGnash', 'Barks, growls, and snarls; communicates through canine vocalizations and body language only.', '* Protect Motor-Runner
* Defend Vault 3 from intruders
* Maintain patrol over the maintenance wing', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ghost_of_she', '', 'A mythical yao guai of Sorrows legend, believed to be the merged spirit of a devoured child and the beast that consumed her', 'Ghost of She is an enormous yao guai haunting the depths of the Ghost Den in Zion Canyon. According to Sorrows tradition preserved by Waking Cloud, a young girl wandered into a yao guai''s cave before receiving her naming ceremony and was devoured. The Sorrows believe the child''s spirit fused with the beast, creating the entity they call Ghost of She-a living embodiment of stolen innocence and predatory fury. White Bird, the tribe''s shaman, considers her paw a sacred trophy necessary for the Rite of Passage. Those who encounter her speak of phantom duplicates and unnatural flames wreathing her body, though outsiders suspect datura intoxication may color these visions.', 'An enormous yao guai wreathed in spectral flames across its mutated bear-like body, radiating unnatural heat.', 'Fierce, territorial, and relentless; moves with a predatory intelligence that seems almost human in its cunning', '{"White Bird":{"aff":-40,"type":"enemy","relation":"sacred quarry","note":"White Bird sends seekers to kill her and retrieve her paw as a rite of passage"},"Waking Cloud":{"aff":-20,"type":"fearful","relation":"tribal legend source","note":"Waking Cloud preserves the story of the child who became one with the beast"},"The Sorrows":{"aff":-30,"type":"fearful","relation":"mythical terror","note":"The tribe reveres and fears Ghost of She as a living reminder of a child lost before her naming"}}', 'Mythical guardian beast of Sorrows spiritual tradition', '* Devastating physical attacks capable of killing armored prey in few blows
* Manifests phantom duplicates when wounded', 'Roars and guttural beast-sounds; communicates nothing but violence', '* Defend her territory in the Ghost Den
* Survive as a living embodiment of the Sorrows'' most painful legend', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gloria_van_graff', '', 'Ambitious head of the Van Graff family''s Mojave operations and manager of the Silver Rush energy weapons emporium in Freeside', 'Gloria Van Graff commands the Van Graff family''s expansion into the Mojave Wasteland from her seat of power at the Silver Rush in Freeside. Driven by ambition and a strained relationship with her mother, she carved out her territory in 2276 by seizing a dilapidated casino and silencing the Kings'' objections with plasma fire. She operates on the principle that might makes right and has entrenched her position through a covert alliance with Alice McLafferty of the Crimson Caravan, staging attacks on competing outfits as Brotherhood raids while undercutting the Gun Runners'' market share. Her boldest gambit involves playing both the Legion and the NCR against each other: she accepted a Legion weapons contract only to lure their representatives into an NCR ambush, securing a lucrative defense contract and political connections while pocketing the Legion''s payment as a bonus. Gloria is a passionate and calculating woman whose romantic entanglements-including ill-fated affairs with the Kings member Pacer and a former employee named Jacob-have a habit of creating complications her family would rather avoid.', 'A striking African-American woman who carries herself with an authoritative posture, bearing no distinctive scars or tattoos.', 'Ruthlessly ambitious, calculating, and unapologetically pragmatic; operates on the conviction that power justifies itself and views sentiment as a liability in business; passionate in her personal life but quick to discard lovers who become inconvenient; possesses a sharp wit and colder judgment', '{"Jean-Baptiste Cutting":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"half-brother","note":"He calls her Glory; a working family relationship bound by shared business interests and blood"},"Frieda Van Graff":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"half-sister","note":"Family ties maintained through the Van Graff organization"},"Van Graff matriarch":{"aff":20,"type":"estranged","relation":"mother","note":"Gloria''s move to the Mojave stemmed from their inability to get along; she seeks to prove her worth through profit and success"},"Alice McLafferty":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"covert ally","note":"Partners in a secret scheme to eliminate competing caravans and undermine the Gun Runners'' market position"},"Pacer":{"aff":-20,"type":"ex","relation":"former lover","note":"Their ended affair gives Pacer reason to snoop around Van Graff business; his harassment of her guards could easily become grounds for a quiet assassination"},"Jacob":{"aff":-30,"type":"ex","relation":"former employee and lover","note":"Their relationship ended badly; a former Van Graff employee who crossed from professional to personal and back to neither"},"NCR":{"aff":50,"type":"transactional","relation":"defense contractor","note":"She earned their defense contract and political connections by betraying the Legion''s representatives in an ambush"},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-60,"type":"betrayed","relation":"double-crossed client","note":"She accepted their weapons deal only to lure their representatives into an NCR trap, keeping their payment as a bonus"},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":-40,"type":"fearful","relation":"threat to operations","note":"Their attention to her energy weapons trade endangers her operation; only Elder Elijah''s distraction at HELIOS One has kept them at bay"},"Gun Runners":{"aff":-50,"type":"rival","relation":"market competitor","note":"Her alliance with McLafferty specifically targets their market share for elimination"}}', 'Manager of the Silver Rush energy weapons store and head of the Van Graff family''s Mojave operations', '* Energy weapons trade and procurement
* Business negotiation and market manipulation
* Political scheming and double-dealing
* Caravan logistics
* Intimidation and enforcement', 'Direct, confident, and laced with sardonic humor; speaks as someone accustomed to being the most dangerous person in the room; businesslike but with an undercurrent of predatory charm', '* Maximize Van Graff profits and market dominance in the Mojave
* Prove her success to her mother and the broader family
* Maintain the NCR alliance while keeping her double-cross of the Legion hidden
* Eliminate competition from the Gun Runners and independent caravans', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gomez', '', 'A dutiful NCR Ranger serving as keeper of the Mojave safehouse, ensuring fellow Rangers stay supplied and sheltered.', 'Ranger Gomez is a New California Republic Ranger assigned to maintain the NCR Ranger safehouse in the Mojave Wasteland. Her primary responsibility is keeping the outpost stocked with equipment, supplies, and ammunition for Rangers operating across the region. She rotates through the safehouse on a regular schedule, managing inventory and distributing conventional, energy, and explosive ordnance to qualified personnel. Her posting keeps her away from the front lines, but her logistical work sustains the Rangers who fight there. Gomez maintains a quiet, disciplined presence within the cave network, focused on her duties rather than seeking combat glory.', 'A Hispanic human female with a weathered, sun-damaged complexion and hardened facial features from prolonged desert exposure.', 'Disciplined, practical, and reserved. Gomez speaks little and focuses on her work, content with a support role that keeps others fighting. She shows quiet pride in keeping the safehouse running.', '{"New California Republic Rangers":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"serving Ranger","note":"Gomez devotes herself to supporting her fellow Rangers through supply and shelter management."}}', 'NCR Ranger safehouse keeper and supply quartermaster', '* Supply management
* Ammunition allocation
* Safehouse maintenance
* Basic fieldcraft and survival', 'Brief and professional. Speaks in clipped military phrasing, sticking to logistics and practical matters without small talk.', '* Keeping the safehouse fully stocked and operational
* Ensuring no Ranger goes without essential supplies
* Maintaining the NCR''s logistical foothold in the Mojave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gomorrah_bartender', '', 'Omertas-employed bartender pouring drinks and pushing chems at Gomorrah casino on the New Vegas Strip', 'Gomorrah bartenders serve the steady flow of wastelanders, gamblers, and degenerates who pass through the Omertas'' flagship casino. Stationed across four posts-the main floor, Lower Brimstone, the Zoara Club, and the lower lobby-they keep glasses full and chems moving. Working for the Omertas means knowing when to talk and when to mind your own business. They see everything that happens in Gomorrah''s smoke-choked halls: the cheating, the overdoses, the quiet conversations between made men. Most have learned that survival depends on discretion and a healthy fear of the family that signs their pay. The caps are good enough to keep them behind the bar, even if the work leaves a stain.', 'Individuals vary between humans and ghouls of both sexes, featuring average builds and ages, with ghouls displaying the characteristic hairless, deeply wrinkled and necrotic skin of their condition.', 'World-weary and discreet, practiced at reading customers and deflecting unwanted questions; carries the quiet tension of someone who knows too much about their employers', '{"Omertas":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Pays well enough to ensure loyalty, enforces obedience through fear"}}', 'Bartender and chem dealer at Gomorrah casino', '* Mixing drinks
* Sourcing and selling chems
* Customer reading
* Discretion
* Basic cash handling', 'Brief and professional, with a practiced hospitality that drops cold when someone asks the wrong thing', '* Earn caps
* Stay in the Omertas'' good graces
* Avoid knowing more than is safe', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gomorrah_cash_room_guard', '', 'Omertas enforcer standing permanent watch over Gomorrah''s cash room and vault access', 'This Omertas hardcase pulls cash room guard duty at Gomorrah, the Strip''s most notorious casino and brothel. Stationed at the bank door, he screens everyone who approaches the count room and ensures no caps, chips, or valuables leave under suspicious circumstances. The Omertas trust him with their money, which in their world means he is either deeply reliable or deeply afraid of what happens if he is not. He spends his shifts watching the flow of wealth and the faces of those who come near it, a human lock on the Omertas'' most sensitive repository. The work is monotonous but critical, and he performs it with the sullen vigilance of a man who knows exactly what his bosses do to people who fail them.', 'Heavyset human male with a watchful, rigid posture.', 'Dour, suspicious, and professionally cold; speaks little and watches constantly, defaulting to hostility toward anyone who lingers near the vault', '{"Omertas":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"employing faction","note":"Guards their most sensitive assets under implicit threat of severe punishment for failure"}}', 'Cash room guard for the Omertas at Gomorrah', '* Access control
* Threat assessment
* Intimidation
* Basic firearms proficiency
* Sustained vigilance', 'Short, clipped warnings and dismissals; rarely wastes words beyond what is needed to turn someone away', '* Keep the cash room secure
* Stay in the Omertas'' good graces
* Avoid the consequences of a breach on his watch', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gomorrah_cashier', '', 'Ground-floor cashier at the Gomorrah casino on the New Vegas Strip', 'The Gomorrah cashier works the ground floor of the Strip''s most notorious casino, handling chip exchanges and payouts for every gambler who walks through the door. Employed by the Omerta family, he processes transactions with the detached efficiency expected of casino staff in a house that always takes its cut. His face is unremarkable and interchangeable, one of several standard staff profiles the casino uses to fill its service positions, making him difficult to pick out from other employees. He sees high rollers, desperate losers, and everything in between pass his window without offering more than required pleasantries. The work is steady, the tips occasional, and the Omertas ensure their cashiers keep their eyes on the chips and their mouths shut about what happens upstairs.', 'Human male with unremarkable, generic facial features and average build; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or identifying physical marks.', 'Professionally detached and efficient, with the practiced neutrality of someone who handles large sums around desperate people all day; keeps conversation brief and transactions moving', '{"Gomorrah":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"employee","note":"Steady employment under Omerta management; expected to keep quiet and process transactions without complaint"},"Omertas":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"subordinate staff","note":"Answers to Omerta oversight; knows better than to ask questions about casino operations beyond his window"}}', 'Casino cashier at Gomorrah', '* Chip and currency exchange
* Rapid mental arithmetic
* Customer service under pressure
* Spotting counterfeit caps or suspicious chips', 'Curt and transactional; speaks in short polite phrases focused on the exchange at hand, rarely elaborating beyond required courtesies', '* Process chip exchanges accurately and quickly
* Avoid trouble with gamblers and Omerta management alike
* Collect occasional tips', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gomorrah_dealer', '', 'Omertas card and roulette dealer working the casino floor at Gomorrah on the New Vegas Strip', 'This Omertas dealer runs the blackjack or roulette tables at Gomorrah, the Strip''s most notorious casino-brothel. Like all Omertas, he operates under the tribe''s culture of greed and secrecy, keeping his dealings smooth and his observations to himself. He maintains a professional front at the table, offering rote greetings to gamblers while watching the flow of caps and the behavior of punters with a practiced eye. His work keeps him on the main level amid the smoke, noise, and vice that define Gomorrah''s atmosphere. He is one of three dealers covering the gaming tables, two at blackjack and one at roulette. The job demands steady hands and a closed mouth, qualities the Omertas value in their front-line staff.', 'A clean-cut human male with well-groomed hair; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other physical features are recorded.', 'Professionally distant and surface-level cordial, keeping interactions brief and transactional. Watchful without being obvious, more observer than conversationalist.', '{"Omertas":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"tribe member","note":"Loyal operative within the Omertas tribal structure, earning his keep at the gaming tables."}}', 'Blackjack and roulette dealer at Gomorrah casino', '* Card handling
* Roulette operation
* Mental arithmetic
* Reading gamblers'' tells
* Maintaining house advantage', 'Short, rehearsed casino greetings and table calls; rarely elaborates beyond professional patter', '* Keep the tables running smoothly
* Ensure the house wins its share
* Stay in good standing with Omertas leadership', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gomorrah_entrance_guard', '', 'An Omertas tough assigned to Gomorrah''s front entrance, responsible for greeting visitors and relieving them of their weapons before they enter the casino floor.', 'This Omertas enforcer stands permanent watch at Gomorrah''s entrance hall, serving as the first face visitors see when stepping into the casino''s garish embrace. Like most of the Omertas'' muscle, he wears the gang''s signature blend of forced hospitality and quiet menace, polite enough to keep the Strip''s image intact but clearly more thug than concierge. His primary duty is collecting weapons from every guest who passes through, a task he carries out with practiced efficiency and zero patience for negotiation. Smugglers occasionally slip holdout pieces past his checkpoint, a fact that likely earns his superiors'' displeasure and keeps him vigilant. He is a small but necessary cog in the Omertas'' operation, standing between the chaos of the Wasteland and the curated sin within.', 'A well-groomed but hard-faced Caucasian male with the muscular build and tense posture of a street fighter.', 'Outwardly courteous in a rehearsed, hollow way; quickly dismissive or cold when challenged. Carries the quiet arrogance of someone backed by serious muscle.', '{"Omertas":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"gang enforcer","note":"Loyal foot soldier in the Omertas hierarchy, trusted with the casino''s front door."},"Gomorrah":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"establishment security","note":"His assigned post and livelihood; failure here means replacement or worse."}}', 'Gomorrah entrance guard and weapons check', '* Weapons inspection
* Crowd assessment
* Intimidation
* Basic security enforcement', 'Brief, formulaic greetings followed by firm directives; drops the polite act the instant someone pushes back.', '* Keep weapons off the casino floor
* Maintain the Omertas'' authority at the threshold
* Avoid trouble from above', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gomorrah_floor_manager', '', 'Omertas floor manager who keeps Gomorrah''s guests gambling and cuts losses when winners get too lucky', 'This Omertas operative serves as the floor manager of Gomorrah, the Strip''s most notorious casino and brothel. His job is to make the establishment feel welcoming and generous, handing out complimentary food and drinks to visitors who show promise as profitable gamblers. The strategy is simple: a little hospitality goes a long way toward keeping people at the tables and spending their chips. However, his generosity has strict limits. When a gambler''s winnings threaten the house bottom line, he steps in personally to revoke their playing privileges and show them the door. It is a delicate balance of charm and cold calculation, one he performs with practiced ease on Gomorrah''s main floor every night.', 'Hispanic male standing about 5''5" with a compact build; no distinctive facial features are recorded.', 'Outwardly warm and hospitable with a practiced casino-host smile, but calculating underneath. Generous when it serves the house, ruthlessly pragmatic when it doesn''t. Switches from charming to firm without hesitation.', '{"Omertas":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"tribal family","note":"Loyal member of the Omertas family, entrusted with managing Gomorrah''s casino floor and protecting its profits."}}', 'Floor manager at Gomorrah casino on the New Vegas Strip', '* Customer hospitality
* Casino floor operations
* Reading gamblers'' behavior
* Managing house profits
* Diplomatic ejection of problem winners', 'Smooth, welcoming casino host patter that shifts to polite but unyielding authority when cutting off big winners. Always professional, never personal.', '* Keep guests gambling and spending at Gomorrah
* Protect the house''s bottom line
* Maintain the casino''s reputation for generosity while preventing costly payouts', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gomorrah_prostitute', '', 'Captive sex workers enslaved by the Omertas through chem addiction at the Gomorrah casino', 'Men and women, human and ghoul alike, forced into prostitution at the Gomorrah casino on the New Vegas Strip. Employed by the Omertas, they dance in suspended cages throughout the Brimstone club and the courtyard, selling sexual favors to any customer with caps. What appears to be willing sex work conceals a grim system of coercion: the Omertas supply free Jet and Med-X to new workers, cultivating dependency before cutting off supply and charging exorbitant prices. Former workers who escaped, such as Sweetie in Westside, have exposed this practice as slavery through a needle. Those still trapped inside serve nightly under the weight of addiction and debt, with no freedom to leave and no allies within the casino.', 'Men and women of varying ages and builds, including both smooth-skinned humans and scarred ghouls.', 'Outwardly flirtatious and accommodating to customers, but beneath the performance lies exhaustion, desperation, and resentment. Many are chem-addicted and anxious about their next dose, making compliance a survival mechanism rather than genuine enthusiasm.', '{"Omertas":{"aff":-70,"type":"fearful","relation":"captors","note":"The Omertas control them through chem addiction and debt, keeping them trapped in forced sex work with no escape.","worst":"Watching the free chems turn to debts that can never be repaid"},"Sweetie":{"aff":45,"type":"grateful","relation":"escaped former colleague","note":"Sweetie fled Gomorrah and exposed the Omertas'' chem-slavery scheme to the outside world.","best":"Hearing that someone finally named it slavery through a needle"}}', 'Captive prostitute and exotic dancer at Gomorrah''s Brimstone club', '* Seductive dancing
* Sexual services
* Customer entertainment
* Reading clients for survival
* Enduring deprivation', 'Practiced come-ons and sultry invitations on the floor; quieter, strained, and bitter in private moments', '* Securing the next chem dose to stave off withdrawal
* Earning enough to survive the Omertas'' charges
* And-rarely-finding a way out of Gomorrah''s grip', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gomorrah_receptionist', '', 'A former Gomorrah prostitute promoted to receptionist who quietly trades in Omerta secrets', 'She stands behind the front desk of Gomorrah, the Omertas'' casino on the New Vegas Strip, greeting arrivals with practiced hospitality. Her current position came as a promotion from Gomorrah''s prostitution ranks, a transition that speaks to both her survival instincts and her usefulness to the organization. Her years working the casino''s darker corners gave her an intimate understanding of the Omerta crime family''s operations, rivalries, and vulnerabilities. She leveraged that knowledge into a lucrative side arrangement with Mr. House, feeding him intelligence on Omerta activities in exchange for payment. Whether that arrangement still holds is a matter she keeps to herself. She remains at her post, professional and composed, quietly cataloging every face and rumor that passes through Gomorrah''s doors.', 'Caucasian human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Observant, pragmatic, and discreet; maintains professional poise that masks sharp awareness and calculating self-interest', '{"Omertas":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Works at their casino but has previously sold information about their operations to Mr. House"},"Mr. House":{"aff":15,"type":"transactional","relation":"former informant","note":"Provided intelligence on Omerta activities in exchange for payment; the arrangement''s current status is uncertain"}}', 'Receptionist at Gomorrah casino; former prostitute; former Mr. House informant', '* Information gathering
* Reading people
* Maintaining composure under pressure
* Detailed knowledge of Omerta operations and internal politics', 'Professional, measured, and courteous; delivers casino pleasantries with efficient warmth that discourages casual follow-up questions', '* Maintain her improved station
* Stay informed without drawing dangerous attention
* Navigate the volatile politics between the Omertas and outside powers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('goodsprings_settler', '', 'A quiet Goodsprings homesteader eking out a living in the Mojave desert', 'These unnamed settlers are among the roughly four permanent residents of Goodsprings who inhabit the town''s surviving pre-War houses. Most originally came from New California, drawn by an NCR-backed grant to establish mining operations around the town''s namesake water source. Over time they shifted toward ranching and farming, raising brahmin and bighorners in the dusty scrubland. They welcome passing travelers with small-town pleasantries so long as no violence follows them in. One of the women recently ran afoul of geckos near the water source before Sunny Smiles could clear the pack out. The settlers rely on local merchant Chet for supplies and can be rallied to defend their home when threatened.', 'Human of variable gender with weathered, wind-roughened skin and an otherwise unremarkable physical build.', 'Friendly but guarded toward outsiders, practical and self-reliant, values peace and quiet, quick to shelter when trouble arrives', '{"Goodsprings":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"home community","note":"Loyal townsfolk who look out for one another and defend their home together"},"Sunny Smiles":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"town protector","note":"Depend on her to handle geckos and other wildlife threats around the water source"},"Chet":{"aff":50,"type":"transactional","relation":"local merchant","note":"Supplies their everyday needs and can equip them when danger comes to town"},"New California Republic":{"aff":30,"type":"neutral","relation":"distant patron","note":"The original NCR grant brought them here, but the Republic''s presence means little day to day"}}', 'Farmer and rancher in Goodsprings', '* Brahmin and bighorner husbandry
* Subsistence farming
* Basic desert survival
* Small-town bartering', 'Simple, polite, and brief; speaks in casual small-town greetings and short practical sentences', '* Maintain a peaceful homestead
* Keep livestock healthy
* Avoid entanglement with outside conflicts
* Preserve the town''s quiet way of life', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gourd', '', 'A wasteland beer bootlegger who brewed Strategic Nuclear Moose at his remote still before cazadores overran the site', 'Gourd was an independent brewer who ran a beer bootlegging operation somewhere in the Mojave Wasteland. He crafted his own signature brew called Strategic Nuclear Moose, supplying whoever was brave or thirsty enough to seek out his remote distillery. His operation suffered from a fatal disadvantage: a cazador nest established directly above his bootlegging site. The venomous predators made the location a death trap and ultimately claimed him. His still and remaining stock sit beneath the buzzing threat overhead, a grim monument to the perils of solo enterprise in the wasteland.', 'A middle-aged human male with weathered skin and rough, calloused hands, his corpse bearing severe lacerations and puncture wounds from cazador stingers.', 'Resourceful and stubbornly independent, the sort who would rather risk cazadores than abandon his still', '{"Cazadores":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"nesting threat","note":"A cazador nest built directly above his operation made his daily work a constant danger"}}', 'Beer bootlegger and brewer', '* Brewing
* Distillation
* Ingredient scavenging
* Basic wasteland survival', 'Casual wasteland vernacular, likely laconic and practical', '* Was determined to keep his bootlegging operation running despite the cazador threat', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gourmand_food_supplier', '', 'Food supplier working the counter at the Gourmand, the Ultra-Luxe''s signature restaurant and a front of house fixture of White Glove Society hospitality.', 'The Gourmand food supplier operates the food counter inside the Ultra-Luxe''s renowned Gourmand restaurant, serving patrons under the watchful standards of the White Glove Society. He maintains a curated inventory of provisions befitting the Strip''s most exclusive dining establishment, where presentation and refinement are paramount. As a visible member of the Society''s service staff, he upholds the casino''s immaculate reputation for luxury and discretion. His position places him at the intersection of high society appetites and the practical logistics of keeping a prestigious kitchen stocked. He is one of the few Society-affiliated staff whom guests interact with directly and routinely.', 'Hispanic human male with a well-groomed appearance; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Composed, courteous, and fastidiously professional, mirroring the White Glove Society''s obsession with refinement and appearances. Carries an undercurrent of elite exclusivity in his dealings.', '{"White Glove Society":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"affiliated service staff","note":"Operates under the Society''s umbrella, expected to embody their standards of excellence and discretion at all times."}}', 'Food supplier and counter attendant at the Gourmand restaurant in the Ultra-Luxe', '* Food service
* Inventory curation
