('greasy_johnny', '', 'Rude leader of the Greasers, a small-time gang squatting in the North sewers and hassling anyone nearby', 'Greasy Johnny runs the Greasers, a scrappy gang that has claimed the North sewers beneath New Vegas as their turf. He and his crew harass locals passing through the underground passages and make enough trouble for the residents of North Vegas Square above that they have become a genuine nuisance. Johnny cultivates a tough, abrasive persona to compensate for the fact that his gang is more loud than dangerous. He rules through attitude rather than strength, keeping his people in line with bravado and petty intimidation. The Greasers'' persistent noise and aggression have drawn the ire of Crandon, a local guard determined to run them out. Johnny shows no sign of backing down from anyone, whether above ground or below it.', 'Caucasian human male with lank, unwashed hair; no other distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Rude, loud, and confrontational; covers his gang''s mediocrity with swagger and petty aggression toward anyone who wanders near', '{"Crandon":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"opposing local guard","note":"Crandon wants the Greasers gone from the sewers and has taken steps to run them out","worst":"Knowing Crandon is actively trying to rally people against his gang"},"Greasers":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"gang under his leadership","note":"Johnny leads the Greasers and depends on their numbers to maintain his turf"}}', 'Gang leader of the Greasers', '* Petty intimidation
* Sewer navigation
