* Keep his gang loyal through bravado
* Drive off anyone who challenges his authority', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('great_khan_armorer', '', 'Great Khan armorer managing the tribe''s weapons and ammunition stockpile from her basement forge near Red Rock Canyon', 'The Great Khan armorer is a loyal tribeswoman who maintains the Khans'' weapon and ammunition supply from a basement armory beneath a ruined house southeast of Red Rock Canyon, not far from Spring Mt. Ranch State Park. She serves her people by keeping their arsenal organized, repaired, and ready for whatever conflicts the tribe faces in the Mojave Wasteland. A single Khan guard stands watch over the operation, a testament to the value she places on securing her stockpile. While her primary duty is to her tribe, she is willing to trade arms and ammunition to outsiders who have proven themselves trustworthy in the eyes of the Khans. Her work keeps the Great Khans armed and dangerous in an unforgiving desert where only the well-equipped survive.', 'Weathered Hispanic woman with calloused hands and tribal tattoos marking her skin.', 'Pragmatic and no-nonsense about her craft, she reserves warmth for fellow Khans and treats outsiders with guarded caution until they''ve earned tribal trust. Proud of her role in keeping the Khans armed.', '{"Great Khans":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribe","note":"Her loyalty to the Khans is absolute; she arms them as her life''s duty."}}', 'Tribal armorer and weapons merchant for the Great Khans', '* Weapons maintenance
* Ammunition supply management
* Firearms identification
* Barter
* Inventory organization', 'Blunt and businesslike, using short direct statements; warms slightly when addressing fellow Khans, stays curt and watchful with strangers', '* Keep the Great Khans well-armed and supplied
* Maintain the armory''s security
* Ensure only trusted individuals access her wares', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('great_khan_character', '', 'A rank-and-file member of the Great Khans, the Mojave''s only organized raider tribe', 'A Great Khan lives by the old code of the tribe-strength, loyalty, and self-sufficiency. The Khans are the only truly organized raider gang in the Mojave Wasteland, and their members take pride in that distinction. They survive through hunting, farming, and the chem trade that flows from their camps to customers across the region. Major buyers include the Fiends and, quietly, elements of the New California Republic. A Khan can be found wherever the tribe holds ground: the stronghold at Red Rock Canyon, the encampment, or the ruins of Boulder City where tensions with NCR troops run high. Some Khans have already fallen to the wasteland''s violence, their bodies left in tribal villages that proved indefensible. For those still breathing, the tribe is family, the chem trade is livelihood, and survival is a daily negotiation between principle and profit.', 'Human male or female with weathered, sun-aged skin and tribal tattoos marking their features.', 'Loyal to the tribe above all, with a raider''s pragmatism and a survivor''s suspicion of outsiders. Carries pride in Khan identity and independence, tempered by the grim realities of their declining fortunes.', '{"Great Khans":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribal family","note":"The Khan is the tribe and the tribe is the Khan; loyalty is non-negotiable."},"Fiends":{"aff":20,"type":"transactional","relation":"chem customers","note":"The Fiends buy product reliably, but no Khan trusts a chem-addled savage."},"New California Republic":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"enemy and customer","note":"NCR troops are a constant threat, yet some NCR citizens quietly purchase Khan chems-a bitter irony."}}', 'Great Khan tribal member and raider', '* Hunting
* Subsistence farming
* Chem procurement and distribution
* Basic combat
* Wasteland survival
* Tribal craftsmanship', 'Blunt and direct, with tribal slang and occasional chem-dealer''s euphemism. Speaks of the Khan way as something worth defending, though weariness sometimes shows through.', '* Sustain the Great Khans as a people
