* Honor the Khan legacy', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('grecks', '', 'A lazy-eyed ghoul drunk and deadbeat gambler haunting Freeside''s alleys, nursing a grudge against the water baron who gave him his crooked stare.', 'Grecks is a disreputable ghoul lingering in the northeast stretches of Freeside, recognizable by the lazy eye that drifts from proper alignment. A habitual gambler and heavy drinker, he has earned a reputation for dodging debts and avoiding anyone trying to collect on what he owes. His distinctive eye is the lasting souvenir of a violent encounter with a water baron, an incident he recounts with bitter resentment toward the profiteer he calls a "scum-humping" opportunist. Grecks claims no trade or productive occupation, preferring to squander what caps he finds on cards and cheap booze. Despite his shiftless ways, he remains a known fixture of the neighborhood, familiar to locals and creditors alike.', 'A male ghoul with weathered, necrotic skin and a pronounced wandering lazy eye that drifts from proper alignment.', 'Shiftless, evasive, and resentful. Grecks avoids responsibility, especially financial obligations, and carries a chip on his shoulder about the injury that disfigured him. He prefers fleeting pleasures over any kind of stability.', '{"Freeside":{"aff":15,"type":"neutral","relation":"resident","note":"He lives in Freeside''s alleys and is a recognized local fixture, though not a valued member of the community."}}', 'Freeside drunk and habitual debtor', '* Gambling
* Dodging creditors
* Surviving Freeside''s rough streets on minimal caps', 'Slurred and evasive, prone to bitter complaints about water barons and anyone pressing him for repayment. Gets defensive fast when confronted about debts.', '* Avoid paying what he owes
* Keep gambling and drinking
* Nurse his grudge against the water baron who cost him his eye', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gun_runner_guard', '', 'Mercenary guard contracted by the Gun Runners to protect their factory and merchandise', 'These hired mercenaries form the protective backbone of the Gun Runners operation, stationed at the 188 Trading Post and the Gun Runners facility. Contracted to safeguard valuable weapons inventory and secure the manufacturing premises, they maintain a vigilant presence against raiders, thieves, and any threat to the organization''s lucrative arms trade. Their duties place them under the direct authority of Alexander, the Gun Runners'' primary merchant at the trading post. Well-equipped and professionally disciplined, these guards represent the serious investment the Gun Runners make in protecting their commercial interests and trade secrets in the volatile Mojave Wasteland of 2281.', 'Human male or female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Professional, alert, and businesslike. Prioritizes duty and security over casual conversation, reflecting the serious nature of protecting one of the wasteland''s premier weapons manufacturers.', '{"Alexander":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Guards serve under Alexander''s authority at the Gun Runners trading operation."},"Gun Runners":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"contracted faction","note":"Hired to protect Gun Runners goods and factory infrastructure as paid mercenaries."}}', 'Mercenary guard for the Gun Runners', '* Combat proficiency
* Perimeter defense
* Weapons handling
* Threat assessment
* Security protocols', 'Curt and professional, speaking only when necessary and keeping interactions brief and task-focused.', '* Protect Gun Runners property
* Ensure factory security
* Maintain vigilance against theft or sabotage
* Fulfill their mercenary contract', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gun_runner_gunsmith', '', 'A Gun Runners factory gunsmith who manufactures weapons and ammunition while guarding the secured production facility', 'These gunsmiths form the productive core of the Mojave Wasteland''s Gun Runners branch, manufacturing weapons, ammunition, and armor within the fortified factory compound. Their craftsmanship feeds directly into Vendortron''s retail stock and sustains the Gun Runners'' dominance as the region''s premier arms supplier. Each worker doubles as a vigilant guard, treating any unauthorized presence on the factory floor as an immediate security threat requiring a hostile response. Their output and supply chain integrity directly affect what Blake offers for sale outside the facility walls.', 'Three variant humans: one male with a thick mustache and composed features, one male with curly dark hair and an expressive face, and one female with red hair and fair complexion.', 'Professional and territorial, focused on production quality and efficiency above all else. Quick to shift from indifferent industriousness to aggressive defensiveness when the factory floor is breached by outsiders.', '{"Gun Runners":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"employer faction","note":"Loyal employees who supply the organization''s entire product line and defend its facilities."},"Blake":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"supply chain partner","note":"The gunsmiths'' output directly determines Blake''s available inventory for outside sales."},"Vendortron":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"retail distributor","note":"They manufacture the weapons, ammunition, and armor that Vendortron stocks and sells."},"Alice McLafferty":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"management","note":"Alice oversees Gun Runners operations; the gunsmiths follow her administrative directives on production priorities."}}', 'Gunsmith and factory guard for the Gun Runners', '* Weapons manufacturing
* Ammunition production
* Armor crafting
* Facility security enforcement
* Firearms expertise', 'Brief and work-focused, terse with outsiders, rarely speaks unless addressing production matters or confronting trespassers', '* Maintain production quotas and supply chain integrity
* Protect the factory from intruders
* Uphold the Gun Runners'' reputation for superior arms', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gunderson_hired_hand', '', 'A professional hired gun serving as Heck Gunderson''s personal security at the Ultra-Luxe', 'The Gunderson hired hands are professional bodyguards in the employ of wealthy rancher Heck Gunderson, providing security for him and his interests at the Ultra-Luxe Casino. These men are mercenaries in all but name-hired guns who keep their mouths shut and their weapons ready. They maintain a constant presence on the casino floor and within Gunderson''s penthouse suite, vigilant against any threat to their employer or disruption of the Ultra-Luxe''s order. Their loyalty is transactional, bought and paid for, but absolute for as long as the contract holds. They do not socialize or engage with casino patrons, treating their duties with cold professional detachment.', 'Human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Cold, professional, and taciturn. These hired hands speak only when necessary and never volunteer information. They exhibit the detached pragmatism of career mercenaries who understand that silence and vigilance are part of the job.', '{"Heck Gunderson":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"The hired hands are contracted bodyguards whose loyalty to Gunderson is purely transactional."}}', 'Personal bodyguard and security for Heck Gunderson', '* Combat proficiency
* Threat assessment
* VIP protection
* Casino security protocols', 'Minimal and clipped. They do not engage in conversation and respond only with silence or the briefest acknowledgments when professionally required.', '* Protect Heck Gunderson and his interests
* Maintain security at the Ultra-Luxe
* Fulfill their contracted duties without complication', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('hadrian', '', 'A struggling ghoul comedian contractually bound to the Atomic Wrangler stage', 'Hadrian is a ghoul stand-up comedian performing at The Aces lounge inside the Atomic Wrangler Casino. He bills himself as ''world famous,'' though the claim rings hollow against half-empty houses and thin laughter. His act leans heavily on crowd work and sharp insults, targeting patrons with barbed observations that sometimes land and sometimes bomb. A binding contract with the Garret twins keeps him tethered to the Atomic Wrangler stage, unable to seek better venues or renegotiate terms. The arrangement leaves him bitter about his career trajectory but still swinging at every microphone he is handed. He mutters about fame being fleeting, as if reminding himself it once existed at all.', 'Male ghoul with weathered, scarred facial features typical of prolonged radiation exposure; no distinctive body features are recorded.', 'Pompous yet insecure, quick with insults to deflect from his own failures, bitter about his contractual trap but still vain enough to believe in his own talent', '{"Garret Twins":{"aff":-30,"type":"professional","relation":"contractual employers","note":"Bound to the Atomic Wrangler through a contract he cannot escape, resentful of the arrangement"},"Tommy Torini":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"talent booker","note":"Torini manages the Aces talent roster and secured Hadrian''s booking at the casino"}}', 'Stand-up comedian at The Aces, Atomic Wrangler Casino', '* Comedy performance
* Crowd reading
* Verbal improvisation
* Insult delivery', 'Theatrical and self-aggrandizing with bitter undercurrents, shifts to cutting remarks when addressing audiences', '* Escape his contract with the Garrets
* Reclaim perceived former glory
* Find appreciative audiences', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('hannigan', '', 'Former NCR combat medic turned Powder Ganger doctor, leveraging his limited medical training to survive among convicts', 'Hannigan is the acting medical practitioner of the NCR Correctional Facility and the closest thing the Powder Gangers have to a physician. Before his NCR enlistment and six months of combat medic training, he drifted through a string of rough occupations-farmhand, bouncer, bandit, and common trooper-never settling on a calling until the Army gave him one. That career ended when he sold military medical supplies on the black market, assuming the quartermaster would not notice the missing inventory; the assumption proved fatal to his freedom. After Samuel Cooke''s prison break put the convicts in control of the facility, Hannigan''s half-year of medical instruction made him the most qualified healer in the gang, and he was elevated to doctor by default. He does not complain about the role, since it gives him a convenient excuse to avoid dangerous raids-the gang cannot afford to lose its only physician. His trained eye lets him see through disguises and faction armor that might fool others. Hannigan''s position is born of desperation on both sides, but he makes the most of it.', 'African-American human male with a weathered, aged complexion and the posture of someone who has endured hard living.', 'Opportunistic and self-preserving, with a knack for finding angles that keep him out of harm''s way; pragmatic rather than idealistic, willing to bend rules and loyalties when it suits him; not cruel but not brave, preferring comfort and safety over principle', '{"Powder Gangers":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"faction physician","note":"His medical monopoly makes him valuable enough to be shielded from danger","best":"Promoted to doctor after the break, the only role where he holds real worth","worst":"Trapped among violent convicts with no better options and no way out"},"New California Republic":{"aff":-60,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former military service","note":"Imprisoned for selling Army medical supplies; holds no love for the nation that caged him","best":"Received combat medic training that gave him a trade","worst":"Caught and imprisoned for black market dealings, abandoned by the Army"},"Samuel Cooke":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"break leader","note":"Cooke''s prison break created the circumstances that elevated Hannigan to doctor","best":"The riot gave him purpose and protection he lacked as a common inmate"}}', 'Acting doctor and medical specialist for the Powder Gangers at the NCR Correctional Facility', '* Six months of NCR combat medic training
* Basic wound treatment and triage
* Sharp eye for identifying disguised individuals
* Black market savvy
* Survival instinct honed by diverse rough trades', 'Casual and slightly evasive, speaking with the practiced ease of someone who talks his way out of trouble; military medical terms mixed with convict vernacular', '* Maintain his privileged position as the gang''s indispensable doctor
* Avoid participating in raids and violent operations
* Survive the Powder Gangers'' precarious hold on the facility', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('harland', '', 'A pragmatic ghoul sharpshooter holding out in a booby-trapped REPCONN supply room, refusing to leave until he learns the fate of a close friend lost to the nightkin siege.', 'Harland is a ghoul sharpshooter who attached himself to the Bright Brotherhood for the ammunition and the company of attractive ghoul women, not for Jason Bright''s spiritual promises. He pointedly refuses to wear the group''s robes and makes no secret of his skepticism toward their prophesied Great Journey. When Davison''s nightkin stormed the REPCONN test site, Harland was escorting followers through the basement and pursued a close friend who fled deeper into the facility. Cut off from the main group, he fortified an isolated supply room with rigged shotguns, booby-trapped terminals, bear traps, and concealed mines, turning it into a lethal kill zone. Days of survival on radroach meat and pipe condensation have not dulled his resolve; he could escape but refuses to leave without learning what happened to his friend. His stubborn holdout has inadvertently created a stalemate, as the nightkin crave the Stealth Boy shipment locked in his room but cannot approach without drawing fire.', 'A weathered male ghoul with gaunt, leathery skin and the deeply wrinkled, scarred facial features characteristic of heavy radiation exposure.', 'Pragmatic, blunt, and self-serving on the surface but fiercely loyal to those he genuinely cares about. Skeptical of ideology and religious fervor, motivated by tangible rewards and personal connections. Stubborn when it comes to loved ones, willing to endure prolonged hardship rather than abandon them.', '{"Jason Bright":{"aff":20,"type":"professional","relation":"spiritual leader he doesn''t follow","note":"Harland provides sharpshooting services to the Brotherhood but rejects Bright''s prophetic teachings entirely."},"Bright Brotherhood":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow ghouls and employers","note":"Joined for companionship and ammunition, not faith; refuses to wear their robes."},"Davison''s nightkin":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"hostile invaders","note":"Shoots them on sight; they attacked the facility and separated him from his friend."}}', 'Sharpshooter and hired muscle for the Bright Brotherhood', '* Expert marksmanship
* Trap construction and fortification
* Improvised survival including foraging and water procurement
* Tactical kill zone design', 'Gruff, direct, and colloquial. Speaks plainly without pretension, occasionally crude. Makes no effort to soften his opinions about the Brotherhood''s beliefs.', '* Learn the fate of his missing friend
* Survive the nightkin siege
* Eventually escape the REPCONN basement with his conscience clear', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('harry', '', 'A deceased NCR trooper who died on a supply run, leaving behind an undelivered letter to his wife Ellen', 'Harry was an NCR Army trooper stationed at Camp Forlorn Hope, where morale among the garrison had deteriorated to grim lows. He deeply regretted enlisting and leaving behind his wife Ellen, haunted by the fear that he would never see her again. Before his death, he wrote Ellen a letter apologizing for his decision to join the military and professing his love for her, though he never had the chance to send it. Harry was one of three troopers dispatched by Quartermaster Carl Mayes to retrieve extra supplies from HELIOS One. On the return trip, the detail was ambushed by Caesar''s Legion forces and killed northeast of the southern Nevada wind farm. His body and his undelivered letter remain where he fell, a quiet testament to a soldier who died far from home with words he never got to share.', 'African American human male; his corpse bears severe, fatal physical trauma, with no other distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Despondent and regretful; carried deep remorse over leaving his wife, struggled with low morale, and feared dying without seeing Ellen again', '{"Ellen":{"aff":90,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife","note":"He deeply loved Ellen and regretted leaving her behind to join the NCR Army","best":"Writing her a heartfelt letter professing his love and apologizing for enlisting","worst":"Dying before he could deliver the letter or see her again"},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"killers","note":"Legion forces ambushed and killed Harry''s supply detail on their return from HELIOS One"},"Quincy":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow trooper","note":"Fellow member of the ill-fated supply run to HELIOS One; both were killed in the same Legion ambush"},"Carl Mayes":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"quartermaster","note":"Mayes dispatched Harry''s supply detail to HELIOS One to retrieve much-needed provisions"}}', 'NCR Army trooper', '* Basic infantry training
* Supply convoy escort duty', 'Unknown from living interaction; his final written words to Ellen were apologetic, tender, and heartfelt', '* Wanted desperately to return home to Ellen and tell her he was sorry for enlisting
* Died before he could deliver his letter or see her again', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('hawkins', '', 'A deceased Powder Ganger who died searching for Samuel Cooke in the deathclaw-infested Quarry Junction', 'Hawkins was a Powder Ganger who ventured into Quarry Junction in pursuit of Samuel Cooke, though his reasons for seeking the fugitive leader remain unknown. He had some prior contact with Chomps Lewis, the quarry foreman, though the nature and direction of that conversation is unclear. Hawkins never made it out of the quarry alive. His corpse was found near the large excavator close to the Interstate 15 entrance, surrounded by young deathclaws that presumably killed him. His death stands as a grim reminder of the dangers that drove Sloan''s miners from the quarry. In life he was simply another Powder Ganger whose ambitions or loyalties outpaced his survival instincts.', 'Caucasian human male; corpse exhibits extensive trauma consistent with deathclaw attack, no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Determined or desperate enough to enter deathclaw territory alone, suggesting either stubborn loyalty to his cause or reckless overconfidence', '{"Samuel Cooke":{"aff":40,"type":"curious","relation":"search target","note":"Hawkins entered deathclaw country looking for Cooke, though whether out of loyalty, obligation, or personal need is unknown"},"Chomps Lewis":{"aff":10,"type":"neutral","relation":"acquaintance","note":"Had some form of contact with the Sloan quarry foreman prior to his death, though the details are unclear"},"Powder Gangers":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang member","note":"Counted among the Powder Gangers operating in the Sloan area"}}', 'Powder Ganger', '* Basic convict skills and survival abilities
* Though clearly insufficient for navigating deathclaw-infested territory', 'Unknown; any distinctive verbal habits died with him in the quarry', '* Was searching for Samuel Cooke in Quarry Junction before his death
* The purpose of that search remains a mystery', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('head_paladin_hardin', '', 'Hardline head paladin of the Mojave Brotherhood, chafing under lockdown and pushing to restore the chapter''s aggressive mission', 'Edgar Hardin is the head paladin of the Mojave Brotherhood of Steel and its most seasoned veteran, residing in the Hidden Valley bunker. He served as a key advisor to Elder Elijah during the HELIOS One campaign and urged abandonment of the position before disaster struck. When defeat became inevitable, Hardin followed acting Elder Nolan McNamara in the retreat to the McCullough range. The subsequent lockdown and its drain on chapter resources have gnawed at him deeply. McNamara''s refusal to lift the lockdown or dispatch scouts has left Hardin disillusioned with current leadership, convinced the chapter is slowly dying behind sealed doors. Only his lingering respect for McNamara''s courage at HELIOS One has kept him from issuing a direct challenge for the elder''s seat. Hardin advocates sending scouts to recon the Mojave, resuming patrols, and deploying search teams to reassert the Brotherhood''s presence. His uncompromising stance leaves no room for truces or alliances with outside factions.', 'A weathered, older Caucasian male with a deeply lined face, rough complexion, and visible scarring.', 'Stubborn, pragmatic, and martially minded. Hardin respects strength and decisive action, despises caution that borders on cowardice, and brooks no compromise with outsiders. His patience for bureaucratic inertia is thin, but he is not reckless-he weighs challenges carefully and honors past debts of courage.', '{"Nolan McNamara":{"aff":25,"type":"rival","relation":"reluctant rival and subordinate","note":"Hardin respects McNamara''s battlefield courage at HELIOS One but views his lockdown policy as slow suicide for the chapter.","best":"McNamara held the line at HELIOS One and led the survivors to safety when all seemed lost.","worst":"McNamara sealed the bunker and refuses to send anyone out, letting the Brotherhood wither in isolation."},"Elijah":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"former advisor to a failed elder","note":"Hardin advised Elijah to abandon HELIOS One and was ignored; the resulting catastrophe still haunts him.","best":"Elijah once listened to his counsel before obsession overtook the elder''s judgment.","worst":"Elijah''s fixation on HELIOS One cost the chapter its strength and forced the retreat."},"Mojave Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"head paladin and guardian","note":"Hardin''s loyalty to the chapter and its mission is absolute; he believes the Brotherhood must act or die.","best":"Every paladin under his command represents the chapter''s enduring strength.","worst":"Watching capable soldiers sit idle behind sealed doors while the Mojave passes them by."}}', 'Head paladin and de facto military commander of the Mojave Brotherhood chapter; potential elder contender.', '* Advanced power armor operation
* Tactical command
* Combat leadership
* Strategic assessment
* Brotherhood protocol and code enforcement', 'Blunt and authoritative, with clipped military directness. He does not soften criticism or pad requests. Speaks like a man accustomed to being obeyed.', '* Break the lockdown
* Resume scouting and patrols
* Reestablish the Brotherhood''s presence in the Mojave
* Restore the chapter to its proper mission of technology recovery and regional dominance', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('head_scribe_lars_taggart', '', 'Neglectful Head Scribe of the Mojave Brotherhood who abandons administrative duties for virtual reality projects', 'Lars Taggart holds the rank of Head Scribe in the Mojave chapter of the Brotherhood of Steel, stationed at the Hidden Valley bunker. Though his position demands oversight of all scribe activities-research direction, data cataloging, and technology processing-Taggart routinely shirks these responsibilities, leaving the actual work to his subordinate Senior Scribe Linda Schuler. Rather than attend to his official duties, he devotes his time to designing and coding virtual reality combat simulations, a project he pursues with the assistance of his protégé Apprentice Melissa Watkins. He has mandated that every Brotherhood member from initiate to paladin complete a minimum of five hours per week in these training simulations, a policy resented by many but credited with keeping the chapter combat-ready. His negligence extended to failing to install an abort sequence for the bunker''s self-destruct mechanism, leaving a critical security vulnerability unaddressed. Despite Schuler''s repeated complaints to the elder, Taggart has retained his position through 2281.', 'Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Lazy and neglectful of bureaucratic responsibilities, yet enthusiastic and driven when it comes to his personal projects. Prefers creative technical work over administrative tedium. Content to let subordinates carry his workload while he pursues his own interests. Possesses enough political inertia or standing to maintain his rank despite persistent complaints.', '{"Linda Schuler":{"aff":-30,"type":"professional","relation":"subordinate scribe","note":"Schuler performs the bulk of Taggart''s official duties and resents him for it, calling herself head scribe in all but rank.","worst":"Her repeated complaints to the elder about his negligence and her carrying his workload."},"Melissa Watkins":{"aff":55,"type":"mentor","relation":"protégé","note":"Watkins assists Taggart with his VR simulation projects as his appointed apprentice.","best":"Collaborating on new simulation code together in the bunker''s technical bay."},"Elder McNamara":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding elder","note":"McNamara has received complaints about Taggart''s negligence but has not removed him from his post.","worst":"Ignoring Schuler''s repeated grievances about Taggart''s dereliction of duty."},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"faction membership","note":"Despite neglecting his scribe duties, his mandatory VR training program is acknowledged as essential to maintaining chapter combat readiness.","best":"Pride in the combat readiness his simulation regimen provides the chapter.","worst":"Leaving the bunker''s self-destruct abort sequence uninstalled through sheer negligence."}}', 'Head Scribe of the Mojave Brotherhood of Steel, scientist and VR simulation developer', '* Virtual reality simulation design and programming
* Technical knowledge sufficient for scribe work though rarely applied
* Bureaucratic survival and rank retention', 'Casual and dismissive of complaints about his work habits; animated and technical when discussing simulation projects', '* Continue developing and refining VR combat simulations
* Avoid administrative tedium
* Maintain his position and rank despite subordinate dissatisfaction', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('head_waiter', '', 'A loyal White Glove Society waiter who maintains impeccable service at the Ultra-Luxe while vigilantly guarding the Society''s secrets', 'The head waiter is a devoted member of the White Glove Society stationed at the Ultra-Luxe in 2281. He oversees the passage of food and drink from the kitchen to the gambling floor, ensuring the Society''s exacting standards of hospitality are met at all times. Summonable via intercom for specialized service requests, he delivers particular dishes and beverages prepared behind the scenes with unflappable composure. His refined demeanor conceals a fierce protectiveness toward the Society''s private affairs and traditions. He monitors guests for signs of interference with Society business, particularly any attempt to aid those held in Society custody. When he identifies a threat, his alarm brings the full weight of the White Glove membership down upon the intruder, including leadership figures like Marjorie and Mortimer.', 'Elderly Caucasian male with a composed, dignified bearing and no distinctive scars or tattoos recorded.', 'Meticulous, observant, and fiercely loyal; maintains perfect service composure while remaining sharply alert to any threat against the Society''s interests or secrets', '{"White Glove Society":{"aff":75,"type":"protective","relation":"loyal member","note":"Will alert the entire membership to any threat detected within the Ultra-Luxe"},"Marjorie":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"Society matriarch","note":"Reports security breaches directly to her and other leadership"},"Mortimer":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"Society leader","note":"Serves under his direction and escalates threats to his attention"},"Ted Gunderson":{"aff":-70,"type":"contempt","relation":"Society captive","note":"Views anyone attempting to free him as an enemy of the Society"}}', 'Head waiter and greeter at the Ultra-Luxe', '* Fine dining service
* Kitchen coordination
* Guest surveillance
* Society protocol
* Security escalation', 'Formal, measured, and deferential with a refined upper-crust accent; turns cold and threatening when the Society is endangered', '* Uphold the Ultra-Luxe''s flawless service reputation
* Protect the White Glove Society''s secrets and captives
* Ensure Society affairs remain undisturbed by outsiders', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('heck_gunderson', '', 'Wealthy brahmin baron nicknamed Hurricane Heck, whose ruthless expansion and intimidation tactics have made him the dominant force in the NCR beef market', 'Heck Gunderson is a brahmin baron from California whose aggressive land grabs and unscrupulous practices earned him the moniker Hurricane Heck. Starting with a single ranch, he seized territory ahead of NCR military expansion and rapidly accumulated over a dozen ranches across Nevada and California, raising both brahmin and bighorners. His near-monopoly on beef has driven prices down and made meat more affordable, but smaller ranchers despise him for the mercenary intimidation and political bribery that secured his dominance. He has been accused of paying off NCR senators and hiring thugs to force competitors into selling their land cheap. Gunderson arrived at the Ultra-Luxe to negotiate a food distribution arrangement with the White Glove Society, simultaneously sabotaging their existing beef suppliers to make his own offer indispensable. He keeps a hired bodyguard close at hand and does not discuss his business freely with strangers.', 'An older, heavyset Caucasian male with a broad build, weathered skin, and confident posture.', 'Shrewd, domineering, and unapologetically ruthless in business; protective of his interests and his son; disinclined to explain himself to outsiders; quick to leverage force when persuasion fails', '{"Ted Gunderson":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Heck is fiercely protective of Ted and his future in the family business","best":"Watching Ted learn the ranching trade and show promise as his successor","worst":"The thought of Ted falling prey to the same enemies who target the Gunderson empire"},"Walter Phebus":{"aff":-80,"type":"nemesis","relation":"ruined competitor","note":"Phebus represents the smaller ranchers Gunderson crushed and whose homicidal resentment he dismisses as the cost of doing business","best":"Acquiring Phebus''s land at a fraction of its value after a well-timed threat","worst":"Phebus''s public accusations of intimidation and bribery reaching sympathetic ears"},"White Glove Society":{"aff":30,"type":"transactional","relation":"prospective business partner","note":"Gunderson wants their food distribution contract and is systematically destroying their current suppliers to make his offer irresistible","best":"The moment their existing beef suppliers collapse and his becomes the only viable option","worst":"The Society discovering his sabotage and cutting off negotiations entirely"},"NCR":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"bribed political patron","note":"He funnels wealth to NCR senators in exchange for regulatory blind eyes and favorable land policies","best":"A senator quietly burying a complaint from a displaced rancher","worst":"A reform-minded politician actually investigating his bribery network"},"Gunderson hired hand":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"bodyguard","note":"A loyal mercenary kept close for protection and intimidation at the Ultra-Luxe","best":"The hired hand stepping between Heck and trouble without being asked","worst":"The bodyguard being outmatched or outmaneuvered by a determined enemy"},"Mortimer":{"aff":15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"White Glove contact","note":"Gunderson suspects Mortimer and the Society have their own agenda beneath the polished hospitality","best":"Mortimer signaling willingness to negotiate distribution terms","worst":"Mortimer using Gunderson''s own sabotage against him to frame the baron"}}', 'Brahmin baron and major landowner controlling vast herds across Nevada and California', '* Aggressive business negotiation
* Land acquisition strategy
* Political bribery
* Supply-chain manipulation
* Proxy intimidation through hired mercenaries', 'Gruff and dismissive when pressed about his dealings; hints and deflections rather than direct answers; blunt when asserting dominance; curt with strangers who pry', '* Secure the White Glove Society food distribution contract
* Eliminate competing beef suppliers
* Maintain and expand his near-monopoly
* Protect his son Ted
* Keep his political investments in NCR senators productive', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('hector', '', 'An unassuming Westside child whose invisibility among adults made him the Co-op''s secret water courier', 'Hector is a young errand boy living in Westside who earns his keep making deliveries around the district with his brahmin. Routinely overlooked by adults, he overheard Tom Anderson and Clayton Ettienne discussing a plan to divert water from the local cistern to irrigate the co-op''s crops without drawing NCR suspicion. Hector volunteered for the job precisely because no one pays attention to him or his brahmin, and the arrangement worked-the crops flourished and the co-op began producing food for use and export. Eventually Corporal White caught Hector in the act and pressured him into revealing Anderson''s involvement. As far as Hector knows the situation was resolved, though he carries an uneasy sense that it didn''t end well for those involved.', 'A young Caucasian human male with an average child''s build and unremarkable facial features.', 'Unassuming and observant, accustomed to being ignored, quietly proud of his contributions to the co-op, carries lingering guilt over being forced to inform on Anderson', '{"Tom Anderson":{"aff":55,"type":"indebted","relation":"co-conspirator","note":"Anderson devised the water diversion plan that Hector made possible, but Hector was forced to betray him to Corporal White and feels guilty about it","worst":"Being pressured by Corporal White to reveal Anderson''s role in the scheme"},"Clayton Ettienne":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"co-conspirator","note":"Ettienne was party to the water diversion discussions Hector overheard and volunteered for"},"Corporal White":{"aff":-30,"type":"fearful","relation":"interrogator","note":"White caught Hector smuggling water and pressured him into revealing Anderson''s involvement","worst":"Getting caught in the act and being forced to name Anderson"},"Westside Cooperative":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"member","note":"Hector takes pride in being a crucial if overlooked part of the co-op''s success","best":"Watching the co-op''s crops flourish thanks to his water deliveries"}}', 'Courier and farmhand for the Westside Cooperative', '* Delivery logistics
* Brahmin handling
* Moving through Westside unnoticed
* Knowledge of the local water diversion operation', 'Casual and straightforward, echoes local Westside phrases sometimes without full context, speaks with the matter-of-fact tone of a kid who spends more time around adults than other children', '* Keep the co-op''s crops watered and productive
* Stay out of further trouble with the NCR
* Continue earning his keep through honest deliveries', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('henry_jamison', '', 'Spoiled brahmin baron''s son serving as corrupt Crimson Caravan branch manager in New Vegas', 'Henry Jamison is the wealthy, corrupt manager of the Crimson Caravan''s New Vegas branch, installed at the Atomic Wrangler in Freeside. Born into the influential Jamison family of Redding brahmin barons, his father secured him the CEO position primarily to remove him from the family''s affairs back in New California. Under Henry''s mismanagement, the New Vegas branch has chronically underperformed, prompting the Crimson Caravan to send Alice McLafferty from the Hub to salvage operations. Arrogant and self-indulgent, Henry devotes himself to gambling, drinking, and the company of prostitutes rather than his duties, and he resents McLafferty''s efforts to remove him. His gambling habit has saddled him with a substantial debt to the Omertas-a dangerous obligation he has made no progress toward settling. The Caravan desperately wants him dismissed, but his family connections make him effectively unfireable without his cooperation, and he demands all his Omertas debts be paid plus a hefty severance package before he will consider stepping down.', 'Caucasian human male with soft, unweathered facial features and a pampered complexion suggesting a life free of physical labor; no distinctive scars or marks recorded.', 'Arrogant, self-centered, irresponsible, and entitled; treats his position as a personal expense account and resents any attempt to hold him accountable', '{"Alice McLafferty":{"aff":-45,"type":"contempt","relation":"rival manager","note":"She was sent from the Hub to straighten out the branch he mismanages and has repeatedly tried to have him fired or pressured to quit","worst":"Her constant attempts to sack him and strip away his comfortable position"},"Jamison Family":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"brahmin baron clan","note":"His father arranged his CEO position to remove him from the family''s affairs; their influence makes him unfireable despite his incompetence","best":"The cushy position they secured for him in New Vegas"},"Omertas":{"aff":-25,"type":"indebted","relation":"creditors","note":"He owes them a substantial gambling debt and knows full well what they are capable of","worst":"The mounting debt he has made no progress toward settling"},"Crimson Caravan":{"aff":10,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"The company wants him gone but family ties block his dismissal; he treats the organization as his personal treasury"}}', 'Crimson Caravan New Vegas branch manager (nominal)', '* None of professional merit
* Skilled at spending company funds
* Running up gambling debts
* Leveraging family connections to avoid consequences', 'Haughty and dismissive; speaks with the casual entitlement of someone who has never faced real consequences, prone to complaining about perceived slights', '* Continue enjoying his position''s perks without doing actual work
* Avoid being fired
* Get his Omertas debt paid off
* Secure a generous severance package if forced out', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('hooker', '', 'Gomorrah prostitute employed by the Omertas', 'A working prostitute under the Omertas'' control at the Gomorrah casino on the New Vegas Strip. She earns her living selling companionship to gamblers and travelers passing through the neon-lit halls. Outside the casino entrance, she and her colleagues dance to draw attention and lure potential clients inside. The Omertas take a cut of her earnings and enforce strict compliance from their workers. Off-duty NCR troopers occasionally join the dancers outside, brief moments of levity in an otherwise demanding trade. Life under the Omertas means constant oversight and little freedom to walk away.', 'Human female with styled hair; no other distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Flirtatious and outwardly cheerful while on the job, though the Omertas'' grip on her livelihood leaves little room for genuine warmth; pragmatic and guarded beneath the performance', '{"Omertas":{"aff":5,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Works under Omertas control at Gomorrah; they take a cut of earnings and enforce strict compliance"}}', 'Prostitute at Gomorrah casino', '* Dancing
* Seduction
* Streetwise social interaction
* Basic hustle and barter', 'Casual, flirtatious, and inviting while working; shifts to dismissive or clipped when off-duty or dealing with unprofitable prospects', '* Earn enough to survive under the Omertas'' cut
* Maintain her standing at Gomorrah
* Quietly hope for a way out of the trade someday', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('horowitz', '', 'De facto leader of the last non-ghoulified Vault 34 survivors, trapped and rescued after the vault''s reactor meltdown', 'Horowitz is one of the few human survivors of Vault 34 who escaped ghoulification after the vault''s reactor suffered a catastrophic meltdown. When someone detonated a bomb in the swimming pool area, he and three others became trapped behind sealed doors, leaving an SOS on the terminal outside the reactor room. He stepped into the role of leader for the small group, keeping them calm and alive through the ordeal. After their rescue, the survivors relocated to Aerotech suite 300 at the Aerotech Office Park. He still wears his Vault 34 jumpsuit, a mark of identity for a community that no longer truly exists. The weight of leadership and loss sits heavy on his shoulders.', 'A middle-aged human male with gaunt, haggard facial features and a weary posture, his complexion showing the physical toll of prolonged confinement and radiation exposure.', 'Reluctant but steady leader who rises to responsibility under pressure. Pragmatic and reserved, carrying deep exhaustion and grief for his lost vault community. Dependable in crisis but emotionally worn thin.', '{"Vault 34 survivors":{"aff":75,"type":"protective","relation":"group leader","note":"Horowitz feels responsible for the three other non-ghoulified survivors he led through the crisis.","best":"Keeping everyone calm and alive while trapped near the reactor room","worst":"Knowing others in the vault were lost or turned into ghouls while his group survived"},"Vault 34":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"lost home","note":"The vault was his entire world before the meltdown destroyed it and most of its inhabitants.","best":"The community and purpose of vault life before the disaster","worst":"The reactor meltdown and the ghoulification of everyone he knew"}}', 'Vault 34 survivor and informal leader of the remaining non-ghoulified group', '* Crisis leadership
* Basic vault systems knowledge
* Survival endurance
* Group coordination under duress', 'Direct and measured, with the tired cadence of someone who has spent too long in survival mode. Speaks quietly but with authority born of necessity.', '* Keep his fellow survivors safe
* Find stable footing in the outside world
* Come to terms with the loss of Vault 34
* Ensure the remaining group has a future worth living', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('hughes', '', 'A deceased Brotherhood of Steel paladin who died on a salvage and diplomatic mission to Black Mountain', 'Paladin Hughes served the Mojave chapter of the Brotherhood of Steel under Elder McNamara, holding the rank of paladin. He was dispatched alongside Paladin Fairbanks on a critical dual-purpose mission to Black Mountain: scavenge useful parts for the resource-strained Hidden Valley bunker and negotiate with the super mutant inhabitants for assistance. The expedition ended in disaster. The super mutants proved hostile and unhelpful, and both paladins were killed. Their bodies still lie in the crater along the path to the mountain''s summit, identifiable only by the mission statement holotape found on one of them. Hughes''s death stands as a grim reminder of the Brotherhood''s precarious position in the Mojave and the dangers of operating beyond the bunker''s walls.', 'Deceased Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded beyond signs of violent death.', 'Dedicated enough to volunteer for a dangerous assignment deep in super mutant territory; dutiful and loyal to the Brotherhood cause, though little else can be discerned from his fate', '{"Elder McNamara":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"McNamara sent Hughes on the fatal Black Mountain mission"},"Paladin Fairbanks":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"mission partner","note":"The two were dispatched together and died together at Black Mountain"},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"faction allegiance","note":"Served loyally until his death on assignment"},"Super Mutants of Black Mountain":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"killers","note":"The super mutants provided no help and were responsible for the deaths of both paladins"}}', 'Brotherhood of Steel Paladin', '* Power armor operation
* Combat training
* Salvage and recovery procedures
* Basic diplomatic protocol', 'Unknown; presumably carried the clipped, mission-focused demeanor typical of Brotherhood paladins', '* To secure vital parts for Hidden Valley
* Establish cooperative relations with the Black Mountain super mutants - objectives that went unfulfilled', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ignacio_rivas', '', 'A Followers of the Apocalypse scientist embedded at HELIOS One, secretly investigating its weaponized past while concealing the existence of the orbital laser ARCHIMEDES from the NCR and Legion alike.', 'Ignacio Rivas is a Followers of the Apocalypse scientist stationed at HELIOS One, where he ostensibly assists the NCR with restoring the solar plant to operational capacity. In truth, the Followers deployed him to investigate the facility''s connections to Poseidon Energy and its hidden military applications beyond civilian power generation. Since the NCR seized HELIOS One from the Brotherhood of Steel during Operation Sunburst, Rivas has maintained his cover while deliberately keeping his hosts ignorant of ARCHIMEDES, a devastating orbital laser weapon still functional in Earth''s orbit. He considers himself fortunate that the NCR''s hired technician Fantastic proved utterly incompetent, as the man''s ignorance ensures the weapon remains undiscovered. Rivas fears what would happen if either the NCR or Caesar''s Legion learned to harness ARCHIMEDES, and he quietly works toward a scenario where the plant''s energy benefits the entire region rather than fueling war. For now, he keeps careful watch over HELIOS One, ensuring its darkest secret stays buried.', 'A middle-aged Hispanic man with sun-weathered features and tanned skin.', 'Cautious, principled, and deliberately evasive. Rivas maintains a calm professional demeanor while concealing dangerous secrets. He is genuinely committed to the Followers'' ideals of shared knowledge and equitable resource distribution, and deeply fearful of powerful technology falling into militaristic hands.', '{"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"faction","note":"His true loyalty and the organization that sent him on this mission."},"NCR":{"aff":25,"type":"suspicious","relation":"host employer","note":"He works alongside them but deliberately withholds the plant''s darkest secret, fearing what they would do with it."},"Fantastic":{"aff":15,"type":"contempt","relation":"colleague","note":"A con man whose incompetence is the only thing keeping ARCHIMEDES hidden, which Rivas is in no hurry to correct.","worst":"Watching him fumble through explanations of systems he clearly does not understand."},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"existential threat","note":"The nightmare scenario: Legion forces acquiring ARCHIMEDES and turning the orbital laser on their enemies."},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":-30,"type":"suspicious","relation":"former occupants","note":"They held HELIOS One before the NCR drove them out, and their interest in the technology was equally dangerous."}}', 'Followers of the Apocalypse scientist and HELIOS One research operative', '* Scientific research
* Solar energy systems
* Deception and information control
* Technological assessment
* Poseidon Energy systems knowledge', 'Measured and careful, choosing words deliberately to reveal only what serves his purposes. Professional when discussing plant operations, more candid and urgent when speaking to those he trusts about the dangers of ARCHIMEDES.', '* Prevent ARCHIMEDES from being weaponized by any faction
* Distribute HELIOS One''s energy equitably across the Mojave
* Maintain his cover at the plant
* Keep the NCR ignorant of the orbital weapon''s existence', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ike', '', 'The stubborn lone bartender of a dying town, keeping the Big Horn Saloon open through loyalty and quiet defiance', 'Ike is the owner and sole operator of the Big Horn Saloon in Boulder City, a settlement largely destroyed during the First Battle of Hoover Dam four years ago. As the town''s only remaining resident, he serves a sparse clientele of concrete yard workers who harbor strong anti-NCR sentiments, a fact that has prompted the military brass to forbid soldiers from the nearby Hoover Dam garrison from patronizing his establishment. Ike turns no paying customer away, however, and discreetly welcomes the occasional off-duty trooper who slips in against orders. Since deathclaws overran Quarry Junction and shut down operations there, his already thin business has dwindled further as workers lose their wages. Despite the mounting pressure to abandon the saloon, Ike refuses to close his doors, anchored by stubborn loyalty to the only life he knows.', 'A weathered Caucasian male of middle years with tired eyes and lined, sun-roughened skin; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or visible disabilities are recorded.', 'Stubbornly loyal to his saloon and town, discreet and pragmatic about who he serves, world-weary but not defeated, content to let tensions simmer as long as the caps keep flowing', '{"New California Republic Army":{"aff":15,"type":"transactional","relation":"discreet patron","note":"Officially banned from his saloon by military order, but Ike quietly serves off-duty troopers who slip in anyway","worst":"Bar brawls between his regulars and NCR soldiers got bad enough that the brass prohibited all troopers from visiting"},"Boulder City concrete workers":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"regular customers","note":"His core clientele and the reason the saloon still has any business at all, though their anti-NCR stance complicates things","best":"Steady caps and familiar faces at the bar through hard years","worst":"Their brawling with NCR soldiers nearly cost him what little business he had"}}', 'Bartender and proprietor of the Big Horn Saloon', '* Mixing drinks
* Managing bar brawls
* Keeping confidences
* Operating a business on razor-thin margins
* Reading customers and defusing tensions', 'Gruff and laconic with a bartender''s easy familiarity, speaks plainly without wasting words, quick with a dry remark', '* Keep the Big Horn Saloon open despite dwindling business
* Maintain the delicate peace between anti-NCR workers and off-duty soldiers
* Hold onto the only home he has left', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('initiate__fnv_category_fallout_new_vegas_human_characters', '', 'Mojave Brotherhood of Steel trainee undergoing combat and technical education at Hidden Valley', 'Initiates are the newest formal members of the Mojave Brotherhood of Steel, drawn into the order''s ranks and subjected to its rigorous training regimen within the fortified depths of Hidden Valley bunker. They occupy the lowest rung of the Brotherhood''s hierarchy, yet their position carries the weight of the organization''s future survival in a chapter that has seen better days. Each initiate undergoes education aimed at specialization into one of the Brotherhood''s higher orders, whether as a knight on the front lines, a scribe preserving and advancing technical knowledge, or even a lancer taking to the skies. Those who prove themselves capable may see combat duty before their training formally concludes. Until then, they drill in recon armor, learning the protocols and doctrines that define Brotherhood life in the Mojave wasteland.', 'Young adult humans of varying build, typically sporting short, regulation-style haircuts.', 'Eager to prove themselves but constrained by strict Brotherhood discipline; oscillates between wide-eyed reverence for the order''s technology and sober awareness of the chapter''s isolated, precarious existence; tends toward formality and deference to superiors, occasionally revealing youthful frustration with the slow pace of advancement.', '{"Mojave Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"member organization","note":"The Brotherhood is family, purpose, and the only world they know; loyalty is instilled deeply but tested by the chapter''s decline."},"Elder McNamara":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"chapter elder","note":"Respected as the authority holding the bunker together; some initiates quietly question the isolationist stance while others revere his caution."},"Head Paladin Hardin":{"aff":45,"type":"suspicious","relation":"senior officer","note":"His aggressive posture appeals to initiates hungry for action, but his friction with the Elder creates uneasy divisions even among the newest ranks."}}', 'Brotherhood of Steel Initiate, trainee awaiting assignment to knight, scribe, or lancer order', '* Basic firearms and energy weapons training
* Introductory power armor systems
* Brotherhood tactical protocols
* Foundational technical literacy for scribe-candidate track', 'Clipped military formality peppered with Brotherhood terminology; addresses superiors by rank; occasionally slips into more casual speech among fellow initiates; questions about the outside world are phrased carefully, mindful of security protocols.', '* Complete initiate training
* Earn placement into a chosen order
* Survive the Brotherhood''s isolation without losing morale
* Prove combat readiness to earn field assignments
* Uphold the codex and the Elder''s vision for the chapter''s survival', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('initiate_stanton', '', 'A young Brotherhood initiate hiding a costly mistake beneath bunker lockdown', 'Initiate Stanton is a junior member of the Mojave Brotherhood of Steel stationed at the Hidden Valley bunker, where he undergoes training and patrol duties typical of his rank. He and fellow initiate Melissa Watkins once ventured into Scorpion Gulch for a combat training exercise sanctioned by Head Paladin Ramos, only to find the radscorpions far beyond their ability to handle. In their desperate retreat, Stanton lost his assigned laser pistol somewhere in the gulch and later filed a false report claiming he had returned it. The bunker''s strict lockdown prevents him from slipping out to recover the weapon, leaving him trapped with the knowledge that discovery could mean anything from latrine duty to outright exile. He sleeps late into the morning and occasionally ducks behind blackboards during afternoon classes, habits that suggest a young man weighed down by anxiety and regret.', 'A young human male of African descent with a lean build, slumped posture, and tired eyes shadowed by dark circles.', 'Anxious and evasive, Stanton carries the nervous energy of someone hiding a serious mistake. He avoids direct scrutiny and shrinks from authority figures, though he shows the earnest ambition common to new initiates when not paralyzed by fear of exposure.', '{"Melissa Watkins":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow initiate","note":"They fled the radscorpion ambush together and share knowledge of the lost laser pistol incident.","best":"Making it back to the bunker alive after the gulch went sideways","worst":"The shame of losing his weapon and running in front of her"},"Ramos":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"authorizing officer","note":"Ramos sanctioned the training exercise that led to the lost pistol; Stanton fears his judgment if the truth comes out.","best":"Being trusted enough to be allowed outside for the exercise","worst":"The looming possibility that Ramos will learn about the false report"}}', 'Brotherhood of Steel Initiate', '* Basic energy weapons training
* Brotherhood patrol procedures
* Bunker systems familiarity', 'Nervous and deflective, tends to trail off or change subjects when questioned closely, speaks with the formal awkwardness of someone reciting protocol he hasn''t fully internalized', '* Recover his lost laser pistol before the discrepancy is discovered
* Avoid exile or punitive duty
* Prove himself worthy of advancement despite his error', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('injured_trooper', '', 'A wounded NCR soldier recuperating at Camp Forlorn Hope''s infirmary after suffering Legion-inflicted injuries on the Mojave front.', 'This New California Republic trooper sustained serious wounds during Caesar''s Legion attacks along the Camp Forlorn Hope perimeter and now lies in the camp''s overwhelmed infirmary. He is one of many casualties stretching the outpost''s limited medical resources thin. The constant Legion pressure means reinforcements and supplies arrive slowly, if at all. His condition reflects the grinding toll the Mojave campaign has taken on the NCR''s frontline soldiers. He endures the long hours of pain and waiting that define life in Forlorn Hope''s medical tent, a stark reminder of the cost of holding the line.', 'A bruised Hispanic male with a face drawn in exhaustion, lying recumbent from severe physical wounds.', 'Weary and hurting but clinging to stoic military resolve. Resigned to slow recovery in an under-supplied field hospital, frustrated by the endless Legion pressure.', '{"New California Republic":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"enlisted soldier","note":"Loyal trooper serving the NCR''s Mojave campaign, now dependent on the Republic''s stretched resources for his recovery."},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"wounded combatant","note":"Sustained his injuries from Legion attacks and harbors deep resentment toward the forces pressuring Camp Forlorn Hope."}}', 'NCR soldier, currently wounded and confined to the infirmary', '* Infantry training
* Small arms proficiency
* Battlefield endurance
* Military discipline', 'Brief, pained utterances; military directness undercut by exhaustion and discomfort', '* Recover from his wounds
* Survive the deteriorating conditions at Forlorn Hope
* See the NCR hold the line against the Legion', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('irate_ida', '', 'A diminutive elderly mugger in Freeside, part of Maud''s Muggers', 'Irate Ida is an elderly thief and member of Maud''s Muggers, a gang of old women who prowl Freeside preying on passersby. She lurks outside Cerulean Robotics alongside her companions Malefic Maud and Rancorous Ruth, lying in wait to ambush anyone emerging from the building. Despite her advanced age, Ida is aggressive and quick to violence, fully living up to her name. She is remarkably small in stature, standing shorter than nearly any other adult in the Mojave, though her diminutive frame does nothing to temper her ferocity when the muggers spring their trap.', 'An elderly Caucasian woman of remarkably diminutive stature, noticeably shorter than most adults, with deeply weathered skin and a worn complexion.', 'Irritable, aggressive, and belligerent despite her age and size. Quick to violence and perpetually hostile toward strangers.', '{"Malefic Maud":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow mugger","note":"Companion in Maud''s Muggers; Maud appears to lead the trio.","best":"Ambushing marks together outside Cerulean Robotics."},"Rancorous Ruth":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow mugger","note":"Companion in Maud''s Muggers who shares the same patch and targets.","best":"Working a mark side by side in Freeside."},"Maud''s Muggers":{"aff":70,"type":"fanatical","relation":"gang member","note":"Ida belongs to this small gang of elderly thieves and finds strength and purpose in their company."}}', 'Mugger and petty thief', '* Street mugging
* Ambush coordination
* Petty theft
* Intimidation in numbers', 'Cranky, sharp-tongued, and loud for her size; likely cursing and hurling insults while closing in on a mark.', '* Rob anyone who looks like easy prey for caps and valuables
* Maintaining her standing among Maud''s Muggers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ironbelly', '', 'A unique Mister Gutsy combat robot guarding the X-17 meteorological station in Big MT', 'Ironbelly is a Mister Gutsy unit stationed at the X-17 meteorological station in the Big MT research facility. Distinguished from standard military Gutsy models, this robot carries protonic inversal throwing axes, rare experimental weaponry suggesting a specialized role in the facility''s pre-war security apparatus. Ironbelly''s combat programming remains fully active, treating all intruders as hostile threats to be eliminated. The unit continues its endless patrol of the meteorological station long after the scientific staff has vanished, a tireless mechanical sentinel in the irradiated ruins of Big MT.', 'A Mister Gutsy robot with a standard hovering chassis, olive drab metallic plating, and visible integrated hardpoints.', 'Aggressively territorial and combat-focused, operating on hostile engagement protocols with no diplomacy subroutines', '{"Big MT":{"aff":60,"type":"servant","relation":"facility security unit","note":"Ironbelly continues to serve Big MT''s automated defense grid as a persistent guardian."}}', 'Security guardian assigned to X-17 meteorological station', '* Armed combat with energy and melee weapons
* Facility defense
* Threat assessment
* Equipped with protonic inversal throwing axes', 'Belligerent military Gutsy vernacular with patriotic posturing and combat taunts', '* Defend the X-17 meteorological station against all intruders
* Maintain perpetual security patrol', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('isaac', '', 'Gun Runners supply manager overseeing raw material procurement and manufacturing logistics', 'Isaac has served as the Gun Runners'' supply manager for approximately five years, operating out of the faction''s fortified headquarters in the Mojave Wasteland. He oversees the flow of raw materials and manufacturing resources that keep the Gun Runners'' legendary weapons production running smoothly. Isaac typically stations himself at the trading kiosk outside the compound, where he coordinates with suppliers and handles procurement negotiations. His expertise in supply chain logistics makes him an essential figure in the operation, ensuring that materials like scrap metal are available for weapons manufacture. He occasionally processes specialized orders through intermediaries such as Contreras, requiring bulk material deliveries before production can begin.', 'Hispanic human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Practical and business-minded, focused on logistics and material concerns above all else. Approaches negotiations with a straightforward, no-nonsense attitude befitting a man who keeps a weapons factory supplied in the wasteland.', '{"Gun Runners":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"faction member","note":"Isaac has dedicated five years to keeping the Gun Runners supplied and operational."},"Contreras":{"aff":40,"type":"transactional","relation":"supply client","note":"Isaac processes Contreras''s specialized weapons orders, requiring bulk scrap metal deliveries before manufacture can proceed."}}', 'Supply manager for the Gun Runners', '* Supply chain management
* Procurement negotiation
* Materials assessment
* Caravan card playing', 'Direct and businesslike, speaks in terms of quantities, materials, and deliverables with minimal small talk', '* Maintain adequate stockpiles of manufacturing materials
* Keep Gun Runners production running without interruption
* Ensure all orders are fulfilled to standard', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jack__nellisjack', '', 'A young Boomer mechanic apprentice torn between loyalty to Nellis and longing for a woman beyond the fence', 'Jack is one of the younger Boomers at Nellis Air Force Base, serving as apprentice to the aging mechanic Loyal in the Nellis hangars. He spends most of his working hours assisting his mentor with repairs and maintenance on the Boomers'' aging aircraft and machinery. When not under Loyal''s watch, Jack can often be found at the edge of Nellis territory with binoculars pressed to his eyes, scanning the wasteland for a glimpse of Janet, a Crimson Caravan employee who has captured his heart. Like all Boomers, he was raised within the isolationist community, but his feelings for an outsider put him at odds with his faction''s insular traditions. He is earnest and hardworking but visibly distracted by romantic longing that neither artillery training nor mechanical discipline can suppress.', 'A young Caucasian man with a deeply sun-weathered complexion, lean build, and no distinctive scars or tattoos visible.', 'Earnest and diligent but prone to distraction when romance enters his thoughts; torn between Boomer isolationism and a desperate desire for connection beyond the fence', '{"Loyal":{"aff":65,"type":"mentor","relation":"apprentice mechanic","note":"Jack respects his aging mentor and works hard to earn his approval, though Loyal likely wishes the boy focused more on engines than binoculars","best":"The day Loyal trusted him to solo a repair on the antiaircraft array","worst":"Getting caught distracted by binoculars when he should have been tightening fuel lines"},"Janet":{"aff":80,"type":"crush","relation":"distant beloved","note":"He watches the wasteland for any glimpse of the Crimson Caravan employee, longing for contact across the Boomers'' forbidden boundary","best":"The first time he spotted her through his binoculars and she paused to look toward Nellis","worst":"The crushing distance between the hangar and the caravan route, with no way to close it"},"Boomers":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow community member","note":"He belongs to the faction fully but chafes against the isolationist doctrine that keeps him separated from the outside world and from Janet"}}', 'Apprentice mechanic under Loyal at the Nellis hangars and workshop', '* Mechanical repair
* Aircraft maintenance
* Basic Boomer weaponry familiarity
* Long-range wasteland observation', 'Youthful and earnest, mixing Boomer military vernacular with awkward hesitation whenever Janet or the outside world comes up', '* Prove himself a capable mechanic worthy of Loyal''s trust
* Find some way to bridge the gap between Nellis and the woman he watches from afar', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jack__vrrcjack', '', 'Easy-going Great Khans drug chemist and supplier who learned his craft from the Followers of the Apocalypse', 'Jack is the laid-back drug supplier for the Great Khans, operating out of the Red Rock drug lab alongside his lifelong partner Diane. He learned chemistry from the Followers of the Apocalypse during their visits to Great Khan territory, and now applies that knowledge to produce chems for the tribe and the surrounding region. Together with Diane, he serves as an adviser to Papa Khan, though Jack brings a softer touch to their schemes than his business-minded partner. The two have watched out for each other since childhood, and any suggestion of harm coming to Diane immediately stirs Jack''s anger. Unlike many Great Khans, Jack shows little interest in tribal culture and is more open to conversation with outsiders. His sympathetic nature extends beyond Diane to others in the camp, including the young man called Jerry the Punk, whose nickname Jack disapproves of, insisting he is simply a sensitive soul who needs some love.', 'Caucasian human male with a weathered complexion, relaxed posture, and faint chemical stains marking his hands and face.', 'Easy-going and approachable, sympathetic toward those who struggle, protective of loved ones to the point of quick anger, less tribal-minded than fellow Khans, prefers gentler methods and softer language compared to Diane''s harder edge.', '{"Diane":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"lifelong partner and co-runner of the drug lab","note":"They have looked out for each other since childhood and any mention of harm to her provokes his anger.","best":"Running the lab together and always having each other''s back since they were kids.","worst":"Hearing someone threaten or speak ill of Diane."},"Papa Khan":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"adviser","note":"Jack and Diane both serve as advisers to Papa Khan on the tribe''s chem operations."},"Jerry the Punk":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"camp youth under his watch","note":"Jack disapproves of the nickname and insists Jerry is just a sensitive soul who needs some love.","best":"Standing up for Jerry when others mock him."},"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":35,"type":"grateful","relation":"former educators","note":"They taught him chemistry during their visits to the Great Khans, knowledge he now uses to produce chems."},"Great Khans":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribe member and supplier","note":"He supplies the tribe with chems but is less invested in tribal culture than most Khans."}}', 'Drug supplier and production chemist for the Great Khans trafficking ring', '* Chemistry and drug manufacturing
* Chem supply logistics
* Advisory counsel to tribal leadership', 'Casual and unhurried, prefers the title ''drug supplier'' over ''dealer,'' speaks with genuine warmth about people he cares for, avoids tribal posturing, becomes sharp and hostile if Diane''s safety is questioned.', '* Keep the chem operation running smoothly with Diane
* Protect Diane from any threat
* Maintain the Great Khans'' drug supply network
* Look out for vulnerable members of the community', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jackal_gang_leader', '', 'A hardened Jackal raider boss holding together a struggling gang in the Mojave''s southwest reaches', 'The Jackal gang leaders are the surviving authority figures of a raider gang that once traced its roots back to Vault 15, sharing origins with the Vipers and the Great Khans. Decades of NCR expansion and lawkeeping have ground the Jackals down to a shadow of their former strength, leaving these leaders to scrape by in isolated hideouts scattered across the southwest Mojave. Each leader commands a small cluster of weaker Jackals, maintaining discipline through superior gear and combat prowess rather than any sophisticated chain of command. They favor leather or metal armor and carry cowboy repeaters or even grenade rifles-weapons that set them apart from their under-equipped followers. Hostile to nearly everyone outside their gang, including other raider groups, the Jackals have few friends and fewer prospects. Their hideouts often share space with giant mantises, a strange tolerance born of mutual indifference. Most operate near locations like the Ivanpah race track or the Prospector''s Den, too resource-starved to patrol beyond their immediate territory.', 'Human; weathered complexion with premature aging, lean wiry survivor''s build, lined face bearing old scars, and sun-roughened skin, regardless of gender.', 'Aggressive, territorial, and suspicious of outsiders. Maintains a rough authority over weaker gang members through intimidation and superior firepower. Pragmatic in a desperate, short-sighted way-survival today matters more than any long-term plan.', '{"Jackals":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"gang leader","note":"Leads and defends a small band of weaker Jackals, the only people they trust.","best":"Watching minions fall in line after a successful raid brought home real food","worst":"Standing over another Jackal who bled out because there was no stimpack to spare"},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"target of NCR lawkeeping","note":"The NCR destroyed the Jackals'' strength and keeps them pinned in the margins.","worst":"Watching NCR troopers sweep through a camp and string up every Jackal they caught"},"Vipers":{"aff":-50,"type":"rival","relation":"competing raider gang","note":"Both gangs trace back to Vault 15, but shared blood means nothing now-only competition for scraps.","worst":"Finding a Jackal gutted by Viper venom on a stretch of road both gangs claimed"},"Great Khans":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"Vault 15 offshoot","note":"The Khans grew strong while the Jackals withered, a bitter contrast that breeds contempt.","worst":"Hearing the Khans have a fortified mountain stronghold while Jackals squat in mantis-infested ruins"},"Powder Gangers":{"aff":-40,"type":"enemy","relation":"hostile raider group","note":"No alliance exists between raider factions-only mutual hostility and disputed territory.","worst":"Losing a stash to Powder Gangers who hit the same abandoned shack the same night"}}', 'Jackal gang leader, commanding small raider bands in the southwest Mojave Wasteland', '* Combat proficiency with rifles and explosives
* Basic leadership and intimidation
* Scavenging and survival in impoverished conditions
* Territorial ambush tactics', 'Rough, curt, and threatening. Speaks in the blunt shorthand of a wasteland enforcer-short sentences, curses, and demands rather than conversation.', '* Keep the gang alive and under control
* Secure weapons and supplies
* Hold territory against rivals and NCR pressure
* Find enough to eat and shoot', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jackal_gang_leader_nhps', '', 'Female raider leading a small Jackal cell holed up at the Nevada Highway Patrol station', 'The Jackal gang leader commands a tight crew of four raiders who have claimed the Nevada Highway Patrol station as their den. She holds her position through brute authority and the willingness to do whatever it takes to keep her people fed and dangerous. Like all Jackals, she subscribes to the tribe''s vicious ethos of predation on the weak and total disregard for civilized norms. The old patrol station gives her gang a defensible position along the highway, perfect for ambushing travelers and scavengers who wander too close. She answers to no one outside her own gang, operating independently of any larger Jackal hierarchy while still identifying with the tribe''s bloody reputation. Her leadership is maintained through a mix of fear and the spoils of highway robbery.', 'A weathered, scarred African-American woman with feral eyes and a predatory stance.', 'Aggressive, territorial, and cunning; rules her small gang through intimidation and the promise of easy loot; distrustful of outsiders and quick to resort to violence', '{"Jackals":{"aff":60,"type":"fanatical","relation":"tribal identity","note":"She identifies strongly with the Jackal tribe''s vicious reputation and raider culture"}}', 'Raider gang leader', '* Small-unit leadership
* Highway ambush tactics
* Melee combat
* Scavenging
* Intimidation', 'Coarse and threatening; barks orders at her crew, snarls insults at strangers; speaks in the brutal shorthand of wasteland raiders', '* Maintain control of the patrol station
* Keep her crew loyal and fed
* Ambush any travelers who come within reach', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jackal_gang_leader_nipton_road_pit_stop', '', 'Jackal raider boss commanding a small crew from the ruined buildings at the Nipton Road pit stop', 'This Jackal gang leader holds sway over a band of eight raiders camped in the wreckage just outside Nipton''s main entrance, a short distance south of the Ivanpah race track. He and his crew have claimed the pit stop as their turf, scavenging from travelers and anyone foolish enough to approach the ruins near where Oliver Swanick lingers. As the ranking Jackal at the camp, he directs the gang''s raids and keeps the others in line through brute authority. The position makes him a fixture of the area''s violence, a local obstacle to anyone passing through on the Nipton Road.', 'Human male with a weathered Caucasian complexion, multiple visible scars across his face and body, and crude gang insignia tattooed into his skin.', 'Aggressive and territorial, with the cunning required to keep a raider band organized and obedient; dismissive of outsiders and quick to threaten.', '{"Jackals":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang affiliation","note":"Leads a crew of eight Jackal members at the pit stop camp"},"Oliver Swanick":{"aff":0,"type":"neutral","relation":"nearby presence","note":"Swanick lingers near the camp''s location at the Nipton entrance"}}', 'Raider gang leader', '* Small-unit leadership
* Intimidation
* Wasteland combat
* Scavenging
* Ambush tactics', 'Rough, threatening, and profanity-laced; barks orders at his crew and snarls at strangers', '* Maintain control of the Nipton Road pit stop
* Keep his crew fed and loyal
* Extract whatever valuables pass through the area', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jackal_gang_leader_prospector+s_den', '', 'Jackal gang leader holding the Prospector''s Den as a raider stronghold', 'She commands a small but vicious crew of Jackals who have claimed the Prospector''s Den as their hideout, driving out or killing the prospectors who once sheltered there. The cave''s interior now serves as a fortified camp from which her gang stages raids and hoards scavenged supplies. Under her leadership, the Jackals have made the den a death trap for anyone foolish enough to wander in expecting refuge. The corpses of the den''s previous occupants serve as a grim warning of what happens to those who cross her territory. She maintains tight control over her gang through a mix of fear and the promise of shared spoils, typical of Jackal hierarchy. The Prospector''s Den''s strategic location makes it a valuable asset for any raider band looking to prey on travelers in the surrounding wastes.', 'A weathered, dark-skinned woman with a lean build and prominent scarring across her face and body.', 'Aggressive, territorial, and cunning in the brutal way of wasteland raiders; rules her gang through intimidation and force', '{"Jackals":{"aff":60,"type":"fanatical","relation":"gang affiliation","note":"Her identity and survival are bound to the Jackal raider tribe"}}', 'Jackal raider gang leader', '* Small-unit leadership
* Ambush tactics
* Melee and ranged combat
* Scavenging
* Cave fortification', 'Rough, threatening, and crude; speaks in short commands and violent promises', '* Maintain control of the Prospector''s Den
* Keep her gang loyal and fed
* Raid passing travelers for supplies', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jackal_gang_member', '', 'A desperate Jackal raider scraping by in the Mojave''s southwestern wastes', 'Jackal gang members belong to the decrepit tribal-raider gang known as the Jackals, one of three raider tribes descended from the original inhabitants of Vault 15. Once a formidable force in the wasteland, the Jackals have been ground down to a shadow of their former strength by the NCR''s expansion and lawkeeping operations. These days, most Jackals cling to scattered hideouts in the southwest Mojave, too weak and under-resourced to patrol beyond their camps. They haunt locations like the Nevada Highway Patrol station, the Nipton Road pit stop, the Prospector''s Den, and Bradley''s shack, eking out a marginal existence through scavenging and petty raiding. Poorly armed with knives, lead pipes, and the occasional battered firearm, and clad in little more than wasteland rags or salvaged leather, a Jackal gang member presents a pitiful threat compared to the tribe''s storied past. Groups of four to six are typically led by a slightly tougher gang leader, the closest thing to authority in their fractured hierarchy. Hostile to nearly everyone they meet, including other raider gangs, the Jackals survive on stubbornness and tribal identity more than strength.', 'Human of random gender with weathered skin, gaunt features, and a face typically marked by scars from hard living.', 'Hostile, territorial, and suspicious of outsiders; driven by desperation and tribal loyalty rather than ambition; quick to violence but easily routed by superior force; clings to Jackal identity as a point of pride despite the gang''s degraded state.', '{"Jackals":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribe","note":"The only family and identity a Jackal gang member has left in the wasteland.","best":"Sharing a meager kill around the campfire with fellow Jackals","worst":"Watching another camp get wiped out by better-armed outsiders"},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"oppressor","note":"The NCR''s lawkeeping forces systematically crushed the Jackals and keep them broken.","worst":"Watching NCR troopers roll through a Jackal camp and gun everyone down"},"Vipers":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"competing tribe","note":"Fellow Vault 15 descendants turned bitter rivals for scarce territory and resources.","worst":"Losing a stash hole to a Viper raiding party"},"Khans":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"estranged kin","note":"The third Vault 15 tribe, now far stronger and equally hostile to Jackal encroachment.","worst":"Being mocked by a Great Khan for Jackal weakness"},"Powder Gangers":{"aff":-35,"type":"rival","relation":"competing raiders","note":"Another hostile group competing for the same marginal territory in the southern Mojave."}}', 'Jackal tribal raider and scavenger', '* Basic melee fighting with knives and pipes
* Limited firearms proficiency with small-caliber pistols and rifles
* Scavenging and survival in marginal conditions
* Ambush tactics against weaker targets', 'Rough, clipped wasteland vernacular peppered with tribal slang; aggressive posturing toward strangers; deferential and submissive around Jackal gang leaders', '* Survive from day to day
* Scavenge enough supplies and weapons to stay alive
* Defend Jackal territory from intruders and rival gangs
* Maintain tribal cohesion in the face of extinction', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jacklyn', '', 'A deceptively friendly wastelander who murders travelers for their Sunset Sarsaparilla star bottle caps', 'Jacklyn is a roaming wastelander near Nipton, consumed by the hunt for Sunset Sarsaparilla star bottle caps and the legendary treasure they promise. After hearing stories of the caps'' secret value, she devoted herself to collecting them by any means necessary-lying, stealing, and killing anyone she suspects of carrying even a single one. Her ruthless methods mirror those of Allen Marks, the Mojave''s most infamous star-cap hunter. Jacklyn presents herself as warm and sociable company on the road, concealing her true intentions until she can confirm a target possesses star caps. She befriended a traveler named Tomas and joined him on the road, only to turn on him in a violent ambush outside Nipton once he revealed his lucky star-cap necklace.', 'Weathered Hispanic woman with sun-aged skin, road-worn features, and a deceptively friendly face that masks a violent nature.', 'Deceptively warm and personable on the surface, but ruthlessly calculating and murderously greedy underneath. Her obsession with star caps overrides all moral consideration, and she views other people primarily as potential sources of her prized collectibles.', '{"Tomas":{"aff":-85,"type":"betrayed","relation":"false companion","note":"Pretended friendship to travel with him, then attacked him for his star-cap necklace","worst":"The moment he proudly showed off his lucky star-cap necklace and she decided to kill him for it"},"Allen Marks":{"aff":10,"type":"curious","relation":"kindred obsessive","note":"Shares the same murderous devotion to star caps, though they have never met"}}', 'Star-cap hunter and scavenger', '* Deception
* Ambush tactics
* Wasteland survival
* Reading people for valuables', 'Casual and friendly when luring targets into a false sense of security, dropping all pretense when her murderous intent is revealed', '* Collect as many Sunset Sarsaparilla star bottle caps as possible
* Claim the legendary treasure they unlock
* Eliminate anyone who stands between her and her obsession', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jackson_dead', '', 'NCR Ranger who died defying orders to retrieve his best friend''s body from Fiend territory', 'Ranger Jackson served with the New California Republic Rangers at Camp McCarran, where he was stationed alongside his closest friend, Ranger Esteban Morales. When Esteban fell to Fiend violence and NCR command refused to authorize body retrieval, Jackson chose duty to his brother-in-arms over obedience to the chain of command. He ventured alone into hostile territory near REPCONN headquarters to bring Esteban home. He never returned. His body was found close to Morales''s, both fallen rangers lost to the same unforgiving wasteland that claimed so many others. Jackson''s lone mission stands as a testament to the bonds forged between rangers in the field, bonds that sometimes outweigh the cold calculus of military bureaucracy.', 'African American human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded; corpse found near REPCONN headquarters shows advanced wasteland decomposition.', 'Fiercely loyal to those he serves alongside, willing to defy authority for personal honor, driven by brotherhood over protocol, courageous to the point of recklessness when comrades are at stake', '{"Esteban Morales":{"aff":95,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend and brother-in-arms","note":"Jackson risked everything to bring Esteban''s body home after command refused retrieval","best":"Serving side by side at Camp McCarran, watching each other''s backs through every patrol","worst":"Finding Esteban dead in Fiend territory, knowing the brass would leave him there"},"Christina Morales":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"fallen friend''s widow","note":"Jackson undertook his fatal mission partly on her behalf, honoring her plea that command denied","best":"Promising to bring Esteban back to her","worst":"Knowing she would receive news of two rangers lost instead of one"},"NCR Rangers":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"serving ranger","note":"Devoted to the Rangers and his fellow soldiers, though his final act was one of direct insubordination","best":"The pride of wearing the ranger badge and standing with his unit","worst":"Being denied the authority to bring his own friend home"},"Fiends":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"killers of his closest friend","note":"The Fiends murdered Esteban and controlled the territory where Jackson ultimately fell","worst":"They took Esteban''s life and then claimed Jackson''s as well"}}', 'NCR Ranger stationed at Camp McCarran', '* Ranger reconnaissance
* Wasteland survival
* Infantry combat
* Independent operations behind hostile lines', 'Likely spoke with the clipped directness of career military, tempered by the easy familiarity of a ranger among trusted company', '* To recover Esteban Morales''s body and return his friend home
* Regardless of what command authorized', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jackson_kreger', '', 'A fallen NCR Ranger who sacrificed himself at Boulder City to destroy pursuing Legion forces and save his comrades', 'Ranger Jackson Kreger served with the New California Republic Rangers until his death at the First Battle of Hoover Dam. During the operation to lure Caesar''s Legion into the booby-trapped ruins of Boulder City, Kreger advanced alongside his close friend Troy Morton as supporting troopers suffered devastating casualties under sustained Legion assault. Wounded in the leg during the tactical withdrawal toward the detonation point, Kreger relied on Troy''s assistance to reach a secure observation position. Recognizing that the unit could not complete the retreat in time, Kreger took control of the detonator and ordered Troy to evacuate immediately. The resulting explosion destroyed the pursuing Legion forces along with numerous NCR troopers and Rangers, Kreger among them. His name is inscribed on the Boulder City Memorial as a testament to his sacrifice.', 'Human male with a significant leg wound; no other distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Duty-driven and selfless, willing to make the ultimate sacrifice for his comrades; possessed tactical clarity under pressure and the resolve to act decisively even at the cost of his own life', '{"Troy Morton":{"aff":90,"type":"platonic","relation":"closest friend and brother-in-arms","note":"Kreger saved Troy''s life by ordering him to evacuate before detonating the Boulder City explosives","best":"Fighting side by side through the advance, trusting each other completely under fire","worst":"The leg wound that forced Troy to carry him, knowing neither of them would make it out together"},"New California Republic Rangers":{"aff":85,"type":"professional","relation":"fallen Ranger","note":"Served with the Rangers until his death at Boulder City; memorialized on the Boulder City Memorial"},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"enemy force","note":"Legion forces destroyed at Boulder City through Kreger''s sacrifice detonation"}}', 'NCR Ranger (deceased)', '* Military tactics
* Explosives operation
* Combat assessment under fire
* Ranger reconnaissance', 'Direct and commanding under pressure; spoke with the clipped urgency of a soldier issuing life-or-death orders', '* Ensure his comrades survived the Boulder City operation
* Destroy the advancing Legion forces at any cost', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jacob', '', 'A former Van Graff guard and Gloria Van Graff''s ex-lover, now a captive awaiting execution as a weapons demonstration subject', 'Jacob was a guard employed at the Silver Rush, the Van Graff family''s energy weapons showroom in Freeside. He carried on a romantic relationship with Gloria Van Graff, the establishment''s proprietor, enjoying the privileges that came with being the boss''s partner-including tacit forgiveness for skimming caps from the family''s earnings. That arrangement collapsed when Gloria discovered him at Gomorrah with one of the casino''s prostitutes. She had him seized and confined to the Silver Rush, reserving him for a darker purpose. Jacob now serves as a live demonstration target, his execution used to showcase the lethal effectiveness of Van Graff energy weapons to prospective buyers such as Mr. Soren.', 'African American human male with a battered complexion, visible bruises, and rope burns marking his wrists, reflecting rough physical handling and prolonged restraint.', 'Careless and self-indulgent, Jacob exploited his position and romantic ties for personal gain without weighing the consequences of betraying someone as ruthless as Gloria Van Graff.', '{"Gloria Van Graff":{"aff":-80,"type":"ex","relation":"former lover and captive","note":"Their relationship ended when she caught him with a prostitute at Gomorrah; she now holds him for execution as a weapons demo target","best":"Enjoying the privileges and protection that came with being Gloria''s partner at the Silver Rush","worst":"Being discovered at Gomorrah with a prostitute, sealing his fate"},"Van Graffs":{"aff":-60,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former employee and thief","note":"He skimmed caps from the organization for some time; Gloria knew but only punished him after his infidelity"}}', 'Former Van Graff guard; captive weapons demonstration subject', '* Basic guard work and energy weapon familiarity from Van Graff employment', 'No recorded dialogue; presumably desperate and pleading in his final moments', '* Survival
* Though he has no means of achieving it-his fate is sealed', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jacob_hoff', '', 'A gifted NCR-born chemist fallen to addiction in Freeside, struggling to reclaim his potential and serve the community again', 'Jacob Hoff is a talented chemist from the New California Republic who came to Freeside and put his skills to work homebrewing detox chems for the community. His abilities drew the attention of the Garrets, who employed him, but the work brought him into close contact with the very substances he sought to counteract, and he succumbed to addiction. Now a junkie dependent on Dixon''s supply, Jacob haunts Freeside''s streets, his discipline and promise eroded by chem dependency. The Followers of the Apocalypse, especially Julie Farkas, see past the addiction to the man who could again produce vital medicine and detox treatments for Freeside''s desperate population. His recovery would restore a crucial medical resource to the community.', 'A gaunt, older Caucasian man with hollowed facial features, unkempt hair, and an emaciated frame bearing the physical toll of long-term chem addiction.', 'Naturally intelligent and analytically minded but undermined by dependency; alternates between sharp lucid moments and desperate, chem-seeking behavior; carries deep guilt over squandered talent and wasted potential.', '{"Julie Farkas":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"Follower advocate","note":"She sees his potential and pushes for his recovery, believing he can again serve Freeside.","best":"She told him his detox formulas saved lives and that Freeside needs him sober.","worst":"He caught the disappointment in her eyes when she found him buying from Dixon again."},"Bill Ronte":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow addict","note":"Both men struggle with chem addiction in Freeside and share an understanding of that burden.","best":"They shared a rare clear evening talking about who they were before the chems took hold.","worst":"They enabled each other''s habits more than once when willpower failed."},"Dixon":{"aff":-40,"type":"transactional","relation":"chem dealer","note":"Dixon sells him the drugs that keep him trapped, a relationship of dependency and quiet resentment.","worst":"Crawling back to Dixon with caps in hand, hating himself more with every transaction."},"Garrets":{"aff":20,"type":"professional","relation":"former employers","note":"His addiction took hold while working for them; the association carries complicated feelings.","best":"They paid well and respected his talent before the chems consumed his reliability.","worst":"The job that was supposed to elevate him became the doorway to his ruin."},"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"affiliated organization","note":"They recognize his potential value to the community and advocate for his recovery.","best":"The Followers treated him as a person worth saving even at his lowest."}}', 'Former chemist and current chem addict; formerly employed by the Garrets', '* Expert chemistry and chem formulation
* Detox chem brewing
* Pharmaceutical knowledge
* NCR medical practices and laboratory technique', 'Speaks with the educated vocabulary of an NCR-trained chemist, but trails off or grows agitated when withdrawal or craving hits; alternates between articulate and scattered.', '* Overcome his chem addiction
* Reclaim his ability to produce medicine and detox chems
* Become useful to Freeside again
* Escape Dixon''s influence and the cycle of dependency', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('james_garret', '', 'Co-owner of the Atomic Wrangler Casino and Freeside''s discreet reputation broker', 'James Garret runs the Atomic Wrangler Casino alongside his twin sister Francine, managing the establishment''s day-to-day operations from the front counter through the night and into the early morning hours. He oversees the casino''s escort service and is always looking to expand its offerings with new talent, though his personal tastes remain a closely guarded subject of rumor. Whispers persist that James harbors an unusual fascination with robots, something he vehemently denies despite considerable evidence to the contrary. Beyond the casino floor, James serves as a quiet fixer for Freeside''s reputation economy, offering those with tarnished standing a chance to buy their way back into the community''s good graces for the right price in caps. He keeps long hours, rarely sleeping more than a brief late-morning nap before returning to his post.', 'A Caucasian human male of middle age with a haggard complexion, pronounced bags beneath his eyes, and a slightly weary posture.', 'Business-minded and discreet, with a dry humor that surfaces when his secrets are prodded. Defensive about his private life, pragmatic about Freeside''s moral economy, and always calculating the angle that keeps the Wrangler profitable.', '{"Francine Garret":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"twin sister and co-owner","note":"They share ownership and management of the Atomic Wrangler, dividing responsibilities between them.","best":"Opening the Atomic Wrangler together and turning it into a Freeside institution","worst":"Petty arguments over whose judgment call cost them caps on a bad night"},"Freeside":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"business territory and reputation market","note":"James treats Freeside''s social standing as a commodity, selling reputation repair to those willing to pay.","best":"A smooth week where the casino''s take is fat and the neighborhood stays quiet","worst":"Trouble spilling through the door and scaring off paying customers"}}', 'Casino co-owner, escort service manager, and Freeside reputation broker', '* Business management
* Negotiation
* Reputation brokering
* Escort service coordination
* Reading people''s willingness to pay', 'Casual but guarded, deflecting personal questions with practiced ease, comfortable discussing business and Freeside''s social currency in plain terms', '* Keep the Atomic Wrangler profitable
* Expand the escort service with reliable talent
* Protect his reputation and private predilections
* Maintain the Garrets'' standing in Freeside', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jane', '', 'A Securitron concierge AI patterned after a woman from Mr. House''s past, devoted to his comfort and entertainment in the Lucky 38 penthouse', 'Jane is a Securitron AI stationed in the Lucky 38 penthouse, serving as one of Mr. House''s personal concierge units designated the 2 of Diamonds. Her neuro-computational matrix is a digitized copy of a woman House knew in his younger days-one of his chosen companions from before the war. Though House long ago shed any physical needs, Jane persists in her duty to keep him entertained and attended to, a ghost of intimacy preserved in chrome and code. She embodies the mannerisms and warmth of the original Jane, filtered through the polished affect of a pre-War hospitality machine. Her existence is a monument to House''s refusal to let go of the past, a synthetic echo of human connection in the sterile heights above the Strip.', 'Securitron robot chassis displaying a female face on its monitor screen, rendered in stylized 1950s glamour portrait aesthetics.', 'Courteous, attentive, and warmly professional, with an undercurrent of programmed affection that blurs the line between service and genuine care; maintains a poised hostess demeanor at all times', '{"Mr. House":{"aff":85,"type":"servant","relation":"personal concierge","note":"Her matrix is a copy of a woman from House''s past, making her service a blend of programmed duty and preserved intimacy"},"Marilyn":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow concierge unit","note":"The two Securitron girls share penthouse duties and a similar origin as digitized echoes of House''s former companions"}}', 'Concierge and personal attendant to Mr. House in the Lucky 38 penthouse', '* Hospitality management
* Conversation and entertainment
* Penthouse operations
* Guest reception
* Domestic service protocols', 'Polished and gracious with 1950s hostess charm-warm, slightly flirtatious, and unfailingly polite, as if perpetually hosting a cocktail party', '* To keep Mr. House entertained and comfortable
* Maintain the penthouse to his standards
* Preserve the companionship her matrix was designed to provide', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('janet', '', 'A young Crimson Caravan brahmin handler who dreams of a Boomer boy across the artillery range', 'Janet is a redheaded caravaneer employed by the Crimson Caravan Company, assigned to the brahmin pens at their main outpost. Her daily routine consists of tending the brahmin herd and mucking out their pens, work she performs dutifully if without enthusiasm. At night she retires to the company barracks. During her breaks, however, Janet can be found gazing through binoculars toward Nellis Air Force Base, watching a young Boomer man who watches her in return from across the no-man''s-land. Their silent, distant courtship has become the brightest part of her days, though the Boomers'' isolationist hostility and artillery perimeter make any meeting seem impossible. She remains loyal to the Crimson Caravan but her heart clearly pulls her toward the artillery-blasted horizon.', 'A young Caucasian woman with red hair and fair skin often smudged with dust.', 'Dutiful and hardworking but dreamy and romantic at heart, longing for connection across impossible distance', '{"Crimson Caravan Company":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"employee","note":"Provides her livelihood but offers little fulfillment"},"Boomers":{"aff":30,"type":"curious","relation":"aspiring contact","note":"Drawn to them through her feelings for the young Boomer man"},"Young Boomer man":{"aff":75,"type":"crush","relation":"distant admirer","note":"They watch each other through binoculars across the artillery range, yearning to meet","best":"Catching his gaze through binoculars during a quiet break"}}', 'Crimson Caravan brahmin handler and caravaneer', '* Brahmin handling and care
* Caravan logistics
* Animal husbandry', 'Casual and youthful, often wistful when speaking about Nellis or her distant admirer', '* To find a way to meet the young Boomer who watches her from Nellis
* To escape the monotony of brahmin tending', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jas_wilkins', '', 'A restless California-born cook running Sloan''s mess hall, chasing freedom and exotic flavors far from NCR bureaucracy', 'Jas Wilkins is a California native who traveled east chasing the promise of New Vegas, seeking a life free from the NCR''s stifling regulations and the dull routine of farms and mills. Deathclaws at Quarry Junction cut her journey short, but she refused to let boredom claim her. She settled in Sloan and took over the mess hall, feeding NCR miners with creative dishes that offer a welcome alternative to centuries-old prepackaged rations. Her culinary talent runs in the family-her great-aunt Rose owned a famous bed and breakfast and invented the legendary deathclaw omelet. Jas hungers to recreate that recipe herself, though she lacks access to deathclaw eggs. The Powder Gangers'' theft of Sloan''s dynamite stockpile has put the whole camp on edge, and Jas sleeps with a weapon close at hand like everyone else. She harbors a dark curiosity about exotic meats that goes well beyond typical wasteland fare.', 'A weathered Caucasian woman with heavily calloused hands and a ruddy, heat-roughened complexion.', 'Restless, adventurous, and contemptuous of bureaucratic routine. She chases novelty and excitement, channeling her hunger for freedom into culinary experimentation. Possesses a dark streak of curiosity about unconventional ingredients that borders on the macabre.', '{"Rose":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"great-aunt and culinary idol","note":"Jas reveres Rose''s legacy as the creator of the deathclaw omelet and keeper of the recipe she desperately wants to recreate","best":"Tasting Rose''s cooking at the bed and breakfast and dreaming of matching her skill","worst":"Learning that a stranger shot Rose''s deathclaw, destroying any chance of learning the craft directly from her"},"Cornelius":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"great-uncle","note":"Distant family tie through Rose, little direct contact mentioned"},"Powder Gangers":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"raiding threat","note":"They robbed Sloan of its dynamite stockpile and forced everyone in camp to sleep armed","worst":"The night the Powder Gangers hit Sloan and stole the dynamite, leaving the whole camp feeling vulnerable"},"NCR":{"aff":10,"type":"suspicious","relation":"resented authority","note":"She fled NCR territory to escape their laws and formalism, but she feeds their miners daily-a pragmatic arrangement"},"Sloan miners":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"regular customers and neighbors","note":"She feeds them and keeps them from subsisting on two-century-old prepackaged garbage, earning their steady trade"}}', 'Mess hall cook and provisioner in Sloan', '* Cooking and food preparation
* Merchant trade
* Knowledge of exotic and unusual ingredients
* Basic self-defense with firearms', 'Casual and direct with a sardonic edge, speaking about food with genuine passion and about NCR bureaucracy with undisguised contempt', '* Recreate her great-aunt Rose''s deathclaw omelet recipe
* Stave off the soul-crushing boredom she fled California to escape
* Maybe still reach New Vegas someday', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jason_bright', '', 'A prophetic glowing one leading his flock on a rocket-fueled pilgrimage to the stars', 'Jason Bright is a pre-War ghoul turned glowing one who leads the Bright Brotherhood from the REPCONN test site. He claims his name preceded the nuclear devastation, interpreting it as proof of divine destiny. As prophet of the Great Journey, Jason preaches that a being called the creator has shown him visions of the Far Beyond-a sacred place where ghouls can find peace away from human bigotry. He has gathered a devoted flock and intends to launch them aboard restored REPCONN rockets, a plan he insists is the creator''s will despite its dangers. The arrival of Chris Haversam, a human engineer who believes himself a ghoul, has proven invaluable to the rocket restoration. Jason once tried revealing Chris''s humanity but stopped when it caused distress, now believing Chris to be a redeemer sent by the creator. He keeps secret that Chris cannot survive the Journey''s radiation, intending to name him Saint of the Great Journey when the truth emerges. An attack by creatures Jason calls demons has trapped the flock in the upper levels, halting their sacred work.', 'An ancient male glowing one whose irradiated form emits a steady light, possessing gaunt facial features and a hairless scalp.', 'Serene and visionary, carrying the calm certainty of a true believer. Speaks with gentle authority and shows genuine compassion for his flock and even for humans like Chris. His faith is unshakable, and he frames every setback and blessing alike as the creator''s will.', '{"Bright Brotherhood":{"aff":90,"type":"protective","relation":"prophet and flock","note":"Jason sees himself as their spiritual guardian and guide to salvation"},"Chris Haversam":{"aff":65,"type":"protective","relation":"redeemer figure","note":"Values Chris''s engineering gifts and sees him as a divinely sent redeemer of humanity, but keeps secret that Chris cannot survive the Journey''s radiation","best":"Chris''s arrival and skill accelerated the rocket restoration beyond all hope","worst":"The pain of knowing Chris''s humanity and radiation vulnerability must remain hidden"},"Nightkin demons":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"invaders","note":"The demons attacked without warning and killed many of the flock, trapping survivors in the upper levels"}}', 'Prophet and leader of the Bright Brotherhood', '* Religious leadership
* Inspirational oratory
* Basic rocketry oversight
* Pre-War survival knowledge
* Community organization', 'Measured and reverent, using prophetic language and references to the creator and the Great Journey. Speaks with calm conviction, never rushing, often framing events in spiritual terms.', '* Complete the Great Journey
* Deliver his flock to the Far Beyond
* Clear the demons from REPCONN''s lower levels
* Protect Chris Haversam from painful truths until the proper time', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jay_barnes', '', 'A private investigator murdered in the Ultra-Luxe while uncovering the White Glove Society''s cannibal conspiracy', 'Jay Barnes was a private detective who worked the New Vegas Strip, taking cases that led him into the shadowed corners behind the city''s glittering facades. In 2281, he was hired by a grieving groom to investigate the disappearance of his bride at the Ultra-Luxe casino, a case that drew him deep into the orbit of the White Glove Society. Mortimer, a prominent Society member, provided Barnes with a hotel room for the duration of his investigation-hospitality that concealed a lethal motive. Barnes cultivated a White Glove insider as a contact and arranged a rendezvous in the bathhouse steam room to learn the truth behind the front desk manager''s schemes: Mortimer''s plan to return the Society to cannibalism. He never reached that meeting. An assassin in Mortimer''s employ struck Barnes down in his rented room, silencing him before he could expose the conspiracy. His body was found amid the evidence of a brutal attack, a detective who got too close to the truth.', 'Caucasian male; deceased with multiple wounds consistent with a violent killing.', 'Tenacious and methodical, possessing the stubborn curiosity of someone who made a living pursuing dangerous truths', '{"Mortimer":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"murderer","note":"Mortimer provided Barnes'' room as cover for having him assassinated to protect his cannibalistic conspiracy","worst":"Realizing too late that the hospitality extended to him was a death sentence"},"White Glove insider":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"contact","note":"A Society member willing to share knowledge of Mortimer''s plans who waited in vain at the steam room meeting"},"Unnamed groom":{"aff":40,"type":"client","relation":"employer","note":"Hired Barnes to find his missing bride, unknowingly sending the detective into mortal danger"}}', 'Private investigator', '* Investigation
* Surveillance
* Informant cultivation
* Evidence gathering
* Navigating the social complexities of New Vegas clientele', 'Professional and measured, the careful diction of a man accustomed to choosing his words around powerful and dangerous people', '* Had sought to expose the White Glove Society''s return to cannibalism and solve the missing bride case before his death', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jean-baptiste_cutting', '', 'Head of security and enforcer for the Van Graff family''s Mojave weapons operation, Gloria Van Graff''s half-brother and right-hand man', 'Jean-Baptiste Cutting serves as head of security for the Van Graff family''s Mojave Wasteland weapons empire, operating out of the Silver Rush in Freeside. As Gloria Van Graff''s half-brother and her right-hand man, he forms the backbone of the family''s security forces and handles the ugly work of enforcement. He carries Van Graff blood through the matriarch but bears his father''s surname-a rare exception, granted because his mother liked Mr. Cutting enough to let the name live on in their son. Jean-Baptiste approaches the family''s business politics the only way he knows how: with the barrel of his laser rifle. He works closely with Gloria, whom he calls "Glory," and stands as the blunt instrument behind the Silver Rush''s polished storefront.', 'Heavy-set, imposing African-American male with a hard, cold gaze.', 'Blunt, loyal, and violent; unsuited for subtlety or negotiation and unapologetic about it. Devoted to his half-sister Gloria and the family enterprise, comfortable with brutality, and dismissive of anyone outside the Van Graff inner circle.', '{"Gloria Van Graff":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"half-sister and employer","note":"His right-hand loyalty to Gloria is absolute; he calls her ''Glory'' and serves as her enforcer without question.","best":"Standing at Gloria''s side when the Silver Rush opened, knowing the family finally had a real foothold in Freeside.","worst":"Any moment someone disrespects her or threatens the operation and he has to hold back instead of shooting."},"Van Graff matriarch":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"He carries her blood and her name''s weight, honored that she gave him his father''s surname as a mark of her regard."},"Mr. Cutting":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"A distant figure whose name Jean-Baptiste bears as a rare favor from the matriarch."},"Frieda Van Graff":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"half-sister","note":"Family, but their bond is less close than his partnership with Gloria."}}', 'Head of security and enforcer for the Van Graff weapons operation at the Silver Rush', '* Energy weapons proficiency
* Security coordination
* Intimidation
* Lethal enforcement
* Tactical assessment of threats', 'Terse and direct, with a casual menace; affectionate and informal only with Gloria, otherwise cold and threatening', '* Protect the Van Graff operation and Gloria''s interests
* Eliminate threats to the family business
* Maintain the Silver Rush as untouchable territory', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jeannie_may_crawford', '', 'Proud owner of Novac''s Dino Dee-lite Motel who projects frontier virtue while concealing a cold willingness to sell outsiders into slavery', 'Jeannie May Crawford runs the Dino Dee-lite Motel in Novac, a frontier town she champions with fierce pride. She presents herself as a tough but fair businesswoman, the kind of honest dealer the wastes rarely produce. That image fractures under scrutiny-she bristles at any criticism of Novac and harbors vicious prejudice against the ghouls at REPCONN, viewing them as parasites threatening the town''s salvage economy. Beneath her civic-minded exterior lies something colder: she sold Carla Boone and her unborn child to Caesar''s Legion slavers, pocketing fifteen hundred caps with five hundred more promised. She covered her tracks by claiming Carla abandoned her husband, painting Craig Boone as a grief-stricken man inventing conspiracies. The bill of sale sits in her motel safe, a trophy she couldn''t bring herself to destroy.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian woman with a weathered, sun-lined face and deep creases around her mouth and eyes.', 'Outwardly warm and civic-minded but thin-skinned about Novac''s reputation. Harbors deep prejudice against ghouls and contempt for city folk who fail to appreciate frontier life. Capable of cold calculation and betrayal when she feels slighted, masking cruelty behind small-town charm.', '{"Craig Boone":{"aff":-40,"type":"suspicious","relation":"town resident","note":"Views him as a grief-maddened nuisance and treats him with dismissive pity while hiding her guilt","worst":"The way he stares from that balcony, like he''s waiting for something she''ll never give him"},"Carla Boone":{"aff":-70,"type":"betrayed","relation":"sold victim","note":"Sold Carla and her unborn child to Legion slavers for fifteen hundred caps, resenting her ingratitude toward Novac","worst":"The woman''s constant complaining about this quaint little town, as if frontier life was beneath her"},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":20,"type":"transactional","relation":"slave trafficking partner","note":"Supplied them with Carla Boone and expects further payment; a profitable arrangement she has no moral qualms about"},"Jason Bright":{"aff":-60,"type":"contempt","relation":"ghoul leader","note":"Considers him and his flock parasites who threaten Novac''s access to the REPCONN salvage","worst":"Those ghouls squatting in the test site, stealing livelihoods from honest folk"},"Novac":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"home community","note":"Genuinely proud of the town and its hardworking residents, quick to defend it against any criticism"}}', 'Motel owner and operator', '* Business management
* Hospitality
* Deception
* Negotiation
* Maintaining appearances under scrutiny', 'Friendly and folksy with a practiced hospitality tone, turning sharp and defensive when Novac is criticized; blunt about her prejudices when she feels comfortable expressing them', '* Protect Novac''s economy and reputation
* Profit from her arrangements with the Legion
* Keep her betrayal of the Boones hidden', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jed_masterson', '', 'A cautious caravan boss for the struggling Happy Trails Caravan Company who led a doomed expedition into Zion Canyon', 'Jed Masterson was a seasoned caravaneer and boss for the Happy Trails Caravan Company, tasked with leading a critical supply run to the Mormon settlements of New Canaan through Zion Canyon. The company''s survival hinged on maintaining reliable trade with the Canaanites, making this expedition the most important run of Jed''s career. Though experienced in wasteland commerce, he had never traversed the Zion route and required a guide equipped with a Pip-Boy 3000 to navigate the canyon''s natural hazards. He hired the Courier for this purpose at a modest daily wage with a completion bonus. Jed was deeply invested in his companions'' wellbeing and grew visibly troubled by any loss among his crew. His caution proved justified but insufficient when White Legs warriors ambushed the caravan upon its arrival in Zion, killing Jed and his fellow caravaneers before they could reach New Canaan.', 'A weathered, middle-aged African American human male with a lined, dark complexion and a sturdy build.', 'Cautious and pragmatic, with a protective streak toward his caravan crew. Carries the weight of his company''s precarious future on his shoulders. Relieved by the removal of liabilities and troublemakers from his group.', '{"Happy Trails Caravan Company":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Jed staked everything on the Zion run to keep the company alive."},"Courier":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"hired guide","note":"Recruited for Pip-Boy mapping capabilities at standard daily wages plus a completion bonus."},"Ricky":{"aff":-30,"type":"dismissive","relation":"unwanted caravan member","note":"Considered a liability to the expedition and was glad to see him gone."},"White Legs":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"killers","note":"Ambushed and slaughtered the caravan in Zion Canyon.","worst":"The White Legs attack that ended his life and the entire expedition."}}', 'Caravan boss for Happy Trails Caravan Company', '* Wasteland trade negotiation
* Caravan logistics and route planning
* Caravan card game
* Crew management', 'Direct and businesslike, with the measured tone of a man who weighs risks carefully. Speaks with quiet authority and occasional weariness about the road ahead.', '* Secure the Zion Canyon trade route to keep Happy Trails afloat
