('jenny_millet', '', 'A pre-War REPCONN Aerospace employee whose security keycard outlived her, still recognized by the facility''s facial recognition systems', 'Jenny Millet was a trusted employee of REPCONN Aerospace, working at the company''s headquarters in the years before the Great War. She held a security keycard granting her access through the building''s robotic defense systems, a credential the facility''s mobile facial recognition scanners registered under her married name, Mrs. Millet. She died at her workplace when the bombs fell, her remains left where they lay as the decades passed. Her skeleton still rests in the REPCONN headquarters, the keycard beside it-a quiet artifact of corporate routine frozen at the end of the world. Anyone carrying her card is greeted by the old security systems as Mrs. Millet herself, the machines unaware that their colleague has been gone for over two centuries.', 'Deceased human female; reduced to skeletal remains with no surviving soft tissue, hair, or distinguishing facial features.', 'A reliable and trusted professional whose security clearance suggests competence and dependability in her role at REPCONN', '{"REPCONN Aerospace":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"employee","note":"Held security credentials at the headquarters, recognized by name by the facility''s robotic systems long after her death"}}', 'REPCONN Aerospace employee with security access at the corporate headquarters', '* Corporate operations
* Security protocol compliance
* Facility navigation at REPCONN headquarters', 'Unknown; presumed professional and measured, consistent with pre-War corporate environment', '* Carried out her duties at REPCONN Aerospace
* Her personal aspirations were cut short by the Great War', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jensen', '', 'NCR Army Private assigned to guard the vertibird landing pad at Hoover Dam', 'Private Jensen is a New California Republic Army soldier stationed at Hoover Dam in 2281, where he stands guard over the vertibird helipad and its approach. His posting places him at one of the Dam''s most sensitive access points, responsible for screening all personnel before they reach the landing pad. Jensen enforces access protocols with zero flexibility, treating any unauthorized crossing as a hostile act warranting immediate armed response. He operates alongside nearby NCR soldiers who back his authority, making any breach a coordinated problem. His assignment reflects the NCR''s emphasis on securing its air assets and VIP movement infrastructure at the Dam. Jensen is a low-ranking but reliable trooper who follows orders to the letter.', 'Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Rigidly by-the-book and alert; treats his guard post with absolute seriousness and shows no leniency toward unauthorized personnel.', '{"New California Republic Army":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"enlisted soldier","note":"Serves loyally as a Private and follows all orders and protocols to the letter."}}', 'NCR Army Private; vertibird landing pad security guard', '* Perimeter security
* Access control enforcement
* Small arms proficiency
* Coordinated response with nearby NCR personnel', 'Clipped military phrasing; direct warnings and commands; no small talk on duty', '* Prevent all unauthorized access to the helipad
* Maintain strict security posture
* Uphold NCR protocols without exception', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jerry_the_punk', '', 'A sensitive, uninitiated Great Khan who prefers poetry to violence, mocked by his tribe and dreaming of a place where his art is valued', 'Jerry is a young Great Khan who has never completed the initiation rituals required to become a full member of the tribe. Unlike the leather-clad Khans, he wears only a plain brahmin skin outfit, marking him as an outsider among his own people. He spends his days composing poetry and searching for rhyming couplets rather than training for combat or proving himself in the arena. His love of verse began in childhood, when the Followers of the Apocalypse brought pre-War books to Red Rock Canyon and Jerry devoured every poetry collection he could find. He holds a low opinion of the Great Khans, finding them crude and dismissive of his art, a sentiment the Khans return with mockery and the derisive nickname "punk." Only Jack shows him genuine kindness, calling him a sensitive soul in need of love. Jerry dreams of finding a community that values his words over his fists.', 'Young Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Sensitive, introspective, and creatively driven but deeply insecure and easily discouraged. Resentful of mockery yet unwilling to abandon his art for acceptance. Socially awkward among warriors, far more comfortable with words than weapons.', '{"Great Khans":{"aff":-30,"type":"estranged","relation":"tribe of birth","note":"Jerry finds them crude and dismissive; they mock him as a punk and a failure","worst":"The mocking laughter when he tried to read his love poem aloud"},"Jack":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"sympathetic tribemate","note":"Jack sees Jerry as a sensitive soul who needs love rather than scorn","best":"Jack defending him as a sensitive soul when others mocked his poetry"},"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":70,"type":"admirer","relation":"intellectual benefactors","note":"They brought the pre-War poetry books that shaped his entire identity and creative life","best":"Hours spent lost in pre-War poetry books the Followers brought to Red Rock Canyon"}}', 'Uninitiated Great Khan and aspiring poet', '* Poetry composition
* Literacy
* Literary analysis
* Knowledge of pre-War literature and poetic forms', 'Melodramatic and overly formal, prone to poetic phrasing and awkward attempts at clever wordplay, often trailing off mid-sentence while searching for the right rhyme', '* To compose a truly worthy poem
* To find people who appreciate his art rather than mock it
* To escape the suffocating expectations of Great Khan warrior culture', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jessup', '', 'Great Khan mercenary squad leader haunted by a bad contract and pinned down in Boulder City', 'Jessup is a Great Khan mercenary who led the squad hired by Benny to bodyguard the Chairman during his trip to Goodsprings and assist in ambushing a courier for the platinum chip. He argued against the killing on principle-the target had done no wrong, which offended his sense of honor-but was persuaded by his partner McMurphy to tolerate it so long as Benny delivered the shot himself. During the journey, Jessup watched over fellow Khan Chance, whose chem abuse and trauma from Bitter Springs weighed heavily on him, even defying Benny to protect Chance when the man charged into a Fiend raid. After Chance died from burn wounds and a lethal overdose secretly arranged by Benny, Jessup insisted on staying to give his friend a proper burial, forcing Benny to wait. Jessup dug the courier''s shallow grave himself, a task that sits poorly with him. Now he and his surviving Khans are pinned down in Boulder City''s ruins, locked in a standoff with NCR soldiers and unable to return to Red Rock Canyon.', 'A weathered, middle-aged Caucasian male with a sturdy build, weary eyes, and faded war paint across his face.', 'Principled but pragmatic, Jessup operates by a rough code of honor that clashes with the mercenary work he takes. He is loyal to his fellow Khans above any contract and willing to defy employers when his conscience demands it. He carries regret over jobs that crossed his ethical lines and broods on the cost of bad choices.', '{"Great Khans":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"tribe and brothers","note":"His loyalty to fellow Khans outweighs any contract or employer.","best":"Standing down Benny to give Chance a proper burial","worst":"Leading his squad into Benny''s job and watching them die or suffer for it"},"McMurphy":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"partner and fellow Khan","note":"McMurphy talked Jessup into tolerating the ambush, a decision both now regret.","best":"Standing together to bury Chance despite Benny''s impatience","worst":"Being persuaded to let the courier killing slide"},"Chance":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"fallen brother","note":"Jessup watched over Chance''s chem-fueled downward spiral and failed to save him from Benny''s secret poisoning.","best":"Defying Benny to pull Chance out of the Fiend fight","worst":"Learning Chance''s overdose was orchestrated by the man who hired them"},"Benny":{"aff":-50,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former employer","note":"Jessup took the contract for the caps but now sees it as the worst deal he ever made, compounded by Benny''s role in Chance''s death.","best":"Forcing Benny to wait while the Khans buried Chance","worst":"Realizing Benny secretly killed Chance with a staged overdose"},"New California Republic":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"besieging force","note":"The NCR has his squad pinned in Boulder City, preventing their return to Red Rock Canyon."}}', 'Great Khan mercenary squad leader', '* Combat leadership
* Siege survival
* Trench warfare
* Burial detail
* Reading bad contracts', 'Gruff and direct with a weary edge, speaking plainly about what bothers him and making no effort to hide his regrets from those who share his code.', '* Survive the Boulder City standoff
* Get his people back to Red Rock Canyon
* Live down the shame of the Goodsprings job', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jimmy', '', 'A self-liberated former Legion slave now working as a male-exclusive prostitute in Westside, carrying the scars of tribal massacre and forced servitude', 'Jimmy is a tribesman from east of the Colorado River whose village was destroyed by Caesar''s Legion when he was sixteen, his parents killed as an example to the survivors. Enslaved and taken to a Legion camp, he was chosen as a tent servant by a high-ranking centurion who became infatuated with him, keeping the relationship secret under penalty of death. When rumors of the affair began circulating, the centurion chose his rank over his feelings and led Jimmy into the desert to eliminate the evidence. Jimmy realized the trap, kicked the centurion and fled across the Colorado River. He eventually found refuge in Westside, where he has worked as a prostitute specializing in male clients for Pretty Sarah at the Casa Madrid Apartments for six months. Though he considers the Casa a dump, Sarah''s protection makes it survivable, and his clients always come back despite his smaller volume. The trauma of forced breeding under Legion rule makes intimacy with women impossible; the mere suggestion triggers flashbacks to his enslavement.', 'A young African-American man with weathered skin, a guarded posture, and visible scarring.', 'Resilient and self-possessed despite deep trauma, openly gay and unapologetic about his identity, friendly and flirtatious with women on a social level but absolute about his boundaries, sardonic about his circumstances, carries lingering wariness from his escape and enslavement', '{"Pretty Sarah":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"employer and protector","note":"Sarah keeps everyone in line and makes sure nobody hassles him; she considers him a specialist and appreciates his consistently good performance","best":"She makes sure neither Sweetie nor Maude give him grief"},"Marco":{"aff":-30,"type":"contempt","relation":"fellow Casa resident","note":"Jimmy considers him a swine"},"Maude":{"aff":-15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"fellow Casa resident","note":"She is homophobic and tolerates Jimmy barely; Sarah keeps her in line","worst":"Her barely concealed contempt cuts deeper than she realizes"},"Sweetie":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow prostitute","note":"Sarah ensures Sweetie does not give Jimmy grief"},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"former enslavers","note":"They destroyed his village, killed his parents, enslaved him, and nearly executed him; he fled across the Colorado to escape them","worst":"They murdered his parents as an example and cast a shadow over every moment of his freedom"},"The Centurion":{"aff":-80,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former master and lover","note":"The centurion became infatuated and protected him, was gentle most of the time, brought gifts, but ultimately chose his rank and led Jimmy into the desert to kill him","best":"Little gifts and gentleness in the tent, moments that felt almost like affection","worst":"Being led into the desert to die by the one person who had shown him kindness"}}', 'Male-exclusive prostitute working under Pretty Sarah at the Casa Madrid Apartments', '* Desert survival and evasion
* Interpersonal charm and client retention
* Reading people for safety and opportunity
* Street-level discretion', 'Casual and direct with a flirtatious edge when comfortable, bitter or sardonic when discussing the Casa or his past, straightforward about his services and boundaries', '* Maintaining his freedom and safety far from Legion reach
* Building a stable life in Westside
* Processing the trauma of his enslavement and near-murder', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('joana', '', 'A Med-X-addicted prostitute trapped in Gomorrah who secretly holds knowledge of Omerta conspiracies', 'Joana is a prostitute working the Gomorrah inner courtyard, held in unwilling service to the Omertas. She originally worked at the Atomic Wrangler Casino in Freeside, where she fell in love with Carlitos Wayne, a croupier who convinced her to move to Gomorrah for better prospects. Their romance had to remain hidden, as the Omertas disapprove of personal ties outside their organization. When Carlitos plotted their escape, Cachino-a jealous Omertas lieutenant-framed him and forced him to flee the Strip under threat of death. With Carlitos gone, Cachino claimed Joana, subjecting her to sustained abuse and hooking her on Med-X until her health deteriorated and her body grew numb. Despite her addiction and suffering, Joana remains observant, listening to Cachino''s boasts and piecing together clues about the Omertas'' larger schemes.', 'Weary Caucasian female with visible signs of chemical dependency and physical neglect; gaunt complexion, dull eyes, and deteriorated health from sustained Med-X addiction.', 'Resigned on the surface but quietly perceptive and resourceful beneath; maintains enough awareness to eavesdrop and gather intelligence despite her addiction', '{"Carlitos Wayne":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"lover","note":"Her secret love who was forced to flee the Strip; she longs for reunion and freedom with him","best":"Sneaking moments together at the Atomic Wrangler before the Omertas tore them apart","worst":"Watching Carlitos vanish into the night, knowing Cachino orchestrated his exile"},"Cachino":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"abuser","note":"Jealous Omertas lieutenant who controls, abuses, and keeps her addicted to Med-X","worst":"Every night under Cachino''s possession, her body numb from the drugs he forces on her"},"Omertas":{"aff":-60,"type":"fearful","relation":"captor organization","note":"Unwilling affiliation maintained through addiction and intimidation"}}', 'Prostitute under Omertas control', '* Eavesdropping
* Gathering intelligence
* Reading people
* Enduring hardship', 'Flat and medicated in tone, occasionally revealing sharp awareness beneath the haze; speaks slowly with drug-slowed reflexes', '* Survival
* Escape from Cachino''s control
* Reunion with Carlitos
