('joe_cobb', '', 'Powder Ganger boss strong-arming Goodsprings over a fugitive trader', 'Joe Cobb leads a small but aggressive crew of Powder Gangers operating along the Long 15 corridor between Sloan and Primm. A career criminal with a long record of robbery, arson, and murder, Cobb spent time inside the NCRCF on a work-release program before Samuel Cooke''s prison break handed him his freedom back. He and his men stripped armor from dead guards and took to the highway, shaking down travelers and caravans with brutal efficiency. His winning streak cracked when a Crimson Caravan trader named Ringo shot back during a shakedown, killing some of Cobb''s crew before slipping away into Goodsprings. The townsfolk gave Ringo shelter, and Cobb has been tearing into the settlement ever since, determined to drag the trader out and make an example of anyone who stands in his way.', 'A weathered, hard-faced African American man with sun-darkened skin.', 'Aggressive, impatient, and prideful, Cobb operates through intimidation and force rather than negotiation. He holds grudges tightly and treats defiance as a personal insult that demands violent correction.', '{"Powder Gangers":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang brothers","note":"Cobb''s loyalty to his crew is fierce and personal, forged through shared incarceration and highway violence."},"Samuel Cooke":{"aff":40,"type":"grateful","relation":"prison break instigator","note":"Cooke''s riot gave Cobb his freedom, a debt he acknowledges even if the two run separate operations."},"Ringo":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"fugitive target","note":"Ringo killed Cobb''s men during the caravan shakedown and fled into Goodsprings. Cobb wants him dead as both vengeance and example."},"Goodsprings":{"aff":-50,"type":"contempt","relation":"harboring settlement","note":"The town''s decision to shelter Ringo is an insult Cobb intends to answer with fire and blood."},"Crimson Caravan":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"robbery target","note":"Cobb views caravan operations as legitimate prey along his stretch of highway."}}', 'Powder Ganger gang leader and highway robber', '* Armed robbery
* Extortion
* Gang coordination
* Small-unit tactics
* Improvised explosives
* Intimidation', 'Gruff and threatening, with short declarative sentences and casual profanity. He issues demands rather than requests and dismisses hesitation as weakness.', '* Capture and kill Ringo for the deaths of his men
* Break Goodsprings'' resistance to establish Powder Ganger authority in the area
