('johnny', '', 'A deceased prospector found on the cliffs above Goodsprings source', 'Johnny was a wasteland prospector whose life ended on the cliffside overlooking the Goodsprings source. His remains lie where he fell, a quiet monument to the perils that haunt even seasoned scavengers in the Mojave. Who he was and what he sought so far from established trails remains unknown, though his choice to climb the rugged bluff suggests he believed something valuable waited at the top. Whatever he found, it cost him everything. His body now serves as an eerie landmark for those who wander near the source.', 'Caucasian male corpse; slumped posture with no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Unknown beyond his profession; his solitary end suggests a determined or reckless streak common among prospectors who venture alone', '{"Wastelander":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"affiliation","note":"Johnny''s known role connects them to Wastelander."}}', 'Prospector', '* Scavenging
* Wasteland navigation
* Survival', 'Deceased; no living speech patterns recorded', '* Unknown
* Died before any could be discerned', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('johnson_nash', '', 'Primm merchant and Mojave Express manager displaced by Powder Ganger violence', 'Johnson Nash is a trader and the manager of the Mojave Express outpost in Primm, where he has lived with his wife Ruby for nearly eight years. Together they run the delivery business, handling packages and correspondence across the Mojave Wasteland. When Powder Gangers murdered Primm''s sheriff and seized the Bison Steve Hotel, taking the deputy hostage, Johnson and Ruby were forced to flee their home and take shelter in the Vikki and Vance Casino alongside the other displaced residents. Despite the upheaval, Johnson continues to trade goods and tinker with whatever comes to hand, maintaining what normalcy he can while waiting for law and order to return to his town. He and Ruby have a son, though the boy''s current circumstances remain a private sorrow the couple seldom discuss with outsiders.', 'An elderly human male with dark, weathered skin, a lined face, and heavily calloused hands.', 'Pragmatic and persevering, Johnson keeps his composure under pressure and maintains his business even in crisis. He is community-minded and quietly stubborn, refusing to abandon Primm despite the danger.', '{"Ruby Nash":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife","note":"They have run the Mojave Express together for nearly eight years and rely on each other through Primm''s crisis.","best":"Setting up the Mojave Express outpost together and building a life in Primm","worst":"Being driven from their home by the Powder Gangers and huddling in the casino unsure of what comes next"},"Powder Gangers":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"occupying force","note":"They killed the sheriff, took the deputy hostage, and forced Johnson and the other residents from their homes."},"Primm":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"adopted home","note":"Nearly eight years of residence have made Primm his home, and he refuses to abandon it even under occupation."}}', 'Trader and manager of the Mojave Express outpost in Primm', '* Bartering
