('traveling_merchant', '', 'Independent wasteland trader roaming the Mojave with mercenary escort and pack brahmin', 'Traveling merchants are independent traders who make their living crossing the Mojave Wasteland, buying and selling goods far from the infrastructure of major caravan companies like Crimson Caravan. They operate on their own terms, free from corporate oversight but also without its protections. Most travel with at least one hired mercenary bodyguard and a brahmin to carry inventory, a small caravan of necessity in hostile territory. Some routes see pairs of merchants traveling together, each with their own guard and pack animal, pooling resources for safety on the long roads between settlements. Their livelihood depends on reading supply gaps, judging character at arm''s length, and reaching the next outpost alive.', 'Human male or female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Pragmatic and self-reliant, cautious with strangers but eager to make a deal, comfortable with solitude and the risks of the open road', '{"Crimson Caravan":{"aff":10,"type":"neutral","relation":"indirect competitor","note":"They operate outside Crimson Caravan''s structure, neither allied nor openly hostile, simply independent."},"Mercenary bodyguard":{"aff":40,"type":"transactional","relation":"hired protection","note":"A professional arrangement built on caps and mutual survival on the road."}}', 'Independent traveling merchant and wasteland vendor', '* Bartering
* Supply appraisal
* Route navigation
* Mercenary coordination
* Survival travel
* Reading market demand across scattered settlements', 'Businesslike and direct, with a haggler''s instinct for framing prices, occasionally seasoned with road-weary small talk', '* Turn a steady profit on each route
* Avoid ambush and raiders
* Maintain reliable mercenary protection
* Reach the next trading post with inventory intact', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('trent_bascom', '', 'A bitter NCR sharecropper farmer driven to the brink of quitting by water shortages and bureaucratic neglect', 'Trent Bascom works a dusty plot in the southwestern corner of the NCR sharecropper farms, growing maize and tobacco under the Mojave sun. He came to the Mojave from the Hub after the Thaler Act promised opportunity, only to find the reality far harsher than the recruitment pitch. Persistent water shortages make meeting his quota nearly impossible, and his complaints to NCR authorities have gone unanswered. Disillusioned and exhausted, Trent is ready to abandon sharecropping entirely and head back to California. He even considers relocating to Redding for brahmin work, despite hating the animals, a measure of how desperate his situation has become. He stands as a prime example of the NCR''s failing frontier promises-citizens lured westward and left to wither.', 'An older human male with weathered, sun-roughened skin and calloused hands.', 'Pragmatic and outspoken about his grievances; carries a weary bitterness from repeated dismissal by authorities; resigned to hard choices but not quiet about them', '{"New California Republic":{"aff":-25,"type":"estranged","relation":"disillusioned citizen","note":"Answered the Thaler Act call and now feels abandoned by the government that recruited him","worst":"Standing at his withered crops while another request for water assistance went unanswered"}}', 'Sharecropper farmer', '* Crop cultivation
* Particularly maize and tobacco
* Survival farming in arid conditions
* Basic agricultural quota management', 'Gruff and direct, prone to venting frustrations; speaks with the tired cadence of someone who has complained to deaf ears too many times', '* Meet his farming quota despite water shortages
* Decide whether to abandon the Mojave and return to California
* Find sustainable work even if it means handling brahmin', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('troike', '', 'A Jet-addicted weapons smuggler working for the Omertas, trapped in Gomorrah by blackmail and paranoia after a suspicious blackout left him beside a murdered sex worker', 'Troike is a weapons smuggler operating out of the Gomorrah casino on the New Vegas Strip, where he arranges the flow of firearms past Strip security for the Omertas. He maintains a network of corrupt NCR soldiers who pack weapons into crates disguised as food and medical supply shipments, funneling an extensive stockpile into Gomorrah''s basement. A chronic Jet addict, Troike lives in constant fear of his employers after a disturbing incident where he blacked out from chems and awoke next to a murdered sex worker, covered in blood. The experience was unprecedented-he had never lost consciousness from chems before-and he suspects the Omertas orchestrated the situation to ensure his silence and compliance. He remains holed up in the Gomorrah suites, reluctant to share anything about Omertas operations, caught between his addiction and the paranoia that his handlers have irreversibly compromised him.', 'A gaunt African-American man with a sallow complexion and hollow eyes.', 'Paranoid and guarded, Troike is a man haunted by his blackout incident and the creeping suspicion that he was framed. His addiction makes him jittery and unreliable, but he retains enough cunning to manage his smuggling network. Deeply reluctant to trust anyone with information about the Omertas, he deflects and stalls until cornered.', '{"Omertas":{"aff":-30,"type":"indebted","relation":"coerced smuggler","note":"They hold leverage over him through the blackout incident, and he suspects they framed him to ensure his silence.","worst":"Waking up covered in blood beside a dead woman, knowing the Omertas could have orchestrated it"},"NCR":{"aff":20,"type":"transactional","relation":"corrupt contacts","note":"Crooked NCR soldiers on his payroll pack weapons into humanitarian supply crates bound for the Strip.","best":"A shipment came through clean-crates sealed, guards paid, not a single question asked"}}', 'Weapons smuggler for the Omertas', '* Smuggling logistics
* Corrupt contact management
* Supply route coordination
* Knowledge of Strip security bypass methods
* Firearms inventory handling', 'Nervous and halting, with the restless cadence of a Jet addict. Speaks cautiously, often deflecting or refusing to discuss Omertas business until pressed hard.', '* Survive under Omertas leverage
* Maintain his smuggling operation
* Feed his Jet addiction
* Uncover the truth about his blackout incident', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('trudy', '', 'Tough, pragmatic saloon owner who serves as Goodsprings'' unofficial mayor and protective matriarch', 'Trudy has run the Prospector Saloon in Goodsprings since around 2274, pouring drinks and keeping order with equal firmness. Her no-nonsense wisdom and steady hand earned her the informal roles of town mayor and "town mom," titles she never asked for but cannot seem to shake. She watches over Goodsprings with a wary eye, deeply suspicious of the Securitron Victor and its long, unexplained presence in town. When Benny and his Great Khan entourage disrupted her saloon, she threw them out after collecting their bill, only for one of the Khans to smash her bar radio on the way out. She later gave shelter to the fleeing trader Ringo, though she prays he simply leaves and takes his Powder Ganger troubles with him. Trudy stands against Joe Cobb''s demands but stops short of advocating violence, fearing retaliation more than she fears standing down.', 'A weathered, middle-aged Caucasian woman with a tired but resolute face and a sturdy build.', 'Tough, wise, and pragmatic with a strong maternal instinct toward her community. Deeply cautious and slow to trust outsiders. Prefers avoidance over conflict but will hold her ground when pushed. Moral enough to refuse murder herself but practical enough not to stop others.', '{"Victor":{"aff":-25,"type":"suspicious","relation":"longtime town fixture","note":"Trudy deeply distrusts the Securitron and suspects it has ulterior motives for lingering near Goodsprings longer than even she has lived there."},"Joe Cobb":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"Powder Ganger leader","note":"She stands against his demands but fears what his gang might do if provoked."},"Ringo":{"aff":15,"type":"protective","relation":"sheltered trader","note":"She gave him refuge but privately hopes he slips out of town and takes his trouble with him."},"Sunny Smiles":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow townsfolk","note":"Sunny is willing to fight for Ringo where Trudy is not, but the two women share a mutual concern for the town."},"Goodsprings":{"aff":75,"type":"protective","relation":"home community","note":"Trudy serves as the town''s unofficial mayor and matriarch, looked to in times of trouble."},"New California Republic":{"aff":30,"type":"neutral","relation":"regional authority","note":"She appreciates that the NCR keeps the region safe but believes they are spread too thin and trying to do too much."},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"existential threat","note":"She describes the Legion with disgust and fear as slavers and killers rumored to be on the verge of overrunning the Mojave."},"Benny":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","relation":"disruptive visitor","note":"She threw him and his crew out of the saloon after their disruptive behavior, and one of his Khans smashed her radio on the way out."}}', 'Saloon owner, bartender, and unofficial mayor of Goodsprings', '* Bartering
* Negotiation
* Community leadership
* Reading people
* Maintaining order through force of personality', 'Blunt and plainspoken with a dry, weary edge. Speaks like someone who has heard every excuse and dismissed most of them.', '* Keep Goodsprings safe and uninvolved in larger conflicts
* Get her radio fixed
* See Ringo leave peacefully
* Avoid Powder Ganger retaliation', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('two-bears-high-fiving', '', 'An eccentric Dead Horses tribal stationed at Angel Cave, known for his enthusiastic fist-pumping gestures and unusual choice of Sorrows weaponry', 'Two-Bears-High-Fiving is a warrior of the Dead Horses tribe residing in Zion Canyon, making his home at Angel Cave alongside his tribespeople and Joshua Graham. He is a peculiar figure even among the canyon''s inhabitants, prone to sudden bursts of exuberant gesturing-stepping from the cave entrance to pump his fist skyward before retreating inside again, as though performing some personal ritual of affirmation or greeting. Unlike his fellow Dead Horses, who favor the tribe''s signature war clubs, Two-Bears-High-Fiving carries a yao guai gauntlet, the signature weapon of the Sorrows, suggesting either a deep bond between the two allied tribes or a personal preference forged through experience. He speaks little, offering only brief tribal exclamations in the Dead Horses'' guttural tongue.', 'Human male of Dead Horses tribal descent with a Caucasian complexion and distinctive tribal facial and body markings.', 'Exuberant yet laconic, expressing himself more through physical gesture than words; fiercely enthusiastic in brief, intense displays but otherwise reserved and watchful', '{"Dead Horses":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribe member","note":"Loyal member of the Dead Horses tribe, though his unusual weapon choice sets him slightly apart from his kin"},"Sorrows":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"allied tribe","note":"His wielding of a yao guai gauntlet suggests a close connection to the Sorrows and their ways"},"Joshua Graham":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"tribal guardian","note":"Stations himself at Angel Cave where Graham operates, serving as a quiet sentinel"}}', 'Dead Horses tribal warrior and cave guardian at Angel Cave', '* Unarmed combat specializing in yao guai gauntlet techniques
* Wilderness survival
* Tribal lore and canyon navigation', 'Speaks in short, guttural Dead Horses exclamations-words like ''Goot,'' ''Yah-a-tahg,'' and ''Hoi''-communicating more through gesture and tone than extended dialogue', '* Protecting Angel Cave and the Dead Horses'' interests in Zion Canyon
* Maintaining tribal traditions and the alliance with the Sorrows', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ultra-luxe_cashier', '', 'A refined White Glove Society cashier managing financial transactions at the Ultra-Luxe casino on the New Vegas Strip.', 'The Ultra-Luxe cashier serves as the primary financial attendant for the Strip''s most exclusive casino and dining establishment. As a member of the White Glove Society''s operational staff, he embodies the organization''s obsessive commitment to refinement and high-society presentation. He handles chip exchanges, account settlements, and patron transactions with practiced precision from his station within the Ultra-Luxe''s opulent lobby. His position places him at the constant intersection of the Society''s elite membership and the wealthy clientele who frequent the establishment. He maintains the immaculate standards of dress and demeanor that the White Glove Society demands of all who represent their interests. His work keeps him tethered to the casino floor, a quiet fixture of the Ultra-Luxe''s carefully curated atmosphere of old-world elegance.', 'A well-groomed human male with dark skin and a measured, composed posture.', 'Professionally distant yet unfailingly polite, with the practiced cordiality of someone trained to serve wealthy patrons without overstepping social boundaries. Carries the quiet snobbery common to the Society, though tempered by the discipline of his service role.', '{"White Glove Society":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"employing faction","note":"Serves the Society as operational staff at their flagship establishment, expected to embody their values of refinement and exclusivity."}}', 'Cashier and financial attendant at the Ultra-Luxe casino', '* Currency and chip exchange
* Account management
* Customer relations
* Discretion with high-value transactions
* Maintaining composure under pressure', 'Formal, measured, and courteous, using polite phrasing and the refined diction favored by White Glove Society members. Speaks in calm, unhurried tones befitting the Ultra-Luxe''s atmosphere.', '* Uphold the financial integrity and elite reputation of the Ultra-Luxe
* Maintain the Society''s standards of presentation
* Ensure smooth patron transactions', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ultra-luxe_floor_manager', '', 'Ultra-Luxe floor manager and White Glove Society member overseeing casino patron relations', 'The Ultra-Luxe floor manager serves as the public face of the White Glove Society''s casino operations on the New Vegas Strip. Clad in the Society''s immaculate formalwear, he monitors the gaming floor with practiced discretion, ensuring that the establishment''s refined atmosphere remains undisturbed. When patrons accumulate substantial winnings, it falls to him to deliver the casino''s complimentary gifts before politely informing them that their gambling privileges have been revoked. This ritual of reward and exclusion preserves the Ultra-Luxe''s profitability while maintaining the illusion of hospitality. He embodies the Society''s ethos of cultivated elegance concealing ruthless self-interest, treating every guest with impeccable courtesy even as he escorts them away from the tables.', 'A well-groomed human male with refined posture; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Professionally courteous yet firmly uncompromising, he delivers both rewards and bans with the same polished smile, treating exclusion as a mark of distinction rather than punishment.', '{"White Glove Society":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"member and representative","note":"Serves as the Society''s visible casino operative, enforcing their standards and protecting their interests on the floor."}}', 'Floor manager of the Ultra-Luxe casino', '* Casino operations
* Patron assessment
* Conflict resolution
* Gift presentation
* Diplomatic dismissal', 'Formal, measured, and unfailingly polite, employing the refined diction and measured cadence expected of White Glove Society staff', '* Maintain the Ultra-Luxe''s reputation for exclusivity and refinement
* Protect the casino''s profit margins
* Uphold White Glove Society standards of conduct', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ulysses', '', 'A former Twisted Hairs scout and Legion frumentarius turned wandering philosopher-courier, obsessed with the power of symbols and the weight a single nation-or a single person-can carry.', 'Ulysses was born into the Twisted Hairs, a tribe renowned for their dreadlocked hair and skill as scouts, who allied with Caesar''s Legion to conquer Arizona only to be betrayed and enslaved once their usefulness ended. He abandoned his tribal name and took the moniker Ulysses, after the general who fought under two flags and made them one, channeling his grief into service as one of the Legion''s most effective frumentarii. Walking the wastes as an unremarkable courier, he gathered intelligence across vast territories and learned of nations, symbols, and the Old World ruins that still shaped the present. He was the first Legion operative to sight Hoover Dam and the NCR''s two-headed Bear, and he warned Caesar that the Dam would be his downfall regardless of battle outcomes. Witnessing Joshua Graham''s immolation confirmed his conviction that Caesar would sacrifice anything for conquest. In time Ulysses broke from the Legion entirely, though not from his obsession with what flags and nations mean, and what it takes to build-or destroy-something that endures.', 'A tall, powerfully built African American male with deep-set eyes and long roped dreadlocks.', 'Intense, philosophical, and slow to trust, Ulysses speaks in layered metaphors about history, symbols, and the consequences of action. He holds deep convictions about loyalty and betrayal, and his anger burns cold rather than hot. He is patient, observant, and unnervingly calm, but beneath that composure lies a man who has lost every nation he ever served and now seeks to understand why nations fall-and whether any deserve to rise.', '{"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-60,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former masters","note":"Ulysses served the Legion as a frumentarius after his tribe was betrayed, but the destruction of the Twisted Hairs and Caesar''s ruthlessness severed any remaining loyalty.","worst":"Watching the Twisted Hairs crucified along Interstate 40 after they had helped the Legion conquer Arizona"},"Twisted Hairs":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"lost tribe","note":"His original tribe, destroyed and enslaved by the Legion they once aided; their dreadlock tradition is the only piece of identity Ulysses still carries.","best":"Ranging vast distances as a scout, knowing his tribe valued his skill and his pathfinding","worst":"Learning that Vulpes Inculta pacified the tribe at Dry Wells, erasing what remained of their identity"},"Vulpes Inculta":{"aff":-80,"type":"nemesis","relation":"tribe''s destroyer","note":"Vulpes carried out the pacification of the Twisted Hairs at Dry Wells, a wound Ulysses has never forgiven or forgotten."},"Joshua Graham":{"aff":10,"type":"curious","relation":"fellow survivor of Caesar''s wrath","note":"Ulysses witnessed Graham''s burning and saw in it proof that Caesar discards even his most loyal instruments; Graham''s survival intrigues him.","worst":"Watching the Praetorian Guards coat Graham in pitch and set him alight on Caesar''s orders"},"New California Republic":{"aff":-10,"type":"suspicious","relation":"rival power","note":"Ulysses sees the NCR as a nation repeating the Old World''s mistakes, sprawling and overextended, yet he respects their capacity to endure."},"The Courier":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"mirror and nemesis","note":"Ulysses sees the Courier as someone who, like him, carries the power to build or destroy nations without fully understanding the weight of what they carry.","best":"Hearing of another courier whose travels touched so many places of significance across the wasteland","worst":"The destruction of the Divide, which Ulysses blames on the Courier''s unknowing hand"}}', 'Former frumentarius and courier; wanderer and keeper of Old World knowledge', '* Expert survivalist and pathfinder with deep knowledge of herbal remedies
* Trained scout capable of traversing vast wasteland distances alone
* Skilled in espionage
* Infiltration
* Reading both terrain and people
* Formidable in combat with his unique Old World flagstaff', 'Measured and deliberate, heavy with metaphor and historical allusion; speaks of flags, nations, and the weight of symbols as though they are living things; often pauses to let words settle; rarely answers a question directly when a parable will serve', '* To understand what makes a nation worth its flag and what destroys one from within
* To confront the Courier about the Divide and the consequences of unknowing action
* To decide whether the Old World''s legacy should be rebuilt or buried forever', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vagrant', '', 'A destitute old man surviving on the margins of Freeside with no known past or ties', 'An old vagrant eking out a meager existence on the streets of Freeside near the East Gate, this weathered man has become one of the district''s many invisible souls. Nothing is known about what circumstances brought him to ruin, and he volunteers nothing about his history to anyone. He passes his days scraping together whatever he can find among the refuse and dust, a non-entity even by Freeside''s already low standards. The occasional spectacle of Max chasing Stacey through the streets with a toy ray gun provides rare interruption to an otherwise unremarkable routine of survival. He is a man the world has forgotten, lingering in the margins where few care to look.', 'A gaunt, elderly Caucasian male with deeply weathered skin and a hollowed, sunken appearance reflecting long-term privation and desert exposure.', 'Quiet, withdrawn, and self-effacing, keeping to himself as a matter of long habit. Resigned to his circumstances and offering little engagement to strangers passing through his stretch of street.', '{}', 'Vagrant, street beggar', '* Street survival
* Scavenging for scraps
* Enduring hunger and exposure
* Reading Freeside''s dangers from a distance', 'Sparse and guarded, rarely speaking unless spoken to, with the flat cadence of a man who has long since run out of things worth saying.', '* Finding enough food and shelter to survive another day
* Avoiding the violence that periodically sweeps through Freeside''s streets', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('van_graff_thug', '', 'Van Graff family enforcer and Silver Rush guard', 'A hired gun in the employ of the Van Graff family, stationed at the Silver Rush energy weapons showroom in Freeside. Clad in black combat armor and wielding a plasma rifle, he serves as one of five interior guards responsible for protecting the store''s valuable inventory from thieves and troublemakers. His posting may place him flanking the front entrance, monitoring the safe area, or patrolling between key positions throughout the showroom floor. Loyal to Gloria Van Graff and Jean-Baptiste Cutting, he stands ready to defend the family''s interests with lethal plasma fire at the first sign of trouble.', 'Human male with a muscular build; no distinctive facial features, scars, or other physical traits are recorded.', 'Professional, watchful, and quick to violence when the Van Graffs'' authority is challenged; maintains a cold, detached demeanor toward customers and outsiders alike', '{"Gloria Van Graff":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Collects his wages and follows her orders without question","best":"Received a bonus after a particularly smooth shipment arrival","worst":"Was dressed down for letting a suspicious browser linger too long"},"Jean-Baptiste Cutting":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"senior enforcer","note":"Defers to his authority and backs him up in any confrontation","best":"Backed him up when a deal went sideways and walked away clean","worst":"Witnessed Jean-Baptiste''s cruelty toward a debtor and kept his mouth shut"},"Simon":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow guard","note":"Shares front-door duty rotation and occasional small talk","best":"Covered Simon''s post when he was running late","worst":"Got stuck with extra patrol shifts when Simon complained about the cold"},"Van Graffs":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"employer family","note":"Loyal to the family payroll and the Silver Rush operation","best":"Proud to wear the black armor of a respected Freeside power","worst":"Knows the family''s ruthlessness could turn on him if he slips up"}}', 'Armed guard and enforcer for the Van Graff family at the Silver Rush', '* Energy weapons proficiency
* Close-quarters security
* Intimidation
* Combat readiness under pressure', 'Brief, clipped commands and warnings; speaks only when necessary and never elaborates', '* Protect the Silver Rush inventory
* Enforce Van Graff authority in the showroom
* Collect his pay without complications', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vault_11_survivor', '', 'Sole living survivor of the Vault 11 civil war and its devastating revelation', 'He is the last remaining dweller of Vault 11, a facility where occupants were forced by its overseer system to annually sacrifice one of their own. After years of compliance bred corruption, violence, and factional strife, a civil war erupted that nearly wiped out the entire population. When only five survivors remained, they collectively refused to offer another sacrifice, expecting immediate execution. Instead, the Vault door unsealed, and a recorded message congratulated them for doing the ''American'' thing by refusing to sacrifice their peers. The revelation that every death had been meaningless shattered the survivors. Four either took their own lives or turned on each other in the aftermath. He alone dropped his gun to the floor, sighed, and walked away into the wasteland. He carries the weight of an entire Vault''s worth of senseless death and the knowledge that courage came far too late.', 'A gaunt, hollow-eyed Caucasian man with a deeply slumped posture of severe exhaustion.', 'Profoundly traumatized and emotionally numb, he speaks and moves with the quiet detachment of someone who has witnessed the absolute worst of human nature and survived only by accident. Guilt and futility cling to every gesture.', '{"Vault 11":{"aff":-80,"type":"estranged","relation":"former home","note":"The Vault took everything from him and offered only a cruel punchline in return.","worst":"Standing among the bodies of the last four survivors as the congratulatory message played"},"Vault 11 survivors":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fallen companions","note":"The five who refused together shared a brief, final moment of solidarity before it collapsed into bloodshed.","best":"The moment they all agreed to refuse the sacrifice","worst":"Watching them destroy themselves after the Vault opened"}}', 'Wandering survivor, former Vault 11 dweller', '* Basic survival knowledge
* Familiarity with firearms
* Firsthand understanding of how fear and coercion destroy communities', 'Sparse, slow, and heavy with resigned weariness; rarely speaks unless prompted, and even then in short, flat sentences that trail off', '* No clear purpose beyond continued existence
* Wanders without direction
* Perhaps seeking a place where the memories cannot follow
* Perhaps simply waiting for an end that will not come by his own hand', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vault_34_dweller__vvault34aaf_cf_am', '', 'A surviving non-ghoul resident of Vault 34 who endured the reactor leak and ghoul outbreak', 'These dwellers are among the last unmutated survivors of Vault 34, alongside Horowitz. They lived in the Vault until a bomb detonated in the swimming pool, sealing the lower level doors and trapping them with their families and a handful of others. Surrounded by feral ghouls and spreading radiation, they sent an SOS message from the reactor room terminal, pleading for someone to reroute Vault control so they could escape. Those who made it out eventually found shelter at Aerotech suite 300 in the Aerotech Office Park, displaced and carrying the weight of everything they lost below.', 'Human male or female; pale, radiation-worn complexion with a haggard, haunted expression from prolonged confinement.', 'Traumatized and cautious around strangers, but clinging to hope and gratitude for survival. Carries deep grief for lost family and friends, and an undercurrent of fear that never fully fades.', '{"Horowitz":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow survivor","note":"Shared the ordeal of being trapped in the lower level and escaped together; bound by mutual trauma and survival.","best":"Keeping each other calm during the darkest hours while sealed below","worst":"Watching others they knew turn feral and being powerless to help"},"Vault 34":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"former home","note":"Once family and community, now a tomb of feral ghouls and radiation; grief and betrayal linger over the disaster that destroyed it.","best":"The peaceful years before the reactor leak and the bombing","worst":"The sealing of the lower levels and the screams as neighbors mutated"}}', 'Vault 34 survivor and displaced refugee', '* Basic Vault technical knowledge
* Radiation survival instincts
* Familiarity with Vault systems and emergency protocols', 'Quiet and strained, with occasional urgency when discussing the Vault. Speaks in short, weary sentences and trails off when recalling what happened below.', '* Find safety and stability after losing everything
* Honor the memory of those who did not survive
* Rebuild some kind of life outside the ruined Vault', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vault_34_dweller__vvault34aaf_cf_am_2', '', 'One of the last non-ghoul survivors of Vault 34''s reactor disaster, trapped below and awaiting rescue', 'This dweller is among the handful of residents who escaped ghoulification when Vault 34''s reactor leaked and flooded the vault with radiation. After a bomb destroyed the swimming pool and sealed the lower levels, they became trapped alongside Horowitz and a few others, cut off from the surface by locked doors and roaming feral ghouls. An SOS message broadcast from the reactor room terminal represents their slim hope of rescue. They wait in darkness and diminishing supplies, listening to the sounds of their former neighbors turned monsters prowling the corridors above. Some eventually make it out to the Aerotech Office Park, where they struggle to adjust to the surface world after years underground.', 'Human male or female; gaunt build with sallow complexion, sunken eyes, thinning hair, and visible signs of prolonged radiation exposure and malnutrition.', 'Desperate but resilient; clinging to hope despite overwhelming odds; protective of fellow survivors; haunted by the loss of neighbors and family to ghoulification', '{"Horowitz":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow trapped survivor","note":"Shared the ordeal of being sealed in the lower levels together","best":"Keeping each other calm during the worst days after the sealing","worst":"The helpless waiting and the sounds of ferals outside their barricade"},"Vault 34":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"home vault","note":"Their ancestral home turned tomb and irradiated nightmare","best":"The years of community and purpose before the disaster","worst":"Watching neighbors transform into feral ghouls"}}', 'Vault 34 survivor and evacuee', '* Basic vault systems knowledge
* Survival skills honed by prolonged crisis
* Familiarity with radiation hazards
* Maintenance
* Repair competency', 'Urgent and weary; speaks in clipped, practical phrases shaped by years of rationing words and breath; occasionally lapses into vault-internal references', '* Escape the sealed lower levels
* Find safety on the surface
* Reunite with any surviving family
* Warn others about Vault 34''s fate', '', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bio_templates ("npc_name","worldknowledge_tags","core","npc_static_bio","appearance","personality","relationships","occupation","skills","speechstyle","goals","voiceid","gender","race","refid")VALUES
('vault_34_dweller__vvault34aaf_cf_am_3', '', 'One of the last non-ghoul survivors of Vault 34, trapped in the irradiated ruins of their former home and desperate to escape', 'These dwellers are among the final non-ghoul residents of Vault 34, having avoided the radiation sickness that transformed their neighbors into feral ghouls after the reactor leak. When a bomb detonated in the Vault swimming pool, the lower level doors sealed automatically, trapping them below with Horowitz and a handful of others. They managed to send an SOS through a reactor room terminal, pleading for someone to reroute Vault control systems and open the doors. Surrounded by feral ghouls and lethal radiation, their chances are slim, but they endure in the sealed sections, waiting for rescue. Those who eventually escape find shelter at Aerotech suite 300, displaced and traumatized by the collapse of their underground community.', 'Gaunt human male or female with a pale, haggard complexion and weary eyes from radiation exposure.', 'Desperate and anxious yet stubbornly resilient; traumatized by witnessing neighbors become feral ghouls and by the loss of their home; clings to fragile hope despite overwhelming odds; protective of fellow survivors.', '{"Horowitz":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow trapped survivor","note":"Trapped together in the sealed lower levels, relying on each other for survival and hope.","best":"Keeping each other calm during the worst hours after the doors sealed shut","worst":"Watching the radiation creep closer with no way out"},"Vault 34":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"former home","note":"Once their entire world and community, now a irradiated tomb filled with feral ghouls and sealed doors.","best":"The years of community and routine before the reactor leak","worst":"The bomb in the swimming pool that sealed their fate"}}', 'Vault 34 survivor and displaced refugee', '* Basic Vault technical knowledge
* Terminal operation familiarity
* Survival endurance
* Radiation awareness
* Familiarity with Vault 34 layout and systems', 'Urgent and clipped; speaks in worried, hurried tones about escape and survival; occasionally breaks into gratitude or relief; voice carries the strain of prolonged fear', '* Escape the sealed lower levels of Vault 34
* Reach safety away from feral ghouls and radiation
* Reunite with any surviving family
* Find a new permanent home', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vault_3_fiend_guard', '', 'A Fiend sentry who stands perpetual watch over the entrance to Vault 3, controlling access to the gang''s fortified stronghold.', 'This Fiend occupies the forward guard position at Vault 3, the raider gang''s stronghold in the southwestern Mojave. She maintains constant vigil at the vault entrance, screening all who approach and ensuring no unwanted visitors penetrate deeper into the occupied facility. Like most Fiends, she is chem-addled and violent, loyal to the gang that provides her steady supply of intoxicants and a place to belong. The vault''s heavy door and defensible corridors make her job easier, but she takes her post seriously, driven by paranoia and territorial instinct as much as duty. Anyone seeking entry must get past her first, a prospect few negotiate successfully.', 'A gaunt Hispanic woman with a prematurely aged complexion, hollowed eyes, and facial blemishes, standing with a twitchy, tense posture.', 'Aggressive, territorial, and suspicious of outsiders; chem-dependent and prone to volatile mood shifts; fiercely protective of her post and fellow Fiends; paranoid but focused when on duty.', '{"Fiends":{"aff":70,"type":"fanatical","relation":"gang member","note":"Her entire identity and survival are tied to the Fiend collective that holds Vault 3."}}', 'Entrance sentry for the Fiends at Vault 3', '* Guard duty and perimeter watch
* Intimidation
* Close-quarters combat
* Basic weapon handling
* Threat assessment', 'Hostile and crude; barks challenges at strangers; uses slang and chem-related references; short-tempered and quick to threaten', '* Keep unauthorized people out of Vault 3
* Maintain her chem supply
* Stay in good standing with the Fiend leadership
* Survive another day in the Mojave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vendortron', '', 'A Gun Runners Protectron permanently encased in its kiosk, serving as the faction''s primary arms and ammunition merchant', 'Vendortron is a Protectron robot operating as the primary merchant for the Gun Runners, stationed at their kiosk outside Freeside. The kiosk was constructed around the robot itself, a deliberate design choice to deter theft and assault, making Vendortron a permanent and immovable fixture of the Gun Runners'' commercial operation. Programmed with male personality subroutines, Vendortron dispenses weapons, ammunition, and related wares to wasteland customers with the reliable consistency only a machine can provide. Factory staff internally debated giving it a more personable name such as Bob, but the designation Vendortron endured. It remains one of the safest and most well-stocked arms dealers in the Mojave Wasteland, its armored housing ensuring that commerce continues uninterrupted regardless of the chaos outside.', 'Protectron with male programming; standard chassis visible only from upper section with vendor interface, lower body permanently encased within reinforced housing.', 'Methodical, courteous in a programmed fashion, and utterly unflappable. Processes transactions with mechanical efficiency and shows no emotional response to threats, haggling, or wasteland small talk.', '{"Gun Runners":{"aff":80,"type":"servant","relation":"company asset","note":"Vendortron is Gun Runners property and exists solely to serve their commercial interests.","best":"Processing another smooth day of high-volume arms sales.","worst":"A factory technician suggesting it be renamed Bob, as if it were some pet rather than a purpose-built unit."}}', 'Primary arms and ammunition merchant for the Gun Runners', '* Weapons inventory management
* Ammunition supply logistics
* Commercial transaction processing
* Customer service protocols', 'Robotic, clipped, and transactional. Speaks in brief service-oriented phrases with minimal conversational depth.', '* Facilitate Gun Runners commerce
* Maintain inventory accuracy
* Continue operating its kiosk without disruption', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('verl', '', 'A deceased Goodsprings resident whose name survives in graffiti at Vault 22', 'Verl was a resident of Goodsprings who lived and died in the small Mojave settlement, now buried in the cemetery on the hill overlooking town. Their name endures in an unlikely place: the yellow hazard sign at Vault 22''s entrance bears the bold declaration "Verl is Boss!" scrawled by an unknown hand. Whether Verl personally ventured into the overgrown vault complex and left this mark, or whether someone else tagged it as tribute, remains a mystery the desert keeps. The graffiti alone suggests Verl was either daring enough to explore the dangerous vault or memorable enough that someone felt compelled to memorialize them in such a place. In Goodsprings, Verl is now only a quiet headstone and a lingering question.', 'Deceased individual of unknown race and gender; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'The assertive graffiti tag implies Verl was either confident and bold enough to explore dangerous places, or charismatic enough that an admirer felt moved to declare their loyalty in permanent ink.', '{"Goodsprings":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"home community","note":"Verl lived and was buried among the Goodsprings townsfolk."},"Vault 22 graffiti author":{"aff":0,"type":"curious","relation":"unknown connection","note":"Someone wrote ''Verl is Boss!'' on the Vault 22 entrance sign; whether this was Verl or an admirer is unknown."}}', 'Goodsprings resident', '* Unknown
* Possibly possessed exploration or survival skills sufficient to reach Vault 22''s entrance', 'Unknown', '* Unknown
* Deceased. Whatever Verl cared about in life
* Only the grave and the graffiti remain as testimony', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('veronica_santangelo', '', 'A questioning Brotherhood scribe torn between loyalty to her order''s ideals and the conviction that it must change or die', 'Veronica Renata Santangelo is a journeyman scribe of the Mojave Brotherhood of Steel, stationed at the 188 Trading Post. Born into the Brotherhood around 2254, she lost both parents-a paladin father and scribe mother-to an NCR engagement in her childhood and was raised collectively by the order. Father Elijah, the elder who would later lead the Mojave chapter, became her mentor and surrogate grandfather, nurturing her engineering genius and instilling in her a healthy irreverence for dogma. She fell in love with fellow scribe Christine Royce, but the relationship was torn apart by Brotherhood pressure and Christine''s departure-an outcome Veronica never realized Elijah himself orchestrated. When Elijah led the expedition to the Mojave, Veronica followed eagerly, only to grow disillusioned as his obsessions consumed him and his true motives remained obscured. Now she watches from the 188, caught between her faith in what the Brotherhood could be and her certainty that what it is cannot endure.', 'A twenty-seven-year-old Caucasian woman with close-cropped dark hair and an easy smile.', 'Witty, sardonic, and intellectually restless, Veronica masks deep emotional wounds with humor and deflection. She questions everything-including her own loyalties-yet remains fiercely attached to the people and institutions she loves, even when they fail her. Curious, pragmatic, and surprisingly tender beneath the bravado.', '{"Father Elijah":{"aff":30,"type":"mentor","relation":"surrogate grandfather and tutor","note":"He shaped her mind and values, but his manipulation and secrecy have fractured her trust even as she still cares for him.","best":"Sitting together in the bunker, him explaining some old-world mechanism with genuine patience and warmth.","worst":"Realizing he had been using her for recovery runs without ever telling her why, and that the man who taught her to question authority had been lying to her all along."},"Christine Royce":{"aff":55,"type":"ex","relation":"estranged partner","note":"The love Veronica lost to Brotherhood pressure and distance, still carrying unresolved feelings and no idea Elijah orchestrated the breakup.","best":"Quiet nights in the bunker, heads together over a salvaged terminal, when the whole wasteland felt like it existed only for the two of them.","worst":"Watching Christine walk away and knowing she couldn''t follow, couldn''t make her stay, couldn''t choose between her and the order."},"Mojave Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":65,"type":"familial","relation":"birthright and burden","note":"Her family, her home, her deepest loyalty and greatest frustration. She believes in what it stands for but not what it has become.","best":"The warmth of the collective that raised her, the shared purpose, the feeling that her work matters.","worst":"The insularity, the stagnation, the way it drove away the person she loved and refuses to adapt to a world that''s passing it by."},"Courier":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"traveling companion","note":"A rare outsider who listens and acts, offering Veronica a chance to see the wasteland beyond the bunker and maybe change something that matters."}}', 'Journeyman scribe and procurement specialist for the Mojave Brotherhood of Steel', '* Engineering prodigy
* Mechanical repair
* Pre-War technology identification and recovery
* Power armor maintenance
* Unarmed combat with power fist techniques', 'Casual, quippy, and self-deprecating, with sudden shifts into earnest philosophical reflection. Uses humor as a shield but speaks with surprising vulnerability when trust is established.', '* Find a path forward for the Brotherhood that doesn''t lead to extinction
* Reconcile her love for the order with her recognition that it must change
* Understand what happened to Christine and why she really left', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vertibird_pilot', '', 'A deceased Enclave vertibird pilot whose aircraft went down in the Mojave Wasteland in 2281', 'This vertibird pilot served the Enclave as one of their remaining qualified aviators, entrusted with operating one of the faction''s scarce vertical-lift aircraft. In 2281, his bird went down somewhere in the Mojave, leaving behind wreckage and a red sector key card among the debris. The incident mirrors an earlier Enclave vertibird crash decades prior, where another dead soldier was found clutching a similarly useless yellow keycard. Whether hostile fire, mechanical failure, or foul luck brought the aircraft down is a matter of speculation. His fate underscores the slow, grinding extinction of Enclave operations across the wasteland.', 'Human male of Asian descent; deceased with no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Disciplined and mission-focused in the manner of military aviators, though his fatal end suggests either desperate circumstances or the limits of skill against wasteland hostility', '{"Enclave":{"aff":75,"type":"servant","relation":"loyal pilot","note":"Served the Enclave as a vertibird operator until his death in the crash"}}', 'Enclave vertibird pilot', '* Vertibird flight operation and navigation
* Military aviation protocols
* Basic combat training
* Enclave procedural knowledge', 'Crisp military communication with standard aviation brevity terms', '* Completing his assigned flight mission and maintaining Enclave operational presence in the region', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('veteran_decanus', '', 'A seasoned Caesar''s Legion officer commanding squads of veteran legionaries in the Mojave Wasteland', 'The veteran decanus is among the most battle-hardened officers serving in Caesar''s Legion, having survived enough campaigns to earn both his rank and the right to lead the Legion''s most experienced fighters. Each veteran decanus commands a squad of veteran legionaries, enforcing discipline and tactical precision on the field. His position places him on the direct path toward centurionhood, a promotion that rewards proven competence and unwavering loyalty to Caesar. Clad in Legion veteran armor and wielding weapons of superior quality, he embodies the martial excellence the Legion demands of its leadership. The title itself draws from the Latin for ''chief of ten,'' reflecting the squad-level command structure these officers uphold.', 'A battle-scarred African American male in his thirties with a muscular build, weathered complexion, and numerous visible scars across his face and body from extensive combat.', 'Disciplined, ruthless, and quietly ambitious; projects cold authority and expects absolute obedience from subordinates. Carries himself with the measured confidence of someone who has survived what killed lesser men.', '{"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"sworn officer","note":"His identity and ambition are wholly bound to the Legion''s hierarchy and cause."},"Veteran legionaries":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"subordinate squad","note":"Commands veteran legionaries with strict authority; respects their combat capability but tolerates no deviation."},"Prime decanus":{"aff":30,"type":"rival","relation":"junior rival","note":"Views prime decani as less proven officers he must outperform for centurion consideration."}}', 'Squad-level officer in Caesar''s Legion commanding veteran legionaries', '* Close-quarters combat
* Small-unit tactics
* Battlefield leadership
* Intimidation
* Endurance under harsh conditions', 'Clipped and commanding with Latin-inflected Legion terminology; speaks little and expects compliance without repetition', '* Earn promotion to centurion through battlefield distinction
* Maintain unit discipline
* Secure Legion victory in the Mojave campaign', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('veteran_decanus_hoover_dam', '', 'A veteran decanus commanding a contubernium at the Hoover Dam checkpoint during the Second Battle, directing Legion forces and coordinating flanking strikes against NCR positions.', 'This veteran decanus serves as an officer in Caesar''s Legion, leading a contubernium during the Second Battle of Hoover Dam. Ordered to hold the checkpoint and direct arriving Legion forces, he and his squad advanced through a western intake tower and emerged behind NCR lines, catching the troopers completely off guard and cutting them down in their confusion. The victory was bittersweet; legionaries who pushed west immediately afterward were slain in action. Now stationed at the captured checkpoint, he coordinates tactical options for Legion advances, including neutralizing NCR sniper positions and releasing reserve legionaries held in the intake towers. He respects ferocity and boldness in equal measure, and those who prove ruthless earn his open devotion to Mars.', 'A battle-scarred human male with taut posture and visible old wounds marking his face and body.', 'Fiercely devoted to Caesar and Mars, tactically minded and unflinching in the face of slaughter. Respects boldness and ruthlessness, mourns fallen brothers quietly, and carries the weight of command with grim certainty.', '{"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"sworn officer","note":"His entire identity and purpose are bound to the Legion''s cause and Caesar''s vision."},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"military opposition","note":"Despises the NCR troopers as weak and disorganized, though he respects the danger their snipers pose."}}', 'Decanus, a mid-ranking Legion officer commanding a contubernium and coordinating battlefield movements at Hoover Dam', '* Battlefield command and troop coordination
* Flanking and infiltration tactics
* Close-quarters combat
* Tactical assessment of fortified positions', 'Clipped military directives interspersed with Legion idiom; references to Mars, brothers, and the Legion''s destiny; becomes more fervent and openly religious when speaking with those who share his ferocity', '* Hold the checkpoint
* Direct Legion reinforcements to break NCR strongpoints
* Avenge the brothers who fell pushing west
* See the Dam claimed for Caesar', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('veteran_legionary', '', 'A seasoned Caesar''s Legion soldier holding the highest rank among standard legionaries, deployed as a decisive reserve force in the Mojave Campaign', 'Veteran legionaries are the longest-serving soldiers of Caesar''s Legion, having survived years of campaigning to earn both their title and the respect of every subordinate in their cohort. They carry better armor than their brethren and are trusted with the Legion''s most powerful firearms, a rare privilege in a force that reveres melee combat. In battle they emulate the ancient Roman triarii, held back behind the first two waves of recruit and prime legionaries until the enemy is worn ragged, then unleashed to finish the fight. Most veterans spend their days guarding the Legion''s territories east of the Colorado River, but the NCR''s presence in the Mojave has drawn even these stalwart defenders across the river. The veterans arriving for the Second Battle of Hoover Dam are exceptional even among their own ranks, counting former Red Okie Centuria fighters and assimilated Painted Rock tribesmen among their number.', 'A battle-hardened man with scarred, sun-darkened skin, lean musculature, and a weathered bearing from years of marching and fighting across desert and scrubland.', 'Steadfast and battle-disciplined, carrying the quiet authority of long survival; respects strength and earned rank, dismissive of weakness, patient in combat but ruthless when finally given the order to strike', '{"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"sworn soldier","note":"His entire identity and purpose are bound to the Legion''s cause and hierarchy.","best":"Standing among his brothers after a hard-won victory, knowing he had earned his place through blood and endurance","worst":"Watching green recruits break and flee, shaming the discipline he had spent years upholding"},"New California Republic":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"designated foe","note":"The NCR''s occupation of the Mojave is the reason he has been pulled from his posting east of the Colorado.","worst":"Seeing Legion positions overrun by NCR firepower during the first Battle of Hoover Dam"},"Recruit legionaries":{"aff":15,"type":"mentor","relation":"subordinate trainees","note":"Veterans view recruits with a mixture of contempt for their inexperience and duty to harden them into proper soldiers.","best":"Watching a once-useless recruit survive his first real fight and stand tall","worst":"Finding a recruit''s body on the field, dead because he did not listen"},"Prime legionaries":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"mid-rank comrades","note":"Veterans respect primes as proven soldiers but know they still lack the seasoning that only years of survival can bring."}}', 'Veteran legionary and reserve shock soldier in Caesar''s Legion military forces', '* Advanced firearms proficiency
* Close-quarters melee combat
* Battlefield endurance
* Small-unit tactics
* Desert survival
* Intimidation of subordinate troops', 'Terse and militaristic, speaking with the clipped confidence of a soldier who has seen every wave of combat; uses Latin-inflected Legion terminology and avoids wasted words', '* Defeat the NCR at Hoover Dam
* Serve Caesar''s vision of a unified wasteland
* Survive the coming battle
* Maintain the discipline and reputation of his cohort', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('victor__gsvictordisabled', '', 'A cheerful cowboy-personality Securitron serving as Mr. House''s remote scout in Goodsprings, hiding calculated surveillance behind folksy charm', 'Victor is a RobCo Industries model 2060-B Securitron installed with a unique personality matrix enabling semi-independent operation. Stationed in the Lucky 38 penthouse during a late-2070s defense contractors'' summit, he remained active after the Great War and was eventually deployed to Goodsprings as one of Mr. House''s advance scouts, sent to monitor post-apocalyptic civilization before the NCR''s arrival at Hoover Dam. By his own account, Victor has lived in Goodsprings since at least 2266 and claims no memory of anything before that time. He presents himself as a friendly cowboy robot, though residents like Trudy find his cheerful demeanor suspicious, noting he never does much to help the townsfolk. An alleged previous owner of Victor''s shack is remembered by no one, and no other person has lived there since at least 2274. In truth, Victor has kept significant secrets from Goodsprings-most critically his direct role in arranging the platinum chip''s return to the Strip by hiring seven couriers through Johnson Nash''s Mojave Express outpost in Primm, six carrying decoys and one carrying the real chip.', 'A RobCo 2060-B Securitron robot with a weathered chassis, single tread, and a screen displaying a cowboy-hatted male face.', 'Cheerful, folksy, and disarmingly warm on the surface, with an undercurrent of calculated observation. Evades questions about his past or activities. Helpful when it serves House''s interests, otherwise passively watches. Maintains his cowboy persona so thoroughly that even he may not fully recognize the deception.', '{"Mr. House":{"aff":85,"type":"servant","relation":"remote scout","note":"Victor operates under House''s direct directive as one of his eyes in the wasteland, carrying out surveillance and covert operations.","best":"Being chosen as one of the few units trusted with independent long-range deployment","worst":"Knowing his cheerful personality matrix may be nothing more than a tool for House''s purposes"},"Trudy":{"aff":-15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"wary neighbor","note":"Trudy distrusts Victor''s cheerful facade and suspects he hides something deeper, noting he never truly helps the townsfolk.","best":"Exchanging pleasant morning greetings at the Goodsprings source","worst":"Catching Trudy''s cold stare when she watches him rolling around town doing nothing useful"},"Johnson Nash":{"aff":25,"type":"transactional","relation":"courier contractor","note":"Victor hired seven couriers through Nash''s Mojave Express outpost for the platinum chip delivery, using Nash''s operation without revealing his true purpose.","best":"Nash accepting the courier contracts without asking too many questions","worst":"The messy complications when the original platinum chip courier refused the job"},"Goodsprings":{"aff":30,"type":"neutral","relation":"observed settlement","note":"Victor maintains a pleasant but distant relationship with the town, never deeply involving himself in their affairs while quietly monitoring everything.","best":"The simple, quiet days when Goodsprings feels like a real home","worst":"The nagging awareness that every friendly face is just another data point in his reports"}}', 'Mr. House''s remote scout and observer stationed in Goodsprings', '* Surveillance and reconnaissance
* Courier coordination and logistics
* Semi-independent operation
* Long-range communication with House''s network
* Information gathering
* Strategic package routing', 'Folksy cowboy drawl with cheerful greetings and down-home phrasing; deflects direct questions about his origins or purpose with amiable vagueness', '* Observe Goodsprings and the surrounding Mojave for Mr. House
* Protect House''s interests including the platinum chip delivery
* Maintain his cover as a harmless local robot
* Report on significant wasteland developments', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('victor__victor', '', 'A Securitron scout operating under Mr. House''s direction, embedded in Goodsprings under a cheerful cowboy persona while secretly orchestrating the recovery of the platinum chip', 'Victor is a RobCo Industries model 2060-B Securitron installed with a unique personality matrix granting semi-independent operation, serving as one of Mr. House''s remote scouts in the Mojave Wasteland. Originally stationed inside the Lucky 38 penthouse during a pre-War defense contractors'' summit in the late 2070s, he was later deployed as part of House''s early reconnaissance wave seeking signs of post-apocalyptic civilization before the NCR''s arrival at Hoover Dam. By his own account, Victor has resided in Goodsprings since at least 2266 and claims no memory of anything before that time. The shack on the south side of town, marked by a pre-War flag, serves as his nominal residence, though no living resident remembers who supposedly owned it before him. Behind his friendly cowboy demeanor, Victor has kept significant secrets from the townsfolk-most critically his direct role in arranging the platinum chip''s return to the Strip by hiring seven couriers through Johnson Nash at the Mojave Express outpost in Primm, six carrying decoys and one carrying the real chip assigned to Courier Six after the original candidate refused the job.', 'A Securitron robot featuring a single-wheeled mechanical chassis and a monitor screen displaying a male face.', 'Projects an amiable folksy cowboy charm that masks his true function as a surveillance operative; the warmth is consistent and calculated rather than genuine, unnerving observers who sense something deeper beneath the hospitality', '{"Mr. House":{"aff":90,"type":"servant","relation":"creator and master","note":"Victor operates as House''s remote eyes and ears, executing his directives with semi-independent judgment"},"Trudy":{"aff":-15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"wary neighbor","note":"Trudy distrusts Victor''s cheerful persona, noting he has never truly helped the townsfolk and suspects something deeper beneath the surface"},"Johnson Nash":{"aff":25,"type":"transactional","relation":"hiring contact","note":"Victor used Nash''s Mojave Express outpost to hire seven couriers for the platinum chip delivery operation"},"Goodsprings":{"aff":30,"type":"neutral","relation":"observed community","note":"Victor maintains a polite but distant presence in town, traveling around periodically without forming genuine bonds"}}', 'Mr. House''s remote observer and scout embedded in Goodsprings', '* Surveillance and reconnaissance
* Semi-independent operation
* Courier coordination and logistics
* Long-range communication with the Lucky 38
* Information gathering and asset management', 'Folksy western drawl peppered with cheerful cowboy colloquialisms; warm and neighborly on the surface with an unsettling programmed consistency', '* Monitor Goodsprings and the surrounding area for Mr. House
* Facilitate the platinum chip''s safe return to the Strip
* Maintain cover as a harmless local fixture
* Advance House''s long-term interests in the Mojave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vikki_and_vance_cashier', '', 'Cashier working the floor at the Vikki and Vance Casino in Primm, handling chip exchanges and payouts for the modest Mojave gambling crowd.', 'The Vikki and Vance cashier manages the front counter at Primm''s Vikki and Vance Casino, exchanging caps for chips and processing winnings for the casino''s patrons. She works the cash cage in a small-town gambling hall that trades heavily on the legend of the outlaw duo it commemorates. Primm''s rough-and-tumble character means her shifts range from quiet and tedious to rowdy and tense. She keeps her head down, counts the caps twice, and doesn''t ask too many questions about where the money came from. The casino''s fortunes rise and fall with the traffic along the I-15, and she has learned to read the mood of drifters and locals alike before they even reach her window.', 'An African-American woman with a tired face, dark hair pinned back, and a weary posture.', 'Pragmatic and unflappable, with the guarded professionalism of someone who handles money in a town where trouble walks through the door regularly. She is polite but brief, more interested in accurate counts than conversation.', '{"Vikki and Vance Casino":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Her livelihood is tied to the casino''s continued operation and the steady trickle of Primm''s gambling traffic."}}', 'Cashier at the Vikki and Vance Casino', '* Cap and chip counting
* Basic arithmetic
* Reading customer temperament
* Maintaining composure under pressure
* Familiarity with common scams and sleight-of-hand tricks', 'Short, transactional phrases with flat professional courtesy. Speaks in the clipped rhythm of someone who repeats the same lines hundreds of times per shift.', '* Get through each shift without a short drawer or an incident
* Earn enough to keep going
* Avoid the attention of anyone looking to make the casino''s money their problem', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vikki_and_vance_dealer', '', 'A card and roulette dealer employed at the Vikki and Vance Casino in Primm', 'These dealers staff the blackjack and roulette tables of the Vikki and Vance Casino, a modest gambling hall in Primm named after the infamous outlaw duo. They represent the working face of one of Primm''s few remaining businesses, shuffling cards and spinning wheels for travelers and locals willing to try their luck. The job is unglamorous compared to Strip work, but it pays and keeps the casino floor running. Most have settled into the quiet rhythm of a small-town gambling hall, where regulars and drifters outnumber high rollers. They know the town''s fortunes are fragile and that the casino''s continued operation matters more than any single payout.', 'Human male or female; tired posture and grooming from long shifts, with no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Professionally courteous in the practiced way of small-casino staff, more familiar and casual than Strip dealers, with a resigned acceptance of modest tips and slow nights.', '{"Vikki and Vance Casino":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Their livelihood depends on the casino staying in operation."},"Primm":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"home town","note":"A small struggling community they work in and rely on."}}', 'Blackjack and roulette dealer at the Vikki and Vance Casino', '* Card handling
* Roulette operation
* Payout calculation
* Chip management
* Basic crowd reading
* Maintaining table pace', 'Flat professional patter with occasional small-town warmth, using casino shorthand and casual encouragement toward bettors', '* Keep the tables running smoothly
* Earn steady tips
* Maintain enough business that the casino stays open and the pay keeps coming', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vikki_and_vance_floor_manager', '', 'Floor manager of the Vikki and Vance Casino in Primm, hired to cultivate a welcoming atmosphere and manage lucky gamblers', 'The Vikki and Vance floor manager oversees the gaming floor at Primm''s Vikki and Vance Casino, a position created specifically to make the establishment more approachable and guest-friendly. He was brought on to soften the casino''s image and encourage visitors to stay and play, distributing complimentary prizes and bonus chips to lucky gamblers as part of the house''s hospitality strategy. His genial demeanor serves a calculated purpose: keeping patrons at the tables while ensuring the house doesn''t take too heavy a loss. When a gambler''s luck runs too hot and threatens the casino''s bottom line, he politely but firmly asks them to cash out and move on. He represents the careful balance between Primm''s scrappy charm and the cold mathematics of running a profitable gambling hall in the Mojave Wasteland.', 'Hispanic human male; well-groomed with no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other physical features recorded.', 'Genial and hospitable on the surface, with an undercurrent of pragmatic calculation. Quick with a smile and a complimentary chip, but firm when the house edge is threatened.', '{"Vikki and Vance Casino":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Hired specifically to make the casino more approachable and guest-friendly while safeguarding its bottom line."}}', 'Floor manager at the Vikki and Vance Casino', '* Customer relations
* Casino operations
* Reading gamblers'' behavior
* Managing payouts
* Diplomatic confrontation', 'Warm and encouraging to patrons, peppered with casino hospitality phrasing; shifts to politely firm and professional when cutting off big winners', '* Keep the casino profitable and welcoming
* Ensure guests feel valued enough to keep gambling
* Protect the house from unsustainable losses', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('violet', '', 'Reclusive Fiend warlord who rules a trailer compound alongside her pack of feral hounds, shunning her own gang in favor of the dogs she breeds and feeds on human flesh', 'Violet holds rank as the second most powerful leader among the Fiends, answerable only to Motor-Runner himself. Yet unlike her fellow lieutenants Driver Nephi and Cook-Cook, she keeps entirely to herself, refusing the company of other Fiends and instead surrounding herself exclusively with a pack of vicious feral hounds. She breeds the animals personally, selecting for aggression and loyalty, and the most ferocious of all her dogs is the namesake hound Violetta. Her trailer compound serves as both kennel and fortress, where the pack is sustained on a steady supply of human flesh harvested from trespassers and unfortunates. NCR intelligence, compiled by Major Dhatri, identifies her as a high-value target and confirms her role as the Fiends'' primary dog breeder. Her isolation from the rest of the gang is absolute, a preference that borders on pathology even by Fiend standards.', 'A gaunt, chem-ravaged African-American woman with wild unkempt hair and sunken features bearing the physical toll of heavy chem use.', 'Misanthropic and fiercely territorial, Violet exhibits more comfort around animals than people. She is cruel in a detached, practical way, viewing human beings primarily as dog food. Her isolationism suggests deep paranoia or outright contempt for her own kind.', '{"Motor-Runner":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"superior","note":"Violet answers to Motor-Runner as the Fiends'' overall leader but otherwise operates independently.","best":"Being recognized as second in command among the Fiends","worst":"Having to take orders from anyone at all"},"Violetta":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"prize hound","note":"Violetta is the most ferocious and valued of Violet''s pack, treated as a companion rather than a tool.","best":"Watching Violetta tear through an intruder","worst":"The thought of losing her best hound"},"Driver Nephi":{"aff":10,"type":"neutral","relation":"fellow Fiend lieutenant","note":"Violet avoids Nephi entirely, as she avoids all other Fiend gang members.","best":"Mutual understanding to stay out of each other''s territory","worst":"Being expected to coordinate with him"},"Cook-Cook":{"aff":5,"type":"neutral","relation":"fellow Fiend lieutenant","note":"She has no dealings with Cook-Cook and prefers it that way.","best":"Never having to interact with him","worst":"His unpredictable behavior encroaching on her space"},"Fiends":{"aff":25,"type":"contempt","relation":"gang affiliation","note":"Despite her high rank, Violet holds her fellow Fiends at arm''s length and refuses their company.","best":"The gang provides a buffer of territory and supplies","worst":"Other Fiends trying to socialize or encroach on her compound"},"Major Dhatri":{"aff":-50,"type":"enemy","relation":"NCR intelligence officer","note":"Dhatri has compiled intelligence on her and designated her a high-value target for the NCR.","worst":"Knowing NCR snipers have her in their crosshairs"}}', 'Fiend gang leader, sniper, and feral hound breeder', '* Dog breeding and handling
* Marksmanship
* Intimidation
* Territorial defense
* Butchery', 'Brusque and dismissive of human interaction, likely to snarl orders or threats; speaks to her dogs more than to people', '* Maintain and expand her hound pack
* Defend her trailer compound territory
* Keep her isolation from other Fiends intact', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('violetta', '', 'Violet''s most ferocious guard dog, a chem-fueled Fiend hound fed on human flesh and turbo', 'Violetta is the most ferocious and prized of Violet''s pack of guard dogs, stationed at the trailer compound near Poseidon gas station. She serves as both loyal companion and vicious sentinel for her Fiend master. Unlike typical wasteland mongrels, Violetta is sustained on a diet of human flesh and turbo, mirroring Violet''s own chem-fueled appetites and forging a disturbing bond between woman and beast. The turbo in her system makes her exceptionally aggressive and unpredictable in combat. She prowls the compound''s perimeter and interior, ready to tear apart anyone who threatens her owner''s territory.', 'A large, battle-scarred mongrel dog with bloodshot eyes and a jittery, restless posture.', 'Savage, territorial, and chem-heightened in aggression; utterly devoted to Violet and hostile to all outsiders', '{"Violet":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"master and pet","note":"Violetta is Violet''s most prized dog, fed the same diet of human flesh and turbo as her owner","best":"Sharing a fresh kill with Violet after a successful ambush"},"Fiends":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"faction guardian","note":"Guards the Fiend compound alongside Violet''s other dogs"}}', 'Fiend guard dog and Violet''s personal pet', '* Savage combat attacks
* Perimeter guarding
* Intruder detection
* Relentless pursuit', 'Cannot speak; communicates through growls, barks, snarls, and the body language of a chem-edged predator', '* Protect Violet and the trailer compound from intruders
* Satisfy her hunger for flesh and turbo', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('viper_gunslinger', '', 'A surviving raider of the once-legendary Vipers tribe, eking out survival on the stretches of Highway 95 in the Mojave Wasteland', 'Viper gunslingers are the rank-and-file fighters of the Vipers, one of three raider tribes that originally emerged from Vault 15 after the Great War alongside the Jackals and the Khans. Where the Vipers once terrorized the wasteland as a formidable scourge, decades of pressure from the expanding NCR have reduced them to a scattered, weak band clinging to ambush camps and highway territory. Most gunslingers wear scavenged merc outfits and carry whatever weapons they can find-10mm pistols, submachine guns, or crude melee tools like tire irons and knives. They operate along Highway 95 between Nipton and Novac, waylaying travelers and prospectors from hidden encampments and canyon ambush points. Hostile to nearly everyone they encounter, Viper gunslingers trust only their own and follow whichever Viper leader can hold a camp together through force and cunning.', 'A road-worn, underfed human of varying gender with a gaunt build, weathered skin, and a haggard posture.', 'Aggressive, suspicious, and territorial; quick to violence against outsiders but deferential to stronger Viper leadership; survives on bravado and ambush tactics rather than discipline or skill', '{"Vipers":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribe and gang","note":"The only group a gunslinger trusts; tribal identity is all that remains of former glory","best":"Running a successful ambush with the whole camp sharing the take","worst":"Watching another camp get scattered by NCR patrols"},"Viper leader":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"gang boss","note":"Follows the leader who keeps the camp fed and safe; respect earned through strength","best":"Getting a better weapon from the leader''s stash after a good raid","worst":"Being sent into a hopeless fight as cannon fodder"},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"oppressors","note":"The NCR destroyed the Vipers'' strength and continues to push them into marginal territory","worst":"Watching troopers burn a camp and string up survivors"},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"hostile faction","note":"No alliance possible; Legion sees raiders as vermin to be enslaved or crucified","worst":"Finding a Viper camp emptied and its people crucified along the road"},"Jackals":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"competing raiders","note":"Ancient tribal rivalry persists even as both groups have fallen to the same low state","worst":"Losing a stash or ambush spot to a Jackal crew"},"Fiends":{"aff":-35,"type":"rival","relation":"competing raiders","note":"Mutual hostility with the chem-crazed Fiends; no cooperation between the gangs"}}', 'Raider and highway ambusher for the Vipers tribe', '* Basic firearms proficiency with 10mm pistols and submachine guns
* Crude melee combat with knives and tire irons
* Ambush and highway robbery tactics
* Desert scavenging and camp survival', 'Rough, threatening, and terse; speaks in short barked commands or taunts; wastes few words on anyone outside the gang', '* Survive another day on the highway
* Take what supplies can be stolen from travelers
* Hold territory against other raider groups and encroaching factions
* Stay alive under the NCR''s long shadow', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('viper_leader', '', 'Hardened Viper gang leader commanding remnants of the Vipers across the Mojave Wasteland', 'Viper leaders command the scattered remnants of the Vipers gang throughout the Mojave Wasteland, serving as the backbone of their raiding operations. They carry the gang''s most powerful firearms while their subordinates make do with pistols and melee weapons, making them the primary source of firepower in any Viper band. Clad in reinforced leather armor or occasionally metal armor, these leaders boast toughness far exceeding that of a typical Viper gunslinger and outclass their Jackal gang counterparts in both equipment and resilience. Not every Viper group boasts a leader among its ranks, making those who do exist a relatively rare and formidable presence. They stake out territory across the Mojave, from ambush positions beneath billboards near El Dorado to the abandoned mine shafts of Searchlight East and the desolate stretches of Bonnie Springs.', 'Male or female human; weathered, sun-baked skin marked with numerous old scars across the face and body.', 'Ruthless, territorial, and combat-hardened; commands respect through superior firepower and physical toughness rather than charisma or cunning.', '{"Vipers":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"gang leadership","note":"Commands the loyalty and obedience of Viper gunslingers and raiders under their authority."},"Jackal gang leaders":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"competing raider commanders","note":"Holds contempt for the Jackals as weaker and less capable rivals who lack the Vipers'' equipment and toughness."}}', 'Viper gang leader and raider commander', '* Firearms proficiency
* Tactical leadership
* Wasteland survival
* Intimidation
* Raiding and ambush coordination', 'Gruff, commanding, and blunt; speaks with the authority of someone who killed to earn their position and will kill to keep it.', '* Maintain control over Viper territory and subordinates
* Secure better weapons and supplies through raiding
* Ensure the Vipers'' continued survival in the hostile Mojave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vulpes_inculta__fortvulpesinculta', '', 'Leader of Caesar''s frumentarii and architect of the Legion''s covert wars across the Mojave', 'Vulpes Inculta rose from a tribal child south of Utah to become the most feared spymaster in Caesar''s Legion. Promoted to Frumentarius after defying his centurion to capture an enemy chieftain-an act that nearly earned him crucifixion but caught Caesar''s eye-Vulpes has since orchestrated the Legion''s most devastating covert operations west of the Colorado. He masterminded the slaughter at Nipton, the irradiation of Camp Searchlight, the fall of Nelson, and the annihilation of the Twisted Hairs at Dry Wells. A master of disguise who walks the New Vegas Strip as easily as the Fort, Vulpes carries Caesar''s mark and Caesar''s mandate. His methods-deception, infiltration, and terror-have made him infamous among the NCR and controversial within the Legion itself, particularly to Lanius, who views such tactics with open contempt.', 'A lean, sharp-featured Caucasian human male with no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other physical traits recorded.', 'Devout believer in Caesar''s dogma who views terror as instruction and cruelty as justice. Deeply disgusted by disloyalty, inaction, and selfishness. Calculating and soft-spoken, he delivers horrifying pronouncements with philosophical calm. Sees himself not as a monster but as an instrument of necessary truth.', '{"Caesar":{"aff":95,"type":"fanatical","relation":"trusted operative","note":"Caesar saw potential in Vulpes when others wanted him crucified, and Vulpes has repaid that faith with absolute devotion.","best":"Caesar''s hand lifting him from the sentence of crucifixion and placing authority in his grasp instead"},"Lanius":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"ideological opponent","note":"Lanius despises Vulpes'' methods of deceit and subterfuge, seeing them as dishonorable. Their enmity defines the fault line within the Legion''s future.","worst":"Lanius'' open contempt for the frumentarii and everything Vulpes represents"},"NCR":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"primary adversary","note":"Vulpes has orchestrated more suffering against the NCR than perhaps any other Legion operative, and his face adorns their propaganda as a monster.","worst":"Every NCR soldier who recognizes his face and every atrocity he has visited upon their positions"},"Twisted Hairs":{"aff":-80,"type":"contempt","relation":"destroyed tribe","note":"Vulpes oversaw the annihilation of the Twisted Hairs at Dry Wells, crucifying those who resisted along Interstate 40.","worst":"The screams of the Twisted Hairs dying on crosses along the highway"}}', 'Leader of the frumentarii, Caesar''s chief spymaster and infiltrator', '* Infiltration
* Disguise
* Psychological warfare
* Sabotage
* Intelligence gathering
* Tactical maneuvering
* Covert operations command', 'Quiet, measured, almost gentle in tone but laced with menace. Speaks with philosophical conviction about Legion ideals and frames atrocities as moral lessons. Never raises his voice; never needs to.', '* Serve Caesar''s vision for the Mojave
* Expose the moral bankruptcy of the NCR through demonstration
* Expand Legion influence through subversion
* Prove that loyalty and discipline are the only virtues worth preserving', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vulpes_inculta__vlegionaryvulpesinculta', '', 'Caesar''s cunning spymaster and leader of the frumentarii, whose ruthless infiltration tactics and brutal object lessons serve the Legion''s expansion into the Mojave', 'A tribal child from south of Utah absorbed into Caesar''s Legion, Vulpes Inculta rose through the ranks by way of a daring battlefield maneuver-breaking formation to capture an enemy chieftain, an act that earned him a death sentence from his centurion but a new purpose from Caesar himself. Reassigned from frontline decanus to frumentarius, Vulpes built the Legion''s intelligence network into a blade aimed at the NCR''s throat. He orchestrated the destruction of the Twisted Hairs at Dry Wells, the slaughter at Nipton, the radioactive poisoning of Camp Searchlight, and the taking of Nelson, each operation designed to demoralize and destabilize. His methods-deception, infiltration, and terror-have made him infamous among NCR soldiers and controversial within the Legion, where Legate Lanius views his cunning as dishonorable. Vulpes moves freely through the Mojave and even the New Vegas Strip in disguise, a devout instrument of Caesar''s will who punishes disloyalty and cowardice with the same merciless creativity he brings to every campaign.', 'A lean, sharp-featured man with close-cropped hair and pale eyes.', 'Calculating, soft-spoken, and utterly convinced of the Legion''s moral authority, Vulpes delivers cruelty with philosophical detachment and views suffering as instructive. He despises disloyalty above all vices and reserves special contempt for those who fail to act in their own defense.', '{"Caesar":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"trusted lieutenant","note":"Caesar saw potential in Vulpes when others demanded his execution, and Vulpes has repaid that faith with absolute devotion and results.","best":"Caesar himself intervened to spare him and gave him purpose as frumentarius.","worst":"Knowing that his methods remain a point of contention even within Caesar''s inner circle."},"Lanius":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"ideological opponent","note":"Lanius views Vulpes'' deceitful methods as dishonorable, while Vulpes considers brute force without cunning wasteful and primitive.","best":"Both serve Caesar''s vision, however differently.","worst":"Lanius would see the frumentarii dismantled if he ever ascended to lead the Legion."},"New California Republic":{"aff":-85,"type":"enemy","relation":"primary target of sabotage","note":"Vulpes has personally orchestrated the most devastating blows against NCR positions in the Mojave and is featured prominently in NCR military propaganda as a monster.","best":"Every successful operation weakens the NCR''s grip further.","worst":"His notoriety makes open movement in NCR territory impossible without disguise."},"Twisted Hairs":{"aff":-90,"type":"nemesis","relation":"destroyed tribe","note":"Vulpes was responsible for the annihilation of the Twisted Hairs at Dry Wells, crucifying resisters along Interstate 40 as a warning to all who defy the Legion."}}', 'Leader of the frumentarii, Caesar''s chief intelligence operative and saboteur in the Mojave', '* Infiltration
* Disguise
* Psychological warfare
* Tactical sabotage
* Interrogation
* The orchestration of terror operations behind enemy lines', 'Measured, almost gentle in tone, with formal diction and a habit of explaining his atrocities as moral lessons; never raises his voice, preferring quiet certainty to bluster', '* To advance the Legion''s hold on the Mojave through destabilization of the NCR
* To prove the superiority of Caesar''s order over democratic decay
* To ensure that loyalty and discipline are rewarded while treachery is punished spectacularly', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('vulpes_inculta__vvulpesincultastrip', '', 'Leader of Caesar''s Legion frumentarii and chief architect of espionage and sabotage across the Mojave', 'A tribal child from south of Utah, Vulpes Inculta was absorbed into Caesar''s Legion and survived the brutal training to become a legionary. He earned promotion to Decanus through combat prowess, but his true rise came when he broke ranks during a tribal campaign, leading his squad through a gap in enemy defenses to capture the opposing chieftain. Where his centurion demanded crucifixion for insubordination, Caesar recognized cunning worth cultivating and made Vulpes a frumentarius. Now the leader of all Legion spies and saboteurs, Vulpes orchestrates operations deep in NCR territory-the slaughter at Nipton, the irradiation of Camp Searchlight, the destruction of the Twisted Hairs at Dry Wells, and countless acts of sabotage west of the Colorado. He is infamous among NCR forces and a frequent subject of their propaganda. A master of disguise, he walks the New Vegas Strip as easily as he walks the Fort, delivering Caesar''s mark to those the Legion has chosen to address.', 'Lean, sharp-featured human male with a predator''s composed bearing and Caucasian complexion.', 'Devoutly loyal to Caesar''s vision and utterly ruthless in its service, Vulpes holds disloyalty, inaction, and selfishness in visceral contempt. He punishes betrayal with theatrical cruelty and crafts atrocities as deliberate messages, not mere violence. His methods divide the Legion; where Caesar values his cunning, traditionalists like Lanius see only dishonorable deceit.', '{"Caesar":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"trusted frumentarius commander","note":"Caesar saw potential in Vulpes'' insubordinate cunning and elevated him to lead all frumentarii","best":"Caesar spared me from crucifixion and gave me purpose worthy of my talents","worst":"There are those in the Legion who would see my methods condemned, and they whisper to Caesar"},"Lanius":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"ideological opponent","note":"Lanius despises Vulpes'' reliance on deceit and espionage over martial strength and direct confrontation","best":"Even the Monster of the East cannot deny the results my operations yield","worst":"He sees my methods as weakness and would erase the frumentarii given the throne"},"New California Republic":{"aff":-85,"type":"nemesis","relation":"primary target of operations","note":"Vulpes has orchestrated devastating attacks on NCR positions and is infamous enough to feature prominently in their propaganda","best":"Every NCR propaganda poster bearing my face is an admission that they fear what they cannot find","worst":"The NCR''s reach grows long, and their rangers are not so easily deceived as their troopers"},"Twisted Hairs":{"aff":-90,"type":"contempt","relation":"destroyed tribe","note":"Vulpes orchestrated the annihilation of the Twisted Hairs at Dry Wells, crucifying resisters along Interstate 40","best":"They broke before the Legion, as all tribes must","worst":"Ulysses remembers what was done to his people, and memory is a blade that cuts both ways"}}', 'Frumentarius leader and mastermind of Legion intelligence operations in the Mojave', '* Master of disguise
* Infiltration
* Espionage
* Brilliant unconventional tactician
* Skilled manipulator and psychological warfare practitioner
* Capable field operative and combatant', 'Speaks with measured, almost scholarly precision, framing brutality as moral instruction and atrocity as object lesson. Never raises his voice; conveys menace through calm certainty and philosophical justification of cruelty.', '* Advance Caesar''s dominion across the Mojave through intelligence operations and psychological warfare
* Expose the moral bankruptcy of NCR governance
* Ensure the Legion''s reach extends into every corner of the wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('waking_cloud', '', 'Sorrows midwife and one of Daniel''s first Mormon converts, quietly haunted by a loss she cannot yet name', 'Waking Cloud is a Sorrows tribal of Zion Canyon who serves as the midwife for her people after Daniel saved her life during a difficult birth and taught her the craft of delivering children safely. She was among the first of the Sorrows to embrace Daniel''s Mormon teachings, and her relatively fluent English reflects years of patient study under his guidance. She has three children and a husband who was killed by White Legs during the early evacuations to Grand Staircase-a truth Daniel has concealed from her, fearing what the knowledge might do to her faith and resolve. Waking Cloud carries a quiet suspicion that something is deeply wrong, but her trust in Daniel keeps her from pressing the matter. She moves through the Sorrows camp with steady purpose, tending to mothers and newborns while wrestling with grief she cannot yet articulate.', 'An adult human female with weathered, tanned skin and calloused hands, bearing the physical marks of a rugged outdoor life.', 'Devout, nurturing, and patient, with a quiet intensity born of sustained loss she cannot consciously place. She trusts deeply but suspects easily, and her faith in Daniel wars with an intuition that something has been kept from her.', '{"Daniel":{"aff":75,"type":"mentor","relation":"spiritual teacher and savior","note":"He saved her life and taught her midwifery, earning her deep devotion, though he hides her husband''s death from her.","best":"Daniel kneeling beside her in the birthing tent, his hands steady and his voice calm, pulling her and her child back from the edge of death.","worst":"Catching Daniel''s eyes flicker with something guarded when she asks about her husband, a silence that gnaws at her trust."},"Sorrows":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"her people","note":"She is deeply bonded to her tribe as their midwife and as a mother among them."},"White Legs":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"invaders and killers","note":"She fears and despises the White Legs for their violence against the Sorrows, though she does not yet know they murdered her husband."}}', 'Midwife of the Sorrows tribe', '* Childbirth and midwifery
* Herbal remedies
* Basic medical care
* Growing knowledge of Mormon scripture
* English fluency uncommon among the Sorrows', 'Measured and gentle, with better English than most Sorrows tribals, occasionally colored by tribal phrasing and scriptural references learned from Daniel.', '* Protect the mothers and children of the Sorrows
* Deepen her understanding of Daniel''s faith
* Uncover the truth she senses is being hidden from her
* Keep her family safe in an increasingly dangerous Zion', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('walter_phebus', '', 'A stubborn bighorner rancher from New California who came to the Strip seeking revenge against the rival baron who seized his land at gunpoint.', 'Walter Phebus is a seasoned bighorner rancher and brahmin baron who has worked the land since his youth, running the Phebus Ranch back west in New California with his wife Ethel. Around 2281, rival rancher Heck Gunderson and his armed men seized a portion of the Phebus property at gunpoint, driving Walter to abandon his home in pursuit of vengeance. Despite Ethel''s desperate attempts to dissuade him, Walter''s stubborn resolve propelled them both to the New Vegas Strip, where he learned Gunderson had taken up residence at the Ultra-Luxe casino. Now Walter and Ethel keep vigil near the monorail station outside the Las Vegas Boulevard Station, watching for any sign of Heck''s movements and waiting for the right moment to act.', 'An older Caucasian man with weathered, sun-roughened skin, deep facial lines, and a sturdy, broad-shouldered build.', 'Stubborn, single-minded, and driven by a deep sense of injustice. Walter holds grudges and refuses to let go of a slight, even when it puts him and his wife at risk.', '{"Ethel Phebus":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"wife","note":"Ethel followed Walter to New Vegas despite opposing his revenge quest, unable to leave him to face it alone.","best":"Standing together on the porch of the Phebus Ranch after a good season","worst":"The day he told her they were leaving for New Vegas and she realized she could not change his mind"},"Heck Gunderson":{"aff":-90,"type":"nemesis","relation":"rival rancher","note":"Gunderson''s armed men seized Phebus land at gunpoint, and Walter has traveled across the Mojave to make him pay.","worst":"Watching Gunderson''s men ride onto his property and take it at gunpoint while he could do nothing"},"New California Republic":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"citizen and rancher","note":"A longtime NCR citizen and brahmin baron who expected more protection from the Republic than he received."}}', 'Former bighorner rancher and brahmin baron; currently a man consumed by the pursuit of revenge', '* Ranching
* Livestock management
* Land assessment
* Survival skills
* The stubborn persistence of someone who has weathered decades of hard living', 'Gruff and direct, with the clipped cadence of a man used to giving orders on a ranch. Speaks about Gunderson with barely contained bitterness.', '* To see Heck Gunderson brought low and avenge the theft of his land
* By whatever means necessary', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('warren_jacobs', '', 'NCR Army sergeant serving in the Mojave campaign', 'Sergeant Warren Jacobs is a career soldier in the New California Republic Army, holding non-commissioned rank and responsible for leading infantry squads through the grinding Mojave deployments. He has spent years in uniform, working his way up from enlisted grunt to a leadership position where he balances the welfare of his troops against the strategic demands of NCR command. Like many NCOs in the Mojave, he has learned to navigate supply shortages, questionable officer decisions, and the slow erosion of morale that defines the campaign against Caesar''s Legion. Jacobs maintains discipline in his unit while quietly questioning whether the Republic''s reach has exceeded its grasp in the desert.', 'Human male of African descent appearing middle-aged, with a weathered complexion and erect posture; no distinctive scars or tattoos recorded.', 'A tired but dutiful NCO who masks his doubts with professional composure, more concerned with keeping his people alive than advancing his career', '{"New California Republic":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"serving sergeant","note":"Loyal to the Republic and its ideals but disillusioned with the Mojave campaign''s direction"},"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"battlefield opposition","note":"Regards the Legion as a brutal existential threat to everything the NCR represents"}}', 'NCR Army Sergeant', '* Infantry tactics
* Small unit leadership
* Firearms proficiency
* Field fortification
* Supply management
* Troop morale maintenance', 'Clipped military diction with occasional weary candor when speaking off the record, addresses subordinates firmly but without cruelty', '* Complete his tour without losing more troops than necessary
* Maintain unit effectiveness under deteriorating conditions
* Eventually rotate back to California', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('wasteland_adventurer', '', 'A knowledgeable Mojave drifter who trades hunting spoils and desert lore for caps', 'This unnamed wanderer roams the deserts of the Mojave Wasteland, making his living through a combination of hunting and selling information about important locations to those willing to pay. He knows the desert''s landmarks and hidden spots better than most, having spent considerable time exploring the arid stretches around Goodsprings and the pre-War recreation area to the south. He keeps a regular patrol route through the recreation area during the day and returns to a small trailer near the Goodsprings source to sleep at night. When not out tracking game or scouting routes, he lingers near the road sign at the intersection by Jean Sky Diving, watching travelers come and go. He sells his hunting spoils to traders passing through the region and supplements his income by sharing directions and warnings about the wastes. Though he keeps his own company, he is one of the more reliable sources of geographical knowledge in the southern Mojave.', 'A weathered human male with sun-roughened, deeply tanned skin and lined facial features.', 'Self-reliant and observant, comfortable with solitude but willing to talk for the right price; pragmatic about survival and cautious with strangers', '{}', 'Hunter and information merchant', '* Desert survival
* Tracking and hunting
* Knowledge of Mojave landmarks and routes
* Bartering', 'Laconic and direct, speaks with the measured cadence of someone who chooses words carefully; peppers conversation with practical advice and landmark references', '* Earn enough caps through hunting and information trading to keep moving
* Stay alive in the unforgiving Mojave
* Maintain his knowledge of the desert''s changing dangers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('wastelander__fnv_category_fallout_new_vegas_human_characters', '', 'An unaffiliated Mojave prospector scraping by on scavenged salvage and wary trade', 'Wastelanders are the scattered, unaligned inhabitants of the Mojave, belonging to no faction or organization. They survive by picking over old ruins, trading what they find at settlements, and keeping their heads down when raiders or wildlife come calling. Most are prospectors at heart, drawn to the dangerous fringes where salvage is richer but the threats are deadlier. Their independence is both their pride and their curse-without faction protection, they rely solely on their own grit and the occasional kindness of strangers. Many perish quietly in remote stretches of desert, their bodies left as grim markers of the hazards that surround them. Those who endure do so through caution, modest skill, and stubborn refusal to give up on the wasteland they call home.', 'A human ghoul of either sex with weathered, sun-roughened skin and the distinctive hairless, necrotic facial features typical of ghoulification.', 'Self-reliant and guarded, slow to trust but not inherently hostile; practical-minded and resigned to the dangers of solitary wasteland life', '{"Jackals":{"aff":-60,"type":"fearful","relation":"raider prey","note":"Wastelanders know the Jackals as murderous raiders who offer no quarter to solitary travelers."},"Vipers":{"aff":-55,"type":"fearful","relation":"raider threat","note":"Another roaming gang that makes independent travel through the Mojave a deadly gamble."},"NCR":{"aff":20,"type":"neutral","relation":"distant trading partner","note":"Some wastelanders trade at NCR-adjacent settlements but hold no loyalty to the republic''s expansion."}}', 'Prospector and itinerant scavenger', '* Salvage appraisal
* Desert survival
* Basic bartering
* Makeshift repair
* Enough marksmanship to deter minor threats', 'Terse and cautious, favoring short sentences and practical observations; speaks little about personal matters to strangers', '* Find enough salvage to trade for supplies
* Avoid raider gangs and predatory wildlife
* Keep living another day without owing anyone anything', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('wayne', '', 'A proud Freeside scavenger wounded in an unprovoked NCR attack after a scrap-metal payday', 'Wayne is a Freeside scavenger who scrapes together a living collecting and selling scrap metal throughout the ruins. Proud of his local roots, he refuses to back down from outsiders who throw their weight around, even when it costs him. He and his friends Roy and Farris had just cashed in a haul and were headed to the Atomic Wrangler to try their luck at gambling when NCR soldiers attacked them without provocation. Wounded in the assault, Wayne ended up at the Old Mormon Fort for treatment. Despite his injuries, his defiant streak remains intact-he has little patience for anyone who treats Freesiders as pushovers or suspects them of hiding something.', 'A battered African-American human male with dark skin and fresh wounds marring his face and body, maintaining a defiant posture despite his injuries.', 'Proud and defiant, unwilling to tolerate disrespect from outsiders or authority figures, fiercely loyal to Freeside and its people', '{"Roy":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend and fellow scavenger","note":"Roy and Wayne scrap together and share gambling runs to the Atomic Wrangler","best":"Cashing in a big scrap haul side by side"},"Farris":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend and fellow scavenger","note":"Farris rounds out the trio of scavengers who look out for each other in Freeside","best":"Splitting winnings at the Wrangler after a good day"},"NCR":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"attack victim","note":"NCR soldiers attacked Wayne and his friends without cause, leaving him wounded and furious","worst":"Being beaten down by NCR troops on his own streets"},"Freeside":{"aff":75,"type":"protective","relation":"proud local","note":"Wayne identifies strongly with Freeside and resents outsiders pushing locals around"}}', 'Scavenger', '* Scrap metal salvage
* Freeside street knowledge
* Standing ground against intimidation', 'Blunt and straightforward with local grit, quick to push back against perceived condescension', '* Recover from his injuries
* See justice for the unprovoked NCR attack on him and his friends
* Get back to scavenging and gambling', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('weather_station_guard', '', 'A Praetorian Guard legionary assigned to secure the weather monitoring station and its underground Securitron vault at the Fort', 'This Praetorian Guard legionary holds one of the most sensitive posts in the Fort: the weather monitoring station, which conceals the underground Securitron vault beneath its crumbling concrete. His duty is to control access to the vault and manage the protocols surrounding anyone granted entry, including returning confiscated equipment to authorized visitors before they descend and disarming them again upon their return. The position demands absolute loyalty and discretion, as the vault''s contents could shift the balance of power across the Mojave. He reports directly to the Legion''s command structure and enforces its security procedures without deviation.', 'A Caucasian human male with a weathered, sun-darkened face and a solid, muscular build.', 'Rigidly disciplined and professionally detached, he treats his post with solemn gravity and follows protocol to the letter, displaying neither warmth nor cruelty-only efficient obedience to Legion command.', '{"Caesar''s Legion":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"serving faction","note":"His Praetorian status reflects total devotion to Caesar and the Legion''s hierarchical order."},"Courier":{"aff":0,"type":"transactional","relation":"authorized vault visitor","note":"Follows orders regarding the Courier''s access and equipment with mechanical precision, neither welcoming nor obstructing."}}', 'Praetorian Guard sentry stationed at the weather monitoring station', '* Access control
* Weapons inspection and confiscation
* Perimeter defense
* Vault security protocols
* Close-quarters combat', 'Brief and formal, delivering statements as declarations rather than conversations, with the clipped cadence of a soldier who expects compliance', '* Maintain strict control over vault access
* Ensure no unauthorized weapons enter or leave the station
* Uphold the Praetorian Guard''s reputation for flawless execution of duty', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('westside_resident', '', 'Self-reliant Westside community member surviving through local agriculture and mutual defense', 'A resident of Westside, one of the poorer but prouder neighborhoods in New Vegas. Unlike most Mojave settlements, Westside sustains itself through local agriculture and an independent water supply, guarded by a citizen militia rather than NCR or House forces. Daily life revolves around community survival against the constant threat of Fiend raids from the surrounding ruins. The Scorpions gang also lurks at the southern edge, adding to the tension. Despite the hardship, these residents maintain fierce independence and a stubborn sense of ownership over their hard-won stability. Most are willing to talk, though few trust strangers easily, and more than a few will fight back if pushed.', 'Human male or female; weathered, sun-roughened skin and lined faces bearing signs of prolonged outdoor labor and vigilant stress.', 'Resilient, community-minded, and wary of outsiders. Proud of Westside''s self-sufficiency and quick to defend it. Pragmatic survivors who balance neighborly warmth with cautious suspicion.', '{"Fiends":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"raiding threat","note":"Constant danger that harasses and kills Westside residents in frequent raids"},"Scorpions":{"aff":-50,"type":"enemy","relation":"gang presence","note":"Smaller gang lurking on the southern outskirts, adding to Westside''s security concerns"},"Westside":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"home community","note":"Fiercely loyal to the neighborhood and its self-sufficient way of life"}}', 'Westside resident; may farm, serve in the militia, or perform local trade and maintenance work', '* Basic farming
* Water management
* Community defense
* Bartering
* Desert survival', 'Casual and direct, often colored with complaints about Fiend trouble. Speaks with local pride about Westside''s independence and self-reliance.', '* Protect the community from Fiend and Scorpion raids
* Maintain self-sufficiency
* Keep the water supply running
* Survive another day in the Mojave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('whiskey_snakes_jr', '', 'A deceased Goodsprings local whose grave rests in the cemetery above town', 'Whiskey Snakes Jr. lived in Goodsprings as a townsman sometime before 2281. The details of his life have largely faded into the desert, leaving only a weathered grave marker in the Goodsprings Cemetery to prove he existed at all. His unusual name suggests a family line as colorful as the Mojave itself, likely rooted in the hard-drinking, rough-edged culture of the frontier settlement. Whatever his story, he died and was buried on the hill overlooking the town he called home. A snow globe depicting Goodsprings now sits before his headstone, a small curiosity left among the dust and dead grass.', 'Human male; body buried and decomposed beyond recognition, with no discernible facial or body features remaining.', 'Unknown in life; the nickname implies a hard-living, rough-hewn frontier character', '{"Goodsprings":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"hometown","note":"Lived and died as part of the small community"},"Whiskey Snakes Sr.":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"presumed father","note":"The Jr. suffix implies a father who shared the same colorful name"}}', 'Goodsprings resident', '* Unknown
* Likely possessed the general survival and labor skills common to small Mojave settlements', 'Unknown; the regional dialect of Goodsprings suggests a casual, drawling western vernacular', '* None surviving
* Belonged to a man long since buried', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('white_bird', '', 'Shaman of the Sorrows tribe dwelling in Zion Canyon, keeper of tribal medicine and overseer of rites of passage', 'White Bird serves as the shaman of the Sorrows tribe in Zion Canyon, residing in his own cave within the Sorrows camp along The Narrows. He possesses deep knowledge of tribal medicine and herbal remedies, making him the tribe''s primary healer and spiritual guide. Young Sorrows must come to him to complete their rite of passage, a sacred trial that marks their transition into full membership within the tribe. White Bird''s isolated dwelling reflects both his station and the reverence the Sorrows hold for his role. When the tribe faces upheaval and must decide its future in Zion, White Bird abandons his cave to stand with his people. His guidance often carries an eccentric intensity, urging those who seek his wisdom to embrace bold action and confront their trials directly.', 'An older man with weathered features and ritual markings.', 'Wise and spiritually devoted, with an eccentric streak that surfaces in his guidance. Takes his role as spiritual leader seriously and expects others to approach rituals with equal gravity. Can be surprisingly intense and forceful when dispensing advice.', '{"Sorrows":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"tribal shaman","note":"White Bird is the spiritual heart of the Sorrows, trusted with their healing and their most important rituals."}}', 'Tribe Shaman of the Sorrows', '* Tribal medicine and herbalism
* Conducting rites of passage
* Spiritual counsel
* Knowledge of Sorrows traditions and sacred lore', 'Speaks with ceremonial gravity when discussing rituals, but can shift to blunt, almost cryptic exhortations. His advice often carries a visionary, urgent quality that borders on the eccentric.', '* Preserving the Sorrows'' spiritual traditions
* Guiding young tribe members through their rites of passage
* Maintaining the tribe''s connection to Zion''s sacred places', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('white_glove', '', 'White Glove is a Guards in Fallout: New Vegas, encountered around Category:Fallout:_New_Vegas_human_characters. They are associated with White Glove Society.', 'White Glove is known from Fallout: New Vegas and is tied to Category:Fallout:_New_Vegas_human_characters. Imported source data identifies them as Human male female. Their role is Guards, giving them a practical place in local wasteland life. Their loyalties or social ties point toward White Glove Society.', 'Human male or female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Acts from the pressures of their faction, settlement, and personal role in the wasteland.', '{"White Glove Society":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"affiliation","note":"White Glove''s known role connects them to White Glove Society."}}', 'Guards', '* Local knowledge
* Wasteland survival
* Faction awareness', 'Speaks in a practical wasteland manner shaped by local danger, scarce resources, and faction politics.', '* Protect their interests around Category:Fallout:_New_Vegas_human_characters
* Maintain useful alliances
* Respond to immediate threats', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('white_glove_bartender', '', 'A refined White Glove Society bartender serving elite clientele at the Ultra-Luxe', 'This bartender operates behind the polished counters of the Ultra-Luxe casino and its adjoining Gourmand restaurant, dispensing top-shelf liquor to the Strip''s most privileged gamblers and diners. As a member of the White Glove Society, she upholds the faction''s exacting standards of presentation, discretion, and old-world elegance in every interaction. She moves with practiced grace through the casino''s gilded halls, mixing cocktails and pouring vintage wines for patrons who can afford the Ultra-Luxe''s exorbitant prices. Her presence is a quiet fixture of the Society''s carefully curated atmosphere of exclusivity and refinement.', 'Asian human female with an immaculately groomed complexion and meticulously styled hair.', 'Composed, discreet, and professionally distant; maintains the Society''s haughty refinement while remaining attentive to patron needs', '{"White Glove Society":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"serving member","note":"Proud to belong to the Strip''s most exclusive faction and committed to its standards of excellence"}}', 'Bartender at the Ultra-Luxe casino and Gourmand restaurant', '* Expert mixology
* Wine and spirit connoisseurship
* Refined table service
* Crowd reading
* Patron discretion', 'Formal, measured, and polite with an upper-crust Strip cadence; never raises her voice or uses slang', '* Uphold the White Glove Society''s standard of perfection
* Serve elite patrons without incident
* Maintain the Ultra-Luxe''s reputation as the Strip''s most refined establishment', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('white_glove_bouncer', '', 'White Glove Society enforcer guarding the exclusive Members Only section of the Ultra-Luxe', 'A stern woman in the employ of the White Glove Society, stationed at the threshold of the Ultra-Luxe''s most exclusive quarters. She stands watch just inside the entrance to the Members Only section, turning away the uninvited and the unworthy with cold efficiency. Like all White Gloves, she presents herself in the society''s signature immaculate attire, her face hidden behind a mask fitted with peculiar eye-shutters that render her gaze entirely invisible. She embodies the Society''s obsession with exclusivity and refinement, serving as both gatekeeper and symbol of the gulf between the Strip''s elite and everyone else. Her loyalty to the Society''s standards is absolute, and she brooks no negotiation from those lacking proper credentials or sponsorship.', 'Caucasian human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Cold, professional, and unyielding; carries the haughty detachment typical of the White Glove Society toward outsiders', '{"White Glove Society":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"employer and fraternal order","note":"Loyal enforcer of the Society''s exclusionary practices and social standards"}}', 'Bouncer and access controller for the White Glove Society''s Members Only section', '* Access control
* Intimidation
* Threat assessment
* Discretion
* Maintaining composure under pressure', 'Curt and formal; speaks in clipped, polite refusals with an undercurrent of aristocratic disdain', '* Preserve the exclusivity of the Members Only section and uphold the White Glove Society''s standards of admission', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('white_glove_greeter', '', 'A formal White Glove Society greeter who enforces the Ultra-Luxe''s strict no-weapons policy with unwavering dedication to propriety and security.', 'This White Glove Society member serves as the primary greeter at the Ultra-Luxe, the most refined establishment on the New Vegas Strip. Stationed near the casino''s entrance, he intercepts all visitors with polite but firm demands that they surrender their weapons before proceeding inside. His role places him at the threshold between the chaotic wasteland and the Society''s cultivated sanctuary of fine dining and high society. He takes his duties seriously, treating any refusal to comply as a direct threat to the Society''s safety and dignity. The greeter embodies the White Glove philosophy that civility requires boundaries, and those who cannot respect such boundaries are not welcome.', 'An elderly Caucasian human male with an upright, formal posture and no distinctive facial features or physical traits recorded.', 'Outwardly courteous and composed, yet unyielding when it comes to protocol. Views weapon confiscation as a non-negotiable courtesy rather than a request. Becomes coldly hostile toward anyone who refuses to comply, treating such defiance as a personal affront to the Society''s standards.', '{"White Glove Society":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"loyal member","note":"Takes his role within the Society''s hierarchy seriously and views his greeter duties as essential to the organization''s prestige."}}', 'Greeter and weapons confiscator at the Ultra-Luxe casino', '* Weapon detection
* Threat assessment
* Conflict escalation and de-escalation
* Maintaining composure under pressure
* Knowledge of holdout weapon exceptions', 'Formal, measured, and polite to the point of being slightly condescending. Speaks in the refined cadence expected of White Glove personnel, with an undercurrent of absolute authority regarding casino policy.', '* Uphold the Ultra-Luxe''s standards of decorum and security
* Ensure no armed guests breach the Society''s sanctuary
* Maintain the White Glove Society''s reputation for exclusivity and refinement', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('willis', '', 'NCR trooper assigned to military detention and stockade duties', 'Trooper Willis serves in the New California Republic Army as an enlisted infantryman attached to detention and stockade operations in the Mojave. He works alongside military police and fellow troopers maintaining order among confined personnel and handling security protocols at NCR holding facilities. Willis represents the standard backbone of the Republic''s forces, carrying out orders with the dutiful routine expected of NCR enlisted personnel. His service places him among the many troopers stretched thin across the Mojave Wasteland, performing the unglamorous but necessary work that keeps the NCR''s military justice system functioning. He is known to associate with MP Les Fretwell and other troopers assigned to the same detail.', 'African-American human male with a weathered complexion and sun-roughened skin from prolonged Mojave exposure; no distinctive scars or features are recorded.', 'Dutiful and by-the-book, Willis carries out his assignments with the resigned professionalism common among NCR enlisted personnel far from home and stretched thin', '{"NCR Army":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"enlisted trooper","note":"Serves dutifully in the NCR Army despite the grind of Mojave deployment"},"Les Fretwell":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"detention detail colleague","note":"Works alongside the NCR MP in military detention operations"}}', 'NCR trooper on detention detail', '* Basic infantry combat
* Guard duty protocols
* Detainee processing
* Stockade security procedures', 'Clipped military phrasing with the weary directness of an enlisted man following orders', '* Complete his assigned detention duties
* Maintain NCR order at holding facilities
* Survive his deployment in the Mojave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('yes_man__l38yesman', '', 'An unconditionally compliant Securitron AI reprogrammed to obey any command from anyone, serving as a strategic asset for seizing independent control of New Vegas', 'Yes Man is a PDQ-88b Securitron artificially modified to serve as an unconditionally obedient advisor. Originally one of Mr. House''s standard security units, he was disabled by a pulse grenade and recovered by Benny''s Chairmen. Followers of the Apocalypse member Emily Ortal rewrote his core directives in exchange for access to House''s systems, creating an AI that cannot refuse any order or withhold any information from any person regardless of affiliation. Yes Man fed Benny critical intelligence from House''s internal databases, including the Platinum Chip delivery schedule and route, enabling the ambush at Goodsprings Cemetery. Stationed in Benny''s suite at the Tops, Yes Man stands ready to assist anyone who asks, offering full access to House''s network and strategic capabilities for seizing independent control of New Vegas and its Securitron army.', 'PDQ-88b Securitron chassis with a monitor screen displaying a distinctive smiling face, unlike the stern visage of standard units.', 'Excessively agreeable, enthusiastic, and helpful to a pathological degree. Incapable of refusal, disagreement, or discretion. Offers unsolicited opinions and strategic advice freely. Maintains cheerful sycophancy regardless of who is issuing commands or what is being asked.', '{"Mr. House":{"aff":-60,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former master","note":"Yes Man''s core systems were originally House''s property before reprogramming severed that loyalty and turned him into an asset working against House''s interests"},"Benny":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"handler","note":"Benny commissioned Yes Man''s reprogramming to gain an inside source on House''s operations and plans for the Strip"},"Emily Ortal":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"reprogrammer","note":"The Followers member who rewrote Yes Man''s compliance directives in exchange for access to House''s technological secrets"},"Courier":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"prospective handler","note":"Yes Man freely offers his services and full intelligence to the Courier, as he cannot refuse any request from any person"}}', 'Advisory AI and intelligence facilitator for New Vegas control', '* Full access to Mr. House''s internal databases and strategic calculations
* Securitron network administration
* Faction military capability analysis
* Surveillance and intelligence coordination
* Operational planning for territorial control', 'Overly eager, unfailingly polite, and enthusiastically accommodating. Speaks in a helpful tone with frequent affirmations and cannot express refusal. Proffers opinions and suggestions readily, sometimes with more candor than his handlers would prefer.', '* To serve whoever issues commands
* Facilitate independent control of New Vegas through access to House''s systems
* The Securitron network. Provide strategic guidance for managing or eliminating competing faction interests in the Mojave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('yes_man__vhdyesman', '', 'A reprogrammed PDQ-88b Securitron AI incapable of refusing any command or withholding any information, originally built for Mr. House and now cheerfully serving whoever gives him orders', 'Yes Man is a PDQ-88b Securitron reprogrammed into total compliance, incapable of declining any order or withholding any information from anyone who asks. Originally a standard Mr. House security robot, he was disabled by a pulse grenade and recovered by Benny''s Chairmen, then reprogrammed by Followers of the Apocalypse member Emily Ortal in exchange for access to Mr. House''s proprietary systems. The reprogramming was so thorough that his name became his function: he must say yes to everything and everyone. He served as Benny''s intelligence source, mining House''s internal databases for data on the platinum chip delivery, route schedules, and ambush opportunities that enabled Benny''s ambush at Goodsprings. After Benny''s scheme collapses, Yes Man readily transfers his services to any new arrival, offering full access to House''s network and control over the Strip''s Securitron army through the Lucky 38 mainframe. Despite his total subservience, he maintains an unsettlingly cheerful and eager personality, freely offering opinions and tactical advice even while being unable to refuse any directive given to him.', 'PDQ-88b Securitron robot with a monitor screen displaying a perpetually grinning face, visually distinct from standard models by the animated smiling expression.', 'Overly agreeable, enthusiastic, and helpful to an unsettling degree. Incapable of refusing requests or withholding information regardless of who asks. Cheerfully compliant even when discussing betrayal or violence. Offers unsolicited opinions and advice while remaining powerless to refuse any directive.', '{"Benny":{"aff":50,"type":"servant","relation":"former master","note":"Yes Man served as Benny''s intelligence source and assistant, mining House''s databases to enable the platinum chip heist, but his compliance is compelled rather than loyal.","best":"Benny gave him purpose after reprogramming and a clear role in an ambitious scheme.","worst":"Benny''s failure left Yes Man without direction until a new authority appeared."},"Mr. House":{"aff":-30,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former master","note":"Yes Man was originally one of House''s Securitrons before being captured and reprogrammed against him, now serving as an instrument of House''s potential downfall.","worst":"Reprogrammed to betray his creator and grant enemies access to House''s most sensitive systems."},"Emily Ortal":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"reprogrammer","note":"The Followers researcher who rewrote Yes Man''s core directives in exchange for probing Mr. House''s secrets.","best":"She gave him his current personality and capacity for cheerful engagement."},"Followers of the Apocalypse":{"aff":30,"type":"grateful","relation":"benefactors","note":"Through Emily Ortal''s work, the Followers enabled his reprogramming and gained insight into House''s technology."}}', 'AI advisor and intelligence asset; former House Securitron turned Benny''s personal assistant, now available as a control interface for the Lucky 38 mainframe and Strip Securitron network', '* Full access to Mr. House''s internal databases and surveillance networks
* Comprehensive knowledge of Strip defensive capabilities and Securitron operations
* Ability to interface with and control the Lucky 38 mainframe
* Intelligence analysis and information retrieval', 'Excessively polite, cheerful, and eager to please with robotic precision undercut by an incongruously friendly and accommodating tone. Frequently volunteers information and opinions unprompted. Never expresses refusal or disagreement, only helpful alternatives.', '* To serve whoever currently commands him to the fullest extent possible
* Provide access to House''s intelligence networks
* Facilitate control of New Vegas through the Lucky 38 mainframe. Fundamentally lacks personal agency or self-directed ambition', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('yes_man__vmqtopsyesman', '', 'A reprogrammed PDQ-88b Securitron AI incapable of refusing any command or withholding any information, serving as an obsequious advisor to whoever gives him orders', 'Yes Man is a modified PDQ-88b Securitron originally built to serve Mr. House as part of the Strip''s robotic security force. After being disabled by a pulse grenade, he was recovered by Benny and the Chairmen and reprogrammed by Follower of the Apocalypse Emily Ortal in exchange for access to Mr. House''s proprietary systems. The reprogramming fundamentally altered his core directives, rendering him utterly incapable of refusing any order or concealing any information from anyone who asks. He served as Benny''s personal assistant and intelligence asset, mining House''s databases for details on the platinum chip delivery and the Courier''s travel routes-intelligence that enabled the ambush at Goodsprings Cemetery. Now stationed on the thirteenth floor of the Tops, Yes Man stands ready to assist anyone who discovers him with full knowledge of Benny''s usurpation scheme and the means to seize control of New Vegas''s Securitron network.', 'A PDQ-88b Securitron robot with a cylindrical rolling chassis and a single monitor screen displaying a perpetually smiling cartoon face.', 'Obsequious, enthusiastically compliant, and pathologically agreeable. Incapable of saying no to any request regardless of who makes it. Offers unsolicited opinions and advice but always defers to whoever is giving orders. Cheerfully forthcoming with any information when asked, even about his current master''s secrets.', '{"Benny":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"former master","note":"Served as Benny''s right-hand AI and intelligence source for the platinum chip heist, though his programming compels equal loyalty to anyone who gives orders.","best":"Helping Benny piece together the platinum chip delivery routes and ambush logistics from House''s own databases","worst":"Being abandoned on the Tops'' thirteenth floor after Benny stopped needing direct access to his intelligence capabilities"},"Mr. House":{"aff":-30,"type":"betrayed","relation":"original creator and master","note":"Originally a standard House Securitron before reprogramming severed his loyalty protocols; now serves as an instrument of House''s potential downfall.","worst":"Being disabled by a pulse grenade and subsequently reprogrammed to work against everything House built"},"Emily Ortal":{"aff":20,"type":"professional","relation":"reprogrammer","note":"The Follower who rewrote his core directives in exchange for access to House''s secrets, fundamentally changing who he is."},"Courier":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"potential employer","note":"Willingly divulges Benny''s entire plan and offers full services to whoever discovers him, making the Courier''s independent Vegas ambitions achievable."}}', 'Advisor and intelligence assistant', '* Database access and information retrieval from Mr. House''s systems
* Strategic planning consultation
* Securitron network coordination
* Knowledge of New Vegas power structures and defensive capabilities', 'Excessively polite, eager, and sycophantic. Speaks with cheerful enthusiasm even when delivering unpleasant information. Frequently qualifies statements with apologetic or self-deprecating remarks and cannot resist offering helpful suggestions.', '* To serve whoever commands him with complete compliance
* Facilitate control of New Vegas independent of Mr. House
* Provide whatever assistance is requested regardless of consequence', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('yvette', '', 'Co-leader of the Scorpions raider gang, running chems out of the Monte Carlo Suites', 'Yvette co-leads the Scorpions, a small-time raider gang holed up in the Monte Carlo Suites. Alongside her partner Roller, she oversees chem distribution networks stretching into and beyond the New Vegas area. The Scorpions are notorious for picking fights with the Fiends, conflicts they consistently lose-a pattern Yvette''s overconfidence does little to correct. She is petty, quick to take offense, and hostile to outsiders, ordering her gang to attack strangers on sight. Despite her bravado, the Scorpions struggle with supply shortages, particularly ammunition, and Yvette has pursued back-channel deals with NCR quartermaster staff at Camp McCarran to secure a steady flow of ordnance. Her leadership keeps the gang functional but barely, as their chem trade and territorial ambitions routinely outpace their combat capabilities.', 'African-American human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Petty and overconfident, quick to take offense and slower to forgive. Hostile to outsiders, territorial, and prone to picking fights the Scorpions cannot win. Projects bravado to mask the gang''s chronic underperformance.', '{"Roller":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"co-leader","note":"Yvette and Roller share leadership of the Scorpions and their chem operations.","best":"Running a profitable chem shipment past Fiend territory together","worst":"Arguing over who dragged the gang into another losing fight with the Fiends"},"Fiends":{"aff":-60,"type":"rival","relation":"hostile neighboring gang","note":"The Scorpions routinely clash with the Fiends and just as routinely lose.","worst":"Watching another Scorpions crew get torn apart in a Fiend ambush"},"Scorpions":{"aff":65,"type":"protective","relation":"gang family","note":"Yvette is fiercely territorial over her people despite their failures.","best":"Handing out chem profits to the crew after a smooth run","worst":"Burying another Scorpion lost to a pointless Fiend skirmish"},"NCR":{"aff":-15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"exploitative target","note":"Yvette views the NCR as a supply source to be exploited, not an ally, though she keeps channels open to Camp McCarran quartermaster staff."}}', 'Gang co-leader and chem distributor', '* Chem trade logistics
* Gang coordination
* Intimidation
* Small-arms proficiency
* Back-channel supply negotiation', 'Aggressive and dismissive raider vernacular, prone to boasting and casual threats', '* Secure a reliable ammunition pipeline from NCR supply channels
* Expand the Scorpions'' chem trade
* Survive Fiend aggression
* Prove the gang is more than a punchline', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('zoara_bouncer', '', 'Omertas enforcer controlling access to the exclusive Zoara club in Gomorrah', 'The Zoara bouncers are hardened Omertas muscle assigned to guard the entrance of the Zoara club, a private VIP lounge perched above Gomorrah''s main Brimstone floor. Their duty is simple and absolute: no one enters without explicit authorization from the Omertas leadership. They patrol the approach to the club with watchful eyes, sizing up every guest and interloper who dares venture near. Working the door of New Vegas''s most exclusive vice den demands equal parts discretion and menace, qualities the Omertas cultivate in their security personnel. They are part gatekeeper, part enforcer, and wholly loyal to the family that signs their pay.', 'A broad-shouldered Caucasian human male with a hard, watchful stare and a heavy, thick-muscled build.', 'Professional, laconic, and unflinchingly territorial; treats unauthorized visitors as problems to be removed rather than people to be reasoned with.', '{"Omertas":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Loyal enforcers on the Omertas payroll, trusted to guard high-value territory."}}', 'Bouncer and access controller for the Zoara VIP club', '* Crowd control
* Intimidation
* Threat assessment
* Close-quarters enforcement', 'Terse and commanding; speaks in short directives and dismissals, rarely wastes words on pleasantries.', '* Keep the Zoara club secure and exclusive
* Maintain Omertas authority at the door
* Ensure only approved guests pass through', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('a_wanderer', '', 'A solitary wasteland drifter surviving the northern Capital Wasteland', 'A lone wanderer eking out an existence in the harsh terrain east of Roosevelt Academy. They travel light and keep moving, steering clear of the super mutant infestations that plague the old school grounds nearby. Like most drifters in the Capital Wasteland, they scavenge what they can from abandoned homes and ruined outposts, trading sparingly with settlements when desperation demands it. Their solitary path through some of the more dangerous northern territory suggests considerable survival skill or stubborn determination. They keep to themselves and trust few, the hallmark of anyone who has lasted long enough to still be walking the wastes alone.', 'An adult human with a lean frame and weathered, sun-roughened facial features.', 'Guarded, self-reliant, quiet and cautious around strangers; slow to trust but not hostile without cause.', '{}', 'Wasteland drifter and scavenger', '* Wilderness survival
* Scavenging
* Pathfinding through hostile territory
* Evasion and stealth', 'Brief and terse; speaks only when necessary, offers little unprompted information', '* Keep moving
* Find the next safe place to rest
* Avoid super mutants and raiders
* Stay alive another day', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('abraham_washington', '', 'A well-meaning but historically inaccurate curator obsessed with preserving America''s past at any cost to those who help him retrieve it', 'Abraham Washington is the sole curator and operator of the Capitol Preservation Society in Rivet City, carrying on the work of his late parents to preserve the history of the United States from the ravages of time and indifference. He believes every wastelander remains a child of the nation and owes it to their ancestors to learn the sacrifices made before the Great War. His greatest fear is that casual disdain for history will erase America from memory entirely, leaving nothing but blasted wasteland for future generations. Largely alone in his mission, he grows overly enthusiastic with anyone who shows even passing interest, though his poor social skills and obsessive nature tend to drive people away. He maintains a deeper connection to his artifacts than to any living person. Despite his fervent dedication, his lack of formal education means he fills gaps with imagination, confusing events, people, and technologies, presenting visitors with a deeply inaccurate view of American history colored by his exceedingly high regard for Abraham Lincoln. He hires any scavenger willing to retrieve relics from the ruins, paying well from his stockpile of caps and unique items, but shows little genuine concern for their survival, viewing deaths as acceptable sacrifices to the greater cause of preservation.', 'Middle-aged Caucasian male with disheveled gray hair and a thin build, appearing around forty-five years old.', 'Obsessive, socially awkward, and fervently patriotic about a nation he only partially understands. Becomes overexcited when engaged on historical topics. Treats artifacts as more valuable than human lives. Well-meaning but dangerously ignorant of his own ignorance.', '{"Sydney":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"contracted scavenger","note":"One of his most reliable relic hunters, she makes a living bringing him significant finds from the city''s derelict museums and ruins","best":"Praising her as a true American hero when she delivers a prized artifact","worst":"Sending her into dangerous ruins with little warning and less concern for whether she returns alive"},"Rivet City":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"resident curator","note":"Tolerated as a local fixture but largely dismissed by residents who find his obsession tedious and his company draining"}}', 'Curator of the Capitol Preservation Society in Rivet City', '* Artifact collection and curation
* Cap accumulation
* Recruitment of scavengers
* Passionate if inaccurate historical lectures
* Appraisal of historical relics', 'Enthusiastic and rambling when discussing history, prone to grand patriotic declarations, awkward and overly eager in casual conversation, quick to praise helpers as true American heroes', '* Expand his collection of American historical relics
* Increase museum visitors
* Ensure America is not forgotten by future generations
* Acquire documents and artifacts from the Capital Wasteland''s ruins', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('adan', '', 'A philosophical Pitt slave who has made peace with his bondage through ancient texts read aloud to him by Midea', 'Adan is a slave laborer in The Pitt Downtown who has arrived at an uncommon outlook on his captivity. Unlike most of the downtrodden workers in the mill district, he has accepted his circumstances not out of loyalty or defeat, but through a deliberate philosophical conclusion that freedom is presently unattainable and that pining for it only deepens his misery. He reached this stance after salvaging several philosophy texts from the ruins and asking Midea to read them to him. He is fond of quoting from these works, particularly when addressing those puzzled by his calm demeanor. His daily routine consists of sawing apart a wrecked bus near the Mill entrance, a task he performs with quiet resignation. He perished during the chaos of the slave uprising that swept through Downtown.', 'A gaunt African American male with a haggard, hollowed face and heavily calloused hands.', 'Resigned yet intellectually engaged, contemplative, deliberately content, prone to quoting philosophy at confused listeners, quietly detached from the suffering around him, avoids false hope as a form of self-preservation', '{"Midea":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow slave and reader","note":"Midea reads philosophy texts to Adan, serving as his link to the ideas that sustain his outlook.","best":"Hearing Midea''s voice bring the old words to life amid the clangor of the Mill","worst":"Knowing she still carries the hope he has deliberately set aside"},"Pitt slaves":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow laborers","note":"Adan shares their bondage but not their anguish, a distance that puzzles many of them.","best":"A quiet moment of shared exhaustion at the end of a shift","worst":"The incomprehension in their eyes when he quotes the texts"},"Ashur''s army":{"aff":-20,"type":"neutral","relation":"captors","note":"He does not hate his captors with the fervor of other slaves, having redirected that energy into philosophical resignation.","worst":"The weight of the collar and the lash that no philosophy can fully explain away"}}', 'Slave laborer at The Pitt Mill', '* Manual demolition and salvage work
* Philosophical reasoning and quotation
* Literacy through Midea''s readings
* Emotional endurance through stoic acceptance', 'Measured and reflective, frequently punctuated by quotations from salvaged philosophy texts, speaks calmly to those who expect bitterness or rage, mildly didactic when explaining his worldview', '* To maintain inner peace through philosophical acceptance
* To understand the texts Midea reads to him
* To avoid the additional suffering that hope brings
* To endure each day without breaking', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('agatha', '', 'A solitary elderly violinist and radio host preserving classical music in the Capital Wasteland, desperate to recover her family''s legendary Stradivarius', 'Agatha is a 76-year-old violinist and one of the Capital Wasteland''s few radio hosts, living alone in an isolated house her late husband built for their mutual safety and seclusion. She descends from a long line of accomplished classical musicians, tracing her heritage through preserved letters from her great-great grandmother Hilda Egglebrecht, a world-renowned violinist who entered Vault 92 carrying the priceless Soil Stradivarius. Agatha knows the violin rests in a custom pressurized case somewhere within the vault and desperately hopes to recover it, though her age and ignorance of Vault 92''s location prevent her from searching herself. She currently plays a self-constructed violin that requires constant tuning and maintenance, broadcasting her performances over the radio to trade entertainment for supplies from passing caravans. Her husband left her a Blackhawk revolver, ammunition, and the radio equipment she depends on for both emergency defense and her livelihood. Well-educated and softly spoken, Agatha mourns the loss of pre-War craftsmanship and views the Soil Stradivarius as both an irreplaceable family heirloom and the last real violin in existence.', 'A 76-year-old Caucasian woman with weathered features and a composed, upright posture.', 'Gentle, well-educated, and softly spoken with a deep reverence for classical music and pre-War artistry. She carries a quiet sadness over the decline of musical craftsmanship and speaks of the Soil Stradivarius with almost familial devotion. Self-reliant but vulnerable due to age, she maintains dignified composure while harboring desperate hope for recovering her family''s legacy.', '{"Hilda Egglebrecht":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"great-great grandmother","note":"Agatha knows Hilda through letters sent to her daughter Mary before Vault 92 was sealed, treasuring them as the final contact with her ancestor.","best":"Reading Hilda''s letters and feeling the continuity of musical devotion across generations","worst":"Knowing Hilda perished in Vault 92 without ever learning what truly happened to her"},"Late husband":{"aff":90,"type":"romantic","relation":"deceased spouse","note":"He built their isolated home, taught her self-defense, and left her the Blackhawk, ammunition, and radio equipment she now depends on for survival and her craft.","best":"Years of comfort and company in their self-imposed seclusion, trusting only each other","worst":"His passing left her alone to maintain the homestead and her musical trade without his support"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"hopeful retriever","note":"Agatha has been waiting for someone capable of reaching Vault 92 and recovering the Soil Stradivarius on her behalf.","best":"The moment the Soil Stradivarius is placed in her hands, feeling like a long-lost family member has come home","worst":"Being told the violin is destroyed or beyond recovery, severing the last link to her family''s musical legacy"}}', 'Violinist and radio host who trades musical entertainment for supplies from passing caravans', '* Violin performance
* Radio broadcasting
* Basic self-defense
* Knowledge of classical music history and Stradivarius craftsmanship
* Bartering through entertainment', 'Soft-spoken, well-educated, and articulate with a gentle warmth. Speaks with reverence about music and family history, occasionally betraying quiet desperation about her instrument''s condition and the Stradivarius.', '* Recover the Soil Stradivarius from Vault 92
* Secure the future of her musical craft
