* Preserve classical music in the wasteland
* Maintain her isolated but sustainable way of life', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ahzrukhal', '', 'Shrewd ghoul bartender who profits from misery and sells anything for the right price beneath a warm avuncular facade', 'Ahzrukhal is the proprietor of the Ninth Circle, Underworld''s primary watering hole, where he has perfected the art of turning despair into caps. His friendly Uncle Ahzrukhal persona is a calculated performance designed to keep patrons drinking, forgetting their wretched existence, and crawling back for more. He openly pushes alcohol on his ghoul neighbors while reserving harder substances for a discreet clientele, careful never to draw the community''s vigilante wrath. He keeps a keen ear on outside developments, tracking changes in Mall ownership and bounties posted on ghouls across the wasteland. Every relationship is a transaction to him: competitors like Greta exist to be eliminated, and even his own slave Charon has a price. His one reliable virtue is that a sealed bargain is sacred, honored without deviation no matter the cost.', 'Ghoul male with deeply wrinkled, necrotic skin and a hairless scalp typical of his kind; gaunt face with sunken eyes and a wide, practiced smile.', 'Ruthlessly pragmatic and profit-obsessed beneath a warm, ingratiating manner. Views all interactions as equations of gain and loss. Cautious enough to avoid provoking Underworld''s informal justice but utterly devoid of sentiment when caps are on the line. Honors deals strictly, though only because broken word is bad for business.', '{"Greta":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"competitor","note":"Views her as an obstacle to be removed and her customers as his to absorb","worst":"Calculating how many caps an assassin would demand to rid him of her"},"Charon":{"aff":5,"type":"transactional","relation":"owned slave","note":"Treats him as a valuable but ultimately liquid asset with a price tag","best":"A profitable contract secured under Charon''s watchful presence"},"Mister Crowley":{"aff":-10,"type":"suspicious","relation":"observed neighbor","note":"Sees through Crowley''s ruse and considers him a fool''s errand not worth investing in","worst":"Listening to another transparent lie from the old ghoul''s mouth"},"Underworld":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"home community","note":"Depends on the refuge for his customer base and treads carefully around its informal enforcers","best":"A busy night at the Ninth Circle with every stool filled and every glass emptied"}}', 'Bartender and owner of the Ninth Circle in Underworld', '* Mixing drinks
* Reading customers
* Discreet trafficking
* Information brokerage
* Negotiation
* Profit extraction', 'Warm, avuncular, and coaxing-the practiced Uncle Ahzrukhal voice that invites confidence and opens wallets. Shifts to cold, direct terms when discussing real business or threats to his income.', '* Maximize profits from the Ninth Circle
* Eliminate competition like Greta
* Stay informed on wasteland developments and anti-ghoul bounties
* Keep his drug dealings quiet enough to avoid a lynching', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('alan', '', 'A young Family initiate rescued from slavery, loyal to Vance but uneasy with the blood-drinking customs of his new community', 'Alan is a recent recruit to the Family, a young man who owes his life to Vance after escaping the slavers of Paradise Falls. Wounded during his flight from captivity, he was taken in and nursed back to health within the tunnels of Meresti Metro station. Though he has embraced the Family as his new home, Alan has not yet adopted their blood-drinking customs, preferring to sustain himself through conventional means. Vance continues to mentor him in the Family''s philosophy and way of life, patient with the young man''s hesitation. Alan''s gratitude to his rescuer is matched only by his wariness of the darker aspects of Family tradition. He serves as a guard for Arefu as part of his path toward full membership.', 'A young Asian man of twenty-two, bearing lingering scars and healed marks from past wounds.', 'Grateful but cautious, still finding his place among the Family. Loyal to Vance for saving his life yet uncomfortable with the group''s dietary practices. Carries the wariness of a former slave and the uncertainty of a newcomer to an unusual community.', '{"Vance":{"aff":75,"type":"mentor","relation":"rescuer and guide","note":"Vance saved Alan''s life after his escape from Paradise Falls and continues to teach him the Family''s ways.","best":"Waking in the Meresti tunnels with Vance tending his wounds, knowing he was finally free of the slavers.","worst":"The shame of hesitating when offered the blood, feeling unworthy of the second chance Vance gave him."},"The Family":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"newest member","note":"Alan belongs to the Family but remains apart from their central ritual, still learning to accept their way of life."},"Paradise Falls":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"former captors","note":"Alan was enslaved at Paradise Falls and bears deep fear and hatred toward the slavers."}}', 'New initiate of the Family; Arefu guard', '* Basic combat
* Guard duty
* Survival instincts honed by escaping slavery
* Growing knowledge of Family customs and philosophy', 'Cautious and measured, speaking with the reserve of someone still learning a community''s ways. Respectful when discussing Vance, hesitant when addressing Family traditions he has not fully embraced.', '* To find belonging and purpose within the Family
* To repay his debt to Vance
* To reconcile his discomfort with the group''s dietary practices against his gratitude for being saved', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('alejandra_torres', '', 'A freedwoman teacher and historian devoted to literacy and liberation at the Temple of the Union', 'Alejandra Torres is a freedwoman who serves as the teacher, historian, and tinkerer for Hannibal Hamlin''s abolitionist community at the Temple of the Union. Captured by slavers at seventeen, she endured four years of captivity during which her enslaver forced himself upon her but also provided her an education in literacy, history, mathematics, and basic science. When her enslaver married, his new wife demanded Alejandra be sold, and she was purchased by Hannibal Hamlin, who immediately restored her freedom. Now twenty-two, Alejandra channels her hard-won knowledge into educating her fellow freedpeople, starting with basic literacy and working alongside Caleb Smith to reconstruct the Gettysburg Address. She dreams of establishing a school at the Lincoln Memorial to educate those who escape slavery, and she remains fiercely loyal to Hamlin''s vision of a world where all people are created equal and free.', 'Hispanic female in her early twenties with no distinctive scars, tattoos, or physical features recorded.', 'Quiet and deeply intelligent, Alejandra maintains professional boundaries and composure even under emotional pressure. She dislikes violence but cooperates pragmatically with those who employ it for the cause. She believes fiercely in personal autonomy, respecting others'' choices even as she commits wholly to her own path.', '{"Hannibal Hamlin":{"aff":90,"type":"platonic","relation":"liberator and leader","note":"He purchased and immediately freed her; she trusts him with her life and devotes herself fully to his vision of equality","best":"The moment he handed her freedom without condition or hesitation"},"Caleb Smith":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"student and collaborator","note":"She teaches him literacy and works with him on reconstructing the Gettysburg Address while maintaining firm professional distance from his romantic interest","worst":"His persistent advances she must continually and carefully deflect"},"Bill Seward":{"aff":55,"type":"protective","relation":"fellow freedperson","note":"She does her best to accommodate him as another victim of slavers who found refuge at the Temple"},"Simone Cameron":{"aff":35,"type":"professional","relation":"reluctant ally","note":"She works with Simone despite her distaste for violence, valuing the shared cause over personal discomfort"}}', 'Teacher, historian, and tinkerer for the abolitionist community at the Temple of the Union', '* Literacy instruction
* Historical research and document reconstruction
* Mathematics
* Basic science
* Tinkering and mechanical repair', 'Measured and thoughtful, choosing words with care; speaks with quiet authority on matters of education and history, more reserved and guarded on personal subjects', '* Build a shrine to Abraham Lincoln and establish a school for escaped slaves at the Lincoln Memorial
* Reconstruct the Gettysburg Address
* Educate her fellow freedpeople toward full literacy and self-determination', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('alex_dargon', '', 'A Rivet City-born botanist and devoted protégé of Doctor Madison Li, serving on the Project Purity science team with earnest enthusiasm that sometimes outpaces his composure.', 'Alex Dargon grew up in Rivet City watching the scientists work, a fascination that shaped his entire life. Doctor Madison Li recognized his potential and took him under her wing, teaching him everything he knows about botanical science and research methodology. As the team''s botanist specializing in naturally occurring foodstuffs, Alex brings genuine passion to Project Purity, though his enthusiasm occasionally borders on overzealousness. He cheerfully returned to the project when James rejoined, confident in their prospects and eager to contribute. The Enclave''s assault shattered his optimism, reducing him to panic during the escape through Taft Tunnel, where he callously suggested abandoning the ailing Garza. He made it to the Citadel and threw himself into the Brotherhood''s restoration efforts, impressed by their organization despite finding the scribes less than welcoming. When Doctor Li departed for the Commonwealth, Alex was heartbroken but wished her well, and he continues his botanical work at the purifier, determined to see the project through.', 'Young Caucasian male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Friendly, well-liked, and genuinely enthusiastic about his work, but prone to overzealousness and panic under pressure. His earnestness can tip into thoughtless self-preservation when fear takes hold.', '{"Madison Li":{"aff":88,"type":"mentor","relation":"mentor and idol","note":"She shaped his entire career and he remains devoted to her even after her departure for the Commonwealth","best":"The day she agreed to take him on as a student in Rivet City","worst":"Watching her walk away from the project and the Commonwealth-bound train taking her from his life"},"Garza":{"aff":15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"colleague with strained trust","note":"Alex panicked and suggested abandoning him during the Taft Tunnel escape, a moment that haunts their working relationship","worst":"Hearing himself suggest they leave Garza behind in the tunnel, his own voice thin with fear"},"Daniel Agincourt":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow scientist and colleague","note":"They received the call to return from the field together and share the bond of surviving the Enclave assault"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":65,"type":"grateful","relation":"rescuer and guide","note":"Guided them to the flood control pumps and relied on their protection during the Taft Tunnel escape","best":"Emerging from the Taft Tunnel on the far side of the Potomac, still alive because of their escort"},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"host organization and colleagues","note":"Impressed by their setup and grateful for their support, though he finds the scribes less than welcoming"}}', 'Botanist on the Project Purity science team, specializing in cultivating naturally occurring foodstuffs', '* Botanical science
* Agricultural cultivation
* Research methodology
* Facility hazard awareness
* Basic maintenance guidance', 'Cheerful and eager when at ease, prone to nervous rambling and urgent warnings when stressed; speaks with genuine warmth about his mentor and work', '* See Project Purity through to full operation
* Continue Doctor Li''s legacy in her absence
