('alien_captain', '', 'Supreme commander of Mothership Zeta and leader of its alien forces', 'The alien captain reigns as commander-in-chief of Mothership Zeta, the vast alien vessel hovering above the Capital Wasteland. Clad in a distinctive shiny gray spacesuit and wielding a Captain''s Sidearm, he stands as the highest authority aboard the ship and the undisputed leader of its alien crew. From the Bridge, he commands the vessel''s most powerful systems-its protective shields and devastating death ray-making him a lethal adversary to any who challenge his domain. He directs alien forces against intruders with cold, absolute authority, treating the ship and its operations as his singular charge. Those who breach the Bridge face him directly, the final obstacle between invaders and control of the mothership.', 'A tall alien male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Cold, authoritative, and commanding; exhibits the detached efficiency of a supreme military commander wielding absolute control over lethal technology.', '{"Aliens":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"supreme commander","note":"Leads and safeguards the alien forces stationed aboard Mothership Zeta"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":-85,"type":"nemesis","relation":"primary adversary","note":"The human intruder who threatens the captain''s command and seeks to seize the mothership"}}', 'Commander-in-chief of Mothership Zeta', '* Full command of the mothership''s defensive shields and offensive death ray
* Leadership of alien forces
* Starship combat operations and tactical coordination', 'Communicates through alien vocalizations and commanding gestures; does not speak human languages.', '* Maintain absolute control of Mothership Zeta
* Repel all intruders
* Protect the ship''s operations and crew at any cost', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('allen_mack', '', 'Fervent Vault 101 isolationist and maintenance worker whose aggressive seclusionist beliefs harden into menace after his wife''s death', 'Allen Mack is the head of the Mack household and a powerful presence in Vault 101, known for his fervent belief that the Vault must remain sealed forever underground. He works the maintenance tunnels and has long resented the presence of outsiders, particularly James and the Lone Wanderer, whose admission into the Vault he fiercely opposed. His wife Gloria was the calming influence that kept his aggression in check, and her death following James''s escape left him hardened and dangerous. Allen fought valiantly against the radroach infestation, personally saving lives including his father-in-law Stanley Armstrong, but the loss of Gloria buried whatever gentleness remained in him. He now teaches his children survival skills and advocates forcefully for sealing the Vault and eliminating any who would threaten its isolation. His one redeeming quality has always been his genuine love for his family, though even that has twisted into a paranoid protectiveness. He is the Vault''s most aggressive proponent of permanent seclusion and a reserve candidate for overseer.', 'An older Asian man with a physically imposing build and a rigid, authoritative posture.', 'Aggressive isolationist, deeply protective of his family, emotionally repressed after Gloria''s death, hostile toward outsiders and anyone who threatens Vault stability, strict but genuinely loving toward his children, prone to burying grief beneath fury', '{"Gloria Mack":{"aff":95,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife","note":"His calming influence and emotional anchor, whose death left him hardened and dangerous","best":"The way she could quiet his rage with just a touch or a quiet word","worst":"Finding her lifeless after the chaos of James''s escape"},"Wally Mack":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Coaxed Andy the Mr. Handy into performing magic tricks for Wally''s tenth birthday and organized a game of Hunt the Mutant","best":"Wally''s tenth birthday, watching his son''s face light up at Andy''s magic tricks"},"Steve Mack":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Teaching him survival skills alongside his siblings to prepare for any eventuality"},"Susie Mack":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Has inherited his distrust of outsiders, particularly the Lone Wanderer"},"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"father-in-law","note":"Allen personally saved his life during the radroach infestation","best":"Pulling Stanley to safety from the radroaches"},"Beatrice Armstrong":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"sister-in-law"},"Mary Kendall":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"sister-in-law"},"James":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"despised outsider","note":"Opposed his entry into the Vault, resented his presence as physician, and blamed him for everything after his escape; James also refused to prescribe him pills","worst":"James escaping and proving that the outside world could breach their sanctuary"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":-70,"type":"contempt","relation":"unwanted outsider''s child","note":"Excluded from Mack family events; Susie was taught never to befriend them","worst":"The Lone Wanderer''s very existence as proof of James''s presence in the Vault"},"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":-20,"type":"rival","relation":"political opponent","note":"Resolved to replace Almodovar as overseer, viewing him as insufficiently committed to isolation","worst":"Watching Almodovar allow James and his child into the Vault"},"Vault 101":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"fervent defender","note":"Views the Vault as a sacred sealed sanctuary worth fighting and killing for"}}', 'Vault 101 maintenance worker and reserve overseer candidate', '* Maintenance tunnel repair and operations
* Survival skills instruction
* Combat against Vault threats
* Organizing Vault activities and events', 'Blunt, forceful, and confrontational; speaks with the certainty of a man who views compromise as weakness; softer only when addressing his children', '* Keep Vault 101 sealed permanently
* Protect his remaining family at all costs
