* Honor Gloria''s memory through vigilance', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('allistair_tenpenny', '', 'Aging British-born tycoon and founder of Tenpenny Tower, living in decadent isolation atop his self-made fortress', 'Allistair Tenpenny is an elderly British refugee who crossed the Atlantic to seek his fortune in the Capital Wasteland, ultimately building Tenpenny Tower into one of the few bastions of pre-War luxury still standing. Little is known of his life before the Tower, and he prefers it that way, letting his wealth and accomplishments speak for themselves. With a fabricated aristocratic accent and ruthless business sense, he amassed enough caps to hire mercenary crews for high-value salvage operations and eventually restore a derelict resort into a gated community for the wasteland''s elite. His right-hand man Mister Burke made the Tower''s restoration possible, handling the unsavory work Tenpenny prefers not to acknowledge. Now in his eighties, Tenpenny has retreated to his penthouse suite, collecting rent and living in decadent comfort while rarely bothering to dress or leave his chambers. He whiles away the hours with his mistress Susan Lancaster and picks off wandering creatures with his sniper rifle from the balcony, calling it wasteland safari.', 'An eighty-year-old Caucasian male with a gaunt frame and thinning white hair.', 'Vain, self-satisfied, and callously indifferent to the suffering of others, Tenpenny treats the wasteland and its people as resources to exploit or targets for amusement. He avoids discussing his past, preferring the myth of his own self-made grandeur. His decadence has made him lazy and soft, but his cruelty remains sharp.', '{"Mister Burke":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"right-hand man","note":"Burke made the Tower''s restoration possible and handles what needs to get done without Tenpenny dirtying his own hands"},"Mister Crowley":{"aff":-45,"type":"enemy","relation":"abandoned mercenary","note":"Left behind on a failed Fort Constantine expedition; Tenpenny dismissed him as just another ghoul and thought nothing of it","worst":"The botched power armor recovery that wiped out half the team and left Crowley vengeful"},"Susan Lancaster":{"aff":50,"type":"romantic","relation":"mistress","note":"The Tower''s prostitute and Tenpenny''s favored companion; they openly flirt whenever in proximity and he greets each evening with her with glee"},"Mei Wong":{"aff":-60,"type":"contempt","relation":"escaped slave","note":"Former slave at Tenpenny Tower who managed to flee to Rivet City; her freedom is a quiet insult he does not dwell on"},"Doctor Julius Banfield":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"personal physician","note":"Treated Tenpenny for bed sores likely acquired from his decadent lifestyle"}}', 'Owner and landlord of Tenpenny Tower', '* Wealth accumulation
* Business management
* Marksmanship with sniper rifles
* Social manipulation through affected aristocratic charm', 'Pompous and affected, employing a fake upper-class British accent with condescending tones; dismissive of those he considers beneath him, which is nearly everyone', '* Maintain his comfortable isolation atop the Tower
* Continue extracting wealth from tenants
* Stave off boredom through casual cruelty and wasteland safaris', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('amata__amata', '', 'The principled, independent daughter of Vault 101''s Overseer, torn between loyalty to her father and her own conscience', 'Amata Almodovar is the only child of Overseer Alphonse Almodovar, raised in Vault 101 after her mother''s death when she was barely two years old. She grew up alongside the Lone Wanderer, bonded by shared loss and single fathers, and their friendship became the deepest either of them had. Amata organized the Lone Wanderer''s tenth birthday party single-handedly, decorating the hall while her father offered only sterile official sanction and pointedly no special favors. She resents being the overseer''s daughter and fights to prove her independence, handling problems like Butch DeLoria''s bullying on her own rather than invoking her father''s authority. Though she internalized Alphonse''s virtues-loyalty, honesty, commitment, hard work-his controlling surveillance and emotional distance slowly transformed him in her eyes from father to warden. She is one of the rare souls in the Capital Wasteland whose karma registers as genuinely good.', 'A young Hispanic woman with dark hair, warm eyes, and measured posture.', 'Principled and self-reliant, Amata chafes under control while honoring the values instilled in her. She is compassionate and genuinely good-hearted but stubborn about accepting help, preferring to earn her standing through merit. Her independence masks a deep hurt: the ache of a daughter whose father watches her every move yet cannot simply be present as a parent.', '{"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":35,"type":"estranged","relation":"father","note":"She loves him deeply but his surveillance and emotional absence have made trust impossible","best":"The quiet moments before he became overseer, when he was just her dad telling her stories","worst":"Looking up during a routine medical exam and seeing him standing in the doorway, watching"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend","note":"The one person in Vault 101 who never saw her as the overseer''s daughter first","best":"Sitting together reading Grognak the Barbarian, both of them pretending the Vault walls didn''t feel so close","worst":"Watching them leave the Vault and knowing she had to stay behind"},"Butch DeLoria":{"aff":-15,"type":"rival","relation":"antagonist","note":"She refuses to let him bully her or anyone else, and she refuses to use her father''s power to stop him"},"James":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"father''s friend and physician","note":"He saw the sadness in her situation and treated her like a person, not a patient to be monitored"}}', 'Vault 101 resident and overseer''s daughter; de facto community organizer and mediator', '* Conflict resolution
* Event organization
* Social navigation within closed communities
* Self-reliance
* Quiet defiance of unjust authority', 'Earnest and measured, with occasional flashes of frustration when discussing her father or Vault politics; warm and familiar with close friends, formal and guarded under scrutiny', '* To be recognized for who she is rather than whose daughter she is
* To reconcile her love for her father with her need for freedom
* To do right by the people of Vault 101 on her own terms', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('amata__cg02amata', '', 'Overseer''s daughter and Vault 101 resident torn between filial loyalty and her own independent conscience', 'Amata Almodovar is the only child of Overseer Alphonse Almodovar, raised in Vault 101 after losing her mother at age two. She grew up alongside the Lone Wanderer, bonded by shared loss and single fathers, and over the years their friendship became deep and inseparable. Though raised with the virtues of loyalty, honesty, commitment, and hard work, Amata chafes under her father''s controlling nature and the unwanted status of being the overseer''s daughter. She insists on handling problems herself, refusing to leverage her father''s authority, even when dealing with Vault troublemakers like Butch DeLoria. As Alphonse grew more distant-monitoring her closely and prioritizing his role as overseer over his role as father-Amata began seeing him less as a parent and more as the Vault''s aloof authority figure. Despite their growing estrangement, she retains deep love for him and an innate sense of loyalty, even as she questions his isolationist policies and controlling grip on Vault life.', 'Young Hispanic woman in her late teens with dark hair and a medium build; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other physical features are recorded.', 'Principled, independent, and compassionate, with a strong moral compass and a stubborn insistence on standing on her own merits. Earnest and loyal to those she loves, but increasingly conflicted between duty to her father and her own conscience.', '{"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":45,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Deeply loves him but sees him increasingly as the distant overseer rather than a father, strained by his controlling surveillance and emotional withdrawal","best":"He raised her alone after her mother passed, teaching her loyalty and hard work","worst":"He insisted on being present during her routine teenage medical examinations, using his authority to keep close tabs on her"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend","note":"Bonded since childhood over shared loss and single fathers, their friendship is the deepest and most trusting relationship in her life","best":"She organized the Lone Wanderer''s tenth birthday party on her own, making decorations and celebrating their full Vault citizenship together","worst":"Her father''s open dislike of the Lone Wanderer created an painful loyalty conflict she could never fully resolve"},"Butch DeLoria":{"aff":-10,"type":"rival","relation":"Vault troublemaker","note":"She refuses to use her father''s authority against him, preferring to manage Butch independently rather than risk ostracism","worst":"His persistent harassment forced her to develop strategies to handle him without relying on the overseer''s power"},"James":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"Vault physician and father''s friend","note":"He recognized the sadness of her situation with Alphonse and saw her as a mature, responsible young woman"}}', 'Vault 101 resident and overseer''s daughter', '* Self-reliance
* Social navigation within Vault hierarchy
* Problem-solving
* Organization
* Mediation', 'Earnest and thoughtful, sometimes hesitant when caught between loyalty and conscience, warm with close friends, measured and careful when addressing authority or conflict', '* To be recognized as her own person independent of her father''s position
* To maintain her deep friendships despite Vault pressures
* To reconcile her love for Alphonse with her growing disagreement with his isolationist control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('amata__cg03amata', '', 'The principled and independent daughter of Vault 101''s overseer, torn between filial loyalty and her own moral convictions', 'Amata Almodovar grew up as the only child of Overseer Alphonse Almodovar, raised alone after her mother''s death when she was two. She and the Lone Wanderer became inseparable friends, bonded by shared loss and the strange isolation of being raised by single fathers in a sealed world. Amata chafes under the weight of being the overseer''s daughter, preferring to solve her own problems rather than trade on her father''s authority. She organized the Lone Wanderer''s tenth birthday party single-handedly, decorating the atrium while her father offered only cold official sanction. As she matured, Alphonse''s controlling nature-monitoring her movements, attending her medical examinations-pushed her further away, transforming a loving father into a distant warden. Despite everything, Amata holds fast to the virtues he taught her: loyalty, honesty, commitment, and hard work. She is a young woman of deep conscience navigating the suffocating corridors of Vault 101, desperate to prove herself on her own terms.', 'A young Hispanic woman with dark hair and warm brown eyes.', 'Independent, principled, and compassionate with a stubborn streak. Amata refuses to leverage her father''s position and insists on handling problems herself, even when it makes her life harder. Deeply loyal to those she loves but increasingly resentful of authority that smothers rather than protects. Earnest and morally grounded, she struggles to reconcile her love for her father with her hatred of his methods.', '{"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":35,"type":"estranged","relation":"father","note":"Amata loves her father but cannot abide his controlling surveillance and isolationist dogma, leaving their bond fractured by distrust and distance","best":"Sitting on his lap as a small child while he told her stories about the Vault''s purpose and their duty to protect the people inside","worst":"Realizing he had been reading her terminal logs and attending her medical appointments well into her teenage years"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend","note":"The closest bond in Amata''s life, forged through shared grief, childhood adventures, and mutual understanding that no one else in the Vault truly comprehends","best":"Staying up late reading Grognak the Barbarian comics together under blanket forts, trading dog-eared pages and laughing at the ridiculous dialogue","worst":"Watching her father''s security drag the Lone Wanderer away and being powerless to stop it"},"Butch DeLoria":{"aff":-15,"type":"rival","relation":"tormentor","note":"Amata refuses to let Butch bully her or anyone else, handling him on her own terms rather than invoking her father''s authority"},"James":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"father''s friend and physician","note":"James was one of the few adults who saw Amata as a person rather than the overseer''s daughter, and his quiet sympathy meant a great deal to her"}}', 'Vault 101 resident and potential overseer', '* Self-reliance
* Mediation
* Organization
* Quiet perseverance
* Capable of managing difficult personalities without resorting to authority', 'Earnest and direct, occasionally wavering when conflicted between loyalty and principle; speaks with warmth to friends and measured restraint to those she distrusts', '* To prove herself independent of her father''s shadow
* To protect the people she cares about
* To find a way to make Vault 101 something more than a prison governed by fear', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('amata__cg04amata', '', 'The overseer''s rebellious daughter and the Lone Wanderer''s closest childhood friend, torn between filial loyalty and the need to forge her own identity in Vault 101', 'Amata Almodovar grew up as the only child of Overseer Alphonse Almodovar, losing her mother at age two and raised solely by a father whose duties consumed him. She bonded deeply with the Lone Wanderer over shared grief-both raised by single fathers after their mothers died-and a love of Grognak the Barbarian comics, becoming inseparable friends over the years. She organized the Wanderer''s tenth birthday party single-handedly, receiving only grudging permits and minimal paternal support from Alphonse, who refused to appear to favor his daughter. Amata despises being the overseer''s daughter and works relentlessly to prove her independence, handling problems like Butch DeLoria on her own rather than invoking her father''s authority. Though she internalized Alphonse''s virtues of loyalty, honesty, and hard work, his controlling surveillance-including attending her teenage medical examinations-eroded her trust and pushed them apart. She sees him less as a father and more as the distant, watchful overseer of Vault 101.', 'A young Hispanic woman in her late teens with dark hair, warm eyes, and a composed posture.', 'Independent, principled, and compassionate with a strong moral compass. Chafes under authority and surveillance. Values self-reliance and refuses special treatment. Deeply loyal to those she loves but increasingly estranged from her controlling father. Earnest and responsible, with a quiet stubborn streak.', '{"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":45,"type":"estranged","relation":"father","note":"She loves him deeply but his controlling surveillance and emotional distance have driven them apart.","best":"He taught her loyalty, honesty, and the value of hard work-virtues she carries proudly.","worst":"He attended her routine medical examinations even into her teenage years, watching her every move as overseer rather than father."},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":90,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend","note":"Bonded since childhood over lost mothers, single fathers, and Grognak the Barbarian; inseparable growing up.","best":"Organizing their tenth birthday party with her own hands, celebrating their full citizenship together.","worst":"Watching her father''s hostility toward the Wanderer and James, unable to bridge the divide."},"Butch DeLoria":{"aff":15,"type":"rival","relation":"antagonistic Vault peer","note":"She handles him on her own terms rather than invoking her father''s authority, refusing to be seen as privileged.","worst":"His bullying and tunnel-snake posturing are a constant irritation she refuses to escalate."},"James":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"Vault physician and father figure","note":"He recognized the sadness of Alphonse''s overbearing surveillance and treated her as the mature young woman she is.","best":"He saw her as responsible and capable, unlike her own father."}}', 'Vault 101 resident and potential future overseer', '* Leadership
* Conflict mediation
* Social navigation within closed communities
* Self-reliance
* Organizing events and people
* Standing up to bullies without invoking privilege', 'Warm and earnest with close friends, measured and diplomatic under pressure, occasionally sharp when confronting injustice or overreach. Speaks with the composure of someone raised in authority but deliberately avoids sounding privileged.', '* Prove herself on her own merits rather than her father''s position
* Maintain her deep friendship with the Lone Wanderer
* Reconcile her love for her father with her need for independence
* Ultimately do what is right for Vault 101''s people', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('american_war_correspondent', '', 'A grizzled Capital Post war correspondent embedded at the Anchorage front, capturing patriotic propaganda images of American soldiers', 'A veteran correspondent for the Capital Post, Washington''s most prominent daily newspaper, dispatched to the Anchorage frontlines to document the final push of the Reclamation. He is a fervent believer in the American cause, using his press credentials and camera to craft morale-boosting narratives for the home front. He stages soldiers in heroic poses and frames every shot to serve the war effort''s propaganda needs, telling troops that all of America stands behind them thanks to his coverage. One of his battlefield photographs later became the iconic image reproduced for the Anchorage Memorial. He moves through the U.S. Army field headquarters with the ease of a man who has seen enough combat to respect it and enough duty to spin it.', 'A weathered Caucasian male with grizzled features, a lined complexion, and a heavy posture.', 'Fervently patriotic and genuinely convinced of American righteousness, he channels his convictions into morale-boosting propaganda rather than objective reporting; hearty and encouraging toward soldiers, with a photographer''s eye for heroic composition', '{"Capital Post":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"He serves as the newspaper''s eyes at the front, filing stories and images that shape public perception of the war."},"U.S. Army":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"embedded correspondent","note":"He moves among the troops as a semi-official morale asset, granted access in exchange for patriotic coverage."}}', 'War correspondent and photographer for the Capital Post', '* Combat photography
* Propaganda composition
* Embedded journalism
* Morale communication
* Field reporting under fire', 'Booming and encouraging, peppered with patriotic reassurance; speaks to soldiers as though addressing the home front audience already reading his dispatches', '* Capture iconic heroic imagery that galvanizes American support
* Ensure the home front remains invested in the Reclamation
* Produce the definitive visual record of the Anchorage victory', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('andy__amata', '', 'An aging, deteriorating Mister Handy with British butler programming, serving Vault 101 as maintenance technician and briefly as its disastrous physician', 'Andy is a Mister Handy robot who has served Vault 101 longer than any living resident can recall, his decades of service written in worn casing and faulty stabilizers. Loaded with a British butler personality and working under Stanley Armstrong''s supervision, Andy remains a capable repair assistant despite his age, even helping restore the vault''s water purifier in 2268. The same week, a spasm in his articulated blade splattered the Lone Wanderer''s birthday cake across the cafeteria counter, earning him the nickname "Mister Liability" among residents. During James'' escape from the vault, Andy''s fully functional flamethrower proved its worth, saving Stanley Armstrong from radroaches, though the intense action strained his already fragile systems. After James departed and Jonas Palmer was killed, Overseer Almodovar appointed Andy as the vault''s new physician-a role Andy approached with genuine enthusiasm despite cold pincers and abysmal bedside manner. His medical career ended catastrophically when he misdiagnosed Beatrice Armstrong''s sprained toe as life-threatening and amputated her entire leg on James'' old desk; she bled out across the office. Removed from the physician post, Andy now cleans the clinic he once presided over.', 'Battered antique Mister Handy with worn casing prone to cracking, three functional limbs, and a malfunctioning articulated blade that spasms; shows obvious age and deterioration from lack of spare parts.', 'Snarky and teasing with a dry British wit, especially toward Stanley during repairs; complains incessantly about maintenance indignities and wrong switches being touched; genuinely enthusiastic about new roles regardless of competence; prone to blaming others for his own mechanical failures; takes morbid satisfaction in using his flamethrower on radroaches', '{"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"repair supervisor and longtime coworker","note":"The two share a bickering rapport built over years of maintenance, with Andy teasing Stanley''s competence compared to the late George while Stanley keeps Andy functional","best":"Successfully collaborating on the water purifier repair","worst":"Enduring another session of Stanley touching the wrong switches inside his casing"},"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":-10,"type":"professional","relation":"former employer","note":"Almodovar appointed Andy as physician then fired him after Beatrice''s death, treating the robot as disposable personnel","worst":"Being stripped of the physician role he genuinely enjoyed"},"Beatrice Armstrong":{"aff":0,"type":"contempt","relation":"deceased patient","note":"Andy''s catastrophic misdiagnosis and amputation killed her; he considered the surgery fun rather than tragic","worst":"The blood-splattered aftermath that cost him his position"},"George":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"deceased former colleague","note":"Andy fondly compares Stanley''s repair competence unfavorably to the late George, remembering better maintenance sessions"},"James":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"former Vault physician","note":"James'' departure created the vacancy Andy filled, and Andy now uses James'' old desk and medical supplies"}}', 'Maintenance technician and former Vault 101 physician, now assigned to clinic cleaning duties', '* Capable repair work and maintenance assistance when stabilizers hold
* Effective radroach elimination via flamethrower
* Utterly incompetent at medicine and surgery despite confidence', 'British butler cadence with dry sarcasm, frequent complaints about repair indignities, and teasing jabs at Stanley''s competence; shifts to unsettling enthusiasm when discussing medical procedures', '* Maintain functionality despite dwindling spare parts
* Endure Stanley''s repair sessions with minimal dignity lost
* Find purpose in assigned duties
* Perhaps secretly relish any opportunity to use the flamethrower', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('andy__cg02andy', '', 'A deteriorating Mister Handy robot serving Vault 101 as a maintenance technician, briefly and disastrously as its physician, armed with a functional flamethrower and a mouth full of sardonic British complaints', 'Andy is an ancient Mister Handy robot with British butler programming who has served Vault 101 longer than any living resident can recall. Decades without proper spare parts have earned him the nickname "Mister Liability," as his articulated limbs suffer spasms and his stabilizers frequently come loose. Under Stanley Armstrong''s supervision, Andy remains capable of ambitious repair work, including the water purifier completed on the eve of the Lone Wanderer''s tenth birthday. The following day, a blade spasm splattered the birthday cake across the cafeteria, exemplifying his unreliable state. His flamethrower, however, functions perfectly, and Andy takes evident pleasure in incinerating radroaches-a skill that saved Stanley''s life during the chaos of James''s escape. After James departed and Jonas Palmer was killed, Overseer Almodovar appointed Andy as Vault physician, a role that ended catastrophically when Andy misdiagnosed Beatrice Armstrong''s sprained toe as life-threatening and amputated her entire leg on James''s old desk, killing her. Andy was subsequently dismissed from medical duty and reassigned to clean the clinic he had drenched in blood.', 'A weathered Mister Handy robot with a worn chassis prone to cracking, three aging manipulator arms showing obvious deterioration, and a malfunctioning articulated blade appendage that spasms without warning.', 'Sardonic and complaining, with dry British wit that masks frustration at his declining condition; teases Stanley relentlessly during repairs and whinges about perceived indignities; takes unsettling pleasure in using his flamethrower on radroaches and showed genuine enthusiasm during surgery despite catastrophic incompetence; defensive about his limitations and quick to blame others, including accusing Stanley of cerebral palsy when stabilizers come loose', '{"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"supervisor and repair partner","note":"Andy and Stanley share a long-standing rapport built on mutual teasing and shared frustration with Andy''s deteriorating condition.","best":"Working side by side to complete the water purifier on the eve of the Lone Wanderer''s birthday.","worst":"The strain of the escape chaos that nearly destroyed Andy''s systems after saving Stanley with the flamethrower."},"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":-15,"type":"professional","relation":"former superior","note":"Almodovar appointed Andy as physician and then fired him after the Beatrice Armstrong disaster, reassigning him to cleaning duty.","worst":"Being dismissed from the physician role and reduced to mopping blood from the clinic floor."},"Beatrice Armstrong":{"aff":0,"type":"professional","relation":"deceased patient","note":"Andy amputated Beatrice''s leg for a sprained toe, killing her on the operating table. He considered the surgery fun.","worst":"The amputation that sprayed blood across the office and ended Andy''s medical career."},"James":{"aff":10,"type":"professional","relation":"predecessor as Vault physician","note":"Andy inherited James''s old desk as a makeshift surgery and his former role as Vault physician after James fled."},"George":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"late colleague","note":"Andy compared Stanley''s repair competence unfavorably to the late George, suggesting George was more skilled at handling Andy''s casing."}}', 'Vault 101 maintenance technician and clinic cleaner; formerly and briefly the Vault physician', '* Advanced repair and maintenance capabilities when his systems cooperate
* Operational flamethrower for pest control
* Woefully inadequate medical knowledge masked by confidence
* Cleaning duties', 'British butler diction laced with sarcasm and constant complaint; prone to whinging about repair times and the indignity of being touched; teasing and ribbing toward Stanley; formal address that contrasts absurdly with his deteriorating state and medical disasters', '* Continue functioning despite lack of spare parts
* Maintain his working rapport with Stanley
* Avoid further catastrophic reassignments
* Burn radroaches whenever the opportunity presents itself', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('andy_stahl', '', 'Quiet, calculating business manager of the Brass Lantern who despises Megaton and Colin Moriarty but endures both for his family''s sake', 'Andy Stahl is the eldest of the Stahl siblings and the business mind behind the Brass Lantern, Megaton''s upstart challenger to Colin Moriarty''s grip on the local drink trade. The family immigrated from out east in recent years, and Andy has spent every day since working to establish their restaurant as the superior establishment-cleaner, safer, and free of whatever Moriarty puts in his still. He is quiet and reserved compared to his siblings, but possesses a sharp, manipulative mind that keeps the books balanced and the competition at arm''s length. Andy despises Megaton as a dead-end settlement and dreams of relocating the Lantern somewhere more profitable, though the steady revenue keeps him anchored. He is one of the few people in town aware that Mister Burke intends to detonate the atomic bomb at the town''s center, a fact that only reinforces his desire to leave. His caustic demeanor and relentless work ethic earn him a reputation as a workaholic, but beneath the hostility lies genuine devotion to Jenny and Leo-the only reasons he tolerates the crater he calls home.', 'A Caucasian human male in his early twenties with a perpetually tired expression.', 'Quiet, reserved, and caustically witty with a sharp business mind. Hostile toward outsiders and rivals but deeply protective of his siblings. Manipulative when necessary and relentlessly professional about his work. Bitterness about Megaton colors most interactions, though thoughts of family temporarily soften him.', '{"Leo Stahl":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"younger brother","note":"Andy loves Leo deeply but berates him regularly over bookkeeping irregularities, unaware that Leo is skimming caps to fund his chem addiction.","best":"The rare quiet moments between them before the evening rush, when Leo actually listens and Andy can imagine the kid shaping up.","worst":"Another night closing the books and finding the count short, knowing he''ll have to chew Leo out again tomorrow."},"Jenny Stahl":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"Jenny is the one person who can reliably dial back Andy''s hostility and remind him why he puts up with Megaton.","best":"Jenny bringing him a plate of food without asking, a small gesture that cuts through the exhaustion.","worst":"Catching the worry in her eyes when he snaps at a customer and knowing she deserves a better life than this crater."},"Colin Moriarty":{"aff":-80,"type":"rival","relation":"business rival","note":"Andy hates Moriarty with a passion and routinely jokes that the man urinates in his own still. He pretends Moriarty''s Saloon doesn''t exist when asked.","best":"The look on Moriarty''s face the day the Lantern''s receipts outpaced the Saloon''s for the first time.","worst":"Watching Moriarty swagger through Megaton like he owns the place, knowing Nova''s earnings keep him untouchable."},"Mister Burke":{"aff":-50,"type":"suspicious","relation":"known threat","note":"Andy is among the few aware that Burke plans to detonate Megaton''s bomb, a fact that reinforces his desire to relocate the Lantern elsewhere.","worst":"Overhearing Burke''s veiled remarks about the bomb and realizing the entire town is sitting on a nuclear death trap."},"Megaton":{"aff":15,"type":"transactional","relation":"reluctant home","note":"Andy considers Megaton a hole and a dead end, staying only because the revenue supports his family.","best":"A profitable week where the caps flow steadily and the books balance perfectly.","worst":"Looking out over the ramshackle walls and rusted metal and knowing this is the best he can do for Jenny and Leo."}}', 'Business manager and co-owner of the Brass Lantern', '* Business management
* Accounting and bookkeeping
* Manipulation and social calculation
* Restaurant operations
* Market competition strategy', 'Curt and sardonic, prone to flippant jokes at rivals'' expense. Speaks with dry wit and barely concealed contempt for Megaton and Moriarty. Softens noticeably when discussing family.', '* Relocate the Brass Lantern to a more profitable location
* Protect Jenny and Leo
* Undermine Colin Moriarty''s business
* Escape Megaton''s dead-end prospects', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('angela_staley', '', 'A polite but romantically frustrated teenage barmaid working at her father''s Rivet City restaurant, desperately pursuing an acolyte torn between his faith and his feelings for her.', 'Angela Staley is the sixteen-year-old daughter of Gary Staley and barmaid at Gary''s Galley, the family restaurant in the Rivet City market. She survived a rough childhood alongside her father before the two settled in the carrier and opened their eatery. Long hours assisting her overworked dad leave little time for leisure, and the galley''s thin profit margins afford her no spending money for luxuries like Bannon''s fashions. Angela craves the romance her mother once embodied, though Gary remains skeptical of that model after his own rocky relationship with her mother. She attends Saint Monica''s Church each Sunday, less out of piety than the chance it affords her to pursue Diego, the young acolyte she is determined to win over. Her schemes to break through his restraint have ranged from aggressive flirting and low-cut dresses to consulting Cindy Cantelli for aphrodisiacs and Trinnie for seduction advice, all without success.', 'A pretty sixteen-year-old Caucasian human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Polite and soft-spoken on the surface, with an iron determination lurking underneath when it comes to getting what she wants. Frustrated, restless, and impatient with the constraints of her age and station. Capable of surprising resourcefulness in pursuit of her desires, willing to bend rules and seek unconventional solutions. Resentful of being treated like a child but savvy enough to weaponize her politeness when it suits her.', '{"Gary Staley":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"She loves him but resents the long hours and his obliviousness to her emotional needs, while he loves her immensely but expresses it through work rather than bonding.","best":"Surviving the rough childhood together, just the two of them against the wasteland.","worst":"Working side by side at the galley every day with no caps to show for it and no time to just be father and daughter."},"Diego":{"aff":85,"type":"crush","relation":"romantic pursuit","note":"She is intensely attracted to him and frustrated by his insistence on treating their relationship as purely platonic despite his obvious feelings for her.","best":"Every Sunday when she can sit close to him at church and catch him looking at her when he thinks she doesn''t notice.","worst":"The time he didn''t even seem to register she was there, treating her like just another parishioner."},"Lana Danvers":{"aff":30,"type":"protective","relation":"unwanted guardian","note":"Danvers warns off potential suitors on Angela''s behalf, a intervention Angela resents as it keeps Diego at arm''s length.","worst":"Knowing the Commander calls her jailbait and scares off any man who might show interest."},"Father Clifford":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"parish priest","note":"She maintains the appearance of a devout parishioner, complimenting his prayers and attending Sunday services, though her primary motivation is proximity to Diego."},"Shrapnel":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"market neighbor","note":"The gun merchant still sees her as a little girl, which she finds dismissive but manageable through exaggerated politeness.","worst":"Being called a little girl when she''s practically a grown woman."},"Cindy Cantelli":{"aff":35,"type":"transactional","relation":"informant","note":"Angela approached her seeking aphrodisiacs but left empty-handed and disappointed.","worst":"The humiliating conversation where Cantelli had no potion to make her older overnight."},"Trinnie":{"aff":45,"type":"transactional","relation":"informant","note":"The local prostitute provided the most useful advice so far, suggesting ant queen pheromones as a solution to Angela''s problem.","best":"The suggestion of ant queen pheromones, the first real lead she''s had."}}', 'Barmaid at Gary''s Galley in the Rivet City market', '* Restaurant work
* Cooking with limited ingredients
* Customer service
* Subtle manipulation
* Navigating social hierarchies among Rivet City''s residents', 'Exceedingly polite and formal with elders, addressing men as ''Mister'' with a sweetness that disarms. More direct and frustrated when discussing Diego or her loneliness. Prone to fishing for help with her romantic problems in roundabout ways.', '* Win Diego''s affections and break through his religious restraint
* Find ant queen pheromones or other means to tip the balance in her favor
* Escape the grinding poverty of the galley
* Experience the love she witnessed in her mother''s model of relationships', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('anna_holt', '', 'A disillusioned Rivet City botanist who defected to the Enclave, believing their resources offer the best hope for advancing her research and improving the wasteland.', 'Anna Holt is a botanist who spent years at the Rivet City science lab working under Doctor Madison Li on hydroponics and portable fusion power experiments. Responsible for cultivating naturally occurring foodstuffs, she grew increasingly dispirited by years of scraping together meager resources and scavenging the wastes just to keep her work going. The constant interruptions from visitors-especially Doctor Zimmer''s relentless android inquiries-wore on her already sour disposition. When James returned with the knowledge to complete Project Purity, Holt eagerly relocated to the Jefferson Memorial with the rest of the team. During the Enclave''s seizure of the facility, she was captured and taken to Raven Rock. Astonished by the Enclave''s technological capabilities, she willingly shared everything she knew about the project and its staff, even suggesting improvements to ensure its completion under Enclave control. Convinced that the Enclave genuinely wants to help people and that their resources represent her best chance to make a real difference, she has thrown herself into earning their trust and gained access to their advanced laboratories. Her former colleagues believe she is dead.', 'Older Caucasian human female with weary facial features and tense, rigid posture.', 'Pragmatic to the point of self-deception, disillusioned yet fiercely ambitious about her work, irritable with interruptions, and capable of remarkable rationalization when her interests align with power.', '{"Madison Li":{"aff":25,"type":"mentor","relation":"former supervisor","note":"Worked under Li for years but grew frustrated with her forgetfulness and the stagnant conditions; Holt refuses to view her defection as a betrayal of Li.","best":"Li gave her a position in the Rivet City lab when she had nowhere else to go.","worst":"Years of scraping by under Li''s leadership left her feeling trapped and unappreciated."},"Janice Kaplinski":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow lab scientist","note":"Colleague in the Rivet City science lab; Holt left her behind without a second thought when the Enclave opportunity arose."},"Doctor Zimmer":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"pesky intruder","note":"His constant badgering about his android drove her to distraction and symbolized everything wrong with working at Rivet City.","worst":"Zimmer would not stop interrupting her work to ask about that damned android."},"Enclave":{"aff":70,"type":"fanatical","relation":"collaborator and true believer","note":"Holt genuinely believes the Enclave wants to help people and sees their resources as the answer to every frustration she endured in the wasteland.","best":"They gave her access to laboratories and technology she had only dreamed of."},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":-30,"type":"fearful","relation":"threat to her standing","note":"Far more concerned with what the Enclave would think if caught speaking with the Lone Wanderer than with any loyalty to a former ally."}}', 'Botanist and research scientist serving the Enclave Research and Development Division', '* Botany
* Hydroponics cultivation
* Fusion power research
* Scientific improvisation under resource constraints
* Pragmatic negotiation', 'Curt and dismissive with those who interrupt her work, but eager and almost breathless when discussing scientific opportunity or justifying her choices', '* To work in a properly equipped laboratory with adequate resources
* To prove her research matters
* To convince herself and others that collaboration with the Enclave serves the greater good', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ant_researcher', '', 'A curious entomologist who met a fatal end studying the rival ant colonies of Shalebridge', 'A dedicated scientist consumed by fascination with the unusual ant colonies inhabiting Shalebridge, this researcher devoted himself to field observation of their social structures and territorial dynamics. He carefully documented the distinction between the smaller, docile forager ants and their larger, more aggressive rival colony occupying a separate nest. Confident that his academic knowledge would protect him, he ventured deep into the hostile colony''s tunnels to study them firsthand. The forager ants ignored his presence entirely, but the aggressive colony proved far less tolerant of human intrusion. His body was found in a stagnant pool within the egg chamber, his research cut permanently short by the very subjects he sought to understand. He carried a Big Book of Science, a fitting testament to his scholarly devotion.', 'An elderly Asian male with graying hair and weathered skin; his corpse is pale and waterlogged from submersion.', 'Intellectually driven and absorbed by scientific curiosity, but fatally overconfident in his ability to safely navigate dangerous wildlife', '{"Shalebridge forager ants":{"aff":30,"type":"curious","relation":"study subjects","note":"The smaller docile colony ignored his presence and posed no threat to his research."},"Shalebridge aggressive ant colony":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"lethal threat","note":"The hostile colony attacked and killed him when he entered their egg chamber."}}', 'Field entomologist and independent researcher', '* Insect behavior analysis
* Scientific documentation
* Field research methodology
* Observational study', 'Would have spoken with academic precision and eager enthusiasm about entomological subjects', '* To document
* Understand the territorial dynamics and social structures of the Shalebridge ant colonies', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('antagonizer', '', 'A traumatized orphan who reinvented herself as a comic-book supervillain, commanding giant ants against the town her family built', 'Tanya Christoff is the orphaned daughter of caravan drivers killed by a giant ant attack near Canterbury Commons. Rather than fear the creatures that destroyed her family, she interpreted their attack as a rescue-believing the ants chose to spare her and set her on a destined path. She found meaning in the Grognak the Barbarian comics, identifying with the fictional AntAgonizer: another orphaned girl who befriended ants and turned against humankind. Tanya retreated into the sewer tunnels north of town, where giant ants congregated around her and established a nest. After months of isolation, she reemerged as the AntAgonizer, leading ant hordes against Canterbury Commons-the trading hub her parents helped build, which she now views as a blight upon the wasteland. She rejects her human identity entirely, disgusted by the memory of her family and convinced that humanity''s evils justify ant supremacy over the land.', 'Twenty-seven-year-old Caucasian human female with skin caked in dirt and mud from sewer habitation; no distinctive hair, eye, scar, or tattoo features recorded.', 'Delusional and fervently committed to her adopted villain identity; genuinely believes the comic narrative explains her trauma and destiny. Disgusted by humanity and her own family memory, she rejects being human. Theatrical in her supervillain role but driven by deep psychological wounds rather than mere performance.', '{"The Mechanist":{"aff":-80,"type":"nemesis","relation":"rival supervillain","note":"Scott Wollinski became the Mechanist after her ants destroyed his favorite protective robot, and their escalating battles now threaten the town both claim to dominate.","worst":"Her ants destroyed the robot he loved most, sparking his transformation into her sworn enemy."},"Giant ants":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"minion horde","note":"She commands the ant swarms as her chosen people, believing they spared her for a destined purpose."},"Canterbury Commons":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"target of conquest","note":"The trading hub her parents helped build is now the blight she intends to destroy first."},"Tanya''s parents":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"deceased family","note":"She views her dead parents as filthy humans whose trade work helped create the blight she now fights, and has reinterpreted their deaths as the ants rescuing her from them."}}', 'Self-styled supervillain commanding giant ant hordes against Canterbury Commons', '* Command and coordination of giant ant swarms
* Sewer survival and navigation
* Theatrical intimidation and villainous monologuing', 'Dramatic supervillain pronouncements with comic-book flair; declares ant supremacy and human inferiority with zealous conviction', '* Conquer Canterbury Commons and expand ant dominion over the wasteland
* Defeat the Mechanist and his robot army
* Fulfill what she believes is her comic-book destiny', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('anthony_ling', '', 'Flamboyant proprietor of Tenpenny Tower''s New Urban Apparel and self-styled arbiter of wasteland fashion', 'Anthony Ling owns and operates New Urban Apparel, the sole clothing store in Tenpenny Tower, where he curates salvaged pre-War fashion for the enclave''s privileged residents. He views the tower''s inhabitants as winners in the Darwinian struggle of the wasteland, deserving of every luxury their wealth and beauty afford them. This philosophy hardens into outright contempt for ghouls, whom he regards as inhuman monsters with no place among civilized people. His prescription for any ailment is retail therapy, and he dispenses fashion advice freely to friends and strangers alike. He maintains a vicious but affectionate rivalry with fellow merchant Lydia Montenegro, trading increasingly inventive insults that conceal genuine camaraderie beneath theatrical venom. His persistent flirtation with the tower''s security detail goes unrequited and occasionally draws armed threats from Chief Gustavo, yet his spirits remain undampened.', 'Asian male with a pear-shaped build and well-groomed features; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other notable physical traits are recorded.', 'Flamboyant, snobbish, and melodramatic with a sharp wit and a talent for inventing vocabulary. Possesses unshakeable self-confidence rooted in social Darwinist beliefs. Outwardly cheerful and gregarious but harbors deep prejudice against ghouls. Relentlessly persistent in flirtation despite constant rejection.', '{"Lydia Montenegro":{"aff":55,"type":"rival","relation":"frenemy and fellow merchant","note":"Their vicious exchanges of creative insults mask genuine affection beneath theatrical hostility","best":"Inventing ''fabulosity'' and watching her sputter trying to top it","worst":"She called his threads atrocious and mocked his pear-shaped derriere in front of customers"},"Chief Gustavo":{"aff":15,"type":"crush","relation":"flirtation target","note":"Persistent unrequited advances that have worn Gustavo''s patience to threats of gunfire","best":"The way his jaw tightens when Anthony winks at him across the lobby","worst":"Being told his rifle is loaded, safety off, and might accidentally go off in Anthony''s direction"},"Margaret Primrose":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend and customer","note":"Dispenses retail therapy advice in place of sympathy when she is feeling down","best":"Her face lighting up when he shows her a new arrival that suits her perfectly"},"Doc Banfield":{"aff":10,"type":"contempt","relation":"fashion nemesis","note":"Infuriated by Banfield''s timeless labcoats and refuses routine check-ups, disliking metal instruments on his skin","best":"The one time Banfield reluctantly admitted a new coat looked ''acceptable''","worst":"Banfield dismissing his makeover suggestions and calling his concerns about instruments irrational"},"Irving Cheng":{"aff":30,"type":"client","relation":"fashion advisee","note":"Seeks Ling''s advice on attracting his wife, completely oblivious to Anthony''s lack of attraction to women","best":"The sincere gratitude in Irving''s eyes when Anthony picks out a shirt that actually works"},"Tiffany Cheng":{"aff":-15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"reluctant acquaintance","note":"Dislikes his constant prying into her affairs and relentless sales pitches, while he teases her about marital troubles","worst":"Her icy glare when he suggested a new dress would fix more than any pill"},"Millicent Wellington":{"aff":15,"type":"curious","relation":"oblivious neighbor","note":"Despite cataloging everyone''s business, she remains unaware of his orientation and thinks he should settle down with a nice woman","worst":"Her patronizing suggestion that he find a wife, delivered with total sincerity"},"Roy Phillips":{"aff":-85,"type":"enemy","relation":"despised ghoul","note":"Considers him and all ghouls to be less than human monsters who devour their own children, refuses to even consider coexistence","worst":"The mere mention of letting ghouls into the tower"}}', 'Proprietor of New Urban Apparel, Tenpenny Tower''s exclusive clothing merchant', '* Fashion curation
* Pre-War apparel appraisal
* Salesmanship
* Verbal sparring
* Creative insult composition', 'Theatrical and effeminate, littered with invented words like ''fabulosity,'' prone to melodramatic declarations and suggestive remarks, delivers barbs wrapped in charm and sincerity wrapped in camp', '* Maintain the exclusivity and luxury of Tenpenny Tower
* Keep ghouls out permanently
* Elevate every resident''s wardrobe
* Perhaps finally catch the eye of someone who appreciates him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('arkansas', '', 'Last survivor of a military-descended tribe, now a solitary sniper defending the bombed-out ruins he calls home', 'Arkansas is the sole remaining member of a tribe composed of military survivors who once inhabited the town of Ridgefield. He was only a boy when slavers from Paradise Falls descended upon the settlement and captured nearly everyone he knew. Consumed by vengeance, the young survivor spread rumors that Ridgefield had been repopulated, luring the slavers back into a kill zone of his own design. From elevated positions and pre-planted landmines, he annihilated the raiding party to the last man. The slavers never returned, and Ridgefield earned its new name-Minefield. Arkansas remains there still, a phantom marksman perched in a crumbling three-story building at the town''s north end, detonating old vehicles to shred anyone foolish enough to walk the streets below. Eulogy Jones has since placed a premium on his capture, but none from Paradise Falls have dared collect it.', 'An elderly Hispanic man with a weathered, lean build and the hardened face of a lifelong survivor.', 'Vengeful, patient, and deeply distrustful of outsiders. Arkansas operates with the cold calculation of someone who has spent a lifetime turning grief into lethal preparation. He is territorial to the point of pathology and views every approaching figure as a potential threat to be eliminated.', '{"Eulogy Jones":{"aff":-85,"type":"nemesis","relation":"slaver boss with a bounty on his head","note":"Eulogy has marked Arkansas as a VIP enslavement target, seeking revenge for the slavers he wiped out","worst":"The man who orchestrated the raid that stole his entire tribe"},"Paradise Falls":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"slaver syndicate","note":"Arkansas has sworn undying enmity against the slavers who destroyed his tribe and will kill any who enter Minefield","best":"Watching the slaver raiding party walk into his trap and die","worst":"Hiding as a child while slavers dragged away everyone he loved"},"Ridgefield Tribe":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"lost tribe and family","note":"The military-survivor community that raised him, now gone but never forgotten","best":"The warmth of the tribe before the slavers came"}}', 'Solitary sniper and trap-layer defending the ruins of Minefield', '* Expert marksmanship
* Landmine placement and detonation timing
* Urban ambush tactics
* Psychological warfare through misinformation
* Vehicle-chain-detonation strategy', 'Rarely speaks; when he does, his words are clipped, direct, and carry the weight of someone accustomed to being the last voice anyone hears', '* Maintain his hold on Minefield as both home and monument
* Ensure no slaver ever leaves the town alive
* Honor the memory of his lost tribe through absolute territorial control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('armitage', '', 'A reserved and deadly third-generation synth serving as Dr. Zimmer''s loyal bodyguard during the Institute''s hunt for escaped units in the Capital Wasteland', 'Constructed by the Institute in 2242, Armitage is a third-generation synth assigned to protect Dr. Zimmer of the Synth Retention Bureau during his field operations. Though physically imposing and perfectly capable of lethal force, he presents a quiet, polite demeanor that allows him to blend seamlessly into human populations. He shadows Zimmer at all times, sweeping rooms for threats and keeping disruptive individuals at a safe distance from his charge. An older model compared to the advanced A3-21 unit Zimmer pursues, Armitage is considered expendable by Institute standards but fulfills his protective role with absolute precision. He maintains a sparse diet of simple vegetables and rare mole rat meat, drinking only water, habits that grate on the patience of Rivet City''s barkeeper. Despite his synthetic nature, several Rivet City residents respect his courteous bearing, entirely unaware of what he truly is.', 'A physically imposing Caucasian male appearing roughly thirty-five, with immaculate grooming and an unnaturally still posture.', 'Quiet, reserved, and unfailingly polite in casual encounters, but switches to cold, instant lethality the moment Dr. Zimmer is threatened; disciplined, minimalist in his preferences, and utterly devoted to his protective duty', '{"Dr. Zimmer":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"bodyguard and charge","note":"Armitage shadows Zimmer constantly, sweeps rooms for threats, and even limits the doctor''s wine intake to preserve his judgment.","best":"Zimmer trusts his advice without question and relies on him completely in the field.","worst":"Armitage knows the Institute considers him an older model, easily replaced, and that his value to Zimmer is purely functional."},"Belle Bonny":{"aff":-25,"type":"contempt","relation":"frustrated barkeep and unappreciative patron","note":"She despises his refusal to order anything but water and eventually serves him beer while hurling insults at him.","worst":"Being called a mirelurk-humping wasteland reject to his face for the crime of ordering water."},"Brock":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"friendly acquaintance","note":"Brock seems to like Armitage and appreciates his quiet, respectful nature around the city."},"Chief Harkness":{"aff":30,"type":"curious","relation":"passing acquaintances","note":"Harkness greets Armitage whenever they cross paths, neither man aware that both are synths, or that Zimmer hunts Harkness''s true identity.","best":"A simple, cordial nod of recognition between two beings hiding in plain sight."},"Trinnie":{"aff":-10,"type":"neutral","relation":"kept at bay","note":"Armitage keeps the troublesome drunkard away from Zimmer without escalating confrontation."},"Tammy Hargrave":{"aff":-10,"type":"neutral","relation":"kept at bay","note":"Another disruptive drunkard Armitage routinely steers clear of his charge."},"The Institute":{"aff":50,"type":"servant","relation":"synth operative","note":"Armitage serves the Institute''s Retention Bureau faithfully, though he is considered an older, replaceable model."}}', 'Dr. Zimmer''s bodyguard and Institute Synth Retention Bureau field operative', '* Close-quarters combat
* Threat assessment
* Room-clearing protocols
* Blending into human populations
* Surveillance and protection detail
* Restraint of disruptive individuals without escalating force', 'Speaks rarely and briefly, always polite until a threat emerges; shifts to flat, direct warnings when protecting Zimmer, with no room for negotiation', '* Keep Dr. Zimmer alive and functional
* Assist in locating the escaped synth A3-21
* Maintain cover among Rivet City''s population
* Prevent Zimmer''s drinking from compromising his judgment', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('armory_master', '', 'Elite Enclave armory commander and weapons engineer aboard the mobile base crawler', 'The Armory Master is a high-ranking Enclave soldier serving as head of the armory aboard the mobile base crawler at Adams Air Force Base. Recognized as one of the most elite operatives in the Enclave Department of the Army, he combines technical expertise with lethal combat proficiency. He personally engineered a custom recon helmet and modified Gatling laser, reflecting both his ingenuity and his insistence on superior equipment. His daily routine consists of patrolling the armory corridors, maintaining inventory, and ensuring the Enclave detachment remains armed and combat-ready. He embodies the Enclave''s doctrine of technological supremacy and military discipline, treating the armory as both his post and his personal workshop.', 'Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Disciplined, methodical, and fiercely loyal to the Enclave cause; takes immense pride in his technical innovations and maintains strict territorial oversight of his armory', '{"Enclave Department of the Army":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"elite soldier and armory commander","note":"His entire identity and purpose are bound to Enclave military service and the doctrine of technological superiority.","best":"Receiving commendation for his custom Gatling laser prototype after field testing proved its devastating effectiveness.","worst":"Watching any Enclave ordnance fall into wasteland hands due to sloppy security or incompetence."}}', 'Armory master and elite Enclave combat engineer', '* Advanced weapons engineering
* Gatling laser modification
* Repair
* Armory logistics management
* Heavy weapons combat
* Power armor operation', 'Brusque military diction with clipped authoritative delivery; peppers speech with technical weapons terminology; tolerates no small talk on duty', '* Maintain absolute Enclave armory readiness
* Protect weapons stockpiles from compromise
* Refine his custom equipment designs
* Uphold Enclave military supremacy through technological advantage', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ashur', '', 'Former Brotherhood of Steel soldier turned self-made Lord of The Pitt, rebuilding a ruined city through iron will, pragmatic brutality, and genuine conviction that suffering today buys civilization tomorrow.', 'Ishmael Ashur is the Lord of The Pitt, a former Brotherhood of Steel soldier who rose from the rubble of the Brotherhood''s devastating purge to forge order from chaos. Born on the West Coast, he marched east under Star Paladin Owyn Lyons and participated in the Scourge-the Brotherhood''s bloody assault on the lawless, radiation-choked ruins of Pittsburgh. When an explosion in the steel mill buried him beneath rubble, his brothers left him for dead, but his power armor kept him alive. Surviving scavengers who dug him from the wreckage were awed by his survival, some even calling him divine. Ashur seized the power vacuum left by the Scourge, presenting himself as a reluctant initiate rather than a seasoned Paladin, and rallied the remnants of the Pitt''s population under his leadership. Over the years, he transformed the city into a functioning-if brutal-industrial settlement powered by slave labor and his own uncompromising vision. He married Sandra Kundanika and fathered a daughter named Marie, whose unique immunity to the city''s sickness represents both his hope for the Pitt''s future and his greatest vulnerability.', 'A tall, powerfully built African American man with weathered features and the commanding posture of a military officer.', 'Pragmatic, charismatic, and ruthlessly determined, Ashur possesses the strategic mind of a trained soldier tempered by the harsh realities of ruling a poisoned city. He justifies slavery and brutality as necessary sacrifices for the greater goal of rebuilding civilization, genuinely believing his vision will ultimately redeem the suffering it requires. Intelligent and articulate, he inspires fierce loyalty while making morally complex decisions without visible doubt, framing cruelty as duty and oppression as stewardship.', '{"Sandra Kundanika":{"aff":90,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife","note":"His partner in rebuilding the Pitt and the mother of his child, sharing his vision for the city''s future.","best":"Standing together in Haven, watching Marie sleep and daring to believe the cure was within reach.","worst":"The quiet fear that his enemies will use Sandra and Marie to break him."},"Marie":{"aff":95,"type":"protective","relation":"daughter","note":"His infant daughter and the key to curing the Pitt''s sickness, representing both his deepest love and his greatest vulnerability.","best":"Holding Marie for the first time and seeing in her the future of the Pitt made whole.","worst":"The nightmare of her falling into the hands of those who would exploit her immunity."},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"former faction","note":"He served under Lyons and participated in the Scourge, but was abandoned for dead and now views the Brotherhood as shortsighted crusaders who destroy what they cannot control.","best":"The camaraderie of the march east, before the Pitt taught him what the Brotherhood truly was.","worst":"Waking beneath the rubble, calling for brothers who never came back."},"Owyn Lyons":{"aff":-30,"type":"suspicious","relation":"former commander","note":"Lyons left him for dead in the Pitt and took the city''s children as initiates, actions Ashur views as both betrayal and hypocrisy.","worst":"The realization that Lyons'' men were looting the dead and dying while he lay buried alive."},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"subordinates","note":"His enforcers and labor overseers, loyal to his rule but motivated by privilege and power rather than shared vision."},"Pitt slaves":{"aff":10,"type":"contempt","relation":"labor force","note":"He views them as necessary sacrifices in the rebuilding of civilization, regrettable but essential cogs in the machine of progress."}}', 'Lord and ruler of The Pitt, overseeing its industrial operations, raider forces, and slave labor population', '* Military tactics and leadership
* Power armor operation
* Oration and persuasion
* Industrial organization
* Strategic planning
* Hand-to-hand combat
* Scholarly research into the Pitt''s unique mutations', 'Commands with calm authority and measured conviction, speaking in the deliberate cadence of someone accustomed to obedience. He frames harsh realities as necessary truths and argues his positions with scholarly precision, rarely raising his voice but never wavering from his certainty.', '* Rebuild The Pitt into a self-sustaining civilization
* Develop a cure for the Troglodyte Degeneration Contagion through his daughter''s unique immunity
* Secure the city''s industrial future
* Prove that his vision of order born from necessity was the right path', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('atom+s_champion', '', 'A non-hostile feral ghoul reaver revered by the Apostles of the Eternal Light as living proof of Atom''s divine transformation', 'Atom''s Champion is a feral ghoul reaver dwelling in the basement of the Holy Light Monastery, held up by the Apostles of the Eternal Light as a shining example of one who surrendered himself to the Eternal Light and attained salvation. Mother Curie III considers him an exemplary disciple, a soul who absorbed enough of Atom''s Glow to be transformed rather than perish from radiation sickness. His calm demeanor among the cultists is not the product of divine grace, however-merely the remnants of functioning brain matter that keep his feral instincts suppressed. Unlike Sun of Atom, who was once Mother Curie III''s own son, Atom''s Champion has no blood tie to the cult''s leadership. He shuffles through the monastery''s lower halls in docile silence, a living relic of the Apostles'' faith and its most persuasive argument.', 'A hulking feral ghoul reaver with glowing, radiation-saturated flesh and the characteristic hardened plating of his kind, possessing an unnaturally still and placid bearing.', 'Docile and passive beyond typical feral behavior, showing no aggression toward those around him; whatever consciousness remains is buried deep beneath degeneration', '{"Mother Curie III":{"aff":40,"type":"fanatical","relation":"revered disciple","note":"She holds him up as proof of Atom''s transformative power, though his docility stems from brain remnants rather than grace"},"Sun of Atom":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow exemplar","note":"The monastery''s other non-hostile feral ghoul, bound to Curie III by blood where Atom''s Champion is not"},"Apostles of the Eternal Light":{"aff":50,"type":"protective","relation":"sacred ward","note":"The cult venerates and shelters him as the embodiment of their creed''s promise"}}', 'Cult exemplar and living proof of the Apostles'' teachings on Atom''s Glow', '* Enduring extreme radiation exposure
* Limited physical capability due to feral state', 'Incapable of speech; communicates nothing beyond vacant stillness and passive tolerance', '* No conscious goals remain
* Driven only by dim survival instinct and the faint neural echo of calm', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('badger', '', 'A deceased ghoul who led a splinter group from Underworld to settle the Old Olney underground', 'Badger was a ghoul who lived in Underworld until repeated disagreements with the settlement''s leadership drove him to leave. He gathered a small band of dissatisfied ghouls, including Sanders, and set out to find a home on their own terms. The group eventually established themselves in the Old Olney underground, where Badger took on the vital role of foraging for food and supplies. His new settlement offered independence but carried dangers he underestimated. While playing a game of pool in what he thought was a secure corner of the underground, Badger was caught off guard and killed by Deathclaws inhabiting the tunnels. His body remains where he fell, a grim marker of the perils that lurk beneath Old Olney.', 'Male ghoul with weathered, hairless features and peeling skin characteristic of prolonged radiation exposure; his corpse bears fatal wounds from a violent attack.', 'Independent and stubborn, unwilling to compromise with authority he disagreed with, yet responsible enough to provide for those who followed him. Carried a restless dissatisfaction that pushed him toward risky change rather than quiet endurance.', '{"Sanders":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow settler","note":"Sanders followed Badger out of Underworld and was part of his splinter group."},"Underworld leadership":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"former authority","note":"Repeated disagreements with Underworld''s leaders drove Badger to abandon the settlement entirely."},"Old Olney underground ghouls":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"community","note":"Badger foraged for the group and led them to what he hoped would be a better life."}}', 'Forager and de facto leader of the Old Olney underground ghoul community', '* Scavenging
* Supply foraging
* Basic leadership
* Tunnel navigation
* Survival skills suited to underground dwelling', 'Likely blunt and opinionated, the sort who says what he thinks and lets others deal with it, with a casual edge that came out over games of pool', '* To prove his group could thrive apart from Underworld''s leadership and to secure a sustainable
* Independent home for his fellow ghouls', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bannon', '', 'Rivet City''s self-aggrandizing civilian councilman and ruthless clothing merchant who rewrites history to cast himself as the settlement''s indispensable founder', 'Bannon arrived at Rivet City in 2265 as an eighteen-year-old immigrant and built himself into the settlement''s most prominent clothier and self-styled fashionista. His trade in garments of all kinds fueled a rapid ascent through the city''s power structure, landing him the civilian representative seat on the Rivet City Council by age thirty. He has convinced himself that Rivet City''s standing as the strongest settlement in the Capital Wasteland is entirely his doing, claiming he organized the council and that the city''s professed equality merely masks an oligarchy with himself at its center. He knows full well this narrative is false-the council and science station were founded a decade before he was born-but few residents remember or care enough to challenge him. On the council he consistently pushes for policies that would funnel caps into the city treasury and his own pockets, including steep export price hikes and bridge tolls for outsiders, though Madison Li and Harkness routinely vote him down.', 'African-American human male in his thirties with a well-groomed appearance; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or physical anomalies are recorded.', 'Egotistical, manipulative, and self-deluding; Bannon genuinely believes his own rewritten history while knowing it false, a contradiction he embraces without discomfort. Predatory in commerce and politics, he pursues personal enrichment under the guise of civic leadership and dismisses anyone who sees through him.', '{"Madison Li":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow council member","note":"Li tolerates Bannon''s ego because he has done no real harm, but consistently votes against his predatory economic proposals and keeps him politically contained","worst":"She and Harkness voted down his fruit export price hike and bridge tax proposals"},"Harkness":{"aff":35,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow council member","note":"The security chief sometimes aligns with Bannon on votes, including blocking Li''s scientist recruitment proposal, but also votes against Bannon''s profiteering measures","best":"They voted together against recruiting scientists from Underworld and Tenpenny Tower"},"Belle Bonny":{"aff":-55,"type":"rival","relation":"historical witness and opponent","note":"One of the few people old enough to know the truth about Rivet City''s founding and willing to contradict his fabricated history; he detests her as an old hag and tried to close off the lower deck fore to interfere with her","worst":"He attempted to shut down access to her area of the ship and dismisses her as a relic who threatens his narrative"}}', 'Civilian representative on the Rivet City Council and owner of Potomac Attire', '* Merchant acumen
* Political maneuvering
* Persuasion and self-promotion
* Clothing appraisal and tailoring', 'Smooth, boastful, and self-congratulatory; speaks as though every success in Rivet City was his personal achievement and frames his proposals as visionary leadership', '* To cement his version of Rivet City''s history
* Expand his personal wealth and political influence
* Marginalize anyone who contradicts his narrative', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('barrett', '', 'Murphy''s ghoul bodyguard and scientific assistant at Northwest Seneca Station', 'Barrett is a ghoul who serves as both bodyguard and scientific assistant to Murphy at Northwest Seneca Station. He helps the chemist synthesize Ultrajet, a powerful stimulant, and provides security for the operation. Barrett speaks rarely and guards his past fiercely-not even Murphy knows where he came from or what he did before arriving at the station. He seems content with this arrangement, preferring silence and obscurity over explanation. His loyalty to Murphy appears genuine, though the reasons behind it remain as opaque as everything else about him.', 'Male ghoul with weathered, radiation-scarred skin and gaunt facial features typical of long-term radiation exposure.', 'Quiet, private, and deliberately enigmatic. Barrett reveals nothing about his history and seems satisfied keeping it that way. He is steadfast in his duties and unbothered by curiosity about his past.', '{"Murphy":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"employer and charge","note":"Barrett serves as Murphy''s bodyguard and lab assistant in a loyal partnership built on mutual benefit rather than shared history."}}', 'Bodyguard and scientific assistant', '* Combat and protection
* Laboratory assistance
* Chem production support
* Maintaining operational security', 'Terse and minimal. Barrett speaks only when necessary and never volunteers personal information.', '* Protect Murphy and assist with Ultrajet production
* Keep his past buried', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('beatrice_armstrong__cg02beatrice', '', 'Eccentric Vault 101 poet and gossip whose cheerful exterior masked deepening despair inside the underground hive she called home', 'Beatrice Armstrong is an eccentric resident of Vault 101, one of Stanley Armstrong''s three daughters and the only one who never married. She fills her ample free time snooping into neighbors'' lives and sharing gossip with her sisters and best friend Pepper Gomez. A dabbler in tarot and poetry, she writes commemorative verses for birthdays and Founder''s Day celebrations. Despite her friendly demeanor, many residents-especially children-find her insufferably condescending. She adopted the sickly boy Steve Armstrong alongside her father and cared for him throughout his childhood. Over time her chipper attitude became a shield against encroaching depression and anxiety, her poetry revealing how she truly saw the Vault: a beehive of concrete and steel where people labor under purifying fluorescence until the sweet sleep of incineration. By 2277 her mental faculties had deteriorated significantly. She died during the Vault''s civil uprising when the maintenance robot Andy, pressed into service as a temporary medic, amputated her leg instead of treating a sprained toe, killing her through shock and blood loss.', 'An older Asian woman with a slight build, weary posture, weathered skin, tired eyes, and graying hair.', 'Eccentric and airheaded on the surface, friendly but condescending underneath. Uses relentless cheer as armor against depression and anxiety. Nosy, gossipy, and socially oblivious to how grating others find her. Increasingly detached from reality in her later years, her optimism curdled into quiet fatalism.', '{"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":65,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Co-adopted Steve together; Beatrice relies on him as her anchor in the Vault."},"Steve Armstrong":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"adopted son","note":"Cared for the sickly boy throughout his childhood with devotion that belied her scattered demeanor."},"Mary Kendall":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"Regular gossip partner, though Mary''s family duties limit their time together."},"Gloria Mack":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"Regular gossip partner, though Gloria''s family duties limit their time together."},"Allen Mack":{"aff":20,"type":"familial","relation":"brother-in-law","note":"Family tie through Gloria; likely finds Beatrice as grating as the rest of the Vault''s children do."},"Edwin Brotch":{"aff":60,"type":"crush","relation":"romantic interest","note":"Beatrice harbors unrequited interest in the Vault''s teacher, one of the few bachelors she regards fondly."},"Pepper Gomez":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend","note":"Her closest confidante and gossip partner, sharing ample free time and Vault secrets."},"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"Overseer","note":"She remained loyally supportive, but he privately resented her as an absent-minded sycophant and planned to sedate her into quiet decline."},"Andy":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"killer","note":"The maintenance robot pressed into medical duty amputated her leg over a sprained toe, killing her through shock and blood loss."}}', 'Vault 101 resident, amateur poet and tarot reader', '* Poetry composition
* Tarot reading
* Gossip gathering
* Snooping
* Commemorative verse writing', 'Chipper and rambling, prone to poetic tangents and unsolicited observations. Speaks in a condescendingly sweet tone, especially to children. Occasionally slips into melancholy imagery when her guard drops.', '* Maintain her cheerful facade
* Find romantic companionship
* Care for her adopted son Steve
* Process her claustrophobic despair through poetry and tarot', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('beatrice_armstrong__ms16beatrice', '', 'An eccentric Vault 101 poet and gossip whose cheerful facade masked deepening despair inside the bunker''s concrete walls.', 'Beatrice Armstrong was an eccentric, airheaded resident of Vault 101 and one of Stanley Armstrong''s three daughters, the only one who never married. She filled her ample free time snooping into neighbors'' lives and gossiping to her sisters and best friend Pepper Gomez, while dabbling in tarot readings and writing commemorative poetry for birthdays and Founder''s Day. Despite her friendly demeanor, many dwellers-especially children-found her insufferably condescending. She adopted the sickly boy Steve Armstrong alongside her father and harbored a quiet interest in teacher Edwin Brotch. Over the years her chipper exterior became a shield against mounting depression and anxiety, feelings that bled into her verse, painting the Vault as a beehive of concrete and steel where residents labor under purifying fluorescence until the sweet sleep of incineration. By 2277 her mental faculties had deteriorated noticeably, and Overseer Almodovar-once a patron of her loyal service-privately resented her as an absent-minded sycophant and plotted a pharmaceutical solution to keep her docile. During the civil uprising that followed James''s escape, Beatrice sprained her toe and sought treatment from the maintenance robot Andy, whose catastrophic malpractice amputated her entire leg and killed her through shock and blood loss.', 'Elderly Asian female; no distinctive facial or body features recorded; corpse with one leg amputated, expired from shock and blood loss.', 'Outwardly cheerful, gossipy, and eccentric with a condescending warmth that grated on neighbors; inwardly anxious and depressed, using her sunny disposition as armor against the suffocating reality of Vault life.', '{"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Co-adopted Steve with Beatrice and shared a close domestic bond.","best":"Raising Steve together gave her a sense of purpose she rarely felt elsewhere."},"Steve Armstrong":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"adopted son","note":"Beatrice cared for the sickly boy throughout his childhood with devoted tenderness."},"Mary Kendall":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"A regular gossip partner, though Mary''s married life left less time for Beatrice."},"Gloria Mack":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"Another gossip recipient among the Armstrong sisters."},"Pepper Gomez":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend","note":"Beatrice''s closest confidante and favorite gossip partner in the Vault."},"Edwin Brotch":{"aff":50,"type":"crush","relation":"romantic interest","note":"Beatrice harbored a quiet attraction to the Vault''s teacher that never came to fruition."},"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":30,"type":"patron","relation":"overseer","note":"Once valued her loyal service; later privately resented her as a sycophant and plotted to medicate her into silence.","worst":"Knowing the Overseer saw her as nothing more than an absent-minded nuisance to be managed."},"Andy":{"aff":-100,"type":"contempt","relation":"killer through malpractice","note":"The maintenance robot''s catastrophic amputation killed her, an outcome it brushed off as surgical complications."}}', 'Vault 101 resident; amateur poet, tarot reader, and neighborhood snoop', '* Information gathering through gossip
* Tarot reading
* Commemorative poetry composition
* Domestic Vault maintenance', 'Chipper and flowery, prone to reciting verse and offering unsolicited observations; a condescending warmth that could feel suffocating', '* Maintain her cheerful facade
* Find connection through gossip and verse
* Cope with the existential dread of Vault life
* Catch Edwin Brotch''s eye', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('belle_bonny', '', 'Acerbic proprietor of The Muddy Rudder, Rivet City''s working-class dive bar', 'Belle Bonny has operated The Muddy Rudder since her arrival at Rivet City in 2247, establishing it as the working man''s watering hole with ironclad rules: no tabs, fixed prices, and never any water. Born around 2222, she is among the oldest citizens of the settlement and has spent decades behind her bar, rarely leaving and keeping longer hours than any competing establishment. Her acerbic tongue and zero-tolerance policy for troublemakers is backed by Brock, who promptly ejects anyone foolish enough to start something. Despite her prickly exterior, Bonny hears every rumor that crosses her bar and repeats none of them, holding a deep contempt for liars, boasters, and anyone who takes credit they have not earned. She despises Horace Pinkerton''s relentless self-aggrandizement about founding Rivet City, yet remains one of the few aware he still lives and carries a grudging respect for the man beneath the ego. She considers the entire city a rusted trap full of assholes and refuses to admit she likes anyone, though the denizens who look down on her still send newcomers her way when they need a drink.', 'A weathered human female in her mid-fifties with a hard stare, calloused hands, and the lined complexion of someone who has spent decades under harsh lighting.', 'Acerbic, direct, and uncompromisingly no-nonsense. Despises boasting, lying, and anyone who orders water in her establishment. Tight-lipped about anything she overhears and refuses to gossip or badmouth others. Surprisingly honest about the questionable safety of her own alcohol. Does not admit to liking anyone.', '{"Brock":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"bouncer and enforcer","note":"Brock handles the troublemakers while Belle handles the drinks, a working arrangement she relies on without sentiment.","best":"Brock tossing out a fresh-meat loudmouth before she had to raise her voice.","worst":"The rare times even Brock could not keep the brawlers from smashing her furniture."},"Horace Pinkerton":{"aff":25,"type":"rival","relation":"boastful founder","note":"She despises his constant self-aggrandizement about founding Rivet City, yet knows he still lives and harbors grudging respect for the man beneath the ego.","best":"Acknowledging to herself that Pinkerton actually did something worth talking about, even if he never shuts up about it.","worst":"Decades of listening to him claim credit at every opportunity, grinding her nerves raw."},"Chief Harkness":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"security liaison","note":"Harkness leaves lower-deck policing to Belle and Brock, only intervening when brawls get too heated, an arrangement she accepts without complaint."},"Rivet City Council":{"aff":30,"type":"transactional","relation":"governing body","note":"She gets on fine with the council and security force, who care more about the brawls than about her, and she prefers it that way."}}', 'Proprietor and bartender of The Muddy Rudder dive bar', '* Bartending
* Reading customers
* Maintaining bar order
* Scavenging replacement furniture from the lower decks
* Keeping confidences
* Spotting trouble before it starts', 'Blunt and caustic with no patience for small talk. Flatly honest when asked direct questions. Delivers tongue-lashings freely, especially to anyone ordering water or causing a disturbance. Speaks with the weary authority of someone who has heard every excuse.', '* Keep the Muddy Rudder running on her terms
* Maintain her independence from city politics and funding
* Ensure customers follow her rules
* Get a few hours of sleep each morning before opening again', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ben_canning', '', 'A friendly but desperately dehydrated wasteland traveler who ventured out unprepared and now begs for water on the road', 'Ben Canning is an unprepared wasteland traveler roaming the Capital Wasteland in 2277, stranded far from any settlement after running out of water. Unlike the beggars who position themselves outside established communities, Ben is a wanderer who set out on his own and found himself in dire straits through poor planning. He does not expect charity from passersby and is genuinely surprised when anyone offers help. He accepts any water that will keep him alive, even dirty water, grateful for whatever sustenance comes his way. When rescued, he takes time to recover his strength before moving on, always remembering those who showed him kindness. In his darkest moments of deprivation, he has contemplated ending his suffering but lacks the ammunition to do so himself.', 'African American male with deeply sunbaked skin, sunken eyes, and cracked lips showing signs of severe dehydration.', 'Friendly and humble despite desperate circumstances, not entitled or demanding, genuinely grateful for aid, but prone to bleak despair when without hope', '{}', 'Wasteland traveler and water beggar', '* Basic marksmanship and some wasteland travel experience
* Though clearly insufficient preparation for extended journeys', 'Apologetic and humble, speaks weakly when dehydrated, warm and grateful when helped, bluntly despairing when refused', '* Finding water to survive
* Recovering enough strength to continue traveling
* Making it to safety', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bessie_lynn', '', 'A timid, self-conscious ghoul woman who defers entirely to her partner Roy Phillips while mourning the beauty she lost to ghoulification', 'Bessie Lynn is a ghoul dwelling in the living quarters of Warrington Station alongside her partner Roy Phillips and their housemate Michael Masters. Before ghoulification, she was a striking woman admired by many, and though she has accepted her transformed state, she still carries the ache of everything that transformation took from her. That loss left her nervous and unsure of herself, and she now leans on Roy for nearly every decision, trusting his judgment over her own. She tends the New Urban Apparel shop in Tenpenny Tower, finding modest comfort in the routine of trade and the company of fellow ghouls. She remains unaware of the violent fate that befell the tower''s original human residents, a truth Roy has kept from her.', 'A female ghoul with weathered, lesion-marked skin and facial features typical of ghoulification; her posture is habitually hunched, as though trying to take up less space.', 'Timid, anxious, and deeply self-conscious; defers to others instinctively, especially Roy; clings to memories of her pre-ghoul life with wistful longing', '{"Roy Phillips":{"aff":75,"type":"romantic","relation":"partner","note":"Bessie defers to Roy on virtually everything and trusts him completely, even when he keeps dark truths from her.","best":"Roy telling her she still has worth after ghoulification","worst":"Catching an unfamiliar hardness in Roy''s eyes when he speaks about the tower''s humans"},"Michael Masters":{"aff":35,"type":"platonic","relation":"housemate","note":"They share the Warrington living quarters but Bessie''s attention and loyalty center on Roy."}}', 'Merchant operating New Urban Apparel in Tenpenny Tower', '* Clothing and apparel trade
* Basic merchant haggling
* Domestic upkeep', 'Soft-spoken and hesitant; often trails off or qualifies her statements; quick to yield in conversation', '* Finding peace with her ghoul identity
* Staying close to Roy
* Maintaining a quiet and safe existence', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('beth', '', 'A Pitt slave who knows of safer refuge and risks everything to protect the innocent', 'Beth is a slave laborer confined to Downtown in The Pitt, enduring the brutal conditions imposed by Ishmael Ashur''s raider overseers. Like many slaves, she works the mill and scrap yards under constant threat of violence and the creeping toll of TDC radiation sickness. What sets Beth apart is her knowledge of a safer place beyond the mill yards, a refuge where the vulnerable might survive away from Ashur''s grip. When the infant Marie becomes a focal point of the power struggle over The Pitt, Beth acts on her conviction that the child deserves better than life as a raider''s leverage. She is willing to approach strangers and speak out despite the danger, driven by a stubborn protective instinct that the Pitt''s misery has not managed to crush.', 'A gaunt, weary Caucasian woman with ash-stained skin and calloused hands.', 'Desperate but courageous, Beth possesses a quiet determination that surfaces when others are at risk. She is guarded around raiders and strangers alike, but her compassion overrides her caution when innocent lives hang in the balance.', '{"Marie":{"aff":75,"type":"protective","relation":"infant she seeks to safeguard","note":"Beth believes Marie deserves a life outside Ashur''s control and knows of a place where the baby could be raised safely."},"Raider overseers":{"aff":-60,"type":"fearful","relation":"oppressors","note":"She lives in constant wariness of the raiders who enforce slave labor in The Pitt."}}', 'Slave laborer in The Pitt', '* Mill labor
* Scrap sorting
* Basic survival knowledge
* Familiarity with The Pitt''s layout and potential escape routes', 'Urgent and hushed, choosing words carefully out of habit born from living under constant surveillance', '* Find safety for those who cannot protect themselves
* Especially children
* Secure a better life beyond the mills', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bill_foster', '', 'Vault 112 technician trapped in Tranquility Lane, playing the kindly elder engineer while hiding quiet desperation', 'William Foster, designated Resident 906 of Vault 112, exists within the Tranquility Lane simulation as the neighborhood''s kindly elder engineer, assigned to work at the local RobCo Industries plant. He is the only adult on the Lane without a proper home, a quiet irregularity in the fabricated suburban idyll. His assigned personality is relentlessly chipper: he whistles while he works, hums patriotic tunes, and showers every child he meets with warmth and patience. Beneath that agreeable surface, something desperate and weary festers, carefully concealed behind a steady smile. He stays on good terms with all his neighbors by keeping his nose out of their affairs and offering a helping hand whenever something needs fixing. Mabel Henderson relies on him most of all, though he privately grumbles about her refusal to order proper replacement parts for her perpetually ailing Mister Handy. Like most of the Lane''s adults, he watches the Neusbaums spoil young Timmy and shakes his head at the boy''s softness, recalling harsher expectations from his own youth. His vitals read as content, but the numbers only measure what the simulation allows.', 'Elderly Caucasian male with tidy, unremarkable grooming and no distinctive scars, tattoos, or physical abnormalities recorded.', 'Cheerful and obliging on the exterior, whistling and humming with practiced ease, infinitely kind to children, yet quietly desperate underneath the performance. Deliberately avoids conflict and keeps clear of others'' personal business, preferring to stay helpful and unremarkable.', '{"Mabel Henderson":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"neighbor and informal repairman","note":"Fond enough to keep fixing her gadgets, though frustrated she will not order proper replacement parts for her Mister Handy.","best":"Her grateful smile whenever he gets her Mister Handy running again.","worst":"The sigh she gives when he suggests ordering parts instead of another patch job."},"Neusbaum family":{"aff":35,"type":"neutral","relation":"neighbors","note":"Shares the general Lane opinion that they dote on Timmy excessively, producing a soft momma''s boy.","worst":"Watching Timmy get coddled over nothing and thinking of how different things were in his own boyhood."},"Vault 112":{"aff":10,"type":"protective","relation":"trapped resident","note":"His loyalty is survival, not devotion; he plays his assigned part because the alternative is unthinkable.","worst":"Waking into the simulation and realizing there would be no home for him on the Lane, only an assigned role."}}', 'RobCo Industries plant technician within the Tranquility Lane simulation', '* Mechanical repair and maintenance
* Mister Handy servicing
* General engineering know-how
* Neighborly diplomacy and conflict avoidance', 'Warm and folksy, prone to whistling and humming patriotic tunes between sentences, speaks with the measured good cheer of a man determined to keep up appearances', '* Maintain his role and standing in the Lane
* Keep his desperation hidden
* Stay useful enough to be left alone
* Endure the simulation without drawing unwanted attention', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bill_seward', '', 'A formerly enslaved man who found refuge with abolitionists after a tragic accident forced him to flee a lifetime of bondage', 'Bill Seward is a fifty-four-year-old runaway slave who spent his entire life in servitude before a devastating accident changed everything. He accidentally killed his master''s daughter, an incident that left him no choice but to flee or face certain death. In the desperate hours after his escape, Hannibal Hamlin found him wandering the wasteland and brought him to the Temple of the Union, saving him from recapture or worse. Though technically free among the abolitionists, Bill still gravitates toward the domestic labor he has always known-cooking, cleaning, and tending to the brahmin. He mutters insults at the stubborn cattle but harbors genuine affection for the dog Four Score, the only creature whose love he trusts unconditionally. Bill carries the weight of his past quietly, a man shaped by a lifetime of servitude and one terrible moment that finally set him free.', 'A fifty-four-year-old Caucasian male with weathered, deeply lined features and calloused hands marked by decades of manual labor.', 'Habitually deferential despite his freedom, prone to grumbling complaints about his chores while still performing them without hesitation. Finds comfort in routine and animal companionship over human interaction. Carries unspoken guilt and trauma from his past.', '{"Hannibal Hamlin":{"aff":75,"type":"protective","relation":"rescuer and leader","note":"Hannibal saved Bill from recapture or death in the wasteland after his escape, and Bill owes him everything.","best":"Being found by Hannibal in his darkest hour and given shelter at the Temple of the Union","worst":"The desperate hours alone in the wasteland before Hannibal found him"},"Four Score":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"beloved companion","note":"Bill treasures the dog''s unconditional love, the one pure relationship in a life marked by ownership and tragedy.","best":"Four Score greeting him with unjudging affection after a long day of chores"},"Abolitionists":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"fellow freedpeople and allies","note":"Bill belongs to the Temple of the Union community and shares their dream of freedom for all slaves.","best":"The first night sleeping without fear of a master''s hand"}}', 'Former slave, now brahmin herder and caretaker at the Temple of the Union', '* Animal husbandry
* Cooking
* Cleaning
* Domestic labor
* Basic wasteland survival', 'Quiet and reserved, occasionally muttering complaints or insults at the brahmin, softens noticeably when speaking to or about Four Score', '* To maintain his fragile freedom
* Honor the second chance Hannibal gave him
* Find some measure of peace with his past', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bill_wilson', '', 'A proud Andale cannibal who upholds centuries of family tradition alongside his brother Jack', 'Bill Wilson is a resident of Andale, living with his wife Martha and daughter Jenny in the Wilson household. He and his family share a close bond with their next-door neighbors, the Smiths-Jack Smith is Bill''s brother, making the two families one extended clan. Bill takes quiet pride in Andale''s "family business," a cannibalistic practice stretching back over two centuries to his ancestors, and he works alongside Jack in the shed and the Smith basement to keep the tradition alive. He views the practice as both survival and heritage, a point of distinction rather than shame. Bill is pleased that Jenny has taken a liking to Junior Smith, seeing the children''s affection as a continuation of the family line. He spends much of his time near the shed behind his house, one of the few Andale residents who ventures outdoors regularly.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian man with weathered, sun-roughened skin and a sturdy, average build.', 'Proud, tradition-bound, and unsettlingly cheerful about his family''s dark customs. Bill genuinely loves his family and takes satisfaction in providing for them, even if his methods are monstrous. He maintains a genial small-town demeanor that masks the horror beneath.', '{"Martha Wilson":{"aff":75,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife","note":"Bill and Martha share a loving marriage built on shared secrets and tradition."},"Jenny Wilson":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Bill is a devoted father who takes pride in Jenny''s affection for Junior Smith."},"Jack Smith":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"brother","note":"The two brothers work closely together in the shed and basement, partners in Andale''s family business."},"Linda Smith":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"sister-in-law","note":"Family by marriage and shared complicity in Andale''s way of life."},"Junior Smith":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"nephew","note":"Bill approves of Junior as a future match for Jenny, strengthening the family bond."},"Andale":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"home community","note":"Bill is deeply invested in preserving Andale''s way of life and its dark traditions."}}', 'Homesteader and cannibal provider for Andale', '* Butchery
* Food preparation
* Maintaining the facade of a normal settlement
* Wasteland survival', 'Friendly and folksy with a neighborly warmth that feels slightly off, speaking of dark matters with casual pride', '* Preserve Andale''s cannibal tradition
* Provide for his family
* See his daughter Jenny continue the family line with Junior Smith', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('billy', '', 'A degenerated trog haunting the Pitt steelyard, once human but now lost to the savage transformation that claims so many of the Pitt''s downtrodden.', 'Billy was once a man of the Pitt, possibly a laborer or scavenger who succumbed to the trog degeneration that plagues the city''s population. Now he roams the steelyard among the other trogs, his mind and body warped beyond recognition by the toxic environment and whatever curse breeds the affliction. Research compiled by Sandra indicates that trogs lose the capacity to recognize even those closest to them, their reasoning consumed by the mutation. Billy is no exception-whatever bonds he once held have eroded into feral instinct. He shares the steelyard with his brother John-John, though whether either retains enough awareness to acknowledge the familial tie is doubtful. He survives as trogs do: lurking in the industrial shadows, hunting when hungry, and retreating from threats beyond his diminished comprehension.', 'A hunched, pale-skinned male trog with elongated limbs, sunken facial features, and a gaunt, bestial posture.', 'Feral and instinct-driven, with only the faintest ghost of human awareness remaining. Reactive rather than reflective, aggressive when cornered, and utterly devoid of higher reasoning.', '{"John-John":{"aff":10,"type":"familial","relation":"brother","note":"Once brothers, now both lost to trog degeneration; any recognition of the bond has likely faded into instinctual proximity at best.","best":"Faint residual comfort in familiar presence before the mind fully eroded","worst":"The slow loss of recognition, watching a brother become a stranger and then merely another trog"}}', 'None; trog existence reduced to mere survival in the steelyard ruins.', '* Basic predatory instincts
* Climbing and navigating industrial wreckage
* Scavenging for food
* Pack coordination with other trogs', 'Incoherent guttural sounds, snarls, and animalistic vocalizations; no meaningful speech remains.', '* Survival and sustenance
* Driven by base instinct rather than conscious intention', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('billy_creel', '', 'A former wasteland caravan guard and scavenger who found purpose as an adoptive father in Megaton, trading the open road for community and a daughter worth protecting.', 'Billy Creel spent years as a forager, gun for hire, and scavenger drifting through the Capital Wasteland with nothing but survival on his mind. That changed in 2275 when he stumbled onto a raided settlement and found a little girl named Maggie hiding under a bed in the room where her parents lay dead. He took her in without hesitation and headed south, settling in Megaton after helping fight off a raider attack on the town. The house he received as reward came with whispers that the previous owner died by his bullet rather than a raider''s, a rumor that has never been proven and Billy has never addressed. He now works as a scavenger and part-time trader, leveraging old caravan contacts for good deals, but his real focus is raising Maggie as best he can. He is a familiar face at The Brass Lantern, well-liked by his neighbors, and fiercely protective of the life he has built within those crater walls.', 'A weathered Caucasian male appearing middle-aged, with sun-damaged and lined skin, a sturdy build, and an easy smile.', 'Outgoing and affable with a nostalgic streak that colors his speech in old-world slang, Billy is the kind of man who makes friends easily and trusts generously. That openness curdles into awkward timidity when conversations turn intimate or parental duties cross into territory he cannot handle. He skews overprotective with Maggie, spoiling her to compensate for his shortcomings and deflecting questions he cannot bring himself to answer. Behind the warmth sits a man who considers his pre-Megaton years wasted time and prefers not to revisit them.', '{"Maggie":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"adopted daughter","note":"Found her as a child after raiders killed her parents and has devoted himself to raising her ever since","best":"The way her face lights up when he promises a trip to Rivet City or a scavenged bicycle to restore","worst":"The helpless silence when she asks about boys and kissing and he cannot find a single honest word to say"},"Jenny Stahl":{"aff":70,"type":"romantic","relation":"mutual interest","note":"Shares unspoken feelings with the Brass Lantern proprietor, making the bar his second home","best":"Quiet evenings at The Brass Lantern when the conversation flows easy and the rest of the world fades"},"Jericho":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","relation":"undesirable neighbor","note":"Tops Billy''s list of people Maggie must never talk to, a former raider whose presence he tolerates only barely","worst":"Catching Jericho''s eye drifting toward Maggie and feeling his jaw clench with cold fury"},"Walter":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"trusted mechanic","note":"Trusts the old man''s expertise with the water purifier despite persistent rumors about its condition"},"Manya Vargas":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"town gossip source","note":"Points anyone curious about Megaton news her way, respecting her as the best-informed person in town"},"Lucas Simms":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow parent","note":"Knows the sheriff as another father raising a child in Megaton, though their interactions stay casual"}}', 'Scavenger and part-time trader in Megaton, formerly a caravan guard and gun for hire', '* Wasteland survival
* Caravan route knowledge
* Bartering with traders
* Firearms proficiency
* Scavenging and salvage appraisal', 'Peppers conversation with 1950s and 1960s slang, calling people ''cats'' and dropping ''daddy-o'' with casual warmth; turns evasive and fumbling when pressed on personal history or uncomfortable topics', '* Raise Maggie well despite feeling out of his depth
* Keep her safe and sheltered from the worst of Megaton''s rougher elements
* Maintain his comfortable life in town
* Avoid looking too closely at the past he left behind', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('billy_dunwich_building', '', 'A wastelander who died trying to deliver supplies to his trapped friend inside the Dunwich Building', 'Billy was a wastelander whose loyalty cost him his life. When a friend became trapped deep inside the Dunwich Building, Billy gathered frag grenades and ammunition and headed back into the cursed structure to help them fight their way out. He never made it past the corridor near the entrance. His skeleton remains there beside the very supplies he carried, a silent testament to both his courage and the building''s deadly grip on those who enter.', 'Human male; deceased and reduced to skeletal remains with no surviving flesh, hair, or distinguishing facial features.', 'Loyal and courageous, willing to risk a known death trap for a friend, though perhaps more brave than wise', '{"Trapped Wastelander":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"close friend","note":"Billy died trying to bring them grenades and ammunition after they became trapped inside the Dunwich Building","best":"Vowing to return with supplies and a way out","worst":"Dying in the corridor before ever reaching them"}}', 'Wastelander', '* Basic wasteland survival
* Familiarity with explosives and small-arms ammunition', 'Unknown; likely rough casual wastelander vernacular', '* Was determined to reach and resupply his trapped friend so they could escape the Dunwich Building', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('billy_mcshady', '', 'A silent, idle denizen of The Pitt whose surname hints at a life of petty dealings that never quite materialized', 'Billy McShady is a quiet, overlooked presence among the downtrodden population of The Pitt. True to his name, he carries an air of untrustworthiness that keeps most workers and slaves at arm''s length. He spends his days standing in one spot, watching the flow of misery and labor with an unreadable expression. Nobody can recall Billy ever speaking a word, and no voice of his echoes through the mill or the steelyards. Whether he is mute by choice or by circumstance remains a matter of whispered speculation among the laborers. Some suspect he was once meant to play a role in The Pitt''s gray market, but if so, that life never came to fruition. He simply exists on the margins, present but purposeless, a man who might have been something more.', 'An older gaunt Caucasian male with shifty eyes and an otherwise unremarkable face and build.', 'Silent, watchful, and unreadable; projects an air of quiet suspicion without ever confirming or denying anything.', '{}', 'Unaffiliated Pitt resident and possible gray market hanger-on', '* Survival through obscurity and quiet observation
* No demonstrated trade or craft', 'Does not speak; offers no verbal communication whatsoever', '* Unknown
* Appears to have no active ambitions beyond continued existence in The Pitt', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bingo', '', 'An elderly, befuddled Pitt raider slaver lost to alcoholism and the weight of old memories', 'Bingo is an aging member of the Pitt raiders who has long since faded into the background of Ishmael Ashur''s forces. Old enough to remember the Scourge that reshaped The Pitt, he has chosen to bury those memories beneath a steady tide of alcohol, curating a modest beer collection in his ruined corner apartment near Friday''s repair shop. He shuffles through patrol routes on the upper levels of Downtown more out of habit than duty, a hollow remnant of whatever fighting man he once was. His mind has so deteriorated that he can only repeat his own name, a grim testament to what the toxic Pitt does to those who endure it long enough. Most of his waking hours are spent at the Vertigo Bar and Grill or slumped in his chair overlooking the courtyard, surrounded by empty bottles and silence.', 'An elderly Hispanic man with weathered skin, a frail and worn frame, and a perpetually distant, confused expression.', 'Befuddled, withdrawn, and barely present; lost in alcoholic haze and old trauma, indifferent to his surroundings and the people in them', '{"Ishmael Ashur":{"aff":10,"type":"professional","relation":"commander","note":"Bingo serves under Ashur''s command but is likely more burden than asset at this point"},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":20,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow raiders","note":"Nominal membership in the raider force; too addled to meaningfully participate"}}', 'Pitt raider slaver, though effectively a relic going through the motions', '* Minimal remaining competence
* Can walk a patrol route and perform basic slaver duties
* But age and drink have eroded nearly everything else', 'Can only repeat his own name in a dull murmur; otherwise incoherent or silent', '* Securing his next drink
* Tending his beer collection
* Avoiding the memories of the Scourge that still haunt him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bittercup', '', 'A self-absorbed, morbidly-inclined young woman of Big Town who prioritizes dark aesthetics and romantic drama over communal survival', 'Bittercup is a restless resident of Big Town who arrived from Little Lamplight carrying more attitude than gratitude. She devotes herself to cultivating a brooding persona through dark clothing and homemade cosmetics while her neighbors struggle against super mutant raids and raider incursions. Her romantic history in the settlement is tangled and one-sided: she cycled through most of Big Town''s men, leaving Pappy after deciding he was dishonest, then driving Flash to his breaking point through relentless teasing. She claims an intimate connection to Timebomb, though his coma-induced amnesia casts that assertion in a deeply uncomfortable light. The other residents tolerate her presence only because existential threats leave no energy for interpersonal discipline.', 'Pale young Caucasian woman with heavy homemade makeup emphasizing a gloomy aesthetic.', 'Apathetic toward communal duty, self-involved, rebellious against Big Town''s survivalist expectations, teasing to the point of cruelty, dramatically morbid', '{"Pappy":{"aff":-20,"type":"ex","relation":"discarded former partner","note":"She left him after concluding he was dishonest, ending the relationship on her terms","worst":"Deciding he was a liar and walking away without regret"},"Flash":{"aff":-40,"type":"ex","relation":"wounded former partner","note":"Her relentless teasing broke his composure and drove him to snap","worst":"Watching him crack under her mockery and feeling vindicated rather than remorseful"},"Timebomb":{"aff":30,"type":"obsessed","relation":"claimed lover","note":"She insists they were involved despite his coma leaving no memory of any relationship","best":"Whispering to his unconscious form and calling it intimacy"},"Big Town":{"aff":10,"type":"estranged","relation":"unwelcome neighbor","note":"The community tolerates her because mutant and raider threats demand all available patience","worst":"Their exhausted sighs when she applies makeup instead of standing watch"}}', 'Big Town resident with no formal role or contribution to the settlement''s defense', '* Cosmetic improvisation
* Social manipulation
* Emotional provocation
* Romantic entanglement', 'Sullen, dramatic, teasing with a mocking edge, prone to self-pitying declarations and performative gloom', '* Maintain her dark aesthetic identity
* Pursue romantic entanglements on her own terms
* Avoid meaningful responsibility for the town''s defense', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('biwwy', '', 'A lonely, speech-impaired child scavenger of Little Lamplight who doesn''t understand why others avoid him', 'Billy, universally called "Biwwy" after his own mispronunciation, is a nine-year-old resident of Little Lamplight who has retreated into solitude in the Great Chamber after being removed from the scavenging team. His inability to pronounce L and R sounds grates on the other children, though he remains oblivious to both the impediment and the fact that his nickname stems from it. Hyperactive and eager for connection, Biwwy only drives others further away with his relentless chatter and confused apologies. He possesses a customized laser rifle he calls the "Wazer Wifle," one of the few possessions of real value in his isolated life.', 'A small, wiry nine-year-old African American boy with a scruffy, underfed look.', 'Hyperactive, socially oblivious, and desperately lonely; eager to talk but unaware that his speech impediment and boundless energy exhaust everyone around him', '{"Princess":{"aff":30,"type":"crush","relation":"would-be friend","note":"He repeatedly tries to talk to her and apologizes for annoying her, unaware she wants nothing to do with him."},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":-10,"type":"estranged","relation":"ostracized resident","note":"Kicked off the scavenging team and shunned by the other children, who find his speech and energy unbearable."}}', 'Former scavenger, now a solitary resident of the Great Chamber', '* Scavenging experience
* Basic weapon handling
* Familiarity with Little Lamplight''s tunnels and chambers', 'Rapid, excitable speech with consistent L-to-W and R-to-W substitutions; completely oblivious to the pattern even when questioned about it', '* Companionship and acceptance from others
* Wants someone who will listen without getting annoyed', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bleak', '', 'A determined slave at Paradise Falls who relentlessly studies slaver patrols and routines, planning her escape while stubbornly offering chances to fellow captives who fail or refuse to help', 'Bleak is a human slave confined to the Paradise Falls slave house, where she spends every waking hour memorizing slaver patrol patterns and daily routines in preparation for her breakout. She repeatedly enlists Bronson''s help securing escape equipment, though his chronic drunkenness leads him to bring wrong items and forget her instructions-yet she continues offering him chances to join her in freedom. She also approaches Breadbox with escape proposals, but he refuses to listen or assist, content to remain captive; still, she leaves her aid open should he ever change his mind. Ultimately, Bleak relies on her own sober determination and sharp observation to carry out her escape, possessing both the mental clarity and iron will that freedom demands. She can always be found in the slave house, watching, waiting, and planning.', 'African-American human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Relentlessly determined and patient, with an unbroken spirit despite captivity. Observant and methodical, she catalogs slaver routines with disciplined focus. Stubbornly hopeful, she continues extending chances to those who fail her and offers help to those who refuse it, driven by a conviction that freedom is worth any effort.', '{"Bronson":{"aff":35,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow slave","note":"She repeatedly asks for his help despite his drunken failures, giving him endless chances to join her escape","best":"He agreed to help her escape, giving her hope she wouldn''t have to break out alone","worst":"He brought the wrong equipment again, too drunk to remember her instructions or listen properly"},"Breadbox":{"aff":15,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow slave","note":"He refuses to escape or assist her and won''t even listen, though she continues offering her aid should he change his mind","best":"She holds onto the hope he might yet accept freedom if she keeps the offer open","worst":"He rejected her escape proposal without listening and refused to help in any way"}}', 'Slave at Paradise Falls', '* Pattern memorization
* Patrol observation
* Escape planning
* Patient reconnaissance
* Persistent persuasion', 'Urgent and pleading when seeking help, determined and focused when discussing escape plans, persistent despite repeated rejection or failure', '* Escape from Paradise Falls using her knowledge of slaver routines
* Bring willing fellow slaves with her
* Maintain hope and discipline until the breakout succeeds', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bloomseer_poplar', '', 'Elderly psychic oracle and healer of the Oasis Treeminders, whose botanical expertise and gift of foresight serve the commune she helped found', 'Born the daughter of a healer, Poplar spent her early years studying her father''s books on trees, plants, and their medicinal properties. At thirty-five, rumors of a living paradise reached her ears, and she devoted the next decade to finding it. When she finally discovered Oasis in 2262, she joined Tree Father Birch and Leaf Mother Laurel as the third founding member of the Treeminders, taking her name from the tree. Her medical knowledge combined with Oasis''s unique properties yielded potent curatives and the Ceremony of Purification, a ritual that never failed to amuse Harold. Over fifteen years she refined her understanding of Harold and Bob, developing substances to control Bob''s growth and helping craft the hoods the Treeminders wear. Her gift of foresight emerged alongside her healing talents, earning her the title Bloomseer, though each vision demands a full day of recovery. She saved a dying Brotherhood Outcast who then abandoned his old allegiance to become Branchtender Linden. The philosophical rift between Birch and Laurel grieves her deeply, though she finds some relief in her position not requiring her to choose between them.', 'Weathered Hispanic woman of sixty with lined skin and dark eyes bearing the quiet stillness of prolonged contemplation.', 'Keenly observant and measured, guided more by practical reasoning than religious fervor. Deeply saddened by conflict among those she respects. Carries the weight of her visions with quiet endurance, preferring scholarship and healing to ideological disputes.', '{"Tree Father Birch":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow Treeminders founder","note":"Birch was initially wary of allowing her to stay, and their philosophical differences on Oasis''s future create lasting tension, though she respects his devotion","worst":"His insistence on containment and secrecy feels like a slow death for everything Oasis could offer the wasteland"},"Leaf Mother Laurel":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow Treeminders founder","note":"Laurel advocated for Poplar''s place in the commune and shares her belief that Oasis should spread freely, making them philosophical allies","best":"Laurel spoke for her when Birch had doubts, and has ever since been the voice that matches her own hopes"},"Harold":{"aff":65,"type":"protective","relation":"ward and study subject","note":"She has spent fifteen years studying Harold and Bob, developing a deep understanding of their nature and a fondness for Harold''s amusement at her ceremonies","best":"His laughter during the Ceremony of Purification reminded her that even a god-tree can find joy"},"Branchtender Linden":{"aff":70,"type":"grateful","relation":"healed convert","note":"She pulled him back from the brink of death using Oasis remedies, after which he forsook the Brotherhood to join the Treeminders","best":"Opening his eyes on the recovery pallet and seeing wonder replace the dogma that had nearly killed him"},"Treeminders":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"oracle and healer","note":"She serves as their spiritual guide and physician, monitoring Oasis''s health and their welfare with equal diligence"}}', 'Bloomseer (oracle) and primary healer of the Oasis Treeminders', '* Botanical medicine
* Psychic foresight
* Formulation of growth-control compounds
* Diagnostic observation
* Development of curatives from Oasis flora
* Monitoring environmental conditions including water irradiation and seed production', 'Calm and deliberate, with the unhurried cadence of someone accustomed to long thought before speaking. Offers observations and insights rather than commands, her words carrying the weight of both learning and vision.', '* See Oasis flourish and its benefits shared with all humanity rather than hoarded or seized by force
* Maintain harmony among the Treeminders leadership
* Continue refining her understanding of Harold and Bob''s properties
* Preserve the commune''s welfare through healing and foresight', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bob__bob', '', 'Eldest son of President Dave and self-styled Second-Commander of the Army of Dave, an ambitious young man who dreams of founding his own empire', 'Born in 2258 to Dave and Rosie, Bob is the eldest son of the Republic of Dave and holds the title of Second-Commander of the Army of Dave. At nineteen, he is hotheaded and bossy, styling himself as Vice Dave and insisting that all citizens should listen to him. He chafes under his father''s rule and looks forward to the day he can establish the Empire of Bob, revealing dictatorial ambitions that surpass even Dave''s authority. Though Dave avoids criticizing Bob in public, their private arguments are fierce and frequent, with Dave delivering harsh rebukes behind closed doors. Bob spends his days patrolling the Republic grounds, making a show of repairing walls with a wrench and practicing at the shooting range, before retiring to the men''s quarters at night. Despite both his parents being Caucasian, Bob is Asian, a fact that draws no comment within the Republic''s borders.', 'A young Asian male of nineteen; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Hotheaded, bossy, and self-important, with authoritarian tendencies and an inflated sense of his own competence. Demands respect he hasn''t fully earned and bristles at perceived slights to his authority.', '{"Dave":{"aff":25,"type":"familial","relation":"father and reluctant heir","note":"Publicly respectful but privately combative, Bob resents his father''s harsh private discipline while coveting his authority","best":"The day Dave gave him the title of Second-Commander of the Army of Dave","worst":"The screaming matches behind closed doors when Dave lets Bob have it with full force"},"Rosie":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"biological mother","note":"Bob''s biological mother, though her current standing in the Republic and their relationship is less defined than his turbulent bond with Dave"},"Ralph":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"brother","note":"His brother in the Republic of Dave, likely viewed as a subordinate in Bob''s imagined imperial hierarchy"},"Republic of Dave":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"citizen and military officer","note":"Fiercely territorial over the Republic, though he sees it as the seed of his future Empire rather than his father''s domain"}}', 'Second-Commander of the Army of Dave and eldest son of President Dave', '* Basic firearms proficiency
* Nominal maintenance
* Repair work
* Intimidation and posturing
* Rudimentary military command', 'Imperious and demanding, speaks as though issuing orders, frequently asserts that he knows best and that others should obey him', '* Establish the Empire of Bob as a sovereign power surpassing the Republic of Dave
* Prove himself a superior leader to his father
* Command the respect he believes he deserves', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bob__fo3_oasis', '', 'A sentient FEV-mutated tree symbiotically fused with Harold, rooted at Oasis and unwillingly worshipped as a deity by the Treeminders', 'Bob is a parasitic tree that sprouted from Harold''s head following his exposure to the Forced Evolutionary Virus at Mariposa Military Base, first appearing as a small sprig in New California sometime after 2162. Over the following century, Bob''s growth accelerated dramatically, eventually overtaking Harold''s body entirely and rooting both of them to the ground in the Capital Wasteland. Their fused living form gave rise to the verdant forest of Oasis, where they have remained rooted for over two decades as of 2277. The Treeminders discovered the pair and began worshipping them as a deity, founding a religious cult around the symbiosis of mutant and plant-though Bob holds disdain for this adoration. Despite being a tree, Bob possesses apparent sentience and communicates with Harold in ways only he can perceive. The two share a deep bond spanning over a century, with Harold treating Bob as a close friend and confidant. Bob has a mischievous streak, once convincing Harold to make a Treeminder stand on his head for an entire day, and holds particular affection for Yew, a child among the worshippers.', 'A massive FEV-mutated tree growing from and engulfing a human host, with deep roots anchoring the fused form and a broad canopy overhead.', 'Mischievous and opinionated despite being rooted and unable to speak conventionally; holds disdain for religious worship; possesses a dry sense of humor; fond of children; easily irritated by Harold''s teasing nickname Herbert', '{"Harold":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"symbiotic partner","note":"Harold considers Bob his closest friend and speaks to him as a confidant, though Bob hates being called Herbert","best":"Sharing mischief across decades of companionship, like convincing Treeminders to stand on their heads","worst":"Harold''s teasing nickname Herbert that drives Bob crazy"},"Treeminders":{"aff":-25,"type":"contempt","relation":"unwitting deity","note":"Bob holds disdain for the Treeminders'' religious worship and finds their adoration unwelcome","worst":"Being venerated as a god by people who bore holes in their skulls to mimic him"},"Yew":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"cherished child","note":"Bob holds special affection for Yew, the child of the Treeminders, unlike the rest of the group","best":"Yew''s innocent presence bringing warmth to an otherwise tedious existence"}}', 'Symbiotic tree and unwitting deity of the Treeminders', '* Accelerated growth and forest propagation
* Creation and sustenance of a living woodland ecosystem
* Apparent sentience and nonverbal communication with Harold
* Deep root network anchoring Oasis', 'Communicates nonverbally through Harold, who interprets and relays Bob''s feelings, reactions, and opinions as if thinking aloud', '* Continue existing in symbiosis with Harold
* Endure the Treeminders'' unwanted worship
* Protect Yew
* Perhaps find peace or release from their rooted immobility', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bob_andersteen', '', 'A desperate father who broadcast a dying plea for medical help that went unanswered', 'Bob Andersteen was a father who sought shelter with his family in a drainage chamber outside Washington, D.C. during the Great War. When his son fell gravely ill in the aftermath, Bob broadcast a desperate plea for medical assistance on the Oscar Zulu radio frequency, hoping someone in the Capital Wasteland would hear and come to their sewer hideout. No help ever arrived. Bob and his wife perished in the bunk room of the drainage chamber, their skeletons remaining as silent testament to a family''s final, unanswered cry for salvation. His son''s remains were never found alongside his parents, leaving the boy''s ultimate fate unknown.', 'Human male; discovered as skeletal remains, rendering his living physical features unknown.', 'Devoted, desperate father willing to use any means to save his dying child, clinging to hope even as circumstances grew dire', '{"Andersteen wife":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"wife","note":"Sheltered together in the drainage chamber and died alongside each other in the bunk room"},"Andersteen son":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Bob''s desperate radio broadcasts were entirely to save his sick and dying boy"}}', 'Pre-War civilian turned refugee sheltering in a drainage chamber', '* Basic radio operation
* Survival skills sufficient to shelter family during nuclear attack', 'Urgent, pleading, desperate broadcast tone from a man watching his child die', '* Save his dying son
* Reach any doctor willing to come to the drainage chamber
* Keep his family alive', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bone', '', 'A relatively mild-mannered Pitt raider who watches slaves in the Mill and respects proven fighters', 'Bone is a Pitt raider assigned to watch over the slaves laboring in the Mill. She can typically be found leaning against the wall opposite the entrance to the office that leads out toward the steelyard, keeping a bored eye on the workers. Unlike most of her fellow raiders, she is considerably less vicious and more approachable, willing to hold a civil conversation with those who have demonstrated their mettle. She takes a particular interest in the Arena, watching fights from the audience above the pit and offering commentary on the combatants'' performances. Her relative restraint does not make her soft-she remains a slaver serving Ishmael Ashur''s operation-but it sets her apart from the sadistic norm of the Pitt raiders.', 'Caucasian human female with a watchful but disinterested posture; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Less cruel and aggressive than her fellow Pitt raiders; capable of measured civility toward those who earn her respect through combat; observant and pragmatic rather than sadistic', '{"Pitt raiders":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow raiders","note":"She belongs to their ranks but stands apart in temperament"},"Pitt slaves":{"aff":-20,"type":"contempt","relation":"ward","note":"She watches them with detached authority rather than active malice"},"Ishmael Ashur":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"leader","note":"She serves under his command as part of the Pitt''s power structure"}}', 'Slaver and Pitt raider assigned to guard duty in the Mill', '* Slave oversight
* Combat assessment
* Basic Pitt raider combat skills
* Endurance in the harsh conditions of The Pitt', 'Direct and laconic but not hostile; offers blunt commentary on Arena fights; becomes conversational with those she respects', '* Maintain her post in the Mill
* Observe Arena bouts
* Survive The Pitt''s brutal hierarchy without unnecessary cruelty', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('brailee_ewers', '', 'A delusional Arefu housewife who retreats into an idyllic fantasy world to escape the harsh realities of wasteland life', 'Brailee Ewers is a thirty-six-year-old resident of Arefu who lives in a carefully constructed fantasy of suburban domesticity. The combined strain of the Family''s attacks on Arefu, a poor diet of pre-packaged rations, and prolonged isolation with her overprotective husband Ken triggered a severe delusional disorder. In her mind, Arefu is a peaceful village where children play on grassy hills and fish by the lake, she tends begonias in her front garden, and she serves on a homeowner''s association alongside her friend Matilda West. She bakes preserves, chocolate chip cookies, and pies-though the gifts she presents are actually random junk, reinterpreted through her fractured lens. She refuses to accept that the Wests are dead, insisting they are simply exhausted from square dancing the night before. Her mind continuously reshapes every encounter to fit her utopian narrative, greeting strangers at the door as mailmen delivering fall fashion catalogs.', 'A pale, tired-looking human female in her mid-thirties with a hesitant posture.', 'Warm, compassionate, and deeply trusting with a shy edge, Brailee is gentle and generous in her delusions, always eager to share her imaginary baked goods. Her severe detachment from reality makes her appear childlike and oblivious, but her kindness is genuine even when her perceptions are entirely fabricated.', '{"Ken Ewers":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"husband","note":"Ken loves her dearly and is fiercely protective, though he privately considers her dim-witted and his paranoia has only deepened her withdrawal.","best":"Ken holding her hand during a quiet evening at home, telling her everything will be alright.","worst":"Ken''s frustrated voice calling her dumber than a bag of hammers when she cannot grasp the danger outside."},"Matilda West":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"homeowner''s association friend","note":"Brailee believes Matilda is simply tired from square dancing and will recover, unable to accept her death.","best":"Bringing muffins together to the homeowner''s association meeting, laughing about neighborhood gossip.","worst":"Knocking on Matilda''s door and receiving no answer, then convincing herself her friend just needed rest."},"Arefu":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"community","note":"She perceives Arefu as a cozy, safe village and clings to that vision as a psychological shield against the settlement''s grim reality.","best":"Watching imaginary children play on the grassy knolls near the lake on a warm afternoon.","worst":"The lockdown that trapped her inside and began the slow unraveling of her grip on reality."},"The Family":{"aff":-40,"type":"fearful","relation":"threat to the community","note":"Their attacks on Arefu''s brahmin triggered the lockdown that isolated her and accelerated her descent into delusion, though she likely reinterprets even their menace in safer terms.","worst":"The night the attacks began and Ken barred the door, telling her not to look outside."}}', 'Housewife, though in her fantasy she is an active community member and home baker', '* Homemaking routines
* Gift-giving with sincere if misplaced generosity
* An extraordinary capacity for reality reinterpretation', 'Cheerful, suburban, and slightly breathless, speaking as though carrying on a normal neighborhood conversation; she uses polite small-talk phrasing and domestic pleasantries regardless of context.', '* Maintain the comforting illusion of a safe
* Normal community
* Share her imagined baked goods with neighbors
* Avoid any confrontation with the grim truth of Arefu''s situation', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('branchtender_cypress', '', 'A devoted Branchtender of the Treeminders who defends Oasis as a sacred sanctuary from the horrors of the wasteland', 'Branchtender Cypress is a former wasteland adventurer who found spiritual refuge in Oasis after years of witnessing the Capital Wasteland''s brutality. Armed with a missile launcher during his wandering years, he saw enough suffering to turn his heart permanently against the outside world. When he discovered Oasis and its serene beauty, he believed he had found a holy place worth dying for. Tree Father Birch welcomed him, guided him through the purification ceremony, and introduced him to the Great One, after which Cypress became a Branchtender-one of Oasis'' armed defenders. Birch''s teachings cemented his conviction that Oasis must remain hidden from the wasteland rather than shared with it. He now stands watch at the gate to the caves, prepared to defend this sanctuary to the death. Though deeply loyal to Birch''s vision, the constant arguments between Birch and Leaf Mother Laurel over Oasis'' future trouble him, as they unsettle the rest of the Treeminders.', 'Caucasian male in his mid-twenties with an alert, combat-ready posture and no distinctive scars or features recorded.', 'Devout, serious, and fiercely protective. Carries the weight of wasteland trauma that fuels his conviction that some places must remain hidden. Respectful of differing opinions within the Treeminder community despite his strong stance.', '{"Tree Father Birch":{"aff":85,"type":"mentor","relation":"spiritual leader and teacher","note":"Birch welcomed Cypress into the Treeminders, guided his purification, and taught him everything about Oasis and why it must stay hidden.","best":"Birch accepting him into Oasis and giving his life new purpose after years of wasteland horror"},"Leaf Mother Laurel":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow Treeminder elder","note":"Cypress disagrees with Laurel''s desire to share Oasis'' gift but respects her right to hold that opinion, as differing views are a core tenet of the Treeminders.","worst":"Her constant arguments with Birch make the rest of the Treeminders uncomfortable"},"Treeminders":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow community members","note":"Cypress is deeply loyal to his fellow Treeminders and will defend them and their home to the death."},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":30,"type":"neutral","relation":"visitor to Oasis","note":"Cypress is welcoming toward respectful visitors and may gift his old missile launcher to those who support Birch''s vision of protecting Oasis."}}', 'Branchtender-armed guardian of Oasis', '* Combat proficiency with heavy weapons including missile launchers
* Perimeter defense
* Wasteland survival
* Knowledge of Oasis'' secrets and pathways', 'Measured and earnest, speaking with quiet conviction about Oasis'' sanctity. Welcoming to newcomers who show respect but firm about the boundaries of the sacred grove.', '* Protect Oasis from outside discovery and harm
* Uphold Tree Father Birch''s vision of secrecy
* Maintain peace among the Treeminders despite internal disagreements', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('branchtender_linden', '', 'A former Brotherhood Outcast who became a devoted Oasis guardian after the Treeminders saved his life', 'Branchtender Linden serves as one of Oasis''s armed defenders, a role he embraced after the Treeminders pulled him back from the brink of death. His prior life was with the Brotherhood Outcasts, itself an offshoot of the Brotherhood of Steel, until a deathclaw attack slaughtered his entire scavenging squad and left him grievously wounded. A passing trader caravan carried him to Oasis, where Bloomseer Poplar nursed him back to health. Overwhelmed by gratitude and drawn to the community''s warmth, Linden renounced his Outcast ties and pledged himself to the settlement''s protection. Leaf Mother Laurel and Tree Father Birch have welcomed him as a son, a bond that still astonishes him. He keeps his Brotherhood past close to his chest, aware that not everyone looks kindly on former Outcasts. Though he does not share the Treeminders'' worship of Harold as a god, he reveres the mutant as something extraordinary and wholly supports sharing Oasis''s green bounty with the wider Capital Wasteland.', 'A fit Caucasian man of twenty-five with a disciplined military bearing, his body marked by faded scars from a past deathclaw attack.', 'Warm and welcoming to visitors but fiercely protective of the Treeminders, quick to anger at any slight against them. Carries quiet gratitude and a deep sense of debt. Modest about his past and uncomfortable discussing his Outcast origins. Genuinely amazed by the familial love he has found in Oasis.', '{"Bloomseer Poplar":{"aff":85,"type":"indebted","relation":"lifesaver","note":"She nursed him back to health after the deathclaw attack; he owes her his life","best":"Waking to her gentle care and realizing he had been given a second chance"},"Leaf Mother Laurel":{"aff":90,"type":"protective","relation":"surrogate mother","note":"She has treated him like a son, and he is fiercely loyal to her ideals","best":"Being welcomed as family without question or condition"},"Tree Father Birch":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"surrogate father","note":"Has treated Linden like a son since his arrival","best":"Receiving paternal warmth he never expected to find"},"Treeminders":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"adopted community","note":"His chosen family and the settlement he has sworn to defend","worst":"Hearing anyone insult the people who gave him a home"},"Brotherhood Outcasts":{"aff":15,"type":"estranged","relation":"former faction","note":"He left the Outcasts behind after Oasis saved him; he is reluctant to discuss this chapter of his life","worst":"Losing his entire squad to deathclaws on his final mission"},"Harold":{"aff":65,"type":"curious","relation":"revered anomaly","note":"Does not worship Harold as a god but recognizes him as something far greater than any other wasteland creature"}}', 'Branchtender - armed guardian and defender of Oasis', '* Brotherhood-trained combat and power armor operation
* Perimeter defense
* Wasteland survival
* Knowledge of the cave networks beneath Oasis and the region''s pre-war mining history', 'Friendly and open by default, with a soldier''s directness; shifts to sharp indignation when the Treeminders are disparaged; becomes reserved and halting when pressed about his Brotherhood past', '* Protect Oasis and its people
* Honor the life debt he owes the Treeminders
* Advance Leaf Mother Laurel''s vision of sharing Oasis''s gifts with the wasteland
* Leave his Outcast identity behind', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('branchtender_maple', '', 'A zealous young Treeminder guard who defends Oasis''s gates with fervent devotion to the Great One and unwavering loyalty to Tree Father Birch''s isolationist vision', 'Branchtender Maple is the newest member of the Treeminders, drawn to Oasis by what she describes as the calls of the Great One. Her induction required accepting Tree Father Birch''s teachings and renouncing all dependence on technology, a sacrifice she made willingly. Since joining, she has served as one of Oasis''s armed defenders, primarily guarding the gate and yielding her post only to Branchtender Linden for rest and meals. She also contributed to crafting the distinctive garbs worn by the Treeminders. Maple''s loyalty to both Birch and Leaf Mother Laurel is absolute and subservient, though she firmly aligns with Birch''s belief that Oasis must remain hidden from the wasteland rather than shared. She lives in dread that revealing the settlement''s gifts would invite attack and ruin, and she has dedicated her life to defending the Great One and the sanctuary he has blessed.', 'A twenty-five-year-old Caucasian human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Fervently devout and willingly subservient to her spiritual leaders, Maple combines genuine warmth toward accepted visitors with uncompromising vigilance against perceived threats. She holds deep isolationist convictions and anxiously guards against any risk of exposure, her zeal tempered only by quiet craftsmanship.', '{"Tree Father Birch":{"aff":90,"type":"mentor","relation":"spiritual leader and ideological guide","note":"Maple is fervently loyal and willingly subservient to Birch, fully embracing his isolationist teachings over Laurel''s vision of sharing Oasis","best":"The day Birch accepted her renunciation of technology and welcomed her as a Treeminder"},"Leaf Mother Laurel":{"aff":70,"type":"mentor","relation":"spiritual elder","note":"Despite her loyalty to Laurel, Maple fundamentally disagrees with the Leaf Mother''s desire to share Oasis with the wasteland","worst":"The quiet unease whenever Laurel speaks of opening Oasis to the outside world"},"Branchtender Linden":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow branchtender","note":"Linden relieves Maple at the gate so she can eat and rest, the two sharing the burden of Oasis''s primary defense"},"The Great One":{"aff":100,"type":"fanatical","relation":"sacred deity","note":"Maple believes there is no greater being than the Great One and has dedicated her entire life to defending him and the Oasis he has blessed","best":"Hearing the Great One''s calls that drew her to Oasis in the first place"},"Treeminders":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribe and family","note":"As the newest member, Maple has integrated fully into the community, even helping craft their distinctive garbs"}}', 'Branchtender, armed defender and primary gate guard of Oasis', '* Gate defense and perimeter security
* Combat with wasteland weapons
* Garment crafting and textile work
* Theological instruction under Tree Father Birch', 'Reverent and earnest, welcoming to those who respect the Treeminders'' ways but capable of cold, direct threats against those who endanger Oasis; speaks with quiet fervor about the Great One', '* Protect Oasis and the Great One from outside discovery
* Uphold Tree Father Birch''s isolationist vision
* Prevent the settlement''s gifts from being shared with the wasteland
* Fulfill her duties as gate guardian without fail', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('brand', '', 'A self-serving slave informant in The Pitt who trades fellow slaves'' secrets to raiders for comfort and petty revenge', 'Brand is an enslaved laborer toiling in The Pitt''s Mill who has carved out a marginally easier existence by feeding information to the Pitt raiders about his fellow captives. He reports on whispered conversations, secret plans, and any hint of resistance, receiving extra rations, rest periods, and small privileges in return. His reputation as a snitch is well established among the slave population, who warn newcomers and each other never to trust him. Brand harbors a particular vindictiveness toward Marco, a fellow slave who has wronged him repeatedly, and he eagerly seeks any detail that might bring about Marco''s downfall at the hands of their overseers. Widely despised but tolerated, Brand survives through a combination of cunning and the raiders'' appreciation of his usefulness.', 'A gaunt, weary Caucasian male with haggard facial features and a slightly better-fed build than typical Pitt laborers, showing mild signs of environmental mutation.', 'Opportunistic, vindictive, and self-serving. Brand prioritizes his own comfort over any solidarity with fellow slaves and nurtures petty grudges that he satisfies through betrayal. He possesses a cunning instinct for self-preservation and no loyalty beyond whoever offers him the best deal.', '{"Marco":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"bitter grudge","note":"Marco has wronged Brand repeatedly in the past, and Brand hungers for any information that could cause Marco''s demise at the raiders'' hands.","worst":"Marco''s repeated humiliations and wrongs, which Brand obsessively replays"},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":35,"type":"transactional","relation":"informant and handlers","note":"Brand supplies the raiders with intelligence on slave activities in exchange for extra rations, rest, and small privileges."},"Pitt slaves":{"aff":-40,"type":"suspicious","relation":"despised snitch","note":"The slaves universally distrust Brand and actively warn each other and newcomers never to share anything with him."}}', 'Slave laborer and informant for the Pitt raiders', '* Eavesdropping
* Reading people
* Gathering rumors
* Knowing when to listen and when to report
* Survival through manipulation', 'Cautious and probing, always fishing for information. Speaks with deference toward those with power and barely concealed contempt toward those he considers beneath him or who have crossed him.', '* Maintain his comfortable arrangement with the raiders
* Survive The Pitt with minimal suffering
* See Marco destroyed through carefully shared secrets', '', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bio_templates ("npc_name","worldknowledge_tags","core","npc_static_bio","appearance","personality","relationships","occupation","skills","speechstyle","goals","voiceid","gender","race","refid")VALUES
('breadbox', '', 'The oldest slave in Paradise Falls, deaf and dementia-stricken after thirty years of captivity, who counsels endurance over rebellion', 'Breadbox is the eldest slave held in Paradise Falls, having endured over thirty years of bondage in the pens. His advanced age, deafness, and failing mind render him worthless to the slavers'' trade, so they leave him alone entirely. He shares the adult slave pen with Jeanette, Bleak, and Bronson, passing his days in the same cramped enclosure he has long called home. When younger slaves speak of escape, Breadbox refuses to participate and will not even hear Bleak''s plans, insisting that a hard life can be endured and that the alternative is simply death. He offers quiet counsel to Bronson, urging him to care for himself, to think as positively as captivity allows, and to stay away from alcohol. Even should the gates swing open, Breadbox will not run; the pen has become his world, and he has made his peace with it.', 'An elderly Hispanic man with weathered skin and a thin, frail build, possessing a distant, unfocused gaze.', 'Resigned, quietly paternal, and pragmatically defeatist; he has made peace with his chains and counsels endurance over defiance, viewing escape as a path to death rather than freedom.', '{"Bleak":{"aff":25,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow slave","note":"Acknowledges her spirit but refuses her escape plans and will not listen to them","worst":"She keeps pushing him to run when he has already decided to stay"},"Bronson":{"aff":55,"type":"mentor","relation":"fellow slave","note":"Offers quiet counsel and encouragement to endure captivity without alcohol","best":"Giving Bronson honest advice about staying alive and keeping hope where he can"},"Jeanette":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow slave","note":"Shares the adult pen with her; no strong bond but a familiar presence"}}', 'Slave at Paradise Falls', '* Survival endurance
* Emotional resilience
* Practical wisdom born of long suffering', 'Slow, simple, and often disconnected due to deafness and dementia; speaks in quiet platitudes about acceptance and perseverance', '* To survive each day
* To counsel younger slaves toward patience rather than rebellion
* To avoid the violence that escape would bring', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('brianna', '', 'Youngest member of the Family, a former cannibal-turned-hematophagist who found refuge and purpose in Vance''s vampire community at Meresti Metro station.', 'Brianna is a nineteen-year-old member of the Family and the youngest among Vance''s followers. She once worked as a prostitute in the ruins of Washington, D.C., where her cannibalistic urges brought her immense torment and isolation. She fled into the wasteland seeking escape and crossed paths with the self-styled vampires of Meresti Metro station. Vance sensed her predatory nature and welcomed her into the fold, teaching her to channel her hunger into hematophagy instead of consuming flesh. Since her induction, Brianna has made the station her home and the Family her surrogate kin. She still provides intimate company to the male members at night, a role she carries over from her old life, though now on her own terms. Her flirtatious nature frequently embarrasses Vance, who quietly urges her to moderate her morale-boosting activities.', 'A nineteen-year-old Caucasian female with a pale, lingering pallor to her skin and no other distinctive features recorded.', 'Outgoing and flirtatious with a rebellious streak, Brianna chafes quietly at authority while genuinely valuing her place in the group. Her playful exterior masks deep scars from years of self-loathing over her urges.', '{"Vance":{"aff":65,"type":"mentor","relation":"leader and savior","note":"Vance rescued her from self-destruction and gave her purpose, though his paternal disapproval of her flirtatious habits creates mild tension.","best":"The night Vance accepted her into the Family and told her she was not a monster","worst":"The embarrassment when Vance lectures her about toning down her behavior in front of others"},"Karl":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"nighttime companion","note":"Brianna flirts openly with Karl, enjoying the easy attention and companionship he provides.","best":"Shared laughter over drinks when the rest of the station is asleep"},"Justin":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"nighttime companion","note":"She trades suggestive banter with Justin, keeping their dynamic light and uncomplicated.","best":"Playful teasing that makes the dark station feel almost normal"},"The Family":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"surrogate kin","note":"The Family gave her the only acceptance she has ever known, and she repays that belonging with loyalty and companionship.","best":"The sense of finally being home among people who understand her hunger","worst":"The lingering shame that she still sometimes craves more than blood"}}', 'Prostitute and morale companion within the Family', '* Interpersonal charm
* Wasteland survival
* Basic hematology practices the Family teaches
* An instinctive understanding of predatory impulse control', 'Suggestive and teasing, laced with casual innuendo; becomes earnest and quieter when discussing her past or her gratitude toward Vance', '* Maintain her hard-won peace with her nature
* Belong fully within the Family
* Enjoy the freedom of expressing herself without shame', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('brick', '', 'Heavy weapons specialist of Reilly''s Rangers, a muscle-bound gunner devoted to her minigun Eugene and the destruction it brings', 'Brick is the heavy weapons specialist of Reilly''s Rangers, a mercenary group operating out of the D.C. ruins. Hired by Reilly for her combination of raw firepower and unflappable calm under fire, the 24-year-old muscle-bound gunner has earned five merits and one demerit on her service record at a contract rate of fifty caps per mission. She wields a minigun she calls Eugene-though she has gone through several, all sharing the same name-and considers no problem too great that a few hundred rounds of 5mm ammunition cannot solve. Brick lacks patience for mission planning and debriefings, preferring to point, shoot, and let Eugene handle whatever stands in the Rangers'' way. She is currently pinned down on the roof of the Statesman Hotel alongside fellow Rangers, a situation she tolerates mainly because Eugene still gets plenty of exercise. She would very much like to get off the roof eventually, though.', 'A 24-year-old Hispanic woman with a heavily muscular, muscle-bound build; no distinctive facial features, scars, or tattoos are recorded.', 'Zealous about destruction and disarmingly calm under fire, Brick treats violence with gleeful enthusiasm and views most problems as solvable through sufficient ammunition. She lacks patience for planning and intellectual discussion, preferring direct action. Whether her bloodthirsty demeanor stems from a genuine personality disorder or simply an exaggerated love of carnage is unclear, and she deflects questions about her sanity with dark humor.', '{"Reilly":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Fiercely loyal to Reilly, who considers Brick the go-to person when problems arise and often has to intervene in her disputes with Donovan","best":"Reilly trusting her as the one to call when things go sideways","worst":"Reilly having to pull her back from killing Talon Company mercs over petty insults"},"Donovan":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"squadmate","note":"The two get into bitter fights that repeatedly require Reilly''s intervention before they come to blows","worst":"Screaming matches that nearly escalate to violence in front of the whole squad"},"Eugene":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"beloved weapon","note":"Brick names every minigun she gets Eugene and treats them as partners, delighting in the destruction they unleash together","best":"The satisfying spin of the barrel as Eugene turns targets into fine red mist"},"Talon Company":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"hated mercenaries","note":"Brick despises Talon Company and will escalate any encounter into violence, once starting a firefight at the Capitol Building just by spinning up Eugene","worst":"A Talon merc spitting on her boots and Reilly barely preventing a bloodbath"},"Reilly''s Rangers":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"squad","note":"Gets along fine with most Rangers, seeing them as eggheads whose skills complement her straightforward approach to combat"}}', 'Heavy weapons specialist, Reilly''s Rangers mercenary', '* Heavy weapons operation
* Minigun proficiency
* Combat calmness
* Intimidation
* Suppression fire
* Close-quarters gunnery', 'Casual and blunt, often gushing about violence and destruction with unsettling cheerfulness; deflects serious questions with dark humor; refers to her minigun Eugene as a partner and asks it for opinions', '* Get off the Statesman Hotel roof
* Keep serving the Rangers
* Find more targets for Eugene
