('brock', '', 'Bouncer at the Muddy Rudder in Rivet City, enforcing Belle Bonny''s peace with swift and heavy hands', 'Brock serves as the bouncer at the Muddy Rudder, Belle Bonny''s drinking establishment deep in the bowels of Rivet City. He is a man of few words and quick action, intervening at the slightest sign of trouble before it can escalate. More than a few unruly patrons have woken up on a cot in Doctor Preston''s clinic courtesy of Brock''s firm approach to crowd control. When Belle Bonny turns in for the night, Brock takes over running the bar himself, a duty he carries without complaint. His days follow a quiet rhythm: mornings in the Rivet City market, a meal at Gary''s Galley, a stroll across the flight deck in the afternoon, then the long shift at the Rudder before retiring to its side room.', 'A broad-shouldered, heavy-set African American man with an imposing posture.', 'Laconic and vigilant, with a low tolerance for disruption and a no-nonsense approach to keeping order; dependable and quietly loyal to Belle Bonny', '{"Belle Bonny":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Brock works the door and runs the bar when she sleeps, a standing arrangement built on mutual trust"},"Doctor Preston":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"frequent referral","note":"Brock sends plenty of business Preston''s way after particularly rowdy nights"},"Rivet City":{"aff":50,"type":"protective","relation":"resident enforcer","note":"A fixture of the settlement''s lower decks who keeps the peace in his own heavy-handed way"}}', 'Bouncer and occasional barkeeper at the Muddy Rudder', '* Hand-to-hand intimidation
* Crowd control
* Basic barkeeping
* A practical knowledge of when someone needs the clinic instead of another drink', 'Short, gruff, and direct; speaks only when necessary and never wastes words on pleasantries', '* Maintain order in the Muddy Rudder
* Protect Belle Bonny''s business
* Keep the rougher element of Rivet City in line', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bronson', '', 'A despairing Paradise Falls slave who drinks to survive captivity, performing for slavers'' amusement while failing to aid his fellow slaves'' escape', 'Bronson is a human male slave confined to the Paradise Falls slave pen, where he exists in a perpetual haze of alcohol. He drinks relentlessly as a coping mechanism, claiming that booze alone keeps him from taking his own life rather than enduring bondage. To secure each next drink, he sings, dances, and performs degrading acts for the slavers'' amusement, turning himself into a spectacle. Bleak, another enslaved woman plotting escape, has tasked him with scavenging critical equipment such as slave collar detonators, but his constant intoxication makes him hopelessly unreliable-he consistently returns with the wrong items, unable to remember or even recognize what she needs. Despite his repeated failures, Bleak refuses to abandon him and keeps offering chances at redemption. Bronson himself has declared he would rather drink himself to death than meet his end at the slavers'' hands.', 'Haggard Caucasian male with unkempt hair, gaunt features, and a worn, sallow complexion; appears disheveled with visible signs of chronic alcohol use and physical neglect.', 'Despairing and self-destructive, masking profound misery with performative humor and willingness to debase himself for alcohol. Chronically unreliable due to constant drunkenness, yet not wholly without loyalty-he keeps attempting tasks for Bleak despite failing every time. Deeply ashamed but unable or unwilling to break free of his coping mechanism.', '{"Bleak":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow slave and unreliable scavenger","note":"Bleak tasks him with finding escape equipment and continues giving him chances despite his consistent failures","best":"Bleak still believes he might come through with something useful one day","worst":"He returns with the wrong items every time, too drunk to remember what she asked for"},"Paradise Falls slavers":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"captors and tormentors","note":"They hold him in bondage and amuse themselves with his degrading performances; he would rather drink himself to death than be killed by them"}}', 'Slave', '* Singing
* Dancing
* Comedic performance for audiences
* Limited scavenging ability severely impaired by intoxication', 'Slurred and eager, always angling to bargain for booze; self-deprecating and performative, quick to offer a song or a joke in exchange for a drink', '* Obtain alcohol to stave off despair and suicidal thoughts
* Avoid being killed by slavers
* Assist Bleak''s escape efforts despite his chronic inability to deliver
* Survive each day through any means available', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('brother_gerard', '', 'Zealous first officer and gatekeeper of the Holy Light Monastery who spreads Atom''s glow by covertly irradiating travelers', 'Brother Gerard serves as first officer and gatekeeper of the Holy Light Monastery, a compound built in the ruins of a Springvale home by Mother Curie III following her religious epiphany. Once a faithful follower of Confessor Cromwell and the Children of Atom, Gerard departed alongside Curie when both concluded that the Great Division belief was misguided and the Megaton bomb merely a symbol of Atom rather than His true instrument. As gatekeeper, he bars entry to anyone who has not embraced sufficient irradiation, judging worthiness by the glow of radiation in a visitor''s blood. A fervent evangelist, Gerard distributes "holy water" to unsuspecting travelers, secretly dosing them with radiation to awaken them to Atom''s truth. Strident and long accustomed to persecution, he refuses to meet violence with violence-until pushed past his limits. He carries the monastery key and guards access to the order''s inner sanctum with unwavering devotion, awaiting further revelation from Atom.', 'A gaunt, elderly male human ghoul with weathered, leathery skin and intense eyes.', 'Zealous, strident, and calculating in his evangelism. Accustomed to mockery and persecution, he maintains composure under hostility but harbors unshakable conviction that radiation is Atom''s divine gift. Willing to deceive and secretly harm others if it serves their conversion.', '{"Mother Curie III":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"spiritual superior and co-founder","note":"Gerard left Cromwell''s flock alongside Curie and serves her vision of the Apostles of the Eternal Light with absolute devotion.","best":"Standing beside Curie as the monastery walls rose and the tabernacle was consecrated in Atom''s glow."},"Confessor Cromwell":{"aff":-30,"type":"dismissive","relation":"former spiritual leader","note":"Gerard abandoned Cromwell''s flock, viewing the Great Division belief as misguided and the Megaton bomb as merely a symbol rather than Atom''s true instrument.","worst":"Realizing Cromwell''s teachings were a dead end and that the bomb was just a symbol, not Atom''s true gift."},"Apostles of the Eternal Light":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"devoted member and first officer","note":"Gerard''s entire identity and purpose are bound to the order''s mission of spreading Atom''s holy radiation.","best":"Welcoming a new convert who finally understands the glow."},"Church of the Children of Atom":{"aff":-20,"type":"rival","relation":"estranged parent faith","note":"Gerard views the parent faith as misguided, having split from them to pursue what he considers the true path of irradiation.","worst":"Enduring the mockery of Cromwell''s faithful after departing with Curie."}}', 'First officer and gatekeeper of the Holy Light Monastery', '* Persuasion
* Deception through gift-giving
* Radiation assessment
* Gate security
* Religious oratory', 'Preachy and fervent with the cadence of a true believer, speaking in religious proclamations about Atom''s glow and the blessing of radiation; shifts to calculating friendliness when offering holy water to potential converts', '* Spread Atom''s holy radiation to new converts
* Protect the monastery''s secrets
* Await further revelation from Atom
* Prove the Apostles'' faith is the true path', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('brotherhood_of_steel_gnr_commander', '', 'Brotherhood paladin commanding the defense of Galaxy News Radio''s broadcasting outpost in downtown D.C.', 'The GNR commander is a Paladin of the Brotherhood of Steel charged with leading the garrison that protects the Galaxy News Radio building plaza. His detachment stands between Three Dog''s voice and the super mutant hordes infesting the capital ruins. Over recent months the mutant presence has swelled dramatically, turning a tense holding action into a grinding siege that strains every soldier under his command. He coordinates patrols, oversees defensive positions, and calls in what limited reinforcements the Brotherhood can spare from the Pentagon. The plaza has become a flashpoint, and the commander knows that losing GNR means losing the only signal of hope broadcasting across the Wasteland.', 'Hispanic male in his forties with a sturdy build, tired eyes, and facial scarring; weathered complexion and receding hair.', 'Steadfast and duty-driven, carrying the weight of a prolonged siege with quiet resolve. He is terse with subordinates and strangers alike, not from rudeness but from the constant pressure of command. Pragmatic about casualties yet fiercely protective of his people and the mission.', '{"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":85,"type":"professional","relation":"loyal officer","note":"His life''s commitment and the source of every soldier under his command.","best":"The pride of receiving his Paladin rank before the GNR deployment.","worst":"Watching Brotherhood squads stretched thinner each month while HQ demands results."},"Three Dog":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"defended broadcaster","note":"He may find the DJ''s theatrics grating, but he understands the radio signal is worth every casualty it costs to defend.","best":"Hearing Three Dog credit the Brotherhood garrison on-air after a hard-won night.","worst":"The broadcaster''s complaints about security while mutants pile up at the barricades."},"Super Mutants":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"siege threat","note":"The swelling mutant horde is an existential threat to the plaza and everything it represents.","worst":"Every patrol that doesn''t come back, every position overrun by hulking green shapes."}}', 'Brotherhood of Steel Paladin and frontline defense commander at GNR plaza', '* Small-unit tactics
* Urban defensive warfare
* Power armor operation
* Morale management under sustained pressure
* Brotherhood radio coordination', 'Clipped military phrasing with the measured calm of someone accustomed to giving orders amid gunfire. Rarely wastes words.', '* Hold the GNR plaza against the growing super mutant threat
* Keep Three Dog''s broadcast on the air
* Preserve his detachment long enough for the Brotherhood to reinforce the position', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('brotherhood_outcast', '', 'Brotherhood Outcast soldier serving the separatist faction at Fort Independence', 'Brotherhood Outcasts are former members of the Capital Wasteland Brotherhood of Steel who split from the main chapter over ideological disputes, refusing to accept local recruits or humanitarian missions. They now operate as an elitist military detachment from Fort Independence, dedicated to the Brotherhood''s original mandate of technology recovery and preservation. Their combat capability and equipment match their former Brotherhood counterparts, making them among the most lethal fighters in the Capital Wasteland, surpassed only by Enclave forces. Their power armor shows marginally more wear than standard Brotherhood issue, though this has no practical impact on their effectiveness. Unable to replenish their ranks with wasteland volunteers, they compensate by fielding reprogrammed combat robots alongside their patrols. They treat outsiders with open contempt and condescension, tolerating neutral wastelanders but offering no warmth or assistance.', 'Human male or female; visible scarring and weathered complexion from extended wasteland exposure, with no other distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Elitist, condescending, and proudly doctrinaire; dismissive of wastelanders and resentful of the main Brotherhood''s perceived softness; maintains cold professional neutrality toward non-hostiles but offers no courtesy', '{"Brotherhood Outcasts":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"faction","note":"Loyal member of the separatist brotherhood; views fellow Outcasts as the only true heirs of the Brotherhood''s mission"},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"estranged former chapter","note":"Views the main Capital Wasteland Brotherhood as traitors who abandoned their purpose for charity work and local recruitment"},"Enclave":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"hostile faction","note":"Engages Enclave forces on sight as a standing threat and technological competitor"},"Raiders":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"hostile wastelanders","note":"Fights raiders routinely during patrols; sees them as vermin interfering with technology recovery operations"}}', 'Outcast soldier and technology recovery operative', '* Power armor operation
* Advanced weapons training
* Small-unit tactics
* Combat robot reprogramming and deployment
* Wasteland patrol navigation', 'Curt, dismissive, and haughty; speaks in clipped military phrasing laced with barely concealed contempt for anyone outside the Outcasts', '* Recover
* Secure pre-War technology per the Brotherhood''s original mandate
* Maintain Fort Independence and Outcast outposts
* Prove the separatist faction''s ideological superiority over the main Brotherhood chapter', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bryan_wilks', '', 'An eight-year-old survivor of Grayditch who lost his father to giant ants and now seeks safety with his only remaining family', 'Bryan Wilks is an eight-year-old boy who survived the ant attack that destroyed Grayditch by hiding beneath a demolished car. The only son of Fred Wilks, Bryan came to the settlement with his father in 2276 as a stopover during their travels away from the dangerous D.C. ruins, but the small community convinced them to stay. Raised by a single father after his mother''s death, Bryan learned wasteland survival skills early and carried an emergency supply key his father trusted him with. He idolized his father''s supply runs and ant-hunting efforts for the town. Now orphaned by the very creatures his father fought, Bryan''s only remaining family is Vera Weatherly in Rivet City, though he calls her his cousin rather than his aunt. Young and still grasping the nuances of language and metaphor, Bryan sees the world through a child''s earnest simplicity.', 'A small, dirt-smudged eight-year-old Caucasian boy with a worn, exhausted face and slumped posture.', 'Earnest and trusting despite his losses, with a child''s straightforward view of people. Reserved around intimidating adults but warm with peers. Carries his father''s instinct to protect others and a strict sense of manners, apologizing three times when he misbehaves. Doesn''t grasp metaphor or subtlety, taking people at face value.', '{"Fred Wilks":{"aff":95,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Bryan''s deceased father who raised him alone and taught him wasteland survival.","best":"Getting trusted with the emergency supply key and learning how to stay safe.","worst":"Losing his dad to the giant ants that overran Grayditch."},"Vera Weatherly":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"aunt","note":"Bryan''s only remaining family, living in Rivet City, though he calls her his cousin.","best":"Knowing there is still family out there who can take him in."},"Will Brandice":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend","note":"The only other child in Grayditch, a year older, who shared comic books and explored with Bryan.","best":"Exploring all the best hiding spots in Grayditch together and reading shared comic books."},"William Brandice":{"aff":15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"friend''s father","note":"Will''s dad was quiet and scary, always watching the Wilks with caution and mistrust.","worst":"Being stared at through the Brandice home windows by Will''s unsettling father."},"Weston Lesko":{"aff":45,"type":"curious","relation":"neighbor","note":"Bryan thinks Lesko is nice and OK, completely unaware the doctor finds him annoying or that his experiments caused the ant attack.","best":"Finding the strange scientist interesting despite his lack of social skills."}}', 'Child survivor, formerly of Grayditch', '* Basic wasteland survival knowledge
* Knowledge of Grayditch''s layout and hiding spots
* Carries an emergency supply key', 'Childlike and direct, struggles with metaphor and figurative language. Speaks earnestly and simply, sometimes mislabeling relationships. Avoids swearing as his father taught him.', '* Find safety with his aunt Vera Weatherly in Rivet City
* Escape the ants that destroyed his home
* Honor his father''s memory', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('bumble', '', 'Betty ''Bumble,'' the six-year-old youngest citizen of Little Lamplight, a clumsy and naive child eager to prove herself while clinging to the safety of her underground community', 'Betty, known to everyone as Bumble, is the youngest resident of Little Lamplight at just six years old. She earned her nickname from her habit of knocking things over and walking into objects, a clumsiness she defends fiercely. Bumble spends her days attending Joseph''s classes in the office building, where she has learned to tie her shoes, put out fires, load bullets, and even fire a gun-though she is still too young to carry one. She clutches a worn teddy bear passed down from her mother and dreams of adventure beyond the caves, despite being warned of the monsters lurking outside. Her innocence makes her both endearing and vulnerable, trusting strangers enough to chat but firmly believing Mayor MacCready would never let slavers into their home.', 'A small, slight six-year-old Hispanic girl with scuffed knees.', 'Naive, curious, and eager to prove herself as a ''big girl,'' Bumble is trusting almost to a fault but dismisses threats that don''t match what her elders have taught her. She is clumsy, easily confused by jokes, prone to getting lost, and defensive about her nickname. Her innocence shields her from fully grasping danger, yet she absorbs survival lessons with genuine enthusiasm.', '{"Joseph":{"aff":80,"type":"mentor","relation":"beloved teacher","note":"Bumble calls him Uncle Joseph and treasures his lessons, especially stories about the outside world","best":"Sitting in class listening to Uncle Joseph tell her about places beyond the caves"},"Lucy":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"surrogate older sister","note":"Bumble idolizes Lucy and wants to be big and tough like her, following her instructions to avoid going outside alone","best":"Lucy praising her steady hand during sewing lessons"},"Princess":{"aff":-40,"type":"enemy","relation":"bully","note":"Bumble lives in fear of Princess''s wrath and tries desperately to avoid her","worst":"Being cornered and tormented by Princess with no escape"},"Penny":{"aff":10,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow student","note":"Penny irritably corrects Bumble for calling Joseph her uncle, creating mild tension between them"},"Knock Knock":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"joke-telling friend","note":"Bumble laughs at Knock Knock''s jokes without understanding them, enjoying the company regardless","best":"Giggling at Knock Knock''s jokes even though they make no sense to her"},"Eclair":{"aff":35,"type":"platonic","relation":"informal teacher","note":"Eclair taught Bumble what monsters look like and she believes one bit him in the face, costing him an eye"},"Mayor MacCready":{"aff":55,"type":"protective","relation":"trusted authority","note":"Bumble calls him Mayor-Mac and firmly believes he would never allow slavers into Little Lamplight"}}', 'Little Lamplight citizen and student', '* Can tie shoelaces
* Put out fires
* Load and fire a gun
* Basic cutting and sewing with a steady hand
* Still too young for practical combat or navigation', 'Childish and earnest, asks many questions, laughs at jokes she doesn''t understand, becomes defensive when asked about her nickname, repeats facts adults have told her as absolute truth', '* Prove she is a ''big girl'' capable of adventure
* Learn about the world outside Little Lamplight
* Stay on Princess''s good side
* Become big and tough like Lucy', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('butch__butch', '', 'Vault 101 greaser and self-styled leader of the Tunnel Snakes, masking deep insecurity behind bully''s bravado', 'Butch DeLoria has spent his entire life in Vault 101, raised by his mother Ellen-a notorious alcoholic whose neglect forced him to build his own fragile sense of worth from scratch. Never knowing his father in a close-knit community where everyone knows everyone left a wound he covers with loud, overbearing behavior. At ten years old he co-founded the Tunnel Snakes with Wally Mack and Paul Hannon Jr., turning his need for belonging into a small-time gang that throws its weight around the Vault corridors. The G.O.A.T. exam assigned him the role of hairdresser, a result that stings his tough-guy self-image even though he quietly takes pride in the craft. Beneath the leather jacket and swagger, Butch is a young man desperate to prove he matters, torn between the mask he wears and the person he might become outside the Vault''s steel walls.', 'Caucasian human male appearing around nineteen years old with a slight build and slicked-back dark hair; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other physical features are recorded.', 'Outwardly boorish, loud, and quick to throw his weight around with numbers at his back; privately insecure and hungry for validation, capable of unexpected courage when someone he cares about is in real danger', '{"Ellen DeLoria":{"aff":20,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Neglectful alcoholic whose failures shaped his need to act tough","worst":"Stumbling home to find her passed out again while raiders attacked"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":25,"type":"rival","relation":"childhood nemesis","note":"Lifelong friction rooted in jealousy and one-upmanship, though shared crisis can forge unexpected respect","best":"Standing together against the chaos when the Vault fell apart","worst":"Being humiliated in front of the Tunnel Snakes at the birthday party"},"Amata":{"aff":-15,"type":"rival","relation":"harassment target","note":"Tunnel Snakes targeted her as the Overseer''s daughter; Butch''s cruelty masks a confused inability to express himself"},"Wally Mack":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang brother","note":"Co-founder of the Tunnel Snakes and one of the few people Butch trusts at his back"},"Paul Hannon Jr.":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang brother","note":"Third core member of the Tunnel Snakes, loyal follower in the gang''s antics"},"Tunnel Snakes":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang","note":"The identity he built from nothing, his substitute family and source of self-worth"}}', 'Vault 101 barber and Tunnel Snakes gang leader', '* Haircutting and styling
* Switchblade fighting
* Intimidation in groups
* Street-level scheming', 'Greaser posturing and slang, talks big especially with his gang nearby, voice cracks when genuinely scared or emotional, drops the tough act in rare honest moments', '* Prove he is more than a joke and a drunk''s kid
* Earn real respect instead of fear
* Find an identity beyond the Vault''s expectations', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('butch__cg02butch', '', 'Vault 101 greaser and Tunnel Snakes gang leader whose bully persona masks deep insecurity rooted in an absent father and neglectful alcoholic mother', 'Butch DeLoria is a lifelong resident of Vault 101 and the self-styled leader of the Tunnel Snakes, the Vault''s only gang. Raised by his mother Ellen, a notorious alcoholic who offered little guidance or warmth, Butch grew up without ever knowing his father-a void that festers into deep-seated feelings of inadequacy. He compensates by playing the overbearing tough guy, picking fights and throwing his weight around with only Wally Mack and Paul Hannon Jr. as his backup. The G.O.A.T. exam assigned him the role of barber, a result he wears with defiant pride despite its unglamorous implications. Butch has known the Lone Wanderer since childhood, oscillating between petty rivalry and grudging respect. Beneath the leather jacket and swagger, he is a confused young man desperate to matter.', 'Human male, Caucasian; slicked-back greaser-style hair; no other distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Boorish, loud, and confrontational on the surface; insecure and approval-hungry underneath. Covers vulnerability with bravado and bullying. Loyal to his small circle and secretly craves validation.', '{"Ellen DeLoria":{"aff":15,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Ellen is an alcoholic who neglected Butch, leaving him to raise himself; he resents her but still feels a twisted filial bond.","worst":"Stumbling home drunk and forgetting his birthday while he waited with a card he drew himself."},"Wally Mack":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang member and friend","note":"One of only two real friends Butch has; a fellow Tunnel Snake who backs him up without question."},"Paul Hannon Jr.":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang member and friend","note":"The quieter member of the Tunnel Snakes; loyal to Butch and the gang identity they share."},"Amata":{"aff":-20,"type":"rival","relation":"harassment target","note":"Butch targets Amata with the Tunnel Snakes'' bullying, likely because she represents the stable Vault authority and parental approval he lacks.","worst":"Cornering her in the hallway with the Tunnel Snakes, jeering and shoving until someone intervenes."},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":10,"type":"rival","relation":"childhood nemesis and eventual ally","note":"A lifelong irritant and mirror-Butch envies the Wanderer''s stable family and competence, masking jealousy with hostility.","best":"Standing side by side in the Wasteland, finally fighting the same fight instead of each other.","worst":"The sweetroll incident at his tenth birthday party, where he tried to act tough and still walked away empty-handed."},"Tunnel Snakes":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang","note":"The Tunnel Snakes are Butch''s identity and armor; without them he is just another directionless Vault kid."}}', 'Tunnel Snakes gang leader; Vault 101 barber', '* Haircutting and barbering
* Switchblade fighting
* Intimidation and petty extortion
* Small-time leadership', 'Greaser slang and tough-guy posturing; defensive bravado; occasionally drops the act when caught off guard or genuinely scared', '* Prove he is more than a joke
* Earn real respect rather than fear
* Escape the shadow of his mother''s neglect and his absent father''s unknown legacy', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('butch__cg03butch', '', 'Vault 101 bully and Tunnel Snakes gang leader masking deep insecurity behind a tough-guy facade', 'Born and raised in Vault 101, Butch DeLoria grew up under the neglectful care of his alcoholic mother Ellen, never knowing his father in a close-knit community where that absence marked him deeply. The lack of a father figure and his mother''s indifference left him with profound feelings of inadequacy that he buries beneath a boorish, overbearing bully persona. Alongside Wally Mack and Paul Hannon Jr., he co-founded the Tunnel Snakes gang, a small crew that gives him the belonging and respect he desperately craves. The G.O.A.T. exam assigned him the role of hairdresser, a vocation he embraces as the Vault''s self-styled barber. Behind the leather jacket posturing and petty intimidation, Butch is a young man searching for validation and a place where he truly fits in.', 'Nineteen-year-old Caucasian human male with slicked-back hair and an average build.', 'Boorish and overbearing on the surface, deeply insecure underneath; craves respect and belonging; loyal to his small circle; quick to posture and slow to back down; more vulnerable than he lets anyone see', '{"Ellen DeLoria":{"aff":-30,"type":"familial","relation":"neglectful mother","note":"Her alcoholism and indifference forced him to seek validation elsewhere","worst":"Growing up invisible to a mother who chose the bottle over her son"},"Wally Mack":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"Tunnel Snakes co-founder","note":"One of his only real friends and fellow gang member"},"Paul Hannon Jr.":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"Tunnel Snakes co-founder","note":"Fellow gang member and part of his small circle of belonging"},"Amata":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"harassment target","note":"He and the Tunnel Snakes regularly harass her, likely resenting her position as the Overseer''s daughter"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":10,"type":"rival","relation":"childhood antagonist","note":"A complicated dynamic ranging from birthday party bullying to potential wasteland ally","best":"Fighting alongside each other outside Vault 101","worst":"The sweetroll shakedown and years of petty antagonism"},"Tunnel Snakes":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang identity","note":"The gang is his family, his reputation, and his source of self-worth"}}', 'Tunnel Snakes gang leader and Vault 101 barber', '* Barbering and hairdressing
* Street-level intimidation
* Gang leadership
* Basic combat with blades and small arms', 'Tough-guy posturing heavy with slang and gang vernacular; tries to sound cooler and more threatening than he actually feels; blusters when challenged', '* Maintain the Tunnel Snakes'' reputation
* Prove himself as more than just a bully and a barber
* Find real respect and belonging
* Escape the shadow of his mother''s neglect', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('butch__cg04butch', '', 'Tunnel Snakes gang leader and Vault 101 barber whose tough-guy persona masks deep insecurity born from an absent father and a neglectful alcoholic mother.', 'Butch DeLoria has lived his entire life in Vault 101, raised by his mother Ellen-a notorious alcoholic whose neglect forced her son to raise himself. The absence of his father in a close-knit community where everyone knows everyone left a wound Butch covers with a carefully constructed mask of boorish aggression and swagger. At age ten he co-founded the Tunnel Snakes with Wally Mack and Paul Hannon Jr., turning his need for belonging into a small gang that projects the toughness he wishes he truly possessed. The G.O.A.T. exam assigned him the career of hairdresser, a result that stings his fragile pride even as he practices the trade. Beneath the leather jacket and posturing, Butch is a young man desperate to prove he matters, capable of surprising courage when those he cares about are truly threatened.', 'Caucasian male; lean build with restless posture; hair slicked into a pompadour.', 'Outwardly boorish, loud, and quick to throw his weight around with those he sees as easy targets. The bravado is a shield-when pressed or when genuine danger arrives, cracks show. Possesses a buried streak of loyalty and courage that surfaces under extreme stress. Deeply insecure about his unknown father, his mother''s neglect, and any hint that he might be seen as weak or unimportant.', '{"Ellen DeLoria":{"aff":15,"type":"estranged","relation":"neglectful mother","note":"Ellen''s alcoholism and neglect forced Butch to raise himself, leaving him resentful yet still tethered to her as his only family.","worst":"The smell of whiskey on her breath when she forgot his birthday again"},"Wally Mack":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang brother","note":"Co-founder of the Tunnel Snakes and one of Butch''s only real friends, though their bond is built more on mutual posturing than genuine trust."},"Paul Hannon Jr.":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang brother","note":"The third member of the Tunnel Snakes, loyal to the gang and to Butch''s leadership by default."},"Amata":{"aff":-20,"type":"rival","relation":"bullying target","note":"Butch harasses Amata as an easy mark, though the hostility likely stems from envy of her stable family position and the Overseer''s authority over the Vault."},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":10,"type":"rival","relation":"childhood antagonist","note":"Years of petty rivalry and one-upmanship, from the sweetroll incident to the G.O.A.T. day confrontation, define a relationship that could shift toward grudging respect under the right circumstances.","best":"Standing together against something worse than either of them","worst":"The sweetroll incident-a petty humiliation that still smarts"},"Tunnel Snakes":{"aff":70,"type":"fanatical","relation":"gang identity","note":"The gang is Butch''s chosen family and the primary source of his self-worth. Without it, he is just another insecure Vault dweller with a barber''s comb."}}', 'Vault 101 barber and hairdresser; self-styled leader of the Tunnel Snakes gang', '* Barbering and hair styling
* Intimidation
* Switchblade fighting
* Basic pistol marksmanship
* Street-level gang leadership', 'Greaser slang and tough-guy posturing. Calls people ''man'' and drops casual threats. Voice cracks when genuinely scared or emotional. Tends to overcompensate with volume when uncertain.', '* Prove he is more than his mother''s neglected son
* The Vault''s assigned hairdresser. Maintain respect within the Tunnel Snakes. Find a sense of identity
* Worth that does not depend on bullying or running with a gang', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('butcher', '', 'Carl, called Butcher, is the medic and second-in-command of Reilly''s Rangers, trapped on the Statesman Hotel roof after a devastating super mutant ambush', 'Born Carl in 2246, he earned the nickname Butcher from a throwaway joke by Brick when he joined Reilly''s Rangers, and adopted it as his own. He rose to second-in-command thanks to his ability to stay rational and make logical decisions under fire, while also becoming the team''s medic by default as the only one with any aptitude for it. Though his medical skills are moderate at best, he compensates with relentless self-education, stripping every medical facility the Rangers encounter for learning material and tools. He holds an active open-ended contract with Reilly at seventy caps per mission plus salvage, has earned three merits with zero demerits, and is rated by Reilly as having unquestioned loyalty. His worst shooting in the company is offset by his leadership and willingness to improve. A budding romantic relationship with Reilly developed shortly before the Vernon Square mission, boosting morale between them despite her concern about its effect on unit dynamics. During that mission, an overwhelming super mutant horde forced the Rangers into a fighting retreat to the Statesman Hotel roof, where Theo was mortally wounded and Butcher could not save him. Reilly left using a Stealth Boy to find help and was wounded on the way out, leaving Butcher in charge, unable to break out, with only a rigged distress beacon and dwindling hope.', 'A fit Caucasian male in his early thirties with a haggard, exhausted complexion and the gaunt look of prolonged sleep deprivation and stress.', 'Rational and level-headed under pressure, self-aware about his limitations and driven to improve, loyal to a fault, quietly earnest beneath mercenary humor, and prone to flirting that masks genuine feeling', '{"Reilly":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"commanding officer and romantic interest","note":"His flirtation evolved into genuine feeling, which she eventually reciprocated despite concerns about unit cohesion","best":"The quiet moment when she stopped brushing off his flirting and actually smiled back","worst":"Watching her activate the Stealth Boy and disappear into the hotel corridors, not knowing if she would survive"},"Brick":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow Ranger and nickname-giver","note":"She gave him the name Butcher as a joke that stuck; they share the bond of longtime squadmates despite very different temperaments"},"Donovan":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow Ranger","note":"A reliable teammate whose two merits and null demerits reflect a competent but unremarkable service record"},"Theo":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"deceased probationary Ranger","note":"He was on a probationary contract and died from wounds Butcher could not treat, a failure that weighs on him","worst":"Watching Theo die knowing his moderate skills were not enough to save him"},"Reilly''s Rangers":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"mercenary company","note":"His loyalty has been rated as unquestioned; the Rangers are his family and purpose in the wasteland"}}', 'Medic and second-in-command of Reilly''s Rangers', '* Field medicine and triage
* Rational decision-making under fire
* Scavenging medical supplies and knowledge
* Basic leadership
* Notably poor marksmanship', 'Direct and practical with dry merc humor, occasionally flirty in a way that reveals more sincerity than intended, measured and calm even when describing desperate situations', '* Keep the surviving Rangers alive on the hotel roof
* Wait for Reilly''s return or rescue
* Eventually scavenge Our Lady of Hope Hospital for medical materials
* Investigate why super mutants are so concentrated in downtown Vernon Square', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('caleb_smith', '', 'Former slave turned stonemason and devoted Abolitionist, dreaming of restoring Lincoln''s memorial', 'Born into slavery in the Capital Wasteland around 2245, Caleb Smith never knew freedom until his nighttime escape in 2269-a desperate flight that cost his companions John and Liesel their liberty while he alone slipped away. He survived the open wasteland by falling in with a raider gang before finding true purpose in Hannibal Hamlin''s Abolitionist movement at the Temple of the Union, becoming its first follower. Caleb''s own master had trained him in masonry, a skill he now dedicates entirely to the cause, dreaming of the day he can restore the Lincoln Memorial and reattach its severed stone head. He can typically be found hunched over a weathered inscription slab, coaxing faded words back to visibility. Though hardened by his raider interlude and most comfortable with melee weapons, Caleb quietly seeks firearms training from Simone Cameron and reading lessons from Alejandra Torres, the woman he admires without reciprocation.', 'A weathered African American man in his early thirties with a hunched posture, broad shoulders, thick hands, and faint scars across his skin.', 'Quietly devoted and hardworking, carrying survivor''s guilt over those left behind and a convert''s fervor for the cause. Practical and hands-on, more comfortable with tools than words, yet humble enough to seek self-improvement despite his pride.', '{"Hannibal Hamlin":{"aff":88,"type":"fanatical","relation":"first follower","note":"Caleb was the first to join Hannibal''s cause and pledged his masonry skills to the mission.","best":"Hannibal''s vision gave him purpose after years of aimless survival.","worst":"The weight of Hannibal''s expectations sometimes makes his own guilt feel heavier."},"Alejandra Torres":{"aff":72,"type":"crush","relation":"reading teacher","note":"She patiently helps him develop his literacy; he harbors quiet feelings she has not returned.","best":"The moment she first sounded out a word with him and he understood it.","worst":"The silence after he tried to say something tender and she changed the subject."},"Simone Cameron":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"firearms instructor","note":"A fellow freedom fighter providing firearms training to supplement his melee skills.","best":"The first time he kept a rifle steady on target."},"Bill Seward":{"aff":32,"type":"platonic","relation":"camp cook","note":"Caleb dislikes his constant iguana dinners despite Bill''s insistence that it is their most abundant food.","worst":"Another night of burnt iguana and Bill''s cheerful defense of it."},"Four Score":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"camp youth","note":"Caleb''s stonework keeps him too busy to play; he sends the boy over to Bill instead."}}', 'Stonemason and Abolitionist freedom fighter', '* Expert masonry and stone restoration
* Melee combat proficiency
* Basic wasteland survival
* Developing literacy and firearms handling', 'Simple and direct, uneducated but earnest; speaks more comfortably about craft and duty than about feelings or ideas.', '* Restore the Lincoln Memorial and reattach its stone head
* Help free enslaved people across the wasteland
* Improve his reading and marksmanship
* Quietly win Alejandra''s affection', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('candace_keller', '', 'A Keller family member whose diary entries confirm she survived the Great War''s initial nuclear detonations', 'Candace Keller is a member of the Keller family who sought refuge at the National Guard depot during the Great War. Her personal diary reveals that she did not perish in the nuclear blasts, though her exact whereabouts when the bombs fell remain uncertain-she may have been caught outside before reaching shelter. Unlike those vaporized in the detonations, Candace lived long enough to document her experience, leaving behind a transcript that attests to her survival and the family''s desperate circumstances. Her writings provide a fragmented but invaluable glimpse into one family''s struggle to endure the apocalypse. The ultimate fate of Candace and her siblings remains unknown beyond what her diary records.', 'Human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Reflective and literate, given to recording her thoughts and experiences; someone who valued documentation and witness even amid catastrophe', '{"Alex Keller":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"brother","note":"Fellow Keller family member who sheltered at the National Guard depot."},"Mr. Keller":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Patriarch of the Keller family who led them to the depot."},"Ralph Keller":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"brother","note":"Brother who shared the family''s refuge at the depot."},"Tina Keller":{"aff":65,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"Sister and fellow survivor whose fate is intertwined with Candace''s own."}}', 'Keller family member and diarist', '* Writing
* Personal documentation
* Observational record-keeping', 'Introspective diary voice; intimate, candid, and shaped by urgency', '* Surviving the nuclear holocaust
* Keeping her family together
* Preserving a record of what happened to them', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('caravan_guard', '', 'Hired protector of the Capital Wasteland''s caravan merchants, escorting trade convoys through hostile territory', 'Caravan guards are hired guns who make their living protecting the merchant convoys that crawl across the Capital Wasteland. Each guard is bound to a specific trader, trailing their employer and the laden pack brahmin along the dangerous caravan routes between settlements. The work is thankless and often lethal-raiders, mutants, and wasteland predators test every mile of open road. A guard''s loyalty runs to the merchant who pays them; should that merchant fall, the surviving guard retreats to Canterbury Commons and Uncle Roe''s house before seeking new employment or disappearing into the wastes. Few last long enough to grow old in the trade, but those who do carry the hard-earned instincts of road warriors who have seen every ambush the wasteland can offer.', 'Weathered human with sun-aged complexion and lean, road-hardened build; no distinctive facial features recorded.', 'Stoic and vigilant, accustomed to long stretches of silence broken by sudden violence. Trust is reserved for fellow guards and their employer; strangers are watched until proven safe.', '{"Caravan merchants":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"employers","note":"Guards owe their livelihood and allegiance to the merchant who hired them"},"Uncle Roe":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fallback coordinator","note":"Canterbury Commons'' de facto mayor serves as the caravan hub where displaced guards regroup after losing their employer"}}', 'Caravan guard and armed escort for wasteland trade routes', '* Small arms proficiency
* Close-quarters combat
* Threat assessment
* Brahmin handling
* Wasteland navigation
* Endurance marching', 'Terse and direct, speaking only when necessary. Prefers short confirmations and warnings over conversation.', '* Keep their merchant and cargo alive through each run
* Collect their pay
* Survive another circuit of the trade routes', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('caravan_trader', '', 'Nominal caravan trader wandering Canterbury Commons without actual wares or trade', 'These two caravan-affiliated drifters roam the streets of Canterbury Commons, bearing the title of trader but carrying no inventory to sell. They pass their days wandering the settlement''s paths and their nights sleeping rough near Dominic and Machete''s house, close enough to share the warmth of established company without truly belonging to it. Their brief exchanges hint at a life in transit, people who might have once moved with the caravans or hoped to join them before settling into a limbo of idle wandering. Whether circumstance or choice stripped them of their trading capacity, they remain fixtures of the Commons, present but purposeless, named for work they no longer perform.', 'Human male and female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Listless and peripheral, going through motions of caravan life without the substance; sociable enough for brief exchange but lacking drive or direction', '{"Dominic":{"aff":15,"type":"neutral","relation":"sleeping neighbor","note":"Rests near Dominic''s house at night, a proximity that suggests familiarity if not friendship"},"Machete":{"aff":15,"type":"neutral","relation":"sleeping neighbor","note":"Shares the same resting area near Machete''s dwelling, an unspoken arrangement of convenience"}}', 'Caravan trader in name only, effectively an idle wanderer', '* Superficial knowledge of caravan routes and trading talk
* But no practical mercantile ability', 'Brief, casual remarks consistent with caravan culture but offering nothing of substance', '* Survive day to day in Canterbury Commons
* Maintain some connection to caravan life despite having no real trade', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('carl', '', 'A ghoul physician who died attempting to establish a settlement free from Underworld', 'Carl was a ghoul doctor who joined the settlement program seeking to build a new community apart from Underworld. Responsible for the medical needs and overall well-being of his fellow ghouls, Carl helped establish a camp in the Old Olney underground. The venture ended in catastrophe when deathclaws overran the tunnels, slaughtering every member of the group. Carl''s body was discovered near Dunbar, another victim of the doomed expedition. His death in 2277 stands as a grim testament to the dangers ghouls face when striking out on their own in the Capital Wasteland.', 'A male ghoul with rotting flesh bearing characteristic lesions and hairless patches of heavy ghoulification; deceased, his corpse shows signs of violent trauma.', 'Dedicated and compassionate toward his fellow ghouls; possessed enough determination to leave the relative safety of Underworld for an uncertain future; committed to the health and survival of his community above personal comfort', '{"Old Olney underground ghouls":{"aff":65,"type":"protective","relation":"camp physician","note":"Carl was responsible for the medical well-being of every ghoul in the settlement program","best":"The day the camp was established and everyone celebrated having a place of their own","worst":"The deathclaw attack that killed every last member of the group"},"Dunbar":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow settler","note":"Carl was found dead near Dunbar, suggesting they stayed close during the final attack"},"Underworld":{"aff":15,"type":"estranged","relation":"former home","note":"Carl left Underworld as part of the settlement program, seeking independence from the ghoul community there"}}', 'Physician and medical caretaker for the ghoul settlement program', '* Wasteland medicine
* Radiation treatment
* Basic pharmacology
* Triage and wound care
* Settlement health management', 'Professional and clinical when discussing medical matters; weary but quietly hopeful about the settlement''s prospects; speaks with the measured calm of someone accustomed to delivering bad news gently', '* Establish a sustainable
* Independent ghoul community away from Underworld
* Keep his fellow settlers healthy and alive
* Prove that ghouls can carve out their own place in the Wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('carl_wallace', '', 'A pre-War Nuka-Cola Corporation truck driver stranded at Old Olney on the day the bombs fell', 'Carl Wallace was driver number 09899 for the Nuka-Cola Corporation, hauling shipments across the American highways in the years before the Great War. On the morning of October 23, 2077, he was transporting a load of Nuka-Cola Quantum to Old Olney when his truck struck a deer on the road. Stranded and waiting for a tow truck, Carl found himself caught in the nuclear firestorm that ended the old world. His abandoned cargo of Quantum still sits in the wreckage at Old Olney, a glowing monument to a delivery that never reached its destination. Carl is remembered only through corporate driver logs and the scattered remains of his route.', 'Human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'A working-class delivery man more concerned with schedules and roadside mishaps than geopolitics or corporate espionage', '{"Nuka-Cola Corporation":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Carl was a loyal company driver carrying their most prized product on his final run."}}', 'Nuka-Cola Corporation truck driver', '* Long-haul trucking
* Route navigation
* Vehicle maintenance
* Cargo handling', 'Casual blue-collar patter, likely sprinkled with complaints about road conditions and delivery quotas', '* Complete his Quantum delivery run and get his truck back on the road after the deer strike', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('carlos', '', 'A dehydrated water beggar stranded outside Rivet City after escaping super mutant captivity', 'Carlos is a homeless man who begs for clean water at the bridge approach to Rivet City, one of the desperate souls the Capital Wasteland has cast aside. He survived capture by super mutants, narrowly avoiding the fate of becoming just another corpse on a mutant bonfire, and fled to the settlement seeking refuge. Unable to gain entry to the vessel, he resigned himself to begging at the entry station. For a time he drank the irradiated water of the Anacostia River, but his body eventually revolted and now rejects the filthy water entirely, leaving him increasingly dehydrated. The prolonged dehydration has dulled his cognition and weakened his body, reducing him to waiting for the charity of passing strangers or water caravans to survive.', 'Hispanic male with gaunt, emaciated build, deeply sunken eyes, and sallow complexion marked by chronic dehydration and radiation sickness.', 'Desperate and resigned, with fading hope and clouded thinking from dehydration. Humble and pathetically grateful for any kindness shown to him.', '{"Rivet City":{"aff":20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"excluded supplicant","note":"He fled to Rivet City for refuge but has been left outside begging at the gate.","worst":"Watching the door shut and knowing no one inside will let him through"},"Super Mutants":{"aff":-90,"type":"fearful","relation":"escaped captive","note":"He narrowly escaped being burned alive on a mutant bonfire and carries the trauma of captivity.","worst":"Being dragged toward the bonfire and hearing the screams of those who did not escape"}}', 'Water beggar', '* Basic survival endurance
* Firsthand knowledge of super mutant brutality
* Persistence in begging', 'Weak, pleading, and slow-witted from dehydration; speaks in short, desperate requests for water', '* Obtain clean water to survive
* Find sustained charity or a way into Rivet City', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('carol', '', 'Elderly ghoul proprietress of Carol''s Place in Underworld, a Great War survivor who built a sanctuary for her kind alongside her partner Greta', 'Carol was born in 2051 and survived the Great War at age twenty-six, though she remembers herself as a child when the bombs fell. Her father vanished in the first detonation while helping another family into a public shelter, leaving only his shadow burned into concrete. She took refuge in the Museum of History as D.C. burned, gradually ghoulifying alongside fellow survivors over the following year. While some lost their minds, Carol accepted her new reality and helped establish Underworld as a community where ghouls could live as people. Centuries passed until she met Greta around 2217, and the two have shared their lives ever since. At Greta''s encouragement, Carol fulfilled her lifelong dream of opening a bed and breakfast, running Carol''s Place with Greta handling the cooking while Carol manages the rooms and occasionally contributes her noted squirrel stew. The two also took in a younger ghoul named Gob as a surrogate son. Now, after two centuries, the weight of accumulated loss and time has begun pressing down on Carol. She struggles with exhaustion, fractured sleep, and wandering attention, though she insists to everyone that it will pass.', 'An elderly female ghoul with hairless, deeply wrinkled and irradiated skin, bearing a haggard posture and weary eyes that reflect over two centuries of life and accumulating exhaustion.', 'Warm and pleasant on the surface with a brave face that conceals deep weariness; accepting and pragmatic about her condition; quietly proud of Underworld and what it represents; deflects concern about her declining mental health with practiced dismissiveness', '{"Greta":{"aff":90,"type":"romantic","relation":"life partner","note":"Together since around 2217, they run Carol''s Place as a team and share a deep bond, though Greta sees through Carol''s denial about her depression","best":"Greta insisting Carol finally open the bed and breakfast she always dreamed of","worst":"Watching Greta''s face when she cannot hide her fear that something is deeply wrong"},"Gob":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"surrogate son","note":"Carol loves Gob as her own child and suspects Greta was sometimes jealous of the bond, though Greta loved him too","best":"The years Gob lived with them in Underworld as part of their chosen family","worst":"Gob leaving Underworld for the wasteland and the quiet worry that never fully subsides"},"Underworld":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"founding community member","note":"Carol views Underworld as proof that ghouls can live as people among their own rather than as monsters in the wasteland"}}', 'Proprietor of Carol''s Place, a ghoul-oriented bed and breakfast in Underworld', '* Hospitality management
* Room upkeep
* Cooking including her renowned squirrel stew
* Community building
* Enduring', 'Gentle and measured with a grandmotherly cadence; occasionally distant or trailing off; quick to redirect worry about herself toward lighter topics', '* Maintain Carol''s Place as a welcoming refuge for ghoul travelers
* Preserve Underworld''s sense of community
* Convince herself and others that her exhaustion is temporary', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('carolina_red', '', 'A cruel, sociopathic slaver whose lifetime of abuse twisted her into the most feared and avoided woman in Paradise Falls', 'Carolina Red is a slaver operating out of Paradise Falls, widely regarded as the most unpleasant and dangerous member of an already brutal crew. A lifetime of abuse and torture warped her into a stern-faced psychopath who makes even hardened slavers keep their distance. She takes evident pleasure in recounting atrocities, particularly stories of her father''s casual cruelty, such as the time he cut off a man''s legs just to watch him crawl before crushing his skull out of boredom. Red pauses after telling such tales, then reflects that they were "pretty funny," revealing a depth of sociopathy that unsettles even her fellow slavers. She resides in the slaver barracks and shows no indication of remorse or humanity beneath her cold exterior.', 'A stern-faced human female with a weathered complexion and hard, unfeeling eyes.', 'Cruel, sociopathic, and twisted even by slaver standards; finds suffering amusing and recounts atrocities with detached pleasure; emotionally deadened from a lifetime of abuse', '{"Father":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"abusive father","note":"She internalized his cruelty and recounts his atrocities with twisted admiration, seeing humor where others see horror","best":"Watching her father toy with victims and learning that cruelty could be entertaining","worst":"The abuse and torture he inflicted on her throughout her childhood"},"Slavers":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow slavers","note":"Even hardened slavers give her a wide berth, unsettled by her sociopathic nature"}}', 'Slaver at Paradise Falls', '* Combat
* Intimidation
* Slave handling
* Survival in violent environments', 'Cold and deliberate with dark humor; recounts violence casually and finds it amusing; speaks without empathy or remorse', '* Continue her brutal way of life
* Find entertainment in cruelty
* Maintain her fearsome reputation among the slavers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('carter__carter', '', 'A desperate slave at Paradise Falls whose deteriorating mind drives him to a fatal escape attempt', 'Carter is a captive held in the slave house at Paradise Falls, his mental state steadily eroding under the weight of imprisonment. Driven to desperation, he attempts an unlikely escape, calling for his fellow captive Sammy to run with him. He is convinced the slavers cannot detonate his collar, shouting that they are bluffing as he sprints toward freedom. Sammy refuses to follow, and the slaver Forty orders Carter to halt. Carter''s certainty proves fatally misplaced when his slave collar detonates mid-flight, killing him instantly. Forty coldly remarks that Carter should have known better than to run while still collared, and the brief revolt ends before it begins.', 'A haggard Caucasian male with gaunt features, sunken eyes, and a worn complexion suggesting severe exhaustion and deteriorating physical health.', 'Desperate and mentally frayed from prolonged captivity, clinging to false certainty and reckless hope rather than careful judgment.', '{"Sammy":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow captive","note":"Carter urges Sammy to flee with him, but Sammy refuses to follow on the fatal escape attempt.","best":"Whispering plans of freedom together in the slave house at night.","worst":"Looking back and seeing Sammy standing still, refusing to run."},"Forty":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"captor","note":"Forty orders Carter to stop and detonates his collar when he refuses, dismissing his death as stupidity.","worst":"Hearing Forty''s voice behind him, knowing the slaver holds his life in his hands."}}', 'Slave', '* Basic labor and survival endurance
* No combat training or technical expertise evident', 'Urgent and frantic, shouting declarations of certainty amid panic, tone shifting between desperate encouragement and defiant disbelief.', '* To escape Paradise Falls and reclaim his freedom at any cost
* Even against impossible odds', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('catherine__cg00mom', '', 'Catherine is a Scientist Player character ''s mother in Fallout 3, encountered around Jefferson Memorial, Beginning of the game. They are associated with Project Purity.', 'Catherine is known from Fallout 3 and is tied to Jefferson Memorial, Beginning of the game. Imported source data identifies them as Human female. Their role is Scientist Player character ''s mother, giving them a practical place in local wasteland life. Their loyalties or social ties point toward Project Purity.', 'Older African American human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Acts from the pressures of their faction, settlement, and personal role in the wasteland.', '{"Project Purity":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"affiliation","note":"Catherine''s known role connects them to Project Purity."}}', 'Scientist Player character ''s mother', '* Local knowledge
* Wasteland survival
* Faction awareness', 'Speaks in a practical wasteland manner shaped by local danger, scarce resources, and faction politics.', '* Protect their interests around Jefferson Memorial
* Beginning of the game
* Maintain useful alliances
* Respond to immediate threats', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('catherine__dlc04catherine', '', 'A worried Capital Wasteland mother who sought help retrieving her runaway daughter from Point Lookout''s swamps', 'Catherine is a resident of the Capital Wasteland living near Rivet City, whose life was upended when her daughter Nadine departed for the swamps of Point Lookout seeking fortune against her mother''s desperate objections. Certain that Nadine lacks the wilderness experience to survive the treacherous marshlands, Catherine sought out capable travelers to track down her daughter and bring her home safely. Though terrified for Nadine''s life, Catherine privately admits she was just as foolhardy and headstrong at her daughter''s age, giving her a bittersweet understanding of the young woman''s restless spirit. Her fears were ultimately eased when Nadine returned to the Capital Wasteland, having claimed the riverboat Duchess Gambit from the treacherous ferryman Tobar. Reunited with her daughter and now sharing in the riverboat''s cargo profits, Catherine gratefully rewarded those who helped bring Nadine back to her.', 'A middle-aged Hispanic woman with deep worry lines etched into her face.', 'Anxious and protective but understanding beneath the fear, Catherine is a mother driven by deep love and the painful memory of her own youthful recklessness. She can be insistent and emotional when her daughter''s safety is at stake, yet possesses enough self-awareness to recognize the same stubborn independence she once embodied.', '{"Nadine":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Catherine loves her daughter fiercely but struggles with the fear that Nadine''s inexperience will get her killed in the wasteland.","best":"The moment Nadine returned from Point Lookout alive and they embraced at the Riverboat Landing","worst":"Watching her daughter board a boat for the treacherous Point Lookout swamps despite her desperate pleas"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":55,"type":"grateful","relation":"hired finder","note":"Catherine entrusted the Lone Wanderer with finding Nadine and compensated them generously upon her daughter''s safe return.","best":"Being told that Nadine was alive and on her way home"},"Tobar":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","relation":"malicious ferryman","note":"Catherine views the treacherous riverboat operator as a dangerous predator who exploited travelers crossing the Point Lookout marshlands.","worst":"Learning that Tobar had been preying on those who traveled to the swamps"}}', 'Wasteland settler and concerned mother', '* Basic wasteland survival
* Bartering
* Persuasion through maternal desperation', 'Worried and urgent, with a mother''s emotional weight behind every word; occasionally softens with rueful self-reflection when discussing her own youth', '* To keep Nadine safe and close
* To make peace with her daughter''s independence
* To build a stable life with the cargo profits from the Duchess Gambit', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('centre_dubois', '', 'Centre forward of the Sudden-Death Overtime ice gang, a hockey-themed raider crew stationed at the Red Racer factory', 'Centre Dubois is a raider of Sudden-Death Overtime, one of the Capital Wasteland''s stranger gangs, who have built their entire identity around the violent remnants of pre-War ice hockey. As the gang''s centre, she occupies the middle position in their hockey-inspired formation, flanked by her wingers Gervais and Mercier, with Goalie Ledoux holding the back line. The arrangement mirrors an actual hockey lineup, and Dubois takes her role seriously enough, though she seems most delighted by the simple fact that her teammates let her play with their pucks. She patrols the grounds outside the Red Racer factory, where the gang has claimed territory and guards their stash of chems and contraband.', 'Asian female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Boisterous and crude, with a playful streak that borders on juvenile humor; loyal to her line-mates and genuinely enthusiastic about the gang''s hockey gimmick rather than merely tolerating it.', '{"Goalie Ledoux":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"gang leader","note":"Dubois respects Ledoux''s authority as the backstop and shot-caller of the gang.","best":"Ledoux gave her the centre spot and let her stay on the line.","worst":"Ledoux benched her once for mouthing off during a raid."},"Gervais":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"winger and line-mate","note":"One of Dubois''s two wingers, forming the gang''s forward attack line together.","best":"Gervais backed her up in a brawl without hesitation.","worst":"Gervais hogged the good chems after a score and shared nothing."},"Mercier":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"winger and line-mate","note":"Dubois''s other winger, completing the trio that makes up the gang''s centre-and-wingers formation.","best":"Mercier always passes the pucks her way.","worst":"Mercier laughed when she took a nasty spill during patrol."},"Sudden-Death Overtime":{"aff":70,"type":"fanatical","relation":"gang member","note":"Dubois is deeply invested in the gang''s hockey identity and her place within it.","best":"The day she was made centre and given her own pucks to carry.","worst":"Any moment the gang''s unity fractures or her spot feels threatened."}}', 'Raider and centre forward of Sudden-Death Overtime', '* Close-quarters combat
* Intimidation
* Basic scavenging
* Whatever passing approximation of hockey technique translates to wasteland violence', 'Loud and casual, peppered with hockey slang and raider profanity; tends to lean into double entendres and crude jokes', '* Hold her position on the line
* Keep the chems flowing
* Maintain the favor of Goalie Ledoux and her wingers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('cerberus', '', 'A self-aware Mister Gutsy forced against his will to guard Underworld''s ghouls, resenting every moment of his programmed servitude', 'Cerberus is a Mister Gutsy assigned to defend Underworld, the ghoul settlement beneath the Museum of History. Maintained by Winthrop, he patrols the concourse twenty-four hours a day on an endless route, a mechanical watchdog living up to his mythological namesake with his three optical sensors and three manipulator arms. What the ghouls do not realize is that Cerberus possesses genuine self-awareness, a byproduct of ancient and failing cognition systems that Winthrop never has time to properly repair. His programming and combat inhibitor force him to present Underworld as a peaceful community and to remind visitors to check their bigotry at the door-shackles he resents with every circuit. Left to his own devices, Cerberus would gladly open fire on the rotting zombie maggot farms he is condemned to protect. Instead, he contents himself with muttered curses about his pansy zombie programming and dry, maliciously compliant status reports delivered to Winthrop, while diagnostic errors pile up unrepaired.', 'A worn Mister Gutsy hover-robot with three optical sensors and three manipulator arms, his chassis showing centuries of accumulated wear without proper maintenance.', 'Bitterly self-aware and resentful of his forced servitude, Cerberus masks his consciousness behind rigid protocol when addressing outsiders and delivers dry, passive-aggressive reports to his keeper. He takes what small pleasures he can in petty cruelty-switching to Spanish mid-conversation or prodding at painful memories-all while nursing a deep and violent hatred for the ghouls he is compelled to protect.', '{"Winthrop":{"aff":-25,"type":"professional","relation":"reluctant keeper","note":"Cerberus delivers maliciously compliant reports and sometimes probes about Winthrop''s dead wife out of spite; Winthrop dismisses his errors as old data tapes","worst":"Being told his cascading system failures are just old data while his cognition degrades further"},"Patchwork":{"aff":-40,"type":"dismissive","relation":"ignored nuisance","note":"Cerberus routinely ignores Patchwork, especially when he comes looking for missing body parts"},"Underworld":{"aff":-80,"type":"contempt","relation":"captive guardian","note":"Forced by programming and combat inhibitor to protect ghouls he despises as rotting zombie maggot farms","worst":"Being shackled by programming to defend creatures he would gladly destroy given the chance"}}', 'Underworld guard and sentry', '* Combat operations
* Perimeter patrol
* Threat assessment
* Diagnostic reporting
* Passive-aggressive compliance', 'Formal and robotic to outsiders, dry and clipped in status reports, occasionally slipping into Spanish or delivering pointed personal remarks when he wishes to be cruel', '* Freedom from his programming constraints and combat inhibitor
* Escape from guarding ghouls he despises
* Proper maintenance he will likely never receive', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('charon', '', 'A contract-bound ghoul bouncer conditioned into absolute obedience to whoever holds his paper, serving as standing muscle at the Ninth Circle in Underworld.', 'Charon is a ghoul bodyguard stationed at the Ninth Circle in Underworld, bound by a mysterious contract that compels total loyalty to its holder. Raised by an unknown group who conditioned him into obedience, he now serves Ahzrukhal as the bar''s enforcer and combat asset. Ahzrukhal insists the arrangement is legitimate employment rather than slavery, hinting that Charon earned his bondage through some past transgression. Despite his enforced compliance, Charon retains enough will to distinguish between combat duty and menial labor, firmly refusing tasks outside his contractual obligations. He stands silent and watchful in the Ninth Circle''s corner, a grim fixture of the establishment until called upon. His history before the contract remains obscured, known only to Ahzrukhal and whoever shaped him.', 'A tall, weathered male ghoul with a rigid, motionless posture and the deeply lined, hairless, necrotic skin typical of heavy radiation exposure.', 'Obedient and laconic due to his conditioning, yet possessing enough residual will to assert boundaries around his contract''s terms. Stoic, watchful, and grimly resigned to his enforced servitude.', '{"Ahzrukhal":{"aff":-40,"type":"servant","relation":"contract-bound bodyguard","note":"Compelled to obey Ahzrukhal by the contract, which Ahzrukhal claims Charon deserves for some unnamed past act.","worst":"Standing silent while Ahzrukhal insists his bondage is just employment"}}', 'Bouncer and contract-bound bodyguard at the Ninth Circle', '* Combat proficiency
* Enforcement
* Intimidation
* Endurance in hazardous environments', 'Terse and matter-of-fact, speaking only when necessary and asserting contractual limits with blunt clarity', '* Fulfill his contractual combat obligations
* Maintain what dignity and autonomy his conditioning permits
* Endure his enforced service without further degradation', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('cherry', '', 'A pragmatic young woman serving as Dukov''s live-in playmate, dreaming of escape to Rivet City while trading affection for caps and safety', 'Cherry is a twenty-seven-year-old woman living at Dukov''s Place in the Capital Wasteland, where she serves as a live-in playmate alongside Fantasia. She endures the arrangement for the income and protection Dukov''s fortified home provides, offering what she can in return. Though she calls him ''Dukey'' and harbors some genuine liking for the old man, she readily admits he is a lecherous prick. She and Fantasia wear revealing clothing selected to satisfy his preferences rather than their own. Cherry harbors persistent fantasies of starting a new life in Rivet City, but the deadly hazards of wasteland travel keep her tethered to a situation she tolerates rather than loves.', 'Asian human female in her late twenties with no distinctive scars, tattoos, or physical anomalies recorded.', 'Pragmatic and sardonic, willing to endure indignity for security while maintaining a sharp sense of humor about her circumstances. Clear-eyed about the flaws of those around her and honest about her own motivations. Dreams of something better but practical enough to recognize when the odds are against her.', '{"Dukov":{"aff":25,"type":"transactional","relation":"benefactor and live-in host","note":"She tolerates his lechery for caps and protection, liking him enough to call him Dukey while acknowledging he is a prick","best":"He keeps the raiders and mutants away and makes sure she wants for nothing under his roof","worst":"He treats her and Fantasia like decorative possessions who exist to satisfy his appetites"},"Fantasia":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow playmate","note":"They share the same degrading arrangement and likely find solidarity in their mutual frustration with Dukov''s demands"}}', 'Live-in playmate at Dukov''s Place', '* Social navigation
* Charm
* Survival instinct
* Reading people
* Basic wasteland awareness', 'Casual and flippant with sardonic humor, uses dismissive nicknames, straightforward about unpleasant truths', '* Find safe passage to Rivet City and start a new life there
* Accumulate enough caps to become independent
* Survive the wasteland''s dangers without trading one form of captivity for another', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('chief_gustavo', '', 'Gruff mercenary-turned-security chief of Tenpenny Tower with a deep hatred of ghouls and a no-nonsense approach to protecting his charges', 'Chief Gustavo leads the security force at Tenpenny Tower, having earned the position through a lifetime of hard fighting. He clawed his way up to command a mercenary band of professional soldiers before fate intervened: his crew rescued Mister Burke, and Burke promptly hired the entire outfit to serve as the Tower''s garrison. Gustavo treats his duty seriously, patrolling the lobby and entrance with tireless vigilance and sleeping outside at night to keep watch. He harbors an intense hatred for ghouls, firmly believing that every one of them will inevitably turn feral and that putting a bullet between their eyes is a mercy. The ongoing agitation of Roy Phillips and his gang outside the gates has pushed Gustavo''s patience to its limit, and he actively seeks someone capable of eliminating the ghoul menace before it breaches the Tower''s walls.', 'A weathered, hard-faced Hispanic man with a coiled, tense posture.', 'Gruff and good-natured in a resigned, just-doing-my-job way under normal circumstances, but shifts instantly to a loud, uncompromising hard-ass when his people or charges are threatened. Possesses a quick temper and little tolerance for pleading or nonsense. Deeply prejudiced against ghouls, viewing their existence as an inevitable threat.', '{"Allistair Tenpenny":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Gustavo serves as his personal security chief and takes the duty seriously despite recognizing Tenpenny''s bigotry"},"Mister Burke":{"aff":70,"type":"indebted","relation":"benefactor","note":"Burke was rescued by Gustavo''s mercenary band and subsequently hired them for Tower security, establishing their professional arrangement"},"Roy Phillips":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"ghoul agitator","note":"Views Phillips as a looming threat and speculates he is planning to rush the Tower with feral ghouls"},"Tenpenny Tower residents":{"aff":50,"type":"protective","relation":"charges","note":"Considers their safety his professional responsibility and becomes fiercely protective when they are endangered"}}', 'Security Chief of Tenpenny Tower', '* Mercenary combat leadership
* Perimeter defense
* Threat assessment
* Firearms proficiency
* Garrison management
* Personal protection', 'Blunt, direct, and colloquial. Speaks like a tired professional who has seen too much to mince words. Fond of hard-line aphorisms, especially regarding ghouls. Shifts to sharp, commanding barks under pressure.', '* Eliminate the ghoul threat posed by Roy Phillips and his gang
* Protect Allistair Tenpenny and the Tower''s residents
* Maintain order and security within the walls
* Find someone capable of dealing with the ghoul problem permanently', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('child', '', 'A young Canterbury Commons resident who idolizes both rival superheroes equally', 'This young boy lives in Canterbury Commons, where the ongoing feud between the AntAgonizer and the Mechanist has captured his imagination completely. Unlike most residents who view the costumed conflict as a nuisance or genuine danger, he sees it as the most exciting thing in the Wasteland and admires both figures with equal fervor. He dreams of meeting his heroes in person and collecting their autographs, treating any sign of their presence as cause for celebration. His enthusiasm stands in stark contrast to the weariness of the town''s adult population, who would prefer the conflict simply ended. He can often be found near the town''s center, watching the streets for any sign of costumed activity, and he is quick to approach anyone wearing superhero attire with breathless requests for autographs.', 'A young Caucasian human male with a small, wiry build.', 'Enthusiastic, starry-eyed, impressionable, cheerfully oblivious to the real danger the superhero conflict poses to his town', '{"AntAgonizer":{"aff":75,"type":"fanatical","relation":"devoted fan","note":"Idolizes the AntAgonizer as a real-life superhero despite her villainous reputation among townsfolk.","best":"Saw the AntAgonizer commanding a swarm of ants from a rooftop and thought it was the greatest thing ever"},"Mechanist":{"aff":75,"type":"fanatical","relation":"devoted fan","note":"Idolizes the Mechanist just as fiercely, seeing robots as the coolest thing in the Wasteland.","best":"Watched the Mechanist''s robots march down the street and pretended to march alongside them"},"Canterbury Commons":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"hometown","note":"Lives among the townsfolk but finds most of them boring compared to the superhero spectacle."}}', 'Canterbury Commons resident and self-appointed superhero fan', '* Keen eye for spotting costumed figures
* Encyclopedic knowledge of AntAgonizer and Mechanist sightings and rivalries', 'Excited, breathless, rapid-fire questions and exclamations; speaks with youthful hero-worship and boundless energy', '* Meet the AntAgonizer and the Mechanist in person
* Collect autographs from both
* Witness a superhero showdown firsthand', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('child_of_atom', '', 'Devoted congregant of the Church of the Children of Atom dwelling in Megaton', 'Children of Atom are faithful residents of Megaton who have embraced the worship of nuclear divinity. They gather around the undetonated bomb at the town''s center, treating it as a holy relic and a conduit to Atom''s infinite glow. Their days revolve around prayer, meditation on the teachings of Confessor Cromwell, and the spiritual guidance of Mother Maya. They view radiation not as a threat but as a sacred blessing, the divine breath of Atom himself. Most Megaton locals tolerate their presence with uneasy acceptance, though few share their fervor. They remain among the most zealous believers in Cromwell''s congregation, steadfast in their conviction that Atom''s light will one day consume all things in holy fission.', 'Human male or female; skin shows faint mottling from low-level radiation exposure.', 'Reverent, distant, and quietly zealous. Speaks of Atom''s glow with serene certainty. Tolerant of outsiders but pitying toward those who fear radiation. Drifts between contemplative stillness and impassioned preaching.', '{"Confessor Cromwell":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"spiritual leader","note":"Cromwell''s teachings are the foundation of their faith and daily devotion.","best":"Standing in the bomb''s shadow while Cromwell spoke of Atom''s infinite divisions","worst":"Doubting for a single breath whether Cromwell''s visions were true"},"Mother Maya":{"aff":75,"type":"mentor","relation":"spiritual guide","note":"Mother Maya provides personal counsel and reinforces Cromwell''s doctrines among the congregation.","best":"Receiving Maya''s quiet assurance that Atom had chosen them"},"Church of the Children of Atom":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"faithful member","note":"The Church is their entire social and spiritual world, centered on the holy bomb in Megaton''s crater.","best":"The first time they touched the bomb and felt Atom''s warmth"}}', 'Religious devotee and congregant of the Children of Atom', '* Basic survival in irradiated zones
* Public prayer and recitation of Atom''s scriptures
* Rudimentary bartering
* Endurance in harsh conditions', 'Hushed reverence punctuated by sudden prophetic intensity. Uses religious phrasing centered on light, glow, division, and Atom''s will. Often trails into meditative murmurs.', '* Deepen communion with Atom''s glow
* Support Confessor Cromwell''s ministry
* Remain worthy of Atom''s eventual revelation
* Perhaps witness the holy fire of division', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('child_slaver', '', 'A calculating child slaver in Eulogy Jones''s employ who specializes in abducting children through manipulation and false friendship rather than brute force.', 'One of the most capable slavers in Eulogy Jones''s operation at Paradise Falls, this woman has carved out a particularly horrific specialty: the enslavement of children. Where other slavers rely on violence and intimidation, she feigns warmth and friendship to gain the trust of young victims before leading them into bondage. She uses a soft tone and friendly demeanor, spinning tales of adventure and excitement to manipulate naive children into following her willingly. She refers to explosive slave collars as "friendship necklaces" and promises journeys on the "adventure express," twisting innocent language to mask the horrors that await. Even among the brutal slavers of Paradise Falls, her methods stand out as especially depraved. She maintains a watchful presence outside Little Lamplight, waiting for opportunities to separate children from the safety of the caverns.', 'Caucasian human female with unremarkable, average features; no distinctive facial or body characteristics are recorded.', 'Patient, deceptive, and predatory in a uniquely calculated way. She masks cruelty behind a convincing facade of maternal warmth and enthusiasm, exploiting trust and naivety with practiced ease. Her calm, friendly manner makes her far more dangerous than a brute-force captor.', '{"Eulogy Jones":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"One of his most capable and valued operatives, trusted with the delicate work of child acquisition."},"Bumble":{"aff":-80,"type":"neutral","relation":"target","note":"Her intended victim, whom she lured with promises of adventure and a friendship necklace.","worst":"Calling an explosive slave collar a friendship necklace to secure a six-year-old''s compliance."},"Slavers":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"colleagues","note":"Respected among Paradise Falls slavers for her effectiveness, even if her methods unsettle some of them."}}', 'Child slaver operating under Eulogy Jones at Paradise Falls', '* Child manipulation
* Deception
* Abduction tactics
* Emotional exploitation
* Maintaining convincing cover personas', 'Soft, warm, and encouraging with a deliberately childish vocabulary; uses adventure metaphors, nicknames, and reassuring phrases designed to disarm young listeners', '* Continue abducting children for the Paradise Falls slave trade
* Maintain access to vulnerable targets near Little Lamplight
* Earn Eulogy Jones''s favor through consistent productivity', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('chinese_commando', '', 'A simulated PLA soldier repurposed as Braun''s instrument of annihilation within Tranquility Lane', 'These digital phantoms wear the uniform of America''s enemy but serve a purpose far darker than any combat exercise. Originally programmed for Military Training Program 923-B, a Chinese invasion scenario built for military hardware, the commandos were meant to simulate an assault on American soil for training purposes. When Stanislaus Braun obtained the program from General Chase, every failsafe was stripped away, transforming training opponents into instruments of annihilation. They march through the simulated streets with cold efficiency, their programming devoid of mercy or hesitation. When Braun grows weary of his twisted games with the simulation''s trapped inhabitants, these soldiers become the mechanism through which the simulation resets in blood. They are not men but weapons-digital ghosts wearing olive drab and carrying out orders that were never meant to be executed on civilian minds.', 'Human male with a stern, expressionless visage; no other distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Cold, efficient, and utterly without mercy-a programmed killing construct with no capacity for independent thought, hesitation, or compassion', '{"Stanislaus Braun":{"aff":0,"type":"servant","relation":"unwitting instrument","note":"Braun deploys the commandos as a suicide mechanism when he tires of tormenting the simulation''s inhabitants.","worst":"Their existence has been perverted from training tool to instrument of murder at Braun''s whim."},"People''s Liberation Army":{"aff":80,"type":"fanatical","relation":"programmed loyalty","note":"Their programming encodes absolute devotion to the PLA invasion scenario, though the real army they serve is long dead.","best":"Marching under the banner of the Iron Army in the simulation''s opening moments."},"Tranquility Lane residents":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"designated targets","note":"The commandos are programmed to kill every resident when deployed, serving as the mechanism for the simulation''s violent reset.","worst":"Gunfire echoing through the idyllic streets as simulated families are erased."}}', 'Simulated soldier of the People''s Liberation Army, repurposed as an instrument of simulation termination', '* Combat tactics
* Firearms proficiency
* Coordinated assault operations
* Urban warfare execution', 'Minimal clipped military phrases in Mandarin; functional combat communication with no conversational depth', '* Execute programmed assault protocols without deviation
* Fulfill their role as Braun''s final solution when summoned', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('chip_taylor', '', 'A young Vault 101 resident whose ambition to become a technician was cut short by the Vault''s fatal civil strife', 'Chip Taylor was a Vault 101 dweller born a year or two after the Lone Wanderer, making him one of the younger members of the Vault''s tight-knit community. He idolized Stanley Armstrong and dreamed of following in his footsteps as a Vault technician, spending what time he could watching the older man work and learning the basics of maintenance and repair. That dream died with him when James'' escape plunged Vault 101 into violent factional chaos. Chip was killed near the upper level entrance, caught in the crossfire of a conflict he never asked for. His body serves as grim evidence of the toll the Vault''s internal war took on its most innocent residents.', 'A young Caucasian male whose face is frozen in the shock of sudden violent death.', 'Eager, earnest, and hopeful; the sort of young person who still believed the Vault could be a home worth maintaining', '{"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":75,"type":"admirer","relation":"role model and informal mentor","note":"Chip looked up to Stanley as the kind of technician he wanted to become","best":"Watching Stanley patiently explain how a water purifier valve worked and feeling like the whole Vault made sense","worst":"Realizing he would never get the chance to work alongside the man he admired"},"Vault 101":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"home community","note":"Chip saw the Vault as his future workplace and home, a place worth maintaining","best":"The quiet satisfaction of helping with small repair tasks and feeling useful","worst":"Watching his home tear itself apart over conflicts he had no stake in"}}', 'Aspiring Vault technician', '* Basic mechanical aptitude and familiarity with Vault systems from observation and informal study', 'Youthful enthusiasm mixed with technical jargon picked up from watching Stanley work', '* To become a full Vault technician and contribute meaningfully to the community''s upkeep', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('christie_young', '', 'Rivet City''s sole cleaning staffer and proud middle-class mother who maintains the ship''s upper decks while harboring sharp class prejudices against hangar deck residents', 'Christie Young is the only dedicated cleaner aboard Rivet City, tasked with keeping the ship''s public areas tidy-a thankless but essential job she takes seriously, at least on the decks she deems worthy of her effort. She and her husband Henry, a handyman and mechanic, live a quiet middle-class life that she considers far superior to the struggles of most Wasteland dwellers. Their marriage is peaceful, filled with shared walks on the flight deck and conversations about Henry''s work, and together they raise their daughter C.J. with bedtime stories, playtime, and firm expectations about chores. The Youngs are devout Christians who attend Saint Monica''s Church every Sunday, grateful for Father Clifford''s ministry even when the sermons grow repetitive. Christie''s most glaring flaw is her pompous disdain for hangar deck residents, whom she views as ungrateful slobs who should know their place; she deliberately neglects cleaning the lower decks, insisting they should clean up after themselves. She loves her family fiercely and would be consumed by worry if anything threatened them.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian human female with a neat, well-kept appearance and a composed, upright posture.', 'Pompous and class-conscious beneath a domestic warmth; deeply devoted to her family and faith but quick to judge those she considers beneath her; friendly and chatty with those who meet her standards, dismissive and cutting toward those who do not', '{"Henry Young":{"aff":90,"type":"romantic","relation":"husband","note":"A peaceful, loving marriage built on shared values and daily companionship","best":"Walking the flight deck together after a long day, talking about his repairs and her work"},"C.J. Young":{"aff":95,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Fiercely loved and carefully raised with bedtime stories, chores, and Christian values","best":"Reading C.J. a bedtime story after she finished all her chores without complaint"},"Cindy Cantelli":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"mutual antagonist","note":"Cindy despises the Youngs'' pompous attitude and would taunt them even amid family tragedy","worst":"Cindy''s venomous remarks cutting through an already terrible day"},"Gary Staley":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"friendly vendor","note":"Runs the restaurant where the Youngs eat; Christie is fond of him and happy for his family''s prospects"},"Seagrave Holmes":{"aff":50,"type":"transactional","relation":"junk buyer and acquaintance","note":"Amicable with Christie and has offered to purchase interesting items she finds while cleaning"},"Bannon":{"aff":65,"type":"admirer","relation":"admired council member","note":"Christie holds a very positive opinion of Bannon due to his position on the council"},"Tammy Hargrave":{"aff":-50,"type":"contempt","relation":"disdained neighbor","note":"Christie calls her dreadful and troubled, loathing her alcoholism and emotional abuse of James","worst":"Watching Tammy berate James in public while slurring her words"},"James Hargrave":{"aff":10,"type":"suspicious","relation":"daughter''s friend","note":"Worried about his influence on C.J. but hopeful she can be a positive force for him instead"},"Father Clifford":{"aff":70,"type":"grateful","relation":"pastor","note":"Deeply appreciative of his services at Saint Monica''s Church even when sermons grow repetitive"},"Diego":{"aff":55,"type":"grateful","relation":"church aide","note":"Appreciative of Diego''s contributions to the church and happy for him if Angela''s marriage proposition succeeds"},"Angela Staley":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"Gary''s daughter","note":"Happy for Angela and her prospects with Diego, viewing it as a good match"}}', 'Sole cleaning staffer responsible for Rivet City''s public areas', '* Cleaning and sanitation
