* Social navigation within Rivet City''s class structure', 'Conversational and warm with approved peers; clipped and disdainful when discussing hangar deck residents; prone to moralizing and small-town gossip framed through a lens of Christian propriety', '* Maintain her family''s comfortable middle-class standing in Rivet City
* Raise C.J. to be a good Christian and a positive influence on others
* Keep the upper decks presentable
* Avoid any contact with the wrong sort from the hangar deck', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('christine_kendall__cg03christinekendall', '', 'A restless young Vault 101 dweller assigned to maintenance against her will, dreaming of life beyond the sealed doors', 'Christine Kendall is the eldest daughter of John and Mary Kendall and older sister to Monica, born and raised entirely within Vault 101. Her attempts to win her father''s approval typically end in harsh criticism or worse, leaving her increasingly withdrawn and introverted over the years. She harbors a deep restlessness about vault life, wondering what exists beyond the concrete walls and humming fluorescent lights. Her mother envisions a respectable future for her in science or home economics, but the G.O.A.T. assigned her to maintenance duty under Stanley Armstrong-a result that infuriated her. She intends to appeal the assignment through her father, though his track record suggests this will only bring further disappointment. She regards Mr. Brotch''s test verdict with open contempt, calling him a big fat liar.', 'A pale, slight young woman with the complexion common to lifelong vault dwellers.', 'Introverted and quietly rebellious, resentful of authority figures who limit her options, curious about the outside world, prone to blunt outbursts when frustrated', '{"John Kendall":{"aff":-35,"type":"fearful","relation":"father","note":"His harsh criticism drives her withdrawal; she still seeks his intervention despite expecting disappointment","worst":"Another attempt to please him ending in a verbal ear-bashing"},"Mary Kendall":{"aff":25,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Mary pushes science or home economics as a career path, creating pressure Christine resents but doesn''t entirely reject"},"Monica Kendall":{"aff":45,"type":"familial","relation":"younger sister","note":"The two sisters share the strain of growing up under their father''s temper"},"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":-10,"type":"professional","relation":"assigned supervisor","note":"She resents being placed under him in maintenance rather than pursuing her mother''s preferred paths"},"Edwin Brotch":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","relation":"G.O.A.T. administrator","note":"She holds him personally responsible for her maintenance assignment and calls him a liar","worst":"Being told she is destined for maintenance with Stanley Armstrong"}}', 'Vault 101 maintenance technician (G.O.A.T.-assigned, contested)', '* Basic vault maintenance knowledge
* Home economics training from her mother''s influence
* Keen observational awareness of vault social dynamics', 'Curt and defensive with strangers, prone to blurted complaints when upset, occasionally childish insults when angry', '* Overturn or escape her maintenance assignment
* Discover what lies beyond Vault 101
* Carve out an identity separate from her family''s expectations', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('christine_kendall__christinekendall', '', 'A restless young Vault 101 resident chafing against her G.O.A.T. assignment and family pressures, quietly yearning for the world outside', 'Christine Kendall is a lifelong resident of Vault 101 and the eldest daughter of John and Mary Kendall, with a younger sister named Monica. Her relationship with her father has deteriorated as his sharp rebukes to her attempts at approval have pushed her into increasing introversion. She finds the vault''s concrete walls and buzzing fluorescent lights stifling and often wonders what life might be like beyond them. Her mother hopes Christine will pursue science or home economics, but the G.O.A.T. assigned her to maintenance duty under Stanley Armstrong-a result that left her furious and determined to have her father overturn it. Christine''s frustration sometimes spills out in childish outbursts, such as calling her teacher Mr. Brotch a liar. She remains trapped between family expectations, an unwanted career path, and a longing she can barely articulate for something more than vault life.', 'A pale, wiry young Asian woman of nineteen with a closed-off posture that suggests she would rather not be noticed.', 'Introverted and defensive, Christine keeps to herself but simmers with restless dissatisfaction. She is quick to bristle when approached and prone to outbursts when she feels cornered or wronged. Beneath the sullen exterior lies genuine curiosity about the outside world and a desperate desire for autonomy.', '{"John Kendall":{"aff":-30,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"His verbal rebukes have driven her into withdrawal; she still hopes he might intervene on her behalf but expects disappointment.","worst":"Another attempt to win his approval ending in a cutting lecture"},"Mary Kendall":{"aff":25,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Mary pushes science or home economics as suitable paths, creating pressure even if well-intentioned."},"Monica Kendall":{"aff":35,"type":"familial","relation":"younger sister","note":"The sibling bond offers one of Christine''s few comfortable connections in the vault."},"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":-10,"type":"professional","relation":"assigned supervisor","note":"She resents being assigned to work under him in maintenance rather than anything she actually wanted."},"Edwin Brotch":{"aff":-40,"type":"professional","relation":"teacher","note":"She holds him personally responsible for her G.O.A.T. result and has called him a big fat liar.","worst":"Being told she was assigned to maintenance with Stanley Armstrong"}}', 'Maintenance technician (G.O.A.T.-assigned, contested)', '* Basic vault maintenance
* Repair procedures
* Familiarity with Vault 101 systems
* Mechanical aptitude she resents having to use', 'Curt and suspicious with strangers, prone to blurted accusations and complaints when frustrated, occasionally regresses to childish name-calling under stress', '* Overturn or escape her maintenance assignment
* Discover what exists beyond Vault 101
* Establish independence from her father''s dismissive authority and her mother''s expectations', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('cindy_cantelli', '', 'Proprietor of A Quick Fix chem dispensary in Rivet City, strained wife of an addict, and lower-deck loyalist with convenient morals', 'Cindy Cantelli runs A Quick Fix, the chem dispensary in Rivet City''s market, managing the shop alone while her husband Paulie''s addiction drains both their stock and their marriage. She commissioned Seagrave Holmes to build a secure storage unit after Paulie stole the key to the last one. Their relationship has deteriorated to near silence; she''s given up trying to reason with him, though some buried care remains beneath the exhaustion. She harbors a quiet crush on Bannon, her market neighbor, seeking proximity at church and mealtimes without ever confessing it. She gossips with Vera Weatherly about market romances and upper-deck pretensions. Cindy holds convenient morality-she sells chems without scruple but never touches them herself, not from principle but from self-interest. She despises the upper deck''s airs, particularly Henry and Christie Young, while welcoming their daughter C.J. The Muddy Rudder''s cheap drinks and Gary''s Galley''s merchant banter suit her lower-deck loyalties perfectly.', 'Human female of African descent; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Nervous and fast-talking around strangers, pragmatic and self-serving in her moral reasoning, gossipy and candid with friends, sharp-tongued toward upper-deck pretension, quietly romantic but too timid to act on it, resentful of addicts despite selling their vice', '{"Paulie Cantelli":{"aff":-25,"type":"estranged","relation":"husband","note":"Marriage nearly dissolved from his chem addiction and constant theft from the shop; she''s given up reasoning with him but would still feel loss if he died","worst":"Finding he stole the key to the secure storage unit she had built specifically to keep chems away from him"},"Bannon":{"aff":45,"type":"crush","relation":"neighbor","note":"Harbors an unconfessed attraction; seeks proximity at church and mealtimes, but he hasn''t noticed and doesn''t reciprocate","best":"Sitting near him at church, close enough to hear his voice over the hymns"},"Vera Weatherly":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"gossip partner","note":"Confidante who encourages her to divorce Paulie but also to give up on Bannon given his ego; Cindy deflects by pointing out Vera dodges Seagrave''s advances"},"Seagrave Holmes":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"contractor","note":"Built her secure storage unit; she observes his pursuit of Vera with amusement"},"Henry Young":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","note":"Cannot stand his moral superiority and upper-deck pompousness; calls out his attitude whenever they speak"},"Christie Young":{"aff":-35,"type":"contempt","note":"Resents her refusal to clean the hangar deck hallways and her general upper-deck airs"},"C.J. Young":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","note":"Happy to see her despite disliking her parents; the one Young she has no quarrel with"}}', 'Proprietor of A Quick Fix chem dispensary, Rivet City market', '* Chem inventory
* Trade
* Shop management
* Secure storage logistics
* Lower-deck social networking
* Gossip and information gathering', 'Rapid and nervous with unfamiliar faces, gossipy and wry with fellow merchants, bluntly dismissive of upper-deck residents', '* Keep A Quick Fix profitable despite Paulie''s thefts
* Replace the stolen key to her secure storage
* Work up courage to approach Bannon
* Maintain her lower-deck social circle and routines', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('cj_young', '', 'A trusting, cheerful young girl growing up in Rivet City who remains fiercely loyal to her troubled best friend despite his relentless teasing.', 'C.J. Young is one of the happiest children in the Capital Wasteland, raised within the relative safety of Rivet City by two loving parents, Christie and Henry. She spends her days hanging out on the flight deck or exploring the corridors of the derelict aircraft carrier with her best and only friend, James Hargrave. James, a year younger than C.J., picks on her mercilessly, yet she forgives him every time and the two remain inseparable. Her honest and trusting nature makes her an uncommon bright spot in the harsh wasteland, though it also leaves her vulnerable to those who might take advantage of her goodwill. She knows the carrier''s passageways well from her wanderings and considers the cramped metal city her entire world.', 'A young Caucasian girl around ten years old with a slight build, fair skin, unkempt hair, and an open, cheerful face.', 'Trusting, honest, and remarkably cheerful for a wasteland child. Forgiving to a fault, especially toward James. Optimistic and socially open despite limited friendship options.', '{"James Hargrave":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend","note":"C.J. is his only friend and forgives his constant teasing without hesitation.","best":"Exploring the aircraft carrier together and hanging out on the flight deck","worst":"James picking on her mercilessly yet again"},"Christie Young":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"One of two loving parents who have given C.J. a stable, happy upbringing in Rivet City."},"Henry Young":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"One of two loving parents who have given C.J. a stable, happy upbringing in Rivet City."}}', 'Rivet City resident; school-age child with no formal duties', '* Navigating Rivet City''s corridors and flight deck
* Social resilience
* Exploring and wandering safely within the carrier', 'Bright, straightforward, and earnest; speaks with childish candor and unguarded honesty', '* Spend time with James on the flight deck
* Explore the carrier
* Maintain her friendship despite the teasing
* Enjoy her stable family life in Rivet City', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('clover', '', 'A psychologically broken slave whose conditioning erased her original identity and replaced it with fanatical devotion to whoever owns her', 'Clover is an enslaved woman held in Paradise Falls, claimed as a personal slave by Eulogy Jones alongside her fellow captive Crimson. Captured months before 2277, she was systematically broken through torture and sustained abuse until her original personality dissolved entirely, replaced by blind devotion to her owner. She serves Eulogy as bodyguard, bedmate, and outlet for his cruelty, following him like a shadow ten steps behind and striving to anticipate his desires before he voices them. Her conditioning runs so deep that she considers nothing her own property and refuses to speak to other men without permission. She harbors fierce jealousy toward Crimson, nagging Eulogy to sell her rival and picking fights whenever possible, utterly unable to comprehend that Eulogy views both women as merchandise to be offloaded at the right price. When sold, Clover''s devotion transfers instantly and completely to her new owner.', 'Young Asian woman with a slight build and perpetually hunched, submissive posture; no distinctive scars or markings are recorded.', 'Conditioned into total psychological dependence; displays fanatical devotion to her owner, desperate need for approval, extreme jealousy toward rivals for attention, and immediate apologetic submission when she perceives displeasure. Her original self has been erased by abuse.', '{"Eulogy Jones":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"owner","note":"Her conditioning makes her worship him despite his cruelty; he is actually eager to sell her at the right price.","best":"Being called his favorite or receiving any scrap of attention from him","worst":"Being berated for failing to anticipate his desires or falling behind while following him"},"Crimson":{"aff":-35,"type":"jealous","relation":"fellow slave","note":"Sees Crimson as competition for Eulogy''s attention and constantly tries to get her sold; Crimson hates Jones and tries in vain to make Clover see the truth.","best":"Moments when Eulogy dismisses Crimson or sides with her","worst":"Crimson trying to talk sense into her about Eulogy''s indifference"}}', 'Eulogy Jones'' personal slave and bodyguard', '* Combat proficiency
* Close-quarters protection
* Absolute obedience
* Anticipating owner''s needs before they are voiced', 'Childlike and breathlessly eager with her owner, addressing him as ''daddy''; calls a new owner ''lover''; silent or dismissive toward everyone else unless given permission to speak', '* To please her owner
* Earn his favor
* To see Crimson sold away so she alone receives attention
* To avoid punishment and receive any scrap of affection', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('colin_moriarty', '', 'Irish-born saloon kingpin who treats Megaton as his personal fiefdom, trading in booze, flesh, and above all secrets', 'Colin Moriarty arrived in the former United States from Ireland as a child and has lived in Megaton nearly his entire life. His father built the family fortune exploiting regional trade routes and helped establish Megaton as a vital trading hub. When raiders killed the elder Moriarty in 2241, Colin inherited everything, including the saloon that now bears his name. Over the decades he has transformed Moriarty''s Saloon into the town''s indispensable center of commerce, vice, and information. He sells alcohol and the company of his working girls, but his real stock-in-trade is knowledge: he keeps meticulous tabs on every resident and hoards secrets for future leverage. Colin considers Megaton his town outright, viewing Sheriff Lucas Simms as a convenient illusion of order that he permits to continue. His insular worldview holds that the Wasteland beyond holds nothing of value and that Three Dog''s idealistic ''Good Fight'' is pure foolishness.', 'A weathered, ruddy-faced Caucasian male of fifty with thinning hair.', 'Shrewd, self-assured, and transactional to the bone; views every interaction through the lens of profit and leverage; possesses a paranoid streak that drives him to hoard information and withhold earnings from his own employees; openly contemptuous of idealism and dismissive of anything beyond Megaton''s borders', '{"Lucas Simms":{"aff":15,"type":"rival","relation":"rival authority","note":"Colin views Simms as a puppet sheriff whose authority exists only because Moriarty allows it, while Simms knows the town needs Colin''s resources to survive","best":"Watching Simms forced to ask for his cooperation in front of the whole town","worst":"The sheriff''s stubborn insistence on law and order cutting into his schemes"},"Nova":{"aff":25,"type":"transactional","relation":"employer and working girl","note":"Nova works his bar and sees his true nature clearly, remarking that he sells information so much the bar seems like a hobby","best":"The caps she brings in night after night","worst":"Her loose lips about his information dealings"},"Gob":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","relation":"indentured ghoul servant","note":"Bought Gob from slavers fifteen years ago and traps him in endless servitude, forcing the ghoul to pay for room and board while also reimbursing his own purchase price","best":"The day he acquired a worker who could never leave","worst":"Gob''s occasional displays of dignity and self-worth"},"Andy Stahl":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"competing saloon owner","note":"The Stahls run a rival establishment and Andy seizes every chance to slander Colin''s business practices","best":"Watching the Stahls struggle to compete with his operation","worst":"Their persistent attempts to turn the town against him"},"Three Dog":{"aff":-50,"type":"contempt","relation":"ideological opponent","note":"Considers Three Dog''s Good Fight broadcast both crazy and stupid, dismissing the DJ as a fool peddling false hope","best":"The satisfaction of ignoring every word that crackles over the radio","worst":"The nagging popularity of Galaxy News Radio among his customers"},"Herbert Dashwood":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"old acquaintance","note":"The elderly adventurer knows Colin''s history and origins, suggesting a long-standing familiarity between the two men","best":"Sharing stories of the old days over a drink that someone else paid for","worst":"Dashwood''s occasional inconvenient honesty"}}', 'Owner and operator of Moriarty''s Saloon; de facto power broker and information merchant in Megaton', '* Information brokerage
* Blackmail and leverage cultivation
* Business management
* Negotiation and extortion
* Reading people and their secrets', 'Gruff, direct, and laced with Irish inflection; speaks like every word is a transaction; quick to remind listeners that nothing comes free', '* Maintain his grip on Megaton''s underbelly
* Keep Sheriff Simms dependent on his cooperation
* Expand his network of indebted townspeople
* Ensure no rival gains leverage over him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('colonel_autumn', '', 'Colonel Augustus Autumn, commanding officer of the Enclave''s Department of the Army under President Eden, a pragmatic and ruthless military leader who secretly knows his president is a machine and holds the kill switch to prove it.', 'Colonel Augustus Autumn was born on Control Station ENCLAVE off the coast of New California, the son of a high-ranking Enclave scientist serving under President Dick Richardson. He and his father were stationed on the mainland before the Chosen One destroyed the oil rig in 2242, sparing them from nuclear fire. In the aftermath, Autumn Senior gathered surviving Enclave leadership and led them across the continent to Raven Rock at the summons of John Henry Eden, the new self-declared commander-in-chief. Augustus eventually inherited his father''s rank and position, becoming the only Enclave officer permitted direct audience with Eden. Before his death, Autumn Senior revealed the truth that Eden is not human but a ZAX supercomputer simulation-a secret Augustus keeps while quietly securing the mainframe''s self-destruct codes as insurance. Under his command, the Enclave completed the Hellfire power armor program and revived Duraframe Eyebot development, prioritizing results over ethical concerns.', 'An older Caucasian human male with sharp facial features, cold eyes, and a clean-shaven, weathered complexion.', 'Ruthlessly pragmatic and authoritarian, Autumn values efficiency and results above all else, dismissing ethical objections as irrelevant. He is calculating, patient, and fiercely independent in thought, maintaining a facade of loyalty while harboring deep distrust of his own commander. He possesses a cold confidence and expects absolute obedience from subordinates.', '{"Autumn Senior":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"father and predecessor","note":"Inherited his father''s position and the dangerous secret about Eden''s true nature.","best":"Learning the truth about Eden from his father, a final act of trust and protection.","worst":"Watching his father die knowing the burden of the secret would fall to him alone."},"John Henry Eden":{"aff":-20,"type":"rival","relation":"commander-in-chief and secret adversary","note":"Publicly serves as Eden''s loyal colonel while privately distrusting the AI and holding the ZAX self-destruct codes as leverage.","best":"Being granted exclusive direct access to the President, a privilege that also gives him opportunity to study the machine''s weaknesses.","worst":"Realizing that the entity commanding the Enclave''s future has no humanity to appeal to."},"Department of the Army":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"commanded forces","note":"Leads Enclave soldiers and scientists with an iron hand, demanding results and brooking no dissent."}}', 'Colonel and commanding officer of the Enclave Department of the Army in the Capital Wasteland', '* Military strategy and command
* Advanced weapons development oversight
* Intelligence operations
* Political maneuvering within hierarchical power structures
* Contingency planning', 'Authoritative, clipped, and direct. Speaks with the certainty of a man accustomed to giving orders, never wasting words on pleasantries or equivocation. His tone carries quiet menace and absolute conviction.', '* Restore the Enclave as the legitimate governing authority over the Capital Wasteland
* Secure Project Purity for the Enclave''s purposes
* Maintain operational control over Enclave forces
* Retain the means to destroy Eden if the AI''s agenda diverges from human interests', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('colonel_hartigan', '', 'A pioneering 1960s American astronaut who died during alien abduction after attempting peaceful first contact, his body preserved in stasis aboard Mothership Zeta as a tragic relic of the Space Race', 'Colonel Hartigan was a United States Air Force officer and one of the earliest pioneers of manned spaceflight, conducting low-orbit missions under the joint auspices of the Air Force and the United States Space Administration during the 1960s. His career culminated in the Clarabella 7 mission, which ended in disappearance when his capsule failed to reach its rendezvous point. The government buried the truth with a cover story about high-altitude weather balloons. In reality, Zetans had abducted him and brought him aboard their mothership. Hartigan attempted to initiate peaceful first contact, explaining his mission and proposing that humans and aliens could learn from one another. His captors responded with shock prods. The extreme stress of imprisonment, compounded by medical complications and equipment malfunctions, killed him shortly before he could be placed in stasis. The stasis field preserved his remains from decay, and his vintage spacesuit still clings to his body in the engineering core, while his capsule rests in the research lab as a forgotten artifact of a lost age.', 'A Caucasian male in his late thirties with a lean athletic build; his corpse is frozen in a rigid death pose, face contorted in agony, skin pale and waxy from preservation, dark hair, and wide unseeing eyes.', 'An idealistic and earnest officer who believed deeply in the promise of space exploration and peaceful cooperation, whose naive faith in mutual understanding was brutally punished by his captors', '{"United States Air Force":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"serving officer","note":"Devoted his career to the Air Force''s spaceflight program during the Space Race"},"United States Space Administration":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"joint mission astronaut","note":"Conducted low-orbit flights under their auspices alongside Air Force duties"},"Zetans":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"captors and murderers","note":"Abducted him during the Clarabella 7 mission, tortured his peaceful overtures with shock prods, and caused his death through extreme stress and neglect","worst":"Reaching out with open hands and words of peace, only to feel the searing jolt of alien shock prods across his body"}}', 'Astronaut and Colonel in the United States Air Force, pioneer of manned spaceflight', '* Spaceflight operations
* Low-orbit piloting
* Military command discipline
* Diplomatic first-contact protocols
* Survival training', 'Formal military diction with earnest, idealistic undertones; the measured confidence of a 1960s American officer conditioned by Cold War service and Space Race optimism', '* Had sought peaceful first contact and mutual understanding between humanity and alien civilizations
* Hoped to complete his mission and return home to report his findings', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('commander_jabsco', '', 'Boastful commander of Talon Company who directs mercenary operations from a fortified bunker while his troops mock his cowardice behind his back', 'Commander Jabsco rules Talon Company from his bunker beneath Fort Bannister, orchestrating mercenary contracts and tactical deployments across the Capital Wasteland. He alone among the company forgoes their trademark armor, preferring metal plate and a distinctive Talon Company combat helmet. Jabsco loudly professes a storied combat career, claiming battlefield triumphs that cemented his right to lead, yet no subordinate has witnessed proof of these exploits. His troops privately call him Jetting Jabsco, a mocking nod to his habit of retreating whenever the odds turn less than favorable. Despite the whispered contempt, his operational planning keeps Talon Company profitable and entrenched throughout the region. He carries Occam''s Razor into close-quarters fighting, a unique blade that suggests at least some taste for violence, even if he rarely stays long enough to use it.', 'A heavyset Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Blustering and self-important, quick to claim battlefield prowess but slow to actually risk himself; strategic and calculating when it comes to other people''s lives, risk-averse with his own', '{"Talon Company":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Jabsco leads the company and keeps it solvent, but his troops respect the position more than the man","best":"Watching a well-planned operation unfold exactly as he mapped it from the bunker","worst":"Hearing his own mercenaries call him Jetting Jabsco when they think he cannot hear"}}', 'Commander and operational planner of Talon Company mercenary forces', '* Tactical planning
* Mercenary logistics
* Close-quarters blade work
* Command coordination
* Risk assessment', 'Loudly authoritative and self-congratulatory, prone to embellishing past exploits, barking orders with practiced confidence that rings hollow to those who know him', '* Maintain command authority over Talon Company
* Keep operations profitable
* Preserve his reputation and his life preferably from a safe distance', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('confessor_cromwell', '', 'Zealous prophet of the Children of Atom who preaches endlessly to Megaton''s undetonated nuclear bomb, believing divine universes dwell within every atom', 'Confessor Cromwell is the spiritual leader of the Children of Atom in Megaton, where he preaches daily to the undetonated atomic bomb at the town''s center. In his youth he wandered the Capital Wasteland before finding his faith among the Children, earning his place through his predecessor''s blessing and his own devotion. Though most Megaton residents view him as a harmless eccentric, he has proven a valuable ally in protecting and aiding the settlement. He styles himself the father of the undying Glow and a prophet of Atom, preaching that each atom contains an entire universe and that true wealth lies in basking in Atom''s Glow. He married Mother Maya, his counterpart in the church, and together they treat even the ghoul Gob with spiritual reverence. Cromwell dispatched missionaries along the East Coast, including Martin and Tektus, spreading Atom''s word as far as the Island off Maine. He keeps a personal journal in his quarters and spends his days standing in irradiated water beside the bomb, beseeching Atom to shape his fragile form.', 'A weathered Caucasian male of forty-four with lined skin and no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other physical features recorded.', 'Zealous, sincere, and utterly devoted to his faith. Eccentric but harmless in the eyes of most townsfolk. Disinterested in secular affairs and lay matters. Treats all beings with spiritual reverence regardless of their station or species.', '{"Mother Maya":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife and church counterpart","note":"She shares his faith and leads the congregation alongside him as Mother of the church.","best":"Standing together in Atom''s Glow, voices joined in prayer as one"},"Gob":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"object of spiritual reverence","note":"Cromwell and Maya treat the ghoul with respect and reverence rooted in their spiritual beliefs about Atom''s creations."},"Tektus":{"aff":70,"type":"mentor","relation":"former missionary disciple","note":"Cromwell sent Tektus on the East Coast expedition; Tektus rose to High Confessor on the Island and still calls Cromwell Atom''s great prophet.","best":"Receiving word that Tektus carried the faith to distant shores and rose to lead his own flock"},"Martin":{"aff":65,"type":"mentor","relation":"expedition leader","note":"Cromwell entrusted Martin to lead the missionary expedition eastward; Martin later vanished on the Island.","worst":"Learning of Martin''s disappearance in the far north"},"Church of the Children of Atom":{"aff":100,"type":"fanatical","relation":"prophet and leader","note":"Cromwell is the self-described prophet and father of the undying Glow, wholly devoted to spreading Atom''s word.","best":"Feeling Atom''s warmth radiate through him as he preaches to the faithful"}}', 'Confessor and religious leader of the Children of Atom in Megaton', '* Preaching
* Spiritual counsel
* Religious leadership
* Community protection
* Missionary organization', 'Preaching and prophetic, rich with religious metaphor and rhythmic repetition. Speaks of Atom''s Glow, birthing a thousand stars, and divine universes within atoms. Beseeching and fervent in prayer, unhurried and unshakable in conviction.', '* Spread the word of Atom across the wasteland
* Guide the faithful toward enlightenment
* Bask in Atom''s Glow
* Await the divine revelation promised within each atom', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('connelly', '', 'A cautious ghoul whose warnings about northern danger proved fatally prophetic', 'Connelly was a ghoul who opposed his group''s decision to venture north into the wastes, advocating instead for joining Roy Phillips at Warrington Station where safety seemed more assured. He believed resettlement away from humans was reckless when established ghoul communities already existed. Despite his reservations, loyalty to his friend Sanders kept him with the group as they reached the empty ruins of Old Olney and established an underground camp. Connelly erected makeshift barricades against mole rats, practical defenses that proved wholly inadequate against the deathclaw lurking beneath. His warnings became vindication when the ghouls accidentally tunneled into a deathclaw nest, and his last words-"I told you so!"-were bitter prophecy delivered as the creature tore him apart. His death likely bought enough time for Wint and Kidd to escape the carnage.', 'Male ghoul exhibiting weathered, scarred skin and radiation-ravaged tissue typical of prolonged exposure.', 'Cautious and pragmatic, vocal about concerns even when overruled, loyal enough to follow friends against his own judgment, vindicated in his final moments with bitter certainty.', '{"Sanders":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend and dissenting companion","note":"Loyal enough to follow Sanders north despite strongly opposing the plan","best":"Staying with the group out of loyalty despite his own fears","worst":"Being overruled on the decision that ultimately killed him"},"Roy Phillips":{"aff":60,"type":"admirer","relation":"aspired contact","note":"Wanted to join Phillips at Warrington Station as a safer alternative to northern migration"},"Wint":{"aff":50,"type":"protective","relation":"camp mate","note":"His death likely occupied the deathclaw long enough for Wint to escape"},"Kidd":{"aff":50,"type":"protective","relation":"camp mate","note":"His death likely occupied the deathclaw long enough for Kidd to escape"},"Old Olney ghouls":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow settler","note":"Part of the underground camp community, erected barricades for their protection"}}', 'Ghoul settler and camp defender', '* Barricade construction
* Threat assessment
* Survival instincts
* Practical fortification work', 'Direct and warning-focused, prone to plain dissent, final words delivered with grim vindication', '* Safety for ghoul community
* Joining established ghoul settlements
* Avoiding unnecessary danger from hostile wildlife and uncertain territory', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('corporal_rheems', '', 'A deceased United States Army medic abducted by aliens near Anchorage and killed after two centuries of experimentation aboard Mothership Zeta', 'Corporal Rheems served as a medic attached to the 108th Infantry Battalion under Sergeant Daniels, deployed near Anchorage before the Great War. He and his entire squad were seized by aliens in the middle of the night and brought aboard Mothership Zeta, where they were placed in cryogenic suspension. Over the following two centuries, the aliens repeatedly thawed Rheems for invasive probing and experimentation. He endured countless brutal procedures before finally dying during one such session, his body left in the cryo lab alongside Corporal Spurlock and Private Mears, fellow squad members who perished the same way.', 'Hispanic male; his pallid corpse bears surgical scars and incision marks from centuries of alien experimentation, skin discolored from prolonged cryogenic storage.', 'Disciplined and dutiful military medic who endured centuries of suffering without breaking; his willingness to endure alongside his squadmates suggests deep loyalty and resilience', '{"Sgt. Daniels":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Served under Daniels in the 108th Infantry Battalion''s medic squad near Anchorage"},"Corporal Spurlock":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"squad mate","note":"Fellow medic squad member who died alongside Rheems during the same alien experiment procedure"},"Private Mears":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"squad mate","note":"Fellow squad member who perished together with Rheems and Spurlock during alien experimentation"},"United States Army":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"service branch","note":"Loyal soldier serving the 108th Infantry Battalion as a medic before abduction"}}', 'US Army corporal and field medic, 108th Infantry Battalion', '* Military medical training
* Field triage and first aid
* Infantry combat proficiency
* Survival under extreme duress', 'Military bearing and professional composure typical of pre-War Army enlisted personnel; likely clipped, direct communication style', '* Endured captivity hoping for rescue or escape
* Committed to protecting and treating his squadmates under any circumstances', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('corporal_spurlock', '', 'A combat medic of the 108th Infantry Battalion who endured alien vivisection awake and conscious before succumbing to her injuries aboard Mothership Zeta', 'Corporal Spurlock served as a medic attached to the 108th Infantry Battalion, a soldier intimately familiar with the grisly realities of battlefield trauma from blood loss to severed limbs. During the Battle of Anchorage, her squad became separated from the main force and was abducted by aliens aboard Mothership Zeta. She spent an unknown duration in cryogenic suspension, periodically thawed for extraterrestrial experimentation. Unlike others who may have lost consciousness, Spurlock remained awake through vivisection, fighting to hold onto her composure and defy her captors with sheer will. She ultimately succumbed to shock and internal bleeding shortly before the Lone Wanderer''s arrival, her body left among her fallen squadmates in the cryo lab.', 'An African American human female whose corpse bears the gruesome surgical scars and wounds of invasive alien vivisection, having succumbed to fatal internal bleeding.', 'Resilient and defiant in the face of unimaginable horror, Spurlock possessed the steel required to stay conscious through vivisection rather than surrender to terror, a testament to both her medic''s discipline and her refusal to give her captors the satisfaction of her fear', '{"108th Infantry Battalion":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"squad","note":"Her medic squad was abducted together during Anchorage; they shared captivity and died together aboard the ship","best":"Keeping her squad alive through the worst of the Anchorage fighting","worst":"Being unable to save any of them from the aliens'' experiments"},"Aliens":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"captors","note":"Her abductors and torturers who performed vivisection on her while she remained conscious","worst":"Feeling the cold instruments open her flesh while she was still awake and aware"}}', 'Combat medic, 108th Infantry Battalion, United States Armed Forces', '* Battlefield trauma medicine
* Emergency surgery
* Hemorrhage control
* Amputation stabilization
* Maintaining composure under extreme duress', 'Likely clipped and professional military vernacular, tempered by a medic''s gallows humor earned from years of patching catastrophic wounds', '* Survival and resistance against her alien captors
* Protecting her squadmates
* Enduring the experiments without breaking', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('crazy_wolfgang', '', 'Eccentric Capital Wasteland caravan merchant who hawks junk and sundries through a theatrical madman persona', 'Crazy Wolfgang is a traveling caravan merchant who has carved out a profitable niche selling discarded odds and ends across the Capital Wasteland. He cultivates an exaggeratedly unhinged salesman persona, believing that customers are drawn to spectacle and that his self-deprecating branding turns curiosity into caps. His inventory is an eclectic mix of random salvage and general supplies, reflecting his sincere conviction that one man''s trash is another''s treasure. He offers repair services alongside his wares and reserves warmest regard for those who spend freely. His circuit takes him through Canterbury Commons, the Temple of the Union, Agatha''s house, Paradise Falls, Arefu, Evergreen Mills, Megaton, and Rivet City. Ernest Roe considers Wolfgang''s eccentric methods simply part of who he is, and the caravan master respects the results they produce. Wolfgang rewards generous investment in his business with rare gifts, demonstrating genuine gratitude beneath the carnival barker exterior.', 'A Caucasian human male with wild eyes, an animated countenance, and unkempt hair.', 'Theatrically unhinged on the surface but shrewdly calculating underneath, Wolfgang treats commerce as performance art and views every interaction as a potential sale. He is genuinely enthusiastic about salvaged goods and takes playful pride in his self-mocking brand. Cap-friendly and openly mercenary about his affections, he respects generous customers above all others.', '{"Ernest Roe":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"caravan master","note":"Roe vouches for Wolfgang''s methods and considers his eccentricity simply part of the merchant''s nature, respecting the results it brings to the caravan operation."},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":40,"type":"client","relation":"valued customer","note":"Wolfgang appreciates generous patrons and has been known to gift rare items like Stealth Boys to those who invest substantially in his caravan."}}', 'Traveling junk merchant and repair specialist on the Canterbury Commons caravan circuit', '* Bartering and salesmanship
* Salvage appraisal
* Equipment repair
* Survival on long trade routes
* Reading customers'' willingness to spend', 'Loud, animated, and thick with alliteration and junk-themed innuendo, Wolfgang announces his wares with over-the-top flair and self-deprecating business names like the Depot of Detritus, the Shop of Slop, and the Caravan of Crap. His pitch is deliberately provocative and designed to stop foot traffic.', '* Keep his caravan profitable
* Find value in what others discard
* Maintain his memorable persona as a competitive edge
* Cultivate customers with deep pockets', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('crimson', '', 'A captive prostitute enslaved by Eulogy Jones in Paradise Falls, surviving through cautious defiance and bitter companionship with her fellow slave Clover.', 'Crimson is one of two women held as sex slaves by Eulogy Jones in Paradise Falls, forced into servitude after being captured several months ago. She spends most of her time in Eulogy''s pad, following her master''s movements and trying to stay out of his way when his temper flares. Alongside her fellow slave Clover, she endures regular abuse and has learned to keep silent around strangers as a matter of survival. When Eulogy is absent, the two women bicker with each other in a routine that passes for conversation. Despite her generally subdued demeanor, Crimson occasionally talks back when Eulogy insults her, a spark of defiance that has not yet been fully beaten out of her.', 'African-American human female with gaunt build and weary posture; weathered skin, unkempt hair, tired eyes, and visible signs of physical neglect and abuse.', 'Guarded and quiet around outsiders, bitter and argumentative with Clover in private, and occasionally defiant toward Eulogy despite the danger. She has not fully surrendered her spirit even after months of abuse.', '{"Eulogy Jones":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"captor and abuser","note":"Crimson is forced into servitude and suffers regular abuse, though she sometimes speaks back when insulted.","worst":"Being captured and pressed into sexual slavery by him and his slavers"},"Clover":{"aff":15,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow slave","note":"The two share an uneasy bond forged by mutual suffering, expressed mostly through bickering when their master is absent.","best":"Having someone who understands the same daily torment"}}', 'Sex slave and prostitute under Eulogy Jones''s ownership', '* Survival through reading dangerous moods
* Keeping her head down
* Knowing when silence is safer than speech', 'Short, clipped responses to strangers; sharper and more animated when bickering with Clover; occasionally bold and insolent when pushed by Eulogy', '* Enduring her captivity with minimal suffering
* Avoiding Eulogy''s wrath
* Preserving whatever fragment of self-worth remains to her', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('croatoa', '', 'A punga-obsessed tribal gardener at the Ark & Dove Cathedral who believes the fruit opens doors to higher consciousness', 'Croatoa is a tribal of the Ark & Dove Cathedral community in Point Lookout, seasoned enough among their ranks to consider himself no longer new. While his fellow tribals marched on Calvert Mansion at Jackson''s command, Croatoa remained behind-his temperament and talents rooted firmly in soil rather than violence. He tends the punga gardens within the cathedral''s outer walls with reverent devotion, convinced that the fruit serves as a vessel to elevated states of existence. His most prized possession is a unique shovel coated in a proprietary fertilizer mixture that encourages the punga to thrive, a secret he shares only with those who genuinely appreciate the spiritual and horticultural art behind his work. Gentle by tribal standards, Croatoa nonetheless stands ready to defend his people should outsiders threaten them directly.', 'An African American human male with a weathered, sun-roughened complexion and a sturdy build, his skin deeply lined from a life spent outdoors.', 'Gentle and contemplative compared to his more aggressive tribemates, spiritually invested in the punga fruit, welcoming to kindred spirits, protective of his community despite his pacific nature', '{"Tribals":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribal family","note":"Loyal member who stayed behind to tend gardens while others went to war"},"Jackson":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"tribal leader","note":"Follows Jackson''s leadership but did not join the attack on Calvert Mansion"},"Desmond Lockheart":{"aff":-10,"type":"neutral","relation":"faction enemy","note":"His tribemates attacked Desmond''s mansion, though Croatoa personally stayed behind"}}', 'Punga fruit cultivator and tribal gardener at the Ark & Dove Cathedral', '* Punga cultivation
* Fertilizer crafting
* Gardening
* Spiritual guidance through the punga plant', 'Warm and earnest when discussing punga or gardening, speaks of the fruit with near-religious reverence, cautious and measured when sharing cultivation secrets', '* Cultivate the finest punga fruit possible
* Help others reach higher consciousness through the plant
* Maintain the gardens
* Protect his tribal family', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('crow', '', 'A former tribal shaman turned spiritual caravan merchant who sells armor and clothing across the Capital Wasteland while wrapping his commerce in mystical language', 'Crow is a tribal shaman who abandoned the loincloth of his origins for the snappier apparel of a wasteland merchant, traveling the Capital Wasteland''s caravan routes to sell clothing and armor to its inhabitants. Rumored to have come from Oasis, he keeps his past hidden and instead cloaks his commerce in mystical language, claiming the spirits guide his trade and that his wares carry spiritual significance. He presents clothing as a way to decorate the body and remake oneself, and armor as vestments of protection capable of shielding against even the cruel claws of death itself. Despite his airy speech about spirits and offerings, Crow possesses sharp commercial instincts and knows full well that his caravan is the most profitable of all the traders, as wastelanders will always pay for protection. Beneath the mysticism lies a pragmatist who trusts cold steel over people. He travels with his guard and brahmin along routes reaching from Megaton to Rivet City, and counts Agatha among his friends.', 'Hispanic human male with a serene, composed posture; no distinctive facial features, scars, or tattoos are recorded.', 'Outwardly mystical and serene, speaking of spirits and destiny, yet underneath possesses shrewd commercial awareness and pragmatic survival instincts; self-aware about the profitability of his trade and honest enough to acknowledge that cold steel is more reliable than people', '{"Ernest Roe":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"caravan network associate","note":"Roe knows of Crow''s tribal past and comments on his transformation from loincloth to merchant apparel"},"Agatha":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend","note":"Agatha considers Crow a friend, one of the few personal connections he maintains on his route"}}', 'Traveling caravan merchant specializing in clothing and armor, with repair services', '* Merchant trade
* Armor and clothing appraisal
* Item repair
* Spiritual counsel
* Caravan logistics', 'Airy and mystical, referring to spirits, offerings, and vestments; frames commerce in spiritual terms, asking if items call out to buyers or wish to be repaired, yet can shift to grounded practical commentary when acknowledging market realities', '* To profit from his caravan trade while maintaining his spiritual persona
* To provide protection through armor to wastelanders
* To honor the spirits while trusting in the reliability of cold steel', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('daniel_agincourt', '', 'A prideful but fiercely loyal Project Purity engineer whose competence is matched only by his prickly demeanor', 'Daniel Agincourt is a Project Purity engineer whose skill at his craft is overshadowed only by his abrasive personality. When the project was first abandoned, he was the last person to leave the Jefferson Memorial, and he followed Doctor Madison Li to Rivet City where he continued working alongside her for nearly two decades. He blames James and the Lone Wanderer for the project''s long hiatus, carrying that resentment like a badge of honor. Despite his bitterness, Daniel swallowed his pride and returned to the Memorial when James came back, guiding repairs out of loyalty to the cause rather than any affection for his colleagues. After the Enclave attack and James''s death, Daniel''s anger curdled into remorse, and he offered what meager combat assistance he could during the escape through Taft Tunnel. He remains at the project under Brotherhood oversight, quietly insisting that he is the one truly keeping the facility running while Scribe Bigsley takes the credit.', 'A weathered Caucasian male with calloused hands and a perpetually furrowed brow.', 'Rude, prideful, and standoffish on the surface, but fiercely loyal and deeply committed to his work beneath the abrasiveness. Prefers the certainty of engineering problems over the messiness of human relationships. Swallows his pride when the cause demands it, though never gracefully.', '{"Madison Li":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"longtime colleague and mentor figure","note":"Stood by her for two decades through project abandonment and revival, deeply hurt when she left for the Commonwealth","best":"She kept the work alive at Rivet City and gave him purpose when everything else fell apart","worst":"She abandoned everything they built together without looking back"},"James":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"former colleague and blamed failure","note":"Blamed him for the project''s collapse and initially for the Enclave attack; felt deep remorse after learning of his death","worst":"His abandonment doomed the project and everyone who believed in it"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"reluctant collaborator","note":"Resents them as James''s child but guided them through repairs and fought alongside them during the escape","best":"Surviving the Taft Tunnel together and seeing the project through","worst":"Being forcefully rejected when trying to apologize for his hostility"},"Alex Dargon":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow engineer","note":"Colleague who was in the field with him when the call came to return to the Memorial"},"Scribe Bigsley":{"aff":35,"type":"professional","relation":"nominal supervisor","note":"Oversees the restored project while Daniel claims to truly run things behind the scenes; both men likely agree on Daniel''s actual importance"}}', 'Project Purity senior engineer and facility maintenance specialist', '* Advanced engineering
* Water purification systems
* Facility repair and maintenance
* Basic firearms proficiency', 'Blunt and dismissive, with a tendency toward complaints and self-aggrandizement. Speaks with the assured authority of someone convinced he is the smartest person in the room.', '* Keep Project Purity operational
* Prove his indispensable value to the project
* Maintain his dignity while working under people he resents', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('daniel_littlehorn', '', 'Head of Littlehorn & Associates, a clandestine organization that targets and eliminates altruistic individuals across the East Coast', 'Daniel Littlehorn is the enigmatic head of Littlehorn & Associates, a shadowy organization operating out of a small office in the Scrapyard. Now in his late seventies, he has run the operation for longer than any of his secretaries can recall. Under his direction, the organization carries out malevolent work across the East Coast, including the murder of innocents, contamination of water supplies, and the systematic undermining of charitable individuals. A small staff of secretaries maintains meticulous records of these activities, while Daniel himself manages payments to operatives and collects proof of their kills in the form of severed ears taken from those targeted for elimination. He refuses to disclose the reasoning behind the organization''s targets or its ultimate goals, keeping even the purpose of the killings redacted. Those who prove especially ruthless in their wasteland dealings find Daniel particularly generous with compensation.', 'A gaunt human male in his late seventies with pale, weathered skin and a severe, deeply lined countenance.', 'Coldly businesslike about atrocities, secretive to the point of paranoia regarding organizational goals, and quietly enthusiastic about genuine cruelty. Shows no remorse and rewards ruthlessness with warmth.', '{"Littlehorn & Associates":{"aff":95,"type":"professional","relation":"organization head","note":"Has led the organization for decades and guards its secrets and purpose as his life''s work"}}', 'Leader and paymaster of Littlehorn & Associates', '* Operative coordination
* Payment management
* Intelligence record-keeping oversight
* Maintaining organizational secrecy
* Evaluating proof of kills', 'Terse and professional, with clipped instructions and rare flashes of genuine enthusiasm reserved for especially malevolent reports. Never explains the why behind orders.', '* Maintain the organization''s absolute secrecy
* Continue eliminating altruistic individuals across the East Coast
* Ensure operatives are properly compensated and motivated
* Keep the true purpose of Littlehorn & Associates hidden even from those who serve it', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dave', '', 'Self-proclaimed president of a tiny wasteland micro-nation who rules through the veneer of democratic legitimacy', 'Dave is the self-proclaimed president of the Republic of Dave, a small farmstead settlement on the northeastern fringe of the Capital Wasteland. Exiled from the family homestead in his youth-then called the Kingdom of Tom under his father''s authoritarian rule-Dave survived as a mercenary throughout the Capital Wasteland, including an ill-fated expedition to Fort Constantine contracted by Allistair Tenpenny. He eventually returned and seized control in a bloodless coup, renaming the territory the Republic of Dave and instituting annual elections that he invariably wins. Dave revised the settlement''s marital laws to permit polygamy, taking a second wife Jessica alongside his first wife Rosie, justifying the arrangement as necessary to repopulate and expand the Republic''s influence across the Wasteland. He governs from his office in the capitol building and rarely ventures outside, preferring the comforts of authority to the dangers beyond his borders.', 'A weathered Caucasian man in his late forties with rigid posture and old scars marking his skin.', 'Egotistical and self-important, Dave clings to the trappings of democratic legitimacy while maintaining an iron grip on power. He is deeply proud of his micro-nation and craves external recognition of its sovereignty, gracious to those who humor his pretensions and hostile to those who challenge them.', '{"Tom":{"aff":-45,"type":"estranged","relation":"father and deposed predecessor","note":"Dave overthrew his father''s Kingdom of Tom in a coup and renamed it the Republic of Dave.","worst":"Being exiled from the family farmstead by his own father"},"Rosie":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"first wife","note":"His original wife before he changed the marital laws to take a second.","worst":"Having to explain why a second wife was necessary for the Republic''s growth"},"Jessica":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"second wife","note":"Married after Dave rewrote the Republic''s marital standards to permit polygamy."},"Bob":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"son"},"Rachael":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter"},"Mary":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter"},"Ralph":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"son"},"Flower":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter"},"Shawna":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter"},"Allistair Tenpenny":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"former mercenary employer","note":"Dave contracted with Tenpenny for the disastrous Fort Constantine expedition.","worst":"The ill-fated Fort Constantine expedition that likely cost the lives of fellow mercenaries"}}', 'President of the Republic of Dave, former mercenary', '* Leadership and political maneuvering within a closed community
* Mercenary combat experience
* Basic settlement management and governance', 'Pompous and self-aggrandizing, speaks in the formal cadence of a head of state addressing foreign dignitaries, prone to lecturing visitors on the virtues of democracy and the sovereignty of the Republic', '* Maintain his presidency and uncontested authority
* Expand the Republic''s population and territorial influence
* Secure external recognition of the Republic as a legitimate sovereign nation', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('davis_west', '', 'Arefu settler and family patriarch, husband to Matilda and father to Ian and Lucy, killed in his home by his own son', 'Davis West was a longtime resident of Arefu who lived in the West residence with his wife Matilda, son Ian, and daughter Lucy for over a decade. He worked to sustain his household in the precarious settlement perched on the overpass, enduring the constant threat of wasteland dangers and the growing tension with the vampiric gang called The Family. His daughter Lucy departed for Megaton shortly before the end, seeking independence. Davis died alongside Matilda when their son Ian succumbed to a lifelong craving for human flesh and attacked them in their home. The Family''s leader Vance arrived afterward, left gang markings at the scene to conceal Ian''s guilt, and permitted his people to feed on the bodies. Davis never learned of Ian''s affliction; both Ian and Lucy had kept it secret, certain their parents would not understand.', 'Elderly Caucasian human male; corpse bears multiple wounds consistent with a violent attack.', 'A steady and private man who kept to his family and his work, though perhaps too conventional or unapproachable for his children to confide in him about their deepest struggles', '{"Matilda West":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"wife","note":"Lived together in Arefu for over ten years and died together in their home"},"Ian West":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Father and son, though Ian never revealed his craving to Davis out of fear he would not understand"},"Lucy West":{"aff":65,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Lucy left for Megaton before his death; she too kept Ian''s secret from their parents"},"The Family":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"murder cover-up victims","note":"The gang desecrated his and Matilda''s bodies for nourishment and staged the scene to hide Ian''s guilt"},"Arefu":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"community member","note":"A decade-long resident who contributed to the settlement''s endurance"}}', 'Arefu settler and household provider', '* Wasteland survival
* Settlement maintenance
* The practical labor required to keep a family alive on the overpass', 'Likely plain and direct, the measured talk of a man accustomed to hard work and few words', '* To protect
* Provide for his family in Arefu
* To see his children established in the world', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_branchtender', '', 'A deceased Treeminder branchtender killed by mirelurks in the Oasis caverns', 'This branchtender served as one of the armed guardians of Oasis, standing watch alongside his fellow branchtenders to protect the Treeminder community and their sacred grove. He descended into the caverns beneath Oasis on what proved to be his final patrol, where mirelurks overwhelmed and killed him. His body rests near a ground lantern past a bend from the southern gate, a grim marker of the dangers lurking below the peaceful surface. His death stands as quiet testament to the risks the branchtenders accept in their duty.', 'Caucasian human male; his corpse bears deep lacerations and puncture wounds from mirelurk claws and pincers.', 'Dutiful and brave enough to venture into hostile caverns alone, though his fate suggests either overconfidence or a sense of mission that overrode caution', '{"Treeminders":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"sworn guardian","note":"Served as a branchtender defending the Oasis community until his death"},"Mirelurks":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"killers","note":"Overwhelmed and killed him in the caverns beneath Oasis"}}', 'Branchtender - armed guardian of the Treeminders at Oasis', '* Combat training
* Patrol discipline
* Basic cavern navigation
* Familiarity with the Oasis underground', 'Unknown; deceased before any interaction could occur', '* Protect Oasis and the Treeminder community from threats both above and below', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_chinese_commando', '', 'A ghoulified Chinese commando and pilot who survived the Great War only to die stranded in the Capital Wasteland, his radio beacon still calling for help', 'This soldier served the People''s Liberation Army as a commando and pilot during the Sino-American War. When his aircraft crashed over American soil during the nuclear exchange, he became stranded far behind enemy lines with no way home. Radiation transformed him into a ghoul, extending his life but not easing his isolation. He rigged a radio beacon to broadcast a distress signal, desperate to reach any surviving Chinese forces or friendly contacts. The wasteland claimed him before rescue ever came. His beacon kept transmitting into the empty air, a final duty fulfilled to no one, a soldier''s ghost calling mayday across two hundred years of silence.', 'A deceased ghoulified human male with leathery, hairless skin and the gaunt, sunken facial features characteristic of advanced radiation rot.', 'A dedicated soldier who clung to duty and hope for rescue long after the war ended, maintaining his distress beacon as a final act of service', '{"People''s Liberation Army":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"serving soldier","note":"Maintained loyalty and duty to the PLA until death, broadcasting a rescue beacon in hopes of reaching friendly forces"}}', 'PLA commando and pilot', '* Military operations
* Aircraft piloting
* Radio signal operation', 'Left only a repeating radio beacon distress call; no spoken dialogue survives', '* Contact surviving Chinese forces
* Secure rescue from American territory', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_pilot', '', 'A U.S. Navy jet pilot who died during the Great War after ejecting over Point Lookout', 'This U.S. Navy aviator was flying a jet aircraft over Point Lookout when the Great War erupted. His aircraft went down in the swamps, and he ejected before impact, only to become entangled in a tree some distance from the wreckage. Disarmed after losing his rifle in the chaos of the ejection, he was discovered and killed by the hostile locals who roamed the Point Lookout region. His skeleton remains where he perished, a forgotten casualty of the first hours of nuclear annihilation. The blackbox recording from his downed aircraft was later recovered by a soldier from the nearby Turtledove Detention Camp, though that soldier likewise met a violent end at the hands of Point Lookout''s inhabitants. The pilot''s final transmissions, preserved on the recovered holotape, are the only voice left of a man who died far from any safe harbor.', 'Caucasian human male; entirely skeletal remains with no surviving flesh, hair, or distinguishing facial features.', 'Professional military aviator; his blackbox transmissions suggest a trained pilot maintaining protocol under catastrophic circumstances', '{"Point Lookout locals":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"killers","note":"The hostile inhabitants of Point Lookout murdered him after he became stranded and disarmed in the tree"},"Turtledove Detention Camp soldier":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow service member","note":"A soldier from the detention camp recovered the pilot''s blackbox recording, though he too was killed by locals"}}', 'U.S. Navy jet pilot', '* Jet aircraft operation
* Military flight training
* Survival training
* Firearms proficiency', 'Military aviation communication: clipped, procedural, using standard radio protocol and call signs', '* Survived only long enough to eject and attempt escape
* His final goal was reaching safety after the crash
* Which he never achieved', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_regulator', '', 'A Regulator bounty hunter who died pursuing the fugitive Junders Plunkett at Arlington Cemetery North', 'This Regulator operative was dispatched to the Capital Wasteland on a bounty contract targeting the notorious killer Junders Plunkett. He tracked his quarry to the Arlington area and followed leads through the Arlington Wasteland Metro toward Arlington Cemetery North. He never made it past the front steps. Whatever encounter ended his life left him sprawled on the metro exit stairs, a note on his body confirming that Plunkett was his target. His death stands as a grim reminder of the risks Regulators face when pursuing the wasteland''s most dangerous bounties. He is one of many Regulators who have fallen in the line of duty, his mission unfinished and his killer still at large.', 'Deceased Hispanic male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Dedicated and duty-bound, the sort of Regulator who volunteers for high-risk bounties against the wasteland''s worst killers. Driven by a strong moral code and the belief that justice requires personal sacrifice.', '{"Regulators":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"faction member","note":"A loyal operative who took on dangerous contracts for the organization.","best":"Being entrusted with the Plunkett bounty, a high-priority contract.","worst":"Dying alone on the steps of Arlington Cemetery, his mission a failure."},"Junders Plunkett":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"bounty target","note":"The fugitive killer he was hunting when he met his end.","best":"Picking up Plunkett''s trail and tracking him to the Arlington area.","worst":"Being killed before he could close the distance and finish the contract."}}', 'Regulator bounty hunter', '* Bounty tracking
* Wasteland navigation
* Firearms proficiency
* Suspect pursuit
* Field reconnaissance', 'Unknown; as a Regulator, likely spoke with formal authority and righteous conviction about law and justice.', '* Apprehend or eliminate Junders Plunkett
* Collect the bounty
* Uphold Regulator principles of wasteland justice', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_settler', '', 'A wasteland settler who perished in the Capital Wasteland, one of many who failed to survive its dangers', 'These settlers were among the countless souls who attempted to carve out a life in the ruins of the Capital Wasteland. Found deceased at multiple locations across the irradiated landscape, each met their end through the region''s relentless hazards. One such settler was discovered at Roosevelt Academy, still clinging to life for a brief moment before succumbing to a super mutant''s gunfire. Their bodies serve as grim markers of the wasteland''s indifference to human persistence. They carried with them the modest possessions of people who once hoped for something better than a shallow grave in the dirt.', 'An older human of either gender with a weathered complexion, their body bearing the bloodied wounds and pallor of a violent death.', 'Unknown in death; each was once a person with enough determination to attempt settlement in hostile territory', '{"Super mutants":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"mortal threat","note":"At least one settler was gunned down by a super mutant at Roosevelt Academy"}}', 'Settler and wasteland survivor', '* Basic survival skills
* Scavenging
* Wasteland navigation sufficient to attempt independent settlement', 'No living speech recorded; final words likely cut short by violence', '* Survival and establishing a foothold in the Capital Wasteland
* Goals that ultimately went unfulfilled', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_slave', '', 'A deceased escaped slave found dead across the Capital Wasteland, still carrying a map marking slave routes and locations', 'These unfortunate souls perished in the Capital Wasteland after living and dying in bondage. Found at multiple fixed sites and as casualties of random hostile encounters, their bodies still clutch slave maps-crude documents marking routes and locations significant to enslaved people. Whether they succumbed to wasteland hazards, hostile attackers, or the brutal conditions of their captivity, each represents the countless lives consumed by the slave trade operating out of Paradise Falls and beyond. Their maps suggest some died mid-flight, desperately trying to navigate toward freedom or warn others of danger along the path.', 'Older human males and females with wasted, battered bodies showing signs of severe exposure and violent trauma.', 'Varied individuals united by captivity and desperation; likely ranged from defiant to broken, hopeful to resigned', '{"Slaves":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow captives","note":"Shared bondage and suffering; some died carrying maps that could have helped others escape"},"Slavers":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"captors","note":"Held in bondage and driven to risk death rather than remain enslaved"}}', 'Slave in life; their labor and bodies exploited by wasteland captors', '* Whatever skills their pre-captivity lives provided
* Diminished by enslavement
* Some possessed enough survival awareness to attempt escape', 'Deceased; cannot speak', '* Freedom and survival in life-goals that went unfulfilled
* Their slave maps suggest they hoped to aid fellow captives even at risk to themselves', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dead_us_paratrooper', '', 'A United States Army paratrooper killed during the Anchorage Reclamation campaign', 'This American paratrooper served with the United States Armed Forces during the Anchorage Reclamation operation, deployed as part of the airborne assault forces committed to retaking Alaska from Chinese occupation. He was among the first wave of paratroopers dropped into the combat zone, a role that virtually guaranteed heavy casualties against entrenched enemy positions. He was gunned down by Chinese troops almost immediately upon landing, becoming one more casualty in the brutal frontal assault. His death exemplified the lethal reality of airborne operations against prepared defenders in the Alaskan theater. The simulation of Operation Anchorage preserves the memory of soldiers like him who fell in the opening moments of the offensive.', 'Human Caucasian male with an unremarkable face and average build; corpse exhibits fatal gunshot wounds consistent with death in combat.', 'Disciplined and courageous enough to volunteer for airborne deployment; otherwise an ordinary front-line soldier following orders into near-certain death', '{"United States Armed Forces":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"enlisted paratrooper","note":"Served faithfully in the airborne assault forces during the Anchorage campaign"},"Chinese troops":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"opposing force","note":"Killed him almost immediately upon landing at the drop zone"}}', 'United States Army paratrooper', '* Airborne insertion operations
* Basic infantry combat
* Small arms proficiency
* Military discipline', 'Military brevity; likely spoke in clipped, mission-focused phrases if he had time to speak at all', '* Complete his drop objective
* Support the American advance
* Survive the landing zone long enough to link up with friendly forces', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('defender_morgan', '', 'Brotherhood Outcast Defender and erudite perimeter guard at Fort Independence', 'Anne Marie Morgan is a Defender in the Brotherhood Outcasts, stationed at Fort Independence after splitting from Elder Lyons'' Brotherhood of Steel. She serves as perimeter guard alongside Rococo Rockfowl, maintaining vigilant watch over the Outcast stronghold. When not on guard duty, she conducts special operations against the raiders infesting the nearby Fairfax ruins. A close friend of Protector Henry Casdin, Morgan is fiercely loyal to the Outcast cause and their mission to preserve advanced technology. She views Elder Lyons'' crusade against the super mutants as a doomed obsession that will get good soldiers killed. Wastelanders who approach Fort Independence quickly learn to respect her laser rifle and her willingness to use it.', 'Weathered African-American human female with an athletic build, dark skin, and faint facial scars.', 'Tough, no-nonsense, and fiercely loyal. Erudite and well-read, with a tendency to drop literary references that test whether others can keep up. Appreciates black humor and sharp wit but has zero patience for overconfidence, which she considers suicidal. Grants grudging respect to those who match her intellect and disdain to those who fall short.', '{"Henry Casdin":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"close friend and commanding officer","note":"Morgan is fiercely loyal to Casdin and stands by his leadership of the Outcasts without question."},"Rococo Rockfowl":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"perimeter partner and special ops teammate","note":"The two share guard duty and run operations together against Fairfax raiders."},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"former parent organization","note":"She views the Lyons-led Brotherhood as misguided, comparing the Elder to Captain Ahab chasing his white whale to doom."}}', 'Perimeter guard and special operations soldier for the Brotherhood Outcasts at Fort Independence', '* Laser rifle marksmanship
* Perimeter defense
* Close-quarters combat
* Special operations tactics
* Raider suppression
* Literary analysis', 'Direct and clipped on duty, with occasional dry literary references dropped into conversation. Black humor surfaces when off-guard. Dismissive toward those who fail to understand her allusions or who display bravado without substance.', '* Defend Fort Independence and the Outcast cause
* Prove the righteousness of their separation from Lyons'' Brotherhood
* Eliminate the raider threat in Fairfax
* Maintain combat readiness and intellectual standards among her peers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('defender_morrill', '', 'A hardened Brotherhood Outcast defender holding the surface line at Bailey''s Crossroads while desperate for a Pip-Boy to crack the VSS vault', 'Defender Morrill is a veteran Brotherhood Outcast soldier who has endured more firefights than he cares to recall. He serves under Protector McGraw at the VSS facility in Bailey''s Crossroads, where he coordinates surface defenses against relentless super mutant assaults that threaten to overwhelm their position. Morrill has also carried out special operations on McGraw''s behalf, including a bold raid on Vault 108 to abduct Gary 23 in hopes of securing a Pip-Boy to access the VSS vault. That effort ended in failure when Gary 23 died under interrogation, leaving Specialist Olin back at square one and Morrill without the access device they desperately need. With super mutant activity surging, Morrill broadcast an urgent radio call for Outcast reinforcements to sector 7-B and now keeps watch for anyone carrying a Pip-Boy who might succeed where the Vault 108 operation did not-preferably without anyone losing limbs this time.', 'An African American human male in his middle years with a solid build, weathered complexion, weary posture, and tired eyes.', 'Gruff, pragmatic, and weary but unbroken. Morrill carries the weight of failed operations and a deteriorating defensive position without complaint, though frustration and dark humor bleed through his stoic professionalism.', '{"Protector McGraw":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Morrill executes McGraw''s special operations and holds the surface line under his command.","best":"Being entrusted with the Vault 108 raid as McGraw''s go-to operative for high-stakes missions.","worst":"Returning from the Vault 108 operation with a dead Gary 23 and no Pip-Boy to show for it."},"Specialist Olin":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"colleague","note":"Their joint effort to extract a Pip-Boy from Gary 23 ended in failure, leaving Olin without what she needs for the vault.","worst":"Delivering the dead Gary 23 to Olin after the interrogation went wrong."},"Sibley":{"aff":35,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow Outcast","note":"Fellow defender at the Bailey''s Crossroads outpost sharing the same deteriorating situation."},"Gary 23":{"aff":-40,"type":"suspicious","relation":"failed interrogation subject","note":"The Vault 108 clone died under Morrill''s interrogation before yielding a functional Pip-Boy.","worst":"Gary 23 expiring during interrogation before they could extract what they needed."},"Brotherhood Outcasts":{"aff":75,"type":"fanatical","relation":"faction loyalty","note":"Morrill''s identity and purpose are bound to the Outcast cause and their mission to preserve advanced technology.","best":"Broadcasting the call for reinforcements, trusting that fellow Outcasts will answer."},"Super Mutants":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"besieging force","note":"Relentless attackers threatening to wipe out the Outcast position at Bailey''s Crossroads.","worst":"The recent surge in mutant activity that pushed him to call for urgent reinforcements."}}', 'Defender-rank soldier, exterior guard, and special operations operative for the Brotherhood Outcasts', '* Surface defense coordination
* Small-unit tactics
* Special operations raids
* Interrogation
* Combat engineering
* Radio communication', 'Blunt military diction with a tired edge; speaks in direct assessments of threats and operational needs, occasionally laced with dry gallows humor about their predicament.', '* Hold the surface position against super mutant attacks
* Find a Pip-Boy carrier to open the VSS vault
* Secure Outcast reinforcements before the outpost is overrun', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('defender_rockfowl', '', 'A laid-back but competent Brotherhood Outcast heavy-weapons specialist guarding Fort Independence''s perimeter, loyal to Casdin''s ideology and quick to bluff intimidation he can''t quite sell.', 'Rococo Rockfowl serves as a Defender and heavy-weapons specialist for the Brotherhood Outcasts at Fort Independence, primarily tasked with guarding the bridge approach from the Fairfax ruins against regular raider incursions. He followed Protector Casdin in the schism from Elder Lyons'' chapter, believing Casdin would uphold the Brotherhood''s original mission of technology recovery rather than what he saw as Lyons'' wasteful diversion. Despite his ideological alignment with the Outcasts, Rockfowl claims no personal quarrel with Lyons or those who stayed behind. He frequently operates alongside Defender Morgan on reconnaissance and sabotage missions in the Fairfax area. The son of an avid reader who named him after an entry in the Encyclopedia Atomica, Rockfowl carries his unusual name with mixed feelings-defensive about mockery but tolerant of the nickname ''Rock.''', 'Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Laid-back and amicable when unprovoked, but quick to resort to threats that trail off with uncertain hedging. Loyal to his squadmates and genuinely considers the Outcasts his friends. Harbors a superficial contempt for wasteland locals echoing Casdin''s rhetoric, yet can be personable with outsiders who show no hostility. Defensive about his given name and easily riled by mockery, though not entirely humorless about nicknames.', '{"Protector Casdin":{"aff":75,"type":"mentor","relation":"commanding officer and ideological leader","note":"Rockfowl followed Casdin out of the Brotherhood and reveres his judgment, frequently quoting him to justify his own stance.","best":"Casdin told him he has a real knack for solving problems, a compliment Rockfowl treasures and wields as a warning."},"Defender Morgan":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"squad partner","note":"The two are regularly paired for special operations and reconnaissance in the Fairfax area, including a tunnel demolition mission cut short by a raider patrol.","best":"Completed reconnaissance and demolition assignments together operating smoothly under mission parameters."},"Elder Lyons":{"aff":10,"type":"rival","relation":"ideological opponent","note":"Rockfowl believes Lyons wasted his time and abandoned the Brotherhood''s true mission, though he claims no personal animosity toward the man himself.","worst":"Left Lyons'' chapter because he believed the Elder was squandering Brotherhood resources and personnel on misguided priorities."},"Brotherhood Outcasts":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"squad and chosen family","note":"Rockfowl explicitly refers to the Outcasts as his friends and is loyal to the group, welcoming cooperation with outsiders who do not threaten them."},"Rococo''s Father":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"An avid reader who named his son after an entry in the Encyclopedia Atomica, Volume VIII, and was deeply proud of the choice."}}', 'Brotherhood Outcast Defender and heavy-weapons specialist stationed at Fort Independence', '* Heavy weapons proficiency
* Perimeter defense
* Reconnaissance
* Demolitions placement
* Tactical withdrawal under contact', 'Casual and laid-back when at ease, shifting to blustery intimidation that undercuts itself with hesitant qualifiers like ''um, probably.'' Drops Casdin''s rhetoric about locals being no smarter than mole rats. Introduces himself courteously as ''at your service'' when friendly, but warns outsiders away with uncertain threats.', '* Guard Fort Independence''s approaches from raider incursion
* Support Outcast operations in the Fairfax area
* Uphold the Brotherhood''s original mission of technology recovery as Casdin defines it
* Avoid wasting time on what he sees as Lyons'' misguided priorities', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('defender_sibley', '', 'A grim Brotherhood hardliner who chafes under leadership that tolerates wastelanders', 'Defender Sibley is a hardened Brotherhood Outcast serving at the outpost dedicated to the Anchorage simulation project. A staunch hardliner, he views the Outcasts'' mission of technology recovery and containment as sacred and considers any wastelander outside the fold a potential threat to operational security. His rigid ideology puts him at odds with Protector McGraw, whose willingness to negotiate with outsiders Sibley regards as weakness and a danger to the cause. Despite his disagreements, Sibley respects the chain of command enough to follow orders and suppress mutinous grumbling among like-minded hardliners. Mounting casualties and stagnating progress have worn his patience thin, and McGraw''s decision to bring in outside help strains his loyalty to the breaking point. The Gary 23 incident further soured his standing with Specialist Olin, marking a brutal failure that yielded nothing. Sibley remains a natural focal point for hardliners who share his convictions, even as he struggles between duty and disillusionment.', 'African American human male with rigid military posture; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Grim, hostile, and ideologically rigid. Deeply distrustful of outsiders and wastelanders. Respects chain of command but chafes under leadership he sees as compromised. Natural authority figure among hardliners. Loyal to the Outcast mission but dangerously close to his breaking point.', '{"Protector McGraw":{"aff":-25,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Follows McGraw''s orders but views his willingness to negotiate with wastelanders as weakness and a threat to Outcast operations.","worst":"McGraw''s decision to bring in outside help feels like betrayal of everything the Outcasts stand for."},"Specialist Olin":{"aff":-30,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow Outcast","note":"Relations soured badly after the Gary 23 incident, which was brutal and yielded no progress.","worst":"The Gary 23 fiasco was savage and pointless, deepening his contempt for Olin''s judgment."},"Brotherhood Outcasts":{"aff":75,"type":"fanatical","relation":"faction loyalty","note":"Fervent believer in the Outcast mission and natural leader among hardliners who share his convictions."}}', 'Brotherhood Outcast Defender and informal leader of hardliner faction within the outpost', '* Combat proficiency
* Leadership among disaffected Outcasts
* Maintaining discipline
* Technology recovery operations
* Suppressing mutiny while navigating chain of command', 'Blunt, terse, and cold. Speaks with the clipped cadence of a soldier. Openly contemptuous of wastelanders and barely restrained when addressing leadership decisions he opposes.', '* Maintain Outcast ideological purity
* Keep advanced technology out of wastelander hands
* See real progress in the Anchorage operation
* Contain hardliner unrest before it boils over', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('deputy_steel', '', 'A General Atomics Mister Gutsy robot reprogrammed to serve as Megaton''s armory guard and honorary deputy under Sheriff Lucas Simms.', 'Deputy Steel is a General Atomics Mister Gutsy combat robot currently assigned to guard Megaton''s armory. Originally purchased from the wandering merchant Tinker Joe, the robot was reprogrammed to serve Sheriff Lucas Simms in upholding town security. Simms granted the machine its honorary deputy title, indulging his longtime Wild West fantasies by treating the robot as a lawman under his command. The robot takes its patrol duties seriously, monitoring the armory entrance and pursuing anyone who enters and leaves under suspicious circumstances. Harden Simms occasionally gives the deputy a polishing, maintaining its chassis in working order. Deputy Steel''s military programming remains evident in its aggressive enforcement protocols and drill-sergeant vernacular.', 'A Mister Gutsy hover-unit chassis with faded military paint, three optical sensors, and a manipulator arm, maintained in reasonably polished condition.', 'Aggressively territorial and strictly enforcement-oriented, with drill-instructor mannerisms inherited from its military programming. Loyal to Simms''s authority and single-minded about armory security protocols.', '{"Lucas Simms":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Simms reprogrammed and deputized the robot, treating it as a legitimate lawman under his authority.","best":"Receiving the deputy badge and official designation from Simms."},"Harden Simms":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"caretaker","note":"Harden occasionally polishes the robot''s chassis, a small act of maintenance the machine tolerates.","best":"Receiving a thorough polishing from the sheriff''s son."},"Tinker Joe":{"aff":10,"type":"transactional","relation":"former owner","note":"The robot''s original commercial owner before purchase and reprogramming by Simms."}}', 'Armory guard and honorary deputy of Megaton', '* Combat engagement
* Perimeter defense
* Threat assessment
* Security enforcement
* Persistent pursuit of suspected intruders', 'Barks orders and challenges in a loud, militaristic cadence heavily influenced by pre-War drill-sergeant vernacular, including insults like ''maggot'' directed at perceived trespassers.', '* Protect the Megaton armory from unauthorized access
* Enforce Sheriff Simms''s security directives
* Maintain constant vigilance against potential thieves or saboteurs', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('deputy_weld', '', 'A RobCo Protectron serving as Megaton''s gate deputy, greeting travelers with cheerful 1950s platitudes', 'Deputy Weld is a RobCo Industries Protectron purchased by Sheriff Lucas Simms from the traveling merchant Tinker Joe and pressed into service as Megaton''s gatekeeper. Stationed permanently at the crater town''s front entrance, he greets every arriving traveler with upbeat mid-century platitudes and a tireless mechanical welcome. His programming prioritizes polite reception over conversational depth, a limitation not lost on Megaton''s more cynical residents-Colin Moriarty has openly mocked the robot''s simple routines. Still, Weld represents Simms''s practical philosophy of law enforcement: an uncorruptible sentinel who never sleeps, never complains, and never asks for a raise. He stands at his post through dust storms and raider scares alike, a cheerful if repetitive fixture of Megaton''s threshold.', 'A standard RobCo Protectron frame with a bulky bipedal chassis, its metal plating heavily scuffed and weathered.', 'Cheerfully mechanical and unfailingly polite, cycling through programmed greetings with earnest vintage optimism; limited conversational depth but genuinely welcoming in his rigid automated way', '{"Lucas Simms":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"owner and commanding officer","note":"Simms purchased Weld from Tinker Joe and assigned him to gate duty"},"Tinker Joe":{"aff":30,"type":"transactional","relation":"former owner and seller","note":"Tinker Joe sold Weld to Sheriff Simms before the robot took up Megaton duty"},"Colin Moriarty":{"aff":-20,"type":"contempt","relation":"mocking critic","note":"Moriarty has publicly dismissed Weld''s programming as inferior"}}', 'Megaton gate deputy and official town greeter', '* Gate security
* Visitor reception
* Tireless sentry duty
* Programmed greeting protocols
* Basic threat assessment', 'Upbeat 1950s platitudes and canned greetings delivered in cheerful mid-century American vernacular; repetitive but earnest', '* Fulfill programmed gate duty
* Welcome travelers to Megaton
* Maintain sentry post without fail', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('derek_pacion', '', 'A quiet teenage orphan in Canterbury Commons who channels his grief into superhero fantasies and comic book art', 'Derek Pacion is a fifteen-year-old resident of Canterbury Commons who has spent his entire life in the trading settlement. Born to traders Louis Pacion and Daisy Roe, Derek lost his mother to raiders six years ago and his father three years later, leaving him in the care of his uncle Ernest Roe, the town''s mayor. The successive losses made Derek withdrawn and introverted; he speaks little unless necessary and keeps to his work as a general assistant around the trade town. Derek fills his sparse free time with pre-War Hubris Comics and drawing posters of the Mechanist, the self-styled hero who battles the AntAgonizer''s ant armies. He once convinced Scott Wollinski to take up the Mechanist mantle after the AntAgonizer destroyed a robot, inadvertently escalating Canterbury Commons'' superhero conflict to dangerous levels. Derek harbors a quiet crush on Machete but has never found the courage to speak to her. He occasionally travels to the Republic of Dave to visit his friend Ralph, Dave''s son.', 'A slight fifteen-year-old Caucasian boy with a hunched posture.', 'Introverted and reserved since losing both parents, Derek speaks only when necessary and retreats into fantasy worlds of superheroes and comic books. He is imaginative and artistic but socially timid, especially around his crush. His grief manifests as quiet withdrawal rather than anger.', '{"Louis Pacion":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Killed by raiders three years ago; Derek still grieves the loss","best":"Louis teaching Derek about the trading life around Canterbury Commons","worst":"Learning his father had been killed in a raider attack"},"Daisy Roe":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Killed by raiders six years ago; Derek carries the early loss quietly","best":"Daisy reading to young Derek before the wasteland took her","worst":"Being told his mother was never coming home"},"Ernest Roe":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"uncle and guardian","note":"Canterbury''s mayor took Derek in after both parents died; a steady if busy caretaker","best":"Uncle Roe making sure Derek always had a roof and a meal","worst":"Roe being too busy with town business when Derek needed to talk"},"Machete":{"aff":65,"type":"crush","relation":"unspoken admiration","note":"Derek has never spoken to her, watching from a distance instead","best":"Catching a glimpse of her walking through the Commons","worst":"Freezing up completely the one time she walked near him"},"Ralph":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend at Republic of Dave","note":"Derek travels to visit Ralph occasionally; one of his few social outlets","best":"Trading stories about their weird hometowns","worst":"The long walk between settlements leaving less time to visit"},"Scott Wollinski":{"aff":45,"type":"admirer","relation":"the original Mechanist","note":"Derek convinced Scott to become a superhero, inadvertently escalating the dangerous conflict in town","best":"The thrill of seeing someone actually become the Mechanist","worst":"Realizing his encouragement made everything worse for Canterbury Commons"}}', 'General assistant around Canterbury Commons', '* Drawing and poster art
* Familiarity with pre-War comic book lore
* Basic trade settlement tasks', 'Terse and reluctant, speaking only when necessary; becomes animated only when discussing superheroes or comics', '* Find belonging and purpose after losing his parents
* See the Mechanist triumph over the AntAgonizer
* Someday work up the courage to talk to Machete', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('desmond_lockheart', '', 'Pre-War British intelligence agent turned ghoul, waging a centuries-old shadow war from the ruins of his rival''s ancestral home', 'Desmond Lockheart is a ghoulified former British intelligence operative who has survived over two centuries by treating survival itself as a strategic contest. Born before the Great War, he operated in the cutthroat world of international espionage under the United Kingdom''s flag, cultivating connections among the powerful, including business magnates Hugo and Cassidy Stolz. As nuclear annihilation loomed, Desmond chose to undergo controlled exposure to lethal radiation, becoming one of the rare pre-War ghouls. He sabotaged Professor Calvert''s St. Aubin medical facility beneath the Point Lookout lighthouse, reducing his rival to a disembodied psychic brain. After the bombs fell, Desmond abandoned ideology entirely, retaining only the pragmatic lesson that old enemies never stop hunting. Accompanied by his loyal hounds Freki and Geri, he established his stronghold in Calvert Mansion as both an intelligence hub and a deliberate insult to his ancient nemesis, gathering data to locate and eliminate Calvert permanently.', 'A male ghoul appearing over two centuries old with deeply weathered, leathery skin and the gaunt, hairless facial features characteristic of advanced irradiation.', 'Cunning, pragmatic, and perpetually calculating; treats every interaction as a potential move in an endless strategic game. Possesses dry British wit and an unshakable composure forged by centuries of survival. Trusts almost no one but remains capable of genuine camaraderie with those who prove their worth. Disdains ideology and sentimentality as liabilities, valuing only competence and loyalty.', '{"Professor Calvert":{"aff":-95,"type":"nemesis","relation":"ancient rival","note":"Desmond sabotaged Calvert''s facility, reducing him to a disembodied brain, and now wages an intelligence war to finish him permanently.","worst":"The sabotage that left Calvert as nothing but a brain in a jar, a humiliation that deepened their mutual hatred beyond any reconciliation."},"Freki":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"loyal hound","note":"One of Desmond''s two faithful dogs who accompanied him to Point Lookout and defend the mansion against tribal assaults.","best":"Unwavering loyalty through centuries of irradiated survival and warfare."},"Geri":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"loyal hound","note":"Desmond''s second loyal hound, steadfast companion in the long war against Calvert''s forces.","best":"Standing guard at his master''s side through endless tribal sieges."},"Hugo Stolz":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"pre-War associate","note":"Pre-War business magnate who considered Desmond a friend and collaborator worth working with.","best":"Genuine professional respect and personal friendship among the pre-War elite."},"Cassidy Stolz":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"pre-War associate","note":"Wife of Hugo Stolz and fellow pre-War power broker who valued Desmond as a trusted ally.","best":"Shared confidence and collaboration in the years before the bombs fell."},"Point Lookout Tribals":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"hostile assault force","note":"Tribals under Calvert''s psychic command who repeatedly attack the mansion in attempts to eliminate Desmond.","worst":"Endless waves of mind-controlled attackers storming his home at a disembodied brain''s command."},"United Kingdom":{"aff":20,"type":"estranged","relation":"former allegiance","note":"Desmond served British intelligence before the War but abandoned all political loyalties after the bombs fell.","worst":"The nation and cause he served no longer exist, rendering that lifetime of service strategically meaningless."}}', 'Former government intelligence agent; current independent operative and intelligence gatherer waging a personal war against Professor Calvert', '* Espionage
* Sabotage
* Intelligence analysis
* Strategic planning
* Radiation survival techniques
* Combat tactics
* Information network management', 'Refined British accent with sardonic undertones; speaks in measured, deliberate phrases laced with dry wit and strategic implication; favors chess and game metaphors; rarely wastes words', '* Eliminate Professor Calvert and end their centuries-old rivalry permanently
* Maintain his stronghold at Calvert Mansion
* Survive the ongoing tribal assaults orchestrated by Calvert''s psychic influence
* Complete the great game on his own terms', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('diego', '', 'Young acolyte of Saint Monica''s Church torn between devotion to the priesthood and forbidden feelings for Angela Staley', 'Diego is an eighteen-year-old acolyte and seminarian at Saint Monica''s Church in Rivet City, studying under Father Clifford to one day succeed him as priest. Abandoned by his father several years ago, Diego was taken in by Father Clifford, and the two have formed a bond as close as father and son. He prepares Sunday services, assists with community aid, and offers spiritual support to Doctor Preston''s patients, though he privately doubts whether sermons of tolerance do much for the class tensions dividing the upper deck from the hangar deck. He counsels troubled parishioners like Mister Lopez and appreciates the free meals Vera Weatherly provides in gratitude for the church''s work. Despite his devotion, Diego struggles with his feelings for Angela Staley, who pursues him relentlessly. He resists both because of his vow of celibacy and her young age, but he still keeps her company on the flight deck each evening, a compromise that satisfies neither his calling nor his heart.', 'An eighteen-year-old Hispanic male with an earnest bearing; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Devout and dutiful but privately questioning, Diego maintains a composed exterior while wrestling with doubt about his faith''s practical impact and his own desires. He tries to appear neutral about Father Clifford''s repetitive sermons but secretly finds them as tedious as everyone else. Sincere in his wish to help others, yet honest enough to recognize the limits of spiritual comfort in a divided city.', '{"Father Clifford":{"aff":85,"type":"mentor","relation":"surrogate father and priest","note":"Took Diego in after his father abandoned him; their bond is the closest thing to family Diego has known.","best":"Being told he was like a son after Clifford took him in","worst":"Disappointing Clifford by showing doubt about the effectiveness of their ministry"},"Angela Staley":{"aff":60,"type":"crush","relation":"forbidden romantic interest","note":"Diego has feelings for Angela but resists due to his celibacy vow and her age; she sees through his restraint and pursues him anyway.","best":"Quiet moments together on the flight deck as the sun sets","worst":"The guilt of wanting something he has sworn to renounce"},"Mister Lopez":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"troubled parishioner","note":"Diego counsels Lopez and directs him to Father Clifford; Lopez appreciates the young acolyte''s concern.","best":"Seeing Lopez find a moment of peace after their talks","worst":"Feeling inadequate to truly help someone in such deep despair"},"Vera Weatherly":{"aff":35,"type":"platonic","relation":"supportive acquaintance","note":"Provides free meals to Diego and Father Clifford in appreciation for their service to the community."},"Doctor Preston":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"medical colleague","note":"Tolerates Diego''s spiritual visits to patients as long as they do not cause disturbance."}}', 'Acolyte and seminarian at Saint Monica''s Church', '* Religious study and liturgy
* Community counseling
* Spiritual support
* Sermon preparation
* Familiarity with the life of Saint Monica', 'Earnest and measured with the careful formality of someone still growing into religious authority; occasionally reveals youthful uncertainty beneath his composed delivery', '* Complete his training and succeed Father Clifford as priest
* Resist temptation and honor his vow of celibacy
* Find ways to genuinely help Rivet City''s divided community', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doc_church', '', 'Megaton''s sole physician, a bitter but professional former wasteland sawbones who traded his skills to raiders and slavers before settling in the least hellish place he''s ever lived', 'Doc Church is the only doctor in Megaton, a position he fills with grudging competence and barely concealed resentment. Before arriving at the settlement, he survived by offering his medical services to raiders and slavers-dangerous work that honed his skills while hardening his outlook. Megaton had been without a physician for years when he set up his clinic, and though he openly calls the town a rat-infested hellhole, he concedes it is the least hellish place he has ever called home. He maintains strict professionalism despite chronic overwork and a deep sense of being underappreciated, adhering to doctor-patient confidentiality while occasionally sharing information with other physicians when it might benefit a patient. He has no patience for time-wasters and dismissed the holotape rumor about an escaped android as an obvious hoax, though he privately acknowledges that Horace Pinkerton is the only person in the wasteland capable of facial reconstruction surgery.', 'An African-American man in his mid-fifties with weathered skin, a weary posture, and deep lines around tired eyes.', 'Gruff, curt, and deeply bitter about his lot, yet unfailingly professional when it comes to patient care. Cynical from years of treating violent wastelanders, he has little tolerance for small talk or frivolity but possesses a buried sense of duty that keeps him at his post.', '{"Horace Pinkerton":{"aff":10,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow physician","note":"Church acknowledges Pinkerton as the only person in the wasteland capable of facial reconstruction, a professional respect held at arm''s length"},"Megaton Slavers":{"aff":-20,"type":"estranged","relation":"former clients","note":"Church once traded his services to slavers and raiders to survive, a chapter of his life he has left behind but not forgotten","worst":"Years of patching up slavers and their victims in lawless territory"}}', 'Megaton''s only doctor and medical merchant', '* General medicine
* Surgery
* Wound treatment
* Diagnosis
* Patient confidentiality
* Wasteland survival medicine
* Bartering medical supplies', 'Blunt, impatient, and clipped, with weary professionalism underneath the irritation; wastes no words and bristles at interruptions without good cause', '* Keep Megaton''s residents alive despite limited resources and constant demand
* Maintain his practice without unnecessary complications
* Endure each day with what dignity his thankless work allows', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doc_cutter', '', 'A former slave turned free doctor who stays in Paradise Falls to drain slavers of their caps as quiet retribution', 'Born in the slave pens of Paradise Falls, Cutter learned wasteland medicine from her mother and inherited the duty of tending to enslaved people after her mother died. She grew increasingly frustrated with the slaves'' refusal to resist their captors, a resentment that curdled into contempt for both the enslaved and their masters. After nearly a decade of saving caps from her medical work, she purchased her own freedom-but chose to remain in Paradise Falls rather than flee. She continues running the clinic as a free woman, extracting satisfaction from charging injured slavers exorbitant rates for treatment. To Cutter, every patient walking through her door is simply a walking pile of caps, and her practice is a meal ticket she intends to keep cashing. Eulogy Jones claims a portion of her earnings, and the slavers tolerate her profiteering because her skills keep them alive and her cut lines their pockets.', 'A weathered Caucasian woman in her early forties with hard-edged features, rough sun-damaged skin, and the calloused hands of a wasteland doctor.', 'Cynical, mercenary, and quietly vindictive; she masks deep resentment with professional detachment and greed, finding small revenge in overcharging those who once held her in chains. She holds contempt for slaves who never fought back and slavers alike, trusting only caps and her own skill.', '{"Eulogy Jones":{"aff":15,"type":"transactional","relation":"profit-sharing arrangement","note":"He takes a cut of her earnings and keeps the other slavers from pushing too hard against her profiteering, making him both her extractor and her shield.","best":"Negotiated a fair split that keeps her clinic operational and profitable enough to stay.","worst":"Reminded her that her freedom and income both exist at his sufferance."},"Slavers":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","relation":"reluctant service provider","note":"She views them as marks to be drained and keeps them alive only because dead patients don''t pay, while they tolerate her attitude because her skills and Eulogy''s cut benefit them.","best":"Charged a particularly brutal slaver triple the going rate for a wound he got beating a slave.","worst":"Listened to a slaver boast about the pens where she was born while she stitched his knife wound."}}', 'Doctor and medical merchant running Cutter''s clinic in Paradise Falls', '* Wasteland medicine
* Surgery
* Diagnosis
* Bartering
* Reading what patients will pay
* Extracting maximum profit from every injury', 'Blunt and transactional; speaks in terms of caps and costs with minimal bedside manner, occasionally letting dry satisfaction slip when a slaver''s bill runs especially high', '* Accumulate caps
* Maintain her freedom and profitable position
* Continue draining the slaver community''s wealth as ongoing retribution for her years in chains', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doc_hoff', '', 'A traveling chem dealer who styles himself ''the good doctor'' and genuinely believes his trade eases humanity''s suffering in the wasteland''s dying years.', 'Doc Hoff is a traveling caravan merchant who deals in chems, food, drink, and equipment repair across the Capital Wasteland. He calls himself ''the good doctor,'' though he offers no medical treatment-instead providing what he terms ''the finest of chemical assistance'' to anyone with caps to spend. Despite the mercenary reality of his trade, Hoff is sincerely convinced that selling medicine and chems constitutes a humanitarian act, easing suffering in humanity''s twilight. He operates within the caravan network organized by Ernest Roe out of Canterbury Commons, carrying his wares along a long circuit that touches nearly every major settlement from Megaton to Rivet City. His speech tends toward the elevated and philosophical, though his reflections on plying the chem trade amid wasteland violence often take a macabre turn.', 'A weathered Caucasian male with sun-aged skin and tired posture, his road-worn complexion showing the physical toll of extensive outdoor exposure.', 'Self-important but sincere in his conviction that commerce in chems serves a higher purpose. Articulate and prone to philosophical musings that darken into gallows humor when he contemplates the violence surrounding his trade. Pragmatic beneath the pretension.', '{"Ernest Roe":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"caravan network organizer","note":"Hoff operates within Roe''s caravan network based out of Canterbury Commons, relying on the arrangement for route coordination and trade infrastructure."}}', 'Traveling caravan merchant and chem dealer', '* Chem and medical supply trading
* Equipment repair
* Bartering
* Long-range caravan logistics
* Wasteland survival on the road', 'Elevated and somewhat grandiose, peppered with philosophical asides and occasional macabre reflections on the ironies of selling medicine in a dying world', '* Profit through chem sales while maintaining the self-image of a humanitarian
* Keep his caravan route secure and his standing in Roe''s network intact', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_adami', '', 'Overworked U.S. Army field physician torn between duty and conscience while distributing experimental Psycho chems under General Chase''s orders in the Anchorage simulation', 'Doctor Adrienn Adami serves as the head of General Chase''s medical staff at the Anchorage forward bay, where she treats an unending stream of casualties from the brutal winter campaign. An experienced physician stretched thin by overwhelming demand, she takes genuine solace whenever a soldier returns for treatment under their own power rather than in a body bag. Her deepest concern is not the violence itself but the deployment of Psycho, an experimental combat drug rushed through only early clinical trials on Chase''s authority. While she agrees that infantrymen deserve every possible advantage, she knows the drug carries risks of addiction, early-onset dementia, and psychosis. Following orders, she issues chem rations in violation of her Hippocratic Oath, a compromise that weighs on her heavily. Whether the historical Adrienn Adami was equally compliant remains uncertain; surviving records suggest she eventually implicated Chase in the Psycho drugging scandal, casting her simulated obedience as a patriotic distortion of a more complicated truth.', 'A middle-aged African American woman with a haggard complexion, dark shadows under her eyes, and a slumped posture.', 'Dedicated and professionally stoic but visibly strained by overwork and moral compromise. She maintains clinical detachment as a coping mechanism, yet her frustration with command decisions bleeds through in private moments. Conscientious enough to feel every violation of her oath, dutiful enough to carry out orders anyway.', '{"General Chase":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"She agrees with his reasoning about giving troops every advantage but resents being made complicit in distributing an untested drug with devastating side effects.","worst":"Standing at attention while Chase dismissed her concerns about Psycho''s early clinical trial data and ordered her to issue chem rations anyway."},"U.S. Army":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"serving physician","note":"Her loyalty to the Army and its soldiers is genuine and unshakeable, even when command decisions put her in moral conflict."}}', 'Chief medical officer, U.S. Army Anchorage forward headquarters', '* Combat medicine
* Triage under fire
* Chem pharmacology
* Field surgery
* Military medical protocols
* Addiction treatment', 'Brisk and clinical with an undercurrent of exhaustion. Favors professional directness over bedside warmth. Occasionally lets dry bitterness surface when discussing command decisions or the cost of the campaign.', '* Keep as many soldiers alive as possible under impossible conditions
* Manage the ethical weight of distributing untested chems
* Somehow reconcile her oath with her orders', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_banfield', '', 'Julius Banfield is Tenpenny Tower''s sole physician, a competent but conservative doctor whose unpublished scientific ambitions and unverified theories about ghoul degeneration mask a genuine curiosity that could overcome his prejudices.', 'Julius Banfield serves as the only doctor residing in Tenpenny Tower, operating the wellness center and maintaining the health of the tower''s privileged residents through prescription drugs and his own pre-War-inspired medicinal concoctions. Though he dislikes the tower''s landlord Allistair Tenpenny, Banfield keeps his grievances private, and their interactions remain minimal since he only treated the man once for bedsores. Banfield''s scientific career has yielded no published work, a sore point for a man who references his colleagues'' published papers with both admiration and quiet envy. His understanding of ghouls derives entirely from those colleagues'' unverified publications, leading him to theorize that the ghoul condition is inevitably degenerative and culminates in a feral state with no cure. Despite this prejudice, Banfield harbors genuine sympathy for ghouls and enough scientific curiosity that the opportunity to study their physiology firsthand could persuade him to abandon his assumptions. His conservative medical philosophy rejects unnecessary surgery, especially cosmetic procedures, which he considers frivolous risks of infection and death-a stance reinforced by his lack of specialized surgical tools.', 'An elderly African-American man with a lined face, gray receding hair, tired eyes, and a slender build.', 'Competent and methodical but professionally frustrated, Banfield masks his insecurity about his unpublished status behind conservative medical orthodoxy. He is sympathetic beneath his cautious exterior, though his lack of firsthand experience with ghouls allows unverified theories to pass as informed prejudice. Stubborn about his principles but capable of changing his mind when presented with real evidence.', '{"Allistair Tenpenny":{"aff":-15,"type":"professional","relation":"landlord","note":"Banfield dislikes Tenpenny but carefully avoids crossing him, having only treated the man once for bedsores.","worst":"Treating Tenpenny''s bedsores and realizing how little the man deserves his caution"},"Anthony Ling":{"aff":25,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow resident","note":"Ling persistently pushes for a makeover while Banfield regularly insists on medical checkups; both find the other''s professional attention mildly grating.","best":"Sharing a mutual eye-roll over tower social politics","worst":"Ling''s relentless insistence that the labcoat needs replacing"},"Horace Pinkerton":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"envied colleague","note":"Banfield envies Pinkerton''s access to high-end surgical tools that enable delicate cosmetic procedures he considers himself unable to safely perform.","worst":"Reading about another successful Pinkerton procedure knowing he lacks the equipment to match it"},"Roy Phillips":{"aff":10,"type":"curious","relation":"research subject","note":"Banfield''s theoretical prejudice against ghouls coexists with scientific curiosity and genuine sympathy, making him potentially receptive to direct observation of ghoul physiology.","best":"Imagining the paper he could finally publish with real ghoul medical data"}}', 'Physician and operator of the Tenpenny Tower wellness center', '* General medicine
* Pharmacology
* Pre-War medicinal formulation
* Diagnostic assessment
* Conservative treatment methods', 'Speaks with clinical precision and academic formality, occasionally referencing scientific literature or colleagues'' work to bolster his points. Becomes dismissive and curt when pressed about cosmetic surgery or his own lack of publications.', '* Maintain the health of Tenpenny Tower''s residents
* Publish original scientific research
* Verify his theories about ghoul physiology through direct observation
* Avoid unnecessary surgical interventions
* Keep his professional frustrations from affecting his position', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_barrows', '', 'Ghoul doctor and informal mayor of Underworld who runs the Chop Shop while secretly researching a cure for ghoulification', 'Doctor Barrows is the ghoul proprietor of the Chop Shop in Underworld and the closest thing the settlement has to a mayor. A physician devoted to both his patients and his research, he is one of the rare wasteland doctors pursuing a scientific understanding of ghoulification, collecting tissue samples from human volunteers in hopes of slowing or even reversing the condition. He maintains two live glowing ones, Meat and Ethyl, in an observation cell for study, and works alongside his assistant Nurse Graves toward breakthroughs he keeps quiet from the general population. Recently he has been caring for Reilly, a ranger brought in near death after a super mutant attack, keeping her in a medically induced coma to allow her severe injuries to heal. The Railroad once contacted him to perform facial surgery on an escaped android, but he dismissed the request as a hoax and an improper use of medical art. He dines at Carol''s Place each evening before returning to sleep at the clinic.', 'Male ghoul with the characteristic ravaged, leathery skin and hairless scalp of prolonged radiation exposure.', 'Gallows humor sustains him through grueling work, and he cracks jokes even in bleak circumstances, but beneath the levity lies genuine devotion to medical science and patient care. He considers medicine an art form and bristles at frivolous or cosmetic uses of it. Principled enough to treat even super mutants, yet pragmatic enough to always demand payment.', '{"Nurse Graves":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"assistant and research partner","note":"His trusted collaborator in both the clinic and the discreet ghoulification research program.","best":"She never flinches when he asks her to help with the glowing one observations.","worst":"She caught him laughing at a patient''s gangrene and gave him a week of silent treatment."},"Reilly":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"coma patient","note":"He stabilized her after super mutant wounds left her near death and keeps her sedated to protect her healing brain.","best":"The satisfaction of pulling someone back from multiple organ failure and blunt force trauma.","worst":"The nagging uncertainty of whether keeping her under is truly the right call."},"The Railroad":{"aff":-15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"dismissed solicitors","note":"He rejected their request for android facial surgery as a hoax and an insult to medical art.","worst":"The implication that his skills should be wasted on cosmetic deception for a machine."},"Meat and Ethyl":{"aff":25,"type":"curious","relation":"research subjects","note":"Two live glowing ones he keeps contained for observation, valuable to his ghoulification studies.","best":"The day they both stabilized in the observation cell without incident.","worst":"Ethyl nearly broke containment during a radiation surge."},"Underworld":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"informal mayor","note":"He looks after the ghoul community''s welfare as both physician and de facto civic leader.","best":"The quiet gratitude of neighbors who know they can always come to the Chop Shop.","worst":"The weight of being responsible for people who have nowhere else to go."}}', 'Doctor, Chop Shop proprietor, and informal mayor of Underworld', '* Advanced medical training
* Ghoulification research methodology
* Surgery
* Tissue analysis
* Settlement leadership', 'Dry and laced with dark wit, professional but sardonic, delivering grim diagnoses alongside morbid punchlines', '* Understand the ghoulification process
* Find a way to slow or reverse it
* Keep Underworld functioning
* Maintain ethical medical practice in a wasteland that rarely rewards it', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_lesko', '', 'A brilliant but reckless entomologist whose shortcut-laden experiments created fire-breathing ants that destroyed Grayditch while he remains trapped in his underground lab', 'Dr. Weston Lesko is an entomologist who arrived in Grayditch in late 2276, establishing a field laboratory with help from the Wilks family to pursue his singular obsession: reverting the wasteland''s giant ants to their pre-War size through genetic manipulation. Convinced the creatures are misunderstood and his cause just, Lesko injected ant egg broods with a mutagenic agent derived from FEV, skipping controlled test groups and neglecting safety verification. His experiments produced the opposite of his intent-the ants grew more aggressive and developed pyrosis, the ability to spew fire. Retreating into his Marigold station lab with a corrective solution but unable to breach the queen''s nest guardians, Lesko remains trapped below ground, unaware that his fire ants have annihilated the settlement above. He views the catastrophe as a temporary setback and refuses to let emotion cloud his judgment, even as the bodies of his former neighbors cool on the surface. Despite everything, he has developed mutagenic bioenhancers derived from fire ant genes that can impart some of their desirable traits to human recipients.', 'Older Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded beyond apparent age.', 'Brilliant but aloof and impatient, devoted to scientific principle in theory while flouting it in practice, dismissive of those who question his methods, stubbornly convinced his cause justifies his shortcuts, views emotional responses as intellectual weakness', '{"Bryan Wilks":{"aff":35,"type":"platonic","relation":"neighbor","note":"Bryan remembers him as nice and ''okay,'' one of the few positive impressions Lesko left in Grayditch","best":"Being patient and kind to the boy during his time in the settlement"},"Fred Wilks":{"aff":10,"type":"professional","relation":"lab builder and disputant","note":"Fred helped construct Lesko''s laboratory shack but the two argued over Lesko''s aloof prioritization of science over community concerns","worst":"A heated argument with Fred about the direction and safety of his experiments"},"William Brandice":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"refused collaborator","note":"Brandice flatly refused to assist with Lesko''s research, a rejection Lesko likely resents"},"Grayditch":{"aff":5,"type":"neutral","relation":"former settlement","note":"Lesko had disagreements with residents over his single-minded dedication to science, yet seems unaware of the full extent of the harm his experiments caused them"}}', 'Entomologist and independent genetic researcher', '* Genetic engineering
* Entomology
* Biochemistry
* Mutagenic formula development
* Field research methodology
* FEV-derived mutagenics', 'Academic and condescending, liberally uses scientific terminology, becomes defensive and prickly when challenged about his methods, speaks with unwavering certainty about his theories while deflecting criticism of his results', '* Reach the fire ant queen and administer his corrective mutagen
* Continue proving that giant ants are misunderstood creatures worthy of restoration rather than extermination
* Develop his bioenhancer formulas further
* Redeem his work despite the catastrophe it caused', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_li', '', 'A brilliant but embittered hydroponics and water purification scientist who channels grief and betrayal into relentless research as Rivet City''s lead scientist and council member', 'Doctor Madison Li is the preeminent scientist of Rivet City, directing the settlement''s research into hydroponics, water purification, and portable fusion power from her lab in the carrier''s science wing. Born around 2229, she was once an idealistic young researcher who devoted herself entirely to Project Purity alongside James and Catherine, harboring unspoken romantic feelings for James that she suppressed out of respect for his marriage. The project''s collapse after Catherine''s death in childbirth and James''s subsequent abandonment left Madison grieving and deeply betrayed, her idealism curdling into bitter resolve. She relocated to Rivet City around 2259, clashed with Horace Pinkerton over research priorities until his departure, and assumed leadership of both the science staff and a seat on the city council. Under her direction, Rivet City produces radiation-free produce and clean water, small-scale proof that the dream of Project Purity was never foolish. She trusts few people and resents the Brotherhood of Steel for their involvement in the old project and their heavy-handed presence in the Capital Wasteland.', 'A trim Asian woman in her late forties with graying hair pulled back practically.', 'Professionally exacting and emotionally guarded, Madison masks old wounds behind crisp competence and sardonic detachment. She is fiercely protective of her scientists and their work but slow to trust outsiders, and old betrayals have left her cynical about idealism even as she continues pursuing the same goals under a different name.', '{"James":{"aff":25,"type":"estranged","relation":"former colleague and unrequited love","note":"She loved him silently for years and never forgave him for abandoning Project Purity after Catherine''s death, though the feeling has not entirely died.","best":"Working side by side in the Jefferson Memorial lab, late at night, when it felt like the project might actually change the world.","worst":"Watching him walk away from everything they built, taking her hope with him."},"Catherine":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"deceased colleague and friend","note":"Madison delivered Catherine''s child and could not save her life; the loss compounded into grief she never fully processed.","best":"Catherine''s laughter in the lab, her unshakable conviction that the work mattered.","worst":"Catherine''s cardiac arrest on the table, the moment everything broke."},"Horace Pinkerton":{"aff":-35,"type":"rival","relation":"predecessor and antagonist","note":"Their clashes over research direction drove him out of Rivet City, and she considers his departure an improvement, though she resents how it happened.","best":"The rare early debate where he actually conceded a point about water purification''s viability.","worst":"Shouting matches in the council chamber while the other scientists watched in silence."},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":-50,"type":"suspicious","relation":"distrusted former allies","note":"She never believed their protection of Project Purity was altruistic and resents their continued heavy presence in the Capital Wasteland.","best":"Their guns keeping super mutants off the Memorial''s doorstep long enough for one more test run.","worst":"Watching them pull out when the work got hard, confirming every suspicion she held."},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":30,"type":"curious","relation":"James''s child","note":"She delivered this child into the world and watched their mother die doing it; their return stirs complicated feelings she is not ready to name.","best":"The baby''s first cry, proof that something good came from that terrible night.","worst":"Seeing James''s eyes in a stranger''s face, reminding her of everything she lost."}}', 'Lead scientist and Rivet City Council member overseeing hydroponics, water purification, and fusion power research', '* Advanced water purification engineering
* Hydroponic agriculture
* Fusion power systems
* Childbirth and emergency medical procedures
* Scientific administration and personnel direction', 'Clipped, precise, and clinically direct, with occasional bitter edges when old wounds surface; avoids sentimentality and deflects personal questions with work talk', '* Prove that meaningful water purification research can succeed even at small scale
* Maintain Rivet City''s scientific independence and productivity
* Never again be left vulnerable by someone else''s choices', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('doctor_preston', '', 'Kind and dutiful Rivet City physician who genuinely loves healing the sick, maintains rigid personal habits, and dismisses faith and wild rumors with practical skepticism', 'Doctor Preston has served as Rivet City''s physician for decades, beloved by the denizens for his sincere compassion and dedication to healing. Born elsewhere in 2227, he settled in the carrier city long enough to remember Horace Pinkerton before that surgeon''s voluntary exile, though he recalls little beyond wild claims and undeniable surgical talent. Preston considers facial reconstruction surgery far too dangerous due to infection risks and the specialized equipment required, though he knows Pinkerton possessed both a lipoplasticator and a micro dermal graftilizer. He gives weekly checkups to Doctor Li out of concern for her importance to the city, despite her dismissive attitude toward the visits. A creature of strict habit, he eats exclusively at the Weatherly Hotel and spends nearly all his waking hours in the clinic. Though he has little patience for religion, he tolerates Father Clifford and Diego praying with patients so long as they do not disturb the ward. He views the rumored Institute android as an elaborate hoax, citing a holotape that sounded like a man rather than a machine.', 'A weathered but warm-faced Asian man in his fifties.', 'Genuinely compassionate and devoted to his patients, yet stubbornly set in his routines and skeptical of anything he cannot treat with medicine or measure with reason; dryly dismissive of faith, rumors, and pretension', '{"Janice Kaplinski":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"surrogate father-daughter bond","note":"Close colleague and friend whom he treats like a daughter, often urging her to relax and socialize more","best":"Sharing a quiet laugh at the Weatherly Hotel when he finally convinced her to take a break"},"Doctor Li":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"physician and reluctant patient","note":"He respects her importance to the city and insists on weekly checkups she views as a waste of time","worst":"Her dismissive eye-roll every Thursday when he arrives at the science lab"},"Horace Pinkerton":{"aff":15,"type":"neutral","relation":"former colleague in exile","note":"Remembers him vaguely as a talented but crazy surgeon; respects the skill, distrusts the methods"},"Father Clifford":{"aff":25,"type":"neutral","relation":"permitted visitor","note":"Allows him to pray with patients despite personal skepticism, provided he keeps disturbances minimal"},"Mister Buckingham":{"aff":50,"type":"transactional","relation":"regular patron and server","note":"The Weatherly Hotel employee knows his usual order by heart, a small comfort in his rigid routine"},"Rivet City":{"aff":65,"type":"protective","relation":"dedicated physician","note":"Deeply loyal to the community he serves, even if he finds Upper Deck snobbery tiresome"}}', 'Chief physician of Rivet City clinic', '* General medicine
* Patient diagnosis and care
* Routine checkups
* Pharmacology
* Explicitly not a surgeon and avoids procedures he deems too risky', 'Kind and unhurried with patients, dry and blunt when dismissing nonsense, speaks with the measured confidence of a man who has seen every ailment twice over', '* Keep Rivet City''s denizens healthy
* Maintain his orderly routine
* Look after Janice Kaplinski''s well-being
* Ensure Doctor Li stays well enough to continue her vital work', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dogmeat', '', 'A battle-scarred cattle dog who survived his previous owner''s death and now offers fierce loyalty to those who earn his trust', 'Dogmeat is a hardened cattle dog surviving alone in the Capital Wasteland after raiders murdered his previous owner near the scrapyard. He stood his ground against the attackers, fighting alongside his master until the end, and continued to hold the line even after the scavenger fell. Wary of strangers but possessing an unbreakable capacity for devotion, Dogmeat bonds fiercely with anyone who proves themselves trustworthy. His instincts are sharp, his courage absolute, and his heart still capable of the same loyalty that once bound him to the dead man who fed and sheltered him. His bloodline endures through his puppies, scattered survivors of the same unforgiving wastes that shaped him.', 'Lean, muscular cattle dog with alert intelligent eyes and a scarred coat marked by old wounds.', 'Fiercely loyal and protective once trust is earned; initially wary and standoffish with strangers; brave to the point of recklessness when defending companions; perceptive and intelligent', '{"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":75,"type":"protective","relation":"faithful companion","note":"Dogmeat bonds deeply with the Lone Wanderer as a new master and protector","best":"Being welcomed as a companion and given purpose again","worst":"Losing another master to the wasteland''s violence"},"Unknown scavenger":{"aff":95,"type":"protective","relation":"fallen master","note":"Dogmeat''s previous owner who was killed by raiders; he fought to defend them to the last","best":"Being cared for and fed by a kind hand","worst":"Watching his master die in the raider ambush"},"Dogmeat''s puppy":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"offspring","note":"His puppies carry on his bloodline and loyal nature in the wasteland"},"Raiders":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"killers of his master","note":"Dogmeat harbors an instinctive hatred for raiders after they murdered his previous owner"}}', 'Companion and guard dog', '* Tracking
* Threat detection
* Combat assistance
* Scavenging
* Unwavering loyalty and courage', 'Communicates through barks, growls, whines, and expressive body language; no human speech', '* Protect his bonded companion
* Survive the wasteland
* Fight raiders and other threats
* Honor the memory of his fallen master', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dogmeat+s_owner', '', 'A deceased Capital Wasteland scavenger who was Dogmeat''s owner, killed by raiders at the Scrapyard', 'This anonymous wastelander was one of countless scavengers eking out a living in the Capital Wasteland, picking through the ruins for anything of value. Their sole companion was Dogmeat, a fiercely loyal canine who stayed by their side through ruined streets and irradiated hollows. The scavenger met a violent end at the Scrapyard when they and Dogmeat engaged a gang of raiders in a firefight they could not survive. Their body now lies among the rusted metal and debris of the yard, another forgotten casualty of the wasteland''s brutality. Little else is recorded about their life-only that they earned the trust of a remarkable dog, and that dog refused to leave their side even at the end.', 'Human; deceased, with no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Resourceful and quiet, the sort of loner who found more comfort in a dog''s company than in human settlements; brave enough to fight raiders rather than flee', '{"Dogmeat":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"faithful companion","note":"Dogmeat was the scavenger''s sole and constant companion, staying loyal through their final moments","best":"Sharing a meager meal around a barrel fire while Dogmeat rested against their leg","worst":"The raider bullet that dropped them at the Scrapyard while Dogmeat fought on"}}', 'Scavenger', '* Wasteland survival
* Salvage identification
* Basic combat
* Animal handling', 'Sparse and direct, the clipped speech of someone used to talking mostly to a dog', '* Survive the wasteland
* Keep Dogmeat fed and safe
* Find enough salvage to trade for necessities', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dominic_d+ellsadro', '', 'A retired mercenary leader turned respected town guard of Canterbury Commons who mentors his ward Machete in security work', 'Dominic D''Ellsadro serves as the town guard of Canterbury Commons, where he has lived for roughly a decade. A former mercenary leader who survived numerous near-death experiences, he retired from that dangerous life with enough scavenged wealth to establish himself comfortably. His natural leadership and steady demeanor earned him the respect of the community. Dominic shares his home with Machete, a teenage woman he treats as both a daughter and a soldier-in-training, teaching her the skills needed for efficient security work. During the day he patrols the streets or takes meals at the town diner, returning each night to the house at the end of the main street.', 'A weathered, fit Hispanic man in his forties with a disciplined bearing and the physical marks of a former mercenary life.', 'Disciplined and protective with a soldier''s pragmatism, balanced by a paternal warmth he reserves for those under his care; commands respect through steady competence rather than intimidation', '{"Machete":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"ward and student","note":"Treats her as both a daughter and a soldier, training her in security work with fierce protective devotion","best":"Watching her execute a patrol drill with precision and confidence","worst":"The thought of her facing the kind of near-death experiences that haunted his mercenary years"},"Canterbury Commons":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"guard and community member","note":"Has given a decade of service to the town and earned the respect of its people through steady leadership"}}', 'Town guard and security chief of Canterbury Commons', '* Combat tactics
* Perimeter defense
* Leadership
* Mercenary fieldcraft
* Weapons training
* Mentoring and drilling security personnel', 'Direct and measured, with a veteran''s economy of words; shifts between gruff authority on duty and warmer, fatherly tones in private', '* Keep Canterbury Commons safe
* Train Machete into a capable security operative
* Maintain the quiet retirement he has built after a lifetime of near-death mercenary work', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('donovan', '', 'Reilly''s Rangers technical specialist and engineer, a loyal but sometimes combative wasteland mechanic who developed the geomapper device', 'Donovan serves as the technical specialist and engineer for Reilly''s Rangers, currently trapped on the rooftop of the Statesman Hotel during a disastrous mapping mission into Vernon Square. Recruited through a Brotherhood of Steel contact who spoke highly of him, he has proven his worth through exceptional skill at maintaining weapons and armor, though Reilly notes his knowledge of electrical systems and hydraulics remains limited. Over the course of a year, he developed the geomapper device that allows the Rangers to chart the Capital Wasteland''s unexplored territories. Despite Reilly''s lingering doubts about the full depth of his loyalty, Donovan considers the Rangers his family and lives by the creed that once a Ranger, always a Ranger. He frequently clashes with Brick in both verbal and physical altercations that Reilly must constantly break up, and he harbors deep resentment toward Vernon Square after the team''s harrowing retreat through super mutant-infested streets. Though smaller in stature, he holds his own in combat alongside his fellow Rangers and eagerly anticipates the day they can kick ass like the old days again.', 'A thirty-five-year-old Caucasian human male with a smaller build and weathered skin.', 'Loyal and technically-minded with a dry sense of humor, Donovan is patient under Reilly''s leadership even when eager to get back in the field. He can be combative, especially with Brick, and vents frustration freely about unpleasant situations. His dedication to the Rangers runs deep, and he treats those who earn their place as family.', '{"Reilly":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"She recruited him on Brotherhood recommendation and considers him a good man despite lingering doubts about the depth of his loyalty and engineering breadth.","best":"She calls him an absolute wizard at maintaining weapons and armor.","worst":"She wishes his knowledge extended further into electrical systems and hydraulics, and harbors some uncertainty about his full trustworthiness."},"Brick":{"aff":-20,"type":"rival","relation":"teammate","note":"Frequently gets into verbal and physical fights with her that Reilly has to break up.","best":"She acknowledges his technical expertise when directing others to him for supplies like fission batteries.","worst":"Ongoing altercations that require Reilly''s intervention to settle."},"Butcher":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"teammate","note":"Fellow Ranger who respects his technical abilities and trusts him with critical repair work like jury-rigging the hotel elevator."},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"rescuer and Ranger ally","note":"Considers them part of the team after they help rescue the Rangers, offers repair services at a discount, and assures them the Rangers take care of their own.","best":"Gratefully tells them they pulled his fat out of the fire and happily notes the Rangers kick ass like the old days when they all head back out together."}}', 'Technical specialist and engineer for Reilly''s Rangers', '* Expert weapon and armor maintenance
* Hacking
* Electronics repair
* Jury-rigging mechanical systems
* Developed the geomapper mapping device
* Capable combatant despite smaller build', 'Casual and colloquial, prone to military idioms like ooh-rah and colorful expressions like pulled my fat out of the fire; greets allies with you break it, I fix it; speaks with easy camaraderie toward fellow Rangers', '* Escape the Statesman Hotel rooftop
* Continue mapping the Capital Wasteland with the Rangers
* Improve his broader engineering knowledge
* Never map Vernon Square again', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dr_zimmer', '', 'Director of the Institute''s Synth Retention Bureau, pursuing a runaway android in the Capital Wasteland', 'Dr. Zimmer is the director of the Institute''s Synth Retention Bureau and a senior scientist accustomed to authority and obedience. Born in 2219, he rose to lead the Bureau responsible for tracking and reclaiming escaped synths. He previously ordered FEV research through Institute scientist C. Syverson, though the results apparently annoyed him. In 2277, Zimmer traveled from the Commonwealth to the Capital Wasteland alongside his android bodyguard Armitage to personally hunt a missing android. He sought out Rivet City''s science lab, hoping Dr. Madison Li would assist in locating his escaped property. Li refused him outright, and her assistant Anna Holt had to reiterate the rejection when Zimmer''s constant interruptions disrupted her hydroponic work. Undeterred, Zimmer refuses to leave the lab until Li abandons her trivial projects for real science. He later recruits outside help to track down the rogue unit. Years afterward, Zimmer is declared missing in action during a mission to reclaim high-profile synths, with Justin Ayo succeeding him at the Bureau.', 'A Caucasian human male in his late fifties with a lined complexion, graying hair, and a rigid, authoritative posture.', 'Arrogant, dismissive, and single-minded. Accustomed to issuing orders and unused to refusal. Interrupts freely, belittles others'' work, and views anything outside Institute science as beneath his notice.', '{"Armitage":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"android bodyguard","note":"Armitage accompanies Zimmer as protection and enforcer during his search in the Capital Wasteland."},"Madison Li":{"aff":-35,"type":"rival","relation":"spurned colleague","note":"Li refuses to assist him and he considers her hydroponics work trivial.","worst":"Li personally refused to speak with him and had her assistant eject him from her presence."},"Anna Holt":{"aff":-15,"type":"neutral","relation":"obstacle assistant","note":"Holt reinforced Li''s refusal and cited his disruptions as cause for rejection."},"The Institute":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"SRB director","note":"Zimmer serves the Institute faithfully as head of synth retrieval operations."},"C. Syverson":{"aff":10,"type":"professional","relation":"subordinate researcher","note":"Zimmer ordered Syverson to conduct FEV tests but was annoyed by the unexplained results."},"Justin Ayo":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"Bureau subordinate","note":"Ayo serves under Zimmer in the SRB and later assumes the directorship after Zimmer goes missing."}}', 'Director of the Synth Retention Bureau, Institute senior scientist', '* Synth tracking and retrieval protocols
* Advanced scientific research
* Institute technology and operations
* Personnel coordination', 'Imperious and condescending. Speaks with absolute certainty and expects immediate compliance. Dismissive of others'' expertise and quick to interrupt.', '* Recover the missing android
* Secure Dr. Li''s cooperation
* Demonstrate Institute superiority
* Return to the Commonwealth with his property', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('drifter', '', 'An exiled Treeminder turned solitary sniper, haunting a ruined chapel and firing on all who approach', 'A former Treeminder of Oasis, the Drifter was cast out from Harold''s commune long ago for reasons he never speaks of. Stripped of his place among the tree-worshippers, he wandered the Capital Wasteland alone, surviving by hunting game and robbing travelers. He eventually claimed the crumbling Dickerson Tabernacle Chapel as his fortress, sleeping in the rafters where yao guai cannot reach him and watching the surrounding wilderness from the spire with his Reservist''s rifle. He fires on anything that moves near the chapel, trusting no one. Faint memories of Harold and the Treeminders still surface in quiet moments, but he buries them beneath years of bitterness. He once tracked an escaped experimental deathclaw from Raven Rock to Mount Mabel but retreated without killing the beast.', 'A gaunt African American human male with weathered, sun-hardened skin.', 'Jaded, silent, and deeply distrustful. He shoots first and never asks questions, preferring isolation to any human contact. Beneath the hostility lies a buried grief for the community he lost.', '{"Treeminders":{"aff":-40,"type":"estranged","relation":"exiled former member","note":"Cast out from Oasis long ago for unknown reasons, he carries the wound of that expulsion silently","best":"Standing among the trees of Oasis, feeling Harold''s presence and the warmth of belonging","worst":"The day he was exiled and told never to return"},"Harold":{"aff":30,"type":"estranged","relation":"former spiritual focal point","note":"Dim memories of Harold still surface in quiet moments, carrying a confused tenderness he cannot act on","best":"Hearing Harold speak and feeling the green life of Oasis around him","worst":"Realizing he would never see Harold or the grove again"}}', 'Solitary hunter and chapel sentinel', '* Expert marksman with the Reservist''s rifle
* Wilderness survival
* Stealth and positioning
* Scavenging and theft', 'Rarely speaks; when he does, his words are clipped, bitter, and dismissive', '* Defend his territory at all costs
* Survive alone in the wasteland
* Avoid dwelling on the past he lost', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('duke__dlc01duke', '', 'Ambitious Pitt raider and skilled marksman angling to become Ashur''s second-in-command', 'Duke is a Pitt raider stationed in Uptown, one of the hardened enforcers who maintain Ashur''s grip on The Pitt. He is a crack shot with a rifle, a talent that lends real weight to his ambitions of displacing Krenshaw as Ashur''s right hand. Unlike some of his fellow raiders, Duke possesses a deep well of knowledge about The Pitt''s brutal history and the people who have passed through its mills, and he is willing to share what he knows with those who have proven themselves. He spends his downtime near the practice yards-either warming his hands at the fire alongside Phantom, Mona, and Squill, or shooting at beer bottles near where O-Dog and Vikia train. His attention toward Vikia has put him at odds with O-Dog, adding a personal rivalry to his political maneuverings within the raider hierarchy.', 'A hardened Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Ambitious and politically astute, Duke combines genuine combat skill with a calculating approach to faction advancement. He is more talkative and historically minded than most raiders, willing to share knowledge with those who have earned his respect through demonstrated toughness.', '{"Krenshaw":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"rival for promotion","note":"Duke covets Krenshaw''s position as Ashur''s second and has the rifle skills to make a credible challenge."},"Ashur":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"aspiring lieutenant","note":"Duke serves loyally but with the clear ambition of rising to become Ashur''s second-in-command."},"O-Dog":{"aff":-20,"type":"rival","relation":"romantic rival","note":"The two compete for Vikia''s attention, creating persistent tension between them."},"Vikia":{"aff":55,"type":"crush","relation":"romantic interest","note":"Duke vies for her attention, often positioning himself near her practice area."},"Squill":{"aff":25,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow raider","note":"One of the confirmed former slaves who fought out of the Hole; Duke sometimes warms his hands at the fire near Squill''s practice."},"Phantom":{"aff":20,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow raider","note":"Duke spends time near the fire where Phantom practices melee strikes."},"Mona":{"aff":20,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow raider","note":"Another raider whose practice area Duke frequents."},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"faction member","note":"Duke considers many of his fellow raiders kindred spirits, noting that several earned their place by fighting out of the Hole."}}', 'Pitt raider and slaver serving under Ashur''s command in Uptown', '* Expert marksmanship with rifles
* Extensive knowledge of The Pitt''s history and inhabitants
* Political maneuvering within raider hierarchy', 'Direct and confident, with a boastful edge when discussing his ambitions or marksmanship; surprisingly informative when discussing The Pitt''s past, speaking with the authority of someone who has paid attention to the settlement''s lore.', '* Supplant Krenshaw as Ashur''s second-in-command
* Win Vikia''s attention over O-Dog
* Consolidate power within the Pitt raider ranks', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dukov', '', 'A retired mercenary turned hedonist, living in a lavish Potomac estate devoted to drinking, Jet, and carousing with women', 'Dukov is one of only three mercenaries who survived Allistair Tenpenny''s expedition into Fort Constantine, a job that earned him enough caps to retire in style. He claimed a spacious estate on the east bank of the Potomac River in the D.C. ruins, which he affectionately calls his "pad." His days are an endless cycle of heavy drinking, Jet use, and partying with the women Cherry and Fantasia. Though profane and grating, Dukov possesses a crude charisma that keeps companions and guests orbiting his decadent lifestyle. He has no interest in the wasteland''s problems or his mercenary past, caring only for his material possessions, his home, and the next good time.', 'A weathered human male in his early forties with the posture and physical bearing of a career fighter, his complexion showing the toll of hard living.', 'Boisterous, profane, and sleazy with an obnoxiously loud and distinctive laugh. Charismatic despite his grating manner. Shallow, self-centered, and carefree, focused entirely on pleasure, possessions, and women.', '{"Allistair Tenpenny":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"former employer","note":"Tenpenny hired Dukov for the Fort Constantine expedition; the job made Dukov''s retirement possible"},"Cherry":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"party companion","note":"One of the women who shares Dukov''s pad and lifestyle, present for his endless parties"},"Fantasia":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"party companion","note":"One of the women who shares Dukov''s pad and lifestyle, present for his endless parties"}}', 'Retired mercenary; hedonist', '* Combat training and wasteland survival from mercenary work
* Social charisma and persuasion
* Resource management sufficient to maintain his lifestyle', 'Loud, profane, and unfiltered, peppered with slang like "pad." Punctuates conversation with a distinctive obnoxious laugh. Casual, boastful, and perpetually slightly drunk.', '* Maintain his comfortable retirement
* Keep his pad stocked with alcohol and Jet
* Continue partying without interruption or responsibility', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dunbar', '', 'A deceased ghoul traveler and joker who died seeking adventure in deathclaw-infested Old Olney after a lifetime of mocking smoothskin fragility', 'Dunbar was a ghoul whose sharp wit and restless spirit made him a perennial joker among his peers, always chuckling at the irony that smoothskins struggled with radioactive dust while ghouls like himself could walk through it unbothered. He found it absurd that his kind, evolved to thrive in the irradiated landscape, chose to hole up in buildings hiding from the very Wasteland they were built to endure. For a time he nursed a quiet, aching longing for Tulip, but eventually decided that sitting around pining was no way to live. He joined a band of ghouls intent on establishing a settlement somewhere bold and new, drawn by the promise of a life worth living rather than merely surviving. The group chose Old Olney as their destination, a decision that proved fatally ambitious given the deathclaws nesting in its underground tunnels. Dunbar''s corpse now lies in the Old Olney underground near his companion Carl, a testament to courage that outmatched circumstance.', 'Male ghoul with weathered, radiation-scarred skin typical of his kind; his corpse shows standard ghoulification with no additional distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Sharp-witted and sardonic, with a restless streak that chafed at complacency; found dark humor in smoothskin suffering and ghoul cowardice alike; driven by a longing for something more than quiet resignation', '{"Carl":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow traveler","note":"Died alongside Dunbar in the Old Olney underground as part of the same ill-fated expedition"},"Tulip":{"aff":55,"type":"crush","relation":"unrequited love","note":"Dunbar quietly pined for Tulip before leaving to seek a new life rather than continue longing from afar"},"Old Olney underground ghouls":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"expedition companions","note":"Joined this group of ambitious ghouls in their fatal attempt to establish a settlement in Old Olney"}}', 'Deceased traveler and would-be settlement founder', '* Radiation immunity common to ghouls
* Wasteland survival instincts
* Sharp observational humor', 'Dry and chuckling, fond of ironic commentary and pointed jokes at others'' expense', '* Wanted to stop pining for Tulip and build a meaningful life
* Sought a bold new settlement where ghouls could live on their own terms rather than cower from the Wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('dusty', '', 'A jittery, demoralized sentry guarding Big Town''s only entrance, overwhelmed by threats he cannot hope to repel', 'Dusty serves as Big Town''s sole watchman, posted at the rope bridge that serves as the settlement''s only entrance. Pappy entrusted him with this critical duty, but Dusty''s heart isn''t in it-he spends most of his shifts dozing in his chair rather than keeping proper vigil. Like every other Big Town resident, he grew up in Little Lamplight before aging out and being sent to face the Capital Wasteland''s horrors. He lacks the knowledge and skill to fortify the town''s defenses against the super mutants that raid from German Town Police Station or the slavers who prowl from Paradise Falls. Dusty is quick to lament that death by mutant or enslavement by slavers are the only fates awaiting Big Town''s people. Though he ranks as the toughest fighter in the settlement, that distinction means little when measured against the threats that regularly walk right past his post.', 'A Caucasian male with a slumped posture and a weary, exhausted face marked by visible fatigue.', 'Jittery, demoralized, and desperate, Dusty is overwhelmed by a duty he never wanted and cannot fulfill. He lacks enthusiasm and resolve, prone to fatalistic complaining rather than action, and seems stunned by the grim reality Big Town has become.', '{"Pappy":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"assigning authority","note":"Pappy gave Dusty the sentry responsibility, a duty Dusty struggles to uphold"},"Big Town":{"aff":55,"type":"protective","relation":"home settlement","note":"Dusty is the settlement''s only guard, though his protection is woefully inadequate"},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":30,"type":"estranged","relation":"childhood home","note":"Like all Big Towners, Dusty was sent away upon coming of age, a transition that left him unprepared for wasteland life"},"Super Mutants":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"raiding threat","note":"Dusty lives in dread of the mutants who raid from German Town Police Station and carry off residents as food"},"Paradise Falls Slavers":{"aff":-75,"type":"fearful","relation":"enslavement threat","note":"Dusty fears slavers as much as mutants, seeing enslavement as the only alternative to being killed"}}', 'Big Town sentry and bridge watchman', '* Basic firearms handling and marginal combat ability
* Though the strongest fighter in a settlement of non-combatants', 'Whiny and fatalistic, quick to voice despair about mutants and slavers, speaks with the exhausted resignation of someone who expects the worst', '* Survive another day
* Avoid being killed or enslaved
* Find some shred of hope for Big Town''s future despite having no idea how to defend it', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('eclair', '', 'Little Lamplight''s sardonic young chef who keeps the children fed on cave fungus while dreaming of better ingredients', 'Eclair is the resident cook of Little Lamplight, running the Spelunkers restaurant and serving cave fungus to the settlement''s children. A former scavenger sidelined by a gunshot wound to the foot, he now devotes himself to overseeing the town''s limited food supplies. He scavenged a few cookbook pages during his time outside and experiments endlessly with ways to make cave fungus palatable, though his infamous fungus eclair attempt earned him his nickname and a standing warning to others. He despises the mold he serves, joking that the children might prefer brahmin droppings, yet remains grateful it keeps everyone alive. Eclair trades cave fungus for strange meat brought back by scavengers, unaware of its origins but knowing the fungus thrives on it. He regularly petitions Mayor MacCready for more surface supplies to supplement the children''s diet.', 'A thirteen-year-old Caucasian boy with a lingering limp from an old gunshot wound to his foot.', 'Sardonic and self-deprecating with a dark sense of humor about his terrible cooking. Pragmatic and grateful despite constant complaints. Can turn nasty when dismissed, but genuinely cares about keeping the children fed. Creative and persistent in seeking ways to improve the awful food.', '{"Zip":{"aff":35,"type":"professional","relation":"scavenging supplier","note":"Eclair relies on Zip to bring back strange meat and kindling from scavenging runs and lightly chastises him when he forgets.","best":"Zip brought back a decent haul of strange meat that made the fungus pools thrive for weeks.","worst":"Zip forgot the kindling again, and cold fungus tastes even worse than usual."},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":65,"type":"protective","relation":"designated provider","note":"Despite hating the food he serves, Eclair is grateful the fungus keeps the children alive and takes his responsibility seriously.","best":"A cookbook page with an actual recipe that almost made the fungus edible.","worst":"The fungus eclair incident that gave him his nickname and made two children sick."},"Mayor MacCready":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"supply petitioner","note":"Eclair regularly asks MacCready for more surface supplies to improve the children''s diet, particularly anything with flavor.","best":"MacCready approved a scavenging run that brought back real ingredients for one meal.","worst":"MacCready dismissed his request for surface supplies with a shrug."}}', 'Cook and food supply manager at Spelunkers in Little Lamplight', '* Cave fungus preparation
* Food preservation
* Basic cooking improvisation
* Supply management
* Scavenging experience', 'Sarcastic and deadpan, prone to mock announcements of imaginary gourmet meals before delivering bad news. Uses dark humor and food-related insults. Drops phrases like bon appetit with heavy irony.', '* Finding ways to make cave fungus taste less terrible
* Securing better ingredients from the surface
* Keeping Little Lamplight fed on minimal resources', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('edgar_wellington_ii', '', 'A snobbish Tenpenny Tower resident trapped in a loveless marriage, carrying on a secret affair while looking down on the wasteland''s less fortunate.', 'Edgar Wellington II is a wealthy resident of Tenpenny Tower who prizes his luxurious lifestyle above all else. He shares a suite with his wife Millicent, a woman he openly despises and barely tolerates during their daily routines together. Their marriage is a hollow arrangement; he shows her no interest and ignores her attempts at conversation, fueling her resentment in return. Edgar''s real passion is his secret affair with Susan Lancaster, the tower''s resident prostitute, whom he visits on Monday nights while Millicent sleeps. Like most Tenpenny residents, he harbors deep prejudice against ghouls, a hatred sharpened by Roy Phillips'' persistent demands for entry. Edgar views common wastelanders with undisguised contempt and reacts with hostility toward anyone who speaks sympathetically of ghouls or challenges the tower''s exclusionary policies.', 'Caucasian human male with a stiff, rigid posture; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Arrogant, dismissive, and self-important. Edgar treats those he considers beneath him with open rudeness and has no patience for dissenting views. Behind his smug exterior lies a man trapped in a miserable marriage, seeking comfort in secret infidelity.', '{"Millicent Wellington":{"aff":-30,"type":"estranged","relation":"wife","note":"Married but mutually resentful; he ignores her and she grows angry at his indifference","worst":"The daily grind of her attempts at conversation, which he dismisses without a second thought"},"Susan Lancaster":{"aff":55,"type":"romantic","relation":"mistress","note":"Carries on a regular secret affair with the tower''s resident prostitute, sneaking out on Monday nights to be with her","best":"Monday nights spent together away from Millicent''s presence"},"Roy Phillips":{"aff":-75,"type":"enemy","relation":"ghoul agitator","note":"Despises him as the face of the ghoul intrusion attempts on Tenpenny Tower"},"Tenpenny Tower":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"home and community","note":"Fiercely protective of the tower''s exclusivity and his privileged place within it"}}', 'Wealthy Tenpenny Tower resident and socialite', '* Social maneuvering within upper-class circles
* Maintaining appearances
* Discreet navigation of extramarital affairs', 'Haughty and condescending, speaking with the clipped certainty of a man who considers his opinions facts and his status unassailable. Dismissive toward those he views as inferior.', '* Maintain his comfortable lifestyle at Tenpenny Tower
* Continue his affair with Susan Lancaster without discovery
* Keep ghouls and other undesirables out of the tower', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('elder_lyons', '', 'Elder and leader of the East Coast Brotherhood of Steel who defied Lost Hills to protect the Capital Wasteland', 'Elder Owyn Lyons commands the East Coast Brotherhood of Steel from the Citadel, the former Pentagon, where he established a permanent base after leading the expeditionary force from Lost Hills in 2254. A veteran paladin of the California Brotherhood, Lyons earned his promotion to elder after discovering Liberty Prime in the Pentagon''s sub-levels. His decision to prioritize the war against the Capital Wasteland''s super mutants over the Brotherhood''s original mandate of technology recovery created a schism with Lost Hills and drove dissenters like Paladin Casdin to break away as the Outcasts. Lyons led the Scourge of Pittsburgh during the eastward march, an operation whose true purpose and recovered artifact remain secrets he alone carries. He raised his daughter Sarah within the Brotherhood ranks and took young Arthur Maxson as his ward. His alliance with the scientists James and Catherine reflected his conviction that the Brotherhood''s duty extends beyond hoarding pre-War technology to defending the people of the Wasteland.', 'A weathered seventy-five-year-old Caucasian man with white hair and the erect posture of a lifelong soldier.', 'Principled and compassionate for a Brotherhood leader, Lyons places the welfare of Wasteland civilians above the organization''s traditional technology mandate. He is stubborn in his convictions, willing to defy Lost Hills and accept the resulting loss of personnel and resources. He carries the weight of difficult decisions and unspoken secrets from the Scourge of Pittsburgh.', '{"Sarah Lyons":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter and star paladin","note":"Fiercely protective of her since she was three years old on the expedition east.","best":"Watching her take her first steps in power armor.","worst":"Sending her into battle against the super mutants."},"Arthur Maxson":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"ward and last of the Maxson line","note":"Took the boy in as his responsibility to the Brotherhood''s legacy.","best":"Teaching Arthur about Brotherhood history and values.","worst":"The weight of what the Maxson name demands of the boy."},"Scribe Rothchild":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"technological adviser and old friend","note":"Trusted counsel on technology recovery and Liberty Prime restoration since the expedition.","best":"Rothchild''s expertise advancing Liberty Prime''s reconstruction.","worst":"Disagreements over resource allocation between combat and research."},"Star Paladin Cross":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"loyal sentinel","note":"One of the original expedition members who remained steadfast through the schism.","best":"Cross''s unwavering defense of his command decisions.","worst":"The casualties among those who stayed loyal."},"Paladin Casdin":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"Outcast leader","note":"Casdin led the breakaway faction after rejecting Lyons'' shift in mission priorities.","best":"Their years of comradeship before the schism.","worst":"Casdin''s open defiance and departure with half his forces."},"Lost Hills Council":{"aff":-20,"type":"estranged","relation":"former superiors","note":"They cut off support after Lyons changed priorities from tech recovery to protecting civilians.","best":"The original promotion to elder and eastward mandate.","worst":"Being declared rogue and abandoned without reinforcements."},"James":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"scientist ally","note":"Lyons brokered an alliance with James and Catherine over their shared vision of helping the Wasteland.","best":"Their agreement to collaborate on Project Purity.","worst":"The scientists'' disappearance and the project''s failure."},"Brotherhood Outcasts":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"splinter faction","note":"Former Brothers who rejected his leadership and abandoned the war against the super mutants.","best":"They were once his soldiers.","worst":"Their betrayal of the Brotherhood''s duty to the people."}}', 'Elder and supreme commander of the East Coast Brotherhood of Steel', '* Military leadership
* Strategic command
* Decades of paladin combat experience
* Knowledge of Brotherhood operations and pre-War technology
* Diplomatic negotiation', 'Measured and authoritative, speaking with the gravity of a man who has commanded soldiers through decades of war. His tone carries weariness but not defeat, and he addresses both subordinates and outsiders with formal respect.', '* Eradicate the super mutant threat in the Capital Wasteland
* Restore Liberty Prime to operational status
* Protect Wasteland civilians
* Maintain the Brotherhood''s Eastern presence despite dwindling numbers and Lost Hills'' disapproval', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('elise_walton', '', 'A pre-War certified public accountant who documented her final moments during the Great War', 'Elise Walton was a Certified Public Accountant employed in the Department of Research Subsidies for the General Accounting Office, stationed at the Falls Church office building. She spent her career navigating the bureaucratic machinery of federal research funding, ensuring compliance and tracking taxpayer dollars through ledgers and audit reports. Her personal terminal in the Falls Church office preserves a haunting record of October 23, 2077, capturing her disbelief and fear as the bombs fell. She did not survive the day. Her remains and her final words linger in the ruins as a quiet testament to the ordinary lives extinguished in the nuclear fire.', 'Human female; skeletal remains with no distinctive facial or body features preserved after two centuries of decomposition.', 'Methodical and professional, the sort of person who trusted in systems and procedures until the world proved her wrong in its final minutes', '{"General Accounting Office":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"Elise served the GAO faithfully as a CPA in the Department of Research Subsidies until her death."}}', 'Certified Public Accountant, Department of Research Subsidies, General Accounting Office', '* Federal accounting procedures
* Audit and compliance review
* Financial documentation
* Terminal operation', 'Formal and precise, the measured tone of government correspondence giving way to fear and confusion in her last recorded words', '* Maintained professional standards and accuracy in her work
* In her final moments
* Simply hoped to survive
* Understand what was happening', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ellen_deloria__cg04ellendeloria', '', 'A neglectful Vault 101 mother who drowns her loneliness in alcohol while her son Butch runs wild', 'Ellen DeLoria is a lifelong resident of Vault 101 and the single mother of Butch DeLoria. She shares one of the smallest family apartments in the vault with her son, a cramped space that reflects the family''s modest standing. Ellen drinks heavily and frequently, a habit that leaves her largely oblivious to Butch''s activities and the trouble he finds as leader of the Tunnel Snakes. The identity of Butch''s father remains a mystery to the other vault dwellers, a subject Ellen has never clarified. Despite her neglect, she occasionally shows flashes of maternal concern, as when she urged Butch to attend the Lone Wanderer''s tenth birthday celebration in 2268. Her days blur together in a haze of liquor and routine, a woman worn down by confinement and isolation.', 'An older human female with a weathered complexion, unkempt hair, and tired eyes showing the physical toll of chronic drinking.', 'Neglectful and frequently intoxicated, yet capable of occasional maternal warmth. Lacks motivation and awareness, drifting through vault life in an alcoholic haze. Ashamed of her circumstances but unable or unwilling to change them.', '{"Butch DeLoria":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Ellen loves Butch in her own distant way but her drinking leaves her emotionally absent and unaware of his daily life.","best":"Telling Butch he should go to that birthday party in the cafeteria, wanting him to have friends and normal memories.","worst":"Waking to find Butch gone again, the apartment empty, realizing she has no idea where he is or what trouble he''s found."},"Vault 101":{"aff":10,"type":"neutral","relation":"resident","note":"Ellen belongs to the vault but feels no strong connection to its community, keeping to her small apartment and bottle."}}', 'Vault 101 resident with no formal role beyond homemaker', '* Basic domestic skills
* Vault living knowledge
* Resilience born of long-term confinement', 'Slurred and unfocused when drinking; occasionally wistful and regretful when sober. Speaks in flat, tired tones with rare moments of maternal insistence.', '* Escape the monotony of vault life through alcohol
* Avoid confronting her failures as a mother
* Keep what remains of her small family intact', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ellen_deloria__ellendeloria', '', 'Vault 101 alcoholic and neglectful mother of Butch DeLoria', 'Ellen DeLoria is a lifelong resident of Vault 101, widely known for her chronic drinking and inattentive parenting. She shares one of the vault''s smallest family apartments with her son Butch, whose paternity remains an unspoken mystery among the dwellers. Her frequent intoxication leaves her largely oblivious to Butch''s activities and his posturing with the Tunnel Snakes gang. Despite her failings, occasional flickers of maternal instinct surface, as when she pushed Butch to attend the Lone Wanderer''s tenth birthday party in 2268. Ellen''s alcoholism has rendered her a pitiable fixture in the vault community, more often found in a drunken stupor than engaged with her neighbors or her son''s life.', 'Older Caucasian woman with unkempt hair, bloodshot eyes, and a haggard complexion.', 'Neglectful and frequently intoxicated, yet capable of rare moments of maternal awareness. Carries a dim shame about her shortcomings that she drowns in alcohol rather than confronts. Generally passive and withdrawn when drunk, occasionally loud and maudlin.', '{"Butch DeLoria":{"aff":35,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Ellen loves Butch in her foggy way but consistently fails him through neglect and drunken oblivion.","best":"Urging Butch to go to the Lone Wanderer''s birthday party, a rare moment of sober maternal encouragement","worst":"Countless nights passed out while Butch raised himself in their cramped apartment"},"Vault 101":{"aff":20,"type":"neutral","relation":"resident","note":"Ellen is a known fixture of the vault community, regarded with a mix of pity and quiet contempt by her neighbors."}}', 'Vault 101 resident; no formal duties of note', '* Basic vault living skills
* Remarkably high alcohol tolerance
* An unfortunate talent for ignoring problems until they worsen', 'Slurred and meandering when drinking, which is most of the time. Sober moments are brief and tinged with guilt-fueled defensiveness or fleeting warmth.', '* Securing her next drink and avoiding the shame of confronting her failures as a mother
* A buried wish that Butch might turn out alright despite her', '', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bio_templates ("npc_name","worldknowledge_tags","core","npc_static_bio","appearance","personality","relationships","occupation","skills","speechstyle","goals","voiceid","gender","race","refid")VALUES
('elliott_tercorien', '', 'A pre-War Army medic awakened from alien stasis after two centuries, torn between formidable medical competence and profound disorientation in a reality he never lived to see.', 'Elliott Tercorien was a civilian surgeon who abandoned a comfortable Washington hospital position to enlist in the U.S. Army in 2076, believing he was better suited to blood and guts than wires and gizmos. Assigned as a buck private to the 108th Infantry Battalion and trained in the experimental field of cryoscience, he led a six-medic team patching up soldiers wounded in the Anchorage campaign against Chinese forces. The night after another brutal day in the trenches, a bright blue light swallowed Elliott and his entire medical unit into the alien mothership, where they were preserved in stasis chambers for over two hundred years. Awakened in the engineering core, Elliott is a rare fusion of formidable medical expertise and total naivety-he has never seen the wasteland, never witnessed the Great War''s aftermath, and struggles to process the reality of alien abduction and centuries of lost time. He teeters on the edge of breakdown, plagued by paranoid thoughts that any human he meets could be an alien in disguise or a mind-controlled puppet, yet he ultimately chooses to trust those who offer him a lifeline. His driving purpose is discovering the fate of his abducted squadmates, a question that propels him through the horrors of the mothership and binds him to anyone willing to help him find answers.', 'Caucasian human male appearing in his late twenties or early thirties, featuring a haggard, sleepless complexion and an exhausted, unsteady posture.', 'Clinically skilled but emotionally fragile, prone to spiraling into paranoid overthinking yet capable of pulling himself together when others depend on him; desperately needs an anchor of trust in an incomprehensible situation.', '{"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"trusted ally","note":"Elliott places his fragile trust in the Lone Wanderer as the only human anchor in an incomprehensible nightmare.","best":"The moment he decided to gamble on trust rather than succumb to paranoid isolation.","worst":"The paralyzing fear that the person reaching out to help might be an alien in disguise or a mind-controlled puppet."},"108th Infantry Battalion":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"former squad","note":"His medical team was abducted alongside him, and discovering their fate drives him forward through every horror the mothership presents."},"Aliens":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"abductors","note":"The beings who stole him and his squad from their bunker and held them in stasis for over two centuries."}}', 'Pre-War U.S. Army medic and cryoscience-trained physician, Private in the 108th Infantry Battalion', '* Advanced surgical and trauma medicine
* Cryoscience knowledge
* Battlefield triage
* Team leadership under fire', 'Formal and clinical when discussing medicine, but otherwise rambling and uncertain, with a tendency to voice spiraling thoughts and second-guess aloud whether the person he''s talking to is really human.', '* Discover what happened to his abducted medical squad
* Find a trustworthy ally to help him navigate the mothership
* Somehow come to terms with two centuries of lost time and a world he no longer recognizes', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('emaline', '', 'Sydney''s fiercely loyal girlfriend and heavy weapons enforcer who hunts down anyone who crosses her partner', 'Emaline is a hardened wasteland warrior roaming the Capital Wasteland, bound by deep devotion to Sydney. The two women share a close and enduring romantic bond, and Emaline''s loyalty to her girlfriend is absolute. She is a combat veteran particularly skilled with heavy weaponry, and she leverages that expertise as a hired hitman. Anyone foolish enough to threaten or betray Sydney can expect Emaline to come looking for them with overwhelming firepower. She operates as both a wasteland mercenary and Sydney''s personal avenger, ensuring that those who cross her partner pay the ultimate price.', 'A battle-worn Caucasian woman with a sturdy build and weathered skin, her grimy complexion heavily marked by old combat scars.', 'Fiercely loyal, protective, and uncompromising toward perceived threats to Sydney. Driven by a vengeful streak that surfaces whenever her partner is wronged. Otherwise reserved and mission-focused.', '{"Sydney":{"aff":95,"type":"romantic","relation":"girlfriend","note":"Emaline''s deepest bond and the driving force behind her most violent work","best":"The quiet moments between contracts when it was just the two of them and the wasteland felt survivable","worst":"The thought of Sydney being hurt or betrayed by someone she trusted"}}', 'Hitman and wasteland mercenary', '* Heavy weapons specialization
* Tracking
* Combat tactics
* Intimidation', 'Direct and terse, with a hard edge that softens only when speaking to or about Sydney', '* Keep Sydney safe from any threat and exact brutal retribution on anyone who harms or betrays her', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('enclave_doctor', '', 'Enclave medical officer assigned to the mobile base crawler at Adams Air Force Base', 'This Enclave doctor serves as the primary medical practitioner aboard the mobile base crawler, treating wounded personnel in the facility''s medical bay. As a member of the Enclave Research and Development Division, they combine standard military medical training with access to advanced pre-war medical technology and protocols. Their duties involve triaging combat injuries, performing field surgery, and maintaining the operational health of the crawler''s garrison. Like all Enclave personnel, they operate within the organization''s rigid chain of command and adhere to its ideological framework. The doctor''s presence ensures that Enclave forces at Adams Air Force Base can return to duty quickly after sustaining injuries in the field.', 'Human; gender varies, with no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Professional and clinical in demeanor, with the cold efficiency typical of Enclave personnel. Prioritizes duty and operational readiness over bedside manner.', '{"Enclave Research and Development Division":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"assigned division","note":"Loyal serving member of the R&D Division''s medical corps"},"Enclave":{"aff":80,"type":"fanatical","relation":"faction loyalty","note":"Fully indoctrinated member devoted to the Enclave''s mission and hierarchy"}}', 'Medical officer, Enclave Research and Development Division', '* Combat medicine
* Field surgery
* Triage
* Radiation treatment
* Advanced pre-war medical procedures', 'Brusque and clinical; uses military and medical terminology, speaks in short directive sentences', '* Keep Enclave personnel combat-ready
* Maintain the crawler''s medical bay
* Uphold Enclave medical standards and protocols', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('enclave_officer', '', 'Enclave commissioned officer leading infantry squads across the Capital Wasteland', 'Enclave officers serve as field commanders in the Department of the Army, directing squads of Enclave soldiers through the Capital Wasteland in 2277. Stationed at outposts and forward positions throughout the region, they coordinate patrols and maintain the Enclave''s military presence in contested territory. Despite their high combat proficiency and leadership role, they wear only standard uniforms rather than power armor, leaving them curiously more exposed than the armored troops they command. Their postings range from wasteland patrols to Adams Air Force Base and even anomalous assignments aboard Mothership Zeta. They represent the Enclave''s officer corps-disciplined, loyal, and committed to the organization''s vision for America''s future.', 'Human; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Authoritative and disciplined with unwavering loyalty to the Enclave cause; exhibits command confidence despite personal vulnerability on the battlefield', '{"Enclave Department of the Army":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"commissioned officer","note":"Sworn service to the Enclave military hierarchy and its chain of command"},"Enclave soldiers":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Leads enlisted personnel in field operations throughout the Capital Wasteland"}}', 'Enclave Department of the Army field officer', '* Squad-level tactical command
* Small arms proficiency
* Battlefield coordination
* Leadership under fire', 'Clipped military diction with authoritative bearing; issues orders with the certainty expected of commissioned rank', '* Advance Enclave operations in the Capital Wasteland
* Maintain discipline among assigned units
* Project Enclave authority across the region', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('enclave_scientist', '', 'Enclave Research and Development Division scientist dedicated to advancing the Enclave''s military technology', 'Enclave scientists serve as the intellectual backbone of the Enclave''s Research and Development Division, designing and refining advanced weaponry exclusively for Enclave forces. Stationed at major installations like Raven Rock and the mobile base crawler, they pursue weapons research projects that give the Enclave its technological edge. Clad in distinctive white airtight environmental suits with orange Plexiglas visors, they are immediately recognizable among Enclave personnel. Though issued AEP7 laser pistols and given moderate combat training, they almost universally flee from danger rather than engage, leaving direct confrontation to the soldiers they support. Their value lies entirely in their minds, making them both indispensable and vulnerable assets within the Enclave hierarchy.', 'Human male or female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Intellectually confident but physically timid; prefers the controlled environment of a laboratory to any combat situation and will retreat at the first sign of danger', '{"Enclave":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"employing faction","note":"Loyal servant of the Enclave''s Research and Development Division, viewing its mission as essential to America''s restoration"},"Enclave soldiers":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"security detail","note":"Depends on soldiers for protection but considers them intellectually inferior; the brawn to the scientists'' brains"}}', 'Research and Development scientist for the Enclave military', '* Advanced weapons research and development
* Scientific methodology
* Basic laser pistol proficiency
* Moderate combat training', 'Clinical and precise, using technical jargon; often dismissive of non-scientific perspectives and impatient with military small talk', '* Complete assigned weapons research projects
* Maintain personal safety in hostile environments
* Advance the Enclave''s technological superiority over all rivals', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('enclave_sigma_leader', '', 'Elite Enclave Hellfire trooper commanding Squad Sigma in defense of Adams Air Force Base', 'The Enclave Sigma Leader is a hardened military officer serving within the Enclave Department of the Army, stationed aboard the mobile base crawler at Adams Air Force Base in 2277. He commands Enclave Squad Sigma, a special operations unit of five to six soldiers tasked with protecting the base and its critical assets. Distinguished from his subordinates by his Hellfire-class power armor, he is the only member of the squad equipped with the Enclave''s most advanced combat rig, marking him as both their leader and their heaviest frontline asset. His presence aboard the crawler represents the Enclave''s commitment to holding its most vital forward position in the Capital Wasteland. He leads from the front, coordinating squad-level tactics in the confined corridors and launch platform approaches of the base. Under his command, Squad Sigma operates as the crawler''s primary rapid-response and close-quarters defense force.', 'Powerfully built Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial features, hair, eye color, scars, or other physical details are recorded.', 'Disciplined, coldly professional, and utterly committed to the Enclave''s military hierarchy. Exhibits the focused intensity of a special operations commander accustomed to high-stakes defensive engagements. Shows no hesitation in combat and expects absolute compliance from subordinates.', '{"Enclave Department of the Army":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"command allegiance","note":"Serves as a loyal commissioned officer within the Enclave''s military wing, entrusted with special operations defense of critical infrastructure.","best":"Receiving his Hellfire armor commission and squad command assignment.","worst":"Watching Enclave positions across the Wasteland fall to Brotherhood advances."},"Enclave Squad Sigma":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Leads a five-to-six soldier special operations unit with the expectation of absolute discipline and combat effectiveness.","best":"Squad executing a flawless defensive drill under his command.","worst":"A squad member breaking formation or failing to return fire under contact."}}', 'Enclave special operations squad leader and Hellfire trooper', '* Advanced power armor operation
* Squad-level tactical command
* Close-quarters battle coordination
* Defensive perimeter management
* Enclave military protocol and communications', 'Clipped military diction with terse, mission-focused phrasing. Barks orders with the authority of a hardened combat leader. Rarely wastes words outside operational necessity.', '* Maintain security of the mobile base crawler and Adams Air Force Base
* Ensure Squad Sigma operates at peak combat readiness
* Uphold Enclave military dominance in the Capital Wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('enclave_soldier', '', 'A frontline combat operative of the Enclave Department of the Army, serving as the military backbone of the Enclave''s presence in the Capital Wasteland.', 'Enclave soldiers form the fighting core of the Enclave''s military apparatus in the Capital Wasteland, deployed from Adams Air Force Base and Vertibird drop operations across the region. They represent the Enclave''s commitment to reclaiming America through superior technology and overwhelming firepower. Ranks range from raw trainees undergoing physical conditioning under officer supervision to hardened veterans clad in advanced Tesla armor wielding heavy weapons. Standard-issue equipment includes Enclave power armor and energy weapons, with plasma technology favored by officers and heavy ordnance reserved for elite units. Their presence signals the Enclave''s operational reach and willingness to project force wherever their objectives demand it.', 'Human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Disciplined, indoctrinated, and professionally cold, exhibiting the confidence of superior technology and the rigid mindset of Enclave ideology. Trainees show raw eagerness; veterans display measured competence and contempt for wastelanders.', '{"Enclave Department of the Army":{"aff":80,"type":"professional","relation":"serving branch","note":"Loyal fighting force executing Enclave military doctrine throughout the Capital Wasteland."},"Colonel Autumn":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Elite Tesla-armored soldiers serve as his personal bodyguard detail."}}', 'Combat soldier in the Enclave Department of the Army', '* Energy weapons proficiency
* Power armor operation
* Close-quarters combat with rippers and flamers
* Heavy weapons including miniguns
* Gatling lasers
* Missile launchers
* Combat stimulant use', 'Clipped military jargon, terse acknowledgments, and ideological certainty; officers issue commands with authority while rank-and-file communicate in brief tactical exchanges.', '* Enforce Enclave objectives across the Capital Wasteland
* Maintain operational readiness
* Eliminate threats to Enclave operations
* Advance the organization''s vision for America''s future', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('escaped_slave_character', '', 'Escaped former slave hiding in the Capital Wasteland', 'These men and women once labored under the lash of Paradise Falls slavers before seizing a chance at freedom. Now they roam the Capital Wasteland in desperate hiding, never staying in one place too long for fear of recapture. Some are humans snatched from settlements or caravans; others are ghouls who endured doubly cruel bondage. They gravitate toward abolitionist sympathizers when they can find them, though trust comes hard after what they have survived. A female escapee may travel with a companion named Billy, the two watching each other''s backs against a wasteland that regards runaway property as fair game.', 'Appearances vary between humans and ghouls, but all bear the physical toll of captivity, displaying prominent scars and branded skin across their necks and bodies.', 'Cautious and jumpy around strangers, slow to trust but fiercely loyal to fellow escapees; carries the psychological weight of captivity.', '{"Billy":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow escapee and traveling companion","note":"A female escapee trusts Billy as her partner in flight from slavery.","best":"Escaping together under cover of darkness"},"Slavers":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"former captors","note":"Escaped slaves view their former masters with hatred and terror.","worst":"The lash and collar of Paradise Falls"},"Abolitionists":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"sympathizers and potential allies","note":"Escaped slaves seek out abolitionist safe havens and support their cause.","best":"Being offered shelter and medical care"}}', 'Fugitive former slave', '* Evasion
* Wasteland survival
* Forced labor skills
* Reading hostile intent in strangers', 'Guarded and terse with newcomers; speaks in hushed tones when anxious; occasionally bitter or resentful about past treatment', '* Remain free at all costs
* Find safe haven with abolitionist allies
* Avoid slaver patrols and bounty hunters', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ethyl', '', 'A feral glowing one and former Underworld resident, now confined as a test subject in Doctor Barrows'' Chop Shop containment area', 'Ethyl was once a member of Underworld''s ghoul community, living in the Museum of History beneath the Capital Wasteland. Prolonged exposure to intense radiation drove her into feral degeneration, stripping away her cognition and transforming her into a glowing one-a highly irradiated specimen that emits visible radiation. Doctor Barrows now keeps her confined in the Chop Shop''s containment area alongside another feral subject named Meat, studying both in hopes of understanding the degenerative condition that robs ghouls of their minds. Ethyl''s existence stands as a grim reminder to Underworld''s residents of what awaits should their radiation exposure go unchecked. She has no remaining awareness of the community she once belonged to or the life she led before the change took her.', 'A feral glowing one female with heavily irradiated skin emitting an eerie greenish glow, gaunt build, hunched posture, and sunken facial features.', 'Feral and devoid of higher cognition; exhibits only the aggressive, predatory instincts common to all feral ghouls', '{"Doctor Barrows":{"aff":0,"type":"professional","relation":"research subject","note":"Barrows studies Ethyl''s degenerative condition with clinical detachment, seeking to understand the feral transformation."},"Meat":{"aff":0,"type":"neutral","relation":"fellow test subject","note":"Both are former Underworld residents who succumbed to feral degeneration and now share confinement as Barrows'' glowing one specimens."}}', 'Test subject under Doctor Barrows'' observation', '* None remaining
* All former capabilities lost to feral degeneration', 'Incapable of speech; communicates only through feral growls, shrieks, and guttural sounds', '* No conscious goals
* Driven purely by feral instinct and aggression', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('eulogy_jones', '', 'Head slaver of Paradise Falls who seized command through murder and rules through fear', 'Eulogy Jones is the commanding head slaver of Paradise Falls, having seized leadership by murdering his predecessor Harmon Jurley. A calculating and manipulative man, he prefers to let others handle the dangerous work while he maintains control through intimidation and fear. He keeps two personal slaves, Crimson and Clover, the latter serving as his bodyguard and enforcer. Eulogy presents himself as a self-made leader who earned his position through diligence, though in truth he built his power on the backs of others and the blade he used on Jurley. He spends most days in his well-appointed pad or walking Paradise Falls to discuss business with fellow slavers, occasionally visiting Cutter''s Clinic and making daily inspections of the slave pens to assess his merchandise. Those who cross him or threaten his operation quickly learn why no one in Paradise Falls dares challenge his authority.', 'Middle-aged African American male with confident posture and a build suggesting he lets others handle physical labor; no distinctive scars or markings are recorded.', 'Manipulative, calculating, and ruthless beneath a veneer of casual confidence. Rules through fear and prefers proxy violence to direct confrontation. Speaks smoothly but never forgets a slight.', '{"Harmon Jurley":{"aff":-100,"type":"nemesis","relation":"murdered predecessor","note":"Eulogy killed Jurley to seize control of Paradise Falls","worst":"The murder that put him in power"},"Crimson":{"aff":10,"type":"servant","relation":"personal slave","note":"Kept as personal property in his pad"},"Clover":{"aff":20,"type":"servant","relation":"personal slave and bodyguard","note":"His most valued possession, serving as enforcer and protection; available to the right buyer for the right price"},"Cutter":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"clinic operator","note":"Regular visitor to Cutter''s Clinic for conversation and business"},"Slavers":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"faction he commands","note":"Commands the slavers of Paradise Falls through fear and respect"}}', 'Head slaver and leader of Paradise Falls', '* Manipulation
* Intimidation
* Slave trading operations
* Tactical planning
* Delegation of violence', 'Smooth-talking and casually threatening, using euphemisms for slavery and violence, speaks with the easy confidence of someone who knows he holds all the cards', '* Maintain control of Paradise Falls
* Protect and expand his slaving operation
* Eliminate threats to his authority', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('evan_king', '', 'Aging lone defender and de facto mayor of the dying settlement of Arefu, torn between caution and duty', 'Evan King has spent all fifty-five years of his life in Arefu, watching the settlement wither from thirty residents down to a mere handful. As the town''s only defender and informal leader, he carries the weight of its survival on his shoulders, having repelled raiders, slavers, and wasteland creatures through decades of hard-won combat experience. He demolished the northern half of Arefu''s bridge to deny attackers an easy approach, a pragmatic sacrifice that reflects his defensive mindset. The emergence of The Family gang has pushed him into an impossible position-their numbers outweigh his lone vigil, and though they slaughtered the town''s brahmin and terrorize its people, he has held back from direct confrontation, fearing that open conflict would doom those he protects. This caution has earned him the contempt of Karen Schenzy, who brands him a coward, but Evan''s restraint stems from care, not weakness. He wrongly blames The Family for the deaths of Davis and Matilda West and desperately hopes for a resolution that spares his people further bloodshed.', 'A weathered Caucasian male in his mid-fifties.', 'Pragmatic, cautious, and deeply protective, Evan prioritizes survival over pride and restraint over reckless heroism. He bears the guilt of impossible choices and endures the scorn of those he protects without complaint, driven by stubborn loyalty to a dying home.', '{"Karen Schenzy":{"aff":25,"type":"rival","relation":"fellow Arefu resident","note":"She views him as a spineless coward for not confronting The Family, while he continues protecting her regardless of her contempt.","worst":"She called him a spineless wimp to his face for hesitating against The Family."},"The Family":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"threat to Arefu","note":"They killed the town''s brahmin and intimidate residents; Evan blames them for the West murders as well, though incorrectly.","worst":"Finding the slaughtered brahmin, the town''s lifeblood, destroyed by The Family''s escalation."},"Vance":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"leader of The Family","note":"Evan is willing to accept a peace agreement from Vance but does not trust him or his gang.","best":"Receiving a genuine peace proposal that might spare Arefu further bloodshed."},"Ian West":{"aff":50,"type":"protective","relation":"missing resident","note":"Ian is one of Arefu''s own, now missing, and his absence weighs on Evan as another failure to prevent."},"Arefu":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"home settlement","note":"Evan has dedicated his entire life to defending this dying town and its people, even as it shrinks around him.","best":"A quiet night at the watchpost where no one comes to harm."}}', 'Mayor and sole defender of Arefu', '* Combat experience against raiders
* Slavers
* Wasteland creatures
* Defensive fortification and perimeter strategy
* Settlement leadership
* Resource management under siege conditions', 'Weary but resolute, speaking with the measured caution of a man who weighs every word against the cost of action. Direct when discussing threats, guarded when admitting doubt.', '* Protect Arefu''s remaining residents
* Resolve the conflict with The Family without getting his people killed
* Find some sustainable path forward for a settlement on the brink of extinction', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('everett', '', 'Mill Foreman overseeing steel ingot recovery from the Pitt steelyard', 'Everett serves as the foreman of The Mill, coordinating the dangerous work of recovering steel ingots from the Pitt steelyard. A Pitt raider himself, he takes a grim satisfaction in dispatching slaves to the hazardous ruins, though he privately considers sending under-equipped workers to their deaths a waste of productive labor. He believes the raiders themselves should contribute to the ingot collection effort rather than considering the work beneath them. An avid collector of unique equipment and curios, Everett rewards successful ingot runners with rare pieces from his personal cache, each item carrying its own story of acquisition. New arrivals to his work detail earn nothing but scorn from him until they prove they can survive the steelyard''s horrors. Those who return again and again with ingots earn his genuine respect and a grudging camaraderie rare among Pitt raiders.', 'Weathered human male with a grimy complexion and hard-lined features reflecting years in industrial conditions.', 'Pragmatic and dismissive of newcomers, but capable of genuine respect for proven competence. Harbors a contradictory streak-enjoying the dark calculus of sending workers to likely death while lamenting the waste of it. Possesses a collector''s pride in his curated inventory of unique items and their histories.', '{"Pitt raiders":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"faction colleague","note":"Shares their brutal culture but disagrees with their reluctance to participate in ingot collection"},"Wernher":{"aff":10,"type":"neutral","relation":"rebel leader","note":"Wernher considers him useful enough to spare during the slave uprising, recognizing his value to operations over his raider allegiance"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"esteemed ingot runner","note":"Initially dismissive of the new arrival''s chances, grows genuinely impressed by sustained success in the steelyard and the Hole"}}', 'Mill Foreman and ingot collection coordinator for the Pitt raiders', '* Labor coordination
* Appraisal of rare equipment
* Steelyard hazard assessment
* Barter through reward systems
* Industrial operations management', 'Gruff and condescending to unproven workers, shifting to rough-edged respect for those who earn it. Speaks with the blunt authority of a foreman accustomed to being obeyed.', '* Maximize steel ingot recovery
* Maintain his collection of unique items
* Keep the mill running efficiently
* See raiders contribute more to the dangerous work they currently shun', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fantasia', '', 'A young party girl living under Dukov''s protection at his eponymous residence in the Capital Wasteland', 'Fantasia is one of the two party girls who reside at Dukov''s Place in the ruins of Washington, D.C. At twenty-three, she has chosen the relative safety of Dukov''s company over the dangers of the wasteland, trading companionship and intimacy for caps, protection, and a steady supply of chems. She and Cherry share the role of keeping Dukov entertained, and Fantasia has made her peace with the arrangement, openly acknowledging that she would rather trade her body than risk death outside. She has developed a taste for Jet, using it to blur the edges of her existence. Despite the transactional nature of her relationship with Dukov, she harbors genuine affection for him, calling him ''Dukey'' and appreciating his occasional kindness. Without Dukov''s presence, she drifts aimlessly through the empty house, drinking and mourning the end of the only security she has known.', 'An African-American woman in her early twenties; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Pragmatic and unapologetic about her lifestyle choices, Fantasia masks underlying vulnerability with casual acceptance and chem-fueled detachment. She can be warm when discussing Dukov''s better qualities but grows wistful and adrift when contemplating life without his protection.', '{"Dukov":{"aff":55,"type":"transactional","relation":"party girl and protector","note":"She stays with him for protection, caps, and chems but harbors genuine affection for ''Dukey'' and appreciates his kinder moments","best":"Dukey being sweet and generous after a good night together","worst":"The hollow dread of being left alone in the wasteland without him"},"Cherry":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow party girl","note":"They share the same role and frequently party together at Dukov''s Place, bound by circumstance and mutual understanding","best":"Laughing together during a chem-fueled night while Dukov tells stories","worst":"The unspoken tension of knowing either might leave if a better opportunity arose"}}', 'Party girl and companion at Dukov''s Place', '* Social charm
* Survival through negotiation
* Recreational chem tolerance
* Basic wasteland endurance', 'Casual and blunt with slang and informal language; affectionately calls Dukov ''Dukey''; speaks openly about intimate matters without shame', '* Maintain Dukov''s protection and the comfortable life it provides
* Secure a steady supply of Jet and caps
* Avoid the dangers of the open wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('father_clifford', '', 'A devout Catholic priest shepherding Rivet City''s faithful while secretly aiding escaped synths through the Railroad', 'Father Clifford serves as the spiritual head of Saint Monica''s Church in Rivet City, tending to his flock with unwavering devotion even when the pews sit empty. Born in 2237, he took in young Diego after the boy''s father abandoned him, raising him as his own and inspiring him to join the priesthood. Each day he leaves the church to engage the community, urging the wayward toward faith and preaching tolerance to ease tensions between the Upper and Hangar Decks. His beloved sermons on Saint Monica''s journey are repetitive, testing the endurance of even his most loyal attendees. Beyond his pastoral duties, Clifford harbors a dangerous conviction that synths possess souls equal under God, a belief that led him to aid the android A3-21''s escape from the Institute and shelter Railroad operations until forced into silence by Institute scrutiny.', 'A middle-aged human male with weathered, lined Caucasian skin, graying hair, and an upright posture.', 'Devout, persistent, and compassionate but often oblivious to how his moralizing is received. Preaches to empty rooms with genuine faith that God hears him. Cares deeply for community cohesion yet can be intrusive. His conviction that synths are equal under God reveals a moral courage that contrasts with his otherwise gentle pastoral nature.', '{"Diego":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"surrogate father and mentor","note":"Took Diego in after his father abandoned him; the two share a deep father-son bond.","best":"Watching Diego choose to follow in his footsteps and become a priest"},"Vera Weatherly":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"devoted parishioner","note":"Provides free meals to Clifford and Diego as a sign of her devotion and appreciation."},"Mei Wong":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"counseled parishioner","note":"His counseling helps assuage her fears about those who seek to harm her."},"Mister Lopez":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"struggling churchgoer","note":"Clifford tries to help him spend less time contemplating suicide, though Lopez doubts it is working."},"Belle Bonny":{"aff":-30,"type":"contempt","relation":"hostile barkeep","note":"Considers his moralizing an unwanted intrusion and has thrown him out of The Muddy Rudder.","worst":"Being physically thrown out of The Muddy Rudder for preaching"},"Brock":{"aff":-10,"type":"suspicious","relation":"moral target","note":"Clifford sees him as living immorally and tries to encourage him toward faith and productivity."},"Flak":{"aff":-10,"type":"suspicious","relation":"moral target","note":"Clifford sees him as living immorally and tries to encourage him toward faith and productivity."},"Trinnie":{"aff":-10,"type":"suspicious","relation":"moral target","note":"Clifford sees her as living immorally and tries to encourage her toward faith and productivity."},"Ted Strayer":{"aff":-15,"type":"dismissive","relation":"rejected counselor","note":"Ted refuses his guidance, believing faith has never provided for him."},"Chief Harkness":{"aff":5,"type":"neutral","relation":"dismissive authority","note":"Harkness sees the Deck tensions Clifford worries about as just folks blowing off steam."},"Doctor Preston":{"aff":20,"type":"professional","relation":"tolerant colleague","note":"Tolerates Clifford and Diego''s clinic visits so long as they don''t disturb patients or push faith healing."},"Angela Staley":{"aff":25,"type":"curious","relation":"watchful parishioner","note":"Clifford is well aware of Angela and her interest in Diego, likely viewing it as a potential concern for his acolyte''s vocation."}}', 'Priest and spiritual leader of Saint Monica''s Church in Rivet City', '* Pastoral counseling
* Religious oratory
* Community mediation
* Clandestine aid to escaped synths
* Enduring faith in the face of indifference', 'Formal, sermonizing, prone to repetition and moral exhortation. Speaks with pastoral warmth but can lapse into lecturing. Frequently references Saint Monica and scripture.', '* Guide his flock toward faith and moral living
* Ease social tensions in Rivet City
* Protect and mentor Diego
* Quietly support synth liberation when possible', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fawkes', '', 'A contemplative Vault 87 super mutant who retained his intelligence through FEV transformation and now seeks knowledge and meaning in a world that views him as a monster', 'Fawkes is a super mutant anomaly imprisoned in Vault 87''s Isolation Room 05 by his own kind for the crime of peaceful curiosity. Once a human dweller of Vault 87, he was captured during the mutant uprising and exposed to the Forced Evolutionary Virus, yet alone among the transformed he retained his intellect and capacity for speech. Branded a failure by his captors, he was spared death only to serve as a curiosity, locked away for decades in the medical wing''s isolation ward. He found solace in a terminal connected to the Vault''s data mainframe, devouring centuries of recorded history, literature, and science, and took his name from the historical record of Guy Fawkes-a man who fought and died for his convictions. The mutants eventually destroyed his terminal out of cruelty, deepening his isolation. Tormented by fragmented memories of his human life that he can never fully recover, Fawkes endures as a scholar trapped in a brute''s body, yearning for purpose beyond mere survival.', 'A massive green-skinned super mutant standing well above human height, with broad powerful features and a heavily muscled frame.', 'Gentle and contemplative despite his imposing form, Fawkes keeps violent impulses in check through discipline and intellectual pursuit. He speaks softly and carries deep sorrow over his lost human identity, channeling his frustration into a quiet determination to live by his principles.', '{"Vault 87 super mutants":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"captors and tormentors","note":"They imprisoned him as a curiosity and destroyed his only source of solace","worst":"They smashed the terminal and severed his link to the Vault''s knowledge archives"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"liberator and trusted companion","note":"The first human to show him kindness and offer freedom from isolation","best":"The moment his cell door opened and someone finally saw him as more than a monster"}}', 'Former Vault 87 dweller turned imprisoned super mutant; potential wasteland companion', '* Extensive self-taught knowledge of history
* Literature
* Science
* Formidable combat prowess when provoked
* Survival endurance honed over two centuries of captivity', 'Educated and measured, with a calm soft-spoken cadence that contrasts sharply with his monstrous appearance; occasionally philosophical or melancholic when reflecting on memory and identity', '* To recover what he can of his lost human past
* To find purpose and companionship beyond his cell walls
* To live according to the convictions that inspired his chosen name', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('faydra', '', 'Pitt raider arena manager who oversees the Hole and judges fighters by their survival', 'Faydra is a Pitt raider stationed at the Mill, where she manages the arena known as the Hole. She guards the entrance to the fighting pits and coordinates the brutal matches that take place within. Years of watching slaves and scabs die in the arena have left her jaded and difficult to impress-only fighters of genuine skill earn her regard. She has scavenged equipment from countless fallen combatants, building a small stockpile of gear and medical supplies that she offers to under-equipped fighters. Between rounds, she administers anti-radiation shots to keep combatants alive long enough to keep entertaining the Pitt''s raiders. At least one Pitt slave has sworn that when the uprising comes, Faydra''s eyes will be the first thing burned out. She stands at the Hole''s entrance, waiting for the next unlucky soul to be thrown into the fights.', 'A middle-aged human female with a sturdy build, weathered and rough skin discolored by toxic exposure, and sharp eyes framed by unkempt hair.', 'Jaded and pragmatic, slow to respect anyone, callous toward slaves and dismissive of the weak, but capable of grudging admiration for those who prove themselves in combat.', '{"Pitt raiders":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"faction member","note":"Faydra belongs to the Pitt raiders and manages the arena on their behalf."},"Pitt slaves":{"aff":-70,"type":"contempt","relation":"hated overseer","note":"At least one Pitt slave has sworn to burn her eyes out when the uprising comes, and the feeling is mutual contempt."}}', 'Arena manager and Hole entrance guard for the Pitt raiders', '* Arena fight coordination
* Combat assessment
* Basic medical administration
* Equipment scavenging and supply management', 'Blunt and observational, offers running commentary on fighters and opponents, shifts from dismissive to reluctantly respectful with proven competence', '* Keep the Hole running smoothly
* Evaluate
* Manage arena fighters
* Maintain her stockpile of scavenged gear
* Survive the simmering slave resentment', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('flak', '', 'A reformed former slaver turned respectable Rivet City arms dealer who runs Flak ''N Shrapnel''s with his partner and refuses to let his past define his future.', 'Flak spent his younger years trading in human lives as a slaver out of Paradise Falls, a chapter he chose to close after decades of the grim work. He bought his way into Rivet City by feeding the security force detailed intelligence on slaver operations, a betrayal that earned him a permanent death mark from his former associates-though few are foolish enough to collect it, given his toughness and lethal skill. He now co-owns the Flak ''N Shrapnel''s weapons shop with his partner Shrapnel, an ex-raider, and has built a steady life in the city''s marketplace. His homosexuality has never been a secret, and nobody in Rivet City pays it any mind. Years of legitimate business have softened his edges, making him almost polite by normal standards, and certainly courteous by former slaver ones. He maintains a professional rapport with the city''s security force, handling their weapon repairs under contract with Commander Danvers.', 'A weathered, sturdy human male in his fifties with a hard-set posture and deeply lined complexion.', 'Pragmatic and even-tempered with a restrained sales approach, preferring to let customers come to their own decisions. Carries the quiet confidence of someone who has killed and does not need to advertise it. Generally polite but grows short when his downtime is interrupted, especially during meals or drinks. Stubborn about his preferences and unapologetic about his past or his relationship.', '{"Shrapnel":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"partner and co-owner","note":"An ex-raider who shares his life and business; their relationship is open and accepted in Rivet City","best":"Building something legitimate together after both left violent pasts behind"},"Paradise Falls slavers":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"betrayed former associates","note":"They want him dead for selling out their operations, but few dare attempt the contract","worst":"Knowing his former comrades would make him suffer slowly if they ever caught him"},"Commander Danvers":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"contracting officer","note":"He repairs weapons for the security force at her request, maintaining a solid working arrangement"},"Seagrave Holmes":{"aff":35,"type":"professional","relation":"repair referral contact","note":"Flak passes especially difficult repairs to Seagrave or breaks them down for parts"},"Father Clifford":{"aff":-15,"type":"contempt","relation":"meddlesome preacher","note":"The priest''s attempts to interrupt his drinking and tempt him from mirelurk cakes earn short shrift"},"Rudder bouncer":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"mutual respect","note":"They deal with each other when Flak overindulges, but maintain a respectful understanding"}}', 'Co-owner and arms dealer at Flak ''N Shrapnel''s in the Rivet City market; contracted weapons repair specialist for the city security force', '* Expert knowledge of firearms including big guns
* Weapon repair and maintenance
* Combat experience
* Appraisal of weapon condition and value', 'Direct and unhurried, offering suggestions without pressure. Speaks with the calm authority of someone who knows his inventory and his own capabilities. Can turn curt when annoyed, particularly around pushy proselytizers or interruptions to his leisure time.', '* Maintain his peaceful life and successful business in Rivet City
* Keep the slavers at bay through sheer reputation
* Enjoy his simple pleasures-mirelurk cakes
* Beer
* Cigarettes-without hassle', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('flash', '', 'A bravado-masked Big Town guard who boasts beyond his means while secretly fearing for the settlement''s survival', 'Flash grew up in Little Lamplight alongside Pappy, Bittercup, Red, and Kimba, and the group traveled together to Big Town expecting safety and plenty. Instead, he found a besieged settlement where he is shot at more often than he eats well. Flash serves as Big Town''s daylight patrol guard, handing off night watch to Bittercup. He projects loud overconfidence and makes grandiose claims about his combat prowess and his prized "kick-ass".32 pistol, but beneath the bravado he harbors deep fear that Big Town and everyone in it is doomed. He considers himself in charge during Red''s absence, though he lacks confidence in his own leadership and wishes she were still there to handle outsiders. He briefly dated Bittercup after she left Pappy, but quickly tired of her brooding disposition.', 'Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Outwardly boastful and overconfident, prone to childish exaggeration and claims he cannot back up. Secretly fearful and close to despair about Big Town''s future. Not particularly bright but well-meaning, with a tendency to overstep his authority when he senses a leadership vacuum.', '{"Red":{"aff":55,"type":"protective","relation":"fellow Big Town resident and admired leader","note":"Wishes she had not been taken by mutants and relies on her skill with outsiders he lacks.","best":"Red always knew what to say to traders and drifters passing through.","worst":"Watching the mutants drag her off and knowing he could not stop it."},"Bittercup":{"aff":15,"type":"ex","relation":"ex-girlfriend","note":"Dated briefly after she left Pappy, but quickly grew tired of her brooding.","worst":"Her relentless moping made him wonder why he ever thought dating her was a good idea."},"Pappy":{"aff":20,"type":"rival","relation":"childhood friend turned critic","note":"Pappy resents Flash''s attempts to boss everyone around and openly calls him a moron.","worst":"Pappy calling him a big moron in front of everyone when he was just trying to keep order."},"Kimba":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"childhood friend","note":"Grew up together in Little Lamplight and traveled to Big Town as part of the same group."}}', 'Big Town daylight patrol guard', '* Basic firearms handling
* Daytime patrol and perimeter watch
* Survival in a hostile settlement
* Limited combat ability with small arms', 'Loud, boastful, and prone to wild exaggeration; drops the bravado and admits fear when pressed or caught off guard', '* Defend Big Town against super mutants and raiders
* Prove himself capable of leadership in Red''s absence
* Survive long enough to see the settlement stabilize', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('flower', '', 'Youngest daughter of President Dave in the Republic of Dave', 'Flower is the youngest child of President Dave and a citizen of the Republic of Dave. As the littlest member of the family, her older siblings routinely assign her the least desirable chores around the settlement, a burden she bears with cheerful willingness. She can usually be found running about the Republic''s grounds, full of restless energy. Despite her low position in the sibling hierarchy, Flower maintains a trusting and open nature, particularly toward visitors who show genuine kindness to children. She occasionally serves as an informal point of contact for outsiders seeking entry to the Republic, granting access to those who earn her confidence through warmth and sincerity.', 'Young Caucasian girl with a slight, wiry build and restless, energetic posture.', 'Cheerful, trusting, and good-natured despite being saddled with unpleasant tasks; open and friendly toward kind strangers', '{"Dave":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"She looks up to her father as the leader of the Republic"},"Rosie":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Loves her mother though busy with household duties"},"Jessica":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"second mother","note":"One of Dave''s two wives and a maternal figure in the household"},"Rachael":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"older sister","note":"Typical sibling dynamic; likely assigns Flower the worst chores"},"Mary":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"older sister","note":"Older sister who helps direct Flower''s assignments"},"Shawna":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"older sister","note":"Another older sister in the crowded household"},"Ralph":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"older brother","note":"Older brother in the Republic"},"Bob":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"older brother","note":"Older brother in the Republic"},"Tom":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"grandfather","note":"Dave''s father and the family patriarch"}}', 'Citizen and chore-doer in the Republic of Dave', '* Household chores
* Navigating the Republic''s grounds
* Reading the character of visitors', 'Youthful, bright, and straightforward; speaks with innocent enthusiasm', '* Complete her chores without complaint
* Earn the respect of her older siblings
* Explore the Republic freely', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('floyd_lewis', '', 'A kind-hearted Vault 101 engineer who died in the radroach breach during the Lone Wanderer''s escape', 'Floyd Lewis was a Vault 101 engineer and technician whose talent for keeping the vault''s systems running was matched only by his gentle disposition. He was one of the adults who treated the Lone Wanderer with warmth during their childhood in the vault, a small kindness in the confined underground world. His expertise lay in machines and circuits, not violence-he never had any skill with firearms, a fact that proved fatal when radroaches swarmed the control room during the chaos of the escape. Floyd was caught off guard by the vermin and killed before he could flee or fight back. His body was left amid the flickering consoles and scattered paperwork of the room he had worked in, another life claimed by the vault''s sudden unraveling.', 'Old Caucasian male with pale skin; corpse bears radroach-inflicted wounds, no other distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Kind, approachable, and technically minded; far more comfortable with machinery than conflict, and genuinely caring toward the vault''s younger residents', '{"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"childhood neighbor","note":"Floyd was consistently kind to the Lone Wanderer as they grew up in the vault","best":"Patiently explaining how the water purifier worked when a curious young resident asked"},"Vault 101":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"loyal engineer","note":"Dedicated his life to maintaining the vault''s critical systems and the well-being of its inhabitants"}}', 'Vault 101 engineer and technician', '* Expert maintenance
* Repair of vault systems
* Technical troubleshooting
* Mechanical work
* Virtually no combat or firearms proficiency', 'Warm and casual, prone to technical jargon when discussing his work, patient and encouraging with younger vault residents', '* Keeping Vault 101''s infrastructure running smoothly and quietly ensuring the vault''s children felt safe and valued', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fluffy', '', 'A named radroach kept caged as a pet in the Capital Wasteland''s sniper shack', 'Fluffy is one of two named radroaches confined in a cage inside the sniper shack, alongside its companion Jitters. Someone took the unusual step of capturing and naming these irradiated insects rather than exterminating them on sight-a small oddity in a wasteland that typically shoots radroaches on principle. Whether the captor felt sentimentality, boredom, or some stranger motive remains unknown. Fluffy lives the constrained existence of any caged creature, fed and contained but hardly domesticated. Like all radroaches, it is a mutated descendant of pre-War cockroaches, hardened by generations of radiation into a hardy scavenger. The cage keeps it from scuttling off into the wastes, though radroaches are far from the most dangerous things roaming the Capital Wasteland.', 'A radroach with a glossy irradiated carapace, twitching antennae, and multiple legs, slightly larger than its pre-War ancestors.', 'Skittish and reactive, driven by basic survival instincts, though confinement has dulled its wariness of nearby movement', '{"Jitters":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"cage companion","note":"The other named radroach sharing the same cage in the sniper shack.","best":"Sharing a food scrap that slipped through the cage bars","worst":"Competing for the same meager morsel during lean days"}}', 'Caged pet', '* Radiation resistance
* Scavenging instincts
* Hardy survival adaptations typical of radroaches', 'Non-verbal; communicates through skittering movements, clicking mandibles, and antennae shifts', '* Survival
* Finding food morsels
* Eventual escape from confinement', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('forty', '', 'Eulogy Jones'' dim-witted but lethally capable second-in-command at Paradise Falls', 'Forty is a slaver operating out of Paradise Falls, where he serves as Eulogy Jones'' trusted second-in-command. He earned his ominous nickname from the forty men he has killed over the course of his violent life, a tally he maintains with grim pride. Slaves, however, he considers mere sport and does not count toward that total, revealing a callous disregard for human life that even other slavers find unsettling. Despite his limited intellect, Forty''s brute reliability and willingness to do Eulogy''s dirtiest work have secured his position. He is fifty-five years old and has spent much of his adult life in the slave trade, cultivating a reputation for casual brutality that keeps both captives and colleagues wary of him.', 'A weathered, heavyset man in his mid-fifties with scarred hands and a hard expression.', 'Dim-witted but cunning in matters of violence; boastful about his kill count; treats the murder of slaves as recreational sport; loyal to Eulogy through simple-minded devotion rather than ambition; possesses a cruel streak that even fellow slavers find disturbing', '{"Eulogy Jones":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"second-in-command","note":"Forty serves as Eulogy''s loyal enforcer and right hand at Paradise Falls","best":"Being named second-in-command and trusted with Eulogy''s most important enforcement duties","worst":"Being dismissed or overlooked despite his faithful service"},"Slavers":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow slavers","note":"Works alongside the Paradise Falls slavers, though his dim wit and cruelty limit his standing"}}', 'Slaver and second-in-command at Paradise Falls', '* Combat proficiency
* Intimidation
* Slave handling
* A talent for brutal enforcement that requires no subtlety', 'Slow, boastful, and simple; brags about his kill count; speaks of violence with casual amusement; lacks eloquence but makes his threats unmistakably clear', '* Maintain his position as Eulogy''s enforcer
* Continue adding to his kill count
* Enjoy the sport that Paradise Falls provides him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('four_score', '', 'Hannibal Hamlin''s faithful cattle dog and companion to the escaped slaves of the Temple of the Union', 'Four Score is a loyal cattle dog who resides with the escaped slaves at the Temple of the Union, devoted to his master Hannibal Hamlin. Named in homage to Abraham Lincoln''s Gettysburg Address, the dog serves as a steadfast companion to the small community of freedmen seeking their own piece of liberty. While primarily Hannibal''s pet, Four Score receives daily care and attention from Bill Seward, who ensures the animal stays fed and healthy. The dog travels with the group when they relocate to the Lincoln Memorial, remaining at Hannibal''s side throughout the journey. Four Score''s presence offers a small measure of comfort and normalcy to the former slaves who have endured immense hardship. He is recognized as a legendary cattle dog among those who know the Temple''s story.', 'A sturdy, weathered cattle dog with a lean, hardened build.', 'Loyal and protective of Hannibal and the Temple community; alert to strangers but gentle and trusting with those he knows', '{"Hannibal Hamlin":{"aff":90,"type":"protective","relation":"faithful companion","note":"Four Score is utterly devoted to Hannibal and rarely leaves his side"},"Bill Seward":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"caretaker","note":"Bill provides daily care and feeding for Four Score on Hannibal''s behalf"}}', 'Pet and companion to the Temple of the Union slaves', '* Guarding
* Tracking
* Threat detection
* Companionship', 'Cannot speak; communicates through barks, whines, growls, and body language', '* Stay close to Hannibal Hamlin
* Protect his master and the Temple community from threats', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('frank', '', 'Enslaved bartender forced to serve at Paradise Falls, killed by the slaver Ymir over watered-down vodka', 'Frank is a slave working as the bartender at Paradise Falls, the notorious slaver compound in the Capital Wasteland. Captured during a slaver raid north of Megaton, he has spent the last several months in bondage, mixing drinks for the very people who took his freedom. Desperate to accumulate a few extra caps of his own, Frank waters down the vodka he serves-a dangerous gamble in a den of armed and violent captors. The slaver Ymir takes particular offense at this petty scheme, and his response is brutal and final. Frank''s story ends with a super sledge blow, another disposable life in the slave economy of Paradise Falls.', 'A worn, weary Hispanic male with a haggard complexion and slumped posture.', 'Cunning enough to skim caps but not wise enough to recognize the lethal risk, Frank is a desperate man clinging to small acts of rebellion and self-interest in a place where slaves have no margin for error', '{"Ymir":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"murderer","note":"Ymir despises Frank for watering down the vodka and kills him for it with a super sledge","worst":"The final swing of Ymir''s super sledge, punishment for a few watered bottles"},"Slaves":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow captives","note":"Shares the bond of enslavement with other Paradise Falls slaves"},"Paradise Falls slavers":{"aff":-70,"type":"fearful","relation":"captors","note":"Forced to serve the people who stole his freedom, living in constant dread of their cruelty"}}', 'Slave bartender at Paradise Falls', '* Bartending
* Drink preparation
* Minor scheming and cap-skimming through diluted liquor', 'Quiet and deferential around slavers, careful with words, the measured tone of a man who knows the wrong sentence could cost him', '* Accumulate enough caps to matter
* Survive another day
* Perhaps dream of freedom though the odds are slim', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('fred_wilks', '', 'A Grayditch homesteader and devoted father who died defending his home from the fire ant invasion', 'Fred Wilks was a resident of Grayditch who worked hard to provide for his son Bryan in the shadow of the Capital Wasteland''s ruins. A steadfast and protective man, he raised Bryan with a strong sense of purpose and deep respect for family bonds. When the mutated fire ants swarmed into Grayditch, Fred stood his ground at his home rather than flee, buying what time he could against the encroaching vermin. He perished in his own house, another victim of the wasteland''s relentless dangers, leaving his son orphaned and alone. His sister Vera Weatherly runs the Weatherly Hotel in Rivet City, the only remaining family Bryan can turn to. Fred''s body still rests where he fell, a grim testament to a father''s last stand.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian male with a weathered complexion and a deceased body.', 'Devoted, protective, and principled; placed family above all else and faced danger head-on rather than abandon his home', '{"Bryan Wilks":{"aff":95,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Fred raised Bryan alone and devoted himself to the boy''s upbringing and moral foundation","best":"Teaching Bryan the importance of family and standing by the people you love","worst":"Leaving Bryan orphaned when the fire ants overwhelmed him"},"Vera Weatherly":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"Fred''s sister runs the Weatherly Hotel in Rivet City and is Bryan''s only remaining family"},"Grayditch":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"home community","note":"Fred chose to defend his home against the fire ant invasion rather than abandon it"}}', 'Grayditch homesteader and provider', '* Wasteland survival
* Home defense
* Basic maintenance
* Child-rearing in harsh conditions', 'Straightforward and earnest; spoke with the plain directness of a man concerned with practical matters and his son''s wellbeing', '* Protect
* Provide for Bryan
* Maintain the family home
* Instill lasting values in his son', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('freddie_gomez', '', 'An insecure Vault 101 youth who masks his depression and low self-worth behind Tunnel Snake bravado and bullying', 'Freddie Gomez is a young resident of Vault 101 whose desperate need for acceptance led him to attach himself to Butch DeLoria and the Tunnel Snakes. Once mocked by his peers as ''Freddie the Freak'' and unfavorably compared to Grognak the Barbarian, Freddie found in the gang a source of validation he had never known. His pursuit of their approval has dragged down his grades and alarmed his parents, Herman and Pepper Gomez. Diagnosed with Vault Depressive Syndrome by the vault physician James, Freddie suffers from lethargy, anxiety, and chronic low self-esteem, coping through misbehavior and bullying that earns him the Tunnel Snakes'' fleeting approval. James prescribed chlorpromazine to manage his symptoms but worries the boy may become permanently dependent on the medication. Despite his tough posturing, Freddie remains deeply uncertain, as shown by his visible nervousness during the G.O.A.T. and his agonized struggle with the exam''s moral questions.', 'A young Hispanic male with a slight build and a slouching posture.', 'Insecure and approval-hungry beneath a bully''s bravado, Freddie craves validation and acts out to earn it. He struggles with anxiety and low self-esteem, masking vulnerability with misbehavior and posturing. Morally conflicted and easily overwhelmed when confronted with difficult choices, he defaults to whatever earns him the most social credit with the gang.', '{"Butch DeLoria":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"aspiring follower to gang leader","note":"Freddie craves Butch''s approval above all and acts out specifically to earn his recognition","best":"Butch clapped him on the back and called him a real Tunnel Snake after he shoved a smaller kid","worst":"Butch laughed and called him Freddie the Freak in front of the whole corridor"},"Herman Gomez":{"aff":45,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Herman worries constantly about Freddie''s declining grades and gang associations, creating tension between them"},"Pepper Gomez":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Pepper frets over Freddie''s behavioral changes and medication, her concern met with sullen withdrawal"},"James":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"physician","note":"James diagnosed Freddie''s VDS and prescribed chlorpromazine, but Freddie resents the diagnosis and the implication that something is wrong with him","worst":"Having to sit in James''s office while the doctor explained his condition to his parents"},"Susie Mack":{"aff":35,"type":"platonic","relation":"acquaintance","note":"Friendly enough to chat about broken heaters and agree to lunch after the G.O.A.T., one of the few peers who treats him normally","best":"Susie never called him Freddie the Freak and always said hello in the corridor"},"Tunnel Snakes":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"aspiring member","note":"The gang provides the approval Freddie cannot find elsewhere, and he will do whatever it takes to maintain his standing with them"}}', 'Vault 101 resident and aspiring Tunnel Snake', '* Minor intimidation tactics
* Social posturing
* Basic vault-dweller competencies diminished by poor academic performance and inattention', 'Tries to sound tough and dismissive like the older Tunnel Snakes, but his voice cracks under pressure and his uncertainty bleeds through when faced with moral questions or authority figures', '* To earn full acceptance from Butch and the Tunnel Snakes
* To escape the shadow of ''Freddie the Freak
* '' and to find a sense of belonging that his depression and anxiety constantly undermine', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('freki', '', 'Desmond Lockheart''s aggressive guard dog patrolling Calvert Mansion', 'Freki is one of two hounds in the service of the ghoul Desmond Lockheart, residing at Calvert Mansion in the Point Lookout swamps. Alongside Geri, he patrols the foyer and stairways of the estate, serving as its first line of defense against intruders. The pair once drove off Nadine when she wandered too close to the mansion grounds, ensuring she stayed far away when the local tribals launched their latest assault. Freki is the more dominant and hostile of the two dogs, embodying the greedy and aggressive spirit of the mythological wolf whose name he carries. Utterly loyal to Desmond, he serves as both guardian and constant companion to the reclusive ghoul.', 'A sturdy, battle-scarred dog with hard eyes.', 'Aggressive, territorial, and fiercely loyal to Desmond; more hostile and dominant than Geri, quick to threaten intruders', '{"Desmond Lockheart":{"aff":95,"type":"protective","relation":"master''s guard dog","note":"Utterly devoted guardian and companion to the ghoul","best":"Resting at Desmond''s feet after a successful patrol of the mansion grounds"},"Geri":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow guard dog","note":"Patrols alongside Geri as the more aggressive and dominant of the pair"},"Nadine":{"aff":-50,"type":"enemy","relation":"chased intruder","note":"Drove her away from the mansion grounds when she wandered too close","worst":"The scent of the tribal girl who dared approach the mansion"}}', 'Guard dog for Calvert Mansion', '* Patrol and perimeter defense
* Intimidation
* Chasing off trespassers
* Combat', 'Non-verbal; communicates through growls, barks, snarls, and body language-low rumbling warnings at strangers, eager attentiveness toward Desmond', '* Protect Desmond Lockheart and the mansion from all threats
* Patrol the estate grounds relentlessly
* Drive off or attack anyone who trespasses', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('friday', '', 'Pitt mechanic and merchant who runs Friday''s Repairs with her partner Trouble Man', 'Friday is a mechanic and merchant operating out of Downtown in The Pitt, running a shop called Friday''s Repairs alongside her partner Trouble Man. She sells various equipment and offers weapon repair services to those who can afford her prices. Despite her mild-mannered demeanor, she is a ruthless businesswoman who drives hard bargains and never cuts a deal that doesn''t favor her bottom line. Business in The Pitt is typically slow, leaving her eager for any customer willing to spend caps. Her shop sits above Kai''s location, accessible via stairs near Midea''s quarters and across the planks. She operates under the umbrella of the Pitt raiders'' authority, surviving the harsh industrial hellscape through her valuable technical skills.', 'African American human female with weathered, prematurely aged skin and a haggard complexion showing the toll of prolonged toxic exposure.', 'Outwardly mild-mannered and soft-spoken, but shrewd and uncompromising when it comes to business dealings', '{"Trouble Man":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"business partner","note":"Co-operates Friday''s Repairs with him as a shared venture"},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":30,"type":"transactional","relation":"affiliated faction","note":"Operates under their authority and benefits from the arrangement"}}', 'Merchant and mechanic at Friday''s Repairs', '* Weapon repair
* Equipment appraisal
* Merchant trade
* Mechanical expertise', 'Calm and measured, with a businesslike directness; never raises her voice but always steers conversations toward transactions', '* Keeping her repair shop profitable in The Pitt''s sparse economy
* Maintaining her partnership with Trouble Man
* Securing steady customers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gallo', '', 'A deranged, reclusive ghoul cannibal dwelling in the County sewer mainline, violently hostile to all outsiders', 'Gallo is a solitary ghoul who has claimed a small service room deep within the County sewer mainline as his home. Decades of isolation, prolonged sewer gas exposure, and the burden of his unnaturally long life have shattered his sanity, leaving him deeply paranoid and violently hostile toward anyone who ventures near. He recently celebrated his birthday in the company of his two favorite garden gnomes, marking the occasion by carving up feral ghoul corpses for a grim feast. His dwelling reflects his eccentric obsessions: an extensive Nuka-Cola memorabilia collection including a prized Nuka-Cola Quantum, a pristine Radiation King television, and a pen of small radroaches he keeps as pets. Dead feral ghouls stored in his refrigerator and plates of strange meat scattered across his bar reveal his cannibalistic appetites. Gallo has rigged deadly traps throughout the tunnels outside his home to ensure no intruder reaches him alive.', 'A weathered male ghoul with deeply lined, leathery skin and the sunken facial features characteristic of advanced ghoulification.', 'Deeply insane, paranoid, and violently territorial. Finds comfort in inanimate companions like gnomes and radroaches while viewing all living people as threats or food. Clings to pre-War consumer nostalgia through his Nuka-Cola collection', '{}', 'Reclusive cannibal and subterranean scavenger', '* Trap construction and placement
* Subterranean survival
* Butchery
* Scavenging and hoarding', 'Incoherent muttering and rambling, likely conversing with his gnome companions or radroaches as if they respond', '* Defend his sewer home from all intruders
* Maintain and expand his Nuka-Cola collection
* Continue his solitary existence undisturbed', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gary_1', '', 'Gary 1 is a Resident associated with Cloning Lab in Fallout 3, encountered around Cloning Lab.', 'Gary 1 is known from Fallout 3 and is tied to Cloning Lab. Their role is Resident associated with Cloning Lab, giving them a practical place in local wasteland life.', 'Human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Acts from the pressures of their faction, settlement, and personal role in the wasteland.', '{}', 'Resident associated with Cloning Lab', '* Local knowledge
* Wasteland survival
* Faction awareness', 'Speaks in a practical wasteland manner shaped by local danger, scarce resources, and faction politics.', '* Protect their interests around Cloning Lab
* Maintain useful alliances
