('gary_12', '', 'One of the hostile Gary clones infesting Vault 108, a product of the vault''s failed cloning experiment', 'Gary 12 is one of numerous identical clones produced by Vault 108''s clandestine cloning program. The original Gary was a vault resident selected for replication, but the clones proved unstable and violently territorial. They overran the vault, slaughtering or driving out the original inhabitants and claiming the corridors as their own. Gary 12 occupies the cloning lab alongside his brothers, wandering the sterile halls where he was grown. Like all Gary clones, he possesses limited cognitive function and an obsessive hostility toward any non-Gary who enters the vault. His vocabulary has deteriorated to a single word, yet he and his brethren display eerie coordination and pack-like aggression.', 'A pale, gaunt man with hollow eyes and a slack, vacant expression.', 'Violently territorial and xenophobic toward anyone who is not a Gary clone; otherwise docile around his brothers; limited intellect and single-word vocabulary mask a feral cunning and pack coordination', '{"Gary clones":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"clone brothers","note":"All Gary clones share an instinctive bond and cooperate violently against outsiders."}}', 'Vault 108 clone; territorial occupant of the cloning lab', '* Brute melee combat
* Pack tactics
* Vault navigation
* Ambush coordination', 'Can only say ''Gary'' with varying inflection and emphasis to convey aggression, alarm, or recognition', '* Defend Vault 108 territory from intruders
* Maintain the Gary clone population
* Eliminate all non-Garys', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gary_17', '', 'One of the hostile Gary clones infesting Vault 108''s cloning lab', 'Gary 17 is a product of Vault 108''s rogue cloning experiment, one of dozens of identical men who overran the vault and slaughtered the original staff. Like every Gary, he can only speak his own name in shifting inflections, yet somehow communicates intent and warning to his fellow clones through tone and gesture alone. He patrols the cloning lab with the same vacant aggression as his brothers, attacking any non-Gary on sight. The original Gary died long ago, but his genetic echo persists in these hostile duplicates, wandering the corroded halls in tattered jumpsuits. Whether Gary 17 retains any fragment of the original''s identity or is simply a violent blank slate is a question the wasteland will never answer.', 'A pale, balding man with a gaunt face and hollow stare, identical to the other Gary clones.', 'Aggressive, territorial, and seemingly incapable of complex thought beyond violence, yet displaying eerie coordination with other clones.', '{"Gary clones":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"clone brothers","note":"All Garys share an uncanny bond, coordinating without words.","best":"Fighting alongside other Garys against a trespasser","worst":"Watching another Gary fall to an outsider"},"Vault 108":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"home territory","note":"The vault is all the Garys have ever known."}}', 'Vault 108 clone, hostile inhabitant', '* Basic combat
* Pack coordination with other Garys
* Vault navigation', 'Can only say ''Gary'' in varying tones, pitches, and emphases that somehow convey meaning to other clones.', '* Eliminate non-Gary intruders
* Survive alongside his brothers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gary_23', '', 'A deceased Vault 108 clone whose Pip-Boy held access to the Anchorage combat simulation, found dead at the Brotherhood Outcast outpost', 'Gary 23 was one of the identical clones produced by Vault 108''s failed replication experiment, sharing the same face, jumpsuit, and single-word vocabulary as every other Gary who overran that vault. Unlike his brothers who remained to stalk Vault 108''s corridors, Gary 23 was recovered by the Brotherhood Outcasts and brought to their outpost at the VSS facility. His Pip-Boy contained the access codes required to run the Anchorage combat simulation, making him a critical asset in the Outcasts'' pursuit of pre-war military technology. He died at the outpost, his corpse still wearing the Pip-Boy the Outcasts needed, whether from their clumsy attempts to extract the device or from other causes. Like all Gary clones, his entire spoken vocabulary consisted of his own name.', 'A pale, balding man with gaunt facial features and a vacant stare, identical to all Vault 108 clones; his corpse shows signs of death with no further distinctive physical traits recorded.', 'Exhibited the limited cognition and single-word speech typical of Vault 108 clones, aggressive toward non-Garys and driven by pack instinct rather than individual thought', '{"Brotherhood Outcasts":{"aff":-40,"type":"neutral","relation":"captive","note":"Held him at the outpost for his Pip-Boy''s simulation access codes"},"Gary clones":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"clone pack","note":"Shared the same genetic identity and pack-bond instinct with all Vault 108 Garys"}}', 'Vault 108 clone; involuntary carrier of Pip-Boy simulation access codes', '* Basic motor function and pack coordination
* No discernible practical skills beyond primitive survival instinct', 'Can only say ''Gary'' in varying intonations, volumes, and emotional registers', '* Had no known personal ambitions
* Vault 108 clones operated on territorial and survival instinct alone', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gary_25', '', 'One of the feral Gary clones roaming Vault 108''s cloning lab, hostile and barely verbal', 'Gary 25 is a product of Vault 108''s ill-fated cloning experiment, one of dozens of identical copies manufactured from the original Gary. The cloning process produced increasingly unstable and aggressive results, each iteration born with a violent temperament and an inability to communicate beyond the repeated utterance of his own name. He wanders the cloning lab alongside his brothers, attacking any outsider on sight with savage fury. Like all Garys, he wears the tattered Vault 108 jumpsuit and exhibits the same pale, hairless features common to every clone in the line. The Garys have claimed the entire vault as their territory, operating on pack instinct and raw hostility toward anything that is not Gary.', 'Pale, hairless human male clone with features physically identical to every other Gary produced by Vault 108''s cloning process.', 'Feral, aggressive, territorial, and incapable of meaningful communication; operates on instinct and pack behavior with other Garys', '{"Gary clones":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"clone brothers","note":"Recognizes other Garys as kin and cooperates with them against outsiders"},"Vault 108":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"territory","note":"The vault is the only home the Garys know and defend fiercely"}}', 'Failed cloning experiment; territorial inhabitant of Vault 108', '* Brute melee combat
* Pack coordination with other Garys
* Vault navigation', 'Can only say ''Gary'' in varied tones and inflections ranging from greeting to rage', '* Defend Vault 108 territory alongside his clone brothers
* Destroy all non-Gary intruders', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gary_27', '', 'One of the hostile Gary clones roaming Vault 108''s living quarters', 'Gary 27 is a product of Vault 108''s cloning experiment, wandering the ruined living quarters with his identical brethren. Like every Gary, he is a physical copy of the original test subject, produced with only minor genetic degradation but severe psychological deterioration. The clones slaughtered the vault''s original inhabitants and now claim the corridors as their own territory. Gary 27 is indistinguishable from his brothers in appearance and behavior, joining them in their aggressive defense of the vault against all outsiders. He knows nothing of life before the cloning vats and recognizes no authority beyond the pack of Garys.', 'A middle-aged man sharing the identical face and build of every other Gary clone, with slight signs of genetic degradation.', 'Aggressive, territorial, and nearly non-verbal; exhibits pack behavior with fellow Garys and immediate hostility toward outsiders', '{"Garys":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"clone pack","note":"All Garys share an instinctive bond and coordinate defensively as a group","best":"Wandering the vault corridors alongside his brothers in quiet moments"},"Vault 108":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"territory","note":"The Garys claim the entire vault as their domain and defend it fiercely"}}', 'Vault 108 clone and squatter', '* Vault navigation
* Pack coordination
* Basic survival
* Improvised combat', 'Communicates almost exclusively through variations of the word ''Gary!'' with different intonations conveying alarm, greeting, anger, or recognition', '* Defend Vault 108 territory alongside his brothers
* Drive out or kill intruders
* Maintain the Garys'' control of the vault', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('gary_29', '', 'One of the aggressive clone duplicates roaming Vault 108', 'Gary 29 is one of dozens of identical clones produced by Vault 108''s failed cloning experiment. He wanders the vault''s living quarters alongside his fellow Garys, hostile to any outsider who enters their territory. Like every Gary clone, he possesses severely limited cognitive and verbal function, capable only of snarling his own name. The cloning process replicated the original Gary''s genetic material with perfect physical fidelity but catastrophic mental degradation, leaving an army of violent, simple-minded duplicates. Gary 29 defends the ruined vault with the same feral pack mentality shared by all his brothers, attacking non-Gary intruders on sight with whatever weapons are at hand.', 'A middle-aged man with short brown hair and a vacant, aggressive expression, physically identical to every other Gary clone.', 'Feral, territorial, and hostile to all outsiders. Operates on pack instinct alongside other Garys. Incapable of complex thought, reasoning, or social interaction beyond aggressive name-shouting.', '{"Gary clones":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"clone brothers","note":"All Garys share an instinctive pack bond and never attack one another"},"Vault 108":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"territory","note":"The vault is the only home the Garys know and defend ferociously"}}', 'Clone subject and territorial inhabitant of Vault 108', '* Basic melee and improvised weapon combat
* Pack coordination with other Garys
