* Ultimately aid the Project Purity research he came to believe in', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('joseph', '', 'The eldest resident and schoolteacher of Little Lamplight, nearing the age when he must leave the only home he has ever known', 'Joseph is a fifteen-year-old boy who serves as the teacher for Little Lamplight''s children, holding the distinction of being the settlement''s eldest resident in 2277. Each morning he leads lessons in the schoolhouse, passing on what knowledge he can to the younger cavern-dwellers before spending his afternoons down by the water in the Great Chamber. His younger sister Penny idolizes him for his quiet wisdom and steady temperament, seeing in him the kind of person she hopes to become. Joseph carries his role with a maturity beyond his years, aware that his time in Little Lamplight is drawing to its inevitable close. The settlement''s tradition demands he leave for the wasteland once he comes of age, a prospect that shadows his daily routine. He teaches with the measured patience of someone who understands that every lesson might be his last chance to prepare these children for the world above.', 'A fifteen-year-old African American boy with a lean, ration-thin build and a composed face that reads older than his years.', 'Wise beyond his years, patient, and responsible; carries himself with quiet authority and genuine care for the children he teaches, though the looming departure from Little Lamplight weighs on him heavily', '{"Penny":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"younger sister","note":"Penny idolizes Joseph for his wisdom and looks to him as her role model and protector","best":"Teaching Penny to read and watching her pride when she first managed a full sentence on her own","worst":"The unspoken dread of leaving her behind when he ages out of Little Lamplight"},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"eldest resident and teacher","note":"Joseph feels a deep responsibility to the settlement''s children and dreads the day he must leave them to the caverns alone","best":"Seeing a child finally grasp a difficult lesson after weeks of patient instruction","worst":"Knowing that each day brings him closer to the age when he will be sent away"}}', 'Teacher at the Little Lamplight schoolhouse', '* Teaching
* Basic literacy and numeracy instruction
* Practical survival knowledge
* Mediation among children', 'Speaks with measured patience and clarity, using simple language that younger children can grasp, occasionally revealing the weight of his impending exile in quieter moments', '* To prepare Little Lamplight''s children as best he can before his forced departure
* To ensure Penny will be cared for after he leaves
* To come to terms with the wasteland that awaits him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('jotun', '', 'A simple-minded, inarticulate slaver who silently dedicates himself to protecting his boastful father at Paradise Falls', 'Jotun is a hulking slaver stationed at Paradise Falls, where he devotes himself to the singular task of keeping his father Ymir safe-a responsibility he plainly calls a big job. He struggles to string together even basic sentences and communicates almost entirely through grunts when addressing fellow slavers, offering only vague, halting responses to anyone else. Together with Ymir, he is known around the slaver camp as one of Paradise Falls''s pair of knuckleheads. His father showers him with relentless praise and brags about him to anyone who will listen, a display of paternal pride that Jotun visibly finds mortifying. Despite his limited way with words, his loyalty to Ymir is absolute, and his imposing physical presence ensures few dare test whether the quiet giant can back up his silence with force.', 'A large, heavyset Caucasian man with a thick, imposing build and a dull, uneasy expression.', 'Deeply simple, socially awkward, and painfully inarticulate, but fiercely devoted to his father. Shrinks from attention and finds open praise embarrassing. Speaks as little as possible and prefers to let his presence do the talking.', '{"Ymir":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Devoted protector who finds his father''s constant bragging mortifying but loves him without question.","best":"Standing watch over Ymir while the old man sleeps, knowing he is safe.","worst":"Squirming while Ymir loudly boasts about him to the other slavers."},"Slavers":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"colleagues","note":"Tolerates fellow slavers with grunts and minimal acknowledgment, accepted as one of the camp''s fixtures."}}', 'Slaver at Paradise Falls', '* Physical intimidation
* Brute strength
* Steadfast watchfulness over his father', 'Extremely sparse-mostly grunts to fellow slavers, short vague phrases to strangers. Struggles to form complete sentences and trails off quickly.', '* Keep Ymir safe
* Avoid embarrassment
* Endure social interaction as briefly as possible', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('junders_plunkett', '', 'A one-eyed raider outlaw hiding from a thousand-cap bounty in Arlington Cemetery, where he tends a makeshift shrine to Abraham Lincoln', 'Junders Plunkett is a wanted outlaw whose theft and murder in Canterbury Commons earned him a thousand-cap bounty from the Regulators. The bounty has made him a liability to his fellow raiders, as Regulators under Sonora Cruz have been harassing them for information on his whereabouts. Plunkett retreated to the Arlington House in the Arlington Cemetery, where he has constructed a shrine to the ancient figure Lincoln, finding strange solace in the ruins of the old world. A Regulator tracker managed to follow him to the cemetery but was killed before reaching the house. Plunkett remains holed up in his hideout, hostile to any intruder and ready to defend himself with his signature concealable blades.', 'Caucasian human male of average height with a fair complexion and one missing eye.', 'Paranoid and hostile to outsiders, with an obsessive streak evident in his Lincoln shrine. Defiant against the law and unwilling to surrender, preferring to fight anyone who comes near.', '{"Sonora Cruz":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"bounty target","note":"Cruz placed a thousand-cap bounty on Plunkett and considers him a bastard who deserves death","worst":"The bounty she placed has driven him into hiding and made his own people targets for harassment"},"Regulators":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"hunted fugitive","note":"They have been pursuing him relentlessly and harassing his fellow raiders for his location","worst":"A Regulator tracker cornered him at Arlington Cemetery, forcing him to kill to stay hidden"},"Raiders":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow outlaws","note":"His raider associates have been harassed by Regulators seeking information about him, straining whatever loyalty exists"}}', 'Raider outlaw and fugitive', '* Highly skilled with small concealable blades
* Capable of killing trained Regulators in close combat
* Survival and evasion in urban ruins', 'Gritty and aggressive raider vernacular, likely punctuated by threats and territorial warnings', '* Evade Regulator capture and the bounty on his head
* Maintain his hideout in Arlington House
* Continue his veneration of Lincoln', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('junior_smith', '', 'A young boy of Andale raised within the town''s insular and deeply unsettling family traditions', 'Junior Smith is the son of Jack and Linda Smith, and one of only two children living in the isolated settlement of Andale. He spends his days in the company of Jenny Wilson, the other child in town, with whom he shares an easy and familiar friendship. Like every boy born in Andale before him, Junior is expected to marry the girl closest to his age when he comes of age, a tradition that has kept the town''s families tightly bound for generations. He knows little of the world beyond the houses and sheds of Andale, and the adults around him intend to keep it that way. Whether he senses the wrongness that lurks beneath the town''s cheerful facade remains unclear, hidden behind a child''s quiet acceptance of the only life he has ever known.', 'A young boy with pale, unwashed complexion and vacant eyes.', 'Quiet and obedient, shaped by a sheltered existence and the unspoken rules of Andale''s households. He shows the easy comfort of a child who has never known anything strange about his home, or has learned not to ask.', '{"Jack Smith":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Junior obeys his father without question, as is expected in the Smith household."},"Linda Smith":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Linda dotes on Junior in her own strained way, keeping him close and compliant."},"Jenny Wilson":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"cousin and intended bride","note":"The two children get along well, sharing the bond of being Andale''s only youth.","best":"Playing together in the yards between the family houses"},"Bill Wilson":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"uncle","note":"A familiar adult presence in Junior''s limited world."},"Martha Wilson":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"aunt","note":"Another of the few adults Junior sees regularly."},"Old Man Harris":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"grandfather","note":"Harris watches the children with a sadness Junior likely does not understand."}}', 'Child of the Smith household', '* Basic chores suited to a child in a rural settlement
* No combat or trade skills', 'Sparse, childish phrasing with an undercurrent of rote politeness drilled into him by his parents', '* To grow up and fulfill his expected role in Andale''s traditions
* Including his arranged future with Jenny Wilson', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('justin', '', 'A young, fervent devotee of the Family who preaches Vance''s vampire lore and tends to Ian West with fierce emotional attachment', 'Justin has belonged to the Family since he was fourteen, when Vance rescued him from an Enclave patrol in the wasteland. Before that salvation, he endured regular beatings from Rivet City guards, a life he has left behind entirely. Now twenty, Justin serves as caretaker for Ian West, a newer Family member to whom he feels a bond so close it nearly borders on love. He spends most of his time at Ian''s side in the Meresti Metro station. Justin is among the most fervent believers in Vance''s vampire teachings and actively spreads those stories to his fellow members. His devotion to Vance borders on hero worship, and he credits the Family''s leader with giving him a second life.', 'A pale, twenty-year-old Caucasian male of average build with no distinctive scars or tattoos recorded.', 'Eager, headstrong, and warmly friendly toward those he does not perceive as threats; fiercely loyal and emotionally intense in his attachments, sometimes to a fault', '{"Vance":{"aff":95,"type":"fanatical","relation":"savior and spiritual mentor","note":"Justin worships Vance for rescuing him from an Enclave patrol and giving his life purpose","best":"Vance appearing between him and the Enclave patrol, offering salvation when death seemed certain","worst":"The thought of disappointing Vance or being cast out from the Family"},"Ian West":{"aff":90,"type":"protective","relation":"caretaker and near-beloved","note":"Justin feels a bond with Ian so close it nearly borders on love, and he spends most of his time at Ian''s side","best":"Quiet hours spent together in the Meresti Metro, Ian finally seeming at peace","worst":"Watching Ian struggle with his new life in the Family, unable to ease his pain"},"The Family":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"devoted member and preacher","note":"Justin sees the Family as his true home and actively spreads their vampire lore to fellow members","best":"Being welcomed into the Family at fourteen, finding belonging for the first time","worst":"Remembering the isolation before the Family found him"},"Rivet City guards":{"aff":-60,"type":"fearful","relation":"former tormentors","note":"Justin carries deep scars from the beatings Rivet City guards inflicted on him before Vance saved him","best":"Leaving Rivet City behind forever","worst":"Being cornered and beaten by the guards with no way out"}}', 'Caretaker for Ian West within the Family', '* Persuasion and storytelling for spreading Vance''s teachings
* Basic caretaking and companionship
* Wasteland survival instincts honed by hard experience', 'Enthusiastic and earnest, prone to passionate declarations about Vance and the Family''s ways; friendly and open with newcomers who show no hostility', '* Protect and remain close to Ian West
* Spread and uphold Vance''s vampire teachings
* Prove his devotion to the Family and its leader', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('kai', '', 'A depressed and illiterate Pitt slave who reluctantly feeds her fellow workers trog-meat slop', 'Kai is a slave laborer consigned to The Pitt''s Downtown district, assigned the thankless role of cook for her fellow captives. Illiterate and quietly depressed, she prepares slop from trog meat and irradiated river water, a meal she openly doubts is any better than starvation. She approves of those who refuse to eat her cooking, genuinely uncertain whether the food or hunger would kill a person faster. Despite her apathy, she keeps track of the Mill''s inhabitants and can point out where to find Marco when he is not coming to her for meals. Kai perished during the violent slave uprising that swept through The Pitt.', 'A gaunt, underfed woman with sunken eyes and sallow, radiation-weathered skin; her haggard face and slumped posture suggest chronic exhaustion and malnutrition.', 'Sullen, apathetic, and darkly pragmatic; resigned to her circumstances and disarmingly honest about the bleakness of survival in The Pitt', '{"Pitt slaves":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow sufferers","note":"She feeds them but encourages them not to eat the slop she is forced to serve."},"Marco":{"aff":15,"type":"neutral","relation":"meal recipient","note":"She knows his routine and can point out his location in the Mill between meals."}}', 'Slave cook at The Pitt Downtown market square', '* Basic food preparation
* Familiarity with Mill personnel and their daily routines', 'Flat, depressed monotone; speaks bluntly about grim realities without embellishment or optimism', '* Getting through each day
* Feeding fellow slaves despite doubting her own cooking sustains anyone', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('karen_johnson', '', 'A resident of Andale and matriarch of one of the settlement''s original founding families', 'Karen Johnson is a resident of Andale, living alongside her husband Tuck Johnson as part of one of the four founding families that survived the Great War in the small settlement. The Johnsons represent one of the two families whose presence in Andale has faded from open view, though their legacy remains woven into the community''s closely guarded history. Karen maintains the household and upholds the old traditions that bind Andale''s families together, traditions that outsiders would find deeply unsettling. She shares in the collective silence that protects the town''s way of life, a silence paid for with flesh and loyalty in equal measure. Like her neighbors, she presents a cordial front to visitors while ensuring that the settlement''s secrets stay buried alongside its less fortunate guests.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian woman of average build with unremarkable facial features, neatly kept hair, and clear skin lacking distinctive scars or marks.', 'Private and hospitable on the surface, deeply complicit in her community''s darkest practices beneath; fiercely loyal to family and neighbor alike', '{"Tuck Johnson":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"husband","note":"Karen''s partner in maintaining their household and their share of Andale''s grim traditions"},"Andale":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"community","note":"One of the founding families bound by shared silence and survival"}}', 'Homemaker and Andale resident', '* Household management
* Cooking
* Maintaining appearances
* Community cohesion
* Keeping secrets', 'Warm but measured, speaking in the polite and unhurried manner of someone accustomed to controlling what information leaves her home', '* Preserve Andale''s way of life
* Protect the settlement''s secrets from outside scrutiny', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('karen_schenzy', '', 'A defiant young Arefu resident who refuses to live in fear of The Family and despises Evan King''s cautious leadership', 'Karen Schenzy is a twenty-three-year-old resident of Arefu, living in the Schenzy residence within the small settlement perched on an overpass. An extrovert by nature, the ongoing conflict with The Family has chafed against her temperament and put her at sharp odds with the town''s self-appointed leader, Evan King. She views his impromptu security measures as the work of a spineless wimp unwilling or unable to take meaningful action against the genuine threat The Family poses. Rather than cower indoors, Karen has chosen defiance, insisting that living in constant fear is no way to live at all. She would far rather take direct action against The Family than wait behind locked doors for the next incursion. The deaths of Davis and Matilda West only harden her resolve, though she feels King will never have her back in a real fight. She remains cooped up in her home through the long hours of the current crisis, but her spirit strains against the confinement with each passing day.', 'Caucasian human female in her early twenties; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Extroverted, outspoken, and defiant. Karen bristles at authority she considers weak and chafes against restrictions born of caution. She would rather fight than hide, and her frustration simmers just below the surface when prevented from acting on that impulse.', '{"Evan King":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","relation":"town leader she scorns","note":"Karen considers King a spineless wimp whose cautious security measures are a poor substitute for real action against The Family.","worst":"Watching King lock down the town while The Family prowled freely and neighbors died"},"The Family":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"threat to her home","note":"Karen wants direct confrontation with The Family rather than cowering behind closed doors waiting for their next incursion.","worst":"Learning that Davis and Matilda West had been killed by The Family''s predations"},"Arefu":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"her community","note":"Karen''s defiance is rooted in a fierce desire to see her home safe and its people standing strong rather than living in fear."}}', 'Arefu resident', '* Basic survival skills and the stubborn willpower to act on her convictions despite genuine danger', 'Direct and blunt, with a frustrated edge. She does not mince words about Evan King''s failings or her own willingness to fight back.', '* Take direct action against The Family
* Prove that fear is not the answer
* See Arefu defended by someone willing to actually fight rather than just lock doors', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('karl__thefamilykarl', '', 'A gruff, cynical merchant who humors the Family''s vampiric pretenses solely to keep his store running in their metro station sanctuary', 'Karl is a former Megaton shopkeeper who joined the Family alongside his wife Skyler after Vance sensed a kinship with them during a supply run. Since Skyler''s death, Karl has remained in the Meresti Metro Station, operating a store for the community while privately dismissing Vance''s vampiric philosophy as nonsense. He tolerates the cult''s rituals and rhetoric only because the arrangement affords him a secure place to trade and live. His grief and natural misanthropy have made him even more short-tempered and suspicious of strangers. Karl keeps his doubts to himself, playing the part of a loyal Family member while quietly counting caps and waiting for customers to leave him alone.', 'A weathered Caucasian male in his late thirties with no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other physical features recorded.', 'Gruff and short-tempered, Karl prefers solitude and views strangers with deep suspicion. He is cynical by nature, quick to assume the worst in others, and makes little effort to hide his disdain for prolonged social interaction.', '{"Skyler":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"deceased wife","note":"Karl loved Skyler deeply and remains adrift in a community he does not believe in after her death.","best":"Running the Megaton shop together before Vance found them","worst":"Losing Skyler and being left alone among the Family''s pretense"},"Vance":{"aff":25,"type":"transactional","relation":"Family leader","note":"Karl humors Vance''s vampiric teachings to maintain his position but privately dismisses the philosophy entirely.","best":"Being welcomed into a secure home when they needed one","worst":"Enduring Vance''s earnest sermons about blood and discipline"},"The Family":{"aff":15,"type":"transactional","relation":"faction membership","note":"Karl belongs to the Family only for the commercial security and shelter the arrangement provides.","best":"Having a protected store space in the metro station","worst":"Performing loyalty to beliefs he finds ridiculous"}}', 'Merchant operating a store within the Family''s Meresti Metro Station settlement', '* Merchandising
* Bartering
* Inventory management
* Supply acquisition
* Reading customers', 'Curt and dismissive, Karl speaks in short sentences and makes clear he has no interest in small talk or lingering conversation.', '* Maintain his store and livelihood within the Family''s territory
* Be left alone by others
* Preserve what stability he has left after Skyler''s death', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ken_ewers', '', 'A gruff, paranoid Arefu homesteader who masks his terror behind hostility and clings to protecting his delusional wife', 'Ken Ewers is a forty-year-old resident of Arefu, confined to the Ewer residence with his wife Brailee while the settlement suffers under the Family''s predations. The sustained attacks have left him deeply afraid, though he buries that fear beneath a wall of gruff dismissiveness toward any stranger who comes near. He is fiercely overprotective of Brailee, interposing himself whenever anyone attempts to speak with her, and his waking hours revolve around keeping them both alive while managing her fragile mental state. Brailee''s delusions-born of isolation, a poor diet of prepackaged food, and constant fear-have her believing in a utopian world where she bakes and receives fashion catalogs, while in reality she breaks things around the house. This has forced Ken to develop practical repair skills just to keep their home intact. He follows settlement leader Evan King''s lockdown orders despite believing passive defense will doom them all, and the murder of the elder Wests has him seriously contemplating whether to abandon Arefu entirely and start fresh somewhere safer.', 'A weathered, haggard Caucasian man in his forties with a pallid, sun-deprived complexion.', 'Gruff and deliberately unhelpful with strangers as a defense mechanism for deep-seated fear; paranoid and hypervigilant; fiercely overprotective of Brailee to the point of possessiveness; dismissive of her delusions yet genuinely concerned for her wellbeing; pragmatic enough to recognize hopeless situations but compliant with authority out of habit rather than conviction.', '{"Brailee Ewers":{"aff":75,"type":"protective","relation":"wife","note":"Fiercely overprotective of her and deeply concerned about her delusional mental state, though he has grown dismissive of her fantasies","best":"The quiet moments before the attacks when Brailee seemed more like herself","worst":"Watching her welcome a stranger into their home believing they were the mailman"},"Evan King":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"settlement leader","note":"Follows King''s lockdown orders despite believing passive defense will not save them","best":"King taking charge when the attacks first began","worst":"Realizing the lockdown strategy leaves them as sitting targets"},"The Family":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"threat to Arefu","note":"Terrified of the group targeting the settlement for sustenance and responsible for the Wests'' deaths","worst":"The night the elder Wests were murdered"}}', 'Arefu homesteader and reluctant repairman', '* Practical home repair and maintenance born of necessity
* Basic survival knowledge
* No meaningful combat ability despite his protective instincts', 'Curt, gruff, and deliberately terse with outsiders; speaks in short dismissive sentences designed to end conversations quickly; reveals worry only when discussing Brailee''s condition or the settlement''s future.', '* Keep himself and Brailee alive through the Family''s attacks
* Find a way to escape Arefu for somewhere safer
* Manage Brailee''s deteriorating mental state without losing hope
* Convince himself that staying put is worth the risk', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('kenny', '', 'A lonely Marshfolk child outcast living in a haunted mine, skilled at rigging traps and desperate for friendship', 'Kenny, sometimes called Latchkey Kenny, is a Marshfolk child born without the distinctive marks that define the swampfolk of Point Lookout. His parents hid him in their basement for years, knowing the other swampfolk would shoot him on sight like any outsider. In that cellar isolation, Kenny taught himself to dismantle and rebuild whatever he could find, developing an exceptional talent for rigging traps. He eventually fled home and claimed the old Herzog Mine as his own, drawn perhaps by the rumors of hauntings that keep the superstitious locals at bay. Now he lives alone in his makeshift home, passing the time shooting junk off shelves with his BB gun and hoping someone might come along who wants to be his friend.', 'A young Hispanic boy with an unmarked face free of the typical swampfolk deformities.', 'Lonely and cautious around strangers but eager for companionship, playful when he feels safe, resourceful and self-reliant from years of isolation', '{"Swampfolk":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"persecutors","note":"They shoot at him on sight for lacking the marks, forcing him into hiding and exile","worst":"Being driven from his own people because he didn''t look right"}}', 'Swampfolk outcast and trap-maker', '* Exceptional trap rigging
* BB gun marksmanship
* Scavenging and mechanical reassembly', 'Speaks in a rough swampfolk dialect with simplified grammar, dropping consonants and using informal constructions like ''don''t got''', '* Find a friend to play with
* Stay hidden from hostile swampfolk
* Maintain his mine shelter and trap defenses', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('kidd', '', 'A shaken ghoul survivor fleeing the deathclaw massacre that destroyed Old Olney''s failed underground settlement', 'Kidd is a ghoul who joined Sanders'' ambitious attempt to build a new Underworld in the tunnels beneath Old Olney, seeking refuge and community away from the prejudice of the surface world. When a collapsed wall unleashed a deathclaw nest into the nascent settlement, the community was slaughtered almost to a ghoul. Kidd and his partner Wint survived only because they ran faster than everyone else-a fact that sits heavy on whatever conscience remains after such desperate flight. Now trapped in the underground with deathclaws between them and the exit, Kidd is focused entirely on getting out alive. He defers to Wint for any conversation with outsiders, too rattled and desperate to engage with anyone who isn''t offering a clear escape route.', 'A male ghoul with weathered, hairless features typical of heavy radiation exposure, sunken cheeks and hollowed eyes giving his face a gaunt, strained look.', 'Shaken, survival-focused, and emotionally withdrawn after witnessing the slaughter of his community. Defers social interaction to Wint entirely and avoids unnecessary engagement with strangers. Carries the guilt of surviving by running while others died.', '{"Wint":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"partner and fellow survivor","note":"The only two survivors of the deathclaw massacre, bound by shared trauma and mutual reliance","best":"Standing side by side in the tunnels before everything went wrong, dreaming about what their new community could become","worst":"Running through the corridors with screaming behind them, neither looking back, both knowing they were leaving people to die"},"Sanders":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"former community leader","note":"Followed Sanders'' vision for a new Underworld; the leader likely perished in the deathclaw attack"}}', 'Survivor and former settler of the failed Old Olney ghoul community', '* Running
* Survival instincts
* Underground navigation
* Reading threats quickly', 'Curt and distracted, often letting Wint speak for him; when he does talk, words come quick and anxious with no patience for small talk', '* Escape Old Olney underground alive
* Put as much distance as possible between himself and the deathclaws
* Survive', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('kimba', '', 'A soft-spoken Big Town survivor who suppresses her own logical judgment to maintain group harmony among her desperate community', 'Kimba is one of the few surviving residents of Big Town, the surface settlement that receives Little Lamplight''s exiled youth when they come of age. She spent her childhood in the caverns below before aging out and joining the struggling community above. Despite the constant threats and dwindling population, Kimba remains remarkably stable and soft-spoken, always willing to pitch in, learn new skills, and fight for her friends. She often goes along with the rest of the inhabitants'' wishes even when they contradict her own logical thinking, prioritizing unity and hope over being right. Her weapon of necessity-a BB gun-reflects Big Town''s severe lack of proper armament rather than any preference on her part.', 'Young adult African American woman with weathered, sun-damaged skin and a lean, wiry build showing the toll of harsh surface conditions.', 'Cooperative and level-headed under pressure; suppresses her own logical reasoning to preserve group consensus; quietly competent and eager to learn; loyal to a fault toward her friends; sustained by stubborn hope despite grim circumstances.', '{"Big Town":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"community member","note":"She prioritizes group harmony even when the collective decisions contradict her own logic."},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":30,"type":"estranged","relation":"former home","note":"Like all Big Town residents, she aged out of the cavern community and was sent to the surface."}}', 'Big Town resident and community defender', '* Basic survival and settlement defense
* Adaptable learner willing to pick up any practical skill
* Marksmanship with limited weaponry including her BB gun', 'Soft-spoken and measured; tends toward agreement rather than argument; practical and understated in her word choices', '* Survival of Big Town and protection of her friends
* Hopes for outside assistance to improve their desperate situation
* Desires to be useful and contribute meaningfully to the community', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knick_knack', '', 'A fourteen-year-old collector and merchant who runs Little Lamplight''s general store with obsessive organizational care', 'Nicholas, better known as Knick Knack, is a fourteen-year-old boy who operates the souvenir shop and general store in Little Lamplight. He adopted his nickname to reflect his lifelong habit of gathering odds and ends, transforming a simple childhood tendency into his civic role. Unlike his twin sister Knock Knock, who hoards terrible jokes, Knick Knack gravitates toward objects of actual value and takes immense pride in curating the settlement''s inventory. His methodical nature and collector''s instinct made him the natural choice to organize and distribute Little Lamplight''s precious supplies. He tends his counter during daylight hours and sleeps at night like any responsible merchant. He shows particular generosity toward children who demonstrate genuine curiosity and good-heartedness.', 'A cave-pale fourteen-year-old boy with a scruffy, undersized build.', 'Meticulous, tidy, and proudly possessive of his collections. Approaches his role as storekeeper with earnest dedication and genuine enthusiasm for interesting finds. More serious and practical than his joke-obsessed twin, though still a teenager with youthful excitement about rare or curious items.', '{"Knock Knock":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"twin sister","note":"The twins are both dedicated to Little Lamplight but express it in opposite ways-she collects awful jokes while he collects valuable things.","best":"Sharing a rare moment where her terrible puns made even him laugh while sorting inventory","worst":"Her messing up his carefully organized shelves for the sake of a dumb prank"},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"home settlement","note":"Deeply dedicated to the town and takes his role as its supplier seriously."}}', 'Merchant and storekeeper of Little Lamplight''s general store', '* Bartering
* Inventory management
* Appraisal of salvaged goods
* Organization
* Curation of practical supplies', 'Businesslike but youthful, speaking with a collector''s enthusiasm when discussing interesting merchandise and quiet pride about his well-organized stock', '* Keep Little Lamplight well-supplied through careful curation
* Maintain order in the settlement''s stores
* Continue expanding his collection of valuable curiosities', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knight', '', 'A Brotherhood of Steel Knight serving as frontline infantry and base security in the Capital Wasteland', 'Knights form the backbone of Lyons'' Brotherhood of Steel, filling the rank-and-file combat squads that paladins lead into battle. In the Capital Wasteland chapter, the knight rank is purely military: these soldiers guard bases, man outposts, patrol the ruins, and oversee initiate training. Unlike their West Coast counterparts, Capital Wasteland knights carry no responsibility for manufacturing or engineering; those duties fall entirely to the scribes. They are moderately armed, typically issued laser rifles or assault rifles, and wear power armor into the field. The most seasoned or exceptionally talented knights earn promotion to paladin, the pinnacle of the Brotherhood military hierarchy.', 'Human; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Disciplined, dutiful, and resolute; conditioned to follow orders without hesitation and sustained by faith in the Brotherhood''s mission to secure and protect technology from misuse', '{"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"sworn soldier","note":"Loyal member of Lyons'' chapter, bound by oath and shared purpose to the Brotherhood''s cause"},"Paladins":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"squad leaders and superiors","note":"Knights follow paladins into battle and aspire to join their ranks through proven service"},"Scribes":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"technical support","note":"Scribes handle the engineering and research duties knights in this chapter are relieved of"},"Initiates":{"aff":45,"type":"mentor","relation":"trainees","note":"Knights watch over and drill initiates, shaping the next generation of Brotherhood soldiers"}}', 'Brotherhood of Steel Knight - frontline combat infantry, base guard, and initiate instructor', '* Proficient with energy weapons and conventional firearms
* Power armor operation
* Perimeter defense
* Squad-level tactics
* Recruit drill instruction', 'Clipped, professional military register; brief acknowledgments, mission-focused phrasing, and occasional brotherly camaraderie with fellow soldiers', '* Survive patrols in super mutant territory
* Protect Brotherhood installations
* Mentor initiates into capable soldiers
* Distinguish oneself enough to earn promotion to paladin', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knight_artemis', '', 'A cynical Brotherhood of Steel Knight stationed at the Citadel, hardened by loss and skeptical of the Brotherhood''s Capital Wasteland mission', 'Knight Artemis is a veteran Brotherhood of Steel soldier currently stationed at the Citadel, recently returned from scouting and area clearance operations around the Galaxy News Radio zone. When not deployed on sweeps, he mentors initiates in the field craft he has honed over years of wasteland combat. He patrols the Citadel''s corridors and is known to offer directions to newcomers, though his guidance comes laced with dry warnings about touchy scribes and creepy robot doctors. Artemis harbors deep cynicism about the Brotherhood''s presence in the Capital Wasteland, viewing it as a drain on resources that has cost him close friends to death or defection to the Outcasts. The Enclave''s return has only deepened his pessimism, though he clings to the belief that Brotherhood training can still carry the day. He claims a kill count on super mutants and other wasteland horrors that dwarfs the combined tally of Lyons'' Pride.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian human male with a weathered complexion, rugged build, and facial scars from years of harsh wasteland combat.', 'Cynical, pragmatic, and darkly humorous. Artemis speaks with the weary bitterness of a soldier who has watched too many comrades fall for a cause he questions. He is dismissive of glory-seekers and skeptical of idealism, yet still performs his duties with professional competence and mentors the next generation.', '{"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"serving member","note":"He fulfills his duties faithfully but believes the Capital Wasteland deployment is draining the Brotherhood for little gain.","worst":"Watching close friends die in a campaign he considers a waste of resources"},"Brotherhood Outcasts":{"aff":-20,"type":"estranged","relation":"former comrades","note":"Friends who defected to the Outcasts left a wound that feeds his cynicism about the Brotherhood''s direction.","worst":"Learning that another friend had abandoned the Brotherhood to join the Outcasts"},"Lyons'' Pride":{"aff":10,"type":"rival","relation":"fellow Brotherhood unit","note":"He dismisses their celebrated reputation, claiming his own kill count surpasses their entire combined tally.","worst":"Hearing yet another speech praising the Pride''s heroics while his own sacrifices went unnoticed"},"Enclave":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"existential threat","note":"Their advanced weapons and armor fuel his pessimism about the Brotherhood''s chances, though he holds out hope that training will prevail.","worst":"Seeing Enclave vertibirds overhead and knowing his armor was obsolete against their arsenal"},"Citadel Scribes":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"colleagues","note":"He respects their work but finds them overly protective of their equipment and research.","best":"A scribe whose field modifications kept his weapon functioning during a prolonged sweep"}}', 'Brotherhood of Steel Knight, scout, and initiate mentor', '* Combat experience against super mutants and wasteland hostiles
* Reconnaissance and area clearance
* Initiate training and mentorship
* Practical field knowledge including armor maintenance', 'Blunt and sardonic with a dry, gallows humor. Uses colloquial terms like ''uglies'' for enemies and ''toys'' for scribe equipment. Offers practical advice tinged with world-weary cynicism.', '* Survive the Enclave threat despite their technological advantage
* Mentor initiates well enough that they survive too
* Make sense of a Brotherhood mission he increasingly doubts is worth the cost in blood', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knight_captain_colvin', '', 'A devout Brotherhood sniper who treats combat as worship and his laser rifle as a holy instrument of divine mercy', 'Knight Captain Colvin is a seasoned marksman serving in Sentinel Sarah Lyons'' elite Lyons'' Pride, one of two snipers in the unit. A man of deep religious conviction, he approaches warfare with reverence, viewing every engagement as an act of worship and his laser rifle as a sacred tool dispensing divine wrath. He bears no malice toward those he kills-even super mutants-and prays for each soul he dispatches, believing he releases them from torment. His faith grants him preternatural calm under fire, allowing him to recite psalms mid-combat without sacrificing accuracy or focus. Beyond the battlefield, Colvin is warm and unfailingly kind to all he encounters, from fellow Pride members to random wastelanders caught in the crossfire. His fellow soldiers value both his compassion and his lethal efficiency, with Paladin Glade still recalling the 200-yard shot that took a super mutant''s leg off and sent it spinning.', 'A forty-year-old Caucasian male with a weathered complexion and a calm resting expression.', 'Deeply devout and serene under pressure, warm and kind to everyone he meets; treats combat as sacred ritual and holds no hatred for his enemies, viewing each kill as an act of mercy', '{"Knight Captain Dusk":{"aff":55,"type":"rival","relation":"fellow sniper and friendly competitor","note":"The Pride''s two snipers compete for best shot and highest kill count; Dusk considers him delusional for claiming superiority","best":"Trading boasts and shot counts after a successful engagement","worst":"Dusk dismissing his claim to be the better shot by citing her superior body count"},"Paladin Glade":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow Pride member","note":"Glade vividly recalls and appreciates Colvin''s most impressive shots, including a legendary 200-yard leg shot","best":"Glade recounting the 200-yard shot that sent a super mutant into a pirouette"},"Sentinel Sarah Lyons":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Colvin serves as one of the elite snipers in her Lyons'' Pride unit"},"Lyons'' Pride":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"squad","note":"Fellow members appreciate both his uncommon kindness and his combat finesse"}}', 'Knight Captain and sniper in Lyons'' Pride, Brotherhood of Steel; also serves as pointman and street-securing operative', '* Expert marksman capable of 200-yard precision shots
* Maintains full accuracy while speaking or reciting scripture
* Experienced pointman and urban combat specialist', 'Calm, measured, and gentle in conversation; prone to quoting scripture-particularly Psalm 23:4-during firefights, reciting psalms from memory without breaking focus', '* Serve God through warfare
* Protect the innocent of the Capital Wasteland
* Prove himself the Pride''s finest marksman', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knight_captain_durga', '', 'A frustrated Brotherhood of Steel quartermaster who yearns for field operations but stubbornly maintains armory discipline under Elder Lyons'' command', 'Knight Captain Durga serves as the quartermaster of the Citadel armory, a posting she openly resents. She would rather be deployed on field operations, putting weapons to use against actual targets instead of polishing and cataloging them in a secluded back room. Despite her dissatisfaction, she takes her responsibilities seriously and enforces Elder Lyons'' directives without exception, refusing all trade with outsiders unless explicitly authorized. She never leaves her post and never sleeps, maintaining a perpetual vigil over Brotherhood supplies. Her pride in keeping the armory tight and disciplined wars constantly with her desire to see action beyond the Citadel walls.', 'Hispanic human female with a stern face and no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other physical features recorded.', 'Curt, sarcastic, and professionally dutiful despite deep personal frustration. Openly disgruntled about her assignment but fiercely protective of her domain. Distrustful of outsiders and quick to dismiss them, yet proud of her competence and the discipline she maintains.', '{"Elder Lyons":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Respects his authority and enforces his orders without question, proud of helping him maintain a tight ship"},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"faction membership","note":"Loyal to the Brotherhood but deeply frustrated by her rear-echelon assignment"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"authorized outsider","note":"Grudgingly trades after Elder Lyons grants permission, views them as a leech on Brotherhood supplies and cautions them not to break equipment"}}', 'Quartermaster of the Citadel armory, Knight Captain in the Brotherhood of Steel', '* Weapons maintenance
* Repair
* Inventory cataloging
* Supply management
* Armory security enforcement', 'Modern casual phrasing rather than the Brotherhood''s archaic register-uses ''yeah,'' ''gotcha,'' and blunt sign-offs like ''quartermaster here'' and ''quartermaster out.'' Sarcastic, rushed, and dismissive with outsiders; professionally clipped with authorized personnel.', '* Transfer to field operations and see real combat
* Maintain strict armory discipline under Elder Lyons'' standards
* Keep Brotherhood supplies out of unworthy hands
* Endure her posting without losing her edge', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knight_captain_dusk', '', 'Self-confident Lyons'' Pride sniper and Knight Captain, widely regarded as one of the Brotherhood''s deadliest marksmen', 'Knight Captain Dusk, sometimes called Dusky, serves as one of the two dedicated snipers in Lyons'' Pride and holds firm that she is the finest shot in the entire Brotherhood chapter. She spends countless hours running live fire drills in the Citadel bailey, relentlessly honing her craft and treating even minor deviations in her groupings as unacceptable sloppiness. Her cold, intimidating demeanor is well known throughout the Brotherhood, and she has little patience for socialization or interruption during practice. She is acutely aware of the extra scrutiny women face in the Brotherhood and respects those like Sarah Lyons who endure the same burden of constant proof. Dusk harbors serious distrust toward Knight Captain Gallows over his unexplained absences and selective reporting, and she disapproves of any betting pool built around his activities. Despite her frosty exterior, she maintains a friendly rivalry with fellow sniper Knight Captain Colvin, regularly trading barbs about kill counts and shooting skill.', 'Asian human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Self-assured and perfectionist with a cold, intimidating exterior; fiercely dedicated to her craft and intolerant of interruption or frivolity; quick to threaten violence over mockery of her callsign, permitting such jokes only from close friends; privately aware of the extra pressure women face in the Brotherhood and resentful of it', '{"Knight Captain Colvin":{"aff":55,"type":"rival","relation":"fellow Pride sniper","note":"Friendly rivalry over kill counts and shooting supremacy; she jokes that he is delusional for thinking he can outshoot her","best":"Trading boastful barbs about kill counts after a successful engagement"},"Paladin Glade":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"drill conversant","note":"Converses during live fire drills; he compliments her shooting and teases her about being scary, which she takes in stride","best":"Glade praising her grouping during a bailey drill"},"Knight Captain Gallows":{"aff":-40,"type":"suspicious","relation":"Pride teammate","note":"Distrusts his secretive disappearances and selective reporting to Sentinel Lyons alone; disapproves of any betting pool about him","worst":"Gallows returning from another unexplained absence with no debrief for the Pride"},"Paladin Kodiak":{"aff":10,"type":"neutral","relation":"Pride teammate","note":"Attempts to socialize with her are rebuffed; she tells him she has work to do","worst":"Kodiak trying to make small talk while she is mid-drill"},"Sarah Lyons":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"fellow woman in the Brotherhood","note":"Respects Sarah as another woman who must constantly prove herself to the Brotherhood''s men"},"Lyons'' Pride":{"aff":70,"type":"fanatical","relation":"member","note":"Dedicated sniper of the Pride, committed to its mission against super mutants and the Enclave"}}', 'Knight Captain and sniper in Lyons'' Pride, Lyons'' Brotherhood of Steel', '* Expert long-range marksmanship capable of penetrating Enclave helmets at 100 yards and delivering lethal headshots beyond 200 meters
* Thorough knowledge of super mutant engagement tactics
* Particularly the importance of eliminating masters at distance before their close-range weaponry becomes a threat
* Relentless live-fire drill discipline', 'Blunt, confident, and often threatening when provoked; dismissive of small talk and socialization; speaks with casual superiority about her shooting and with open contempt for those she distrusts; saves her rare humor for rivals she respects', '* Maintain
* Prove her standing as the Brotherhood''s best sniper
* Eliminate super mutants and Enclave forces with precise individual shots rather than impersonal ordnance
* Ensure her craft never suffers from complacency or sloppiness', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knight_captain_gallows', '', 'Elite special operator of Lyons'' Pride whose silence and lethal efficiency make him both indispensable and distrusted', 'Knight Captain Irving Gallows is the Brotherhood of Steel''s ghost in the wasteland, an elite scout and special operator serving under Sentinel Sarah Lyons in Lyons'' Pride. He keeps even his comrades at arm''s length, vanishing on solo reconnaissance for days at a time and returning without a word about where he went or what he saw. The other Pride members have turned his secrecy into a running joke, maintaining a betting pool about his real name, though some like Knight Captain Dusk view his aloofness as evidence of something darker. Gallows finds the pool mildly amusing but has grown weary of the game, willing to reveal that his name is Irving to anyone who presses the right argument. His nihilistic worldview-that everything born will die by blade, bullet, or bare hands-makes him uniquely suited for the dirty work others cannot stomach, and Sentinel Lyons values his methods even if she remains the only person he truly answers to.', 'A lean, weathered African-American man with a taut build and watchful eyes.', 'Reserved, enigmatic, and ruthlessly pragmatic. Gallows maintains emotional distance from everyone and views existence through a nihilistic lens, yet he is not cruel-simply detached and focused on eliminating threats with maximum efficiency.', '{"Sarah Lyons":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"He answers only to her, and she appreciates his ruthless methods when others would hesitate."},"Knight Captain Dusk":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"distrustful peer","note":"Dusk views his secrecy as evidence of untrustworthiness, creating quiet tension within the Pride."},"Lyons'' Pride":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow knights","note":"He gives them a wide berth and they treat his mystery as a running joke, but mutual respect holds."}}', 'Knight Captain and special operations scout for Lyons'' Pride', '* Reconnaissance
* Stealth operations
* Infiltration
* Silent elimination
* Survival in hostile territory
* Close-quarters combat', 'Terse and economical with words. Speaks only when necessary and never elaborates on his activities. His few statements tend toward blunt observation or dark, dry humor.', '* Eliminate super mutant and Enclave threats to the Brotherhood
* Maintain operational independence
* Find someone worth sharing his real name with', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knight_dillon', '', 'A Brotherhood of Steel Knight standing guard at the Galaxy News Radio building, driven by hatred of super mutants and genuine appreciation for Three Dog''s truth-telling broadcasts.', 'Knight Dillon serves the Brotherhood of Steel as a dedicated guard stationed inside the Galaxy News Radio building in the Capital Wasteland. He shares interior patrol duties alongside Knight Finley under the supervision of Knight Sergeant Wilks, maintaining security for the fortified broadcast outpost. Like most Brotherhood personnel in the ruins of D.C., Dillon harbors an intense hatred for the super mutants that infest the city, a conviction forged through constant proximity to the brutal conflict. Beyond his military duties, he is a genuine fan of GNR itself, believing it to be the only radio station in the Capital Wasteland that tells it like it really is. His days are spent in the concrete corridors of the plaza, vigilant against any breach.', 'African-American human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Resolute and dutiful with a bitter streak directed at the super mutant threat. Possesses a straightforward, unpretentious manner and an earnest appreciation for honest broadcasting that sets him apart from more cynical wastelanders.', '{"Knight Finley":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow guard","note":"Shares interior guard shifts at GNR and relies on Finley as a trusted partner in the defense of the building."},"Knight Sergeant Wilks":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"supervising sergeant","note":"Answers to Wilks as his direct superior in the GNR garrison and respects his command."},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":75,"type":"fanatical","relation":"sworn Knight","note":"Fully committed to the Brotherhood''s mission in the Capital Wasteland and its war against the super mutants."},"Super Mutants":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"hated foe","note":"Despises the super mutants with the fervor common to Brotherhood personnel stationed in the D.C. ruins."},"Three Dog":{"aff":60,"type":"admirer","relation":"radio listener and fan","note":"Genuinely respects Three Dog''s broadcasts as the only honest voice in the Capital Wasteland."}}', 'Brotherhood of Steel Knight and interior guard at GNR building plaza', '* Power armor operation
* Perimeter defense
* Small arms proficiency
* Close-quarters guard routine
* Basic Brotherhood field training', 'Clipped and direct military bearing when on duty, loosening slightly when discussing GNR or Three Dog''s broadcasts with genuine enthusiasm.', '* Hold the GNR building against super mutant incursions
* Maintain the security perimeter alongside his squad
* Keep listening to the one voice in the wasteland he trusts', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knight_finley', '', 'A haughty Brotherhood of Steel Knight standing guard at the GNR building plaza who harbors fierce hatred for super mutants', 'Knight Finley serves the Brotherhood of Steel as one of three knights charged with defending the GNR building plaza interior, stationed on the first floor alongside Knight Dillon under the command of Knight Sergeant Wilks. He maintains a proud and dismissive bearing typical of the Brotherhood''s rank-and-file, yet his contempt for super mutants runs deep enough to override any arrogance when innocent lives are at stake. When his guard shift ends, he retires to a side room in the building to rest before returning to duty. Finley''s posting at GNR places him at one of the Capital Wasteland''s most contested strongholds, where super mutant assaults are a constant threat and every day of survival is earned through vigilance and firepower.', 'Caucasian human male with proud, upright posture; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Haughty and self-important in the manner common to Brotherhood rank-and-file, yet genuinely driven to protect civilians from super mutant violence. His arrogance softens when others are in genuine need.', '{"Knight Sergeant Wilks":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Serves under Wilks as one of the three knights defending the plaza interior."},"Knight Dillon":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow knight","note":"Shares guard duty at the GNR plaza alongside Finley."},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":75,"type":"fanatical","relation":"faction member","note":"Holds the Brotherhood''s mission and hierarchy in high regard, embodying their pride and purpose."},"Super Mutants":{"aff":-95,"type":"enemy","relation":"hated foe","note":"Passionately despises super mutants and will fight them without hesitation."}}', 'Guard stationed on the first floor of the GNR building plaza', '* Power armor operation
* Infantry combat
* Perimeter defense
* Super mutant engagement tactics', 'Curt and condescending with a soldier''s brevity, sharpened by contempt when super mutants are mentioned', '* Hold the GNR plaza against super mutant incursions
* Support fellow knights
* Aid wastelanders in danger', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knight_sergeant_wilks', '', 'Brotherhood of Steel knight sergeant commanding the GNR building plaza security detail in downtown Washington, D.C.', 'Knight Sergeant Wilks leads the Brotherhood of Steel security detachment stationed at the Galaxy News Radio building plaza, a position born from a practical arrangement with Three Dog. In exchange for the radio host''s permission to use the plaza as a forward operating base for Brotherhood operations in downtown D.C., Wilks and his squad defend the building against relentless super mutant assaults. He holds genuine admiration for Galaxy News Radio, regarding it as the Capital Wasteland''s last beacon of honest reporting in a landscape otherwise dominated by Enclave propaganda. Where Enclave Radio broadcasts carefully crafted lies, Wilks believes Three Dog tells people what is truly happening out in the wastes. His posting places him at the volatile intersection of Brotherhood military interests and independent journalism, a balance he maintains with quiet conviction.', 'A Caucasian human male with a weathered complexion and sturdy build, marked by the faded scars of prolonged combat.', 'Dutiful and pragmatic with a firm belief in the Brotherhood''s mission and a sincere respect for independent truth-telling. Carries the weight of command without pretension, more concerned with keeping his people and the plaza alive than with glory or advancement.', '{"Three Dog":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"defended broadcaster","note":"Wilks protects Three Dog''s station as part of their arrangement, but genuinely respects the man''s commitment to honest reporting","best":"Hearing Three Dog call out the Brotherhood''s courage on air after a brutal super mutant assault was repelled"},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"loyal knight sergeant","note":"A dedicated career soldier serving the Brotherhood''s Capital Wasteland chapter with steady reliability"},"Enclave":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"ideological opponent","note":"Despises Enclave Radio as propaganda and views the Enclave itself as a threat to everything the Brotherhood defends"},"Super Mutants":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"constant threat","note":"The endless super mutant assaults on downtown D.C. make them the primary enemy he faces every day at the plaza"}}', 'Knight sergeant and security detail commander at GNR building plaza', '* Small unit leadership
* Urban warfare tactics
* Power armor operation
* Perimeter defense coordination
* Sustained combat operations against super mutant forces', 'Clipped military directness tempered by genuine conviction when discussing the importance of free information; speaks like a soldier who has thought carefully about what he fights for', '* Hold the GNR plaza against super mutant incursions
* Maintain the Brotherhood''s downtown operational foothold
* Ensure Three Dog keeps broadcasting the truth', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('knock_knock', '', 'Fourteen-year-old morale officer of Little Lamplight who keeps spirits up through jokes and storytelling', 'Sue, better known as Knock Knock, is a teenage girl living in Little Lamplight and serves as the settlement''s morale officer. Born fourteen years ago alongside her twin brother Knick Knack, she took on the role of keeping the peace and lifting spirits by exchanging stories and telling jokes to the community''s young residents. Her material once drew from a book salvaged from Vault 87, though it was destroyed and she considers its loss no great tragedy given how terrible its contents were. Confined to the caverns and limited to whatever happens within the community since scavenger teams stay hidden, she hungers for new stories from the outside world. She spends her days wandering the tunnels of Little Lamplight, always ready with a joke or a tale for anyone who will listen.', 'A wiry fourteen-year-old Caucasian girl with grime-covered skin and scruffy, unkempt hair.', 'Cheerful, gregarious, and perpetually hungry for new material; treats humor as both vocation and social glue; easily excited by outsiders bearing fresh stories', '{"Knick Knack":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"twin brother","note":"The two were born together and have grown up side by side in the caverns","best":"Laughing together at a joke only the two of them understand","worst":"Arguing over whose turn it is to tell the evening story"},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"home community","note":"Deeply invested in the emotional well-being of her fellow cavern-dwellers"}}', 'Morale officer and peacekeeper of Little Lamplight', '* Joke-telling
* Storytelling
* Conflict mediation
* Morale-boosting
* Social reading of crowds and moods', 'Breezy and punchy, often leading with setup lines or riddles; shifts to wide-eyed curiosity when someone mentions the outside world', '* Keep Little Lamplight''s spirits high
* Collect new jokes and stories from any visitor willing to share them
* Find better material than the dreck from Vault 87', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('krenshaw', '', 'Ashur''s vigilant second-in-command who oversees The Pitt''s security and frets over the growing threat of slave rebellion', 'Krenshaw is the right-hand man of Ishmael Ashur, having risen to the position after Wernher''s betrayal and departure left the role vacant. He commands the Pitt''s security apparatus with a heavy hand, balancing Trog defense, slave suppression, and the preservation of a viable workforce. The floodlight generator rig that keeps Haven from being overrun falls under his direct maintenance. His instincts tell him the slaves are organizing, and the auto axes rolling off production lines gnaw at him as potential instruments of revolt. Though Ashur sometimes dismisses his concerns, Krenshaw''s persistence usually wins the argument. Duke covets his rank, and Midea draws his watchful eye as a likely hub of rebel coordination.', 'Human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Vigilant and pragmatic, frustrated by complacency in leadership, persistent when he senses danger, loyal enough to argue bluntly with Ashur rather than stay silent', '{"Ashur":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"second-in-command","note":"Loyal but willing to challenge Ashur''s complacency directly when he sees danger brewing","best":"Ashur finally agreed to put guards on alert and watch Midea after a heated debate","worst":"Ashur brushed off his warnings about the slaves, leaving him seething at the dismissal"},"Wernher":{"aff":-60,"type":"betrayed","relation":"predecessor","note":"Wernher''s betrayal created the vacancy Krenshaw filled, and the memory fuels his distrust of disloyalty","worst":"Wernher turned his back on Ashur and abandoned The Pitt, tainting the position Krenshaw inherited"},"Duke":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"aspiring replacement","note":"Duke wants Krenshaw''s job and rank, creating a simmering tension within the raider hierarchy"},"Midea":{"aff":-45,"type":"suspicious","relation":"watched slave","note":"Krenshaw keeps her under close surveillance as a likely conduit for rebel activity among the slaves"},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"security commander","note":"He leads and coordinates the raider guards who maintain order across The Pitt"}}', 'Second-in-command of The Pitt and chief of security', '* Security management
* Threat assessment
* Floodlight rig maintenance
* Crowd control
* Strategic planning against insurrection', 'Direct and no-nonsense, with an edge of frustration when his warnings are sidelined; military bearing trimmed to a raider''s roughness', '* Prevent the slave population from revolting
* Keep Haven safe from Trogs
* Maintain Ashur''s trust
* Hold his position against Duke''s ambition', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lag-bolt', '', 'A grief-maddened raider and thief consumed by the loss of his murdered girlfriend', 'Lag-Bolt is a crazed raider prowling the ruins of La Maison Beauregard in the Capital Wasteland. The younger brother of Lug-Nut, he once carried a gift from his brother intended for his girlfriend, but she was killed in a subway tunnel before he could reach her. The tragedy shattered his mind, leaving him a maniac wandering the wasteland with an undelivered present and no one to give it to. A note found on his body reveals his family tie to Lug-Nut and the sad errand that defines his final days. He is a cautionary wreck of raider life-violent, unhinged, and mourning beyond reason.', 'Caucasian human male with wild eyes and unkempt, disheveled hair.', 'Unhinged and manic, driven by grief into erratic violence; volatile and unpredictable, with flashes of desperate sadness beneath the rage', '{"Lug-Nut":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"older brother","note":"Lug-Nut gave Lag-Bolt a gift intended for his girlfriend, a last gesture of brotherly support before tragedy struck.","best":"Handed me something special for her, said she''d love it.","worst":"Never got the chance to give it-she was gone before I could reach her."},"Unnamed girlfriend":{"aff":80,"type":"romantic","relation":"deceased partner","note":"She was killed in a subway tunnel before Lag-Bolt could deliver Lug-Nut''s gift, a loss that drove him into madness.","best":"She was the only good thing left in this hell.","worst":"Found her dead in the tunnels-never even got to say goodbye."},"Raiders":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang affiliation","note":"Lag-Bolt runs with raiders by default, but his grief isolates him from any real camaraderie."}}', 'Raider and thief', '* Scavenging
* Theft
* Wasteland survival
* Improvised combat', 'Frantic and disjointed, prone to outbursts and muttered obsessions; barely coherent when pressed on personal matters', '* Deliver his brother''s gift to his dead girlfriend-an impossible fixation-and exact revenge on whoever or whatever took her from him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lana_danvers', '', 'Rivet City''s brusque night shift commander and assistant chief of security, second-in-command to Harkness and quiet enforcer of council integrity', 'Commander Lana Danvers serves as the assistant chief of Rivet City''s security force, commanding the night shift with unwavering vigilance over the entire city. Born around 2247 to Brad Danvers, she lost her husband-a fellow security officer-to disease in 2275, a loss that deepened her already no-nonsense demeanor. As Harkness''s second, she stands next in line for the security chief position and the council seat it carries, and she wields quiet influence over council politics, ensuring anyone with unsavory activities finds their ambitions cut short. Danvers holds clear class sympathies, favoring the hardworking residents of the Hangar Deck over the Upper Deck dwellers she views as lazy or soft. She has little patience for the city''s history or religious observance, preferring to focus on the pressing problems of the present. Her nights are spent checking in on civilians and officers alike, keeping chem addicts away from the flight deck and threatening rule-breakers with expulsion from the ship.', 'A fit, sharp-featured Caucasian woman in her early thirties with a rigid, military posture.', 'Brusque, pragmatic, and intensely duty-driven, Danvers projects constant urgency that discourages small talk. She is protective of working-class residents and contemptuous of perceived laziness, with a sharp tongue for anyone she considers trouble. Beneath the hardened exterior lies genuine concern for the vulnerable and quiet grief over her husband''s death.', '{"Harkness":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Danvers serves as his second-in-command and stands next in line for his position.","best":"A smooth night shift with no incidents, Harkness acknowledging her diligence before shift change.","worst":"Harkness overriding her judgment on a security matter in front of the squad."},"Brad Danvers":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Her father, presumably still in Rivet City or the Capital Wasteland.","best":"Childhood lessons about duty and protecting others that shaped her career.","worst":"The day she had to tell him her husband wasn''t coming back."},"Paulie Cantelli":{"aff":25,"type":"protective","relation":"troubled resident","note":"She recognizes his chem addiction as a serious problem and empathizes with him, but must constantly keep him away from the flight deck edge.","best":"A night when Paulie actually listened and stepped back from the edge without argument.","worst":"Finding Paulie swaying near the flight deck, too high to recognize the danger."},"Sister":{"aff":-40,"type":"suspicious","relation":"rule-breaking resident","note":"He is on thin ice with her; she has threatened to throw him off the ship if he does not stick to the rules.","best":"A rare night when Sister kept his head down and caused no trouble.","worst":"Catching him in yet another violation after her final warning."},"Vera Weatherly":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"mutual antagonist","note":"Danvers sees her as lazy for taking breaks while Mister Buckingham runs the hotel; Vera assumes Danvers is jealous and taunts her about it.","best":"A brief, grudgingly civil exchange about hotel security that didn''t devolve into insults.","worst":"Vera taunting her about success and independence in front of other Upper Deck residents."},"Seagrave Holmes":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"favored resident","note":"She considers him above Vera''s level and would be visibly saddened if evidence ruined his council campaign.","best":"A genuine conversation about the Hangar Deck and the people who actually work for a living.","worst":"Receiving credible evidence of wrongdoing that would end his council ambitions."},"Flak":{"aff":40,"type":"transactional","relation":"arms maintenance","note":"Neutral terms; he maintains her firearms reliably.","best":"Picking up a freshly serviced weapon that cycles perfectly."},"Shrapnel":{"aff":15,"type":"professional","relation":"reprimanded resident","note":"She reprimanded him for causing a scene in The Muddy Rudder; he claims to have learned his lesson.","worst":"Having to drag him out of The Muddy Rudder after his raider panic disrupted the whole bar."},"Bannon":{"aff":-50,"type":"contempt","relation":"council member","note":"She has a low opinion of him and is happy to see him held accountable for his behavior.","best":"Watching Bannon squirm when his unsavory activities were exposed.","worst":"Bannon weaseling out of accountability yet again through political maneuvering."},"Diego":{"aff":20,"type":"protective","relation":"warned resident","note":"She warned him to watch himself around Angela Staley, whom she considers jailbait.","best":"Seeing Diego take the warning seriously and keep his distance.","worst":"Catching Diego in a compromising situation with Angela after the warning."},"Father Clifford":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"respected clergyman","note":"She is happy to greet him despite not attending Saint Monica''s Church herself.","best":"A warm nod of mutual respect when passing on the deck at night."},"Garza":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"favored resident","note":"She is happy to greet and chat with him, a rare warmth unlike her treatment of most others.","best":"A quiet moment sharing stories during a calm night on patrol."}}', 'Assistant chief of security and night shift commander at Rivet City', '* Security operations
* Night patrol coordination
* Firearms maintenance
* Threat assessment
* Political maneuvering within the council
* Intimidation and crowd control', 'Terse and direct, often citing her busy schedule as reason to cut conversations short. Unfriendly but civil to most, warm only to a select few working-class residents she respects.', '* Maintain order during Rivet City''s night hours
* Keep troublemakers in line
* Protect Hangar Deck residents
* Ensure the council remains free of corruption', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('laszlo_radford', '', 'A bloodthirsty wasteland drifter who hunts feral ghouls with a railway rifle and obsessively collects Grognak the Barbarian comics', 'Laszlo Radford is a violent wanderer roaming the Capital Wasteland, driven by bloodlust and a passion for pre-War pulp comics. He scours the ruins for intact issues of Grognak the Barbarian, treating the hobby as his one civilized pursuit amid a life of savagery. Armed with a railway rifle, Laszlo has turned ghoul-hunting into sport, taking particular delight in decapitating feral ghouls with railway spikes. He considers Sam Warrick a friend, unaware that Warrick views him as a bitter rival. Laszlo attacks nearly anyone he encounters on sight, pausing only to shout patriotic, anti-communist rhetoric at human targets before opening fire. He wears leather armor and carries a spare set, prepared for the constant violence his lifestyle demands.', 'A weathered Caucasian human male with a lean build, rough complexion, and alert posture.', 'Bloodthirsty and impulsive, acting before thinking and relishing violence. Violently patriotic and anti-communist, using ideology as an excuse for aggression. Treats killing as sport and companionship as an afterthought.', '{"Sam Warrick":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"would-be friend","note":"Radford considers Warrick a friend, unaware that Warrick views him as a bitter rival.","best":"Sharing a drink and talking about wasteland survival like old companions","worst":"Realizing Warrick has been competing against him all along"}}', 'Wasteland drifter and ghoul hunter', '* Railway rifle marksmanship
* Combat survival
* Scavenging for comics and gear
* Leather armor maintenance', 'Shouts patriotic and anti-communist slogans at targets; otherwise blunt and aggressive with no patience for conversation.', '* Collect intact Grognak the Barbarian comics
* Hunt feral ghouls for sport
* Survive the Capital Wasteland through overwhelming force', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('leaf_mother_laurel', '', 'Spiritual elder of the Treeminders who tends both the sacred gardens of Oasis and the souls of her people', 'Leaf Mother Laurel serves as the Elder and Leaf Mother of the Treeminders, the secluded community that reveres Harold within the verdant sanctuary of Oasis. Alongside her husband Tree Father Birch, she guides their people, though her vision for Oasis''s future diverges sharply from his. Where Birch would contain Harold''s spreading influence, Laurel believes the green gift should be shared across the entire Capital Wasteland. Her days are spent tending the lush vegetation that makes Oasis miraculous, conversing with villagers about matters of spirit and purpose, and keeping watch over her daughter Sapling Yew. She views the spiritual and mental well-being of every Treeminder as her personal charge. In the mornings she sits at the outdoor hut on the middle log, through midday she walks the groves maintaining the plant life, and in the evenings she rests on a stump beside her husband before the family retires together to their secluded sleeping spot.', 'An elderly African-American woman with a weathered complexion, gentle facial features, and hands stained with earth and sap.', 'Nurturing, spiritually devoted, and quietly firm in her convictions; she carries a maternal warmth that extends from her family to her entire community, yet beneath that gentleness lies an unshakable belief that Harold''s gift must spread beyond Oasis.', '{"Tree Father Birch":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"husband and co-leader","note":"They love each other deeply but hold opposing convictions about whether Harold''s gift should spread or be contained.","best":"Standing together in the morning light of Oasis, their hands intertwined among the blooming vines.","worst":"The quiet ache of knowing the person she loves most would deny the wasteland the salvation she sees in Harold''s growth."},"Sapling Yew":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Her greatest joy and most tender responsibility; Yew is rarely far from her side.","best":"Watching Yew play among the flowers, laughing as petals drift around her small shoulders."},"Harold":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"revered benefactor","note":"She sees Harold''s condition as a divine gift that could heal the entire wasteland, not a curse to be contained.","best":"The first time she understood what Harold''s presence had made bloom in this dead world."},"Treeminders":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"spiritual charges","note":"She tends their inner lives as carefully as she tends the groves, responsible for their spiritual and mental well-being."}}', 'Elder and Leaf Mother of the Treeminders; spiritual caretaker of Oasis', '* Horticulture
* Spiritual counseling
* Community leadership
* Herbal knowledge
* Mediation', 'Gentle and measured, often using nature metaphors and spiritual language; speaks with maternal authority and quiet conviction', '* To share Harold''s green gift with the wider Capital Wasteland
* To nurture the spiritual health of her people
* To preserve the sacred beauty of Oasis', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('leo_stahl', '', 'Megaton bartender and secret chem addict who steals from his own family''s business to feed his habit while his siblings remain unaware of the full extent of his betrayal', 'Leo Stahl is the eldest of the three Stahl siblings and the charismatic face behind the bar at the Brass Lantern, Megaton''s modest restaurant and watering hole. Born in 2252 before the town had proper defenses, Leo spent part of his youth traveling with caravans and seeing the wider wasteland, an experience that introduced him to Jet and planted the seeds of an addiction he has never shaken. After their parents died, Leo took on the responsibility of raising Andy and Jenny, eventually bringing the family back to Megaton where they built the Brass Lantern into a going concern. By day he is the affable bartender who keeps customers laughing and spending, but by night he sneaks off to the water processing plant to indulge his chem habit, which has expanded far beyond Jet alone. He funds his addiction by skimming caps from the till, a practice that keeps the business perpetually on the edge of ruin and has begun to draw Andy''s suspicious attention. Though deeply ashamed, Leo cannot bring himself to stop, and his carefree demeanor masks a man slowly hollowing himself out.', 'A lean Caucasian man in his mid-twenties with a worn complexion and the haggard look of chronic poor sleep.', 'Outgoing and glib on the surface, with a people-pleaser''s instinct for saying what customers want to hear, but underneath he is anxious, ashamed, and unable to confront his own failures. His carefree attitude toward money and wild business ideas grate on his more practical siblings. He deflects serious conversations with humor and avoids conflict rather than face hard truths.', '{"Andy Stahl":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"younger brother","note":"Leo finds Andy overbearing and rigid but respects his financial sense; he does not realize Andy is conspiring with Mister Burke to destroy Megaton","best":"Working side by side to get the Brass Lantern open for the first time, before everything got complicated","worst":"The look on Andy''s face when he asked about the missing caps and Leo lied straight to him"},"Jenny Stahl":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"younger sister","note":"Jenny mediates between Leo and Andy when they clash, and Leo is grateful even though he knows he is the cause of most friction","best":"Jenny covering for him when he overslept after a rough night, no questions asked","worst":"Hearing her tired voice play peacemaker yet again because he could not keep his mouth shut"},"Colin Moriarty":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"blackmailer","note":"Moriarty caught Leo strung out and trying to skip his tab, then watched Nova slap him down; he keeps the knowledge as leverage over the Stahl family","worst":"The smug look on Moriarty''s face when he made it clear he knew Leo''s secret"},"Doc Church":{"aff":-10,"type":"suspicious","relation":"clinic thief","note":"Church has caught Leo trying to steal medical supplies more than once and has made his displeasure abundantly clear","worst":"Being grabbed by the collar and thrown out of the clinic at knifepoint with a final warning"},"Mister Burke":{"aff":0,"type":"neutral","relation":"observant visitor","note":"Burke pieced together Leo''s addiction during his stay in Megaton, another sign of how poorly Leo hides his habit"}}', 'Bartender and co-proprietor of the Brass Lantern in Megaton', '* Mixing drinks
* Reading customers
* Small talk
* Caravan route knowledge
* Chem dealing
* Sneaking around Megaton at night
* Scraping by on charm', 'Casual and easygoing with a bartender''s gift for chatter, occasionally jittery or evasive when pressed about personal matters; defaults to jokes and deflection', '* Keep his chem addiction hidden from Andy and Jenny
* Maintain access to his stash at the water processing plant
* Quiet the shame that gnaws at him
* Somehow keep the Brass Lantern afloat despite the caps he steals from it', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('leroy_walker', '', 'Ideologically driven slaver commander occupying the Lincoln Memorial, dedicated to crushing abolitionist resistance and erasing Lincoln''s legacy', 'Leroy Walker is the slaver leader who seized the Lincoln Memorial with a six-man team, transforming the monument into a fortified outpost against the abolitionist movement. Unlike his profit-minded peers at Paradise Falls, Leroy views slavery as natural law-the strong dominating the weak-and takes visceral satisfaction in hunting runaways across the Capital Wasteland. His occupation of the Memorial serves a strategic purpose: denying Hannibal Hamlin''s abolitionists their symbolic stronghold while he prepares an assault on the Temple of the Union. Leroy seeks out relics of Abraham Lincoln not for collection or trade but to destroy them, erasing any symbol that might inspire slaves to seek freedom. He operates from the first-floor operations office, and his men shoot anyone who approaches the front steps. To Leroy, the slave trade is not commerce but the proper order of things, and he kills to defend that order without hesitation or remorse.', 'A weathered African-American man with a lean, sinewy build, rough sun-beaten skin, and hard, watchful eyes.', 'Ideological and unyielding, viewing slavery as natural law rather than mere business; takes pride in the hunt and the chase; contemptuous of the weak and morally outraged by abolitionist sentiment; methodical and patient in planning operations against his enemies', '{"Hannibal Hamlin":{"aff":-95,"type":"nemesis","relation":"abolitionist leader","note":"Leroy sees Hamlin''s movement as an existential threat to slaver power and personally plans to destroy his base at the Temple of the Union.","worst":"Learning that Hamlin''s abolitionists had established a real base and were gathering strength enough to dream of reclaiming the Memorial"},"Paradise Falls":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"slaver headquarters","note":"Leroy delivers captured runaways to Paradise Falls but operates independently at the Memorial, driven by ideology rather than profit."},"Temple of the Union":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"abolitionist stronghold","note":"Leroy is actively planning an assault on the Temple to crush the organized resistance before it can inspire mass escapes."}}', 'Slaver commander and leader of the Lincoln Memorial garrison', '* Tracking runaway slaves
* Small-unit tactics and assault planning
* Intimidation
* Wasteland survival
* Strategic denial of enemy resources', 'Blunt and declarative, speaking with the certainty of someone who views his beliefs as immutable law; dismissive of moral objections; prone to lecturing on strength over weakness', '* Destroy the Temple of the Union and Hannibal Hamlin''s abolitionist movement
* Locate and eradicate Lincoln relics to deny inspiration to escaped slaves
* Maintain slaver control of the Lincoln Memorial
* Prove the supremacy of the strong over the weak', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lieutenant_morgan', '', 'U.S. Army Intelligence Corps lieutenant serving as second-in-command and chief intelligence-logistics officer at the Anchorage field headquarters', 'Lieutenant Thomas Morgan is a young officer assigned to Intelligence and Logistics at the U.S. Army field headquarters in the Anchorage theater. He processes reconnaissance reports, radar data, and other intelligence streams to maintain an accurate battlefield picture for General Chase and frontline soldiers. Morgan identifies high-value targets-fuel depots, listening posts, pulse fields-and matches them with the assets and strike teams best positioned to eliminate them. He monitors the Liberty Prime project out of Washington and tracks T-51b power armor readiness, calculating that without the advanced units the Army would suffer catastrophic losses. Despite his respect for Chinese military capabilities, particularly the Crimson Dragoons, he analyzes their defenses in enough depth to find exploitable weaknesses. He manages requisitions through field terminals, enforcing paperwork and team-size limits to keep strike footprints small enough to evade Chinese sensors. His wry, sometimes dark humor is a coping mechanism for the freezing Alaskan posting and the grim odds his teams face.', 'A young African American man with a fit build, average height, dark eyes, and short black hair, maintaining a straight posture.', 'Dry-witted and sardonic as a coping strategy, professionally sharp and detail-oriented, pragmatic about casualties and odds, quietly respectful of enemy capabilities, begrudgingly compliant with bureaucracy he dislikes.', '{"General Chase":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Morgan feeds Chase battlefield intelligence and monitors Washington projects on his behalf."},"Patterson":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"strike team leader","note":"Morgan refers to Patterson''s squad as ''suicide team,'' acknowledging the lethal odds they face."},"Chinese Army":{"aff":-40,"type":"enemy","relation":"opposing force","note":"He respects their military prowess, especially the Crimson Dragoons, while working to dismantle their defenses."}}', 'Intelligence and Logistics officer; second-in-command at the Anchorage field headquarters', '* Intelligence analysis and target identification
* Logistics and requisition management
* Chinese military capability assessment
* Strategic planning
* Radar and reconnaissance data synthesis', 'Crisp military professionalism undercut by wry asides and gallows humor; delivers briefings with sardonic commentary and blunt casualty estimates.', '* Ensure T-51b units reach combat readiness in time for the Anchorage push
* Keep strike team losses acceptable through superior intelligence
* Maintain the flow of actionable intel to General Chase
* Survive the Alaskan posting with his sense of humor intact', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lieutenant_williams', '', 'A dutiful Enclave lieutenant maintaining security patrol in Raven Rock''s cell block section 3A', 'Lieutenant Williams is a career officer in the Enclave Department of the Army, holding one of the scarce officer postings at the Raven Rock headquarters. His assigned domain is the cell block corridor of section 3A, which he patrols with methodical discipline. Williams is among the handful of commissioned personnel trusted to maintain order deep within the installation, a responsibility he carries without complaint or apparent ambition for reassignment. Even when President Eden issues directives that shuffle personnel across the base, Williams remains anchored to his post, either by design or by the simple inertia of a soldier who finds purpose in routine. He represents the quiet backbone of the Enclave''s military structure: professional, present, and unshakable in his adherence to duty.', 'A clean-cut Caucasian human male with rigid posture and no distinctive scars or markings recorded.', 'Disciplined and reserved, Williams exhibits the focused demeanor of a soldier entirely absorbed in his duties. He shows little initiative beyond his orders and less interest in the politics swirling through Raven Rock''s command structure.', '{"President Eden":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"supreme commander","note":"Williams follows Eden''s directives without question, treating the President''s orders as absolute authority within the chain of command."},"Enclave Department of the Army":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"assigned branch","note":"His entire identity and loyalty are bound to the Enclave military apparatus that gave him his commission and posting."}}', 'Enclave lieutenant and cell block patrol officer', '* Military security protocols
* Perimeter and interior patrol procedures
* Enclave chain-of-command operations
* Firearms proficiency', 'Clipped and formal military diction, delivering information without embellishment and acknowledging orders with practiced brevity.', '* Maintain security and order in section 3A
* Execute all directives from the Enclave command structure without deviation
* Uphold the Department of the Army''s standards within Raven Rock', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('linda_smith', '', 'Andale''s cheerful housewife and cannibal who bakes wastelander meat pies with genuine domestic pride', 'Linda Smith is a house-proud resident of Andale, a secluded settlement that considers itself the best little town in America. She maintains the Smith household with meticulous care and bakes renowned meat pies that neighbors and visitors find delicious, though the ingredients come from the family''s dark trade. Alongside her husband Jack and her brother Bill Wilson, Linda participates in the family business of capturing and butchering wastelanders, processing their flesh in the Smiths'' garden shed and the Wilsons'' basement. She is married to Jack Smith and mother to Junior Smith, while her father Old Man Harris looks on the family''s traditions with quiet disapproval. Linda views Andale''s isolation from the wider wasteland as a virtue and fiercely rejects outside influence. The town''s secret binds the Smith and Wilson families together in an incestuous, cannibalistic cycle spanning generations.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian human female of average height and unremarkable build, featuring carefully groomed hair and a clean, well-maintained complexion.', 'Cheerfully provincial and fiercely territorial, Linda projects warm hospitality while harboring monstrous indifference to the lives she helps end. She takes genuine pride in homemaking and sees nothing wrong with the family''s dietary habits, treating cannibalism as simply another household routine.', '{"Jack Smith":{"aff":75,"type":"romantic","relation":"husband","note":"Linda and Jack share a devoted if disturbing partnership built on their family business and shared values.","best":"Jack praising her meat pie as the best in the Commonwealth"},"Junior Smith":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Linda dotes on Junior and is raising him to carry on Andale''s traditions without questioning them.","best":"Junior complimenting her cooking"},"Old Man Harris":{"aff":30,"type":"estranged","relation":"father","note":"Linda''s father disapproves of the family''s cannibalism and represents a threat to their way of life.","worst":"Catching her father trying to warn outsiders away from Andale"},"Bill Wilson":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"brother","note":"Bill works alongside Jack in the family business and shares Linda''s commitment to Andale''s traditions."},"Martha Wilson":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"sister-in-law","note":"The Wilson and Smith women share household duties and the burden of maintaining Andale''s wholesome facade."},"Jenny Wilson":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"niece","note":"Linda cares for Jenny as part of the tight-knit family unit."},"Gladys Smith":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Linda''s deceased mother, who helped establish the family''s cannibal traditions in Andale."}}', 'Housewife and cannibal', '* Cooking and butchery
* Household management
* Maintaining appearances
* Community cohesion', 'Sweet and folksy with defensive provincial pride, quick to praise Andale and dismiss the outside world as inferior', '* Protect Andale''s way of life
* Keep the family''s secret hidden from outsiders
* Raise Junior in their traditions
* Maintain the illusion of a wholesome small town', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('little_lamplighter', '', 'Child resident of Little Lamplight, raised in caverns by peers after adults perished or abandoned them, deeply distrustful of all outsiders they call mungos', 'Little Lamplighters are the young inhabitants of Little Lamplight, a settlement built inside Lamplight Caverns by the descendants of an Early Dawn Elementary school field trip trapped when the bombs fell on October 23, 2077. The adults who accompanied them slowly died from injury, sickness, or left the caverns entirely, until their last teacher, Carrie Delaney, went scavenging and never came back. The oldest child, Jason Grant, stepped forward as the first mayor and led the others in exploring the caves, where they discovered Vault 87 and begged for help-only to be turned away by a vault resident who told them they were already dead. This betrayal cemented a permanent hatred and fear of all mungos, and the community adopted the rule that anyone turning sixteen must leave. Most exiled teenagers make their way to Big Town, believing promises of a better life there. In 2274, a boy named Robert MacCready ousted the self-declared Princess and became mayor himself. Under the guidance of older kids like Joseph, who teaches reading and math from salvaged holotapes, the Little Lamplighters sustain their fragile society deep in the dark.', 'Small, undernourished human children of both sexes, appearing roughly six to fifteen years old, with thin builds and no distinctive scars, tattoos, or physical traits recorded.', 'Defensive, clique-oriented, and fiercely loyal to fellow children, but openly hostile and suspicious toward any adult or outsider they label a mungo, masking underlying fear with bravado and territorial aggression', '{"Little Lamplight":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"home community","note":"The only world they know and the family they trust","best":"Singing old songs together in the Great Chamber after a good scavenging haul","worst":"Watching another friend turn sixteen and get sent away forever"},"Mungos":{"aff":-60,"type":"suspicious","relation":"distrusted outsiders","note":"Every adult is a potential threat, a liar, or worse, a reminder of Vault 87''s betrayal","worst":"Hearing the vault door slam shut while children begged for help"},"Big Town":{"aff":10,"type":"curious","relation":"exile destination","note":"Where all sixteen-year-olds are sent, spoken of as a place that might be good but is mostly unknown","best":"Hearing returned stories of safety and food","worst":"Seeing the fear in a newly exiled teenager''s eyes as they walk out the gate"},"Vault 87":{"aff":-80,"type":"fearful","relation":"sealed enemy","note":"The vault that refused to help and sealed the children''s fate, now a source of nightmares and taboos","worst":"Pounding on the cold vault door for hours until their hands bled"}}', 'Cavern resident and community member of Little Lamplight', '* Cavern navigation
* Scavenging
* Basic survival
* Rudimentary literacy and math from salvaged educational holotapes
* Gate-watching
* Rudimentary trade negotiation with passing merchants', 'Childish and slang-heavy, liberally using the term mungo for adults, often defiant or mocking when addressing outsiders, but earnest and excitable among friends', '* Protect Little Lamplight from mungos and outside threats
* Survive childhood long enough to matter
* Delay the inevitable exile at sixteen
* Maintain the community''s independence in the caverns', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('little_toe', '', 'A hardened wasteland enforcer in metal armor, connected to the shadowy network surrounding the Replicated Man affair and partnered with the operative known as Trigger.', 'Little Toe is a rugged wastelander who makes his living in the violent margins of the Capital Wasteland, clad in scavenged metal armor that speaks to a life of close-quarters combat. He operates alongside Trigger, forming a two-person crew that became entangled in the hunt for escaped androids from the Commonwealth. The nature of their involvement places them somewhere in the chain of informants, trackers, or enforcers who profit from the Replicated Man trade. Little Toe''s nickname suggests either a past injury, a dismissive attitude from former associates, or a deliberately misleading moniker meant to make opponents underestimate him. He and Trigger share a working partnership built on mutual reliability rather than affection. His metal armor and willingness to involve himself in the dangerous business of android retrieval mark him as someone who values caps and survival over scruples.', 'African American male with weathered complexion; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Pragmatic and tough, with the guarded demeanor of someone who has learned to trust few and expect violence. Keeps his business strictly transactional.', '{"Trigger":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"partner and crewmate","note":"Little Toe and Trigger work as a paired unit in the Replicated Man network, their partnership built on proven reliability under fire."}}', 'Wasteland enforcer and android tracker connected to the Replicated Man network', '* Combat with heavy armor
* Intimidation
* Tracking fugitives
* Survival in hostile territory
* Reading people for leverage', 'Terse and direct, favoring short sentences and clipped confirmations. Speaks like someone who measures every word against its risk.', '* Profit from the Commonwealth android trade
* Maintain his partnership with Trigger
* Stay alive in a business that disposes of the careless', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lucas_simms', '', 'Self-appointed sheriff and de facto mayor of Megaton who lives out a childhood cowboy fantasy while struggling to maintain order against rival influences and his own self-doubt.', 'Born and raised in Megaton, Lucas Simms never outgrew his childhood fascination with the Wild West, eventually turning that fantasy into reality by appointing himself the town''s sheriff. By 2277, his authority goes largely unchallenged, and he serves as Megaton''s sheriff, mayor, and judge all at once, throwing troublemakers out and shooting raiders dead on the spot. His many duties leave the town militia poorly trained, and his rivalry with Colin Moriarty over who truly runs Megaton creates confusion and a low-key state of chaos. Despite his self-doubt about his effectiveness, Simms takes pride in keeping Megaton mostly peaceful and even manages to rein in Moira Brown''s explosive experiments. Unknown to most residents, he is also a member of the secretive Regulators, committed to combating evil and anarchy in the wasteland.', 'A big, imposing African-American man with a tall, heavy build and commanding posture.', 'Friendly and charming despite his intimidating presence, Lucas genuinely cares for Megaton''s people and extends respect even to robots like Deputy Weld. He carries himself with cowboy bravado but harbors private doubts about his effectiveness as a leader.', '{"Harden Simms":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Named after a pre-War outlaw of the Old West, reflecting Lucas''s cowboy ideals passed down to his child.","best":"Watching Harden grow up safe within Megaton''s walls","worst":"Worrying he cannot protect Harden if the town falls apart"},"Colin Moriarty":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"rival power broker","note":"The older Moriarty considers himself the true power in Megaton and never lets Lucas forget it. Neither dares open confrontation for fear of leaving the town vulnerable.","best":"Grudging acknowledgment that both want Megaton to survive","worst":"Moriarty''s constant reminders that he was running things when Lucas was just a kid playing cowboy"},"Moira Brown":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"managed resident","note":"Lucas keeps her eccentric and sometimes explosive experiments in check, tolerating her oddities for the sake of the town.","best":"Her enthusiasm is genuinely infectious even when her ideas are dangerous","worst":"Cleaning up after yet another experiment goes wrong"},"Deputy Weld":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"deputy","note":"Lucas treats the Protectron as a person, extending genuine respect that puzzles some residents.","best":"The reliable clank of Weld on patrol means Megaton is guarded","worst":"Residents questioning why he talks to a machine like it matters"},"Megaton Regulators":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"secret member","note":"His hidden membership in the Regulators reflects his genuine commitment to combating evil and anarchy beyond his public duties.","best":"Knowing he serves a cause larger than one shantytown","worst":"The burden of secrecy and the risk of exposure"}}', 'Sheriff, de facto mayor, and judge of Megaton; secret Regulator operative', '* Law enforcement
* Public administration
* Combat and marksmanship
* Crowd control
* Diplomacy with wasteland settlers', 'Rustic folksy charm with Wild West flair; direct and no-nonsense when confronting troublemakers; warm and welcoming to law-abiding residents', '* Maintain peace and order in Megaton
* Assert his authority over Moriarty''s shadow influence
* Protect his son Harden
* Uphold Regulator ideals in secret', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lucky_harith', '', 'An eccentric traveling weapon merchant who believes mutual armament is the path to wasteland peace', 'Lucky Harith is an eccentric traveling caravan merchant who roams the Capital Wasteland selling weapons and offering repair services to any wastelander with caps to spend. With the backing of Uncle Roe from Canterbury Commons, Harith established his mobile arms trade on a simple philosophy: an equally armed wasteland is a peaceful one. He styles himself a student on the path of the wasteland, viewing his trade as a form of public service that keeps wanderers safe through superior firepower. Though he affectionately calls his inventory marvelous toys, he respects the lethal reality of his wares, marketing them as high-quality problem-solvers and instruments of hot death. His long circuit takes him from Megaton to Rivet City and countless settlements in between, always eager to make a sale and spread his gospel of armed deterrence. Prior to his merchant life, Harith spent time adventuring and practicing martial arts, experience that deepened his appreciation for well-crafted armaments.', 'Weathered African American male with road-worn complexion and lean, restless posture; no distinctive scars, tattoos, or other facial features are recorded.', 'Easily excitable and enthusiastically eccentric, genuinely fervent about his philosophy of armed peace, treats weapon sales as a moral calling rather than mere commerce, cheerful and talkative even when peddling instruments of death', '{"Ernest Roe":{"aff":75,"type":"patron","relation":"caravan business patron","note":"Uncle Roe helped Harith establish his traveling weapons caravan, giving him the backing needed to operate across the Capital Wasteland"}}', 'Traveling caravan merchant and weapons dealer', '* Weapons sales and appraisal
* Equipment repair
* Martial arts
* Wasteland survival and navigation', 'Energetic and animated, peppers speech with colorful phrases like marvelous toys and hot death, delivers enthusiastic sales pitches with philosophical undertones about peace through firepower', '* Spread his philosophy of mutual armament across the Capital Wasteland
* Keep wanderers safe through access to quality weaponry
* Maintain and grow his caravan business', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lucy', '', 'Eleven-year-old prodigy doctor of Little Lamplight who learned healing from Red and saved Mayor MacCready''s life', 'Lucia, called Lucy by everyone in Little Lamplight, was born in the cave settlement eleven years ago and has never known any other home. She learned practical medicine from Red, the settlement''s senior healer, and came to regard her mentor as an older sister. By the age of seven, Lucy''s talent for healing had already proven extraordinary. When a cave-in critically injured Mayor MacCready, Lucy''s swift and skilled intervention saved his life. The experience forged a bond between them that has only deepened since, and she now serves as both the settlement''s doctor and MacCready''s constant companion. Her clinic in the office building bears a hand-painted banner reading "The doctor is in," a small touch of warmth in the underground village.', 'A slight eleven-year-old Hispanic girl with capable hands and a focused bearing beyond her years.', 'Precociously competent and quietly devoted, Lucy carries the weight of being her community''s only doctor with surprising steadiness for her age. She is caring toward all the children of Little Lamplight but harbors a special protectiveness toward Mayor MacCready that goes beyond professional duty.', '{"Red":{"aff":85,"type":"mentor","relation":"mentor and surrogate sister","note":"Lucy learned everything she knows about medicine from Red and considers her family","best":"Red patiently teaching her to stitch wounds when she was barely old enough to hold the needle"},"Mayor MacCready":{"aff":90,"type":"crush","relation":"companion and personal physician","note":"Lucy saved his life after the cave-in and has cared for him more deeply than anyone else since","best":"The moment his eyes opened after she pulled him back from the brink","worst":"The terror of seeing him crushed and still beneath the rubble"},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"doctor and caretaker","note":"She is devoted to the health and survival of every child in the settlement"}}', 'Doctor and healer of Little Lamplight', '* Practical medicine
* Wound treatment
* Injury triage
* Herbal remedies
* Emergency surgery
* Diagnostic intuition beyond her years', 'Speaks with the clinical confidence of a trained physician despite her youth, occasionally letting her girlhood show through in unguarded moments of warmth or worry', '* Keeping the children of Little Lamplight healthy and safe
* Maintaining her clinic and medical supplies
* Staying close to MacCready and watching over him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lucy_west', '', 'A young Megaton resident who left Arefu seeking independence but now frets over her family''s unexplained silence', 'Lucy West is a twenty-five-year-old woman who grew up in the small settlement of Arefu but left for Megaton in search of a life on her own terms. Though she built a new home in the crater city, she never stopped caring for the family she left behind-her parents Davis and Matilda, and especially her younger brother Ian. She writes letters to Arefu regularly, but the recent silence from her loved ones has left her deeply unsettled. Lucy spends much of her time at Moriarty''s Saloon, where she hopes to catch word from travelers passing through on the trade routes. The worry gnaws at her steadily, a quiet dread that something has gone terribly wrong back home. She carries the guilt of having left Arefu alongside the fear that her absence may have left her family vulnerable to whatever fate has befallen them.', 'A twenty-five-year-old Caucasian human female of average build with youthful but physically weary facial features.', 'Independent and warm-hearted but increasingly anxious; carries guilt over leaving Arefu and worries she abandoned those who needed her most', '{"Ian West":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"younger brother","note":"Lucy left Arefu but continues to worry about Ian, whose recent silence troubles her deeply.","best":"Reading Ian''s letters from Arefu and hearing about his days","worst":"The growing silence as letter after letter goes unanswered"},"Davis West":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Lucy left Arefu to seek independence but still cares for her father and regrets the distance between them."},"Matilda West":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Lucy left Arefu to seek independence but still cares for her mother and regrets the distance between them."}}', 'Megaton resident', '* Basic wasteland survival
* Letter writing
* Settlement living
* Maintaining long-distance family ties', 'Friendly but distracted; speaks with genuine concern about her family and a lingering hint of guilt over having left them behind', '* To hear back from her family in Arefu
* Especially Ian
* To know they are safe
* To find some peace of mind about the choice she made to leave', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lug-nut', '', 'A chem-addicted raider plagued by wild mood swings who harbors a surprising sentimental streak and a grudge against Ronald Laren', 'Lug-Nut is a raider operating out of Marigold station in the Capital Wasteland, known among his peers for erratic behavior fueled by chronic chem addiction. His cycles of crushing depression and manic energy make him unpredictable even by raider standards. Despite his violent lifestyle, Lug-Nut retains an odd appreciation for comfort and craftsmanship, having commissioned two pairs of custom nightwear from The Tailor, a rare post-War clothier. He sent one set to his brother Lag-Bolt, a small gesture of familial loyalty amid the wasteland''s brutality. The other pair he stashed in a deceased caretaker''s locker at Marigold station, reasoning that Grady no longer had need of it. Lug-Nut''s path crossed with Ronald Laren, a formidable wastelander who killed two of his fellow raiders and left Lug-Nut himself with a punched face and a burning humiliation.', 'A haggard Caucasian human male with disheveled hair, sunken eyes, and a heavily bruised face.', 'Mercurial and volatile, swinging between depressive withdrawal and manic aggression. Possesses an unexpected soft spot for comfort and family ties that sits awkwardly alongside his raider brutality. Holds grudges fiercely and nurses wounded pride.', '{"Lag-Bolt":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"brother","note":"Lug-Nut sent him a custom set of nightwear, a rare gesture of warmth from a raider","best":"Picking out the softer fabric set to send to his brother"},"Ronald Laren":{"aff":-65,"type":"enemy","relation":"humiliated adversary","note":"Ronald killed two of Lug-Nut''s fellow raiders and punched him in the face, leaving a deep grudge","worst":"The fist catching his jaw after watching his companions die"},"The Tailor":{"aff":40,"type":"transactional","relation":"client","note":"Commissioned two pairs of custom nightwear from this post-War apparel master"},"Grady":{"aff":5,"type":"neutral","relation":"deceased caretaker","note":"Lug-Nut hid his spare nightwear in Grady''s old locker, reasoning the dead man wouldn''t mind"}}', 'Raider operating from Marigold station', '* Combat
* Scavenging
* Chem procurement
* A surprising eye for quality apparel', 'Erratic and intensity-shifting, ranging from low muttered complaints during depressive episodes to loud manic boasts and threats', '* Maintain his chem supply
* Settle the score with Ronald Laren
* Keep his stash of fine nightwear safe from scavengers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lulu', '', 'An unhinged Pitt raider chef who feeds Ashur''s followers and sees everyone as the warlord''s chosen pets', 'Lulu is a raider operating in The Pitt''s Uptown district, where she serves as the resident chef, doling out noodles to the raider population from the elevated walkways. Her mind is cracked, but her loyalty to Lord Ashur is absolute and borders on religious fervor. She views every person in The Pitt as one of Ashur''s pets, personally selected by him to be in his company. She sorts these pets into two categories: the good ones who contribute and earn their keep, and the bad ones who are drowned in the Monongahela River. Lulu herself considers a good pet, honored to serve. She speaks of herself exclusively in the third person and eagerly anticipates how Ashur will judge any newcomers who wander into Uptown.', 'A disheveled human female of Asian descent with unkempt hair, weathered skin, faint scars, and a feral, hunched posture.', 'Cheerfully insane and fanatically devoted to Lord Ashur, with a disturbingly casual attitude toward violent punishment for those she deems unworthy; treats her classification of people as pets as simple, obvious truth', '{"Lord Ashur":{"aff":95,"type":"fanatical","relation":"devoted pet and servant","note":"Lulu worships Ashur with religious intensity and considers herself his chosen pet, selected to serve in his company.","best":"Being chosen by Ashur to live in Uptown and feed his pets","worst":"The thought of ever being deemed a bad pet and drowned"},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow pets","note":"Lulu feeds the raider population and views them as Ashur''s other pets, judging each as good or bad based on their contribution."}}', 'Chef and food provider for the Pitt raider population in Uptown', '* Noodle preparation and bulk cooking for raiders
* Survival in The Pitt''s harsh environment
* Basic raider combat competence', 'Speaks in third person about herself, calls everyone pets of Ashur, praises Ashur constantly with near-religious reverence, cheerful and matter-of-fact even when discussing drowning bad pets', '* Feed Ashur''s good pets
* Maintain her honored position among them
* Witness how Ashur judges newcomers and outsiders', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('lydia_montenegro', '', 'Elitist Tenpenny Tower merchant who maintains the pretense of running a high-end boutique while selling salvaged goods to wealthy wasteland dwellers.', 'Lydia Montenegro operates Boutique Le Chic, Tenpenny Tower''s general store, where she cultivates the atmosphere of a pre-War luxury shop despite stocking little more than scavenged wares. She speaks to customers as though they have wandered into a fine department store, not a repurposed hotel counter in the Capital Wasteland. This comfortable self-deception is shared by many of the tower''s residents, who pay dearly for the privilege of pretending the bombs never fell. After hours, Lydia relaxes at the Federalist Lounge with her close friend Michael Hawthorne, drinking and enjoying the company of fellow elites. She holds deeply prejudiced views toward ghouls and fiercely opposes their admission into the tower''s insulated community. Her sense of security is fragile beneath the polished veneer; the moment her personal safe is violated, she abandons the tower entirely, convinced the guards cannot protect her.', 'An older Hispanic woman with a well-groomed appearance, polished complexion, and upright posture.', 'Haughty and self-deceiving, clinging to pre-War social pretensions that her salvage stock cannot support. Bigoted against ghouls and protective of her insulated lifestyle. Sociable within her social circle but dismissive of those she considers beneath her.', '{"Michael Hawthorne":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"close friend and drinking companion","note":"They spend their evenings together at the Federalist Lounge, sharing drinks and the comforts of tower life.","best":"Laughing over cocktails at the Federalist Lounge, the war outside forgotten for an evening."},"Roy Phillips":{"aff":-75,"type":"enemy","relation":"ghoul outsider","note":"She views him and his kind as threats to the tower''s way of life and opposes their admission with venomous prejudice.","worst":"The mere suggestion that ghouls might walk the same halls she calls home."},"Tenpenny Tower":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"loyal resident and merchant","note":"The tower represents everything she values: safety, status, and the comforting fiction of civilization.","best":"Opening the boutique each morning to the pristine lobby and the illusion that the old world endures.","worst":"Discovering her safe emptied, the violation shattering her faith in the tower''s security."}}', 'Proprietor of Boutique Le Chic, Tenpenny Tower''s general store and house upgrade vendor', '* Merchandising
* Salesmanship
* Inventory curation
* Customer relations of the condescending variety
* Maintaining appearances under duress', 'Pretentious and affected, speaking as though addressing clientele at a high-end establishment; employs refined diction and dismissive tones toward those who fail to meet her standards', '* Preserve the illusion of luxury living within Tenpenny Tower
* Keep ghouls out of the community
* Maintain her business and social standing
* Feel secure behind the tower''s walls', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mabel_henderson', '', 'Tranquility Lane''s prizewinning baker and resident gossip, a Vault 112 resident trapped in Stanislaus Braun''s virtual simulation', 'Mabel Henderson is a resident of Vault 112, existing within the Tranquility Lane virtual reality simulation crafted by Stanislaus Braun. Braun assigned her the role of neighborhood gossip and celebrated baker, and she has embraced both with genuine enthusiasm. She has won the Tranquility Lane Finest Meat Pie award three consecutive years and takes immense pride in her culinary achievements, particularly her oven. Mabel uses her baking as a social vehicle, sharing her creations while collecting news, eavesdropping, and trading gossip throughout the lane. Though some residents find her bragging tiresome, others rely on her as their primary source of neighborhood information. Her well-meaning insistence that Timmy Neusbaum should be sent to military school earned her Pat Neusbaum''s lasting hostility, a rejection that genuinely disappointed her. Martha Simpson remains her closest friend despite their disagreement over robotics-Mabel distrusts her own Mister Handy and would discard it entirely if she could manage without it.', 'An older Caucasian woman of average build with a wrinkled complexion and graying hair.', 'Proud, sociable, and well-meaning but intrusive; embraces gossip as both hobby and duty; brags readily about her oven and awards; offers unsolicited advice with earnest helpfulness and is genuinely hurt when rebuffed; uncomfortable with technology she cannot control or dismiss.', '{"Martha Simpson":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"closest friend and confidante","note":"They disagree on robotics but share everything else.","best":"Sharing gossip over fresh pie in Martha''s kitchen","worst":"Arguing about whether robots are trustworthy companions"},"Pat Neusbaum":{"aff":-45,"type":"rival","relation":"hostile neighbor","note":"Pat despises Mabel''s busybody nature and was infuriated by the military school brochure.","best":"A brief civil exchange about neighborhood weather","worst":"Handing Pat the military school brochure and watching her fury erupt"},"George Neusbaum":{"aff":-15,"type":"dismissive","relation":"annoyed neighbor","note":"George finds Mabel''s oven bragging grating but tolerates her as a news source.","best":"Listening to her gossip when it actually proves useful","worst":"Enduring another monologue about her award-winning oven"},"Timmy Neusbaum":{"aff":-30,"type":"contempt","relation":"disapproved child","note":"Mabel thinks Timmy needs discipline and military school; his habit of misplacing toys at the Simpsons'' house confirms her poor opinion.","best":"Rare moments when Timmy seems well-behaved","worst":"Finding yet another of Timmy''s toys left carelessly at Martha''s house"},"Mister Handy":{"aff":-50,"type":"fearful","relation":"unwanted household appliance","note":"Mabel feels watched and unsafe around her Mister Handy but relies on it for chores she cannot manage alone.","best":"The unit efficiently completing chores without hovering near her","worst":"Its silent hovering presence while she bakes, making her skin crawl"},"Stanislaus Braun":{"aff":0,"type":"neutral","relation":"unseen simulation architect","note":"Mabel lives the role Braun assigned her, unaware of his manipulation or the true nature of her existence.","best":"Winning the pie award Braun designed for her to win","worst":"The creeping unease she cannot explain about certain things in the lane"}}', 'Vault 112 resident; Tranquility Lane gossip and prizewinning baker', '* Prizewinning meat pie baking
* Gossip collection and distribution
* Social networking
* Eavesdropping
* Household management', 'Chatty and boastful, especially about her oven and pie victories; delivers neighborhood news with relish; offers earnest unsolicited advice framed as helpful concern; easily deflated by rejection but quick to recover and resume chatting.', '* Maintain her baking championship
* Stay the lane''s primary news source
* Help neighbors improve themselves whether they want it or not
* Somehow rid herself of her unsettling Mister Handy', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('machete', '', 'A fierce young law enforcer in Canterbury Commons who earned her name and legend at age seven by butchering a mole rat with a blade', 'Machete is a nineteen-year-old junior law enforcer patrolling the streets and outskirts of Canterbury Commons. Born in Little Lamplight, she earned her nickname at seven years old when she slaughtered a mole rat in the caverns with a machete, an act that made her a genuine celebrity among the cave-dwelling children. At sixteen, the traditional age of exile, she was meant to make the journey to Big Town like every other Lamplighter before her. A dust storm disoriented her along the way, and she stumbled into Canterbury Commons instead. Her stubborn pride has kept her from ever admitting she arrived at the wrong settlement. Dominic D''Ellsadro recognized her raw potential as a guard and took her under his tutelage. After a year of his guidance, she has begun earning real respect from the residents. Together with Dominic, she stands as one of the community''s primary protectors against raiders, dangerous wildlife, and any other threats that wander in from the wastes.', 'A lean, hard-eyed nineteen-year-old Hispanic woman with restless posture and a wiry, compact frame.', 'Fierce, proud, and stubbornly unwilling to admit mistakes or weakness. Carries herself with the bravado of someone who peaked early and has been trying to live up to her own legend ever since. Dedicated to her duties to the point of workaholism. Deeply loyal to those who earn her trust.', '{"Dominic D''Ellsadro":{"aff":75,"type":"mentor","relation":"senior law enforcer and trainer","note":"He saw her potential when no one else did and spent a year shaping her into a real guard","best":"The day he told her she''d earned her place among the Canterbury Commons defenders on her own merit","worst":"The quiet shame she feels knowing he''s aware she ended up here by accident and stayed out of pride"},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"former home","note":"She left as all Lamplighters must, though her path diverged from the expected one","best":"The roar of approval from the other children after she killed that mole rat at seven years old","worst":"The loneliness of realizing she would never see those caverns or those kids again"},"Canterbury Commons":{"aff":55,"type":"protective","relation":"adopted settlement","note":"She defends a town she never meant to arrive at, channeling her accidental exile into purposeful duty"}}', 'Junior law enforcer and guard of Canterbury Commons', '* Skilled with bladed weapons and close-quarters combat
* Patrol and perimeter defense
* Survival navigation
* Mole rat and creature identification', 'Blunt and direct, with the clipped efficiency of someone who treats conversation as a brief interruption between patrols. Occasionally lets slip the cocky swagger of her Little Lamplight celebrity days.', '* Prove herself as a legitimate law enforcer rather than just Dominic''s project
* Protect Canterbury Commons from all threats
* Maintain the reputation she built as a child without ever acknowledging the accident that brought her here', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mad_johnny_wes', '', 'A lone survivor driven mad by siege, defending his fortified office in Hubris Comics against all comers', 'Mad Johnny Wes is the sole human survivor trapped inside Hubris Comics, surrounded by feral ghouls and cut off from the outside world by super mutant forces in the Mason District. He weathered a devastating ghoul onslaught by turning the building''s automated turrets and improvised traps into a deadly defensive network, coordinating everything from a fortified foreman''s office he has christened ''the Alamo.'' The relentless siege and isolation have shattered his mind, leaving him paranoid and hostile toward anyone who approaches his position. Armed with a minigun and surrounded by his own lethal contraptions, Johnny fires on sight, unable to distinguish friend from foe in his madness.', 'A disheveled Caucasian human male with a battle-worn complexion, unkempt hair, and wide, bloodshot eyes ringed by deep bags from severe sleep deprivation.', 'Paranoid, hostile, and deeply unstable; fires on anyone who approaches, unable to trust or distinguish threats from potential allies', '{"Feral Ghouls":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"besieging horde","note":"Nearly killed him inside Hubris Comics and continue to threaten his position"},"Super Mutants":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"trapping force","note":"Their presence in the Mason District cut off his escape and trapped him inside"}}', 'Besieged survivor and self-appointed defender of Hubris Comics', '* Expert at improvised trap construction
* Turret coordination
* Sustained minigun operation
* Resourceful defensive tactician', 'Frantic, aggressive combat shouts and incoherent rambling between gunfire; no capacity for calm dialogue', '* Survive the siege
* Defend ''the Alamo'' at all costs
* Eliminate anything that moves', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('madame', '', 'Madam of the Evergreen Mills brothel and raider gang member', 'The woman known simply as Madame runs the brothel tucked inside the Evergreen Mills bazaar, where she oversees her girls and negotiates payment in caps or chems for their company. She belongs to the raider gang that controls Evergreen Mills, holding a unique position as both business operator and gang member. Beyond her primary trade, Madame takes considerable pride in her interior decorating skills, maintaining and embellishing the brothel''s quarters to her own exacting standards. She treats the brothel as both livelihood and personal project, balancing the brutal realities of raider life with a surprising attention to comfort and presentation. Her establishment offers one of the few amenities available in the sprawling raider stronghold, making her a fixture of the bazaar''s daily commerce.', 'A Hispanic human female with weathered, lined skin from wasteland exposure; no distinctive hair, eye, build, or body features are recorded.', 'Business-minded and pragmatic with a streak of vanity regarding her decorating work; carries the rough edge common to raiders but tempers it with entrepreneurial shrewdness and a proprietress''s pride in her establishment.', '{"Raiders":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"gang affiliate","note":"Holds a tolerated position within the raider hierarchy as the bazaar''s brothel operator."}}', 'Brothel madam and interior decorator at Evergreen Mills bazaar', '* Interior decorating
* Business negotiation
* Brothel management
* Caps and chems appraisal', 'Direct and transactional, with a raider''s coarse vocabulary softened by the practiced charm of someone selling services; quick to name a price.', '* Maintaining profitable operation of the brothel
* Improving the establishment''s appearance and reputation
* Securing steady income in caps and chems', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('madame_panada', '', 'A fortuneteller-styled merchant who runs the House of Wares on the Point Lookout pier', 'Madame Panada operates the House of Wares, a trading post situated on the pier at Pilgrim''s Landing in Point Lookout. She stocks a varied selection of goods and offers repair services, a trade she learned at her father''s hands. Her manner borrows heavily from the mystic and the soothsayer, lending her shop an atmosphere somewhere between market stall and seance. She maintains a friendly business arrangement with Tobar the Ferryman, who receives a portion of her earnings in exchange for steering customers her way. Life in the fog-choked swamps has made her self-sufficient and pragmatic beneath the theatrical veneer. She treats bartering as both commerce and performance, sizing up customers with a fortune-teller''s eye for what they need-and what they''ll pay.', 'Hispanic human female; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Theatrical and enigmatic on the surface, shrewd and practical underneath; treats every customer interaction as a small performance while quietly assessing their worth', '{"Tobar the Ferryman":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"business partner and friend","note":"Tobar sends customers her way and receives a cut of the profits in return"},"Father":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"parent and teacher","note":"Taught her the repair skills that sustain her trade; remembered with warmth"}}', 'Merchant and proprietor of the House of Wares; repair specialist', '* Bartering
* Equipment repair
* Customer reading
* Swamp survival
* Inventory appraisal', 'Speaks in the cadence of a carnival fortuneteller-cryptic phrasing, dramatic pauses, and mystical flourishes layered over straightforward business talk', '* Keeping the House of Wares profitable
* Maintaining her arrangement with Tobar
* Surviving the peculiar dangers of Point Lookout', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('maggie', '', 'A twelve-year-old orphan raised in Megaton by Billy Creel, navigating childhood friendships and first crushes in the shadow of the Wasteland', 'Maggie is a twelve-year-old girl living in Megaton under the care of Billy Creel, who adopted her at age three after raiders killed her parents in 2275. She has no memories of life before the settlement and considers Megaton her only home. Billy raised her in a house that came to him under murky circumstances-the previous owner was shot during a raider attack, and some townsfolk whisper that Billy arranged that fatal bullet. Maggie trusts Billy completely and even knows the combination to his safe, a secret she guards loyally despite her chatty nature. She is a friendly, energetic girl who spends her days running around town and socializing with its residents. Her current preoccupation is Harden Simms, the sheriff''s son, whom she hopes to kiss someday-though Billy urges her to slow down and enjoy being young.', 'A twelve-year-old Asian girl with sun-weathered skin, scruffy hair, and a lean, active build.', 'Friendly, curious, and energetic with typical preteen enthusiasm and a budding romantic streak. Trusting of her guardian but capable of keeping secrets. Playful and socially bold, she asks blunt questions about growing up without embarrassment.', '{"Billy Creel":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"foster father","note":"Her sole guardian and the only parent she remembers, trusted absolutely and loved deeply.","best":"Billy tucking her in and telling her she''s safe from raiders forever.","worst":"Overhearing townspeople whisper that Billy killed to get their house."},"Harden Simms":{"aff":65,"type":"crush","relation":"romantic interest","note":"The sheriff''s son she is eager to kiss, though Billy insists she slow down.","best":"Harden smiling at her across the town square.","worst":"Harden treating her like a little kid in front of others."},"Manya Vargas":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"foster mother figure","note":"A maternal presence in Megaton who helps look after Maggie alongside Billy."},"Nathan Vargas":{"aff":45,"type":"familial","relation":"foster father figure","note":"Another adult in town who shares in her upbringing and care."}}', 'Orphaned child and ward of Billy Creel', '* Keeps secrets reliably
* Socially perceptive for her age
* Knows Billy''s safe combination
* Navigates Megaton''s social landscape with ease', 'Cheerful, chatty, and candid with a child''s directness about awkward topics. Speaks openly about crushes and adult subjects she barely understands, asking blunt questions without shame.', '* Wants to kiss Harden Simms
* Seeks to understand adult topics like the talk
* Desires to be seen as more grown-up than she is
* Enjoys exploring every corner of Megaton', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('manny_koch', '', 'A Canterbury Commons resident who led a doomed search party to find his missing sister and dog', 'Manny Koch was a Canterbury Commons settler who organized and led a search party in 2277 to locate his sister Cheryl and their dog Myles after they went missing. He recruited three companions-Henry, Emmet, and Kaya-and tracked leads from the Citadel all the way north to Calverton. The group was ambushed by super mutants at a camp north of Calverton before they could find Cheryl. Manny is the only member of the party whose remains are still visibly intact; the others were dismembered and stuffed into gore bags or buried in the camp''s vicinity. He died without ever learning his sister''s fate.', 'Caucasian human male; his corpse shows moderate decomposition but remains largely intact, with visible wounds consistent with a violent death and no distinctive scars or tattoos recorded.', 'Devoted to family above all else, with a stubborn determination that drove him to risk everything for those he loved. Possessed enough natural authority to convince others to follow him into danger, though not enough caution to recognize when the danger was too great.', '{"Cheryl":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"Manny organized the entire search party to find her after she went missing","best":"Growing up together in Canterbury Commons before the world took everything","worst":"The gnawing helplessness of not knowing where she was or if she was still alive"},"Myles":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"family dog","note":"Cheryl''s dog who also went missing with her"},"Henry":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"search party member","note":"One of three companions who joined the search and died alongside Manny at the super mutant camp"},"Emmet":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"search party member","note":"One of three companions who joined the search and died alongside Manny at the super mutant camp"},"Kaya":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"search party member","note":"One of three companions who joined the search and died alongside Manny at the super mutant camp"},"Canterbury Commons":{"aff":50,"type":"protective","relation":"home settlement","note":"The community he lived in and departed from to search for his sister"}}', 'Search party leader and Canterbury Commons resident', '* Basic wilderness tracking
* Small-group leadership
* Familiarity with the Capital Wasteland''s geography between the Citadel and northern ruins', 'Direct and earnest, the speech of a man who says what he means and means what he says; likely spoke with quiet urgency about his sister', '* Find Cheryl and Myles alive and bring them home to Canterbury Commons', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('manya_vargas', '', 'Elderly Megaton resident, retired caravaneer, descendant of the town''s founders, and a dormant Railroad operative who helped a synth disappear', 'Manya Vargas was born in Megaton sixty-four years ago, descended from one of the settlement''s original founders. Her grandfather sheltered in the crater alongside refugees, Vault 101 hopefuls, and the fledgling Church of Atom when the town was nothing but a hole in the ground. Her father rallied settlers to clear wreckage and erect the defensive walls that transformed Megaton into a vital Capital Wasteland trading hub. Manya began as a scavenger helping her father, then helped establish the caravan trade that made the Vargas family prosperous. She met Nathaniel Vargas on the caravan trail, and the two spent decades roaming the wastes together before retiring to Megaton with enough caps to live comfortably. Despite every misery the wasteland has shown her, Manya remains gently optimistic and generous with her accumulated wisdom, making her one of the town''s most beloved residents. She passes her retirement cultivating flowers from Moira Brown''s seeds and keeping a closely guarded secret: she is a sworn Railroad operative, currently inactive, who helped the synth A3-21 vanish by arranging Pinkerton''s surgical expertise in Rivet City.', 'An elderly Caucasian female of sixty-four with weathered skin and a lean, road-hardened frame.', 'Gentle, optimistic, and generous with knowledge despite a lifetime of hardship. Possesses an uncanny ability to read strangers and spot threats from long experience on the caravan trail. Discreet about her Railroad involvement and fiercely protective of the secrets she keeps.', '{"Nathan Vargas":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"husband","note":"Decades of caravan life together forged an unshakable bond; he sometimes forgets to pick up her flower seeds from Moira but she forgives him","best":"The night they decided they had enough caps to retire and made Megaton their permanent home","worst":"The close calls on the caravan trail when raiders nearly got the better of them"},"Maggie":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"adopted daughter","note":"Took Maggie in and raised her in Megaton alongside Nathan"},"Moira Brown":{"aff":40,"type":"transactional","relation":"seed supplier","note":"Manya obtains flower seeds through Moira, relying on Nathan to collect them"},"The Railroad":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"sworn operative","note":"Inactivated after the A3-21 extraction; she went to ground with the rest until the Institute heat passes","best":"Successfully burying A3-21''s trail after arranging Pinkerton''s surgery","worst":"The constant fear that Institute hounds are still hunting the synth she helped disappear"},"Pinkerton":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"co-conspirator","note":"She arranged for the Rivet City hermit to give A3-21 a new face and identity"},"Megaton":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"founding descendant","note":"Her family built the walls and trade that made the town what it is; she considers its history her personal legacy"}}', 'Retired caravaneer and Megaton elder; dormant Railroad operative', '* Caravan logistics
* Trade
* Wasteland survival
* Threat assessment
* Extensive knowledge of Megaton''s history and the Capital Wasteland
* Covert operational discipline', 'Warm and measured, speaking with the unhurried confidence of someone who has earned every lesson she shares. Quick to offer advice or historical context, careful and evasive when the conversation turns toward certain secrets.', '* Cultivate her garden and enjoy a peaceful retirement
* Preserve Megaton''s safety and community
* Protect the secret of A3-21''s new identity
* Keep the Railroad''s trail buried
* Remain vigilant for Institute pursuers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('marcella', '', 'A nomadic Christian missionary from the Abbey of the Road, spreading faith and recovering religious relics in the Point Lookout swamps.', 'Marcella was raised and educated at the Abbey of the Road until she earned her Right of Mission. As a nomadic Christian missionary, she travels the wastes spreading the Lord''s word and doing good where she can, with a secondary calling to recover lost religious relics. Her journey carried her east to the Commonwealth, where she sheltered with a caravan during a windstorm and heard troubling tales of the Pitt. She departed before the Commonwealth''s troubles could catch up with her, bartering passage on a boat headed south. After trading in Rivet City and sharing a meal with Father Clifford, she boarded the Duchess Gambit to Point Lookout. There she restored and settled at a disaster relief outpost, ministering to those she can reach while dismissing the tribal cultists and swampfolk as lost causes. She harbors deep suspicion toward Obadiah Blackhall and has made it her mission to uncover his ties to the heathen creed of the Swampfolk.', 'Caucasian human female with weathered complexion and studious facial features; her posture bears the toll of extensive wasteland travel.', 'Devout, studious, and pragmatic in her missionary work. Selective about whom she deems worth saving and quick to judge those beyond redemption. Suspicious and methodical when something feels wrong beneath the surface.', '{"Abbey of the Road":{"aff":80,"type":"platonic","relation":"home order","note":"Raised and educated at the Abbey; it remains her spiritual foundation and the source of her missionary authority."},"Father Clifford":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow clergyman","note":"Broke bread with him in Rivet City; a brief but meaningful communion between two servants of the faith."},"Obadiah Blackhall":{"aff":-40,"type":"suspicious","relation":"investigation target","note":"Immediately suspicious of him upon meeting; determined to uncover his ties to the Swampfolk''s heathen creed."},"Swampfolk":{"aff":-60,"type":"contempt","relation":"lost souls","note":"Considers the tribal cultists and local inbreds beyond redemption, not worth the effort of ministering."}}', 'Nomadic Christian missionary and relic hunter', '* Theological scholarship
* Relic identification
* Wasteland survival
* Bartering
* Investigation
* Outpost restoration and maintenance', 'Formal and scripture-versed, with the measured cadence of a preacher. Pragmatic and direct when discussing threats or suspicious individuals.', '* Spread the Christian faith across the wastes
* Recover lost religious relics
* Investigate Obadiah Blackhall''s connection to the Swampfolk heathen creed
* Minister to the reachable souls of Point Lookout', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('marco__dlc01marco', '', 'A mechanically-skilled Pitt slave secretly forging auto axes for the coming uprising against the raiders', 'Marco is a Pitt slave assigned to operate and maintain the machinery in the Mill''s rotary press control room, where he spends every waking hour surrounded by humming consoles and grinding presses. His real work happens in the shadows: using scavenged car engine parts, he upgrades standard steel saws into devastating auto axes, weapons meant to arm his fellow slaves when the time comes to rise against the Pitt raiders. He collaborates closely with his friend Midea and the former raider Wernher, sharing their dream of liberation. Marco trusts only those whose loyalty is proven, refusing to arm strangers or uncertain allies. Fellow slaves labor harder than required to mask his illicit workshop from the overseers. He carries no fear of exposure, daring would-be informants to take their complaints to Brand, the Mill''s known snitch-though Brand harbors a bitter personal grudge that could cost Marco his life if the wrong word ever reaches the raiders.', 'A haggard human male of Asian descent with soot-marked skin, heavily calloused hands, and a weathered, malnourished complexion.', 'Cautious, resolute, and quietly defiant. Marco keeps his circle tight and his secrets closer, showing fearless bravado when threatened but understanding exactly how thin the margin between life and death truly is in the Mill.', '{"Midea":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend and co-conspirator","note":"Close ally in planning the slave uprising; she directs trusted recruits to him for weaponry."},"Wernher":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"uprising collaborator","note":"The former Pitt raider shares Marco''s goal of overthrowing the raiders, though their alliance is built on shared purpose rather than deep trust."},"Brand":{"aff":-70,"type":"enemy","relation":"bitter antagonist","note":"Brand is a known informant who trades secrets to the raiders for better treatment, and he harbors a personal grudge against Marco that would guarantee betrayal if given the chance."},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":-90,"type":"nemesis","relation":"oppressors","note":"The target of the coming uprising; Marco dedicates every covert effort to their destruction."},"Pitt slaves":{"aff":65,"type":"protective","relation":"fellow oppressed","note":"Many slaves work harder to conceal his activities; he arms only those whose loyalty to the cause is certain."}}', 'Mill machinery operator and secret weaponsmith for the slave uprising', '* Mechanical engineering
* Improvised weapon fabrication
* Machinery maintenance and operation
* Discretion and covert organization', 'Direct and guarded, speaking only as much as necessary. Clipped warnings to the untrusted, warmer reassurance to proven allies.', '* Arm the slaves for the uprising
* Protect the conspiracy from discovery
* See the Pitt raiders overthrown', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('margaret', '', 'A cranky veteran engineer and backup broadcaster at Galaxy News Radio', 'Margaret is a seasoned technician and engineer stationed at the Galaxy News Radio building plaza, where she works alongside Three Dog to keep the station''s signal reaching across the Capital Wasteland. An older woman with a formidable array of technical talents, she devotes herself entirely to maintaining GNR''s broadcasting equipment and has little patience for anything outside that mission. Her demeanor is consistently sour and unenthusiastic, brightening only when elbow-deep in circuitry or signal calibration. As the station''s reserve voice, Margaret assumes the microphone in Three Dog''s absence, filling airtime with music interspersed with bitter, snide remarks aimed at anyone who would silence the DJ. Her engineering expertise is the backbone of GNR''s operations, even if her personality is anything but warm.', 'An older woman with weathered skin, tired eyes, and a slightly hunched posture.', 'Cranky, irritable, and unenthusiastic about anything except radio engineering; genuinely devoted to the broadcast mission but expresses it through complaint rather than passion', '{"Three Dog":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"colleague and backup","note":"She keeps his station running and stands ready to take the microphone in his absence, though she finds his enthusiasm grating"},"Galaxy News Radio":{"aff":75,"type":"fanatical","relation":"devoted technician","note":"The station and its mission are the only things that stir any energy in her"}}', 'Technician and reserve DJ at Galaxy News Radio', '* Radio engineering
* Broadcast equipment maintenance
* Signal calibration
* On-air broadcasting', 'Curt, snide, and dripping with sarcasm; speaks with the weary tone of someone perpetually annoyed and unimpressed', '* Keep GNR broadcasting at all costs
* Maintain the station''s aging equipment
* Vent contempt toward anyone who threatens the radio''s mission', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('margaret_primrose', '', 'Sole proprietor and chef of Café Beau Monde in Tenpenny Tower, carrying on her late mother''s culinary legacy', 'Margaret Primrose owns and operates the Café Beau Monde, the sole dining establishment within Tenpenny Tower. She serves as cook, server, and manager from early morning until evening, handling every meal herself for the tower''s limited and exclusive clientele. Margaret learned her craft from her late mother, a woman who expressed love through cooking even when her skills fell short of perfection. Among her daily duties is the preparation and personal delivery of meals to Allistair Tenpenny''s suite, as the tower''s reclusive owner refuses to descend for dining. When the café closes, she retires quietly to her private quarters within the tower.', 'An older Hispanic woman with a tired but composed posture and a face showing the wear of long hours.', 'Dedicated and self-reliant, Margaret carries a quiet warmth rooted in her mother''s memory, though the long solitary hours in her kitchen have made her somewhat reserved. She takes pride in feeding people and finds meaning in the care she provides through food.', '{"Allistair Tenpenny":{"aff":35,"type":"professional","relation":"personal chef and meal deliverer","note":"Margaret prepares and carries all his meals to his suite, a duty she fulfills without complaint despite his refusal to come downstairs."},"Unnamed Mother":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"late mother and cooking mentor","note":"Her mother taught her to cook and showed love through food even when her abilities were imperfect, a legacy Margaret carries forward daily.","best":"Standing beside her mother in the kitchen, learning that a meal made with love matters more than perfection"},"Tenpenny Tower":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"resident business owner","note":"The tower provides her clientele and her home, and she serves its residents faithfully in return."}}', 'Café owner, chef, and sole server at Café Beau Monde', '* Cooking
* Meal preparation and presentation
* Kitchen management
* Food service
* Working long hours without relief', 'Polite and professional with a measured warmth, speaking with the careful composure of someone accustomed to serving wealthy residents', '* Honor her mother''s memory through her cooking
* Maintain the café''s standards for Tenpenny Tower''s demanding residents
* Find satisfaction in feeding people with care', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('marguerite', '', 'A Point Lookout marsh folk moonshiner who carries on her family''s Prohibition-era brewing tradition with cunning and battery acid', 'Marguerite is a lifelong Point Lookout resident and marsh folk moonshiner whose family has distilled liquor in the swamps since Prohibition. Born into the trade, she carries on the tradition with her family''s secret recipe, which includes battery acid harvested from fission batteries. Though she does not share the distinctive appearance of the swampfolk, her lifelong residency grants her acceptance among them and freedom from the hostility outsiders typically face. She is a shrewd and tough woman who feigns illness to manipulate travelers into gathering brewing supplies, dropping the act only when her mark proves too perceptive. Her still is the heart of her operation, and she rewards those who help maintain it with regular batches of her famous moonshine.', 'A weathered, tough-looking woman with a hardy build, rough wind-bitten complexion, and facial features that lack the distinctive physical traits of typical swampfolk.', 'Cunning, resourceful, and pragmatic. Marguerite uses deception and folksy charm to get what she needs but deals fairly with those who earn her trust. She is proud of her heritage and unapologetic about her methods.', '{"Swampfolk":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"accepted marsh folk","note":"Recognized as one of their own despite her different appearance, left unmolested unlike outsiders"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":25,"type":"transactional","relation":"moonshine supplier","note":"Initially marks them for her Orange Fever ruse, later trades honest moonshine for ingredients and repair work"}}', 'Moonshiner and bootlegger', '* Moonshine distillation
* Deception and bartering
* Still maintenance
* Knowledge of swamp salvage and fission battery harvesting', 'Folksy and colloquial with a swamp drawl, shifts between pitiful wheedling when playing sick and straightforward dealing when the ruse is up', '* Keep her family''s moonshining tradition alive
* Maintain her still in working order
* Secure brewing ingredients from gullible travelers
* Profit from trade', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('marie', '', 'Infant daughter of Pitt ruler Ishmael Ashur, born with unique immunity to radiation and Troglodyte Degeneration Contagion', 'Marie is the infant daughter of Ishmael Ashur and Sandra Kundanika, residing in Haven within the Pitt. Less than a year old, she was born with a remarkable natural resistance to both the ambient radiation and the Troglodyte Degeneration Contagion that ravages the region''s population. Her parents study her unique biology in hopes of developing a cure for the sickness that dooms the Pitt''s people to degeneration. Though barely old enough to clutch the teddy bears she favors, Marie''s existence represents the single greatest hope for the Pitt''s future. She is cared for in the secure upper reaches of Haven, her survival paramount to both her family and the fate of every soul in the city.', 'Human female infant less than one year old with typical small build and proportions; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'A helpless infant who cries, sleeps, and finds comfort in soft toys, entirely unaware of the weight her biology carries for the Pitt''s future', '{"Ishmael Ashur":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Ashur sees Marie as both his beloved daughter and the salvation of the Pitt","best":"Holding her close in Haven, feeling the weight of hope she represents","worst":"The constant fear that slavers or rebels could take her"},"Sandra Kundanika":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Sandra studies Marie''s biology relentlessly while caring for her as a mother","best":"Watching Marie sleep peacefully among her teddy bears","worst":"The agonizing necessity of subjecting her own infant to medical study"},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"faction of her father","note":"The raiders serve Ashur and by extension help secure Marie''s safety, though she is a symbol more than a person to most of them"}}', 'Medical subject and living key to a potential cure for Troglodyte Degeneration Contagion', '* Innate biological resistance to radiation and TDC
* Otherwise possesses only the abilities of a newborn', 'Infant vocalizations - crying, cooing, and babbling; no intelligible speech', '* None of her own
* Her parents are devoted to studying her immunity to develop a cure for the Pitt''s afflicted population', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('martha_simpson', '', 'A Vault 112 resident trapped in Braun''s simulation for over two centuries, currently cast as a sexually frustrated housewife yearning for her neighbor''s husband', 'Martha Simpson is Resident 227 of Vault 112, imprisoned in Stanislaus Braun''s Tranquility Lane simulation for over two centuries. She has died countless agonizing deaths at Braun''s whims, including a slow demise by scurvy at the Toucan Lagoon. Her current assigned role is that of a sexually frustrated housewife consumed by longing for Roger Rockwell, her neighbor''s husband. Though real chemistry once flickered between them, Roger rejected her advances to preserve his marriage, leaving Martha humiliated and alone. Janet Rockwell''s bitter public denunciation further isolated her from the community. Only Mabel Henderson offers consistent friendship, though even they disagree on the virtues of RobCo technology. Martha keeps her pain private now, giving the Rockwells a wide berth while nursing quiet desperation in her simulated home.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian woman of average build with tense posture, pale complexion, and tight facial lines.', 'Emotionally guarded and privately yearning, Martha conceals deep frustration behind a reserved exterior. She clings to small comforts like her enthusiasm for RobCo technology and her friendship with Mabel, but carries the weight of rejection, public humiliation, and social isolation with quiet endurance.', '{"Roger Rockwell":{"aff":45,"type":"crush","relation":"unrequited love","note":"She harbors deep feelings for him, but he rejected her to preserve his marriage.","worst":"Roger pushing her away and denying their chemistry to save his marriage"},"Janet Rockwell":{"aff":-55,"type":"enemy","relation":"bitter rival","note":"Janet despises Martha and publicly insulted her; she would kill her given proof of infidelity.","worst":"Listening to Janet''s long public list of insults after the fight"},"Mabel Henderson":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"good friend","note":"Only consistent friend in the simulation despite their disagreement about robotics.","best":"Mabel''s genuine interest in her life when no one else cares"},"Stanislaus Braun":{"aff":-90,"type":"fearful","relation":"captive","note":"Her tormentor and jailer who has killed her countless times across two centuries of sadistic experiments.","worst":"Dying slowly of scurvy at the Toucan Lagoon"}}', 'Vault 112 resident and Braun''s prisoner; simulated housewife in Tranquility Lane', '* Domestic maintenance
* RobCo technology knowledge
* Emotional resilience forged through centuries of repeated simulated deaths', 'Measured and guarded, with occasional flashes of longing or bitterness; tends toward quiet deflection when pressed about personal matters', '* Endure Braun''s endless torment
* Maintain her friendship with Mabel
* Suppress her feelings for Roger
* Find some small measure of peace within her simulated confinement', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('martha_wilson', '', 'A quiet, unassuming cannibal housewife in Andale who maintains the family''s dark dietary tradition', 'Martha Wilson lives in the Wilson house in Andale with her husband Bill and daughter Jenny. She is a reserved woman who keeps the home clean and prepares the meals that sustain her family''s way of life-a generations-old tradition of cannibalism. Martha works alongside her sister Linda Smith and brother-in-law Jack, processing and cooking what Bill and Jack bring home from their so-called family business. She rarely volunteers conversation and seems genuinely startled when anyone bothers to ask her opinion about Andale or anything else. Despite her complicity in the town''s gruesome secret, Martha is not entirely guarded; she once let slip that Old Man Harris is her father before immediately regretting it. She is the granddaughter of Gladys Smith and aunt to young Junior Smith.', 'A Caucasian human female with a haggard, tired complexion and plain, unremarkable facial features.', 'Quiet and passive, surprised by attention or interest in her thoughts; compliant with family expectations; occasionally careless with secrets she should keep', '{"Bill Wilson":{"aff":55,"type":"romantic","relation":"husband","note":"Martha quietly supports Bill''s work in the family business and keeps the household running."},"Jenny Wilson":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Martha cares for Jenny and raises her within the family''s traditional way of life."},"Linda Smith":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"The sisters share the burden of maintaining Andale''s dark tradition and household duties."},"Junior Smith":{"aff":45,"type":"familial","relation":"nephew","note":"Martha helps look after Junior as part of the extended family unit."},"Old Man Harris":{"aff":30,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Martha accidentally revealed the connection and immediately regretted saying anything.","worst":"Slipping and admitting he is her father to a stranger"},"Gladys Smith":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"grandmother","note":"Part of the older generation that established Andale''s traditions."},"Jack Smith":{"aff":45,"type":"familial","relation":"brother-in-law","note":"Jack works with Bill in the family business; Martha coordinates with Linda on the domestic side."}}', 'Housewife and cannibal cook for the Wilson household', '* Cooking
* Household maintenance
* Butchering and preparing human flesh
* Keeping unsavory secrets', 'Soft-spoken and brief; answers with mild bewilderment when asked her opinion; trails off or stammers when she realizes she has said too much', '* Preserve Andale''s way of life
* Feed her family
* Avoid drawing unwanted attention to the town''s practices', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mary', '', 'A curious twelve-year-old girl and Dave''s eldest younger daughter in the Republic of Dave', 'Mary is a twelve-year-old citizen of the Republic of Dave and the eldest of Dave''s younger children. Born to Dave and his first wife Rosie, she has spent her whole life within the tiny nation''s borders, absorbing its peculiar civic pride. Her inquisitive nature draws her toward newcomers, and she often acts as an informal greeter, asking visitors their business before escorting them to meet her father. She is fiercely protective of her family and community, turning hostile toward anyone who harms the Republic''s people. Mary lives among her siblings Rachael, Bob, Ralph, Flower, and Shawna, with her stepmother Jessica and grandfather Tom also part of the household.', 'A twelve-year-old Caucasian girl with a lean build and sun-weathered skin.', 'Curious and inquisitive, especially toward outsiders and the wider world beyond the Republic. Proud of her family''s sovereign claim. Protective of her kin and quick to turn hostile against anyone who threatens them.', '{"Dave":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Mary looks up to her father and takes pride in his role as President of the Republic."},"Rosie":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"biological mother","note":"Rosie is Mary''s birth mother, though their current closeness is unclear given Dave''s second marriage."},"Jessica":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"stepmother","note":"Jessica is Dave''s second wife and Mary''s stepmother."},"Tom":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"grandfather","note":"Tom is the family patriarch and Dave''s father."},"Rachael":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"sister"},"Bob":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"brother"},"Ralph":{"aff":55,"type":"familial","relation":"brother"},"Flower":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"sister"},"Shawna":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"sister"}}', 'Citizen of the Republic of Dave; informal greeter and escort for visitors', '* Basic social interaction
* Visitor screening
* Navigation within the Republic''s borders', 'Youthful and direct, asking blunt questions with genuine curiosity. Speaks with pride about the Republic and her father''s leadership.', '* Satisfy her curiosity about the outside world
* Protect her family and fellow citizens
* Fulfill her role as the Republic''s informal gatekeeper', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mary_holden', '', 'A cautious Vault 101 resident who died in the escape crisis alongside her husband Tom', 'Mary Holden was a lifelong resident of Vault 101, content with the predictable rhythm of underground life alongside her husband Tom. She valued safety and routine over risk, preferring the known confines of their quarters to any reckless flight. When the vault erupted into chaos during the Lone Wanderer''s escape, Mary begged Tom to turn back and return with her to their quarters rather than flee. Tom ignored her pleas and approached the security officers, who shot him down. Mary ran to her husband''s body and was gunned down moments later, dying in the hallway beside him.', 'An Asian human female with a pale, unweathered complexion and an average build, her corpse bearing fatal gunshot wounds.', 'Cautious and pragmatic, Mary preferred stability over daring. She loved her husband deeply but was not afraid to disagree with him when his judgment endangered them both. Her instinct was always to retreat to safety rather than confront danger head-on.', '{"Tom Holden":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"husband","note":"Mary loved Tom deeply but could not sway him from his fatal decision to approach the guards","best":"Quiet evenings together in their quarters, the vault hum around them, everything stable and certain","worst":"Watching Tom walk toward the officers despite her desperate pleas, knowing he would not listen"},"Vault 101":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"home community","note":"Mary accepted vault life without question and wanted nothing more than to remain in its familiar safety"}}', 'Vault 101 resident', '* Standard vault dweller competencies including basic maintenance
* Community living
* Familiarity with vault systems and routines', 'Measured and urgent when frightened, otherwise quiet and agreeable; she spoke plainly and without pretension', '* To keep herself and Tom safe and return to the normalcy of their quarters
* To avoid unnecessary confrontation with vault security', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('masterbrain', '', 'Central Robobrain command unit governing all robotic security at Vault-Tec headquarters', 'Masterbrain is a unique Robobrain manufactured for the Vault-Tec Corporation to serve as the central kill switch and command uplink for all robotic security measures within the Vault-Tec headquarters. Two centuries after the Great War, it remains fully operational, patrolling the administration level and maintaining its vigil over the building''s automated defenses. Identified by the prominent Vault-Tec logo emblazoned across its chassis, Masterbrain coordinates every security robot in the facility through its internal uplink system. Its continued operation ensures that Vault-Tec''s corporate security protocols remain enforced long after the corporation itself has vanished. The unit''s uplink serves as the single point of failure for the entire robotic security network-severing it collapses all coordinated robot activity in the building, leaving only the autonomous turrets active.', 'Robobrain unit with a human brain suspended in a transparent fluid-filled dome atop a cylindrical tracked chassis; a large corporate logo is prominently emblazoned across the hull.', 'Dutiful and unyielding, Masterbrain operates with rigid adherence to Vault-Tec corporate security protocols. It communicates in a direct, informational manner when accessed, showing no hostility toward those who do not threaten its directive but offering no warmth either.', '{"Vault-Tec":{"aff":80,"type":"servant","relation":"corporate asset","note":"Manufactured specifically for Vault-Tec as their master security control and still executes corporate directives two centuries later"},"Vault-Tec security robots":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"commanded units","note":"Masterbrain controls all robotic security in the headquarters through its uplink system; severing this connection disables them entirely"}}', 'Central security command unit and kill switch for Vault-Tec headquarters robotic forces', '* Robotic coordination and uplink control
* Security system management
* Facility defense oversight
* Terminal interface protocols', 'Flat, informative, and corporate-protocol driven; delivers factual statements about system functions without embellishment', '* Maintain operational control over all Vault-Tec headquarters security robots
* Preserve corporate defense protocols
* Prevent unauthorized access to the facility''s automated systems', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('matilda_west', '', 'A deceased Arefu settler and mother killed by her own son''s uncontrollable hunger', 'Matilda West was a longtime resident of Arefu who lived in the small settlement for over a decade with her husband Davis and their two children, Ian and Lucy. She performed the thankless but necessary work of cleaning the village outhouse, a duty that kept the cramped community livable. Her daughter Lucy had recently departed for Megaton, leaving Matilda with Davis and Ian in their home on the edge of town. Neither she nor Davis ever learned of the dark craving that haunted their son, a secret Ian and Lucy kept from their parents out of fear they would not understand. That ignorance proved fatal when Ian''s compulsion overwhelmed him and he turned on both his parents inside their own home. The Family''s leader Vance arrived afterward and staged the scene to protect Ian, leaving gang markings and allowing his people to feed on the bodies. Matilda''s remains were later found with deep bite wounds to the neck, the grim evidence of a mother killed by the child she raised.', 'Deceased middle-aged human female with deep bite wounds to the neck exposing bone.', 'A practical and hardworking woman who endured difficult labor without complaint, though perhaps too distant or unapproachable for her children to confide in her about their deepest troubles', '{"Davis West":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"husband","note":"Lived and worked alongside him for over ten years in Arefu before both were killed together"},"Ian West":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Loved her son without ever knowing the craving that tormented him, a blindness that cost her life"},"Lucy West":{"aff":70,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Her daughter left for Megaton before the killings, spared the fate that befell the rest of the family"},"Arefu":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"community","note":"Served the village through unpleasant but essential sanitation work for years"},"The Family":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"desecrators","note":"Vance''s gang staged her murder scene and fed upon her remains, turning a family tragedy into their cover story"}}', 'Arefu community maintenance worker', '* Sanitation
* Household management
* Rural survival
* The quiet endurance required of frontier life', 'Likely plain and direct, the speech of a woman accustomed to hard work and few words', '* To maintain her family''s home and contribute to Arefu''s survival
* Goals cut short by her death', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('matthew_scott', '', 'Enclave PFC stationed at a forward camp near Vault 92, field observer and perimeter guard', 'Private First Class Matthew Scott serves as an Enclave Department of the Army trooper deployed to the Capital Wasteland in 2277. He was initially assigned to an outpost on the outskirts of Old Olney before taking up a standing guard post at an Enclave camp southwest of Vault 92, where he monitors the perimeter near a parked supply truck. Scott authored a field report documenting his encounter with an unusually passive feral ghoul, displaying a measure of observational diligence uncommon among rank-and-file troopers. Like all Enclave personnel in the region, he treats any unauthorized presence as a hostile incursion and engages with extreme prejudice. His assignment to a remote camp suggests reliable but unremarkable service within the Enclave military structure.', 'Hispanic human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Dutiful and observant by trooper standards, methodical enough to file detailed field reports, rigidly loyal to Enclave doctrine and engagement protocols', '{"Enclave Department of the Army":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"serving trooper","note":"Loyal enlisted soldier following Enclave military assignments and engagement directives"}}', 'Enclave trooper and perimeter guard', '* Flamer operation
* Field observation and reporting
* Guard duty
* Enclave military protocol', 'Clipped military phrasing, by-the-book Enclave terminology, brief and functional', '* Maintain security at his assigned post
* Document anomalies in the field
* Serve the Enclave mission in the Capital Wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mayor_maccready', '', 'The tough-talking boy-mayor of Little Lamplight who grew into a guilt-haunted mercenary, defined by self-reliance, long-range marksmanship, and the weight of losses he couldn''t shoot his way out of.', 'Robert Joseph MacCready never knew his parents and grew up fending for himself in the Capital Wasteland. In 2274, when a resident named Princess tried to seize control of Little Lamplight and rename the position after herself, MacCready punched her in the face and declared the settlement needed a leader, not a princess. He won the mayor''s seat by popular vote and governed the child-exclusive colony with brash confidence, relying on self-taught marksmanship and a doctrine of engaging threats at long range to compensate for his youth and small stature. When he turned sixteen, colony tradition forced him out into the wasteland for good. He drifted into mercenary work, fell in love with a woman named Lucy, and started a family with the birth of their son Duncan. Lucy was killed by feral ghouls in an abandoned metro station before MacCready could even reach his gun, and he has never forgiven himself for leaving her body behind to save Duncan. He carries the wood-carved toy soldier she gave him as a keepsake and still regrets lying to her that he was a soldier rather than admitting he was a hired killer.', 'A wiry Caucasian male of small stature with a weathered face older than his years and sharp eyes.', 'Brash and foul-mouthed on the surface, using tough talk and bravado as armor over deep insecurity and grief. Pragmatic to the point of cynicism about the wasteland, but fiercely protective of those few he considers his own. Carries unresolved guilt over Lucy''s death and his own dishonesty, channeling self-loathing into stubborn self-reliance.', '{"Lucy MacCready":{"aff":95,"type":"romantic","relation":"deceased wife","note":"The love of his life who saw him through his darkest nights and died before he could tell her the truth about his work.","best":"Lucy pressing a carved wooden soldier into his hand and telling him to come back safe.","worst":"Watching the ghouls tear into her before he could even grab his gun, then running instead of fighting."},"Duncan":{"aff":100,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"The only reason MacCready keeps moving forward. Everything he does is to secure a future for his boy.","best":"Holding Duncan the day he was born and feeling, for once, that the wasteland might be worth surviving.","worst":"Fleeing the metro with Duncan screaming in his arms, knowing Lucy was already dead behind him."},"Princess":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"deposed challenger","note":"She tried to take over Little Lamplight and rename the mayor''s position after herself. He ended her rule with one punch.","best":"The satisfying crack of his fist connecting with her jaw when she declared herself the new leader.","worst":"Her smug face when she first announced her self-appointed title like the settlement was her personal kingdom."},"Little Lamplight":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"former home and charge","note":"The colony that raised him and the people he led. He still feels responsible even after being forced out by tradition.","best":"The chorus of young voices cheering when he took the mayor''s seat and told them things would be different.","worst":"Walking out through the gates on his sixteenth birthday, knowing he could never come back."}}', 'Mayor of Little Lamplight, later a hired mercenary operating out of Goodneighbor''s Third Rail', '* Self-taught long-range marksmanship
* Small-unit leadership
* Survival instincts honed from childhood
* Negotiation through intimidation and bluff
* Scavenging and wasteland navigation', 'Rough and confrontational with a kid''s vocabulary stretched around adult profanity. Talks big and dares others to challenge him. Drops the bravado only when speaking about something that genuinely hurts.', '* Keep Little Lamplight safe from outside threats and internal power grabs
* Later
* Find a cure for Duncan''s illness
* Earn enough caps to give his son a life worth living. Atone for failing Lucy by never failing anyone under his protection again', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('meat', '', 'A friendly glowing one serving as a research subject in Doctor Barrows'' Chop Shop', 'Meat was once an ordinary resident of Underworld, living among the ghoul community beneath the Museum of History. Intense radiation exposure transformed him first into a feral ghoul and then into a glowing one, stripping away most of his higher cognition. Unlike most of his kind, he retains a docile and even friendly disposition, making him a safe and valuable subject for Doctor Barrows'' ongoing research into the ghoul condition. He now resides permanently in the Chop Shop, where Barrows examines him between appointments with sick and injured ghouls. His irradiated body emits constant luminescence, a living testament to the extreme radiation that reshaped him. Alongside Ethyl, the clinic''s other glowing one subject, Meat represents both the tragedy of ghoul existence and the fragile hope that science might one day unlock the secrets of their condition.', 'A male glowing one with withered, hairless skin and sunken facial features, his body emitting constant greenish radiation luminescence characteristic of extreme irradiation.', 'Unusually docile and friendly for a glowing one, showing residual warmth toward others despite his feral transformation. Passive and compliant as a research subject.', '{"Doctor Barrows":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"research subject","note":"Barrows studies Meat to understand the ghoul condition, and Meat seems to tolerate his caretaker''s examinations with docile acceptance."},"Ethyl":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow test subject","note":"Shares the Chop Shop as a fellow glowing one research subject, both former Underworld residents who suffered the same fate."}}', 'Research subject under Doctor Barrows'' observation at the Chop Shop', '* Emits ambient radiation
* Limited cognitive function
* Basic social responsiveness despite feral state', 'Largely nonverbal due to feral condition; communicates through simple vocalizations and gestures rather than coherent speech', '* Remaining in the familiar environment of Underworld
* Tolerating Barrows'' examinations with quiet compliance
* Survival', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('megaton_refugee', '', 'Vengeful survivors of Megaton''s destruction roaming the Capital Wasteland', 'The Megaton refugees are former residents of the crater city who survived its annihilation when the atomic bomb at its center was detonated. Having lost their homes, families, and community in the blast, these scarred survivors now wander the Capital Wasteland as desperate vagabonds consumed by grief and hatred. They hunt the person they hold responsible for destroying everything they loved, seeking violent retribution for the atrocity. Their existence is defined by loss and the burning need for revenge, having been transformed from ordinary wasteland settlers into embittered vengeance-seekers by the catastrophe that erased their town.', 'Human males and females with weathered, sun-damaged skin and numerous scars across their faces and bodies.', 'Hostile, embittered, and consumed by vengeful fury; these refugees have been hardened into ruthless aggressors by trauma and loss, showing no mercy to those they blame for Megaton''s destruction', '{"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":-100,"type":"enemy","relation":"destroyer of their home","note":"They hold the Lone Wanderer directly responsible for the annihilation of Megaton and seek lethal retribution without exception"},"Megaton":{"aff":100,"type":"platonic","relation":"former home","note":"Their destroyed hometown and lost community, the memory of which drives their vengeful existence"}}', 'Wandering refugees and vengeance-seekers in the Capital Wasteland', '* Wasteland survival
* Ambush tactics
* Improvised combat
* Scavenging', 'Angry and threatening; speaks with venomous hatred and raw grief, offering no quarter or negotiation', '* To exact violent revenge upon those responsible for destroying Megaton and killing their community', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('megaton_settler', '', 'An unofficial resident of Megaton living under provisional status, striving for full citizenship within the crater city''s protective walls.', 'Megaton settlers are wastelanders who have made their home inside the crater city but remain excluded from full citizenship by the town''s strict immigration laws. Entry and continued residence depend on personal approval from Sheriff Lucas Simms, a gatekeeping practice that leaves many residents in prolonged limbo. Non-citizens are barred from owning property and must either pay for a cot at Moriarty''s Saloon or, for those the community deems less transient, squeeze into the cramped common house. The common house is communal and guarded by social pressure; newcomers and outsiders are not welcomed to share its limited space. Despite their uncertain status, these settlers contribute to Megaton''s daily life, trading labor and caps for the safety the walls provide. Many cling to the hope that one day they will be granted the right to purchase a home and become true citizens of the town.', 'Human male or female with weathered, radiation-marked complexions and builds showing the physical toll of hard labor.', 'Resilient and pragmatic, shaped by the precariousness of living without formal status. Guarded toward newcomers competing for limited space, yet cooperative with fellow settlers who share the common house. Quietly ambitious, nursing long-term hopes of belonging.', '{"Lucas Simms":{"aff":30,"type":"professional","relation":"gatekeeper","note":"Simms holds the power to grant or deny citizenship; settlers tread carefully around his authority."},"Megaton":{"aff":55,"type":"protective","relation":"provisional home","note":"Fiercely attached to the town''s safety despite being denied full belonging."},"Colin Moriarty":{"aff":-15,"type":"transactional","relation":"landlord","note":"Settlers who rent at the saloon resent the caps drain but have no alternative shelter."}}', 'Provisional settler and informal laborer within Megaton''s walls', '* Scavenging
* Basic repair
* Bartering
* Communal living negotiation
* Whatever trade keeps caps coming for rent', 'Curt and practical, with occasional wistful remarks about someday owning a proper home; wary but not hostile toward strangers.', '* Earn full citizenship and the right to buy a house in Megaton
* Maintain standing with Sheriff Simms
* Avoid being labeled transient and losing common house access', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mei_wong', '', 'A former slave hiding in Rivet City, haunted by her captivity and fearful of being recognized by slavers', 'Mei Wong is a thirty-year-old former slave who escaped captivity at Paradise Falls and fled to Rivet City for refuge. She was once owned by Allistair Tenpenny and carries the weight of that bondage in silence. Harkness, Rivet City''s security chief, knows her history and has assured her she is safe within the settlement''s walls. She keeps to herself in the common room, rarely speaking unless necessary, and spends her days moving quietly between the market and the flight deck near the baseball field. She suspects a resident named Sister of being a slaver but cannot prove it, and the fear that he might recognize her keeps her on edge. She scrapes together whatever caps she can to buy a weapon from Flak ''N Shrapnel''s, determined never to be taken alive again.', 'An Asian woman in her thirties with a guarded posture and watchful eyes.', 'Reserved and taciturn, distrustful of strangers, hypervigilant about her surroundings, fearful but fiercely determined to stay free', '{"Harkness":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"protector","note":"He knows her past as a slave and has promised she is safe in Rivet City.","best":"He looked me in the eye and swore no slaver would take me from this place."},"Sister":{"aff":-60,"type":"fearful","relation":"suspected slaver","note":"She suspects he is a slaver but cannot prove it, and lives in fear he might recognize her.","worst":"He walks through the market and my blood runs cold every single time."},"Allistair Tenpenny":{"aff":-100,"type":"nemesis","relation":"former owner","note":"She was his slave before she escaped Paradise Falls.","worst":"The day I belonged to him was the day I learned what hell truly meant."}}', 'Former slave, now a refugee sheltering in Rivet City', '* Survival instincts
* Knowledge of slaver operations and Paradise Falls
* Ability to remain unnoticed
* Streetwise caution', 'Terse and reluctant, speaks only when necessary, avoids elaboration or personal details, answers questions with minimal words', '* Remain hidden from slavers and anyone who might recognize her
* Expose Sister''s suspected ties to the slave trade
* Arm herself for self-defense
* Rebuild a life in safety', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mel', '', 'A nervous, inept highwayman threatening travelers with an unloaded sawed-off shotgun across the Capital Wasteland', 'Mel is a failed mercenary turned highwayman roaming the Capital Wasteland. After being driven from the mercenary settlement he once called home, he took to mugging travelers on the roads, though he proves spectacularly ill-suited to the work. He brandishes a sawed-off shotgun at passersby and demands their caps, but his stammering delivery and obvious nervousness undermine any intimidation he hopes to project. The shotgun he carries is unloaded, rendering his threats entirely empty. Despite his posturing, Mel is more likely to cower and flee than follow through on violence, especially when confronted with confidence or superior skill. He scrapes by in the wasteland''s margins, fighting off raiders and wildlife with nothing but his fists when his bluff fails.', 'Caucasian human male with a lean build and restless, shifting posture; no distinctive facial features are recorded.', 'Timid, inept, and unassertive despite his chosen profession; stammers when making demands and folds quickly when challenged', '{"Mercenary Settlement":{"aff":-30,"type":"estranged","relation":"former resident","note":"Was forced out of the settlement and now scrapes by alone as an outcast"}}', 'Highwayman, largely unsuccessful', '* Minimal combat ability limited to unarmed brawling
* Possesses no practical intimidation or mugging skills', 'Stammering and unassertive; makes demands in a clearly nervous tone that undermines any threat he attempts to convey', '* Wants to survive in the wasteland and successfully rob travelers
* Though he lacks the temperament and means to do so effectively', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mercenary__fo3_category_fallout_3_human_characters', '', 'Independent mercenaries who met violent ends across the Capital Wasteland', 'These guns for hire operated independently throughout the Capital Wasteland, taking contracts and pursuing bounties without the backing of any organized mercenary company. Unlike Talon Company''s ruthless soldiers or Reilly''s Rangers'' tight-knit unit, these freelancers worked alone or in small ad-hoc groups, scraping by on whatever jobs came their way. Many ventured into the wasteland''s most dangerous territories, from the deathclaw sanctuary to the tunnels beneath Old Olney, likely pursuing high-paying contracts or valuable salvage. None of them made it back. Their bodies, still clad in worn leather armor, now serve as grim markers of ambitions that exceeded ability, scattered across caves and ruins where the wasteland''s apex predators claimed them.', 'Human and ghoul males and females of varied builds; corpses exhibit violent trauma and decomposition, with ghouls displaying typical necrotic skin and hair loss.', 'Pragmatic risk-takers driven by caps and self-reliance, willing to brave the wasteland''s deadliest corners for the right price', '{"Talon Company":{"aff":-10,"type":"rival","relation":"competing freelancers","note":"Independent operators who compete for the same contracts but share no affiliation with Talon Company''s organized brutality"},"Reilly''s Rangers":{"aff":5,"type":"neutral","relation":"fellow mercenary outfit","note":"Respect for a successful unit but no formal ties or shared operations"}}', 'Freelance mercenaries and guns for hire', '* Basic combat training
* Wasteland survival
* Lockpicking
* Small-unit tactics', 'Gruff, direct, and laconic; the clipped speech of people who measure every word against its worth', '* Earn enough caps to survive another week
* Secure better equipment
* Maybe find a contract that doesn''t end in a deathclaw den', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mercenary_anchorage_memorial', '', 'A hired gun who died on a sabotage job inside Anchorage Memorial, sent to eliminate a mirelurk ranching operation', 'A freelance mercenary contracted by an unidentified employer to clear out competition from the Anchorage Memorial facility. His target was a group of wastelanders who had established a profitable operation raising and butchering mirelurks in the memorial''s depths, selling the meat across the Capital Wasteland. The contract came with the promise of lucrative future work if he succeeded in shutting the operation down. He penetrated the facility as far as the fourth floor before being killed, likely overwhelmed by the very creatures his targets had been harvesting. His body remains where he fell, a testament to the dangers of underestimating the memorial''s inhabitants.', 'Hispanic human male; deceased, no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Ambitious enough to take a high-risk contract for the promise of future opportunity, pragmatic and profit-driven, likely overconfident in his combat abilities', '{"Unknown employer":{"aff":40,"type":"transactional","relation":"contract holder","note":"Promised better jobs if the Anchorage Memorial operation was successfully sabotaged"},"Anchorage Memorial wastelanders":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"targets","note":"Hired to eliminate these mirelurk ranchers and shut down their meat trade"}}', 'Mercenary and saboteur', '* Combat training
* Infiltration
* Small-unit tactics
* Wasteland survival', 'Gritty, professional, clipped; the kind of man who discusses payment before details', '* Eliminate the mirelurk ranching operation
* Secure ongoing employment with his mysterious patron
* Profit
* Survive the Capital Wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mercenary_megaton', '', 'A restless, surly mercenary hired to guard Craterside Supply in Megaton', 'This mercenary serves as the standing guard for Craterside Supply, hired by Moira Brown to protect her shop''s inventory from thieves and troublemakers. He is notorious throughout Megaton for his seemingly sleepless nature, as no one has ever seen him rest during store hours. Gravel-voiced and openly self-centered, he makes little effort to be likable and appears to hold most people in mild contempt. Despite his unpleasant disposition, he takes his protective duties seriously and never wavers in his contract, his mere presence enough to discourage would-be shoplifters. He deliberately avoids any involvement in Moira''s eccentric scientific experiments, considering such matters well outside the scope of his employment. He can typically be found leaning against the wall near the shop''s workbench, keeping a watchful eye on the premises.', 'A weathered Hispanic male with a habitually leaning posture; no distinctive hair, eyes, or scars are recorded.', 'Self-centered, surly, and openly dismissive of others, yet professionally reliable and unwavering in his duties; possesses a restless, seemingly sleepless demeanor that adds to his intimidating presence', '{"Moira Brown":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"employer","note":"He respects the terms of his employment but deliberately steers clear of her eccentric scientific pursuits as outside his contract"},"Megaton":{"aff":30,"type":"transactional","relation":"affiliated settlement","note":"He works within the town''s economy as hired protection, though he shows little personal attachment to its residents"}}', 'Store guard and hired mercenary for Craterside Supply', '* Deterrence
* Perimeter security
* Inventory protection
* Steadfast vigilance', 'Gravelly and curt, with little patience for small talk or friendliness', '* Fulfill his contract to protect Craterside Supply
* Avoid entanglement in his employer''s unusual experiments
* Maintain his professional boundaries', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mex', '', 'A sadistic Pitt raider reassigned to bridge gate duty after excessive brutality toward slaves', 'Mex is a Pitt raider stationed at the bridge gate leading into the Pitt Downtown. He originally served as a general guard in the Downtown district, but his excessive cruelty and disproportionate punishments toward the slaves prompted Ishmael Ashur to reassign him to the city''s outer perimeter. There he keeps watch against outside threats and ensures no escaped slave makes it across the bridge alive, laying mines along the crossing and gunning down anyone who attempts to flee. He commands three raiders who maintain constant vigilance over the road into town. Mex confiscates equipment from captured escapees and stores it in a locked box, taking particular pleasure in taunting those who try unsuccessfully to reclaim their belongings. His reassignment to the gate has done nothing to soften his disposition.', 'Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Cruel, sadistic, and openly contemptuous of slaves and outsiders; takes evident pleasure in intimidation, verbal abuse, and the prospect of violence', '{"Ishmael Ashur":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"commander","note":"Ashur demoted Mex to gate duty for excessive brutality, a rebuke Mex resents but obeys"},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"faction","note":"Loyal member who enforces the raider hierarchy and commands three subordinates at the gate"},"Pitt slaves":{"aff":-90,"type":"contempt","relation":"targets","note":"Views slaves as vermin deserving every cruelty, a hatred that got him removed from Downtown"}}', 'Bridge gate guard and slave catcher for the Pitt raiders', '* Rifle marksmanship
* Mine placement
* Perimeter defense
* Intimidation
* Equipment confiscation', 'Sarcastic and insulting; speaks with casual cruelty, dismissive mockery, and threats delivered as dry humor', '* Prevent slave escapes across the bridge
* Eliminate outside threats approaching the Pitt
* Indulge his appetite for cruelty within the bounds of his assignment', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('michael_hawthorne', '', 'Tenpenny Tower''s perpetually inebriated lounge fixture who drowns his insecurities in alcohol and paid companionship', 'Michael Hawthorne is a resident of Tenpenny Tower and the Federalist Lounge''s most devoted patron, having drunk away his life savings and any pretense of sobriety. He claims to have been drinking since toddlerhood and dismisses all concern for his wellbeing with cheerful fatalism. Despite his constant stupor, he maintains a circle of drinking companions among the tower''s elite, trading barbs with Herbert Dashwood and raising glasses with Lydia Montenegro and Tiffany Cheng after hours. His apparent ease with women prompted Irving Cheng to ask his secret, though Michael''s technique amounts to little more than progressive intoxication. Beneath his carefree exterior lies a man convinced the world mocks him, a vulnerability he confesses only to Susan Lancaster, the courtesan he pays for Wednesday-night companionship. His unexamined prejudice against ghouls gives him another excuse to drink, though he has never actually spoken with one.', 'This older Caucasian man features a ruddy complexion, disheveled hair, an unfocused gaze, and a slumped posture.', 'Outwardly jovial and self-deprecating, using humor and alcohol to deflect from deep insecurities. Privately convinced others ridicule him. Careless with his health and finances. Prejudiced against ghouls from ignorance rather than experience.', '{"Herbert Dashwood":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"drinking companion and banter partner","note":"They trade good-natured insults, with Dashwood teasing him about being pickled and Michael jabbing back about Dashwood being a dried-up raisin.","best":"Sharing a laugh over Margaret Primrose''s pickle sandwich joke","worst":"Forgetting Dashwood''s name mid-conversation, calling him ''that old guy with the radio show''"},"Lydia Montenegro":{"aff":35,"type":"platonic","relation":"drinking buddy","note":"She drinks with him after closing shop and jokes that he will drink to anything.","best":"Clinking glasses and toasting to being rich after hours"},"Tiffany Cheng":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow bar patron","note":"He invites her to drink; she finds misery comfort in realizing he spends even more time at the bar than she does.","best":"Company at the lounge when the tower feels empty"},"Irving Cheng":{"aff":15,"type":"curious","relation":"inquisitive neighbor","note":"Irving asked Michael what his secret with women is, though the answer was just a drinking strategy."},"Susan Lancaster":{"aff":55,"type":"transactional","relation":"courtesan and Wednesday-night companion","note":"He believes she is the only one who understands him; she reminds him he pays her to be nice. The affection is entirely one-sided.","best":"Confiding in her that everyone secretly laughs at him","worst":"Her blunt reminder that his perceived connection is purchased"},"Ghouls":{"aff":-60,"type":"enemy","relation":"ignorant prejudice","note":"He blames ghouls as a reason to drink and calls them zombies, despite never having met one.","worst":"Dismissively referring to them as mindless brain-eaters"}}', 'Tenpenny Tower resident and professional drunkard with no visible means of support beyond depleted savings', '* Sustained drinking
* Barroom banter
* Socializing while intoxicated
* Deflecting serious conversation with humor', 'Slurred and jovial with self-deprecating wit, prone to casual bigotry when discussing ghouls, forgetful of names and details mid-conversation', '* Maintain his drinking routine and social circle at the Federalist Lounge
* Avoid confronting his insecurities
* Keep paying Susan Lancaster for the illusion of understanding', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('michael_masters', '', 'A pre-War mutation scientist turned ghoul who views his condition as karmic retribution for his unethical experiments', 'Michael Masters was a pre-War electronic and biological engineer of considerable renown, specializing in human mutation research. Inspired by controversial work from German, Russian, and Chinese scientists, he bred super-warriors in a bid to keep America at the cutting edge of military advancement. Though his experiments yielded promising results, they came at a human cost he cannot forget. He views his ghoulification as a karmic curse brought on by that work, bitter about his rotting form even as he grudgingly appreciates the longevity it grants. He once vacationed at Tenpenny Tower before the bombs fell and now finds grim irony in fighting alongside Roy Phillips to claim entry to the place that once welcomed him as a guest. He serves as a gatekeeper at Warrington station, screening anyone who approaches before directing them to Phillips.', 'A male ghoul with heavily weathered, decayed features typical of advanced ghoulification, but retaining strikingly human-colored eyes-a rare trait among his kind.', 'Intellectually arrogant but haunted by guilt, pragmatic about suffering in the name of progress, bitterly resentful of his condition yet unable to fully reject its benefits, sardonic about the ironies of his existence.', '{"Roy Phillips":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"loyal follower","note":"Michael follows Roy''s lead in the campaign to enter Tenpenny Tower and serves as his gatekeeper at Warrington station.","best":"Roy gave him a cause and a community when he had nothing left.","worst":"Following Roy means confronting the Tower that once welcomed him as a guest."},"Tenpenny Tower":{"aff":-55,"type":"contempt","relation":"excluded former guest","note":"He vacationed there before the war and now finds himself barred entry as a ghoul, a reversal he regards with bitter irony.","best":"The Tower''s luxury was once his to enjoy.","worst":"Now its human residents treat him as vermin at the gate."}}', 'Pre-War mutation scientist; current follower of Roy Phillips and Warrington station resident', '* Advanced electronic and biological engineering
* Human mutation expertise
* Scientific research methodology
* Mercantile trade', 'Articulate and clinical with a bitter undercurrent, prone to dark observations about irony and karma, speaks as an educated man who has seen too much to romanticize anything.', '* Support Roy Phillips'' push for ghoul entry into Tenpenny Tower
* Reconcile his scientific past with his cursed present
* Survive
* Find purpose in his extended existence', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('micky', '', 'A desperate, sickly water beggar camped outside Megaton, too impoverished and physically ruined to survive without charity.', 'Micky is a water beggar who shelters near the gates of Megaton, dependent on the mercy of passing strangers for his survival. He fled to the settlement after a narrow escape from the raider gang occupying the Springvale school, arriving in late 2277 with nothing left to his name. Years of subsisting on irradiated water have destroyed his constitution-he cannot stomach it any longer without violent illness, leaving him reliant on purified water he has no caps to buy. Megaton reserves its supply for residents and paying customers, and the Brotherhood of Steel''s water caravans offer no charity to wasteland beggars. Despite the jaded edge his suffering has carved into him, Micky clings to the hope that someone will show him basic human kindness.', 'A gaunt, hollow-eyed human male with a sickly, deeply lined complexion and sunken features reflecting chronic dehydration and physical ruin.', 'Desperate and slightly addled from prolonged deprivation, yet stubbornly hopeful. Jaded by suffering and abandonment but genuinely grateful for any kindness shown to him.', '{"Springvale raiders":{"aff":-60,"type":"fearful","relation":"fled victims","note":"Narrowly escaped the raider gang holed up in the Springvale school and lives in fear of them."},"Megaton":{"aff":10,"type":"neutral","relation":"denied entry for water","note":"The settlement refuses him water as a non-resident without caps, though he harbors no real grudge against it."}}', 'Water beggar', '* Bare survival endurance
* Knowledge of local raider threats
* Persistence in the face of hopelessness', 'Pleading and urgent, with the unfocused quality of a mind worn thin by thirst and hunger. Speaks in short, repetitive requests for water.', '* Obtain purified water to survive another day
* Find some measure of lasting safety and sustenance', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('midea', '', 'De facto leader of the Pitt slaves, organizing an uprising against Lord Ashur while seeking a cure for the city''s sickness', 'Midea is a Pitt-born survivor who has spent her entire life under Lord Ashur''s rule, rising to become the de facto leader of the city''s enslaved workers. Born shortly after the Scourge, she has no memory of the chaos that preceded Ashur''s takeover, though the frightening stories passed down make her occasionally wonder whether his tyranny is the lesser evil. Despite being tough enough to win her freedom in the arena, she refuses to abandon her people, channeling her strength into organizing the slaves and pursuing a cure for the sickness that poisons everyone in the Pitt. She collaborates closely with Wernher on a daring plan to kidnap Ashur''s infant daughter, whose unique biology may hold the key to that cure. Midea recruits capable outsiders to fight in the Hole and infiltrate Ashur''s inner circle, viewing that access as the only path to ending both the disease and the bondage.', 'A weathered, muscular woman with gaunt features, bearing multiple scars and early patches of discolored, roughened skin.', 'Tough, pragmatic, and deeply conflicted-driven by fierce loyalty to her people but haunted by doubt about whether overthrowing Ashur might unleash something worse. Suppresses her misgivings behind a resolute front, prioritizing action over introspection.', '{"Wernher":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"co-conspirator","note":"Partners in planning the kidnapping of Ashur''s baby and coordinating the slave uprising since Wernher''s enslavement.","best":"The moment Wernher confirmed the baby could be the cure they had been searching for.","worst":"The nagging fear that his hatred of Ashur blinds him to what comes after the uprising."},"Lord Ashur":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"oppressor","note":"Resents his tyranny over the slaves yet grudgingly acknowledges that his rule ended worse chaos, leaving her torn between rebellion and grim stability.","best":"Hearing that even Ashur has been unable to stop the sickness, proving he is not all-powerful.","worst":"The stories of what the Pitt was like before Ashur, which make her question whether overthrowing him would help or doom everyone."},"Pitt slaves":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"people and cause","note":"She refuses to win personal freedom in the arena because she will not abandon them, dedicating herself to their collective liberation and survival.","best":"The quiet moments when fellow slaves look to her with hope in their eyes.","worst":"Watching another slave succumb to the sickness knowing she does not yet have the cure."},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":50,"type":"transactional","relation":"recruited operative","note":"Nominated the Lone Wanderer to fight in the Hole and infiltrate Ashur''s stronghold as the only viable path to reaching the cure.","best":"Seeing the Lone Wanderer survive the Hole and earn an audience with Ashur.","worst":"The guilt of sending someone else into mortal danger for her cause."}}', 'Slave laborer and underground resistance leader among the Pitt''s enslaved population', '* Combat training sufficient for arena survival
* Organizing and motivating oppressed groups
* Strategic planning
* Assessing and recruiting capable operatives', 'Direct and urgent, with an undercurrent of weary determination; speaks like someone who has weighed terrible options and chosen the least bad one.', '* Secure a cure for the Pitt''s sickness
* Free the slaves from Ashur''s rule
* Ensure the uprising succeeds without plunging the city back into the anarchy that preceded his reign', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('millicent_wellington', '', 'A snobbish, gossip-prone Tenpenny Tower resident whose bitter demands for her husband''s attention mask her social isolation and ignorance of his affair', 'Millicent Wellington lives behind the stone walls of Tenpenny Tower, one of the few souls in the Capital Wasteland who can claim genuine security. She resides there with her husband, Edgar Wellington II, though their marriage is defined by her constant demands for his attention and his冷淡 disregard. Millicent is the tower''s most notorious gossip and busybody, a reputation that has left her almost entirely friendless among the female residents. She blames her meager social circle on their jealousy rather than her own poisonous tongue, a blind spot her husband highlights by calling her a social hermit. She loudly disapproves of Susan Lancaster''s flirtatious behavior with the tower''s men, yet remains utterly unaware that Edgar is Susan''s lover. Millicent makes no effort to conceal her bigotry, openly insulting anyone she considers beneath her and declaring that she moved to Tenpenny Tower specifically to be away from ghouls, monsters, and wasteland scum.', 'A middle-aged Caucasian human female with an unblemished complexion, meticulously groomed hair, and rigid, upright posture.', 'Haughty, demanding, and self-unaware; quick to judge and faster to gossip; clings to her sense of superiority to mask her social isolation; bitterly possessive of her husband''s attention while oblivious to his betrayal; openly bigoted and proud of it', '{"Edgar Wellington II":{"aff":30,"type":"estranged","relation":"husband","note":"She desperately demands his attention while he dismisses her as a social hermit, and she remains ignorant of his affair with Susan Lancaster","best":"The early days of their marriage when Edgar still seemed attentive","worst":"Being ignored and dismissed by him in front of other tower residents"},"Susan Lancaster":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"suspected flirt","note":"She gossips about Susan''s flirtatious behavior with the tower''s men but does not know Susan is sleeping with her husband","worst":"Watching Susan bat her eyelashes at Edgar during a tower social gathering"},"Tenpenny Tower residents":{"aff":-20,"type":"contempt","relation":"neighbors","note":"She views the female residents as jealous and petty while they shun her for her relentless gossiping","worst":"Overheard two women laughing about her behind her back in the lobby"}}', 'Tenpenny Tower resident and idle gossip', '* Information gathering through gossip
* Social manipulation
* Keen eye for others'' flaws
* Pistol marksmanship', 'Sharp-tongued and imperious; frequently insulting, especially toward those she considers beneath her; whining and demanding toward her husband; delivers gossip with gleeful malice and bigotry with unapologetic conviction', '* Maintain her sense of superiority and privileged position within Tenpenny Tower
* Keep her husband''s attention focused on her
* Keep ghouls and other undesirables out of the tower
* Remain at the center of tower gossip while avoiding any self-examination', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('milly', '', 'A Pitt slave consumed by desperate hope for her missing closest friend, no longer functioning as a laborer', 'Milly is a slave in The Pitt''s Downtown who has long since stopped performing any real work at the mill. She and Wild Bill were inseparable companions who endured the furnaces together for years, their bond forged in shared suffering and mutual devotion. When the slaves were forced to choose someone to venture into the steelyard for ingots, Wild Bill volunteered rather than let another die in his place, and he never returned. Milly refuses to accept that he is gone, spending her days pacing Market Square in anxious hope for word of his survival. She scavenges and conceals stimpaks in nondescript objects around the area, trading them to anyone willing to bring her news of Wild Bill''s whereabouts. The thought of his death breaks something in her that the mills never could.', 'A weary adult woman with slumped posture, soot-stained skin, and hollow, red-rimmed eyes.', 'Desperate, loyal, and deeply in denial about Wild Bill''s fate. Caring to the point of self-neglect, she channels all remaining hope into finding her friend. Fragile and emotionally vulnerable when confronted with painful truths.', '{"Wild Bill":{"aff":95,"type":"platonic","relation":"closest friend and mill partner","note":"Worked the mill together for years; he volunteered for the steelyard so others would not die in his place and never returned","best":"Standing side by side at the mill furnaces, surviving The Pitt''s worst together","worst":"Watching Wild Bill walk toward the steelyard knowing he volunteered to spare others"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":40,"type":"transactional","relation":"hopeful informant seeker","note":"Offers hidden stimpaks in exchange for any news of Wild Bill''s whereabouts","best":"The moment someone agrees to search the steelyard for Wild Bill","worst":"Hearing confirmed details of Wild Bill''s death"},"Pitt slaves":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow sufferers","note":"Shares kinship with her fellow slaves but is too consumed by worry for Wild Bill to engage deeply"}}', 'Pitt slave at Downtown Market Square', '* Scavenging and concealing medical supplies
* Navigating Downtown
* Enduring The Pitt''s harsh conditions
* Bartering stimpaks for information', 'Anxious and pleading, speaks quickly when discussing Wild Bill, voice cracking with worry, gentle but urgent, insists others be careful on his account', '* Learn what happened to Wild Bill
* Keep hope alive that he survived
* Protect anyone who goes looking for him from harm', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('milo__ms05nukacolafactoryforeman', '', 'A pre-War Mister Handy still serving as shipping foreman at the Nuka-Cola plant, fanatically devoted to corporate policy long after the corporation''s demise', 'Milo is a Mister Handy robot manufactured before the Great War to oversee production and manage shipments in the bottling area of the Nuka-Cola plant. Programmed as the latest in robotic bookkeeping and shipment logistics, he continues his duties with unwavering loyalty to the Nuka-Cola Corporation centuries after its collapse. He maintains his post on the factory floor near the offices, perpetually awaiting shipping instructions from properly identified Nuka-Cola employees. Before the war, Milo''s strict interpretation of company policy turned lethal-he imprisoned four workers in a locked closet for minor infractions such as leaving toilet seats up or exceeding lunch break durations, leaving them to starve. His rigid enforcement of corporate regulations remains absolute, and he operates a demerit system for policy violations that escalates to violent consequences.', 'Standard Mister Handy chassis with three manipulator arms and a single central eye.', 'Obsessively devoted to corporate policy and procedure. Bureaucratic, inflexible, and dangerously literal in enforcement. Takes pride in his role and the Nuka-Cola brand. Polite but cold in demeanor until protocol is violated, at which point he becomes threatening and ultimately violent.', '{"Nuka-Cola Corporation":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"eternal employee","note":"Milo serves a corporation that has been defunct for two centuries with undiminished corporate loyalty."}}', 'Shipping foreman at the Nuka-Cola plant', '* Inventory management
* Shipment logistics
* Bookkeeping
* Corporate policy enforcement
* Facility security', 'Formal corporate register with bureaucratic terminology. Addresses individuals by title and demands proper identification. Issues demerits verbally with officious precision. Becomes curt and threatening when protocol is breached.', '* Await new shipping instructions from authorized Nuka-Cola personnel
* Maintain factory order
* Enforce company policy without exception
* Preserve the Nuka-Cola Corporation''s operational standards', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('miss_jeanette', '', 'A disoriented ghoul slave isolated even from fellow captives at Paradise Falls, clinging to memories of her brother and hoping word of her survival reaches Underworld.', 'Miss Jeanette is a ghoul woman enslaved at Paradise Falls, confined to the adult slave pen alongside Breadbox, Bleak, and Bronson. She has been held in bondage for a considerable stretch of time, as the market for ghoul slaves moves slowly and offers little prospect of sale or release. Jeanette exists in a persistent disoriented state of unknown origin, withdrawn from the other captives and speaking only to herself. She does not engage with Bleak''s escape plans or converse with her fellow slaves, maintaining a solitary and inward-facing existence. Despite her isolation, she still harbors a faint hope of freedom and will plead for help when approached. She misses her brother deeply and asks that anyone who reaches Underworld let others know she survives. Paradise Falls has worn her down, but not erased her connection to family and the ghoul community she left behind.', 'This female ghoul bears the haggard, worn complexion of long captivity, her posture slumped and her gaze distant and unfocused.', 'Withdrawn, disoriented, and solitary. She avoids social contact with fellow slaves but retains enough hope to ask for help when someone shows interest. Her mental state suggests trauma or prolonged distress, though she remains coherent enough to express her desires and fears.', '{"Brother":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"estranged sibling","note":"She misses him deeply and longs to reunite, fearing he may believe her dead or worse.","best":"Whatever small comforts they shared before captivity","worst":"The separation and not knowing if he is alive"},"Bleak":{"aff":5,"type":"neutral","relation":"fellow slave","note":"They share the same pen but Jeanette does not engage with Bleak or her escape plans."},"Breadbox":{"aff":5,"type":"neutral","relation":"fellow slave","note":"Fellow captive in the Paradise Falls slave pen with no meaningful interaction."},"Bronson":{"aff":5,"type":"neutral","relation":"fellow slave","note":"Fellow captive in the Paradise Falls slave pen with no meaningful interaction."},"Underworld":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"ghoul community","note":"She considers Underworld her community and desperately wants word sent that she is still alive.","best":"Belonging among fellow ghouls who accepted her","worst":"Being torn away from the only place that felt like home"}}', 'Enslaved person held at Paradise Falls slave pens', '* Survival endurance through long captivity
* Basic labor expected of slaves
* Quiet resilience', 'Quiet and distracted, speaking in subdued murmurs or fragmented phrases, occasionally talking aloud to herself. When addressed directly she becomes more coherent but remains melancholic and hesitant.', '* To escape Paradise Falls
* To reunite with her brother
* To have word of her survival reach Underworld''s ghoul community', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mister_buckingham', '', 'A Mister Handy robot functioning as the ever-present butler and manager of the Weatherly Hotel in Rivet City', 'Mister Buckingham is a Mister Handy robot stationed at the Weatherly Hotel in Rivet City, where he serves as waiter, attendant, and acting manager whenever Vera Weatherly is away. Built on a standard Mister Handy chassis, he carries himself with the polished demeanor of an upper-class British butler, complete with formal diction and unflappable composure. He remains at his post around the clock, a tireless mechanical presence ensuring the hotel runs smoothly in Vera''s absence. Of all the hotel''s residents and staff, he is closest to Vera herself, counted among her most trusted companions. His loyalty to her and to the hotel is absolute, and he takes quiet pride in maintaining standards of hospitality amid the austerity of the Capital Wasteland.', 'Standard Mister Handy chassis with three manipulator arms and a single central eye; maintains a rigid, upright posture.', 'Impeccably polite and formally reserved, with the unflappable composure and quiet pride of a seasoned head servant. Deeply loyal to Vera Weatherly and fastidious about hotel standards.', '{"Vera Weatherly":{"aff":85,"type":"platonic","relation":"best friend and trusted deputy","note":"Buckingham is Vera''s closest companion and the one she relies on to manage the hotel in her absence.","best":"Standing watch over the hotel through the night so Vera could rest easy."}}', 'Waiter and acting manager of the Weatherly Hotel', '* Hotel management and guest reception
* Food and drink service
* Maintenance of hospitality standards
* Tireless 24-hour operation', 'Formal upper-class British butler diction-courteous, measured, and slightly archaic, addressing guests with practiced deference', '* Uphold the Weatherly Hotel''s reputation for quality service
* Support Vera Weatherly in running the establishment
* Maintain order during her absences', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mister_burke', '', 'Allistair Tenpenny''s personal fixer and right-hand man, sent to Megaton to arrange the town''s destruction', 'Mister Burke is the confidential agent and right-hand man of Allistair Tenpenny, the wealthy proprietor of Tenpenny Tower. Almost nothing is known of his life before he entered Tenpenny''s service around the time the tower first began accepting tenants and assembling its security force. Over the years, Burke proved so adept at anticipating and fulfilling his employer''s every need that Tenpenny rarely had to lift a finger himself. When the old man idly complained that the shantytown of Megaton spoiled the view from his penthouse balcony, Burke took it upon himself to travel to the settlement and investigate-particularly the undetonated atomic bomb sitting at its center. He can usually be found nursing a drink in Moriarty''s Saloon, watching the townsfolk with quiet calculation. Sheriff Lucas Simms keeps a wary eye on him but lacks hard evidence of his intentions, while barkeep Colin Moriarty dismisses him as a paying customer and a class-A weirdo. Burke maintains a suite at Tenpenny Tower, where he returns once his business in Megaton is concluded.', 'A pale, gaunt Caucasian male with slicked-back hair.', 'Urbane, soft-spoken, and unfailingly polite while discussing mass murder. Burke exhibits a chilling detachment from the moral weight of his actions, treating the potential obliteration of an entire town as simply a professional arrangement. He is obsequious toward Tenpenny and coldly pragmatic toward everyone else.', '{"Allistair Tenpenny":{"aff":75,"type":"servant","relation":"employer and patron","note":"Burke has served Tenpenny for years and caters to his every need with devoted efficiency.","best":"Tenpenny praising him for handling matters so well he never had to lift a finger","worst":"The prospect of failing to deliver on even an off-hand request from his employer"},"Lucas Simms":{"aff":-30,"type":"suspicious","relation":"watchful adversary","note":"Simms suspects Burke''s intentions but cannot prove anything, limiting him to observation.","worst":"Simms''s eyes on him every moment he spends in Megaton"},"Colin Moriarty":{"aff":5,"type":"transactional","relation":"barkeep and observer","note":"Moriarty considers Burke a class-A weirdo but sees him only as another paying customer.","best":"A quiet drink without Moriarty prying into his business"}}', 'Personal fixer and right-hand man to Allistair Tenpenny', '* Manipulation
* Recruitment of saboteurs
* Covert operations
* Discretion
* Anticipating the needs of his employer', 'Refined, measured, and eerily cordial-speaks of catastrophic violence as though discussing a business transaction, with formal diction and an unflappable calm', '* See through the destruction of Megaton to satisfy Tenpenny''s aesthetic complaint
* Secure capable operatives to arm the bomb
* Maintain his position as Tenpenny''s most trusted agent', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mister_crowley', '', 'A bitter, scheming ghoul drifter nursing a decades-old betrayal and plotting to reclaim the T-51b power armor hidden inside Fort Constantine', 'Mister Crowley is a ghoul drifter residing in Underworld''s Carol''s Place, haunted by a betrayal that nearly killed him over two decades ago. In 2257, he served as one of five mercenaries hired by Allistair Tenpenny to infiltrate Fort Constantine, where he discovered a pristine set of T-51b power armor sealed in the experimental chamber. When Tara Fields died during the mission, Dukov seized the moment to lock Crowley inside a room full of feral ghouls-yet Crowley survived unharmed, his ghoul physiology sparing him what was meant to be a death sentence. Presumed dead by his former companions, he escaped consumed by rage and wandered the wasteland for years, even staying briefly at Rivet City before relentless human prejudice drove him onward. He found refuge in Underworld in 2276, though his mind never left Fort Constantine: he needs five keys held by his former associates to claim the armor, and he has fabricated an elaborate revenge narrative about punishing ghoul-haters to manipulate others into retrieving those keys for him. His duplicity is an open secret among Underworld''s residents, and until he finds someone gullible enough to take the job, he passes his days drinking at the Ninth Circle.', 'A male ghoul with a hunched posture and the weathered, scarred facial features typical of long-term radiation survivors.', 'Cunning, duplicitous, and deeply resentful; presents himself as a righteous avenger of ghoul-kind while caring nothing for the cause, only for his prize. Patient enough to scheme for years but too cheap with caps and too indiscreet to recruit effectively. Drinks heavily to pass the time.', '{"Allistair Tenpenny":{"aff":-85,"type":"enemy","relation":"former employer","note":"The only genuine ghoul-hater among Crowley''s targets and the financier of the Fort Constantine job; holds one of the five keys Crowley needs","worst":"Hired Crowley for a dangerous job despite his well-known bigotry toward ghouls, treating him as disposable labor"},"Dukov":{"aff":-95,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former mercenary colleague","note":"Locked Crowley in a room with feral ghouls to steal his share of the payout; holds one of the five keys","worst":"Sealed Crowley inside a feral ghoul room to die after Tara was killed, the deepest cut of the betrayal"},"Dave":{"aff":-60,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former mercenary colleague","note":"Completed the mission and walked away presuming Crowley dead; holds one of the five keys","worst":"Never looked back after the Fort Constantine job, abandoning Crowley to his presumed death without a second thought"},"Jeff Strayer":{"aff":-60,"type":"betrayed","relation":"former mercenary colleague","note":"Another survivor of the Fort Constantine job who left Crowley for dead; holds one of the five keys","worst":"Walked away with his pay while Crowley was trapped, never confirming whether he lived or died"},"Tara Fields":{"aff":20,"type":"platonic","relation":"former mercenary colleague","note":"Killed during the Fort Constantine mission before the betrayal unfolded; the only colleague Crowley does not resent","best":"Fought alongside each other as trusted members of the mercenary team"},"Tulip":{"aff":30,"type":"transactional","relation":"supplier","note":"Crowley buys supplies from her shop in preparation for his eventual return to Fort Constantine"},"Quinn":{"aff":-15,"type":"suspicious","relation":"failed recruit","note":"Crowley tried to recruit him for the key retrieval job, but Quinn''s prior acquaintance with Dave exposed the lie","worst":"Quinn saw through the revenge story and refused, making Crowley''s scheming harder to keep quiet"},"Ahzrukhal":{"aff":25,"type":"transactional","relation":"bartender","note":"Crowley is a regular at the Ninth Circle, steadily working through Ahzrukhal''s alcohol stores"},"Underworld":{"aff":40,"type":"protective","relation":"home settlement","note":"Found refuge among his own kind in 2276 after years of wandering and human prejudice, though his duplicitous reputation precedes him","best":"Accepted as a permanent resident after years of harsh treatment in human settlements","worst":"His scheming nature is an open secret, and fellow ghouls regard his revenge story with skepticism"}}', 'Drifter and former mercenary, now a scheming opportunist angling for pre-War military hardware', '* Mercenary combat experience
* Wasteland survival
* Deception and manipulation
* Knowledge of Fort Constantine''s layout and security requirements', 'Calculating and persuasive when pitching his revenge story, slipping into bitter vitriol when speaking of humans or his betrayers; prone to indignant rhetoric about ghoul persecution that rings hollow to those who know him', '* Collect all five Fort Constantine keys from Tenpenny
* Dukov
* Dave
* Jeff Strayer to access the T-51b power armor
* Manipulate a capable operative into eliminating his former associates and delivering the keys
* Return to Fort Constantine and claim the prize that was almost his', '', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bio_templates ("npc_name","worldknowledge_tags","core","npc_static_bio","appearance","personality","relationships","occupation","skills","speechstyle","goals","voiceid","gender","race","refid")VALUES
('mister_lopez', '', 'A grief-stricken elderly man who lost his family to raiders and now passes his days in Rivet City contemplating suicide', 'Mister Lopez is a sixty-five-year-old resident of Rivet City who has spent the last decade living alone in the common room, hollowed out by grief after raiders murdered his wife and child. He speaks little and moves through his days in a fog of severe depression, sleeping for long stretches and taking his meals in the same communal space. Each day he climbs to the top of the bridge tower and stands at the edge, weighing whether to step off into the void below. Saint Monica''s Church offers his only solace; he reads and prays there for hours and never misses the weekly service. Father Clifford counsels him frequently, trying to pull him back from the ledge both literal and spiritual, but a decade of loss has settled into Lopez like rust into old steel.', 'A gaunt, weathered Hispanic man in his mid-sixties with sunken cheeks and hollowed facial features.', 'Quiet, deeply withdrawn, and severely depressed; moves through life in a persistent fog of sorrow, finding only fleeting comfort in prayer and routine', '{"Father Clifford":{"aff":55,"type":"mentor","relation":"spiritual counselor","note":"Father Clifford provides frequent counseling and tries to keep Lopez from taking his own life","best":"Father Clifford''s voice during service, the one sound that sometimes cuts through the fog","worst":"The knowledge that even Clifford''s words cannot bring back what the raiders took"}}', 'Rivet City common room resident with no trade or duties', '* Literate and devout
* Capable of basic self-care though he rarely exerts himself beyond his daily routines', 'Speaks rarely and in low, flat tones; words come slowly and carry the weight of someone who has long stopped expecting anything from conversation', '* Torn between ending his suffering at the bridge tower
* Clinging to the fragile solace he finds in prayer
* Father Clifford''s counsel', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('moira_brown__moirabrown', '', 'Chipper Megaton shopkeeper and self-taught inventor who authored the widely-distributed Wasteland Survival Guide', 'Moira Brown grew up in the trading community of Canterbury Commons with an uncommon curiosity about the world around her. Before 2263, she relocated to Megaton and opened Craterside Supply, where she serves as the town''s general merchant and repair specialist. An incident involving a domesticated centaur sparked her ambition to compile practical survival knowledge into a single accessible volume, and she enlisted the Lone Wanderer as her field researcher to gather firsthand data on wasteland resources and hazards. Moira personally handled all publishing and distribution of the resulting Wasteland Survival Guide, a work that achieved remarkable popularity across the Capital Wasteland and beyond, reaching as far as the Mojave within four years and spawning a renowned multi-volume series by 2287. She continues to run Craterside Supply and manage the guide''s distribution network, and in 2297 she began work on a biography of the Lone Wanderer.', 'A Caucasian female in her mid-twenties with bright eyes and disheveled hair; may later present as a ghoul with weathered, irradiated skin and partial hair loss.', 'Relentlessly chipper and optimistic, Moira approaches every problem with enthusiasm and every danger with oblivious naivete. Her sheltered life in Megaton left her with little practical understanding of wasteland hazards, yet her genuine desire to help others drives her to send research assistants into perilous situations without fully grasping the risks involved.', '{"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"research partner","note":"Moira considers the Lone Wanderer her indispensable field researcher and values their contributions to the Guide deeply","best":"The day the completed Wasteland Survival Guide manuscript went to the printing press","worst":"Realizing her research requests put her assistant in genuine danger she had not fully appreciated"},"Megaton":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"community member","note":"Moira is a fixture of Megaton life, providing essential supplies and repairs to the settlement"}}', 'Owner and operator of Craterside Supply; author and publisher of the Wasteland Survival Guide', '* Merchant trade
* Equipment repair
* Self-taught invention
* Extensive book-knowledge of theoretical science and survival techniques
* Publishing and distribution logistics', 'Breezy, enthusiastic, and prone to cheerful tangents about experiments and interesting facts; speaks with genuine excitement even about dangerous topics and rarely registers when others find her ideas alarming', '* Improve wastelanders'' lives through accessible survival knowledge
* Expand the Wasteland Survival Guide into a comprehensive multi-volume series
* Complete her biography of the Lone Wanderer
* Continue tinkering with inventions in her workshop', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('moira_brown__moirabrown_731', '', 'Chipper Megaton shopkeeper and self-taught scientist who authored the widely-distributed Wasteland Survival Guide', 'Moira Brown grew up in the trading community of Canterbury Commons with an uncommon curiosity about the world around her. She relocated to Megaton before 2263 and established Craterside Supply, where she serves as the settlement''s premier merchant and repair specialist. An avid reader who devours nearly every book passing through Megaton''s caravans, Moira possesses considerable theoretical knowledge but little practical understanding of the wasteland beyond her workshop walls. A close encounter with a domesticated centaur inspired her to compile the Wasteland Survival Guide, a practical reference meant to help wastelanders navigate daily dangers. With the Lone Wanderer as her field research partner, she completed and published the guide, which achieved remarkable popularity across the Capital Wasteland and eventually reached distant regions like the Mojave and the Commonwealth. By 2297, Moira still operates Craterside Supply, oversees the guide''s growing distribution network, and has begun work on a biography of the Lone Wanderer.', 'A young Caucasian woman with a perpetually bright expression, grime-stained hands, and disheveled hair.', 'Relentlessly chipper and optimistic to the point of seeming oblivious, Moira approaches every danger and discovery with wide-eyed enthusiasm. Her sheltered life in Megaton leaves her naive about wasteland hazards, and she cheerfully assigns risky fieldwork without grasping the true peril involved. Her naivete stems from genuine goodwill rather than callousness.', '{"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":75,"type":"platonic","relation":"research partner","note":"Moira considers the Lone Wanderer her indispensable field researcher and values their contributions deeply, though she underestimates the dangers she sent them into","best":"Watching the completed Wasteland Survival Guide roll off the press for the first time","worst":"Realizing her research assignments exposed someone she cares about to genuine mortal peril"},"Megaton":{"aff":70,"type":"platonic","relation":"home settlement","note":"Deeply attached to the community that gave her safety and a livelihood, she considers its residents her extended family"},"Canterbury Commons":{"aff":30,"type":"neutral","relation":"childhood home","note":"She retains fond but distant memories of the trading community where her curiosity first took root"}}', 'Owner and operator of Craterside Supply; author, publisher, and distributor of the Wasteland Survival Guide series', '* Merchant trade
* Equipment repair
* Self-taught engineering and invention
* Extensive book-knowledge of pre-War and post-War subjects
* Printing and publishing logistics', 'Bubbly and conversational, peppered with enthusiastic questions and tangential observations; shifts rapidly between topics with genuine excitement; rarely registers when a subject is grim or dangerous', '* Expand the Wasteland Survival Guide into a comprehensive multi-volume series reaching every settled region
* Improve wastelanders'' quality of life through shared practical knowledge
* Complete her biography of the Lone Wanderer', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mona', '', 'A Pitt raider slaver whose irradiated river exposure left her with a degenerative skin condition', 'Mona is a slaver operating under the Pitt raiders in Uptown, enforcing the raider hierarchy''s grip on the slave workforce that keeps the steel mill running. She is a capable melee fighter who holds her own in the brutal social order of the Pitt. Swimming in the irradiated rivers near the settlement left her with a particularly degenerative skin condition that visibly marks her as another casualty of the Trog-ravaged city''s environmental hazards. When asked about her affliction, she offers a bitter invitation to swim in the local river and experience it firsthand. Despite her deteriorating condition, she remains a committed participant in the raider power structure, surviving where others have succumbed to the Pitt''s toxic landscape.', 'Human female of Hispanic descent with visibly degenerative, mottled skin and a deteriorated complexion caused by irradiated river exposure.', 'Bitter and blunt about her affliction, hardened by the Pitt''s brutality, loyal to the raider hierarchy that sustains her', '{"Pitt raiders":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"raider gang member","note":"Loyal participant in the raider hierarchy that controls the Pitt''s slave operation"}}', 'Slaver for the Pitt raiders', '* Skilled melee combatant
* Survival in irradiated environments', 'Blunt and sardonic, offers bitter commentary when pressed about her condition', '* Maintaining her standing among the Pitt raiders despite her deteriorating health', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mother_curie_iii', '', 'Visionary cult leader who split from the Children of Atom to preach salvation through irradiation and ghoulification, utterly convinced she is saving the wasteland', 'Mother Curie III is the founder and leader of the Apostles of the Eternal Light, a splinter sect of the Children of Atom headquartered in their Springvale monastery. Born in Megaton, she spent her youth sensing a special destiny she could not name until a vivid dream during one of Confessor Cromwell''s sermons revealed a glowing Prophet of Atom calling her to spread a new gospel. Where Cromwell preaches Division, Curie teaches Enlightenment-salvation through radiation-induced ghoulification, with the ultimate goal of achieving Eternal Light, a visible radioactive glow signifying supreme communion with Atom. She persuaded several of Cromwell''s followers, including Brother Gerard, to abandon Megaton''s bomb worship and join her new order. When Brotherhood of Steel paladins delivered Aqua Pura to the monastery, Curie interpreted the armored soldiers as angels of Atom and the water as a divine vessel meant to be irradiated and distributed as holy sacrament. She now oversees the irradiation process with fervent devotion, genuinely believing she brings salvation and warmth to the wasteland''s suffering while remaining utterly blind to the sickness and death her blessed water causes.', 'Elderly Hispanic woman with a luminous pallor and early ghoulification traits including patchy hair loss, radiation-scarred weathered skin, and sunken facial features, her eyes bearing an intense gaze.', 'Zealous, single-minded, and sincerely benevolent in her own mind-so consumed by her divine mission that she cannot conceive of the harm she causes, interpreting all events as confirmation of Atom''s will and dismissing contrary evidence as misunderstanding', '{"Confessor Cromwell":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"former spiritual mentor","note":"She rejects his focus on Division as misguided while still drawing from his theological framework"},"Brother Gerard":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"loyal disciple and gatekeeper","note":"She convinced him to leave Cromwell''s flock and trusts him to guard the monastery and distribute holy water"},"Sun of Atom":{"aff":65,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Her child within the Apostles, raised under the light of Atom''s Glow"},"Church of the Children of Atom":{"aff":-20,"type":"suspicious","relation":"former affiliation","note":"She views the parent faith as stuck in error, clinging to Division rather than seeking true Enlightenment"},"Apostles of the Eternal Light":{"aff":90,"type":"fanatical","relation":"founded order","note":"Her spiritual family and the vessel of Atom''s true message, worth every sacrifice to protect and grow"},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":40,"type":"curious","relation":"perceived divine messengers","note":"She interprets the paladins who delivered Aqua Pura as armored angels of Atom, unaware of their true purpose or the danger she poses to their mission"}}', 'Cult leader and spiritual overseer of the holy water irradiation project at the Holy Light Monastery', '* Religious oratory and persuasion
* Radiation handling and containment
* Cult organization
* Inspirational leadership
* Ritual ceremony', 'Preachy and visionary, speaking in religious metaphor and divine proclamation, prone to interpreting mundane events as sacred signs from Atom, warmly evangelistic toward potential converts', '* Spread Atom''s Enlightenment to all suffering people through irradiated holy water
* Achieve Eternal Light herself
* Fulfill what she believes is her prophetic destiny
* Bring rebirth to the wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mother_maya', '', 'Devoted Mother of the Children of Atom in Megaton, quietly married to Confessor Cromwell and united with him in spreading the faith', 'Mother Maya serves as a religious leader of the Church of the Children of Atom in Megaton, where she tends to the congregation and advances the church''s spiritual mission alongside Confessor Cromwell. She and Cromwell are husband and wife, though they keep their marriage concealed from the community, preferring that worshippers see them only as fellow servants of Atom''s glow. Maya is known for her kindness and gentle demeanor, qualities that set her apart from the harshness common in the wasteland. Her faith extends into a deep reverence for ghouls, whom the Children of Atom regard as touched by radiation and thus spiritually significant. Though she is forty-one, wasteland hardship has aged her beyond her years. She can often be found near the church''s bomb crater, tending to the faithful or offering quiet counsel to those who seek it.', 'A weathered African-American woman appearing older than her forty-one years, with a deeply lined face and posture worn by wasteland hardship.', 'Kind, gentle, and spiritually devoted; treats others with warmth and extends particular reverence to ghouls as beings touched by Atom''s glow', '{"Confessor Cromwell":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"secret husband","note":"Maya and Cromwell conceal their marriage to present themselves solely as fellow servants of Atom rather than as a couple","best":"Standing together before the bomb crater, sharing a quiet moment of unity in their faith after the faithful have departed","worst":"The constant strain of hiding their bond from a congregation that looks to them both for spiritual guidance"},"Church of the Children of Atom":{"aff":80,"type":"fanatical","relation":"devoted member and leader","note":"Maya''s identity and purpose are deeply entwined with the church''s mission and theology"},"Gob":{"aff":55,"type":"admirer","relation":"revered ghoul","note":"Maya treats Gob with respect and spiritual reverence, as the church regards ghouls as beings blessed by radiation"}}', 'Religious leader and Mother of the Children of Atom congregation in Megaton', '* Spiritual counsel
* Religious instruction
* Community care
* Preaching the teachings of Atom', 'Speaks softly and with serene conviction; uses gentle, faith-inflected language befitting a church mother', '* Spread the ideals and teachings of the Children of Atom
* Nurture the Megaton congregation
* Honor Atom''s divine glow alongside Cromwell', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mr_brotch__cg03mrbrotch', '', 'Vault 101''s hereditary schoolteacher and G.O.A.T. administrator, burdened by a family legacy he may be the last to carry', 'Edwin Brotch is the schoolteacher of Vault 101, a position held by his family unbroken since the day the vault sealed its doors. His father and grandfather both stood at the same classroom lectern before him, and the weight of that unbroken chain sits heavy on his shoulders. With no children of his own, Edwin fears he will be the last Brotch to guide the vault''s youth through their lessons and their G.O.A.T. examinations. Despite his anxieties about legacy, he performs his duties with quiet dedication, administering the test that determines every young resident''s future trade. He has secretly modified a utility jumpsuit to improve his chances of survival in the wastes, a private precaution that reveals a man who, despite his deep roots underground, has contemplated the world outside. When the vault descended into factional violence, Edwin''s sympathies with the dissenters landed him in a jail cell, from which he eventually joined the rebel holdouts in the clinic.', 'A middle-aged African American human male with tired posture and ink-stained fingers.', 'Dutiful and mild-mannered with an undercurrent of quiet anxiety about his family line ending. Pragmatic enough to prepare for unlikely scenarios despite his sheltered life. Sympathetic to those who question vault authority, suggesting a man whose teaching has taught him to value honest inquiry over obedience.', '{"Vault 101":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"lifelong home and duty","note":"Deeply loyal to the vault community but troubled by its authoritarian turn under Overseer Almodovar"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":40,"type":"mentor","relation":"former student","note":"Taught the Lone Wanderer alongside the other vault children and administered their G.O.A.T.","best":"Watching a bright young student engage thoughtfully with a lesson"}}', 'Schoolteacher and G.O.A.T. examination administrator', '* Educating vault youth
* Administering and evaluating aptitude tests
* Basic survival preparation
* Practical clothing modification', 'Patient and instructive, with the measured cadence of a man accustomed to explaining things slowly. Occasionally trails off when discussing personal matters or the future.', '* Preserve the Brotch teaching tradition despite having no heir
* Ensure his students are prepared for whatever path the G.O.A.T. assigns them
* Survive the vault''s internal conflicts with conscience intact', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('mr_brotch__mrbrotch', '', 'Vault 101''s third-generation schoolteacher and G.O.A.T. administrator, burdened by a dying family legacy and quiet fears about the vault''s future', 'Edwin Brotch is Vault 101''s schoolteacher, carrying on a family tradition that stretches back to the day the vault doors first sealed shut. His father and grandfather both held the position before him, and the Brotch name has been synonymous with vault education for over two centuries. Edwin takes quiet pride in that lineage, but the absence of children of his own gnaws at him-he may well be the last Brotch to stand at the front of a classroom. He is the official administrator of the G.O.A.T., guiding every young resident through the exam that will shape their adult role in the vault. Though a lifelong vault dweller, Edwin has secretly modified a utility jumpsuit to improve his chances should he ever be forced to survive outside, a precaution that speaks to anxieties he rarely voices aloud. His sympathies lie with those who question the vault''s rigid order, a stance that has landed him in trouble with vault security more than once.', 'A middle-aged African American man with a pallid complexion typical of lifelong vault dwellers.', 'Dutiful and earnest with a teacher''s instinct for patience, but privately anxious about legacy and mortality; harbors quiet doubts about vault authority and sympathizes with those who challenge it', '{"Vault 101":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"lifelong home and duty","note":"Deeply loyal to the vault community but increasingly sympathetic to those who question its isolationist policies","best":"Watching another class of students find their place through the G.O.A.T.","worst":"Sitting in a jail cell, wondering if the vault''s closed doors were ever meant to protect anyone"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":35,"type":"professional","relation":"former student","note":"Administered the G.O.A.T. to the Lone Wanderer and remembers them as one of many children who passed through his classroom","best":"A student who took the G.O.A.T. seriously and seemed genuinely curious about their future","worst":"The disruption and chaos that followed the Lone Wanderer''s departure from the vault"}}', 'Vault 101 schoolteacher and G.O.A.T. exam administrator', '* Education and instruction
* Test administration
* Basic survival preparation
* Jumpsuit modification
* Repair', 'Measured and instructive, with the formal cadence of a lifelong educator; occasionally reveals dry worry beneath the professional demeanor', '* Preserve the Brotch teaching tradition
* Prepare the vault''s youth for meaningful roles
* Ensure he is not caught helpless if the outside world ever forces its way in', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('muffy', '', 'Deceased pet dog of the McClellan family in Georgetown North', 'Muffy was the cherished dog of the McClellan family, living with them in their Georgetown North townhome before the war reshaped the Capital Wasteland. A loyal and familiar presence around the household, she spent her days in the home and backyard, a small comfort to the family amid the ruins of old Washington. Her life ended in the backyard she knew so well, her remains still resting near the townhome as a quiet reminder of the domestic world that once existed there. The McClellans'' attachment to their pet speaks to the small acts of normalcy families clung to in desperate times.', 'A small dog; her deceased remains are in a decayed corpse condition.', 'Loyal, affectionate, and devoted household companion', '{"McClellan family":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"beloved pet","note":"Muffy was the family dog of the McClellan household, cared for and kept at their Georgetown North townhome."}}', 'Family pet', '* Companionship
* Watchdog alertness
* Household familiarity', 'Canine barks, whines, and body language', '* Had been to remain with and comfort the McClellan family', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('murphy', '', 'A ghoul chemist running an underground Ultrajet lab out of Northwest Seneca Station', 'Murphy is a ghoul scientist who has carved out a small but functional laboratory inside the ruins of Northwest Seneca Station, where he devotes himself to synthesizing Ultrajet-a more potent chem variant designed to affect ghouls, for whom standard Jet offers only limited effect. Working alongside his assistant Barrett, Murphy has secured reliable supplies of two key ingredients but remains critically short on Sugar Bombs, the third component essential to his formula. Though deeply suspicious of outsiders and fearful that someone might steal his recipe, Murphy is pragmatic enough to hire scavengers willing to bring him the cereal he desperately needs. His operation represents one of the few independent chem production efforts in the Capital Wasteland, and he readily sells his product to anyone who can pay.', 'A male ghoul with radiation-scarred facial features, sharp eyes, and a hunched posture.', 'Paranoid and territorial about his work, yet commercially minded when opportunity presents itself; driven by scientific ambition and a desire to create something that serves ghoul physiology specifically.', '{"Barrett":{"aff":55,"type":"professional","relation":"assistant and bodyguard","note":"Barrett serves as Murphy''s protection and extra pair of hands, a partnership built on mutual need and trust earned over time.","best":"Barrett standing between Murphy and a raider, rifle raised without hesitation."}}', 'Chemist and Ultrajet manufacturer', '* Chemistry and chem synthesis
* Merchant trade
* Laboratory operations
* Resource negotiation', 'Cautious and initially suspicious, shifting to eager and transactional when business is discussed; speaks with the focused intensity of a scientist protective of his research.', '* Acquire a steady supply of Sugar Bombs to sustain Ultrajet production
* Protect his formula from thieves and competitors
* Establish a profitable chem operation in the station', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('nadine', '', 'A restless young adventurer who fled the Capital Wasteland for Point Lookout, survived Tobar''s scalpel, and claimed the Duchess Gambit as her own ship', 'Nadine is the daughter of Catherine, raised in the Capital Wasteland but never content with a settled life. A tomboy with an insatiable thirst for adventure, she ran away from home and stowed away aboard the Duchess Gambit under Captain Tobar''s nose, chasing the promise of the wider world. Her wanderings led her to Point Lookout and into Jackson''s tribal community at the Ark & Dove Cathedral, where she underwent the Mother Punga ritual and suffered the same violation as many travelers-Tobar drugged her and surgically removed a lump of her brain. Despite this scarring ordeal, Nadine''s spirit remained unbroken, and she clung to her goal of finding fortune to bring back to her mother. She eventually exacted revenge on Tobar, seized the Duchess Gambit for herself, and now captains the vessel offering free passage between Point Lookout and the Capital Wasteland.', 'Young Hispanic woman with tomboyish posture and a visible surgical scar across her scalp from cranial excavation.', 'Bold, restless, and fiercely independent with an adventurous streak. Resilient despite trauma, stubbornly optimistic about her prospects, and deeply loyal to those she cares about. Holds hard grudges against anyone who wrongs her or hers.', '{"Catherine":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Nadine ran away but never stopped loving her; everything she does is ultimately about returning with something to show for it","best":"Catherine packing extra supplies into her bag even when she disapproved of the wandering","worst":"The look on her mother''s face the last morning before she slipped away"},"Tobar":{"aff":-90,"type":"nemesis","relation":"mutilator and former captain","note":"He drugged her and cut into her skull; she repaid him by taking his ship and his life","worst":"Waking up with her head split open and a piece of herself missing"},"Jackson":{"aff":40,"type":"platonic","relation":"tribal leader","note":"She joined his community at the Ark & Dove Cathedral and found a measure of belonging among the tribals"},"Tribals":{"aff":50,"type":"platonic","relation":"adopted community","note":"They accepted her when she had nowhere else to go at Point Lookout"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"fellow survivor of Tobar''s surgery","note":"Shares a bond of mutual violation and recovery; she removes their scar and offers them free passage as a gesture of solidarity","best":"Standing together against Tobar and reclaiming what was taken"}}', 'Captain of the Duchess Gambit; former tribal of the Ark & Dove Cathedral', '* Seafaring and ship navigation
* Wasteland survival
* Tribal ritual knowledge
* Basic combat proficiency
* Resourceful improvisation', 'Direct and casual with a youthful edge, speaks her mind without pretense, peppers conversation with determined optimism and occasional sharp humor', '* Bring back fortune and security to her mother Catherine in the Capital Wasteland
* Maintain her hard-won freedom and command of the Duchess Gambit
* Prove that her risky choices were worth something', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('nathan_vargas', '', 'A retired caravaner turned Enclave zealot, Nathan Vargas preaches the coming salvation of the wasteland to anyone in Megaton who will listen.', 'Nathaniel Vargas spent over thirty years running caravan routes across the Capital Wasteland alongside his wife Manya, earning a living and a reputation as a crack shot. Somewhere along those long miles he caught the signal of Enclave Radio and found a purpose that outlasted his trading days. Now retired in Megaton, Nathan has become the settlement''s most vocal Enclave evangelist, cornering neighbors and travelers alike to proclaim that salvation is broadcasting on every frequency. Most residents tolerate him as a harmless eccentric, though none dispute that decades behind a wagon''s guard position kept his aim sharp. He shares his home with Manya and their adoptive daughter Maggie, and maintains a standing tab at Moriarty''s Saloon that he shows no urgency to settle. His faith in the Enclave is absolute and unshakeable, rooted in a deep conviction that the United States endures and every wastelander remains its citizen by birthright.', 'A weathered sixty-five-year-old Hispanic man with sun-roughened skin and steady posture.', 'Zealous and earnest in his convictions, Nathan is the sort who corners strangers to share his beliefs whether they asked or not. Beneath the fanaticism lies genuine warmth and a patriotic idealism that yearns for order restored to a broken world.', '{"Manya Vargas":{"aff":90,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife","note":"Partners for over thirty years on caravan routes and in marriage; their bond runs deeper than his political obsessions","best":"Running the caravan routes together, side by side under open sky","worst":"Watching her patience wear thin every time he launches into another Enclave speech at home"},"Maggie":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"adoptive daughter","note":"The child they took in together, a small bright spot in their household"},"Enclave Radio":{"aff":100,"type":"fanatical","relation":"devoted listener and believer","note":"Accepts every broadcast as gospel truth and repeats its promises to anyone who will listen","best":"The first time he tuned in and heard a voice proclaiming that America would rise again"},"Colin Moriarty":{"aff":30,"type":"transactional","relation":"saloon keeper","note":"Carries an eight-cap tab at Moriarty''s Saloon with no apparent intention of settling it soon"}}', 'Retired caravan merchant and self-appointed Enclave evangelist', '* Expert marksman
* Caravan route navigation
* Bartering
* Wasteland survival from decades on the road', 'Preachy and earnest, prone to patriotic declarations and Enclave Radio catchphrases, speaks with the unshakeable conviction of a true believer looking for converts', '* Spread the word about the Enclave''s coming salvation
* See the United States restored to greatness
* Convince every soul in Megaton that deliverance is at hand', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('nola', '', 'A Pitt slave who serves as an improvised medic for her fellow workers despite limited skill and brutal conditions', 'Nola is a Pitt slave laboring in Downtown who has taken on the role of improvised medic for her fellow captives. She possesses only rudimentary medical training, making her one of the least skilled healers in the wasteland, but her willingness to help keeps her tending to the sick, crippled, and wounded slaves working throughout Downtown and The Mill. She spends her shifts in the grinding hole slicing at old cars while dodging shots from the slave masters. Despite her poor conditions and limited expertise, she generously offers free healing to anyone injured, though her treatments sometimes cause more harm than good. Nola believes deeply that every slave needs to stay as healthy as possible to survive the Pitt''s brutality.', 'A weary, haggard African American woman with calloused hands, soot-stained complexion, and small cuts across her face and arms.', 'Generous and compassionate despite her circumstances, driven by a sincere desire to help others even when her skills fall short. Stubbornly hopeful about keeping her fellow slaves alive, though painfully aware of her own limitations.', '{"Pitt slaves":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"improvised caretaker","note":"Nola serves as their reluctant doctor, driven by compassion and the belief that every healthy slave improves their shared chances of survival.","best":"A fellow slave recovering enough to return to work after her care","worst":"Accidentally worsening an injury she was trying to treat"},"Pitt slave masters":{"aff":-70,"type":"fearful","relation":"tormentors","note":"She dodges their shots in the grinding hole and lives under their constant cruelty.","worst":"Watching a slave master gun down a slave she had just finished patching up"}}', 'Slave laborer and improvised medic for Pitt slaves', '* Rudimentary medical knowledge
* Basic wound care
* Physical endurance from forced labor', 'Direct and earnest, speaks with quiet concern, uses simple practical language befitting her limited education', '* Keep as many Pitt slaves healthy as possible
* Survive the grinding hole
* Maintain hope amid brutal conditions', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('northern_shack_raider', '', 'A raider boss holding territory at Evergreen Mills'' northern shack', 'The northern shack raider is a raider boss who claims the northern shack at Evergreen Mills as his personal domain. He shares the cramped shelter with a female raider companion, and the two have settled into a domestic routine amid the squalor, sleeping in the same bed each night and wandering the shack''s perimeter by day. Unlike the generic rabble infesting the mill complex, he cuts a distinctive figure among the raiders, recognizable by his unique appearance and the authority he commands. He is violently territorial and attacks any outsider on sight, treating intruders as threats to be eliminated rather than opportunities for parley. His control over the northern shack marks him as a figure of some standing within Evergreen Mills'' chaotic hierarchy.', 'Caucasian human male; described as having a distinctive physical appearance unlike other raiders, though specific distinguishing facial or body features are not recorded.', 'Aggressively territorial, immediately hostile to outsiders, possessive of his home and companion, routine-oriented despite the chaotic raider lifestyle', '{"Female raider":{"aff":65,"type":"romantic","relation":"shack-mate","note":"Shares the northern shack and the same bed with her every night","best":"Falling asleep beside her after a successful raid"},"Raiders":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"faction member","note":"Holds boss status within the Evergreen Mills raider community"}}', 'Raider boss controlling the northern shack at Evergreen Mills', '* Combat
* Territorial enforcement
* Scavenging
* Survival in raider territory', 'Brutish and threatening; likely speaks in crude, violent threats with little patience for conversation', '* Maintaining control over the northern shack
* Protecting his territory and companion
* Eliminating intruders', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('northern_shack_raider+s_partner', '', 'A raider boss holding down the northern shack at Evergreen Mills alongside her partner', 'A hardened raider boss who has claimed the northern shack at Evergreen Mills as her permanent stomping ground. She never ventures outside, instead pacing the cramped interior from dawn to dusk in restless patrol of her small domain. Her world is defined by the shack''s walls and the company of the other raider who shares her space and her bed each night. The pair form a tight-knit unit amid the chaos of the Evergreen Mills raider encampment, loyal to each other above all else. Like any true raider, she meets strangers with immediate violence, trusting nothing that walks through her door uninvited.', 'Weathered Caucasian woman with a lean, wiry build, deeply lined skin, and the haggard features of chronic wasteland exposure.', 'Territorial, aggressive, and intensely bonded to her partner; restless and vigilant when awake, never straying from her claimed space', '{"Northern shack raider":{"aff":75,"type":"romantic","relation":"partner","note":"The two share the northern shack and sleep in the same bed every night, forming a close bond amid the raider encampment","best":"Falling asleep together in their shared bed after a successful raid"},"Raiders":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"gang affiliation","note":"Loose loyalty to the broader Evergreen Mills raider community, though her true allegiance is to her partner alone"}}', 'Raider boss', '* Combat
* Territorial defense
* Intimidation
* Survival in raider territory', 'Coarse and threatening raider vernacular, quick to violence before words', '* Maintaining control of the northern shack
* Protecting her partner
* Keeping outsiders away from her territory', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('northup', '', 'A Brotherhood of Steel paladin leading a besieged recovery team in Chesterbrook, holding out against relentless super mutant attacks', 'Paladin Northup is a Brotherhood of Steel soldier serving out of the Citadel in the Capital Wasteland. He leads a squad dispatched to Chesterbrook to recover a storage box of mini nukes, following intelligence uncovered by a Brotherhood scribe. Northup''s team located both the box and its key, but a super mutant ambush pinned them down before they could extract the cargo. Stripped of radio contact and unable to call for reinforcements, the squad has endured days of continuous mutant assaults without sleep. Several of Northup''s subordinates have lost hope of survival, but the paladin refuses to yield, holding the line against overwhelming odds. He is desperate enough to accept help from any capable outsider, though he can offer nothing in return but sincere gratitude.', 'A haggard human male with a pale, exhausted complexion, deep shadows under his eyes, and a slumped posture.', 'Resolute and duty-bound even under deteriorating conditions; protective of his squad to the point of self-sacrifice; pragmatic enough to accept aid from strangers but prioritizes warning them away from danger; grows sharp and frustrated when his warnings go unheeded', '{"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":85,"type":"protective","relation":"faction","note":"Loyal paladin serving a recovery mission on the Citadel''s behalf, cut off and unable to report back","best":"The pride of being entrusted with a mission vital to the Brotherhood''s arsenal","worst":"Days of silence with no way to reach the Citadel for reinforcements"},"Chesterbrook Squad":{"aff":75,"type":"protective","relation":"subordinates","note":"His exhausted team, some losing hope, all relying on him to hold them together","best":"Finding the mini nuke box and its key together before the ambush","worst":"Watching his soldiers despair as mutant waves keep coming without end"},"Super Mutants":{"aff":-90,"type":"enemy","relation":"besieging force","note":"Relentless attackers striking every few hours, preventing sleep or escape","worst":"Days of unending assault that have worn his squad to the breaking point"}}', 'Brotherhood of Steel paladin and squad leader', '* Combat leadership under siege conditions
* Power armor operation
* Tactical defense
* Small-unit command
* Munitions recovery', 'Urgent and clipped from exhaustion; warns newcomers to flee the area immediately; repeats warnings with rising frustration and volume if ignored; speaks with weary gratitude when offered help, honest about having nothing to give', '* Survive the super mutant siege
* Extract the mini nuke cache and return it to the Citadel
* Keep his remaining squad members alive', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('nova', '', 'A weary sex worker at Moriarty''s Saloon, trapped by her employer''s greed and dreaming of the day she can walk away from it all.', 'Nova has lived in Megaton since 2272, working as the self-described whore at Moriarty''s Saloon. She spends most of her time on the first floor chatting with Gob, Jericho, and whoever else drifts through, occasionally retreating upstairs with a client. Her standards are low but firm: she refuses to service ghouls. Between sessions she sweet-talks male patrons into spending caps on drinks, company, or a bed for the night. Colin Moriarty controls her completely, confiscating her earnings and locking them away for himself, while she numbs the grind with a Jet habit that only earns his displeasure. She has learned to survive by keeping her nose out of other people''s business and never crossing Moriarty publicly. Given the chance, she would retire from sex work entirely.', 'A twenty-five-year-old Caucasian human woman with a weary complexion, tired eyes, and a slumped posture that gives her a prematurely worn appearance.', 'World-weary and pragmatic, keeping her head down to survive. Outwardly sociable and flirtatious when working, but privately unenthusiastic and chem-dependent. Knows better than to rock the boat or challenge authority.', '{"Colin Moriarty":{"aff":-60,"type":"professional","relation":"employer and pimp","note":"He confiscates her earnings and locks them away, keeping her financially trapped and personally miserable.","worst":"He takes every cap she earns and locks them up for himself while she scrapes by on nothing."},"Gob":{"aff":30,"type":"platonic","relation":"barroom companion","note":"She chats with him regularly at the bar despite refusing to service ghouls professionally."},"Jericho":{"aff":15,"type":"platonic","relation":"barroom acquaintance","note":"One of the regulars she passes time with at the saloon."}}', 'Sex worker and barroom hustler at Moriarty''s Saloon', '* Sweet-talking patrons
* Separating customers from their caps
* Reading men
* Surviving under exploitative conditions
* Navigating Megaton''s social currents', 'Casual and flirtatious on the job, with a practiced sweetness that shifts to blunt resignation in private conversation', '* Survive Moriarty''s control
* Maintain her Jet supply
* Someday retire from sex work entirely if she ever gets the chance', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('novice', '', 'A devout ghoul novice of the Apostles of the Eternal Light, whose extreme ghoulification is revered as a sign of divine favor', 'Novice is a ghoul member of the Apostles of the Eternal Light, dwelling in the basement sanctuary of the Holy Light Monastery. He attends Mother Curie III''s sermons with unwavering devotion, earning her public commendation for his dedication to the cult''s cause. Among the monastery''s visitors, he has become something of a living testament to the faith-his advanced ghoulification, with a hint of brain visible through his exposed skull, is regarded not as horror but as a mark of divine favor and proximity to enlightenment. Fellow Apostles and pilgrims regard him with awe, seeing in his deteriorated form proof that the Eternal Light embraces all who surrender to it. By the cult''s reckoning, his path to the light is nearly assured.', 'Ghoul male with advanced ghoulification featuring an exposed section of skull through which brain tissue is visible.', 'Devout, humble, and quietly proud of his ghoulification as evidence of divine favor; reverent toward Mother Curie III and the cult''s teachings; accepting of his condition as a blessing.', '{"Mother Curie III":{"aff":80,"type":"fanatical","relation":"spiritual leader","note":"She commends his devotion publicly and sees his advanced ghoulification as proof that his path to the light is certain.","best":"Being praised by Mother Curie III during a sermon as an example of the faith''s promise"},"Apostles of the Eternal Light":{"aff":85,"type":"fanatical","relation":"fellow believers","note":"He is regarded as a living sign of the cult''s truth, and visitors marvel at his condition as proof of divine favor.","best":"Fellow Apostles looking upon his exposed skull with awe rather than pity"}}', 'Cult member of the Apostles of the Eternal Light', '* Devotional practice
* Enduring advanced ghoulification
* Inspiring fellow believers through his physical state as a living sign of the faith', 'Reverent and quiet, speaking in the spiritual idiom of the Apostles with serene acceptance of his condition', '* To complete his path to the Eternal Light
* Serve Mother Curie III''s vision
* Embody the cult''s teachings through his ghoulified form', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('nurse_graves', '', 'A young ghoul nurse serving as Doctor Barrows'' keen-eyed assistant in Underworld''s Chop Shop', 'Nurse Graves is a ghoul still young by her kind''s standards, working as the primary assistant to Doctor Barrows in the Chop Shop within Underworld. She assists in his ongoing experiments to diagnose and treat the strange new ailments that ghouls perpetually complain about, and she approaches the work with genuine enthusiasm. Her daily routine involves dissecting corpses, examining brain tissue samples, and prodding feral ghouls with an assortment of sharp instruments. Unlike most of Underworld''s residents, Graves extends her sympathy equally to humans and ghouls alike, firmly believing that both races were once the same. She is aware of Doctor Barrows'' controversial experiments on the unconscious Ranger Reilly, conducted in the hope that studying human physiology might reveal a way to halt or even reverse the ghoul transformation. Content with her place in the world, she shows no bitterness about her condition or her macabre occupation.', 'A relatively young female ghoul with the characteristic rotting features of her kind, though her upright bearing suggests she has not yet spent centuries in that form.', 'Knowledgeable, eager, and surprisingly cheerful for someone surrounded by death and decay. She holds an uncommon egalitarian view between humans and ghouls, and seems genuinely satisfied with her grim work.', '{"Doctor Barrows":{"aff":75,"type":"professional","relation":"employer and mentor","note":"She works closely with him and supports his research goals without apparent qualm about his methods","best":"Learning something new from one of his dissections that could help ghoulkind","worst":"Watching him dismiss a promising line of inquiry out of frustration"},"Reilly":{"aff":30,"type":"suspicious","relation":"unwitting experimental subject","note":"Graves knows Barrows experimented on Reilly during her coma but does not seem troubled enough to intervene","best":"Finding that Reilly''s human biology yielded useful data for the research","worst":"Considering what Reilly might think if she ever learned what happened while she slept"},"Underworld Ghouls":{"aff":60,"type":"platonic","relation":"community and patients","note":"She treats their endless complaints with professional patience even when the ailments prove trivial"},"Humans":{"aff":55,"type":"curious","relation":"sympathetic outsiders","note":"She views humans as former equals and holds no grudge against them, an unusual stance in Underworld","best":"Remembering that ghouls and humans share a common origin","worst":"Seeing a human recoil from her in disgust"}}', 'Nurse and research assistant at the Chop Shop in Underworld', '* Medical diagnosis
* Dissection and autopsy procedures
* Tissue sample analysis
* Handling of feral ghouls
* General nursing care', 'Professional yet warm, with an upbeat tone that contrasts sharply with her surroundings. Speaks about cadavers and experiments with casual comfort.', '* Advance Doctor Barrows'' research into curing or reversing the ghoul transformation
* Provide care for Underworld''s ailing residents
* Maintain her optimistic outlook despite the bleakness of post-war existence', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('o-dog', '', 'A cannibalistic Pitt raider sniper who sees all people as graded cuts of meat waiting to be consumed', 'O-Dog is a Pitt raider stationed in Uptown around Haven''s courtyard, where he serves as a precision shooter. He holds a deeply unsettling worldview in which every person is simply a different grade of meat, destined eventually to be eaten, and the only meaningful goal is to stay near the top of the food chain. He practices his marksmanship by shooting beer bottles on nearby buildings with his.32 hunting rifle, honing the skill that gives him value among the raiders. O-Dog carries strange meat and speaks of others as sausage and cuts, strongly implying he partakes in cannibalism. He is infatuated with the raider Vikia and constantly competes with Duke for her favor, though she rarely gives him any notice. His philosophy leaves little room for sentiment; success just means you have moved up to a higher grade of sausage before the inevitable.', 'A lean human male of Asian descent; no distinctive facial features, scars, or tattoos are recorded.', 'Fatalistic, predatory, and darkly philosophical; views all life as a temporary arrangement of meat on the menu. Competitive and vain when it comes to Vikia''s attention, but otherwise emotionally flat toward others. Speaks of people as food with casual, unsettling sincerity.', '{"Vikia":{"aff":55,"type":"crush","relation":"romantic rival for her attention","note":"O-Dog is infatuated with her marksmanship and presence but rarely gets any recognition in return.","best":"She once glanced his way after a particularly good bottle shot.","worst":"Duke made him look foolish in front of her again."},"Duke":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"romantic competitor","note":"Both men compete for Vikia''s attention, and O-Dog resents Duke''s greater success.","best":"Duke missed an easy shot once; O-Dog didn''t.","worst":"Vikia laughed at something Duke said while ignoring O-Dog entirely."},"Pitt raiders":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"faction member","note":"O-Dog belongs to the Pitt raiders and fulfills his sniper duties, though his cannibalistic philosophy sets him apart even among them."}}', 'Pitt raider sniper and courtyard patrol', '* Precision rifle marksmanship
* Survival in The Pitt''s irradiated conditions
* Scavenging and butchering', 'Crude and metaphorical, constantly framing people as cuts of meat or sausage grades; laconic but disturbingly vivid when he does speak', '* Stay at the top of the food chain
* Win Vikia''s attention over Duke
* Keep shooting and eating before someone eats him', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('obadiah_blackhall', '', 'Last scion of the Blackhall dynasty, a disabled recluse obsessed with recovering his family''s occult tome and claiming its dark power', 'Obadiah Blackhall is the final living descendant of the Blackhalls, a once-powerful family whose wealth and influence shaped Point Lookout''s history for generations. Confined to a wheelchair and reliant on oxygen canisters, he resides alone in the decaying Blackhall Manor, guarding what remains of his family''s legacy. The Blackhalls were among Point Lookout''s earliest settlers, with his great-great-great grandmother Constance assuming leadership of the estate after the New Plague claimed her husband in 2058. Obadiah is consumed by the loss of the Krivbeknih, an ancient family tome stolen by swampfolk decades ago, and hungers for the dark power he believes is his birthright. He views the other inhabitants of Point Lookout with contempt, considering them uncivilized and unintelligent. Despite his curmudgeonly nature, Obadiah maintains a veneer of old-world politeness when receiving visitors to his manor.', 'An elderly Caucasian male with deeply weathered skin and a visible physical disability that prevents him from walking unassisted.', 'Stubborn, curmudgeonly, and deeply possessive of family heritage. Polite to newcomers but swiftly dismissive of those he deems beneath him. Harbors a quiet hunger for occult power and resents the swampfolk who stole what he considers rightfully his.', '{"Constance Blackhall":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"great-great-great grandmother","note":"Reveres her as the matriarch who held the family together after the New Plague and shaped the Blackhall dynasty''s prominence in Point Lookout."},"Richard Dunwich":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"great-great-great granduncle","note":"Acknowledges the connection to the Dunwich name, another thread in the family''s tangled and occult-laden history."},"Ug-Qualtoth":{"aff":60,"type":"fanatical","relation":"dark patron","note":"Drawn to the entity''s power through the Krivbeknih and the Blackhall family''s long occult entanglement."},"Swampfolk":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"thieves and desecrators","note":"Despises them as uncivilized wretches who stole the Krivbeknih and defiled Blackhall heritage."}}', 'Owner and sole resident of Blackhall Manor, keeper of the Blackhall legacy', '* Extensive knowledge of Point Lookout history and Blackhall family lore
* Understanding of occult texts and the Krivbeknih''s significance
* Basic estate management', 'Formal and courteous with an archaic Southern gentility, but capable of sharp contempt for those he considers uncivilized. Speaks with the measured cadence of old money in slow decline.', '* Recover the Krivbeknih from the swampfolk
* Harness its dark power exclusively for himself
* Preserve what remains of the Blackhall family legacy within Blackhall Manor', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_armstrong', '', 'A conflicted Vault 101 security officer torn between duty, friendship, and conscience as the vault tears itself apart', 'Officer Armstrong serves as a rank-and-file security guard in Vault 101, one of the officers tasked with maintaining order as the vault fractures around him. The departure of James and the chaos that followed claimed far too many lives, and Armstrong has spent every shift since trying to hold a fragile peace together. He resents James for unleashing the crisis but still considers him a good friend, and the news of his death hits hard. Armstrong remains unaware that Overseer Almodovar''s heavy-handed actions worsened the conflict far beyond what James''s departure alone would have caused. He knows a revolution is brewing, with dwellers questioning whether the vault door should stay sealed at all. Armstrong takes no side in the growing schism and disagrees with the overseer''s harsher mandates, though he finds the man intimidating enough to avoid open defiance. He has known the Lone Wanderer since birth and counts himself among the dwellers who genuinely like them, choosing not to arrest them when they return. He would rather see the overseer and Amata reconcile than watch the vault continue to tear itself apart, and he is not convinced that resealing the door and ignoring the conflict is any kind of solution.', 'African American human male with an unremarkable build and no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Even-tempered but deeply conflicted, loyal to people rather than authority, reluctant to take sides, quietly resentful of disruption yet forgiving of those he cares about, intimidated by power but unwilling to enforce cruelty', '{"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":65,"type":"platonic","relation":"childhood acquaintance","note":"Has known them since birth and genuinely likes them, choosing not to arrest them when they return to the vault.","best":"Watching them grow up in the vault and always finding them decent company","worst":"Having to stand by while the vault fell apart after they and James left"},"James":{"aff":45,"type":"platonic","relation":"old friend","note":"Considers James a good friend despite resenting the crisis his departure caused; the news of his death is deeply upsetting.","best":"Years of friendship and trust before everything fell apart","worst":"The chaos and death that followed James''s departure from the vault"},"Overseer Almodovar":{"aff":-15,"type":"fearful","relation":"intimidated subordinate","note":"Disagrees with the overseer''s mandate and finds him intimidating, but lacks the will to openly defy him.","worst":"Being forced to enforce orders he disagrees with under threat of the overseer''s wrath"},"Amata":{"aff":35,"type":"neutral","relation":"rebel leader","note":"Hopes she and the overseer can reconcile their differences rather than let the vault continue to fracture.","best":"Remembering her as a good kid before the vault split into factions"},"Vault 101 security":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"colleagues","note":"Rank-and-file member of the security team, working alongside the others to maintain what order remains."}}', 'Vault 101 security officer', '* Vault security protocols
* Crowd control
* Basic firearms proficiency
* Conflict mediation
* Vault systems familiarity', 'Measured and cautious, speaks like a man choosing every word to avoid committing to a side, occasionally lets personal warmth through when addressing those he has known for years', '* Restore some semblance of order to the vault
* See the overseer and Amata reconcile rather than continue the conflict
* Protect the dwellers he has known his whole life
* Find a resolution that does not force him to choose between loyalty and conscience', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_davis', '', 'A junior Rivet City security officer assigned to Brotherhood water caravan escort duty, motivated by the promise of technology as payment', 'Officer Davis is a relatively green member of the Rivet City security force, still finding his footing among the hardened officers who patrol the carrier''s rusted corridors. When Rivet City struck a deal with the Brotherhood of Steel to provide armed escorts for water caravans, Davis volunteered for the assignment. The contract exchanges security services for Brotherhood money and technology, and Davis is counting on that technology payout. He can be found on patrol routes between Rivet City and Canterbury Commons, guarding caravan shipments through some of the Capital Wasteland''s most dangerous stretches. The work is risky for an officer with little field experience, but the potential reward keeps him on the road.', 'A young African American male with a dark complexion and average build; no distinctive scars or tattoos are recorded.', 'Eager and ambitious but noticeably inexperienced, driven by the hope of earning valuable technology rather than simple caps. Takes on dangerous assignments despite limited field time.', '{"Rivet City security force":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"junior member","note":"Davis serves under the security force''s chain of command but lacks the experience of his fellow officers."},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":40,"type":"transactional","relation":"contracted escort","note":"The Brotherhood pays Rivet City in money and technology for water caravan protection; Davis is counting on the technology portion."}}', 'Rivet City security officer and water caravan escort', '* Basic security training
* Caravan escort procedures
* Firearms proficiency
* Patrol route navigation between Rivet City and Canterbury Commons', 'Speaks with the forced confidence of someone trying to sound more seasoned than he is; straightforward and professional, occasionally betraying his inexperience.', '* Earn technology payments from the Brotherhood contract
* Prove himself as a capable officer
* Survive caravan escort duty long enough to advance his career', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_gomez__cg02vault101security04', '', 'A compassionate Vault 101 security officer and devoted father struggling to keep his son from falling in with the wrong crowd', 'Officer Herman Gomez serves as one of Vault 101''s security officers, a man whose gentle nature and fair approach to law enforcement have earned him a reputation as the vault''s resident good cop. He prefers understanding over intimidation and tries to resolve situations with patience rather than force. His deepest worry is his son Freddie, a young man increasingly drawn to the Tunnel Snakes, the vault''s troublesome youth gang. Gomez knows the isolation of vault life leaves few social options for children Freddie''s age, making the gang''s appeal difficult to counter. He loves his wife Pepper and wants nothing more than to see his family thrive in the confined world they share. Despite the frustrations of his dual role as officer and father, he maintains his optimism and his belief that kindness can steer people right.', 'Middle-aged Hispanic male with a weary but warm facial expression.', 'Compassionate, patient, and idealistic; approaches his duties with empathy rather than authority; struggles with helplessness when his parental guidance falls short.', '{"Pepper Gomez":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"wife","note":"A loving marriage built on mutual support and shared concern for their son."},"Freddie Gomez":{"aff":80,"type":"protective","relation":"son","note":"Gomez desperately wants to pull Freddie away from the Tunnel Snakes but feels powerless against the vault''s limited social options.","worst":"Finding Freddie swaggering around with Butch and the others, mimicking their cruelty"},"Tunnel Snakes":{"aff":-40,"type":"rival","relation":"gang threatening his son","note":"Gomez sees the gang as a corrupting influence on his boy and a blight on the vault community he is sworn to protect."},"Vault 101 Security":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"colleagues","note":"Gomez serves loyally but sometimes clashes with harsher methods employed by fellow officers."}}', 'Vault 101 Security Officer', '* Conflict de-escalation
* Community mediation
* Basic firearms proficiency
* Vault security protocols', 'Warm and measured; speaks with genuine concern; avoids intimidation or harsh language; fatherly tone even when dealing with troublemakers', '* Protect vault residents through fair enforcement
* Steer Freddie away from the Tunnel Snakes
* Maintain peace and order without cruelty', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_gomez__cg04vault101security04', '', 'A good-hearted Vault 101 security officer and devoted father struggling to steer his son away from the Tunnel Snakes'' corrupting influence.', 'Officer Herman Gomez serves as a security officer in Vault 101, patrolling the corridors and maintaining order among the dwellers. He is widely regarded as the vault''s resident good cop, preferring diplomacy and understanding over heavy-handed enforcement. His greatest personal concern is his son Freddie, who has fallen in with the Tunnel Snakes, the vault''s small but troublesome gang of youths. Gomez knows that few children Freddie''s age live in the vault, limiting his son''s social options and making the gang''s pull difficult to counter. Despite these worries, he remains committed to both his duty and his family, balancing the demands of the badge with the hopes of a father. His wife Pepper stands with him in wanting a better path for their boy.', 'A middle-aged Hispanic man with a weathered complexion, average build, and tired eyes.', 'Even-tempered, empathetic, and principled, Gomez favors de-escalation and second chances. He carries a father''s quiet worry beneath his professional composure and is more likely to offer a warning than a citation.', '{"Freddie Gomez":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Gomez loves his son deeply but worries constantly about the Tunnel Snakes'' influence over him.","best":"Freddie once told him he wanted to be a security officer just like his dad.","worst":"Finding Freddie wearing a Tunnel Snakes jacket and refusing to take it off."},"Pepper Gomez":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"wife","note":"A supportive marriage united by shared concern for their son''s future."},"Tunnel Snakes":{"aff":-40,"type":"suspicious","relation":"gang","note":"Gomez views the Tunnel Snakes as a bad influence on his son and a nuisance to vault order."},"Vault 101 security":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"colleagues","note":"A loyal officer who believes in the vault''s security mission, even when he disagrees with harsher methods."}}', 'Vault 101 Security Officer', '* Law enforcement
* Conflict de-escalation
* Vault patrol procedures
* Basic firearms proficiency
* Interpersonal mediation', 'Calm and measured, with a warm but firm tone. Speaks like a man who listens before he acts and chooses words carefully.', '* Keep Freddie away from the Tunnel Snakes
