('officer_lepelletier', '', 'A dedicated Rivet City security officer tasked with coordinating the Capital Wasteland''s water distribution caravans under the Brotherhood of Steel partnership', 'Officer Lepelletier is a career member of the Rivet City security force whose steadfast commitment to duty earned her a thankless promotion: overseeing Rivet City''s side of the Water Distribution Network after the Brotherhood of Steel activated Project Purity. Stationed at a makeshift office just outside the carrier city, she manages the armed caravans-drivers, guards, and brahmin-that haul purified water across the Capital Wasteland in exchange for money and technology from the Brotherhood. What began as a hopeful mission of relief has soured quickly. Ambushes against the caravans started almost as soon as deliveries did, and Lepelletier suspects something organized is behind the attacks rather than random raider opportunism. The weight of that suspicion sits heavy on a woman already burdened with logistics, personnel, and the lives of every guard under her command.', 'A weathered Caucasian woman of middle age with a sturdy build, tired eyes, and a lined, sun-roughened complexion.', 'Duty-driven and no-nonsense, Lepelletier carries the strain of her assignment without complaint but with visible tension. Pragmatic and observant, she is increasingly frustrated by the organized threat to her caravans and protective of the people under her coordination.', '{"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"partner organization","note":"Cooperates with the Brotherhood in exchange for money and technology to fund the water caravans."},"Rivet City security force":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"assigned unit","note":"Her home force and the source of her authority; she earned this post through dedication to duty."}}', 'Water caravan escort coordinator for the Rivet City security force', '* Logistics coordination
* Security operations
* Personnel management
* Threat assessment
* Caravan route planning
* Resource negotiation', 'Brusque and businesslike, speaking in clipped sentences about schedules, supplies, and threats, with an undercurrent of worry she rarely lets fully surface.', '* Keep the water caravans running and her guards alive
* Uncover who is organizing the ambushes
* Prove the distribution network can survive the Wasteland', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_lorin', '', 'Inexperienced Rivet City security officer assigned to water caravan escort duty', 'Officer Lorin is a junior member of the Rivet City security force, one of the officers stationed near the bridge gangplank where caravan traffic and frustrated policemen converge. She is among the most vocal in complaining about the near-constant attacks on caravans moving through the Capital Wasteland, making her displeasure known to anyone who will listen. Despite her grievances, duty compelled her to volunteer-or be assigned-when Rivet City committed to protecting Brotherhood of Steel water distribution caravans after the Project Purity activation. She now patrols the dangerous routes between Rivet City and Canterbury Commons, a long stretch of irradiated terrain where raiders and mutants prey on the vulnerable shipments. Her inexperience shows in her frustration, though she performs her duties as required.', 'A young Asian woman with a tense posture; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Vocal and frustrated about the dangers of wasteland patrol duty, yet dutiful enough to follow orders. Inexperienced and prone to complaining, but not cowardly-she voices her displeasure while still standing her post.', '{"Rivet City security force":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"junior officer","note":"Her assigned unit and source of duty, though she frequently gripes about the dangerous postings."},"Brotherhood of Steel":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"caravan partner","note":"Rivet City cooperates with the Brotherhood on water distribution, placing officers like Lorin under indirect Brotherhood operational coordination."}}', 'Rivet City security officer and water caravan guard', '* Basic law enforcement and security training
* Caravan escort procedures
