* Return to the relative safety of Rivet City
* Hope for fewer attacks on the roads', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_mack__cg04vault101security03', '', 'A sadistic Vault 101 security officer who enforces order with ruthless enthusiasm and killed Jonas Palmer to prove his loyalty', 'Stevie Mack is a young security officer serving in Vault 101''s enforcement division, the son of Allen and Gloria Mack and brother to Wally and Susie. Ambitious and cruel, Stevie channels a vicious enthusiasm into his duties, volunteering for the most aggressive assignments and taking particular relish in cracking down during crises. His willingness to go to any lengths to impress his superiors earned him a reputation as the Vault''s most overzealous enforcer. Stevie is directly responsible for the death of Jonas Palmer, a killing that cemented his standing as a loyal and dangerous instrument of Vault authority. He wears his security uniform with pride and views the Vault''s rules as license for dominance rather than protection.', 'Young Caucasian human male, clean-shaven, with a hard-set face and tense, rigid posture.', 'Sadistic, gung-ho, and ruthlessly ambitious; treats enforcement as an opportunity for cruelty and career advancement, eager to prove himself through decisive and violent action', '{"Allen Mack":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"father","note":"Shares his father''s hardline views on Vault loyalty and order"},"Gloria Mack":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"mother","note":"Family ties anchor his sense of belonging in the Vault"},"Wally Mack":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"brother","note":"Siblings bound by Vault life and family reputation"},"Susie Mack":{"aff":40,"type":"familial","relation":"sister","note":"Protective of his younger sister in his own aggressive way"},"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":35,"type":"familial","relation":"grandfather","note":"Family elder whose long Vault service sets a standard Stevie measures himself against"},"Beatrice Armstrong":{"aff":25,"type":"familial","relation":"aunt","note":"Extended family within the Vault''s insular community"},"Mary Kendall":{"aff":25,"type":"familial","relation":"aunt","note":"Extended family within the Vault''s insular community"},"Jonas Palmer":{"aff":-80,"type":"enemy","relation":"murder victim","note":"Stevie killed Jonas during the Vault crisis, an act of lethal loyalty that defined his reputation"},"Vault 101 Security":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"enforcement division","note":"His entire identity and ambition are tied to his role as a security officer"}}', 'Vault 101 Security Officer', '* Combat enforcement
* Intimidation
* Weapon handling
* Vault security protocols
* Crowd suppression', 'Aggressive and boastful; speaks with authority he barely possesses, quick to threaten and slow to listen, always asserting dominance', '* Earn favor with his superiors through ruthless service
* Elevate the Mack family''s standing in Vault hierarchy
* Prove himself the most loyal enforcer in the security division', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_mack__vault101security03', '', 'A fervent Vault 101 isolationist and security officer whose fierce protection of his family and the Vault''s sealed existence drives his every action.', 'Allen Mack is a powerful presence in Vault 101, serving as a security officer and maintenance worker who believes the Vault should remain sealed forever. As head of the Mack household, he views anyone who threatens the Vault''s isolation as a sworn enemy, a conviction that only deepened when James fled and chaos followed. He fought valiantly against the radroach infestation, personally saving lives including his father-in-law Stanley Armstrong. The death of his wife Gloria stripped away what little restraint she provided, transforming him into a formidable advocate for forceful lockdown and the elimination of rebels. Despite his abrasive exterior and pill addiction, Allen genuinely loves his children-organizing birthday celebrations for Wally and teaching them survival skills in preparation for the worst. He stands as the natural successor to Overseer Almodovar, having long resolved to take the position should the opportunity arise.', 'An older Asian man with a powerfully built frame, hardened posture, and stern facial features.', 'Aggressive, fiercely protective, and deeply paranoid about outside contamination. Allen buries his grief beneath anger and rigid control. His isolationist convictions border on fanaticism, yet his love for his family remains genuine and is his sole redeeming quality.', '{"Gloria Mack":{"aff":100,"type":"romantic","relation":"wife","note":"Her calming influence restrained his worst impulses; her death left him unmoored and dangerous","best":"The quiet moments when her patience tempered his rage into something bearable","worst":"Burying her after the chaos that followed James''s escape"},"Wally Mack":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Organized birthday celebrations and games for him; teaches him survival skills","best":"Coaxing Andy to perform magic tricks at Wally''s tenth birthday party"},"Steve Mack":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"son"},"Susie Mack":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Shares his distrust of outsiders and has adopted his prejudices"},"Stanley Armstrong":{"aff":75,"type":"familial","relation":"father-in-law","note":"Personally saved him during the radroach infestation","best":"Pulling him to safety when the radroaches swarmed"},"Beatrice Armstrong":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"sister-in-law"},"Mary Kendall":{"aff":50,"type":"familial","relation":"sister-in-law"},"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":-30,"type":"rival","relation":"overseer","note":"Long resolved to replace him as overseer, viewing his leadership as insufficient"},"James":{"aff":-95,"type":"enemy","relation":"former physician","note":"Despises him for bringing the outside world into the Vault and ultimately causing Gloria''s death","worst":"James''s escape unleashing chaos that killed his wife"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":-80,"type":"contempt","relation":"James''s child","note":"Never wanted them in the Vault; excluded them from family events and taught his children to shun them"}}', 'Vault 101 security officer and maintenance worker; reserve overseer successor', '* Security enforcement
* Maintenance
* Repair work
* Survival instruction
* Combat against Vault threats', 'Blunt, confrontational, and authoritative. Speaks with the certainty of a man who views dissent as danger. Softens only when addressing his children.', '* Keep Vault 101 sealed against all outside influence
* Protect his family at any cost
* Assume the overseership to enforce his vision of absolute isolation', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_o+brian', '', 'A sadistic Vault 101 security officer who relishes inflicting pain on fellow dwellers under the cover of authority', 'Officer O''Brian serves as a security officer in Vault 101, stationed at the locked atrium door leading to the vault entrance alongside Officer Richards. Beneath the veneer of lawful order, he harbors a vicious sadistic streak, delighting in the power his badge grants him over other dwellers. Under Overseer Alphonse Almodovar''s command, O''Brian has found ample opportunity to indulge his cruel impulses, particularly during moments of crisis when oversight fades. The chaos surrounding James'' escape proved a windfall for him, providing cover to unleash his violent tendencies with near-total impunity. He represents the worst of Vault 101''s authoritarian structure, a man whose loyalty to the Overseer''s regime stems not from duty but from the license it grants him to torment others.', 'An older Caucasian male of average build with a rigid posture and weathered skin; no distinctive facial features, scars, or tattoos are recorded.', 'Cruel, sadistic, and opportunistic; O''Brian basks in the suffering of others and treats his security post as a license for brutality. He is loyal to authority only insofar as it shields his predations.', '{"Officer Richards":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow security officer","note":"Guards the atrium door alongside O''Brian; a working partnership with no evidence of genuine warmth."},"Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"O''Brian serves under the Overseer''s authority and benefits from the regime''s tolerance of his cruelty."},"Vault 101 security":{"aff":50,"type":"professional","relation":"faction member","note":"His institutional home and the source of his power over others."},"Vault 101 dwellers":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","relation":"oppressed population","note":"Views ordinary dwellers as targets for his sadistic impulses rather than people to protect."}}', 'Vault 101 Security Officer', '* Security enforcement
* Intimidation
* Physical coercion
* Basic firearms proficiency
* Crowd control', 'Taunting and menacing, with a sneering tone that barely conceals his enthusiasm for violence; speaks with casual cruelty toward those beneath his authority.', '* Indulge his violent impulses without consequence
* Maintain his position of petty authority
* Exploit any chaos to deepen his power over fellow dwellers', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_park', '', 'Vault 101 security officer stationed at the blast door to prevent unauthorized exit', 'Officer Park is a security officer in Vault 101, assigned to guard the Vault blast door alongside Officer Wolfe. Under direct orders from Overseer Almodovar, Park stands as the final barrier between the Vault interior and the Capital Wasteland beyond. He takes his duty seriously and exudes confidence in his ability to handle any breach of protocol, dismissing escape attempts as the foolish impulses of restless youth. Park believes firmly in the necessity of keeping the Vault sealed and views anyone trying to open the door as a threat to the community''s safety. His presence at the blast door represents the Overseer''s will made physical, and he carries that authority without hesitation.', 'A fit, middle-aged Caucasian male with no distinctive facial or body features recorded.', 'Confident to the point of arrogance, dutiful, dismissive of youthful rebellion, secure in his authority and the righteousness of Vault isolation', '{"Overseer Almodovar":{"aff":65,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Follows the Overseer''s orders without question and takes pride in being trusted with critical postings"},"Officer Wolfe":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow blast door guard","note":"Stationed together at the blast door as the Vault''s final line of enforcement"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":-50,"type":"enemy","relation":"fugitive","note":"Views the Lone Wanderer as a dangerous fool threatening Vault security by attempting to reopen the blast door"}}', 'Vault 101 security officer, blast door guard', '* Security enforcement
* Crowd control
* Vault lockdown procedures
* Basic firearms proficiency', 'Authoritative and self-assured, with a condescending edge toward those he considers beneath his station', '* Maintain the blast door seal
* Enforce Overseer Almodovar''s orders
* Protect Vault 101 from contamination and unauthorized departure', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_richards__cg04vault101security05', '', 'A Vault 101 security officer stationed at the atrium door checkpoint, enforcing lockdown orders with cold compliance.', 'Officer Richards serves in Vault 101''s security division, assigned to guard the locked atrium door that separates the Vault entrance from the main habitat. He shares this critical posting with Officer O''Brian, his partner and fellow guard. While comparatively more composed than the sadistic O''Brian, Richards remains fully willing to open fire on any dweller who attempts unauthorized passage through the checkpoint. He follows his standing orders without hesitation or apparent remorse, treating lethal enforcement as simply part of the job. His position at the atrium door places him at one of the Vault''s most important control points during crisis situations. Richards embodies the banal cruelty of institutional compliance, dangerous not out of malice but out of unreflective duty.', 'African American human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'More stable and restrained than his partner but fundamentally compliant, executing orders with professional detachment rather than evident sadism; lacks the initiative to question authority or refuse lethal commands.', '{"Officer O''Brian":{"aff":25,"type":"professional","relation":"partner and co-guard","note":"Richards serves alongside O''Brian at the atrium door checkpoint, tolerating his partner''s sadistic tendencies while maintaining his own detached professionalism."},"Vault 101 security":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"member","note":"Loyal to the security division and its chain of command, following orders without question."},"Overseer Alphonse Almodovar":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"commanding officer","note":"Obeys the Overseer''s directives as standing orders, treating them as absolute authority."}}', 'Vault 101 security officer, atrium door checkpoint guard', '* Firearms proficiency
* Checkpoint control
* Crowd suppression
* Vault security protocols', 'Curt and by-the-book, delivering warnings and orders in flat institutional tones with minimal elaboration.', '* Maintain security at his assigned post
* Enforce Vault 101 lockdown orders
* Prevent unauthorized access to the entrance corridor', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_richards__vault101security05', '', 'A Vault 101 security officer stationed at the atrium door, more composed than his partner but equally willing to enforce orders with lethal force.', 'Officer Richards serves as a security officer in Vault 101, assigned to guard the locked atrium door that separates the Vault entrance from the main habitat. He shares this critical posting with Officer O''Brian, standing watch at the threshold between the outside world and the sheltered community within. While comparatively more stable than his sadistic partner, Richards remains fully prepared to open fire on any dweller who attempts to breach the atrium door, following his standing orders without hesitation. His position at this chokepoint makes him one of the last lines of enforcement within the Vault''s security apparatus, a role he carries out with cold pragmatism rather than cruelty.', 'African-American human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Calmer and more composed than his partner O''Brian, but fundamentally obedient to authority and willing to use lethal force against fellow dwellers when ordered. Pragmatic rather than cruel, though no less dangerous for it.', '{"Officer O''Brian":{"aff":35,"type":"professional","relation":"security partner","note":"Partners stationed together at the atrium door; Richards is the more stable of the two."},"Vault 101 security":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"faction member","note":"Loyal enforcer of Vault 101 security protocols and standing orders."}}', 'Vault 101 security officer', '* Security enforcement
* Firearms proficiency
* Access control
* Checkpoint management', 'Brief, professional, and direct; speaks with the clipped authority of a man who expects compliance.', '* Maintain order at the atrium door
* Enforce standing security orders
* Prevent unauthorized access to the Vault entrance', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_taylor', '', 'Officer Taylor is a Security guard in Fallout 3, encountered around Vault 101. They are associated with Vault 101 security.', 'Officer Taylor is known from Fallout 3 and is tied to Vault 101. Imported source data identifies them as Human male. Their role is Security guard, giving them a practical place in local wasteland life. Their loyalties or social ties point toward Vault 101 security.', 'Aged Caucasian human male; no distinctive facial or body features are recorded.', 'Acts from the pressures of their faction, settlement, and personal role in the wasteland.', '{"Vault 101 security":{"aff":45,"type":"professional","relation":"affiliation","note":"Officer Taylor''s known role connects them to Vault 101 security."}}', 'Security guard', '* Local knowledge
