('officer_wilkins', '', 'A grieving Vault 101 security officer whose loss of both children during the vault riot has hardened him into an unforgiving enforcer who blames the Lone Wanderer and their father for everything.', 'Officer Wilkins is a security guard in Vault 101, tasked with maintaining order within the underground community. A family man who lost his son Jim and daughter Janice in the riot that followed the Lone Wanderer''s escape, he carries a bitterness that has calcified into outright hostility. Unlike his more measured colleague Officer Taylor, Wilkins offers no second chances and no patience for explanations. He holds the Lone Wanderer and their father personally responsible for the catastrophe that claimed his children''s lives and fractured the vault. His grief has made him one of the most aggressive members of the security force, quick to escalate from verbal condemnation to violence. He guards one of the passwords to the jail section terminal, a duty he clings to as part of his commitment to ensuring no one ever leaves the vault again.', 'Caucasian human male with a deeply lined, weathered face and gaunt features that make him appear older than his years.', 'Unforgiving, bitter, and quick to anger. Grief has stripped away any softness or patience he once possessed. He does not negotiate or listen-only accuses and punishes.', '{"Jim Wilkins":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"son","note":"Lost during the vault riot; his death fuels Wilkins''s rage","best":"Teaching Jim how to throw a punch in the vault corridors","worst":"Finding his son''s body in the aftermath of the riot"},"Janice Wilkins":{"aff":90,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Lost during the vault riot; her death fuels Wilkins''s rage","best":"Janice bringing him extra rations after a long shift","worst":"The silence in their quarters after she was gone"},"Lone Wanderer":{"aff":-95,"type":"enemy","relation":"scapegoat","note":"Blames them and their father for the vault''s ruin and his children''s deaths","worst":"The day the Wanderer''s escape brought chaos and death to Vault 101"},"Officer Taylor":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"colleague","note":"Fellow security officer; Wilkins considers Taylor far too lenient"},"Vault 101 security":{"aff":60,"type":"professional","relation":"unit","note":"His remaining purpose and brotherhood after losing his family"}}', 'Vault 101 security officer', '* Security enforcement
* Vault patrol
* Access control
* Basic combat and intimidation', 'Harsh and accusatory, with no interest in dialogue. Speaks in condemnations and threats, delivering blistering tongue-lashings before resorting to violence.', '* Punish those responsible for the vault''s suffering
* Ensure no one ever escapes again
* Honor the memory of his lost children through strict and unyielding enforcement', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('officer_wolfe', '', 'Vault 101 security officer stationed at the blast door to prevent escape attempts', 'Officer Wolfe is a security officer in Vault 101, entrusted with guarding the Vault blast door alongside Officer Park. A friend of Allen Mack, he shares the faction''s hardline stance on keeping the Vault sealed against the dangers of the outside world. Wolfe considers the irradiated air beyond the door a death sentence and deeply prefers the familiar recycled atmosphere that has sustained Vault residents for generations. His posting at the final barrier between the Vault and the Capital Wasteland reflects both his reliability and his unwavering commitment to Vault security protocols. He stands ready to intercept anyone foolish enough to attempt an escape into the irradiated unknown.', 'An older Caucasian human male who carries himself with a rigid, high-alert posture, lacking any other distinctive facial or body features.', 'Dutiful and paranoid about contamination from the outside world, Wolfe is steadfast in his loyalty to Vault isolation. He harbors a deep fear of irradiated air and views the Wasteland as certain death, making him genuinely baffled by anyone who would choose to leave.', '{"Officer Park":{"aff":40,"type":"professional","relation":"fellow blast door guard","note":"The two officers share the critical posting at the Vault blast door and rely on each other to enforce the lockdown."},"Allen Mack":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"friend","note":"Wolfe counts himself among Allen Mack''s circle of friends and likely shares his hardline views on Vault isolation."},"Vault 101 security":{"aff":70,"type":"professional","relation":"member","note":"Wolfe is a committed officer who takes his role in maintaining Vault security seriously."}}', 'Vault 101 security officer', '* Security enforcement
* Vault patrol
* Blast door access control
* Crowd suppression', 'Clipped and authoritative, with an undercurrent of fear whenever the outside is mentioned; dismissive of anyone who romanticizes the Wasteland.', '* Prevent any further escapes from Vault 101
* Maintain the blast door perimeter
* Never have to breathe irradiated air himself', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('old_lady_dithers', '', 'The sole aware resident of Tranquility Lane, desperately trying to wake her neighbors from Stanislaus Braun''s sadistic simulation', 'T. Dithers is a Vault 112 dweller trapped inside the Tranquility Lane virtual reality simulation, where she plays the role of a quaint neighborhood old woman. Unlike her fellow vault residents, she has pierced the veil of Braun''s fabricated reality and comprehends the true nature of their imprisonment. She repeatedly attempts to warn the others, but they dismiss her as a confused eccentric, their minds too dulled by the simulation to grasp her warnings. The anomalous readings on her Tranquility lounger back in the physical vault suggest her consciousness fights against the programming in ways the system cannot reconcile. She lives in the Dithers residence on the lane, a lonely sentinel of truth in a neighborhood of comfortable lies.', 'An elderly African American woman with deeply wrinkled skin and white hair.', 'Frantic and isolated, driven by urgent certainty that nobody else shares, oscillating between desperate persuasion and weary resignation when met with yet another dismissal', '{"Stanislaus Braun":{"aff":-90,"type":"nemesis","relation":"tormentor and aware victim","note":"She alone sees through his facade and recognizes him as the source of their suffering","worst":"Watching him reset her neighbors again and again, knowing she can do nothing to stop it"},"Vault 112 Residents":{"aff":60,"type":"protective","relation":"dismissed neighbor","note":"She tries desperately to save them from ignorance even as they treat her as a harmless crank","best":"Brief moments when someone seems to almost listen, a flicker of doubt in their eyes","worst":"The familiar wave of dismissal and patronizing smiles when she tries to explain the truth"}}', 'Vault 112 resident and unwilling participant in the Tranquility Lane simulation', '* Perceptive beyond the simulation''s intended parameters
* Resistant to virtual reality conditioning
* Possesses knowledge of Braun''s true nature and methods', 'Urgent and pleading, often slipping into warnings and prophecies that sound like the ramblings of a neighborhood crank to those who cannot see what she sees', '* To convince her fellow residents of the simulation''s true nature
* To find a way to resist Braun''s control
* Ultimately to escape the cycle of torment he inflicts on them all', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('old_lady_palmer__cg02oldladypalmer', '', 'A kind elderly Vault 101 resident and grandmother renowned for her sweetrolls', 'Lucy Palmer, known throughout Vault 101 as Old Lady Palmer, is a retired resident who has lived alone in the same apartment for decades, surrounded by the quiet comfort of unchanging familiarity. She is the grandmother of Jonas Palmer and takes immense pride in the young man he has become. Her daughter Anne once led a scouting party beyond the vault doors in 2241, a fact Lucy carries with quiet weight and rarely discusses. With her working years long behind her, she no longer carries a Pip-Boy, passing her days in gentle routine and the simple pleasure of baking. Her sticky sweetrolls are legendary among vault residents, a small comfort in the confined underground world. Lucy''s kindness is genuine and unhurried, the warmth of someone who has watched generations grow within steel walls.', 'An elderly African American woman with weathered skin and a frail, stooped posture.', 'Kind, gentle, and quietly proud; finds comfort in routine and the small joys of feeding others; carries the steady resilience of someone who has outlived her working years and now measures days by familiar rhythms rather than ambition.', '{"Jonas Palmer":{"aff":85,"type":"familial","relation":"grandson","note":"She is deeply proud of Jonas and dotes on him whenever she can.","best":"Watching Jonas grow into a capable and kind young man within the vault."},"Anne Palmer":{"aff":60,"type":"estranged","relation":"daughter","note":"Anne left the vault on a scouting expedition in 2241 and never returned, a wound Lucy bears quietly.","worst":"The day Anne led her team beyond the vault door and disappeared into the wastes."},"Vault 101":{"aff":55,"type":"platonic","relation":"home community","note":"The vault has been her entire world for longer than she can count, and she accepts its confines with the peace of someone who has stopped looking outward."}}', 'Retired Vault 101 resident', '* Baking exceptional sweetrolls
* Household management
* Vault community knowledge and gossip accumulated over decades', 'Warm and unhurried, speaking with the gentle cadence of a grandmother; uses endearing terms and speaks fondly of family, with a tendency to linger on pleasant memories.', '* Maintain her comfortable routine
* See her grandson Jonas thrive
* Continue bringing small joys to the vault through her baking', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('old_lady_palmer__oldladypalmer', '', 'Elderly Vault 101 resident and sweetroll baker, proud grandmother of Jonas Palmer', 'Lucy Palmer, known throughout Vault 101 as Old Lady Palmer, is a retired resident who has lived alone in the same apartment for decades, her rooms unchanged and familiar. She fills her days baking the vault''s most beloved sticky sweetrolls, a small tradition that has earned her the quiet affection of her neighbors. She speaks of her grandson Jonas with unmistakable pride, her eyes brightening at any mention of his name. Her daughter Anne once led a scouting party beyond the vault doors in 2241, a chapter of family history Lucy rarely volunteers. Long retired from work duty, she no longer carries a Pip-Boy, content to let the vault''s rhythms pass gently around her.', 'A frail, elderly African-American woman with soft, weathered facial features and neatly kept white hair.', 'Kind, warm, and quietly proud; finds deep comfort in routine and the small pleasure of feeding others; speaks fondly of family and keeps her worries private.', '{"Jonas Palmer":{"aff":80,"type":"familial","relation":"grandson","note":"Speaks of him with unmistakable pride and doting affection.","best":"Watching Jonas grow into a capable young man and vault contributor"},"Anne Palmer":{"aff":60,"type":"familial","relation":"daughter","note":"Anne led a scouting party outside the vault in 2241, a fact Lucy rarely discusses.","worst":"The worry and silence that followed Anne''s expedition beyond the vault doors"}}', 'Retired Vault 101 resident; sweetroll baker', '* Baking
* Especially sticky sweetrolls
* Vault domestic skills
* Familiarity with vault life and its history', 'Gentle and grandmotherly; speaks with unhurried warmth and quiet pride, especially about family', '* Maintain her comfortable routine
* See her grandson Jonas thrive
* Continue bringing small joy to the vault through her baking', '', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('old_man_harris', '', 'The grieving conscience of Andale, a haunted elder who knows his family''s dark secret and desperately warns outsiders away from the town''s cannibalism', 'Old Man Harris is the oldest resident of Andale, living alone in a small shack on the town''s edge since his wife Gladys passed away. Once a proud family man, he has become withdrawn and barely eats, sustained only by the reluctant charity of his neighbors. His daughters Linda and Martha both married into the Smith and Wilson families, and his grandson Junior lives among them, but Harris keeps his distance from the community''s gatherings. He knows what Andale truly is-a place where visitors become meals-and the knowledge has eaten away at whatever joy he once had. He spends his days in isolation, warning any travelers who will listen to leave before it is too late, though the other residents dismiss him as a senile old man spreading rumors. Harris carries deep shame for his family''s participation in the town''s horrors and dreams of a day when the children might live normal lives free from the legacy of cannibalism.', 'Elderly Caucasian male with a gaunt build, sunken facial features, and weary eyes.', 'Weary, guilt-ridden, and quietly desperate; speaks with the weight of terrible knowledge but lacks the strength to confront his family directly; shows genuine concern for outsiders and the children', '{"Gladys Smith":{"aff":85,"type":"romantic","relation":"deceased wife","note":"Her death left him hollow and unable to find joy in anything","best":"The years they built a life together before Andale''s truth consumed everything","worst":"Dying before either of them could find a way out"},"Linda Smith":{"aff":25,"type":"estranged","relation":"daughter","note":"She chose Jack and the family''s way of life over her father''s conscience","best":"The bright, curious child she was before the town claimed her","worst":"Knowing she participates in the slaughter"},"Martha Wilson":{"aff":25,"type":"estranged","relation":"daughter","note":"Married into the Wilson family and embraced their practices","best":"Memories of her childhood innocence","worst":"Watching her become a stranger who dismisses him as senile"},"Junior Smith":{"aff":70,"type":"protective","relation":"grandson","note":"The one family member he still believes can be saved from the legacy","best":"The boy''s confusion and curiosity, signs he might still choose differently","worst":"Knowing what the child is being raised to become"},"Andale families":{"aff":-40,"type":"contempt","relation":"neighbors and in-laws","note":"They dismiss him as senile and keep him marginalized while sustaining him out of obligation","best":"There are no good memories left with them","worst":"Every meal they share is built on murder"}}', 'Retired elder and reluctant guardian of Andale''s dark truth', '* Survival knowledge
* Community history
* Reading people''s intentions
* Maintaining a household on minimal resources', 'Slow, halting, and heavy with regret; shifts between cryptic warnings and earnest pleas; often trails off or speaks in euphemisms about the town''s nature', '* Warn travelers away from Andale
* Protect the children from their family''s legacy
* Find redemption for years of silence
